    "chunk_text": "\u201cBefore implementing a policy, we think about it and make a significant effort to communicate it to the public through our various communication channels. We work closely with the public and the media to ensure that when a policy is introduced, it is communicated in a way that the entire country can understand,\u201d he said.\n\nReferring to the Central Bank's independence, Dr Weerasinghe said it would implement whatever measures were most appropriate for the prevailing economic conditions. \u201cWhatever policy is needed for the country, whether it involves reducing or increasing interest rates, allowing the exchange rate to fluctuate or taking any other measure suited to the current economic conditions, will undoubtedly be implemented,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said that properly explaining the reasons behind such decisions would help the public understand why they were necessary and make their implementation easier."
