    "chunk_text": "He accused the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) Government of abandoning the democratic principles it advocated during the 2022 public uprising, which challenged political corruption and economic mismanagement.\n\nMudalige said the Government\u2019s economic policies, centred on the International Monetary Fund (IMF) program, had imposed a heavy burden on ordinary citizens through taxation and rising living costs.\n\nHe also criticised the Government over alleged police violence and warned that expanding police powers under the proposed legislation could further undermine civil liberties.\n\nRecalling the repression faced by the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) under the PTA, Mudalige said it was a tragedy that a political movement which had experienced such repression was now preparing to introduce laws that could restrict the democratic rights of citizens.\n\n\u201cWe demand that the Government immediately withdraw these anti-people, repressive laws \u2014 the PTA, PSTA and OSA,\u201d he said.\n\nMudalige invited the public to join tomorrow\u2019s protest, warning that the movement would continue its campaign until the legislation was repealed."
