    "chunk_text": "The collision occurred in the area between Kafr Ammar and Al-Raqqa stations in Al-Ayyat, close to where Egypt's deadliest train tragedy occurred in February 2002, when a fire engulfed a passenger train travelling from Cairo to Luxor.\n\nThere were calls in Egypt on Sunday for the transport minister to resign over the latest deadly rail disaster.\n\nForeign leaders and dignitaries have shared condolences and support for the victims.\n\nSaudi Arabia's ministry of foreign affairs expressed \"solidarity\" with Egypt and wished those hurt a speedy recovery.\n\nTurkey's ambassador to Egypt wrote on X that he extended \"heartfelt condolences and sincere sympathy\" to the victims, their families, and the Egyptian people."
