    "chunk_text": "The program opened with an address by Deputy High Commissioner of Sri Lanka for Southern India Dr. Ganesanathan Geathiswaran. \u201cIndia and Sri Lanka are bound by geography, history and commerce, and that relationship is stronger than ever. There is considerable scope to deepen these ties through greater business engagement and investment. Chennai, with its strong industrial base and entrepreneurial ecosystem, is an important market for this conversation. We hope the forum will help build lasting partnerships between businesses in our two countries and translate shared opportunities into meaningful economic outcomes,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cFor investors, the strength of a proposition lies not just in the opportunity it offers, but in the certainty of the framework within which they operate. Port City Colombo has been designed to provide that clarity through a statutory framework and defined investor safeguards. For Indian businesses looking to grow their reach, Sri Lanka offers proximity, familiarity and access to wider regional opportunities. This is about extending business capabilities and reaching new markets as a complementary partner, with the centre of growth remaining in India,\u201d said Colombo Port City Economic Commission Chairman Harsha Amarasekera, PC. He further emphasised that Port City Colombo is a project of national importance, operating under the direct purview of the Office of Sri Lanka\u2019s President, Anura Kumara Dissanayake, who also serves as Finance Minister, underscoring the Government\u2019s interest in the project."
  },
