    "md5": "8103131f6b1c28fea8ae9ec977c8e66a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Trump says Qatar, Saudi prefer peace in Iran conflict\n\nReuters\u00a0- US President Donald Trump said on Monday he plans to hold off on new military strikes against Iran for \u200bthe time being after appeals from countries in the region, including from Qatar's prime minister in White House talks.\n\nTrump, in a Reuters interview and a later appearance in the White House \u200cpress briefing room, said he plans to keep up a naval blockade in the Strait of Hormuz for now.\n\n\"The United States of America is fully locked and loaded with the best equipment ever made, and we don't think there's going to be any reason to use it,\" Trump told reporters.\n\nHe said he was acting \"at the behest of countries that are their neighbors\" and specifically cited Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain, Kuwait and others that prefer the US \u200bnot launch new attacks.\n\nTrump spoke after meeting with Qatari Prime Minister Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al-Thani, a key intermediary with Tehran, as efforts to end the war ramp up following last \u200bweek's US midterm election.\n\nMore than eight months into the conflict he launched alongside Israel on February 28, Trump has played down the likelihood of major warfare \u2060restarting soon but remains unwilling to accept an existing Iranian truce plan. Senior US and Gulf officials have cast doubt on the chances of an imminent deal.\n\nMutual attacks continue, with the US striking Iran's \u200bQeshm island overnight, according to Iranian state media, and Iran attacking tankers in the Gulf and Strait of Hormuz this month while its Yemeni Houthi allies have hit Saudi Arabia.\n\nAl-Thani, who is both prime minister and \u200bforeign minister of Qatar, met Trump after visiting Tehran last week.\n\nThe prime minister called his talks with both Trump and Vice President JD Vance positive.\n\n\"Grateful for the positive discussions on reaching a deal and bringing peace to the region,\" he said on X."
  },
