    "chunk_size_bytes": 1341,
    "chunk_text": "Vance, who led the negotiations for a \u200bshort-lived truce in June, will also meet Al-Thani, \u200bwhose country has been a prime mediator since \u2060early in the war, conveying messages between the sides and proposing ways to bridge their differences.\n\nAnxiety over the war has pervaded the region for months, and Turkish President Tayyip Erdogan said on Monday he had told Trump that Ankara did not want to see a new escalation.\n\nSunday night's strikes on Qeshm island did not impact vital infrastructure or services, a provincial official told Iran's semi-official Fars news agency on Monday. The US has not commented on the Iranian media reports.\n\nA senior Iranian source told Reuters that US strikes were targeting Iranian radar systems serving both air defence and ship navigation, as well as bases for missile launchers and mine-laying systems.\n\nAttacks on tankers in the Gulf and Strait \u2060of Hormuz ramped \u200bup sharply in October and have continued at the highest rate since the start of the war, figures from international \u200bmaritime agencies showed last week.\n\nIran, which typically does not acknowledge striking vessels that report being hit by projectiles, said on Sunday a tanker had hit a mine east of the Strait of Hormuz.\n\nA state television reporter said on Monday that 11 tankers \u200bhad been \"disabled\" over the past 10 days."
