    "chunk_text": "Elsewhere, Russia \u200band Ukraine are coming to US-brokered talks to end \u200bMoscow's war on Ukraine with good intentions, \u2060a US official said on Monday.\n\nIn a briefing ahead of Tuesday's talks in Abu Dhabi, a US official told reporters that both sides have shown a little bit of flexibility privately on territorial issues.\n\nThe global oil \u200bmarket is showing signs \u2060of a return to excess supply as demand drops because of high prices, some analysts said. The global oil surplus is estimated at around 1.4 million barrels per day in October, JPMorgan said in a report last week.\n\nOPEC oil output rose in October, a Reuters survey found, led by gains in Saudi Arabia, Kuwait and Iraq despite continued constraints on exports.\n\nCrude output from the 11-member Organization of the Petroleum \u2060Exporting Countries \u200brose by 1.38 million bpd from the previous month to 22.87 million bpd, the survey found.\n\nUS crude oil and product stockpiles \u200bwere expected to have fallen last week, a preliminary Reuters poll showed on Monday.\n\nStocks of crude oil in the US Strategic Petroleum Reserve fell to 279.5 million barrels last week, the lowest level since October 1982, according to data from the Department \u200bof Energy."
