    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "UK\u2019s Russell Brand sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in jail for rape, sexual assault\n\nReuters\u00a0- Comedian Russell Brand, once one of Britain's most \u200bhigh-profile broadcasters and a Hollywood star, was jailed for 10-and-a-half years on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and sexually \u200cassaulting three others around two decades ago.\n\nBrand \u2013 the former husband of US pop singer Katy Perry who in recent years moved away from the mainstream \u2013 was found guilty on Thursday of committing the offences between 2004 and 2009. He had denied the charges.\n\nThe 51-year-old stood in the dock at London's Southwark Crown Court as Judge Joel Bennathan sentenced him to 10 years and six \u200bmonths in prison. Brand will serve two-thirds of the sentence in custody before being released on licence.\n\nThe judge said Brand was a sexual predator \u200bwho believed \"fame meant you could act how you liked, when you liked, unhindered by the rules by which decent people live\".\n\n\"Whatever \u2060women wear, wherever they go, indeed whatever they drink, they retain the right to say no and to demand justice from the criminal courts when sexual predators \u200blike you, Russell Brand, act without their consent,\" Bennathan said.\n\nBrand mouthed \"I love you\" to his wife before he was led down to the cells.\n\nSpeaking \u200boutside court, Detective Superintendent Andy Furphy from London's Metropolitan Police paid tribute to Brand's victims, saying, \"they have shown immense bravery, dignity and resilience\".\n\n\"Their courage in coming forward has not only led to this outcome but may also give confidence to others who have suffered sexual violence to seek help and report what happened to them,\" he added.\n\nThe Met has said Brand was under \u200binvestigation for two other alleged rapes, one involving a then-16-year-old girl, and the force's chief Mark Rowley said on Friday that he \"wouldn't be surprised if many more came \u200bforward\"."
