    "chunk_size_bytes": 1760,
    "chunk_text": "Larger-than-life Leo statue awaits the pope on Peru\u2019s Pacific coast\n\nReuters\u00a0- Before Pope Leo \u200breaches Peru later this week, a larger-than-life version is already waiting for him on the Pacific shore. \u200cA towering white statue of the pontiff, arms stretched wide, was inaugurated on Monday ahead of Leo's final and most personal leg of his South American tour.\n\nThe 14-meter (46-foot) monument stands in Callao, a port city adjoining Lima, and is billed by its municipality as the world's tallest \u200bsculpture of a pope. It depicts the first US-born pope in flowing white robes in a country that \u200bhas embraced him as one of its own.\n\nLeo\u2019s arrival in Peru on Wednesday will cap his \u206012-day, three-country tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru, his first to South America as pope and a return to \u200ba region where he spent years as a missionary. The 71-year-old pontiff has used the trip to call for greater unity in a \u200bpolitically divided region and to address an array of social, economic and environmental issues.\n\n\"It's a perfect welcome for the pope,\" said Natalia Moran, 29, who came to the unveiling with her mother. They both wore T-shirts with an image of the pontiff and the message \"Welcome home, \u200bPope Leo.\"\n\nShe was among the hundreds of people who turned out for the statue's inauguration in a seaside park. The \u200bcrowd cheered and a youth choir sang as an enormous white draping was pulled off the sculpture, revealing a precise likeness of Pope \u200cLeo that \u2060even features a small mole above his upper lip.\n\nWorkers last week transported the enormous statue, made of steel, fiberglass and resin, across the capital in sections aboard trailers before cranes hoisted its body and outstretched arms into place overlooking the city."
