    "chunk_text": "Workers last week transported the enormous statue, made of steel, fiberglass and resin, across the capital in sections aboard trailers before cranes hoisted its body and outstretched arms into place overlooking the city.\n\nFor Callao, Peru's main port city and an area hit by a recent surge in violent crime, \u200bWong said he hoped the statue would transmit a message of \"peace that should prevail \u200bhere among everyone \u2060who lives in the district.\"\n\nLeo's return to Peru has generated intense excitement in a country preparing for what officials and businesses hope will be a tourism bonanza.\n\nMillions of people are expected to turn out for Leo's largest Masses in Lima and Chiclayo, \u2060while merchants \u200bin the capital are selling pope-themed shirts and souvenirs. Another statue of \u200bthe pontiff also already stands in Chiclayo, the northern city where Leo remains affectionately remembered from his years as bishop.\n\nLeo is due to arrive at \u200ban air base in Callao on Wednesday before meeting President Keiko Fujimori."
