    "chunk_size_bytes": 1048,
    "chunk_text": "Nuwara Eliya records lowest 12.5\u00b0C, Mannar highest 24.9\u00b0C\n\nColombo, Nov. 10 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Nuwara Eliya recorded the lowest minimum temperature in the country at 12.5\u00b0C today (10), the\u00a0 Meteorology Department said.\n\nThe temperature recorded in Nuwara Eliya was the lowest among the weather stations monitored by the Department.\n\nMeanwhile, Bandarawela recorded a minimum temperature of 17.2\u00b0C, while Badulla recorded 19.2\u00b0C. Katugastota recorded 21.7\u00b0C and Monaragala 22.7\u00b0C.\n\nSeveral other areas recorded minimum temperatures between 23\u00b0C and 25\u00b0C.\n\nThe readings included 24.2\u00b0C in Jaffna, 24.5\u00b0C in Mullaitivu, 24.9\u00b0C in Mannar, 24.1\u00b0C in Vavuniya, 24.4\u00b0C in Trincomalee, 24.5\u00b0C in Anuradhapura and Puttalam, and 24.2\u00b0C in Batticaloa.\n\nIn the Western Province, Colombo recorded 24.7\u00b0C, Katunayake 23.9\u00b0C and Rathmalana 24.5\u00b0C.\n\nGalle recorded 24.6\u00b0C, Hambantota 24.8\u00b0C and Matara (Matlla in the chart) 24.0\u00b0C.\n\nThe figures are based on minimum temperatures reported by the Department of Meteorology on November 10, 2026."
