    "chunk_text": "While in Vietnam, crew members reportedly bought food from local grocery stores because the company owed money to a vendor who refused to deliver food, according to CBS News, the BBC's partner in the US.\n\nHolly Hennessey, one of the ship's passengers, had earlier told the BBC guests were asked to consider paying a fuel surcharge as prices soared, and that their itinerary had been \"severely curtailed\".\n\nThe vessel sailed again into Singapore earlier this month, weeks after the cruise came to a sudden end while in Cambodia.\n\nAs the Iran war sent fuel prices soaring earlier this year, monthly fuel cost per cabin in parts of Asia had risen to as much as $8,000 from $1,800, Villa Vie Residences said in a statement on 27 October.\n\nIt added that it had taken \"significant steps to reduce fuel consumption\" but those measures turned out to be insufficient to offset the \"extraordinary increase in fuel costs\".\n\nThe company also said it was working with residents to \"identify temporary living arrangements\" while in Cambodia."
