    "chunk_size_bytes": 1958,
    "chunk_text": "Ladies\u2019 Circle Sri Lanka celebrates nine years of service\n\nCelebrating nearly a decade of dedicated community service and lasting friendships, Ladies\u2019 Circle Sri Lanka (LCSL) marked another successful year at its Annual General Meeting, held at Cloud Wine, Cinnamon Life.\n\nThe AGM brought together members from across the country to reflect on a year of outstanding achievements in service, leadership, fellowship, and international representation. Built on the international motto \u201cFriendship and Service,\u201d Ladies\u2019 Circle Sri Lanka continues to demonstrate that meaningful social change begins when passionate women come together with a shared purpose.\n\nChartered by Ladies\u2019 Circle Great Britain & Ireland in 2017, Ladies\u2019 Circle Sri Lanka has grown into a dynamic organisation of young women aged 18 to 45 committed to serving their communities while building lifelong friendships. As the sister organisation of Round Table Sri Lanka, the association believes that true leadership is demonstrated through service, collaboration, and the desire to leave every community better than it was found.\n\nAs the Sri Lankan affiliate of Ladies\u2019 Circle International (LCI), a global movement founded in 1932 with approximately 13,000 members across more than 40 countries, LCSL provides members with opportunities to exchange ideas, share best practices, and participate in international service initiatives while fostering friendships across borders.\n\nThroughout the past year, Ladies\u2019 Circle Sri Lanka carried out numerous service projects supporting education, healthcare, women\u2019s empowerment, and families in need. Members volunteered countless hours, raised funds for worthy causes, and worked alongside community partners to ensure that assistance reached those who needed it most. These projects are entirely member-driven, reflecting the passion and commitment of women who volunteer their time to create meaningful and sustainable change."
  },
