    "md5": "0676afb316868e7cd439ba16d1f7b30e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018FiNAC HROptimizer\u2019 leads as most effective remote workforce mgt. software\n\nAs fuel supply disruptions linked to the Middle East create uncertainty, remote work offers businesses a practical way to conserve fuel, reduce costs and maintain productivity\n\nFuel shortages and disruptions to global energy supplies can directly affect businesses and employees. For organisations that depend on daily commuting, limited fuel availability, rising transport costs and long journeys, can impact attendance, productivity and operating expenses.\n\nIn this environment, remote work is more than an employee benefit; it is a practical strategy for business continuity, fuel conservation and cost management, according to a leading IT company in Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cHowever, allowing employees to work from home is only part of the solution. Businesses must maintain visibility into workloads, ensure accountability and deliver customer assignments on time. This is where a secure and comprehensive workflow management software platform becomes very effective,\u201d Datamation Systems (Pvt.) Ltd Chairman and Managing Director Fazal Issadeen points out.\n\nDuring the Covid pandemic, Datamation Systems faced the challenge of managing a workforce with more than 70 percent of employees working remotely. Limited visibility into employee activities and difficulties in managing distributed teams contributed to a productivity decline of nearly 50 percent.\n\nThe company implemented its in-house developed \u2018FiNAC HROptimizer (FHRO)\u2019 workflow management software across remote and office-based employees, enabling flexible working while providing management with greater visibility into performance, task progress and accountability. \u201cThe experience demonstrated how the right systems can help organisations manage distributed teams effectively.\u201d"
