    "chunk_size_bytes": 1755,
    "chunk_text": "The company implemented its in-house developed \u2018FiNAC HROptimizer (FHRO)\u2019 workflow management software across remote and office-based employees, enabling flexible working while providing management with greater visibility into performance, task progress and accountability. \u201cThe experience demonstrated how the right systems can help organisations manage distributed teams effectively.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhen applied across an organisation, these savings can be substantial. Fewer daily commutes mean less fuel consumed, reduced pressure on transport availability and lower employee personal expenses.\u201d\n\nRemote work can also help organisations reduce office space requirements and expenses associated with rent, electricity, maintenance, parking and administration. Using FHRO, managers can monitor workloads, identify unproductive activities and improve workforce utilisation without requiring employees to be physically present in the office.\n\n\u201cWe witnessed employee productivity increase to more than 30 percent above pre-pandemic levels. Billable man-hours increased by 30 percent, net profitability improved by 10 percent, and the company achieved an annual return on investment equivalent to nine times its investment. FHRO by ensuring every employee contributes his fair share of work, creates a motivated team and reduces attrition,\u201d Issadeen explains.\n\nFHRO supports organisations across industries, particularly those with ten or more employees using desktops or laptops.\n\nBy combining remote work with measurable accountability, businesses can conserve fuel, reduce costs and maintain productivity - even during periods of energy supply uncertainty, the company says. \u2018FiNAC HROptimizer\u2019 is now effectively used by 350 employees worldwide."
