    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e71699d433ad40d884aa8916b84c567f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "CT Holdings reaffirms long-term confidence in the Group and Sri Lankan economy\n\nCT Holdings PLC and its key subsidiary, Cargills (Ceylon) PLC, recently reported a strong performance for the second quarter of FY2026/27, driven in large part by growth across the Group\u2019s key operating sectors of Retail, FMCG and Restaurants. Alongside this performance, the Group announced a series of senior executive appointments, effective from January 2027, as part of its long-term succession planning and continued commitment to developing leadership from within the organisation.\n\nCommenting on the results and appointments, Louis Page, Chairman of CT Holdings PLC and Cargills (Ceylon) PLC, said:\n\n\u201cCargills, which is a key subsidiary of CT Holdings, has always been built with a long-term perspective. Through different generations and different periods in our country\u2019s history, we have continued to invest, grow and evolve. That commitment has not changed.\u201d\n\nThe new appointments encompass leadership positions across Retail, Dairy and Food & Beverage, as well as Group Finance. They bring together a team of experienced executives who have grown within the Group and played important roles in developing and expanding its businesses over many years. Collectively, the strengthened leadership team brings deep institutional knowledge, extensive operating experience and a strong understanding of the values and culture that have shaped the Group for decades.\n\nReflecting on the appointments, Mr. Louis Page went on to say, \u201cThe appointments we are announcing are an important part of that journey. One of the greatest strengths of Cargills has been its people and our ability to develop leaders from within. These are individuals who have grown with the Group, understand our businesses and our values, and have demonstrated their ability to lead.\u201d"
  },
