    "md5": "c62a8c8db3e7e71224ccd485a51e268c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1694,
    "chunk_text": "Through the trust arrangements associated with Odeon Holdings, a significant part of the economic benefit derived from the Group is intended ultimately to support charitable causes in Sri Lanka. Elaborating on this commitment, Mr. Louis Page said, \u201cIt is intended that the ownership held through Odeon Holdings will, through trusts, increasingly serve a wider social purpose. I am committed to contributing 50% of the economic interests in the capital and profits of Odeon Holdings, derived through its investments in CT Holdings PLC, towards charitable initiatives in Sri Lanka, with particular emphasis on education, supporting and advancing women\u2019s causes, and the development of art and theatre.\u201d\n\nSpeaking of his longer-term vision for the Group, he added, \u201cWe want Cargills to remain a strong and growing Sri Lankan institution. We want it to be led by capable professional managers who are empowered to take the business forward. We want its ownership to remain stable and committed for the long term. And we want a meaningful part of the wealth generated through that ownership ultimately to serve the country and communities that have supported Cargills over generations.\u201d\n\nTaken together, these developments reflect a clear long-term direction for CT Holdings and Cargills: stable and committed ownership, increasingly strong professional management, continued investment and growth, and a wider social purpose. \u201cStable, committed ownership and professional management are not alternatives. Together, they provide the foundation for CT Holdings and Cargills to continue growing, creating opportunity and contributing to Sri Lanka for generations to come,\u201d Mr. Page said."
