    "md5": "8aa054d8435416abb89308c75d709082",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "HNB Life delivers highest industry performance with 41% GWP growth\n\nHNB Life PLC continued its strong growth trajectory during the nine months ended September 30, 2026, while maintaining a disciplined approach to profitability, investment management and long-term value creation.\n\nThe company recorded a gross written premium (GWP) of Rs.19.4 billion, representing a strong 41 percent year-on-year growth, compared with Rs.13.8 billion during the corresponding period of 2025. The net written premium increased by 42 percent to Rs.18.5 billion, reflecting the continued strong momentum of the life insurance business.\n\nReflecting this strong premium growth, HNB Life\u2019s net income increased by 31 percent to Rs.24.9 billion, compared with Rs.19.0 billion in the corresponding period of 2025. The interest and dividend income also increased by approximately 14 percent to Rs.6.2 billion, contributing positively to the company\u2019s overall financial performance.\n\nHNB Life recorded profit before tax of Rs.862.6 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, while profit after tax stood at Rs.602.3 million, without any surplus transfer from the Life Insurance Fund, which usually happens after the actuarial valuation at the end of the year.\n\nHNB Life continued to strengthen its investment base during the period, with financial investments increasing to Rs.70.2 billion as of September 30, 2026, representing a growth of approximately 12 percent from Rs.62.5 billion at end-2025. The company\u2019s overall financial position continued to expand alongside business growth, with total assets reaching Rs.77.1 billion as of September 30, 2026, an increase of approximately 13 percent from Rs.68.4 billion at end-2025.\n\nSignificantly, the Life Insurance Fund expanded by 22 percent to Rs.59.8 billion, from Rs.48.9 billion as of e31 December 2025, further strengthening the company\u2019s long-term financial position."
  },
