    "md5": "2917ed522a73f49cfc3a519e5da05d5f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1765,
    "chunk_text": "Nawaloka Hospital Negombo opens Sreeni Dharmadasa Heart Care Centre\n\nNawaloka Medicare Hospital Chairman Harshith Dharmadasa cutting the ribbon to inaugurate the new facility\n\nNawaloka Hospital Negombo has marked a significant milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s private healthcare sector with the opening of the Sreeni Dharmadasa Heart Care Centre, a purpose-designed facility dedicated to delivering advanced cardiac care.\n\nThe centre features a Guided Therapy Platform, complemented by advanced cardiovascular and interventional technologies designed to enhance clinical precision, safety and efficiency while delivering patient-centred care.\n\nThe opening ceremony was attended by Prof. Chrishantha Abeysena - Minister of Science & Technology and W.E. Dulip Chamara Fernando - Mayor of the Negombo Municipal Council, as Chief Guests.\n\nSpeaking at the opening ceremony, Harshith Dharmadasa said, \u2018\u2019This investment brings modern imaging technology closer to our communities while keeping specialist expertise and patient safety at the centre of care. As Sri Lanka moves towards greater use of AI and digital healthcare, innovation must translate into timely treatment, better value and a smaller gap in access to quality services.\u201d\n\nAt the heart of the new facility is the Philips Azurion 7 C20 diagnostic and image-guided therapy system, an advanced medical imaging\u00a0 platform that integrates imaging technology, clinical software and streamlined workflow capabilities to support specialists during diagnostic assessments and image-guided interventions.\n\nThe system enables medical professionals to perform image-guided procedures with enhanced visual information, supporting precise clinical assessment and minimally invasive treatment approaches where appropriate."
