    "chunk_text": "INSEE forum unites stakeholders to advance SL\u2019s construction sector\n\nEng. Thusith Gunawarnasuriya addresses the forum, while\u00a0 Sitthichai Siriuvithtaya looks on\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s construction and infrastructure sectors enter a new phase of transformation, INSEE, a leading construction solutions provider in Sri Lanka, hosted INSEE Industry Connect 2026, bringing together key stakeholders from across the country\u2019s construction ecosystem.\n\nWith renewed economic activity and infrastructure development creating new opportunities, the construction industry faces a growing need to build smarter, more efficiently and more sustainably. Advances in technology, changing customer expectations and a growing focus on environmental responsibility are also strengthening the need for greater industry collaboration. Held under the theme \u2018Innovate. Integrate. Impact\u2019, INSEE Industry Connect 2026 served as a thought-leadership and collaboration platform, bringing together industrial customers, contractors, ready-mix concrete customers, architects, consultants, technology providers, government engineers, institutional project managers, policymakers and academics.\n\nThe forum reinforced INSEE\u2019s commitment to \u201cBuilding Sri Lanka\u2019s Future\u201d, encouraging stronger collaboration across the construction ecosystem to build sustainable and resilient infrastructure while creating lasting value for future generations."
