    "md5": "1fe1f7f0f2ca997c9312e3e8333c74dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1881,
    "chunk_text": "Ceylon Chamber facilitates new trade opportunities through Yunnan biz delegation\n\nThe Ceylon Chamber of Commerce and the Chamber\u2019s Sri Lanka\u2013China Business Council (SLCHBC) hosted a business delegation from China\u2019s Yunnan Province on 28 October, opening discussions on trade, investment and commercial partnerships across a range of industries.\n\nThe delegation, led by the Yunnan Provincial Federation of Industry and Commerce, comprised representatives from leading companies in pharmaceuticals and healthcare, agriculture, dairy, industrial machinery, construction materials, IT, steel, tea, food manufacturing, hospitality and logistics. The meeting provided Sri Lankan businesses with an opportunity to engage directly with the visiting companies and explore areas of mutual interest.\n\nWelcoming the delegation, Shiran Fernando, Secretary General and CEO of the Ceylon Chamber, noted that the visit came at a timely stage as Sri Lanka\u2019s economy moves beyond stabilization and focuses on growth, with opportunities emerging for businesses to expand trade and attract investment. Direct engagement between companies, he observed, can help identify areas where commercial interests align and lead to new business relationships.\n\nAddressing the gathering, the President of the Sri Lanka\u2013China Business Council noted that there is considerable scope to expand Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to China and diversify the range of products entering the market. He observed that Sri Lanka\u2019s export basket remains concentrated in a relatively small number of products, and that engagements such as this delegation visit can help local businesses identify new buyers, explore market opportunities and develop commercial relationships.\n\nHe also pointed to areas of potential cooperation across agriculture, food processing, healthcare, manufacturing, technology, engineering and tourism."
  },
