    "chunk_text": "October inflows lift Sri Lanka\u2019s remittances to US $ 7.6bn\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s worker remittances rose 3.3 percent year-on-year to US $ 735.6 million in October, taking the inflows for the first 10 months of 2026 to US $ 7.60 billion, the Central Bank data showed.\n\nThe October receipts were up from US $ 712 million a year earlier and edged higher from US $ 734.4 million in September, according to the Central Bank\u2019s Weekly Economic Indicators.\n\nThe remittances rose 16.5 percent in January-October, from US $ 6.52 billion in the same period last year, bringing in about US $ 1.08 billion more. In rupee terms, the inflows increased 25.8 percent to Rs.2.46 trillion over the 10 months.\n\nThe inflows are a key source of foreign exchange for Sri Lanka. The Central Bank was a net buyer of US $ 191 million in the domestic foreign exchange market in October, while the gross official reserves stood at a provisional US $ 7.09 billion at the end of the month, including the proceeds from the People\u2019s Bank of China swap.\n\nThe rupee had depreciated 6.7 percent against the US dollar since the start of the year as of November 6."
