    "chunk_size_bytes": 1762,
    "chunk_text": "CIC quarterly profit rises 20% as tax charge falls\n\nCIC Holdings PLC\u2019s quarterly profit attributable to the shareholders rose 20.3 percent, as a lower tax bill lifted the earnings, even as the higher costs squeezed the margins and the operating profit declined.\n\nThe attributable profit rose to Rs.1.66 billion in the three months ended September 30, from Rs.1.38 billion a year earlier, according to the group\u2019s unaudited interim results.\n\nThe earnings per share increased to 87 cents, from 73 cents. The group profit, including the non-controlling interests, rose 14.1 percent to Rs.1.98 billion. Revenue increased 3.4 percent to Rs.20.89 billion but the cost of sales rose 5.2 percent. That pushed the gross profit down 1.2 percent to Rs.5.68 billion and narrowed the gross margin to 27.2 percent, from 28.5 percent.\n\nThe higher selling and administrative expenses also weighed on the operating profit, which fell 7.3 percent to Rs.2.66 billion.\n\nThe net finance costs climbed 35.4 percent to Rs.712.3 million. A more than twofold increase in CIC\u2019s share of profit from the equity-accounted investees, to Rs.590.5 million, helped offset the higher finance costs and weaker operating result.\n\nThe pretax profit was broadly flat at Rs.2.59 billion, while the income tax charge fell 29.4 percent to Rs.606.2 million.\n\nFor the six months ended September 30, the attributable profit rose 21.7 percent to Rs.3.17 billion on revenue of Rs.42.91 billion, up 3.1 percent.\n\nThe agri solutions, the group\u2019s largest segment by revenue, recorded a 12.4 percent decline in sales and a 27.2 percent drop in segment profit. The segment profit rose 47.4 percent in industrial solutions, 30.9 percent in livestock solutions and 10.0 percent in health and personal care."
