    "md5": "08cd11f22852c7afd815ff100b157617",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1740,
    "chunk_text": "HNB and IFC partner to advance supply chain finance and strengthen risk management\n\nHNB Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Damith Pallewatte and IFC Regional Vice President for Asia and the Pacific Sarvesh Suri\n\nHatton National Bank PLC (HNB) announced yesterday a strategic partnership with the International Finance Corporation (IFC), a member of the World Bank Group focused on the private sector, to expand supply chain finance for Sri Lankan businesses and enhance HNB\u2019s risk management and responsible finance frameworks.\n\nThe partnership combines HNB\u2019s relationships with corporates and small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) across Sri Lanka with IFC\u2019s global expertise in supply chain finance and financial-sector advisory.\n\nIFC will help HNB develop scalable supply chain finance solutions, connecting its corporate clients with suppliers and distributors.\n\nThe initiative aims to ease the working capital constraints for the SMEs in these value chains, strengthen competitiveness and build more resilient, inclusive businesses, with a focus on expanding financing for women-owned businesses.\n\nIFC will also review HNB\u2019s responsible finance and risk management practices against the international benchmarks and recommend improvements to its frameworks, analytics, governance and processes.\n\nHNB Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Damith Pallewatte said, \u201cThis partnership with IFC represents an important step in HNB\u2019s strategy to build a more connected, inclusive and resilient financing ecosystem. Sri Lankan businesses require financial solutions that respond not only to their individual balance sheets but also to the commercial relationships and value chains through which they operate."
  },
