    "md5": "ced03e80dceb3a334d66f4813f421a88",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1276,
    "chunk_text": "Commercial Bank tops Fitch\u2019s local ratings for Sri Lankan private banks\n\nFitch Ratings upgraded Commercial Bank of Ceylon PLC\u2019s national long-term rating by one notch to AA(lka), from AA-(lka), effective October 30, after revising its Sri Lankan rating scale following the September sovereign upgrade.\n\nThe move makes Commercial Bank the highest-rated private-sector bank in Sri Lanka on Fitch\u2019s national scale, the lender said in a statement.\n\nNational ratings compare the creditworthiness among the issuers within Sri Lanka.\n\nThe sovereign upgrade prompted Fitch to recalibrate its local scale, giving the agency room to distinguish Commercial Bank\u2019s credit profile more clearly from those of other large private lenders, according to the statement.\n\nFitch pointed to Commercial Bank\u2019s position as Sri Lanka\u2019s largest private-sector bank and its ability to raise funds at a lower cost than other large private lenders. It also cited the bank\u2019s ability to generate business as a factor supporting its credit profile.\n\nThe bank\u2019s asset quality, profitability and capital coverage of impaired loans after provisions have generally been among the stronger levels recorded by the Sri Lankan banks rated by Fitch, the lender said, citing the agency\u2019s assessment."
  },
