    "md5": "a4f82182b08c847dfc48d3643a9e5274",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1682,
    "chunk_text": "Former Prime Minister Naftali Bennett \u2013 leader of the Together alliance (seen as a key contender to oust Netanyahu) has threatened to cut subsidies to the Haredi community if they continue to defy the draft. Gadi Eisenkot, leader of the centrist Yashar party (another top contender to replace Netanyahu) has proposed allowing only 3% of Haredi men exemption from the draft, and that too, only to enable them to study. Seven in 10 Jewish Israelis favour drafting the Haredim.\n\nWhen the Haredi parties exited Netanyahu\u2019s coalition, Likud replaced them with Jewish nationalist parties that emphasised the State. Particularly notable was the decision to include the Jewish Power party, an offshoot of an earlier group banned for racism.\n\nThe Arab parties, the \u201cJoint List\u201d and \u201cRa\u2019am\u201d, also hold the key to government formation in Israel. Israel has 2.1 million Arabs (20% of the population). The Arabs voted massively in the recent elections and got 19 out of 120 seats. \u201cThey\u2019re the kingmakers,\u201d said\u00a0 journalist Christiane Amanpour on X.\n\nBut the more important question is whether those who want to form a government are willing to invite the Arab parties to join them.\n\nAt one extreme, there are voices like that of Yair Netanyahu, the son of the Prime Minister Netanyahu who said on X: \u201cThese elections proved that the greatest danger to the survival of the State of Israel, aside from the Iranian nuclear programme, is what is called Israeli Arabs. A country cannot survive long-term when 20% of its population identifies with its enemies and wants its destruction. Muslims cannot, and can never, live peacefully with \u201cinfidels\u201d as their neighbours.\u201d"
