    "chunk_size_bytes": 1200,
    "chunk_text": "At one extreme, there are voices like that of Yair Netanyahu, the son of the Prime Minister Netanyahu who said on X: \u201cThese elections proved that the greatest danger to the survival of the State of Israel, aside from the Iranian nuclear programme, is what is called Israeli Arabs. A country cannot survive long-term when 20% of its population identifies with its enemies and wants its destruction. Muslims cannot, and can never, live peacefully with \u201cinfidels\u201d as their neighbours.\u201d\n\nGiven the fractured nature of Israeli Jewish politics, Arab participation in the country\u2019s democracy would become critical for the stability and survival of governments, and for treaties and productive changes in the entire West Asian region.\n\nAs senior journalist Dan Perry wrote in an opinion piece for \u201cThe Jerusalem Post,\u201d Israeli parties should \u201cstop overthinking, thank the Arabs for their support, and get on with saving the country.\u201d\n\nWhile some observers have spoken of repeating the election to enable a Jewish grouping to emerge with a clear majority, President Herzog has ruled out a fresh poll. Thus, both the Netanyahu and the Eisenkot blocs have to find ways of forming a government."
