    "md5": "75ceed0d4fcf910103fef8f4a007521a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1659,
    "chunk_text": "Chennai hosts Port City\u2019s first Indian investor forum\n\nColombo, Nov. 10 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Over 200 business leaders, investors, policymakers and industry representatives from India and Sri Lanka gathered at the Colombo Port City Investor Forum \u2013 Chennai 2026 in Chennai, organised by the Deputy High Commission of Sri Lanka in Chennai in collaboration with Port City Colombo.\n\nMarking Port City Colombo\u2019s first investor forum in India, the event provided a platform to explore investment opportunities and strengthen cross-border business partnerships in real estate, financial services, logistics, IT and technology.\n\nThe programme commenced with an address by\u00a0 \u00a0Deputy High Commissioner\u00a0 \u00a0for Southern India, Dr. Ganesanathan Geathiswaran, who highlighted the longstanding economic and cultural ties between the two countries and the potential to further strengthen bilateral trade, investment and business cooperation.\n\nDelivering the keynote address, the Chairman of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission, Harsha Amarasekera, PC, highlighted Port City Colombo\u2019s investor-friendly statutory framework, regulatory certainty and safeguards, positioning Sri Lanka as a strategic partner for Indian businesses seeking regional expansion.\n\nThe Deputy Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd, Thulci Aluwihare, presented the investment opportunities offered by Port City Colombo, highlighting its status as Sri Lanka\u2019s only foreign currency-designated Special Economic Zone, with facilities including a single-window approval mechanism, 100% foreign ownership and transactions in 16 foreign currencies, including the Indian rupee."
  },
