    "md5": "7bb4cce75057a445a92f4c7c49131a0a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1780,
    "chunk_text": "Turkey steel factory blast kills at least 17 people\n\nBBC - At least 17 people have died and 12 others have been injured in an explosion at an iron and steel factory near the port city of Izmir in western Turkey.\n\nAll those killed and injured were workers at the Habas Demir Celik plant in Aliaga, one of the country's leading steel producers, authorities said. Footage from the scene showed a large fire inside the facility and a towering column of smoke rising into the air.\n\nThe local governor said the blast happened around midday after a crane carrying a replacement boiler collapsed, causing materials to fall into a furnace below.\n\nWorkplace accidents remain a chronic problem in Turkey, the Turkish Health and Safety Labor Watch, an independent civil society organisation, said.\n\nPresident Recep Tayyip Erdo\u011fan originally said the death toll was 16, but the Health Minister, Kemal Memi\u015fo\u011flu, later announced that one of those who had been critically injured had later died, taking the toll to 17.\n\nEyewitnesses at the scene said the explosion shook the ground, with one person initially believing an earthquake had struck.\n\nIn a statement, the company that runs the factory said the accident occurred during scheduled maintenance work on one of the plant's electric arc furnaces.\n\nIzmir Governor S\u00fcleyman Elban told media that some people were believed to still be under the rubble.\n\nSpeaking after a cabinet meeting on Monday, Erdo\u011fan confirmed the deaths and said investigations were under way, while search and rescue operations continued.\n\nAt least five people have been arrested, according BBC News's Turkish service, citing local media reports.\n\nThe Habas plant is in the Izmir district of Aliaga which is a major port and one of Turkey's main shipbreaking hubs."
