    "md5": "3a94270a84582bc3f595aab02ac755c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1857,
    "chunk_text": "Public officers to receive training in Azerbaijan under new MoU\n\nNov. 10 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Public officers are to receive training programmes and internship opportunities in Azerbaijan under a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signed between Sri Lanka's Ministry of Public Administration and Azerbaijan's ASAN Service.\n\nThe agreement was signed on November 7 by Minister of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government Prof. Chandana Abayarathna, on behalf of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe MoU aims to modernise public administration and improve the efficiency of public service delivery in Sri Lanka, with particular emphasis on developing the skills of public officers involved in service delivery.\n\nUnder the agreement, Sri Lankan trainers in relevant fields will receive training in Azerbaijan. They will subsequently develop and conduct training programmes in Sri Lanka, sharing the knowledge and expertise gained.\n\nThe agreement is expected to contribute to significant improvements in Sri Lanka's public administration and public service delivery over the next three years.\n\nIt was signed on the sidelines of the United Nations Governance Innovation Summit, held on November 5 and 6 at Gulustan Palace in Baku, Azerbaijan, under the theme \"Advancing Future-Ready Institutions\".\n\nAddressing a panel discussion during the summit's second session, Minister Abayarathna stressed the importance of public service reforms, digitalisation and strengthening public trust.\n\nHe also highlighted the need to ensure that public services are accessible, simple and efficient for all sections of society, particularly rural communities and vulnerable groups.\n\nThe summit was jointly organised by the United Nations Department of Economic and Social Affairs (UN DESA) and Azerbaijan's State Agency for Public Service and Social Innovations under the President."
