    "chunk_text": "He also highlighted the potential impact on employees and their families, pointing out that the loss of employment could affect their children\u2019s education, housing commitments and responsibilities towards elderly parents.\n\nMoreover, Karunanayake, who has also served as Minister of Foreign Affairs and Minister of Finance, said he was prepared to work with the Government, relevant authorities and industry partners to help address challenges and ensure that HSBC could continue its operations in Sri Lanka.\n\nHe stressed that retaining the investment was a national responsibility that went beyond political differences.\n\nEmphasising the importance of employment opportunities for the younger generation, he said HSBC had provided young Sri Lankans with valuable exposure to international business practices, professional development and opportunities to work across cultures.\n\nHe urged HSBC\u2019s global leadership to reopen the decision and hold an urgent, time-bound discussion on possible changes to costs, recruitment, training, infrastructure and policy that could help retain its Sri Lankan operations.\n\nAs such, Karunanayake said a renewed commitment by HSBC would not only protect jobs but also send a positive message about Sri Lanka\u2019s efforts to rebuild its economy and attract investment."
