    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ca52e0240314f7dfe07b46029ef6fb6d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1986,
    "chunk_text": "Russia and Ukraine hold first peace talks for nine months, Trump envoy says gaps have narrowed\n\nReuters\u00a0- Russian and Ukrainian officials met in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday for their first US-brokered talks since February, after President \u200bDonald Trump suggested last week that a broad deal was possible on ending the war in Ukraine and guaranteeing security in Europe.\n\nUS envoy Jared Kushner \u200ctold delegates that recent contacts with both sides had \"really identified, narrowed the gaps\", and that Trump was committed to achieving peace.\n\n\"He really has asked us to put extra effort into trying to find a solution that hopefully ends the war but also leaves both sides in a much stronger position to start pursuing the full potential of what their two amazing countries have the ability to reach,\" Kushner said at the \u200bstart of the meeting.\n\nBut more than 4-1/2 years after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine, and with Russian forces holding about a fifth of the country, Moscow \u200band Kyiv remain far apart - despite Trump's optimism - on terms for a possible settlement.\n\nUkraine's chief delegate, Rustem Umerov, said in his opening \u2060remarks that Kyiv was focused on achieving security guarantees and a lasting peace.\n\nRussian delegation chief Vladimir Medinsky said Moscow hoped for progress towards peace in the interest of the \u200bpeoples of both countries.\n\nThe new American drive for a deal has galvanised European officials into pushing for a place at the table to \u200bseek an end to the continent's deadliest conflict since World War Two.\n\nBefore the start of the main meeting, the Ukrainians met separately with European, NATO and EU representatives and the two American envoys, Kushner and Steve Witkoff.\n\nFrance said there could be no lasting peace in Ukraine without addressing European security, and that this required the involvement of the Europeans.\n\nRussia had made clear it did not see a place for Europeans \u200bat the meeting with the Ukrainians and Americans."
  },
