    "chunk_text": "France said there could be no lasting peace in Ukraine without addressing European security, and that this required the involvement of the Europeans.\n\nRussia had made clear it did not see a place for Europeans \u200bat the meeting with the Ukrainians and Americans.\n\nTrump has frequently said an agreement was \u200cclose, without a \u2060deal emerging. However, negotiations have picked up again in recent weeks after months in which Washington's attention was focused on the war in Iran.\n\nPublicly, there has been no sign that Putin is willing to drop his insistence that Ukraine surrender the entire eastern region of Donbas before a peace deal can be struck.\n\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy has refused to hand over land that his forces have died defending.\n\nRussian front-line advances have slowed to a virtual halt this year but Moscow has been pounding Ukrainian cities and energy facilities, while Ukraine \u200bhas stepped up attacks on oil refineries \u200band other infrastructure deep inside Russia.\n\nA source \u2060in the Russian delegation said Russia believed the main thrust of the talks would be trying to hammer out the key elements of a new post-war security framework for Europe.\n\nOn the eve of the negotiations, Zelenskiy said Ukraine's leverage in the talks was increasing as \u200ba result of its recent battlefield performance, which has included retaking some territory in Donetsk, a coal-mining area of the Donbas.\n\n\"Ukrainian \u200bforces are currently genuinely \u2060strengthening Ukraine's negotiating position,\" Zelenskiy said in his nightly video address on Monday. He said Russia was suffering \"record losses\" \u2014 an assertion disputed by Moscow \u2014 and urged Washington to convince the Kremlin to end the war.\n\nUS negotiators believe that Zelenskiy and Putin may be willing to strike a compromise on the vital question of territory, each ceding a little, a US official told Reuters.\n\nUnder \u2060the proposed \u200bdeal, Ukraine would get an end to the war, security guarantees and a roadmap to accession to the \u200bEU."
