    "chunk_text": "Government aims to make SriLankan Airlines profitable\n\nColombo, Nov. 10 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Government is determined to turn SriLankan Airlines into a profitable national carrier, despite the airline continuing to face mounting financial losses, Cabinet Spokesperson Minister Nalinda Jayatissa said.\n\nHe said some progress had already been made towards improving the airline\u2019s financial position, adding that the Government hoped to make it financially sustainable as tourist arrivals to the country continued to increase.\n\nJayatissa said the Government was committed to bringing the airline to a position where it could operate without incurring losses. The financial allocation required for the initiative is expected to be outlined in the 2027 Budget, he added."
