    "chunk_text": "The Court also issued a series of directions in paragraph 897, requiring further investigations into offences arising from the disaster and consideration of criminal proceedings against all offenders.\n\nThe Criminal Investigation Department was also directed to conduct further investigations into matters identified by the Attorney General, ensuring that such investigations were completed within three months. The Attorney General was required to report to the Supreme Court every three months on the investigative and prosecutorial action taken to implement the judgment.\n\nThe Court further directed the Attorney General to undertake a review of existing maritime and environmental legislation, in consultation with relevant authorities and independent experts, and advise the Government on necessary legislative reforms to bring domestic laws in line with international standards.\n\nMeanwhile, the CEJ stated that it had submitted a Bill of Costs to the Attorney General on January 16, 2026, seeking reimbursement of expenses incurred in pursuing the fundamental rights litigation. However, it claimed that it had received neither a response nor reimbursement.\n\nThe CEJ has requested the Attorney General to respond within 14 days, identifying the steps taken to implement the judgment and explaining any outstanding matters or delays."
