    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s Rumesh Tharanga among world\u2019s top 10 athletes\n\nColombo, Oct. 10 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lankan javelin thrower Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage has secured eighth place in the 2026 Men\u2019s World Athlete of the Year rankings.\n\nPathirage was among 10 athletes nominated for the prestigious World Athletics award following an impressive season on the international stage.\n\nHe enjoyed a remarkable 2026 campaign, claiming gold medals at the Asian Games and Commonwealth Games, while also winning the Diamond League title and the World Athletics Ultimate Championship.\n\nPathirage also set a new Sri Lankan national record with a throw of 92.62 metres at the Diamond League meeting in Rome, becoming the second-best Asian javelin thrower in history."
