    "md5": "783ce675d70ed99d2f80395e914b4c7d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1578,
    "chunk_text": "Japan grants Rs. 2 b to boost Sri Lanka Navy capabilities\n\nThe Treasury yesterday said the Government of Japan has agreed to provide grant assistance amounting to \u00a5 1 billion (approximately Rs. 2.08 billion) under its Official Security Assistance (OSA) Program 2026 to further strengthen the defence and maritime surveillance capabilities of the Sri Lanka Navy.\n\nThe Exchange of Notes pertaining to this grant assistance was signed on 10 November 2026 by Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, and Ambassador of Japan Akio Isomata on behalf of the Government of Japan.\n\nUnder this project, 25 Rigid Hull Inflatable Boats (RHIBs) will be provided to the Sri Lanka Navy. These vessels are expected to be deployed across the Northern, Eastern, North Western, Western and Southern Naval Commands to support coastal surveillance operations and law enforcement.\n\nAgainst the backdrop of evolving regional security challenges, increasing maritime activities in the Indian Ocean, and emerging threats associated with illegal activities at sea, the need to further strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s maritime surveillance and security capabilities has become increasingly important. The assistance is expected to enhance the operational capabilities of the Sri Lanka Navy, improve its readiness to respond to both traditional and non-traditional security challenges, and contribute to the promotion of regional peace, stability and security. In addition, the project is expected to support humanitarian assistance and disaster response operations."
