    "chunk_size_bytes": 1554,
    "chunk_text": "Veteran banker Bhanu Wijayaratne becomes OPA President-Elect for 2026/27\n\nBhanu Wijayaratne, a distinguished banking and financial services professional with over four decades of experience, was elected President-Elect of the Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA) for the 2026- 2027 term at the 51st Annual General Meeting, held on 30 October 2026.\n\nFollowing his tenure as President-Elect, he will assume the Presidency of the OPA for the 2027-2028 term.\n\nHis election marks a significant milestone in a professional career in banking and finance, serving in senior executive leadership, institutional governance, professional service and a sustained commitment to the advancement of the country\u2019s professional community.\n\nAn alumnus of the Royal College, Wijayaratne possesses an impressive portfolio of academic qualifications and professional credentials. He holds a Master\u2019s Degree in Financial Economics from the University of Colombo and a Master of Business Administration (MBA) from the University of Manipal. He is a Senior Fellow of the Institute of Bankers of Sri Lanka (FIBs -SL) and a Fellow of the Institute of Chartered Professional Managers (FCPM). He also holds\u00a0 \u00a0membership of the Institute of Internal Auditors, USA (Sri Lankan Chapter). Beyond his distinguished career in banking and financial services, Wijayaratne possesses a strong grounding in economics and maintains professional memberships in both the Sri Lanka Economic Association and Institute of Quality and Productivity Management- Sri Lanka."
