    "chunk_text": "His commitment to professional service extends well beyond his corporate responsibilities. He has served the Association of Professional Bankers of Sri Lanka in several important leadership capacities, including Treasurer, Vice President and Senior Vice President, and currently serves on its Council of Advisors. He has also served as General Secretary and Chairman of the Association of Compliance Officers of Banks - Sri Lanka.\n\nThrough the National Issues Committee, he has supported professional deliberations, seminars and initiatives addressing critical national concerns, including economic challenges, energy and supply-chain resilience, governance, anti-money laundering and countering\u00a0 \u00a0financing of terrorism (AML/CFT), public-sector effectiveness and environmental sustainability. His approach has consistently emphasised the importance of moving beyond discussion towards evidence-based recommendations, constructive engagement and practical outcomes.\n\nHe has also been actively involved in strengthening OPA\u2019s engagement with Government institutions, exploring opportunities to mobilise the specialised knowledge and capabilities of its Member Associations in addressing national priorities. His vision recognises the considerable potential of OPA to serve as a credible professional resource to policymakers and public institutions.\n\nIn addition, Wijayaratne served as the Convener of the 39th OPA Annual Conference and Chairman of its Technical Sessions Committee, held under the theme \u201cEnvisioning Sri Lanka: Beyond Recovery.\u201d The conference brought together distinguished personalities and professionals from diverse disciplines to deliberate on the challenges, opportunities and strategic imperatives shaping Sri Lanka\u2019s future."
  },
