    "chunk_size_bytes": 1791,
    "chunk_text": "In addition, Wijayaratne served as the Convener of the 39th OPA Annual Conference and Chairman of its Technical Sessions Committee, held under the theme \u201cEnvisioning Sri Lanka: Beyond Recovery.\u201d The conference brought together distinguished personalities and professionals from diverse disciplines to deliberate on the challenges, opportunities and strategic imperatives shaping Sri Lanka\u2019s future.\n\nIn presenting his vision for the Organisation ahead of his election as President-Elect, Wijayaratne advanced the theme, \u201cStrengthening OPA: Uniting Professional Excellence for National Progress\u201d, setting out a forward-looking agenda centred on institutional unity, the consolidation of professional excellence and a renewed commitment to national progress.\n\nAt the heart of this vision, lies the conviction that OPA\u2019s greatest institutional strength is derived from the collective knowledge, professional expertise and intellectual capabilities of its 52 Member Associations from 32 diverse professions. He believes that the Organisation\u2019s future influence will depend on its ability to unite these diverse professional constituencies and channel their collective strengths towards a common national purpose.-His proposed priorities encompass five key areas: strengthening unity and inclusiveness among Member Associations; translating professional expertise into tangible national impact; building strategic partnerships; enhancing OPA\u2019s visibility and influence; and strengthening institutional effectiveness and continuity.\n\nWijayaratne\u2019s vision seeks to build upon this institutional strength, fostering a more united, engaged and influential professional community while reinforcing OPA\u2019s contribution to the economic, social and institutional progress of Sri Lanka."
