    "chunk_text": "Dr. Jayatissa said the Government has also identified the need to address capacity constraints caused by the existing single-track railway infrastructure, while improving the reliability and connectivity of train services.\n\n\u201cThe restoration will carry on without interruption. Building the new bridge is happening alongside it,\u201d he added.\n\nThe Cabinet Spokesman noted that the Black Bridge, a single-track structure first built in 1865, was badly damaged in the cyclone. Given its age and structural limitations, the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB) is handling the repairs, with technical support from the University of Peradeniya.\n\nThe proposal to this effect was submitted by Transport, Highways and Urban Development Minister Bimal Rathnayake."
