    "md5": "886edbe90e856338d349d5a25a964856",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "Neil Marine Sports and Leisure launches Hidea outboard motors in Sri Lanka\n\nNeil Marine Sports and Leisure Ltd., a member of the Neil Marine Group of companies has launched Hidea Outboard Motors in Sri Lanka, bringing a range of 2.5HP to 200HP two- stroke and four-stroke petrol, kerosene and electric engines to the local market under an exclusive agency agreement.\n\nThe product was launched at the Granbell Hotel, Colombo, on 26 October, and the new product range targets fishermen, leisure boaters, commercial operators and marine professionals, offering a selection of engines designed to provide reliable performance, fuel efficiency and affordable operation.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Neil Marine Group CEO Shan Perera said the partnership marked a new chapter for the company, which has been building boats in Sri Lanka for more than five decades.\n\n\u201cSince 1969, Neil Fernando and Company Ltd. has been building boats in Sri Lanka. Over more than five decades, we have delivered over 40,000 vessels to customers around the world. Everything we have achieved is based on three qualities - craftsmanship, trust and the dedication of our people,\u201d he said.\n\nHe noted that the partnership would enable the company to offer a complete marine solution to the customers by combining its boat-building expertise with Hidea\u2019s engine technology. \u201cA boat is only as good as the engine that drives it. For years, we have built the hull. Now, with Hidea, we can offer the power as well as a complete marine solution under one trusted brand name,\u201d Perera said.\n\nHe emphasised that the company\u2019s objective was to introduce economical and dependable engines to the fisheries and tourism sectors, which are the two lifelines of the Sri Lankan economy.\n\nHighlighting the challenges faced by fishermen, he said fuel costs and engine breakdowns directly affected their family incomes and livelihoods."
