    "chunk_text": "He emphasised that the company\u2019s objective was to introduce economical and dependable engines to the fisheries and tourism sectors, which are the two lifelines of the Sri Lankan economy.\n\nHighlighting the challenges faced by fishermen, he said fuel costs and engine breakdowns directly affected their family incomes and livelihoods.\n\nPerera also identified marine tourism as a growing market for the new engines, particularly for whale watching, island transfers, fishing charters and leisure boating.\n\nHe said tourism operators needed dependable and cost-effective engines to expand their services while ensuring safe and enjoyable experiences for visitors.\n\nThe introduction of electric outboards was another important aspect of the partnership. Available alongside the petrol range under Hidea\u2019s Ultimate Mobility vision, the electric engines offer quieter and cleaner propulsion options for environmentally sensitive marine locations.\n\n\u201cQuiet, clean and efficient, they are ideal for our lagoons, rivers and sensitive coastal waters, and for operators who want to give guests a calmer, more sustainable experience,\u201d Perera said.\n\nHe added that the partnership would bring benefits beyond individual boat owners and operators. \u201cWhen fishermen earn more and tourism operators grow, the benefit reaches whole communities. That is the real value of tonight\u2019s launch,\u201d he said.\n\nPerera thanked the Hidea team for its confidence in Neil Marine Sports & Leisure and Sri Lanka, reaffirming the company\u2019s commitment to quality products, reliable service and long- term customer support.\n\nHidea China Regional Director Michael Zhou also spoke at the product launch and said the company had confidence in the Group. He added that the Hidea product range would contribute to boosting productivity in the fisheries industry and other sectors of the economy."
