    "chunk_size_bytes": 1645,
    "chunk_text": "BOI presents Sri Lanka\u2019s investment proposition to British investors at Sri Lanka\u2013UK Trade and Investment Forum in London\n\nThe Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) set out Sri Lanka\u2019s investment opportunities, incentives and facilitation framework to British investors and business leaders during an official Sri Lankan delegation visit to the United Kingdom on 21 and 22 October 2026. The two-day promotional program was organised by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) in collaboration with the High Commission of Sri Lanka in the United Kingdom, and was led by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe.\n\nThe delegation comprised Industries and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara, Export Development Board Chairman/CEO Mangala Wijesinghe, and Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Executive Director (Investment Promotion and Research) Priyanka Samaraweera. They were accompanied by, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to the United Kingdom, Nimal Senadheera and Minister Commercial Premathilake Jayakody.\n\nThe program set out to position Sri Lanka as a reliable and competitive trade and investment partner in the UK market; to promote Sri Lanka Expo 2027, to be held in Sri Lanka from 14 to 17 January 2027, and encourage strong British participation; to encourage UK companies to explore sourcing, investment and business partnerships with Sri Lanka; to help Sri Lankan exporters make full use of preferential market access under the UK Developing Countries Trading Scheme (DCTS); and to build direct links with prospective British business partners."
  },
