    "md5": "d265a72316c89d24131189fff6b98457",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "Frontier Research appoints Thilina Panduwawala Executive Director\n\nFrontier Research yesterday said it has appointed economist Thilina Panduwawala as Executive Director, effective 1 January 2027.\n\nHe will lead the firm\u2019s strategy and research agenda. His mandate is to deepen the conviction of its macroeconomic research on Sri Lanka, strengthen relationships with institutional investors, Boards, treasury teams and trading desks, and develop Frontier Research\u2019s next generation of research talent.\n\nThe appointment marks Panduwawala\u2019s third stint at Frontier. Recruited and trained by the firm\u2019s late founder, Amal Sanderatne, he first joined in 2016, where his work included embedding political analysis into the firm\u2019s forecasting. After 18 months with the Asian Development Bank\u2019s Sri Lanka Resident Mission, he returned in 2022, at the height of the economic crisis, and led the firm as Head of Research through the sovereign default and debt restructuring.\n\nOver that period he steered Frontier\u2019s views on the exchange rate, interest rates and inflation through the rupee\u2019s collapse, record inflation and sharp policy tightening, and then through the domestic debt optimisation and the restructuring of Sri Lanka\u2019s external debt.\n\nFor the investors and trading desks Frontier Research serves, his research offered a steady, independent read of an economy in flux.\n\nSince October 2025, Panduwawala has served as Senior Consultant to Parliament\u2019s Committee on Public Finance. There he has supported the Committee\u2019s oversight of fiscal and monetary policy across Budget 2026, the ongoing Budget 2027, and the fiscal packages that followed Cyclone Ditwah and the Middle East conflict. The role has also given him a view from inside the fiscal machinery of the State, the economy\u2019s single largest participant."
  },
