    "chunk_size_bytes": 1122,
    "chunk_text": "Since October 2025, Panduwawala has served as Senior Consultant to Parliament\u2019s Committee on Public Finance. There he has supported the Committee\u2019s oversight of fiscal and monetary policy across Budget 2026, the ongoing Budget 2027, and the fiscal packages that followed Cyclone Ditwah and the Middle East conflict. The role has also given him a view from inside the fiscal machinery of the State, the economy\u2019s single largest participant.\n\nAmal Sanderatne founded Frontier\u2019s Macroeconomic Research Service on the conviction that getting the macro call right is essential to superior investment returns in Sri Lanka, and that a firm should do one thing with depth and conviction. Founded in 2003, Frontier is not a think tank or an advocacy institute. It delivers independent, high-conviction macroeconomic research for institutional investors, boards, treasury teams and trading desks. It serves as the independent macro research provider to most of the country\u2019s asset managers and its largest banks, and its clients together represent more than a third of the Colombo Stock Exchange\u2019s market capitalisation."
