    "chunk_text": "EDB recognises partners of \u2018Sri Lanka Expo 2027\u2019\n\nA special ceremony to recognise the contribution of leading local and international organisations who partnered to support the successful organisation of \u2018Sri Lanka Expo 2027\u2019, was held on 9 November 2026 at the premises of the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB). \u2018Sri Lanka Expo 2027\u2019 is the country\u2019s foremost international trade exhibition, organised by the EDB and Industries and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry.\n\nThe organisations extending their collaboration and sponsorship to the international exhibition are: Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, National Design Centre (NDC), SLT-Mobitel, Akbar Brothers Ltd., Hayleys PLC, Coconut Development Authority, Sri Lanka Export Credit Insurance Corporation (SLECIC), Deutsche Gesellschaft f\u00fcr Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ), Hatton National Bank, Colombo West International Terminal Ltd., Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (SLIM), PEO TV, Barberyn Ayurveda Resort, SriLankan Airlines, Rhino Roofing Products Ltd., Orel IT, Time Plan Publishing Ltd., Postgraduate Institute of Management Alumni (PIMA), and Bio Foods.\n\nEDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe, Director General Erandika Dissanayake, Additional Director General (Development) Kumuduni Mudaliage, Additional Director General (Finance and Administration) Roshan Jayasinghe, together with other officials and representatives of the partner organisations, attended the event.\n\nThe Chairman highly appreciated the contributions both monetary and in-kind extended by the partner organisations.\n\nSri Lanka Expo 2027 is scheduled to be held from 14-17 January at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH), Colombo.\n\nAround 750 exhibitors are expected to take part repressing 25 product and Services Sectors, along with approximately 1,500 international participants, including international buyers, investors and media representatives representing more than 50 countries."
