    "chunk_text": "Hegseth has repeatedly defended the \u200bconflict, calling Trump courageous and saying Iran's military \u2060has been left in ruins. He also said his orders to US forces were lawful, despite Massie's accusations of \"high crimes and misdemeanors\".\n\n\"History will judge the Iran war quite differently than the conventional wisdom right now,\" Hegseth said on Tuesday at his first Pentagon briefing in six months.\n\nA Democratic-led push to \u200bimpeach Hegseth could be far \u2060more intense, with lawmakers calling in top brass to testify, including generals and admirals fired by Hegseth who have remained silent so far. Hegseth, who has railed against diversity efforts at the Pentagon, fired the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, who is Black, and the Navy's top admiral, a woman, among others.\n\nIn such an effort, Democrats could also raise other issues of concern to voters including Pentagon policy toward Ukraine and the US \u2060military's strikes on \u200bsuspected drug trafficking boats in Caribbean and Pacific waters.\n\nSome Republicans say Hegseth's strained relations with Congress are becoming a political liability \u200bas the Trump administration seeks a huge increase in the military's budget to $1.5 trillion from $950 billion.\n\nMassie said he was disappointed by the vote, comparing Republicans to passengers content to go down with the Titanic.\n\n\"They know it's a sinking ship but committed to stay \u200bon board,\" he said."
