    "md5": "750bc10768b7169e821c878bd0311f31",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1974,
    "chunk_text": "It\u2019s very important. I could have a perfect system giving a perfect forecast. But if you don\u2019t understand it, you don\u2019t know what\u2019s going to happen. You also need to get it in a timely way. It\u2019s not only about the quality of the forecast, but there are other components that are very critical.\n\nQ\u00a0\u00a0 Sri Lankans mainly speak Sinhala and Tamil. Could this software be used in other languages as well?\n\nQ\u00a0\u00a0 Is open source data one way of getting accurate forecasts in future?\n\nWhen modeling forecasts into the future,\u00a0 the models have to know the correct information. For instance, the state of a river basin; are they wet, dry or somewhere in between. The models can only know that with good input data that\u2019s been observed. Right now there are multiple rain gauge networks in Sri Lanka. They need to be integrated. I think this project would help bring them into an integrated system to prove the overall depiction of rainfall patterns across Sri Lanka. There is software that can help bring in satellite estimates of rainfall, rain gauge networks,\u00a0 and in the future I know that there are radar systems that are going to be used for rainfall estimation. When that data is available,\u00a0 it could be brought in to create a detailed, high resolution hourly mapping of rainfall over Sri Lanka. That would benefit everybody.\n\nI mentioned that there was at least one person attending the meeting who\u2019s trying to predict and identify areas at risk for landslides. We had a brainstorming session about how we could collaborate to make improvements in that area. We also discussed about improvements in modelling in coastal areas where erosion and deposition of sediment could create problems. People could collaborate to make improvements in a wide range of things including agriculture. One of the things that the modelling system can do is estimate soil moisture. We can make predictions out into the future about soil moisture changes on a seasonal time scale."
  },
