    "md5": "d85b03cb578b700ee1b694810e33c702",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1188,
    "chunk_text": "I mentioned that there was at least one person attending the meeting who\u2019s trying to predict and identify areas at risk for landslides. We had a brainstorming session about how we could collaborate to make improvements in that area. We also discussed about improvements in modelling in coastal areas where erosion and deposition of sediment could create problems. People could collaborate to make improvements in a wide range of things including agriculture. One of the things that the modelling system can do is estimate soil moisture. We can make predictions out into the future about soil moisture changes on a seasonal time scale.\n\nPeople will pay attention to things that they feel are important to them. People are used to seeing the world in a certain way. When you provide them with more information,\u00a0 it just opens up a world of possibilities to them. The head of RIMES has worked in Sri Lanka with farmers to help them to understand this probabilistic forecast. With a probabilistic forecast,\u00a0 the question is to what extent would you take action. For every person it\u2019s probably going to be different because it\u2019s a measure of how risk adverse or risk tolerant they are."
