    "chunk_size_bytes": 962,
    "chunk_text": "Nalinda elected Chairman of first BIMSTEC Health Ministers\u2019 Meeting\n\nColombo, November 11 (Daily Mirror) - Health and Mass Media Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa has been elected Chairman of the first BIMSTEC Health Ministers\u2019 Meeting.\n\nThe meeting, aimed at taking regional health cooperation to a new level, commenced this morning (11) at the Hilton Colombo.\n\nWith Sri Lanka assuming the chairmanship, the country has been entrusted with the responsibility of leading collective efforts to strengthen health cooperation among BIMSTEC member states.\n\nThe meeting is attended by representatives from all seven member countries \u2014 Sri Lanka, India, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Nepal, Myanmar and Thailand.\n\nKey areas of discussion include strengthening regional public health security, controlling communicable diseases, enhancing collective preparedness to respond to health emergencies, and promoting technical cooperation and knowledge-sharing in the health sector."
