    "md5": "0c0170f824b24f7ca29fb41eb9571926",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1595,
    "chunk_text": "Accor marks a new milestone in Sri Lanka\n\nCelebrates brand\u2019s debut with arrival of Pullman Colombo Downtown and Pullman Bentota Resort & Spa\n\nPullman, the Accor brand built around exchange, marked a major milestone in Sri Lanka, with an exclusive gathering at Vistas Rooftop Bar, Pullman Colombo Downtown, recently.\n\nThe evening celebrated the brand\u2019s debut in the country with the introduction of two landmark properties \u2013 Pullman Colombo Downtown and Pullman Bentota Resort & Spa.\n\nThe occasion brought together Accor South Asia CEO Ranju Alex, property owners, leadership teams from both hotels, distinguished dignitaries, including Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and prominent members of Sri Lanka\u2019s media fraternity to celebrate this exciting new chapter for Pullman in the country.\n\nThe introduction of Pullman strengthens Accor\u2019s presence across two of Sri Lanka\u2019s most compelling business and leisure destinations. Bringing together the energy of Colombo\u2019s commercial landscape and the natural beauty of Bentota\u2019s coastline, the two hotels extend Pullman\u2019s contemporary hospitality to both corporate and leisure travellers.\n\nMore than a celebration, the evening offered a platform for meaningful exchange with Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate leadership and key industry stakeholders, reflecting Accor\u2019s commitment to building lasting relationships as it continues to grow in the market.\n\nThe guests also experienced first-hand Pullman\u2019s approach to contemporary hospitality, where business, leisure and social moments come together."
  },
