    "chunk_size_bytes": 1475,
    "chunk_text": "Nutriline introduces Corn Flakes\n\nStrengthens agricultural value creation via local sourcing and connects food manufacturing with consumer needs\n\nNutriline, the breakfast nutrition brand of Plenty Foods (Pvt.) Limited, a fully-owned subsidiary of CBL Group, recently unveiled Nutriline Corn Flakes, a new addition to its breakfast cereal portfolio made with 100 percent locally sourced corn, reinforcing the group\u2019s commitment to building food businesses that create value for consumers while supporting local agriculture and livelihoods.\n\n\u201cCBL Group has always been in the business of food that creates an impact on people\u2019s lives and on society. The food we produce reaches you and me every day but the impact of our business extends much further, to the farmers through initiatives such as Govi Paula, who grow our raw materials and more than 21,000 families that depend on agriculture for their livelihoods. Nutriline Corn Flakes is another outcome of this thinking. By using 100 percent locally sourced corn, we are connecting local agricultural production with a product that serves an everyday consumer need,\u201d said CBL Food Cluster Director and Chief Executive Officer Manjula Dahanayake.\n\nThe newly launched Nutriline Corn Flakes contains no added colours or flavours, offers high iron content, provides a source of protein and is enriched with 10 essential vitamins. The product is available on retail shelves in convenient pack sizes at an accessible price."
