    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan talent helps power SAGE as Sysco earns Gartner recognition\n\nSysco LABS Sri Lanka team that contributed to SAGE, recognised at 2026 Gartner Eye on Innovation Awards\n\nSysco named Runner-Up in Americas Category of 2026 Gartner Eye on Innovation Awards for Retail and Consumer Goods\n\nSysco LABS Sri Lanka\u2019s engineering teams have contributed to the development of the Sysco Agentic Ecosystem (SAGE), the enterprise AI platform for which Sysco Corporation was named Runner-Up in the Retail and Consumer Goods, Americas Category at the 2026 Gartner Eye on Innovation Awards.\n\nThe recognition reflects Sysco\u2019s continued pursuit of technological excellence through investment in AI and new approaches to business challenges. Sysco LABS plays a pivotal role in this work, bringing Sri Lankan engineering expertise to a collaborative effort across Sysco\u2019s global technology organisation.\n\nSysco is the world\u2019s largest global foodservice distributor supplying restaurants, hotels, healthcare facilities and other businesses that prepare meals away from home.\n\nSAGE brings governed agentic AI into its operations across sales, supply chain and administrative functions. It connects AI agents, software that can perform tasks, with business data and systems, enabling them to recommend actions and carry out workflows within a common governance framework.\n\nSysco LABS Sri Lanka Managing Director and Sysco Vice President GIC Strategy and Operations Thushera Kawdawatta said, \u201cBeing recognised by Gartner validates the exceptional dedication and ingenuity of the team behind this milestone. As Sri Lanka continues to strengthen its role as Sysco\u2019s global AI epicentre, it is our people who are driving this paradigm shift. Through seamless collaboration across our global technology ecosystem, we are deploying world-class talent to solve complex challenges at scale, proving that we are not just embracing the future of AI but actively shaping it together.\u201d"
  },
