    "md5": "ff1ddf92ff0f0ef468e7053f46ea7655",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1811,
    "chunk_text": "Alliance Finance and LeMS partner to make electric three-wheeler conversions more accessible\n\nAlliance Finance Company PLC (AFC) has entered a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Lanka E-Mobility Solutions (Pvt) Ltd (LeMS) to make the conversion of petrol-powered three-wheelers to electric more accessible to owners across Sri Lanka.\n\nThrough this partnership, AFC will offer preferential leasing facilities to customers seeking to convert their existing three-wheelers to electric, while LeMS will undertake the conversions and provide batteries on a rental basis. By combining financing solutions with an alternative to purchasing a battery outright, the initiative aims to reduce the financial barriers to adopting electric mobility.\n\nFor most three-wheeler owners in Sri Lanka, their vehicle is more than a mode of transport; it is their primary source of income. With daily operating expenses, particularly fuel and maintenance, putting pressure on their earnings, the transition to electric mobility presents an opportunity to minimize costs while continuing to earn a livelihood.\n\nHowever, the initial investment required to convert a conventional three-wheeler to electric, together with the cost of a battery, can be a significant obstacle for many owners.\n\nThe AFC-LeMS partnership seeks to address these challenges through a combination of preferential leasing and a battery rental model, making the transition more financially accessible.\n\nLeMS converts existing petrol-powered three-wheelers to electric by replacing the conventional engine with an electric drivetrain. Under its battery rental model, customers pay the conversion cost upfront, while LeMS provides the battery on a rental basis over an agreed period, typically three to five years, subject to the applicable terms and warranty."
  },
