    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "22037085f63bae232b398395687ff89f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1909,
    "chunk_text": "Blue Yonder Cognitive Solutions to power future of Sri Lankan retail\n\nHayleys Retail Holdings Ltd announced that it has selected Blue Yonder to build its grocery retail operations from the ground up with AI and connected supply chain technology. Hayleys Retail plans to open a number of stores in the near future to bring reliable service and greater convenience to consumers across Sri Lanka. The company is Blue Yonder\u2019s first retail customer in Sri Lanka.\n\nHayleys is Sri Lanka\u2019s number one ranked public listed company and a multinational conglomerate, accounting for approximately 5 percent of Sri Lanka\u2019s export income, with operations spanning 17 business sectors across five continents.\n\nEntering the large-scale supermarket sector and drawing on the Group\u2019s strengths in manufacturing, logistics and services, the company looked beyond the applications it would need on day one to how it wanted the business to operate at scale.\n\nHayleys Retail selected Blue Yonder for three reasons: a unified data foundation that connects merchandising, replenishment and space decisions; AI agents that monitor operations, detect anomalies and recommend actions before problems cascade; and a cloud-native platform that can grow with the business from its first stores to a national network without re-platforming.\n\nThe rollout begins with Blue Yonder Merchandise Operations, giving Hayleys Retail a single source of truth for item, supplier, cost and pricing data and the operational discipline to execute consistently at the store, region and channel level.\n\nAs the business scales, Blue Yonder Allocation and Replenishment will apply machine learning forecasting to keep inventory aligned with demand, including seasonal peaks. Because every capability runs on the Blue Yonder Platform, each solution Hayleys Retail adds draws on the same data and the same AI, so the business gets smarter as it grows."
  },
