    "md5": "c59b916b77ddd10056bb9fb8c005e62e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1237,
    "chunk_text": "Through such discussions and negotiations, the employees collectively or through trade unions will have the opportunity to table their concerns while the employers will have the opportunity to put forward their expectations. This will create a relationship that is more transparent and it will further reduce the communication gap between the employer and the employee.\n\nThe substantial number of collective agreements signed between the selected period (2022-2024) represents the current trend of adopting the collective bargaining process as a forum of discussion between the employer and the employee, notes EFC\u2019s Director General, Yashoravi Bakmiwewa. \u201cThe publication aims to serve as avaluable reference for employers, HR professionals, industrial relations practitioners, researchers and other stakeholders interested in understanding the developments in remuneration and employment benefits negotiated through the collective bargaining process,\u201d says Bakmiwewa.\n\nThe data presented in the publication constitutes a consolidated representation of salary increments, benefits, and other compensation-related information collected from multiple organizations across key industries. The publication can be purchased at the EFC."
