    "md5": "c0a011c4102dbb7c78d0db516c4ad707",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1651,
    "chunk_text": "Public warned against travelling abroad for employment on visit visas\n\nColombo, Nov. 11 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Ministry of Foreign Employment and Tourism has warned the public against travelling overseas for work on visit visas, noting that a large number of Sri Lankan nationals are currently facing severe hardships in countries such as Malaysia, Dubai, and Oman after falling prey to false promises of employment.\n\nIn an official advisory, the Ministry urged prospective migrant workers to seek foreign employment strictly through proper legal procedures to avoid putting their lives and futures at risk.\n\nAuthorities highlighted that working while on a visit visa violates local laws in host countries, exposing individuals to serious legal trouble, arrest, detention, and deportation.\n\nFurthermore, those who travel through unauthorized channels risk failing to receive their promised jobs, having their wages withheld, or being paid significantly less than originally agreed upon.\n\nThe Ministry also cautioned that individuals using visit visas for work are highly vulnerable to fraud and human trafficking, which can lead to the loss of their passports, severe financial loss, and acute mental distress.\n\nJob seekers are specifically advised not to be misled by deceptive promises such as \u201cGo on a Visit Visa and we will change it to a Work Visa.\u201d or \u201cYou can find a job after you go there.\u201d\n\nTo ensure their safety and legal protection, the Ministry strongly advises all citizens travelling abroad for employment to register with the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE) and depart strictly through established legal channels."
  },
