    "chunk_size_bytes": 734,
    "chunk_text": "Indian Health Minister in town\n\nIndia\u2019s Health and Family Welfare Union Minister Jagat Prakash Nadda (right) being welcomed by Indian High Commissioner to\n\nIndia\u2019s Health and Family Welfare Union Minister Jagat Prakash Nadda arrived in Colombo yesterday (11) to attend the inaugural BIMSTEC Health Ministers\u2019 Meeting, as Sri Lanka hosts the regional grouping\u2019s first ministerial-level discussions on public health cooperation.\n\nNadda was received at the airport by Indian High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Santosh Jha.\n\nSri Lanka is hosting the inaugural meeting in its capacity as the lead country for public health cooperation within the Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC)."
