    "md5": "b02205119c8af5df6daa54a026b6b799",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1400,
    "chunk_text": "Saudi Arabia drops case against Anojan Sivarasa\n\nForeign Minister Vijitha Herath (left) with Anojan\u2019s parents last evening\n\nGovt. expects to facilitate his return to Sri Lanka within one to two weeks\n\nForeign Minister Vijitha Herath announced last night that the Saudi Arabian authorities have discontinued all remaining legal proceedings against Sri Lankan national Sivarasa Anojan, who was previously sentenced to death over a Facebook post, paving the way for his return to the motherland.\n\nAddressing the media, Herath said the Saudi Public Prosecution had decided on 9 November not to proceed further with the case, effectively bringing the legal proceedings against Anojan to an end.\n\nAnojan was sentenced to death by an appeals court in Saudi Arabia\u2019s Eastern Province on 17 September 2026 over allegations linked to a Facebook post deemed offensive by Saudi authorities.\n\nFollowing diplomatic and other interventions by Sri Lankan authorities, the Saudi Court overturned the death sentence on 14 October. However, other penalties remained in place, prompting the Government to continue efforts to secure the conclusion of all legal proceedings.\n\nThe latest decision by the Saudi Public Prosecution removes the remaining legal obstacles, with the Government now making arrangements for Anojan\u2019s return. Herath said he was expected to arrive in Sri Lanka within the next one to two weeks."
