    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "TWC Holdings appoints Harin de Saram CEO\n\nTWC Founder and Executive Chairman Thilan Wijesinghe yesterday announced the appointment of Harin de Saram as Chief Executive Officer of TWC Holdings Ltd., succeeding him in the role as the Group continues to strengthen its leadership team to support its expanding domestic and regional operations.\n\nTWC Holdings serves as the Group\u2019s strategic advisory platform, providing strategic and transaction advisory services to corporates, governments, multilateral agencies, and development partners.\n\nDe Saram joined TWC in 2024 following a distinguished international banking career spanning more than two decades. He previously worked with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) and spent 19 years with Westpac Banking Corporation in Australia and Singapore where he held senior leadership positions in corporate banking, structured finance, and risk management. De Saram started his career in Sri Lanka working at DFCC Bank and was a founding member of Citi National Investment Bank (now NDB Investment Bank).\n\nFounder and Executive Chairman Thilan Wijesinghe said:\u00a0 \u201cHarin\u2019s appointment reflects TWC\u2019s evolution from a founder-led corporate finance and real estate focused advisory practice into a diversified professional services platform. His international banking experience, technical depth and understanding of both public and private sector financing will play an important role as we continue to expand our advisory platform across Sri Lanka and selected regional markets.\u201d\n\nDe Saram\u2019s sector experience spans infrastructure, renewable energy, agriculture, mining and minerals, transport and logistics. He has expertise in structured asset finance, commodity finance for the mining sector, project finance, mezzanine and subordinated debt, and sustainability-linked financing solutions."
  },
