    "md5": "1d3bd15643ae14ef0f16e87ae6165da0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1907,
    "chunk_text": "Aberdeen Group announces leadership transition at Ex-pack Corrugated Cartons PLC: Sattar Kassim retires as Chairman, Thulci Aluwihare appointed\n\nAberdeen Group announced that Sattar Kassim will retire from the Board of its listed subsidiary, Ex-pack Corrugated Cartons PLC, with effect from 18 November 2026, relinquishing his position as Chairman from the same date. At its meeting held on 9 November, the Board of Ex-pack resolved to appoint Thulci Aluwihare, an Independent, Non-Executive Director of the company, as Chairman of the Board with effect from 18 November 2026.\n\nKassim\u2019s retirement on his 70th birthday marks the close of a distinguished chapter. A founding figure of Aberdeen Group, he played a central role in shaping the Group\u2019s strategic direction and building it into the diversified business it is today. During his tenure as Chairman, he steered Ex-pack onto a path of sustained profitability, strengthening its financial foundations for the future. Under his leadership, Ex-pack also completed its Initial Public Offering and listed on the Colombo Stock Exchange, a significant milestone for both the company and the Group.\n\nAberdeen Group extends its deep appreciation to Kassim for his vision, guidance and steadfast commitment to Ex-pack, and for the strong foundation he leaves for the company\u2019s next phase of growth.\n\nThe Group welcomes Aluwihare, the Deputy Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo Ltd., who brings over 25 years of international experience across London, Melbourne and Colombo in mergers and acquisitions, public\u2013private partnerships, transaction advisory and restructuring. Aluwihare played a pivotal role in establishing Sri Lanka\u2019s first foreign-currency-designated, multi-services Special Economic Zone, working closely with the Presidential Secretariat as a member of the Colombo International Financial Centre Steering Committee Task Force."
  },
