    "chunk_text": "The Company also commissioned the 5 MW Diya Janani floating solar project at Dambulu Oya Reservoir in September. As one of Sri Lanka\u2019s pioneering private-sector floating solar developments, the project demonstrates WindForce\u2019s commitment to innovative, land-efficient renewable energy solutions.\n\nThe portfolio represents an investment exceeding Rs. 22.5 billion and is being developed under a 15-year Build, Own and Operate model. Once completed, these projects are expected to enhance grid stability, support renewable energy integration and reduce pressure on the national grid during peak evening demand.\n\nBeyond these milestones, WindForce continues to advance a development pipeline exceeding 240 MW. This includes the proposed 50 MW Mullikulam Wind Power Project through Aeroforce (Pvt) Ltd and a 10 MW wind project through Safe Power International Ltd., reinforcing the Company\u2019s focus on a diversified generation mix and Sri Lanka\u2019s long-term energy security.\n\nManaging Director Manjula Perera said: \u201cOver the past 16 years, WindForce has built a strong renewable energy platform. Our ambition now is to double the capacity we have built over those 16 years within the next three years. With major projects moving through construction and commissioning, and stronger access to international financing, we are well positioned for the next phase of growth.\u201d"
