    "chunk_size_bytes": 1788,
    "chunk_text": "Haycarb posts Rs. 40.6 b 1H revenue, PBT up 75% to Rs. 4 b\n\nHaycarb PLC, has delivered a strong financial performance for the six months ending 30 September 2026, recording revenue of Rs. 40.6 billion, up 42% year-on-year, while profit before tax increased 75% to Rs. 4.0 billion. Attributable Profit to shareholders grew 98% to Rs. 2.5 billion, with earnings per share increasing to Rs. 8.41.\n\nThe Group strengthened its position in gold recovery and water treatment applications through increased market penetration and product development initiatives, diversifying its revenue base and supporting margin enhancement. A key contributor to growth during the period was the continued expansion of Haycarb\u2019s energy storage carbon portfolio, where global demand for specialized activated carbons used in advanced energy storage applications remains robust.\n\nHaycarb PLC Chairman and its parent company Hayleys PLC Chairman Mohan Pandithage said: \u201cThe Group\u2019s performance reflects the continued successful execution of its transformation strategy, focused on expanding its portfolio of value-added activated carbon solutions, market growth, strengthening its global manufacturing footprint, and enhancing resilience across its supply chain within the ESG framework.\u201d\n\nThe period was also characterised by significant volatility in coconut shell charcoal availability and pricing across several sourcing markets. Amid these challenges, Haycarb\u2019s established sourcing and manufacturing ecosystem of extensive supplier network, diversified raw material sourcing model, and geographically distributed manufacturing operations served as a strategic competitive advantage and enabled the Group to maintain continuity of supply and support customer requirements across key global markets."
