    "chunk_size_bytes": 1755,
    "chunk_text": "The current NPP Government will present its third Budget to Parliament on 12 November 2026. Among citizens\u2019 many expectations, the Government also aims to deliver on its election manifesto commitments in this Budget. It will allocate the necessary funds to continue initiatives already underway since 2024. In my view, five national initiatives share overlapping sustainable development objectives, including building a prosperous, inclusive, and sustainable nation. These are: (1) A Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life (the NPP Government\u2019s election manifesto), (2) Digital Economy, (3) Prajashakthi, (4) Clean Sri Lanka, and (5) the work of the Sustainable Development Council (SDC). The last is not a national-level initiative; however, it measures the country\u2019s overall performance in development activities. These initiatives have distinct mandates and implementation mechanisms. However, they share a common aspiration from NPP\u2019s Election Manifesto: to enhance people\u2019s quality of life and well-being through economic progress, social inclusion, environmental sustainability, and good governance.\n\nThese capitals are not unrelated or independent resources; they reinforce one another and collectively shape a nation\u2019s ability to produce goods and services, build resilience, and support well-being. The IECF can be understood as the seeds of economic growth and sustainable development. Just as seeds require suitable conditions to grow, Government and the private sector should invest continuously in the formation of these capitals. Effective institutions, scientific knowledge, and community participation are needed to deliver lasting economic and social benefits. In fact, institutional capital can serve as a catalyst for capital."
  },
