    "chunk_size_bytes": 1665,
    "chunk_text": "In the light of these considerations, I propose that employment income be treated as a distinct category for personal income taxation, with a simpler and more predictable method of assessment. The proposed arrangement would rest on three basic principles:\n\nA common tax-free threshold: Every employee should enjoy the common personal tax-free threshold applicable under the general tax framework.\n\nSeparate assessment of other income: Employment income should not thereafter be aggregated with income from other sources for the purpose of determining the progressive tax rate applicable to those other sources.\n\nIncome from investments, rental properties, business activities and other sources could continue to be assessed under the relevant tax provisions, with appropriate safeguards to ensure that the common tax-free allowance is not duplicated.\n\nSuch an arrangement would introduce greater simplicity and predictability into the taxation of employment income. It would also prevent an employee\u2019s remuneration from being pushed into a higher marginal tax bracket merely because the individual happens to receive additional income from another source. The proposal does not seek to exempt employees from their responsibility to contribute to public revenue. On the contrary, it seeks to establish a more rational and transparent method of determining that contribution. The appropriate uniform rate would, of course, need to be determined after careful fiscal analysis, taking account of revenue requirements, distributional consequences and the overall tax structure.\n\nAnother important consideration is the relationship between taxation and economic growth."
