    "chunk_size_bytes": 1729,
    "chunk_text": "Such an arrangement would introduce greater simplicity and predictability into the taxation of employment income. It would also prevent an employee\u2019s remuneration from being pushed into a higher marginal tax bracket merely because the individual happens to receive additional income from another source. The proposal does not seek to exempt employees from their responsibility to contribute to public revenue. On the contrary, it seeks to establish a more rational and transparent method of determining that contribution. The appropriate uniform rate would, of course, need to be determined after careful fiscal analysis, taking account of revenue requirements, distributional consequences and the overall tax structure.\n\nAnother important consideration is the relationship between taxation and economic growth.\n\nThe sustainability of economic reforms cannot be secured through fiscal consolidation alone. There must also be visible progress in creating economic opportunities, expanding production, attracting investment and improving the earning capacity of the population. A tax system that is perceived as unreasonable or unpredictable can weaken public confidence and discourage individuals from undertaking additional productive activities. The objective should therefore be to broaden the revenue base through economic expansion rather than rely excessively on increasing the burden on existing taxpayers.\n\nThe question of taxation cannot be considered in isolation from Government expenditure and borrowing.\n\nBorrowing may be necessary for a country facing extraordinary economic circumstances. However, it cannot become a permanent substitute for sound revenue management or a means of financing unlimited expenditure."
