    "chunk_size_bytes": 1266,
    "chunk_text": "Borrowing may be necessary for a country facing extraordinary economic circumstances. However, it cannot become a permanent substitute for sound revenue management or a means of financing unlimited expenditure.\n\nAs the Government prepares to present the 2027 Budget, there is an opportunity to reconsider certain aspects of the existing taxation framework. The purpose of this appeal is not to question the Government\u2019s legitimate need to raise revenue or to undermine the economic reform program. It is to encourage a more balanced and equitable approach to achieving those objectives.\n\nA taxation system must command public acceptance not merely because it is imposed by law, but because the principles underlying it are reasonable and defensible. The proposed separate treatment of employment income, with a common tax-free threshold followed by a uniform rate, is one such reform deserving serious consideration.\n\nA good Budget is not measured solely by the amount of revenue it collects, but also by the fairness of the methods through which that revenue is raised and the economic value generated by its expenditure. The ultimate objective of taxation should be to strengthen the State without weakening the people and the productive economy that sustain it."
