    "chunk_size_bytes": 1125,
    "chunk_text": "Indeed, the Budget has already been prepared. Nevertheless, the first reading of the 2027 Budget provides an appropriate occasion to remind the country\u2019s leadership of the expectations, anxieties and aspirations of the people on whose behalf public finances are managed.\n\nSri Lanka has paid an extraordinarily high price for years of economic mismanagement, institutional weaknesses and policy inconsistency. Its people have made painful sacrifices. They deserve an economic future that does not demand endless sacrifice without delivering meaningful rewards.\n\nAs the President presents Budget 2027, the hope of the nation is therefore neither extravagant nor unreasonable. It is simply that the coming year will bring fewer hardships, greater opportunities, fairer economic conditions and renewed confidence in tomorrow.\n\nUltimately, the success of Budget 2027 should not be measured by how impressively it is presented in Parliament, but by how much easier it makes life for the ordinary people of Sri Lanka.\n\nThat is the prayer of the people. And that is the responsibility of those entrusted with governing the country."
