    "chunk_size_bytes": 1976,
    "chunk_text": "ENCARE SECURES NATIONAL BRONZE AT CNCI ACHIEVER AWARDS 2026\n\nBuilding on its foundation in clinical waste management, EnCare has expanded into environmental engineering, bringing specialist waste services, recycling and resource recovery together through one trusted partner.\n\nSisili Hanaro EnCare (Pvt) Ltd received the National Bronze Award in the Large Category, Service Sector, at the CNCI Achiever of Industrial Excellence Awards 2026, organised by the Ceylon National Chamber of Industries (CNCI). The achievement marks an important milestone for a Sri Lankan company working in one of the country\u2019s most demanding service sectors: the safe management of hazardous and specialised waste.\n\nThe award also draws attention to work that is often out of sight, yet essential to hospitals, industries and communities. Over more than a decade, EnCare has developed its services around the technical and regulatory demands of the waste it handles.\n\nEnCare was established as a joint venture between Sisili Projects Consortium and South Korea\u2019s Hanaro Eng. Co. Ltd. Its clinical waste management operations were developed under a tripartite agreement involving the Ministry of Health, the Central Environmental Authority (CEA) and the Sisili Hanaro joint venture. The arrangement combined local knowledge with international engineering experience within a regulated operating framework.\n\nEnCare commenced clinical waste management operations in early 2014, when major hospitals were dealing with substantial backlogs. With its pilot facility still under development, the company handled approximately 30,000 kg of accumulated clinical waste alongside daily service requirements. During the COVID-19 pandemic, its in-house engineering team designed and built an interim treatment line within two weeks to help keep essential operations running. These experiences shaped the operational discipline and engineering expertise that remain central to EnCare\u2019s continued progress."
