    "chunk_text": "EnCare commenced clinical waste management operations in early 2014, when major hospitals were dealing with substantial backlogs. With its pilot facility still under development, the company handled approximately 30,000 kg of accumulated clinical waste alongside daily service requirements. During the COVID-19 pandemic, its in-house engineering team designed and built an interim treatment line within two weeks to help keep essential operations running. These experiences shaped the operational discipline and engineering expertise that remain central to EnCare\u2019s continued progress.\n\nFor industrial and commercial clients, the portfolio includes pharmaceutical and cosmetic waste, hazardous chemical waste and marine waste management, alongside certified secure destruction of confidential documents and data. EnCare also operates an established business-to-business e-waste service covering segregation, recycling and secure handling of discarded electronics. These services allow clients to address different waste requirements through a single provider without overlooking the controls each stream demands.\n\nThrough its established Material Recovery Facility (MRF), EnCare collects, sorts and recycles plastic waste from business clients. Alongside its e-waste management services, these operations contribute to a circular economy by recovering valuable materials and returning them to productive use, reducing the volume of waste sent for disposal. This approach builds on EnCare\u2019s core expertise in managing specialised waste streams.\n\nNot all waste streams, however, are suitable for recycling. Clinical, pharmaceutical and hazardous chemical waste require controlled handling and where necessary, specialised treatment and disposal. EnCare\u2019s integrated approach addresses both priorities, recovering resources wherever safe and practicable while ensuring that waste requiring specialised treatment is managed responsibly."
