    "md5": "1b94bb090f2f41cddab90571a6edeeb4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1951,
    "chunk_text": "Blue tsunami: American reformist revolution and new progressivism\n\nBernie Sanders and AOC \u2018Fighting Oligarchy\u2019 tour 2025 revived Democratic base\n\nSome events act as a \u2018tester\u2019 of your determinant drives and motivating passions, manifested in spontaneous reflexes. I rejoiced at the Blue Tsunami (or \u2018Blunami\u2019 as American youngsters say) of the US Democrat victory in both Houses of Congress\u2014though aware of the possible implications for Ukraine-Russia, and for Sri Lanka, of a much more liberal Congress.\n\nThe Sri Lankan angle didn\u2019t dampen my delight at the Democratic triumph because my core identity is as a human being and is therefore universalist, and I am convinced that on balance, this Democratic victory is also a victory more generally for humanity. I also think the Democrat tsunami provides a great example for Sri Lanka.\n\nWhen I emailed my old PhD supervisor and friend, Emeritus Professor John Kane, author of \u2018Between Virtue and Power: The Persistent Moral Dilemma of US Foreign Policy\u2019 (Yale University Press), about the Republican rout in both houses of Congress, he wrote back exultantly: \u201cCan\u2019t take my eyes away. It is much more devastating than even I\u2019d hoped for!\u201d.\n\nAs observed by CNN, come 3 January, 75% of the USA will be governed by the Democrats.\n\nSir Isaiah Berlin made a breakthrough in political discernment when he said that in politics we often have to make painful choices between desirable values or clusters of values. The three great ideals of the French Revolution\u2014Liberty, Equality, Fraternity\u2014are almost never available together in the real world. It is almost always a lacerating choice. I\u2019d say we are lucky if any two of the three are together, but are luckiest when the three great values appear, however episodically or ephemerally, interlinked.\n\nThe victory of this generation of US Democrats re-bundles the values of Liberty, Equality and Fraternity, even for a moment."
