    "chunk_size_bytes": 1687,
    "chunk_text": "85-year-old Bernie Sanders inspired a peaceful revolutionary change in public consciousness by combining moral-ethical leadership with sharply analytical socioeconomic critique in his decades-long career and tireless campaigning over the last ten years, all over the United States. The winning Democratic candidates are \u2018Bernie\u2019s Children\u2019, who could \u2018Feel the Bern\u2019 back in 2016. At that election the Democratic party establishment sabotaged Bernie Sanders and threw the nomination to neoliberal Hillary Clinton, though the New York Times had editorialised that the only one who could possibly defeat Trump that year was Bernie because he, unlike Hillary, epitomised change and had fired-up the enthusiasm of youth and blue-collar voters. Trump decisively beat Hillary.\n\nThe multi-city, cross-country Bernie-AOC tour, billed \u2018Fighting Oligarchy\u2019, ran from February to April 2025. Drawing large crowds, it inspired the \u2018No Kings\u2019 protest movement of mid-2025 through to 2026. That was how the progressive mass movement of resistance to Trump was reignited, which revived, renovated and repositioned the Democratic party, shifting the tectonic plates of American consciousness and generating the Blue Tsunami.\n\nThe open secret of the 2026 \u2018Blue Tsunami\u2019 is that the Democrats focused on economics\u2014not in the sense of abstract macroeconomic statistics, but of the impact of economic policy on the lives and livelihoods of the common citizens, i.e. the \u201caffordability\u201d theme. The Democrats challenged the economic model pursued both by the Republicans and previous Democratic administrations, of the dominance of \u2018the 1%\u2019: the billionaires over the citizens."
