    "chunk_size_bytes": 1611,
    "chunk_text": "The open secret of the 2026 \u2018Blue Tsunami\u2019 is that the Democrats focused on economics\u2014not in the sense of abstract macroeconomic statistics, but of the impact of economic policy on the lives and livelihoods of the common citizens, i.e. the \u201caffordability\u201d theme. The Democrats challenged the economic model pursued both by the Republicans and previous Democratic administrations, of the dominance of \u2018the 1%\u2019: the billionaires over the citizens.\n\nIn the USA today, neoliberal economic doctrine has been rejected, with economic policies and models being assessed from the standpoint of outcome and impact; of material consequence: what they deliver to the people\u2014whether they grind-down or uplift the majority of citizens.\n\nThe ideology of the progressive Democrats, and even the pro-socialist agenda of the DSA-backed candidates, fall squarely within Social Democracy shared by Canada, Scandinavia, Spain, Brazil, Mexico, and UK Labour.\n\nThe new progressivism could be defined as \u2018populist Social Democracy\u2019 or \u2018Social Democratic populism\u2019.\n\nThe US, the birthplace of neoliberalism, was also the birthplace of a viable progressive counter to neoliberalism\u2014not capitalism as such\u2014by Nobel Prize-winners Joe Stiglitz and Paul Krugman and other renowned economists such as Robert Reich, Jeff Sachs and James Galbraith.\n\nEconomic neoliberalism including \u2018the Washington Consensus\u2019 has now been discredited and dislodged in the metropolis, the citadel of world capitalism, and is sought to be replaced by a new pragmatic-progressive, people-centric economic philosophy from bottom-up."
  },
