    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "Economic neoliberalism including \u2018the Washington Consensus\u2019 has now been discredited and dislodged in the metropolis, the citadel of world capitalism, and is sought to be replaced by a new pragmatic-progressive, people-centric economic philosophy from bottom-up.\n\nEconomic neoliberalism is being rejected throughout the Western hemisphere. Hundreds of thousands of students, workers and farmers in France, and a great many young people in Germany are demonstrating against the dominant economic doctrines that had made them and their families poorer while robbing them of the public services and educational facilities they had enjoyed.\n\nA major element of the Blue Tsunami is the victory of progressive Christianity/Christian progressivism over the colossally wealthy right-wing Evangelical variant. In his acceptance speech, the young Senator-elect from Texas, Harvard-educated James Talarico, a Presbyterian with a Master\u2019s in Divinity who follows biblically-sourced Christian social teaching, said he entered politics inspired by Jesus Christ\u2019s injunction to \u2018love thy neighbour\u2019. He denounces \u2018Christian nationalism\u2019, and hails Pope Francis and Pope Leo XIV as his heroes.\n\nIn the fissure within Populism between on the one hand, Far-Right ultranationalism and on the other, Progressive Populism and Left Populism, the Far-Right ultranationalist Populist project has historically peaked and is in parabolic decline, from the defeat of Boris \u2018Brexit\u2019 Johnson through the (two) Bolsonaros and Netanyahu to the Trumpian Republicans.\n\nIn Britain, the Conservatives and the Labour Right (Sir Keir Starmer) have been replaced by Manchester\u2019s Andy Burnham whose hero is Neil Kinnock. Burnham has pledged to rebuild Britain\u2019s public services and revive the economy\u2019s public sector, rejecting \u2018New Labour\u2019 Tony Blair\u2019s neoliberal economic roll-back of the State."
