    "chunk_size_bytes": 1783,
    "chunk_text": "In Britain, the Conservatives and the Labour Right (Sir Keir Starmer) have been replaced by Manchester\u2019s Andy Burnham whose hero is Neil Kinnock. Burnham has pledged to rebuild Britain\u2019s public services and revive the economy\u2019s public sector, rejecting \u2018New Labour\u2019 Tony Blair\u2019s neoliberal economic roll-back of the State.\n\nIn France, Le Pen\u2019s nationalist Right could win the presidency, but Jean-Luc M\u00e9lenchon is a viable Left candidate. His left bloc could prevail at the National Assembly elections, proving a powerful counterweight even if he loses the presidential race.\n\nAmerica\u2019s tectonic shift is an eye-opener for anyone but the most obdurate and ostrich-like:\n\nnBoth (a) economic neoliberalism and (b) ethnoreligious ultranationalism are in crisis and decline.\n\nnA new progressivism \u2013 social democratic populism\u2014has won in the world\u2019s leading power. As went New York City for Mamdani, so went the USA.\n\nLos Angeles has elected a Democratic mayor Nithya Raman, born in Kerala to a Tamil Brahmin family. She is America\u2019s first woman mayor of South Asian origin. Both key mayors, Mamdani and Raman, are DSA-backed.\n\nThe Blue Tsunami broke the stranglehold of the hardline pro-Israeli AIPAC lobby over Jewish voters, Democratic voters and US politics. 72% of the Jewish vote went for Democrats. Senator-elect Dr Abdul El-Sayed of Michigan won a majority of Jewish votes despite his opposition to the Gaza genocide and support for Palestinian self-determination.\n\nIn a rare favourable conjunction, the Democratic triumph came only days after Prime Minister Netanyahu was unable to win a majority in the Israeli election. The Netanyahu \u2018brand\u2019 and the Netanyahu-Trump axis no longer constitute a bridge but rather a wall between Israel and US voters."
  },
