    "md5": "cffa2d9f7cc88928183dedab1b208a2c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1758,
    "chunk_text": "In a rare favourable conjunction, the Democratic triumph came only days after Prime Minister Netanyahu was unable to win a majority in the Israeli election. The Netanyahu \u2018brand\u2019 and the Netanyahu-Trump axis no longer constitute a bridge but rather a wall between Israel and US voters.\n\nA former IDF Chief-of Staff whose son and nephews died in combat, Gadi Eisenkot is hardly a dove. He is author of the notorious Dahiya doctrine of disproportionate force against civilian infrastructure and areas. However, in their time, Menahem Begin, Yitzhak Rabin and Ariel Sharon were hawks but were persuaded into negotiated agreements and partial withdrawals by the US. The fall or retreat of Netanyahu and his religious-ultranationalist Government will end or pause the worst period in Israeli-Palestinian history, making possible a new equation with a Democratic administration in 2028 which can reopen negotiations with the Palestinians.\n\nAn Eisenkot administration may reduce Zionist settler violence in the West Bank.\n\nMost crucially for the region and the world, a Democratic US President (2028) will return to some version of Obama\u2019s JCPOA with Iran.\n\nThe Democratic tsunami provides an inspiration and model for the Sri Lankan citizenry and the Opposition.\n\nIn the face of an arrogant President, the dramatic positive changes in the USA became possible only because the main Opposition party transformed. We don\u2019t have mid-term elections in Sri Lanka and the Provincial Council elections which could function as such are nowhere on the horizon. Any positive change becomes possible only if the main Opposition party/parties \u2013 SJB, SLPP\u2014change for the better and campaign differently. The US Democrats have shown how, so there is no excuse not to."
