    "chunk_size_bytes": 1970,
    "chunk_text": "2.That the SLPP, SLFP and allies shift from the 2019 deviation of Trump-Netanyahu ultranationalism, back to its progressive center-left roots and draw inspiration from Bernie Sanders, AOC and Mamdani.\n\nSri Lanka had its precursor of the US Democrats 2025-2026 re-generation. Not yet 50, Ranasinghe Premadasa stepped away from Dudley Senanayake\u2019s sluggish UNP in defeat in 1970, and facing a Government with a 2/3rds majority ruling under Emergency, launched a political movement called the Citizens\u2019 Front (\u2018Puravesi Peramuna\u2019) in 1972-1973. That catalysed and commenced the transformation of the UNP into the dynamic populist-democratic party of the 1977 \u2018Green Tsunami\u2019.\n\nWith that legacy, and the current example of the US Democrats, the SJB has every reason not to restrict its political activity to Parliament, and to amend its ideology that has failed to seize the public imagination.\n\n\u2018March separately, strike together\u2019 advocated Trotsky. Civic organisations and Opposition parties from the SJB to the FSP dissented separately and resisted sequentially, delaying the PSTA and Organised Crime Bills.\n\nHowever, History shows that no single party can successfully resist and roll-back dictatorship.\n\nIn 1921 Lenin introduced the United Front concept at the Communist International\u2019s 3rd Congress. The 1930s Anti-Fascist Popular Front incorporated liberal democrats, defenders of a democratic republic but not necessarily socialism. In China and Vietnam, the Anti-Imperialist United Front included the \u2018national bourgeoisie\u2019, patriotic capitalists who valued national sovereignty and opposed foreign invasion/domination.\n\nThe parents of the Anti-Fascist Alliance came from Left and Right. Churchill catapulted to the prime ministership from backbencher because he had insisted for the longest time that Hitlerite fascism was the greatest global danger and western democracies should unite not only with each other but also with Stalin\u2019s USSR."
