    "chunk_text": "Rs. 2 trillion capital spending in focus as government presents third Budget\n\nColombo, Nov. 12 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The government will present its maiden third Budget for 2027 today, with a major focus on capital expenditure allocations, the *Daily Mirror* learns.\n\nAn informed government source said the total allocation for capital expenditure in the Budget would amount to Rs. 2 trillion.\n\nThis indicates that the government, now entering the midterm of its tenure, will place greater emphasis on the implementation of infrastructure projects.\n\nBesides, public servants are expected to receive salary increases starting next year.\n\nIn the previous two Budgets, the government focused more on stabilising the macroeconomy in conformity with the IMF's Extended Fund Facility (EFF). The programme is scheduled to end in March next year.\n\nSpeculation is rife that the government will negotiate a fresh programme with the IMF to avert a possible foreign exchange crisis.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake, in his capacity as Finance Minister, will present the Budget in Parliament today at 1.30 p.m."
