    "chunk_size_bytes": 1299,
    "chunk_text": "Former Minister Nimal Siripala de Silva is said to be the party leader now. He noted last January that only one out of 18 cases remained unresolved\u2014the one filed against the party leadership by Dayasiri Jayasekara, the current Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP who previously served as the SLFP General Secretary. Jayasekara filed the lawsuit claiming his removal from the General Secretary post was illegal.\n\nRemarkably, this development concerning a party that ruled the country for over 40 years did not become major news in the national media. Some media outlets chose not to publish it at all. The primary reason is that the party had already lost its political relevance years ago. Among the country\u2019s younger generation, many might not even know that a party called the SLFP once governed Sri Lanka.\n\nThis obscurity can be attributed to the party not having contested any election under the standalone \u201cSLFP\u201d name as a major contender since the 1989 general election, 38 years ago. Following defeats in the 1988 presidential election and the 1989 general election, the SLFP contested and won the 1994 general and presidential elections under the banner of the People\u2019s Alliance (PA), a coalition, led by Chandrika Kumaratunga. Several leftist parties were also part of that coalition."
