    "chunk_size_bytes": 1978,
    "chunk_text": "This obscurity can be attributed to the party not having contested any election under the standalone \u201cSLFP\u201d name as a major contender since the 1989 general election, 38 years ago. Following defeats in the 1988 presidential election and the 1989 general election, the SLFP contested and won the 1994 general and presidential elections under the banner of the People\u2019s Alliance (PA), a coalition, led by Chandrika Kumaratunga. Several leftist parties were also part of that coalition.\n\nThe true collapse of the SLFP \u2014 where it lost its status as one of the country\u2019s two major political parties \u2013 happened when Maithripala Sirisena defected from the Mahinda Rajapaksa-led government to contest the upcoming presidential election against Rajapaksa.\n\nDecades earlier, in the early 1980s, the SLFP faced another massive leadership tussle when former Minister Maithripala Senanayake challenged the leadership of Sirimavo Bandaranaike. Her son Anura Bandaranaike, also sided with Maithripala Senanayake. At one point, the SLFP headquarters on Darley Road in Colombo was even targeted in a bomb attack. However, both factions eventually resolved the dispute accepting the status quo in leadership.\n\nUnlike that Maithripala, this Maithripala (Maithripala Sirisena) successfully challenged the party leadership, won the 2015 presidential election with the backing of UNP votes, defeating Mahinda Rajapaksa. Within a week of the election conclusion, Rajapaksa voluntarily handed over the SLFP leadership to Maithripala Sirisena and handed over the leadership of the UPFA as well within two months.\n\nHowever, the vast majority of loyalists within the SLFP and the broader UPFA remained steadfast supporters of Rajapaksa. In 2016, when Basil Rajapaksa formed the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) under Mahinda Rajapaksa\u2019s leadership, those loyalists also change party allegiance. Sirisena was left with only a handful of supporters and the empty nameplate of the \u201cSLFP.\u201d"
  },
