    "md5": "d2a07828e68d8b3fafac12cc03f2a250",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1772,
    "chunk_text": "Venkadeshwara Agro unveils Director Board\n\nFrom left: Dr. Bradley Emerson, Kanakasingam Suganthon, Rizvi Mowlana, R. Suresh, Manjula Priyadarshana, Michael Ranasinghe, L. Chiranthi Cooray\n\nVenkadeshwara Agro Industry Ltd, the largest edible oil manufacturer in Sri Lanka\u2019s Northern Province, has constituted a seven-member Director Board that pairs founder leadership with expertise in banking, finance, FMCG, exports and sustainability.\n\nThe appointment of Michael Ranasinghe and L. Chiranthi Cooray to Venkadeshwara\u2019s Board has strengthened the company\u2019s existing leadership which includes Dr. Bradley Emerson (Non-Executive Chairman), Kanakasingam Suganthon (Founder/ MD), Rizvi Mowlana, R. Suresh, and Manjula Priyadarshana.\n\nL. Chiranthi Cooray, is appointed as an Independent Board Director and specialist in ESG, Enterprise Transformation & Risk Expert. She is the Founder, of Accedo Intel. Her work focuses on helping boards and senior leadership teams strengthen accountability, culture, leadership capability, internal controls, and sustainable performance.\n\nMichael Ranasinghe is appointed as an Independent Non-Executive Director. He boasts of dual qualifications in marketing and digital marketing and a MBA from UK with International experience in marketing, management and strategic advisory.\n\n\u201cWe started this journey in Jaffna in 2001 with a simple belief: that the North could produce oils as good as any on a Sri Lankan table. Today our refinery supplies households, bakeries and food manufacturers. This Board gives us the experience to take the next step, with more capacity, stronger brands and new markets overseas, without losing the quality and the community that got us here,\u201d said Kanakasingam Suganthon, Founder and Managing Director."
  },
