    "md5": "1df4030e62659b748a8e3b1f008cd649",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1577,
    "chunk_text": "SDF to support SME investment in EV charging infrastructure\n\nSarvodaya Development Finance PLC (SDF) is strengthening its commitment to sustainable development by supporting small and medium enterprises (SMEs) and entrepreneurs seeking to invest in electric vehicle (EV) charging infrastructure across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe initiative forms part of SDF\u2019s broader focus on promoting green financing, sustainable entrepreneurship and the country\u2019s transition towards cleaner mobility.\n\nThrough this initiative, SDF aims to facilitate the expansion of EV charging infrastructure by exploring suitable financing solutions for SMEs interested in establishing and operating charging stations.\n\nThe programme seeks to encourage entrepreneurship within the emerging EV ecosystem while creating new opportunities for businesses to contribute towards environmentally responsible economic development.\n\nAs a practical demonstration of this commitment, SDF is introducing an EV fast-charging facility at its Head Office in Colombo 08, with Vdrive, which is a fully owned subsidiary of Vidulanka PLC serving as the charging service provider. Located on Dr. Danister De Silva Mawatha, the facility will operate 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, improving charging accessibility and convenience for EV users.\n\nThe facility is supported by a 70 kW solar power system, which also contributes to the SDF Head Office\u2019s daily energy requirements. This integration demonstrates how renewable energy can support commercial operations while encouraging environmentally sustainable transport solutions."
  },
