    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "Uber backs Sri Lanka\u2019s next wave of tech entrepreneurs\n\nUber announced the winners of Uber Springboard 2026, its annual mentorship initiative supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging entrepreneurs.\n\nSelected from a record 150 applications this year, winning start-ups Thingsnode, MonChron and NeuroFleets will now receive hands-on mentorship from senior Uber technology and business leaders at the company\u2019s Tech Centre of Excellence in Hyderabad, India.\n\nNow in its third edition, Uber Springboard continues to serve as a platform connecting promising Sri Lankan startups with global technology expertise. Organised in collaboration with the Ministry of Digital Economy, the initiative offers founders practical guidance on product development, technology, business strategy and scaling operations. This year\u2019s winners are working across clean energy, artificial intelligence and logistics, demonstrating how Sri Lankan innovation is addressing challenges with relevance far beyond the island.\n\nEranga Weeraratne, Deputy Minister of Digital Economy, Government of Sri Lanka said, \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s digital economy will be shaped by entrepreneurs who can turn bold ideas into globally competitive businesses. Our role is to help create the ecosystem for that ambition to succeed, including access to technology, expertise and international networks. The record 150 applications to Uber Springboard this year are an encouraging sign of the innovation and enterprise emerging from Sri Lanka. I congratulate the three winning startups and commend Uber for its continued commitment to nurturing Sri Lankan talent and helping our entrepreneurs realise their global ambitions.\u201d\n\nThingsnode, founded by MigaraAmithodhana, is helping make renewable energy operations smarter through technology that monitors and optimises clean-energy assets. Its solutions already support over 500 MW of renewable energy capacity."
  },
