    "md5": "697b6e379d20c7951d1f445666e08333",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1139,
    "chunk_text": "Thingsnode, founded by MigaraAmithodhana, is helping make renewable energy operations smarter through technology that monitors and optimises clean-energy assets. Its solutions already support over 500 MW of renewable energy capacity.\n\nNeuroFleets, a Jaffna-based startup co-founded by Lavanya Ratanbala and Robinroy Peter, is using edge AI and autonomous hardware to coordinate logistics fleets and eliminate downtime in third-party logistics warehouses.\n\nVarun Wijewardane, Country Manager \u2013 Delivery, Uber Sri Lanka said, \u201cWhat stands out about this year\u2019s winners is the future-facing sectors they represent - from artificial intelligence and autonomous technology to clean energy. It is equally encouraging to see innovation emerging from beyond Colombo, reflecting the depth of entrepreneurial talent across Sri Lanka. Through Springboard, we remain committed to nurturing this talent, sharing Uber\u2019s global expertise and helping promising startups build businesses that can scale in Sri Lanka and beyond.\u201d\n\nThe selected start-up founders will participate in structured mentorship sessions at Uber\u2019s Hyderabad Tech Centre."
