    "md5": "e70075e3ec22d241076f596360208304",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1995,
    "chunk_text": "JXG together with CCC launches \u2018BREAKTHROUGH\u2019 to advance national entrepreneur development\n\nFrom left: Representing The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, Manori Dissanayaka, Senior Assistant Secretary General; Dr. Nirmal De Silva, Lead Consultant; Shiran Fernando, Secretary General & CEO; and Krishan Balendra, Chairperson, exchange a cheque to mark the launch of BREAKTHROUGH with C.T.A. Schaffter, Founder & Chairman Emeritus; Ramesh Schaffter, MD/Group CEO; Dilshan Wirasekara, Deputy CEO; and Gamika De Silva, Group Chief Marketing Officer of JXG (Janashakthi Group).\n\nJXG (Janashakthi Group), together with The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, has launched BREAKTHROUGH, a National Entrepreneur Development Programme aimed at identifying and supporting promising businesses across Sri Lanka, helping entrepreneurs overcome barriers to growth, strengthen their capabilities and realise their commercial potential.\n\nBREAKTHROUGH represents a significant private-sector commitment to supporting the country\u2019s entrepreneurial talent. While Sri Lanka has produced businesses that have grown into internationally recognised enterprises, many promising entrepreneurs continue to face challenges in accessing capital, professional expertise, business networks and the guidance needed to scale their operations.\n\nThe initiative draws inspiration from the entrepreneurial journey of JXG\u2019s Founder and Chairman Emeritus, C.T.A. Schaffter, whose contributions to Sri Lanka\u2019s insurance industry and ventures across several other business sectors helped shape the Group. Demonstrating an ability to recognise opportunities beyond his established field of insurance, Schaffter ventured into different industries, including education, manufacturing, exports and agriculture, taking calculated risks to build successful businesses. His journey reflects the entrepreneurial conviction to look beyond conventional boundaries, explore new possibilities and turn opportunities into successful business ventures."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
