    "md5": "1d76e4b9cb10b2c918985c9983b0891f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "The initiative draws inspiration from the entrepreneurial journey of JXG\u2019s Founder and Chairman Emeritus, C.T.A. Schaffter, whose contributions to Sri Lanka\u2019s insurance industry and ventures across several other business sectors helped shape the Group. Demonstrating an ability to recognise opportunities beyond his established field of insurance, Schaffter ventured into different industries, including education, manufacturing, exports and agriculture, taking calculated risks to build successful businesses. His journey reflects the entrepreneurial conviction to look beyond conventional boundaries, explore new possibilities and turn opportunities into successful business ventures.\n\n\u201cThere are businesses across the country with the potential to grow, innovate, create employment and make a meaningful contribution to the economy. Yet, many need access to capital, professional expertise and experienced guidance to move beyond their current capabilities. Through BREAKTHROUGH, JXG is making its business experience and professional capabilities available in support of this national cause.\n\nTogether with The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, we want to give promising entrepreneurs the means and guidance to take their businesses further. We want to see more homegrown businesses develop into significant enterprises, creating value for themselves and for Sri Lanka. This is how we put our purpose of \u2018Breaking Barriers, Forging Futures.\u2019 into action.\u201d\n\nBREAKTHROUGH brings together JXG\u2019s experience in building and managing businesses with The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce\u2019s extensive business network and institutional reach. The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce also welcomes ecosystem partners to contribute their expertise, resources and networks to support the programme and advance this national initiative."
  },
  {
