    "md5": "0e6a43d549aed14fd805ceb6240c4bf4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1868,
    "chunk_text": "BREAKTHROUGH brings together JXG\u2019s experience in building and managing businesses with The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce\u2019s extensive business network and institutional reach. The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce also welcomes ecosystem partners to contribute their expertise, resources and networks to support the programme and advance this national initiative.\n\nA total of Rs. 70 million will be awarded as funding to 20 selected businesses, with individual funds ranging from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 5 million. Allocations will be determined according to each business\u2019s requirements, development stage, growth objectives and potential impact.\n\nBeyond financial assistance, selected businesses will participate in a structured 12-month post-award development programme, providing access to mentoring, investor networks, banking and insurance support, professional expertise and quarterly progress reviews. JXG\u2019s senior leadership and professionals across its businesses will contribute expertise in finance, human resources, information technology, marketing and legal services. This support is intended to help businesses address operational challenges, strengthen governance, improve decision-making and prepare for sustainable growth.\n\nShiran Fernando, Secretary General/CEO of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, said, \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s economic progress will depend significantly on our ability to develop competitive enterprises and enable businesses to access wider markets both locally and globally. While entrepreneurial talent exists across the country, many businesses require access to finance, professional expertise, mentoring and commercial networks to move beyond their current scale.\n\n\u201cWe believe this initiative can make a meaningful contribution to business growth, employment generation and the development of more competitive Sri Lankan enterprises.\u201d"
  },
