    "md5": "57235875baa758fcecd3f6d366302295",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1842,
    "chunk_text": "Aberdeen Group announces leadership transition at Ex-pack Corrugated Cartons\n\nAberdeen Group announced that Sattar Kassim will retire from the board of its listed subsidiary Ex-pack Corrugated Cartons PLC, with effect from November 18, 2026, relinquishing his position as Chairman from the same date.\n\nAt its meeting held on November 9, the board of Ex-pack resolved to appoint Thulci Aluwihare, an Independent, Non-Executive Director of the company, as Chairman of the board, with effect from November 18, 2026.\n\nKassim\u2019s retirement on his 70th birthday marks the close of a distinguished chapter. A founding figure of Aberdeen Group, he played a central role in shaping the group\u2019s strategic direction and building it into the diversified business it is today.\n\nDuring his tenure as Chairman, he steered Ex-pack onto a path of sustained profitability, strengthening its financial foundations for the future.\n\nUnder his leadership, Ex-pack also completed its initial public offering and listed on the Colombo Stock Exchange, a significant milestone for both the company and group.\n\nAberdeen Group extended its deep appreciation to Kassim for his vision, guidance and steadfast commitment to Ex-pack and for the strong foundation he leaves for the company\u2019s next phase of growth.\n\nThe group welcomed Aluwihare, Deputy Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd, who brings over 25 years of international experience across London, Melbourne and Colombo in mergers and acquisitions, public-private partnerships, transaction advisory and restructuring.\n\nAluwihare played a pivotal role in establishing Sri Lanka\u2019s first foreign-currency-designated, multi-services Special Economic Zone, working closely with the Presidential Secretariat as a member of the Colombo International Financial Centre Steering Committee Task Force."
  },
