    "md5": "cef2291cc4290a40d5a4a95a0bad749b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1884,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Solar introduces SL\u2019s 24/7 Renewable Energy Operations Centre\n\nHayleys Solar has introduced Sri Lanka\u2019s first dedicated 24/7 Renewable Energy Operations Centre (ROC), enabling continuous monitoring and performance management of renewable energy assets through a centralised digital platform.\n\nDesigned and technologically backed by Fentons Information Technology (FIT), the ICT arm of Hayleys Fentons, the ROC brings together renewable energy expertise and advanced digital technology to enhance operational efficiency across residential, commercial and industrial (C&I), and utility-scale solar, wind and battery energy storage projects.\n\nA key technological strength of the ROC is its ability to integrate multiple inverter brands and renewable energy projects into a single, centralised dashboard, eliminating the need to monitor individual systems separately. With thousands of solar panels and inverters currently in operation, the platform provides real-time visibility into energy generation, inverter performance, device connectivity, weather conditions and overall plant performance.\n\nThrough its intelligent alarm management system, the ROC can instantly detect and highlight operational abnormalities, including low energy generation, power outages, inverter faults and communication disconnections. These issues trigger immediate on-screen pop-up alerts, enabling operational teams to identify affected sites and prioritise corrective action.\n\nThe platform further minimises the need for manual intervention through automated monitoring and fault identification. An automated SMS alert mechanism will notify the engineer responsible for the affected location, enabling prompt action. Where physical intervention is required, the nearest available engineer can be assigned to inspect and resolve the issue, supporting faster response times and reduced downtime."
  },
