    "chunk_text": "The platform further minimises the need for manual intervention through automated monitoring and fault identification. An automated SMS alert mechanism will notify the engineer responsible for the affected location, enabling prompt action. Where physical intervention is required, the nearest available engineer can be assigned to inspect and resolve the issue, supporting faster response times and reduced downtime.\n\nCommenting on the initiative, Hasith Prematillake, Managing Director, Hayleys Fentons Limited said, \u201cAs a diversified organisation, Hayleys Fentons brings together deep expertise across multiple disciplines. The ROC demonstrates how we are combining the strengths of our Energy and ICT businesses to deliver more connected, responsive and efficient solutions, creating greater value and an enhanced experience for our customers.\u201d\n\nRoshane Perera, Deputy Managing Director \u2013 Energy, Hayleys Fentons Limited, stated, \u201cRenewable energy assets operate continuously, and effective monitoring must do the same. Through the ROC, we are strengthening our ability to identify issues instantly, minimise downtime and optimise asset performance through real-time intelligence and faster operational response.\u201d\n\nYoosoof Ihthisham, General Manager \u2013 FIT, added, \u201cThe ROC represents a significant step towards intelligent renewable energy management. By integrating diverse technologies into one platform and enabling automated alerts, advanced analytics and on-demand reporting, we are transforming complex operational data into actionable insights.\u201d\n\nLooking ahead, the second phase of the ROC will extend its capabilities beyond Hayleys Solar\u2019s existing customer portfolio, offering third-party renewable energy asset owners and operators access to its centralised monitoring and performance management services. This expansion aims to make advanced, technology-driven operational support more widely accessible across Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy sector."
  },
