    "chunk_text": "Peugeot and TotalEnergies extend 30-year global partnership to Sri Lanka\n\nPeugeot and TotalEnergies Lubricants are extending their global partnership of more than 30 years to Sri Lanka, through a Marketing and Technical Support Agreement signed on 27 October 2026 between their local partners: Energy Core Lanka (Pvt) Ltd (ECL), the authorised distributor of TotalEnergies Lubricants, and Carmart (Pvt) Ltd, the authorised distributor of Peugeot, as well as sister brand, Leapmotor.\n\nTotalEnergies Lubricants is Peugeot\u2019s recommended lubricant brand worldwide. Engineers from both companies work together from the earliest stages of engine and transmission design, formulating the first-fill lubricants in every new Peugeot, developed for smooth running, longer engine life, and lower fuel consumption and CO\u2082 emissions.\n\nThe relationship extends from the road to the track and to the next generation of mobility. TotalEnergies is the official motorsport partner of Peugeot Sport, co-developing the battery and specialist fluids behind Peugeot\u2019s hybrid Hypercar programme in the FIA World Endurance Championship, including the 24 Hours of Le Mans. The two companies are also working together on electric vehicles, batteries, low-carbon and bio-sourced fuels, and eco-designed lubricants.\n\nUnder the agreement, ECL will supply Carmart\u2019s Peugeot service network with TotalEnergies lubricants, including Quartz Ineo 5W-30, sourced from France and fully complying with Peugeot\u2019s stringent specifications. ECL will also train CARMART\u2019s technicians, and the two companies will run joint campaigns for Peugeot customers.\n\nFor Peugeot owners, it means their vehicles are serviced with the same products their engines were developed with. Carmart\u2019s Peugeot service and health check campaign, from 16 November to 18 December 2026 at Union Place, Colombo 2, offers fixed-price service packages using TotalEnergies lubricants."
