    "chunk_size_bytes": 1648,
    "chunk_text": "SPTDE signs contract to expand Sri Lanka\u2019s power transmission network\n\nThe National Transmission Network Service Provider (Private) Limited (NTNSP) and Shanghai Electric Power Transmission & Distribution Engineering Co., Ltd., (SPTDE) part of China\u2019s Shanghai Electric Group, signed an engineering, procurement and construction (EPC) contract recently to expand Sri Lanka\u2019s electricity transmission network. ComCorp will serve as Shanghai Electric\u2019s local Engineering partner, bringing nearly three decades of experience working with electricity utilities in Sri Lanka and the region.\n\nThe contract covers Package 2 of the Asian Development Bank-funded Power System Strengthening and Renewable Energy Integration Project (PSSREIP). The scope comprises the construction of a 78 km, 132 kV Matara - Hambantota transmission line, a 7.7 km double-circuit in-and-out connection to Homagama Grid Substation from the existing Horana -Padukka 132 kV transmission line, a 1.5 km single-circuit in-and-out connection to Mirigama Grid Substation from the existing New Habarana - Veyangoda 220 kV transmission line, and a 0.5 km in-and-out connection to Negombo Grid Substation from the existing Katunayake - Bolawatta 132 kV transmission line.\n\nThe new lines and connections are expected to increase the amount of electricity the network can carry and improve the reliability of supply. The work forms part of a wider effort to prepare Sri Lanka\u2019s grid for more wind and solar generation. As new generation comes online, expanding the transmission network helps carry electricity from where it is produced to where households and businesses need it."
  },
