    "chunk_text": "The new lines and connections are expected to increase the amount of electricity the network can carry and improve the reliability of supply. The work forms part of a wider effort to prepare Sri Lanka\u2019s grid for more wind and solar generation. As new generation comes online, expanding the transmission network helps carry electricity from where it is produced to where households and businesses need it.\n\nThe project pairs Shanghai Electric\u2019s experience delivering high-voltage infrastructure internationally with ComCorp\u2019s experience coordinating engineering work in Sri Lanka. That local experience is relevant to a package that spans a long-distance transmission corridor in the south and three separate grid connections. For ComCorp, the appointment builds on its work with international engineering companies serving electricity utilities in Sri Lanka and the region.\n\nNTNSP Chairman Nusith Kumaratunga and Chief Executive Officer Eng. N. S. Wettasinghe attended the signing alongside Director of Design Eng. Anuruddha Thilakarathna, Project Director Eng.S. W. Kumarawadu and Project Manager Eng.R. Jeewagan. Other senior NTNSP officials and engineers were present, together with representatives of SPTDE and ComCorp."
