    "chunk_size_bytes": 1743,
    "chunk_text": "CMA Sri Lanka to host Budget Highlights 2027 Forum on Monday\n\nThe Institute of Certified Management Accountants of Sri Lanka (CMA Sri Lanka) will host its annual Budget Highlights 2027 forum under the theme \u2018Beyond Stabilization: Building for Growth \u2013 Impact on Business, Economy and Society\u2019 on 16 November from 2.00 p.m. to 6.00 p.m. at the Crystal Ballroom, Lower Level, Taj Samudra, Colombo.\n\nThe forum will bring together leading economists, tax professionals, industry experts, policymakers and business leaders to examine the key proposals of Budget 2027 and their implications for Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery, business environment and future growth prospects.\n\nThe programme will commence with the welcome address by Prof. Lakshman R. Watawala, Founder President of CMA Sri Lanka. The keynote address will be delivered by Dr. W. A. Wijewardena, Former Deputy Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe technical presentations will cover several important areas, including Budget 2027 tax proposals, indirect taxation and VAT, the impact on pricing and cost of living, IMF reforms, economic recovery and debt repayment, achieving national export development plan, and the importance of cost accounting in improving industrial efficiency, productivity and competitiveness.\n\nThe forum will feature distinguished speakers, including Athula Ranaweera, Managing Partner of Ranaweera Associates; Suresh Perera, Principal \u2013 Tax & Regulatory, KPMG; Talal Rafi, Economist;\u00a0 Mangala Wijesinghe, Chairman of the Sri Lanka Export Development Board; Mahendra Jayasekera, Chairman of the CMA Sri Lanka Cost and Management Accounting Standards Board; and Mr. Felix Fernando, Chairman of the Joint Apparel Association Forum Sri Lanka."
