    "chunk_size_bytes": 885,
    "chunk_text": "The briefing also covered the health of bank balance sheets. The officials said the banking sector\u2019s Stage 3 nonperforming loan ratio had fallen to 8.8 percent, from 9.7 percent, while capital and liquidity remained above the regulatory requirements.\n\nThe Central Bank also imposed restrictions on dividend distributions, branch expansion and directors\u2019 remuneration at the bank.\n\nThe committee reviewed the illegal deposit-taking and financial scams that use AI-generated images and voices of public figures, including the Governor and Prime Minister. The Central Bank said it was coordinating with the telecommunications regulator, Sri Lanka CERT, police and Meta to counter such scams.\n\nThe lawmakers also discussed the regulation of virtual assets and cryptocurrencies, supervision of banking activities in Colombo Port City and the proposed consolidation of state-owned banks."
