    "chunk_text": "Dialog 3Q underlying profit rises 67% to Rs.10.2bn\n\nDialog Axiata PLC\u2019s group net profit rose 62 percent year-on-year (YoY) to Rs.9.2 billion in the September quarter, as data and home broadband drove the revenue growth, though the reported earnings fell 9 percent from the previous quarter, amid the unrealised foreign exchange losses.\n\nExcluding those losses, the underlying net profit rose 67 percent from a year earlier and 6 percent from the previous quarter to Rs.10.2 billion, the telecom operator said in its earnings release on Tuesday.\n\nThe group revenue increased 6 percent YoY and one percent quarter-on-quarter to Rs.48.5 billion. The earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation (EBITDA) rose 15 percent from a year earlier and one percent from the previous quarter to Rs.25.9 billion.\n\nAt company level, the quarterly net profit rose 41 percent YoY to Rs.6.4 billion, as the lower net finance costs more than offset the unrealised foreign exchange losses. Excluding the currency impact, the profit rose 50 percent to Rs.7.2 billion.\n\nFor the nine months ended September 30, the group net profit rose 92 percent to Rs.28.5 billion, helped by a higher EBITDA and lower net finance costs. The underlying net profit increased 82 percent to Rs.28.9 billion.\n\nThe nine-month revenue rose 8 percent to Rs.144.1 billion, with a growth across the mobile, fixed and digital pay television businesses. The EBITDA increased 20 percent to Rs.75.8 billion, while the EBITDA margin widened by 5.4 percentage points to 52.7 percent.\n\nDialog Broadband Networks\u2019 nine-month profit rose 46 percent to Rs.6.1 billion, supported by a higher EBITDA and lower depreciation and net finance costs.\n\nDialog Television earned Rs.400 million over the period, as the revenue rose 13 percent to Rs.11 billion, helped by the higher advertising sales."
