    "chunk_text": "The electric vehicle registrations rose 5.4 percent to 6,374, driven by the electric two-wheelers, which increased to 5,342, from 5,030. The electric motor car registrations fell to 345, from 495. The large-tractor registrations climbed 49.1 percent to 407.\n\nThe share of two-wheeler registrations financed rose to 59.9 percent, from 54.4 percent in September. For the three-wheelers, it increased to 48.9 percent, from 43.9 percent.\n\n\u201cThe passenger vehicle imports, however, have moderated considerably, declining from over US $ 200 million per month to below US $ 150 million,\u201d JB Securities CEO Murtaza Jafferjee said in the report.\n\nJafferjee attributed the slowdown to the easing pent-up demand, a weaker rupee, tighter credit conditions and higher border taxes, including a 50 percent surcharge on motor vehicle import duties.\n\nHe said softer passenger vehicle imports could weigh on tax collections, with the surcharge and higher rupee valuations potentially offsetting part of the impact."
