    "chunk_text": "Family thanks President for securing Anojan\u2019s release\n\nColombo, Nov. 12 (Daily Mirror) - Family members of Anojan Sivarasa, who had been sentenced to death in Saudi Arabia, have thanked President Anura Kumara Dissanayake for his intervention in securing his release and acquittal on all charges.\n\nSivarasa\u2019s family met the President at the Presidential Secretariat this morning (12) and expressed their gratitude for the efforts made to save his life and bring him back from the death sentence.\n\nDuring the meeting, President Dissanayake said it was his responsibility to stand up for Sri Lankan citizens wherever they were in the world.\n\nHe also acknowledged the support extended by the Government of Saudi Arabia and thanked all those who had worked towards securing Sivarasa\u2019s release, regardless of differences in ethnicity, religion or political affiliation.\n\nSivarasa\u2019s parents informed the President that their son was currently in good health.\n\nHis mother expressed particular appreciation to the President for intervening from the beginning to secure her son\u2019s release from the death sentence and clear him of all charges.\n\nShe also thanked Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath, Deputy Minister Arun Hemachandra, Sri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Saudi Arabia O.L. Ameer Ajwad and embassy officials, as well as the lawyers who travelled to Saudi Arabia to provide legal assistance.\n\nShe further appreciated all Sri Lankans who contributed to the efforts to secure her son\u2019s freedom.\n\nSocial activist Rajkumar Rajeevkanth also thanked the President for fulfilling the assurance he had given during their first meeting regarding efforts to secure Sivarasa\u2019s release.\n\nRajeevkanth revealed that Sivarasa\u2019s parents had suffered severe psychological distress during the same period following the execution of a Bangladeshi couple who had also been sentenced to death."
