    "chunk_size_bytes": 1913,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka calls for greater global investment in children at Paris Peace Forum\n\nColombo, Nov. 12 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Minister of Women and Child Affairs Saroja Savithri Paulraj has called for greater investment in children, stressing that their well-being should remain a global priority despite growing financial constraints.\n\nAddressing a special roundtable discussion titled \u201cMaking the Case for Investing in Children\u201d at the 9th Paris Peace Forum in Paris, France, the Minister said investments in children were essential responsibilities that could not be postponed.\n\nThe Minister represented Sri Lanka at the Forum held on November 10 and 11, where discussions focused on child protection and care, safe digital environments, child health and nutrition, and quality early childhood development.\n\nAddressing the gathering, she said Sri Lanka's vision for children was to create \u201cA Safer World for Children \u2013 A Creative Future Generation\u201d, as outlined in the country's National Policy Statement.\n\nShe stressed that every child, regardless of where they were born, deserved equal opportunities to survive, grow up healthy, receive an education and realise their full potential.\n\nThe Minister outlined three key areas in which Sri Lanka was making investments: ensuring equitable and quality early childhood care and development, strengthening child protection and psychosocial well-being, and ensuring the inclusion of all children while maximising their human potential.\n\nShe said investing in children was not merely a moral obligation but also a means of building a stronger economy, reducing the burden of unpaid care work on women and strengthening social cohesion.\n\nShe also highlighted the importance of partnerships among international organisations, development partners, the private sector, civil society and communities, noting that governments could not fulfil these responsibilities alone."
