    "chunk_text": "The President further announced plans to establish a re-export hub within BIA on a Build-Operate-Transfer (BOT) basis, with private sector participation, to develop the airport as an air cargo handling hub.\n\nMeanwhile, the Ratmalana International Airport will be developed to facilitate pilot training, domestic flights, business aviation and regional aviation.\n\nReferring to Mattala International Airport, the President said it had accumulated losses exceeding Rs. 70 billion since commencing flight operations in 2013. The airport was constructed with a loan of US$190 million, and its losses continued to increase annually.\n\nHe said Expressions of Interest (EOIs) had already been called and concluded to develop several areas of the airport in partnership with international companies.\n\nThe proposed investment areas include airport operations, data centres, food and catering services, and aircraft services and maintenance.\n\nSteps are now being taken to call for Requests for Proposals (RFPs) from the selected companies, with the Government expecting to select new investors within the next year."
  },
