    "chunk_text": "Budget 2027: Rs. 77 billion allocated for drinking water and sanitation projects\n\nNov 12 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has announced an allocation of Rs. 77 billion to expand drinking water supply and sanitation facilities across the country under Budget 2027.\n\nPresenting the Budget in Parliament today (12), the President said the Government aims to ensure an uninterrupted supply of clean drinking water while meeting the growing water requirements of households, businesses and industries.\n\nThe Government is also considering opportunities to attract private sector investment into the water supply sector.\n\nAs part of the programme, Rs. 5.19 billion has been allocated to commence 13 new water supply projects covering areas including Jaffna, Mannar, Mullaitivu, Vavuniya, Nagadeepa, Valachchenai and Kotte.\n\nAmong the major projects announced is the Greater Kilinochchi Water Supply Project, which will receive Rs. 1.8 billion in 2027. The project has an estimated total cost of Rs. 41.14 billion and will cover the Karachchi, Kandavalai, Poonakary and Pachchilaipalli Divisional Secretariat divisions.\n\nThe Greater Galle City Water Supply Project, estimated to cost Rs. 37.501 billion, will receive Rs. 3 billion to commence construction.\n\nMeanwhile, Rs. 1.8 billion has been allocated to begin the Kundasale-Haragama Water Supply Project, which has an estimated cost of Rs. 34.368 billion.\n\nA further Rs. 1 billion has been allocated to commence the Eheliyagoda Water Supply Project, estimated to cost Rs. 4.775 billion.\n\nOther projects include the Haldummulla-Beragala Water Supply Project, which will receive Rs. 700 million towards its estimated cost of Rs. 3.262 billion, and the Yatimahana-Ma Oya Water Supply Project, for which Rs. 300 million has been allocated to begin work in 2027. The latter has an estimated total cost of Rs. 22.158 billion.\n\nRs. 1 billion to address drinking water issues in Jaffna and Vanni"
