    "chunk_size_bytes": 1562,
    "chunk_text": "Other projects include the Haldummulla-Beragala Water Supply Project, which will receive Rs. 700 million towards its estimated cost of Rs. 3.262 billion, and the Yatimahana-Ma Oya Water Supply Project, for which Rs. 300 million has been allocated to begin work in 2027. The latter has an estimated total cost of Rs. 22.158 billion.\n\nRs. 1 billion to address drinking water issues in Jaffna and Vanni\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 1 billion has been proposed to gradually address these issues and improve access to safe drinking water in the affected areas.\n\nThe Government has allocated a further Rs. 12 billion for projects aimed at increasing the capacity of existing drinking water schemes, expanding distribution networks and improving sanitation facilities.\n\nIn addition, Rs. 2 billion has been allocated to improve community-based water supply schemes across the country.\n\nAnother Rs. 250 million has been earmarked for feasibility studies to identify solutions to meet the water requirements of industrial and commercial activities in Kuliyapitiya, Pannala, Bingiriya, Udubaddawa, Trincomalee and Gampola-Jayamalapura.\n\nMeanwhile, Rs. 1.74 billion has been allocated for wastewater management projects in Ella, Moratuwa and Ekala.\n\nThe projects aim to improve sanitation facilities and establish more systematic wastewater management services.\n\nThe proposals form part of the Government's wider investment programme under Budget 2027 to strengthen water infrastructure, improve access to safe drinking water and support future industrial and economic development."
