    "chunk_text": "Budget 2027: President Anura Kumara Dissanayake\u2019s Full Budget Speech (Download)\n\nNov 12 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake presented Sri Lanka\u2019s Budget 2027 in Parliament, outlining the Government\u2019s economic priorities, proposed tax reforms, public sector salary increases and development plans for the year ahead.\n\nThe Budget includes several key proposals, including an increase in the personal income tax-free threshold, the removal of VAT on school exercise books and printed books, higher allowances for public sector employees and additional financial relief for pensioners.\n\nThe President also outlined plans for investments in infrastructure, education, healthcare, agriculture, tourism, digital transformation and the promotion of new economic opportunities.\n\nBudget 2027 is the third Budget presented by the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) Government since assuming office.\n\nThe full Budget Speech, including detailed policy proposals, financial allocations and annexures, is available to read and download below."
