    "description": "Rs. 2,500 monthly allowance for pensioners retiring between 2020 and 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/Rs-2-500-monthly-allowance-for-pensioners-retiring-between-2020-and-2024/108-354795",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794487535.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-12-dailymirrorlk-30a7db08-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c0c64da70e9b5e0ef09dc956a4fa5ad4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1720,
    "chunk_text": "Rs. 2,500 monthly allowance for pensioners retiring between 2020 and 2024\n\nColombo, Nov. 12 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Pensioners who retired between 2020 and 2024 will receive a monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500 from July 1, 2027, until the proposed pension revision under the 2025 basic salary structure is implemented, President Anura Kumara Dissanayake announced in his 2027 Budget.\n\nThe Government is implementing a phased pension revision programme to address disparities in pensions received by retired public servants who retired at different times.\n\nUnder the first Budget presented in 2025, the Government introduced a three-phase programme to convert the pensions of public servants who retired before 2020 to the 2020 basic salary scale. The first two phases have already been completed, while the final phase is scheduled for 2027.\n\nThe Government also plans to gradually address disparities between pensioners who retired before 2025 and those who retired in or after 2025 following the introduction of the new basic salary structure in 2025.\n\nThe next pension revision, based on the 2025 basic salary structure, is expected to begin with the 2028 Budget and will be implemented in several phases.\n\nOnce the revised pensions are implemented and payments commence, the proposed monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500 for pensioners who retired between 2020 and 2024 will be discontinued.\n\nThese measures will also apply to public sector pensioners whose salaries were determined under Department of Management Services Circulars 02/2025, 03/2025, 04/2025 and 05/2025.\n\nThe Government said the measures aim to gradually reduce pension disparities while ensuring a fair and financially sustainable pension system."
  },
