    "chunk_text": "The Government also expects to maintain public investment above 4 per cent of GDP from 2027 onwards.\n\nThe President said the Government would continue to strengthen public finances, manage debt and improve the efficiency of public institutions.\n\nA considerable allocation has been made for improving school education, higher education and vocational training.\n\nThe monthly allowance paid to trainee teachers at Colleges of Education will be increased from Rs. 10,500 to Rs. 20,000 with effect from April 2027.\n\nThe Government has allocated Rs. 3,000 million for the digital transformation of provincial schools. The five-year programme aims to provide computers, smart boards, internet facilities and other digital learning equipment to schools.\n\nThe Government expects to provide reliable internet connections to the remaining 750 secondary schools that have not yet received them.\n\nA further Rs. 35,000 million has been allocated for digitalisation, teacher training and infrastructure development, including improvements to teachers' colleges, National Colleges of Education, school buildings and laboratories.\n\nThe academic allowance paid to university lecturers will be increased by Rs. 25,000, with 50 per cent of the increase scheduled to be paid from July 2027 and the remaining amount from July 2028.\n\nPayments to visiting lecturers will also be increased threefold, from Rs. 1,500 to Rs. 4,500 per hour.\n\nThe daily allowance for student monks at Pirivenas will increase from Rs. 15 to Rs. 50, while the allowance for lay students will rise from Rs. 5 to Rs. 25.\n\nThe annual allowance for Dhamma School teachers will increase from Rs. 7,500 to Rs. 12,500.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 11 billion for the development of vocational education and training facilities, including the modernisation of 25 selected Technical Colleges.\n\nA total capital allocation of Rs. 131 billion has been made to maintain and improve public healthcare services."
  },
