    "chunk_text": "The Government has also allocated Rs. 11 billion for the development of vocational education and training facilities, including the modernisation of 25 selected Technical Colleges.\n\nA total capital allocation of Rs. 131 billion has been made to maintain and improve public healthcare services.\n\nAn additional Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated for medical equipment, while Rs. 3,000 million has been allocated for purchasing ambulances.\n\nThe Government also plans to establish 1,000 Arogya Wellness Centres between 2027 and 2029, with an investment of Rs. 17,440 million. An allocation of Rs. 3,600 million has been made for 2027.\n\nThese centres are expected to provide healthcare services closer to communities, particularly in areas where access to hospitals is limited.\n\nThe Thambuttegama Base Hospital will receive Rs. 300 million to develop a modern Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit.\n\nThe Government also plans to introduce robotic technology for surgical procedures.\n\nAllowances paid to medical officers will increase by Rs. 25,000, from Rs. 70,000 to Rs. 95,000. Special duty allowances for nursing officers and paramedical staff will also be increased from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 12,000.\n\nThe increases will be implemented in two stages, with 50 per cent being paid from July 2027 and the balance in 2028.\n\nThe Government has allocated Rs. 230 billion for social protection programmes, including the continuation of Aswesuma benefits for poor and extremely poor families.\n\nThe monthly allowance for kidney patients and persons with disabilities will be increased from Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 12,500.\n\nA further Rs. 25,000 million has been allocated for an island-wide rural development programme under the Praja Shakthi National Movement, with priority given to poverty reduction.\n\nAnother Rs. 4,500 million has been allocated to empower selected families through programmes aimed at helping them improve their economic conditions."
