    "chunk_text": "A further Rs. 25,000 million has been allocated for an island-wide rural development programme under the Praja Shakthi National Movement, with priority given to poverty reduction.\n\nAnother Rs. 4,500 million has been allocated to empower selected families through programmes aimed at helping them improve their economic conditions.\n\nThe Government has proposed a monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500 for public sector pensioners who retired between 2020 and 2024.\n\nThe payment will begin on July 1, 2027, and continue until the planned pension revision under the new 2025 basic salary structure is implemented.\n\nThe final phase of the pension revision programme for public servants who retired before 2020 will also be implemented in 2027.\n\nSeveral allowances paid to public sector employees will be revised, including allowances for health workers, field officers, Grama Niladharis, members of the armed forces, police personnel and judicial staff.\n\nThe monthly transport allowance for eligible public officers who use their private vehicles for official duties will increase from Rs. 50,000 to Rs. 100,000.\n\nThe Government has allocated Rs. 251 billion for highway, expressway and railway development through the Budget. Including additional proposals and reconstruction funding, total spending on these sectors is expected to reach Rs. 487 billion.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 30,000 million has been made for the Kurunegala-Galewela section of the Central Expressway, while Rs. 27,000 million has been allocated for the first phase of the Ruwanpura Expressway from Kahathuduwa to Ingiriya.\n\nAnother Rs. 53,450 million has been allocated to complete the Kadawatha-Mirigama section of the Central Expressway by September 2028.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 4,500 million to complete the Pothuhera-Rambukkana section by May 2027.\n\nA further Rs. 23,050 million has been allocated for the Rambukkana-Galagedara section."
