    "chunk_text": "Another Rs. 53,450 million has been allocated to complete the Kadawatha-Mirigama section of the Central Expressway by September 2028.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 4,500 million to complete the Pothuhera-Rambukkana section by May 2027.\n\nA further Rs. 23,050 million has been allocated for the Rambukkana-Galagedara section.\n\nThe Government also plans to invest Rs. 80 billion in railway electrification.\n\nThe first phase will cover the Kelani Valley railway line from Maradana to Homagama, the Main Line from Maradana to Ragama and the Coastal Line from Maradana to Panadura.\n\nThe Government also plans to purchase five new trains and allocate Rs. 2,000 million to renovate railway stations.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 95 billion has been made to modernise railway and passenger bus services, improve connections between transport networks and promote sustainable public transport.\n\nThe Metro Bus service, currently operating around Colombo, is expected to be extended to Kandy, Galle and Jaffna.\n\nThe Government plans to introduce 100 electric buses received as a donation from China. An allocation of Rs. 4,500 million has been made for the construction of depots, charging facilities and training.\n\nAnother Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated to purchase 250 small buses for rural and upcountry areas.\n\nThe Government also plans to introduce improved digital systems for vehicle registration, ownership transfers and road safety.\n\nThe Budget places emphasis on increasing agricultural production, improving rural livelihoods and strengthening food security.\n\nA total of Rs. 77 billion has been allocated for irrigation development, including the rehabilitation of damaged irrigation systems and the implementation of new projects.\n\nThe Government has allocated Rs. 21 billion for the rehabilitation of tank systems, minor irrigation infrastructure and agricultural roads damaged by Cyclone Ditwah."
