    "chunk_text": "A total of Rs. 77 billion has been allocated for irrigation development, including the rehabilitation of damaged irrigation systems and the implementation of new projects.\n\nThe Government has allocated Rs. 21 billion for the rehabilitation of tank systems, minor irrigation infrastructure and agricultural roads damaged by Cyclone Ditwah.\n\nA further Rs. 15 billion has been allocated for the maintenance and development of minor irrigation systems.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 5,000 million for the development of the Wayamba Canal Project and other irrigation improvements.\n\nIn the fisheries sector, Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated for the construction of fisheries anchorages and the upgrading of the Pesalai Fisheries Harbour.\n\nAnother Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated to improve the Peliyagoda Fish Market, while Rs. 500 million has been allocated for the renovation of the North Sea Fishing Net Factory.\n\nThe Government has also proposed financial assistance for goat farming, aquaculture and fisheries-related businesses.\n\nA sum of Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated for fertiliser for tea cultivation and Rs. 1,000 million for fertiliser for rubber cultivation.\n\nThe Government plans to strengthen local industries and attract more investment to create employment and increase exports.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 4,000 million has been made for the development of the Valachchenai Industrial Estate, feasibility studies for the proposed Puliyankulam Industrial Estate and further development of industrial estates, including Ingiriya, Dambulla, Raigama-Millaniya and Katunayake.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 67,687 million for interest subsidies and refinancing facilities for micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs).\n\nThrough these schemes, the Government expects to provide approximately Rs. 174 billion in concessionary loans to entrepreneurs through State and private banks."
