    "chunk_text": "The Government has also allocated Rs. 67,687 million for interest subsidies and refinancing facilities for micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs).\n\nThrough these schemes, the Government expects to provide approximately Rs. 174 billion in concessionary loans to entrepreneurs through State and private banks.\n\nA Sri Lanka-European Union Sustainable Trade and Economic Integration Project will be implemented with a grant of Rs. 3,430 million between 2027 and 2030 to improve export competitiveness and diversify exports.\n\nThe Budget proposes several measures to expand the digital economy and improve the use of technology in public services.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 10,000 million has been proposed for digital economy development programmes.\n\nThese include establishing a National Artificial Intelligence Centre of Excellence, improving digital government services, expanding the Lanka Government Cloud and strengthening digital payment systems.\n\nThe Government also plans to provide broadband vouchers to 750,000 selected school students.\n\nA further Rs. 9,000 million has been allocated through the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission to expand broadband coverage under the Gamata Sannivedanaya programme.\n\nThe programme aims to complete 573 new telecommunications towers by 2028.\n\nThe Government has also allocated Rs. 23,800 million for research and development activities in 2027.\n\nThe Government plans to increase the contribution of renewable energy to the national electricity supply and strengthen the electricity transmission network.\n\nThe share of renewable energy in installed electricity generation capacity is expected to increase from around 62 per cent to 69 per cent by 2029.\n\nA subsidy of Rs. 25,000 per kilowatt of battery storage capacity will be provided to domestic consumers installing new rooftop solar systems, subject to a maximum payment of Rs. 250,000.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 3,500 million has been made for this programme."
