    "chunk_text": "A subsidy of Rs. 25,000 per kilowatt of battery storage capacity will be provided to domestic consumers installing new rooftop solar systems, subject to a maximum payment of Rs. 250,000.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 3,500 million has been made for this programme.\n\nThe programme to expand wind power generation is expected to add 370 MW by 2029, including 50 MW in 2027.\n\nFloating solar panels are also planned for 10 reservoirs, with the potential to generate around 500 MW of electricity.\n\nThe Government plans to strengthen Sri Lanka's position as a regional shipping and logistics hub by expanding port capacity and related services.\n\nThe Colombo Port is expected to increase its shipping capacity to more than 30 million twenty-foot equivalent units by 2040.\n\nPlans include developing the West Terminal II, studying the development of the Colombo North Port and establishing a logistics centre through a public-private partnership.\n\nThe Government also plans to increase bunkering capacity at the Port of Colombo by 50,000 metric tons with private sector participation.\n\nThe development of the Trincomalee Port as a fuel storage and energy hub will also receive attention.\n\nAn allocation of Rs. 100 million has been made to improve passenger facilities at the Sigiriya Domestic Airport, while Rs. 200 million has been allocated to improve access roads to the Katunayake Airport and conduct a feasibility study on additional passenger facilities.\n\nSeveral housing programmes have been included in the Budget to support low-income families, displaced people and those affected by disasters.\n\nRs. 5,000 million has been allocated to complete houses that were partially constructed under previous housing programmes.\n\nAnother Rs. 4,000 million has been allocated for houses for displaced people in the Northern and Eastern provinces."
