    "chunk_text": "Budget 2027 spending: where Sri Lanka\u2019s money goes\n\nThe 2027 budget sets aside Rs. 2,000 billion for public investment in 2027, or 5.12% of GDP, including Cyclone Ditwah rebuilding. Highways, expressways and railways receive Rs. 251 billion; social protection, including Aswesuma, Rs. 230 billion, and the first phase of suburban rail electrification Rs. 80 billion.\n\nThe speech also announces 73 new spending proposals worth Rs. 363 billion, with transport taking the largest share. A further Rs. 260 billion is set aside separately to finish rebuilding after the cyclone.\n\nThe Daily Mirror used AI to turn the 367-page Budget Speech into this interactive dashboard and checked every figure against the official document. Filter the allocations by theme, or tap a sector to see every new proposal in it.\n\nThe largest allocations, the 73 new spending proposals and the separate plan to finish rebuilding after Cyclone Ditwah.\n\nAll figures from the official Budget Speech 2027, Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development\n\nCapital spending of Rs. 2,000 billion is allocated for 2027: Rs. 1,750 billion in the Budget and Rs. 250 billion more through the Ditwah Supplementary Estimate. That is 5.12% of GDP.\n\nAllocations named in the Budget Speech, in Rs. billion. Pick a theme to narrow the list. Some headings overlap (rail appears under both transport and highways), so these should not be added together.\n\nAllRoads, rail & transportPeople & servicesFarming & waterBusiness & digital\n\nPlus Rs. 90 bn from the Ditwah estimate for damaged roads, rail and bridges\n\nThird and final phase of the revision begun in the 2025 Budget\n\nRs. 55 bn rural roads, Rs. 20 bn provincial roads, Rs. 5.5 bn rural bridges, plus district funds\n\nKelani Valley, Main and Coastal lines. Whole programme: over Rs. 1,200 bn\n\nAim: lift plantation exports from USD 3 bn to USD 5 bn by 2030\n\nSeparate from the main Budget and financed from the available cash buffer"
