    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka women dominate Emerging Nations opener as Pakistan hold test advantage\n\nGunaratne and Perera Power Sri Lanka Women to Dominant Victory\n\nNOV.12 (Mirror Sports) - Sri Lanka made an impressive start to their ICC Women's Emerging Nations Trophy 2026 campaign, securing a convincing 10-wicket victory over Ireland in their opening Group A fixture in Ajman.\n\nAfter winning the toss and bowling first, Sri Lanka restricted Ireland to 105 for nine in 20 overs, with Sathya Sandeepani and Kaveesha Dilhari leading the bowling effort with three wickets each.\n\nIreland had reached 84 for three before losing six wickets for just 18 runs, struggling to recover against Sri Lanka's disciplined attack.\n\nIn reply, Vishmi Gunaratne and Hasini Perera produced an outstanding batting display, scoring unbeaten half-centuries to guide Sri Lanka home without losing a wicket.\n\nBoth batters finished on 53 not out, sharing an unbroken 110-run opening partnership as Sri Lanka reached 106 without loss in just 13 overs, sealing victory with seven overs to spare.\n\nSri Lanka v Ireland, Karwan Sports Club Cricket Ground, Ajman, UAE\n\nIreland 105/9 in 20 overs (Louise Little 28, Amy Hunter 21; Sathya Sandeepani 3/9, Kaveesha Dilhari 3/20)\n\nSri Lanka 110/0 in 13 overs (Vishmi Gunaratne 53 not out, Hasini Perera 53 not out)\n\nPapua New Guinea v Scotland, Seven Districts Sports Club, Ajman, UAE\n\nPapua New Guinea 93 all out in 20 overs (Pauke Siaka 24, Tanya Ruma 22; Katherine Fraser 3/10, Kirstie Gordon 2/15)\n\nScotland 95/3 in 13.1 overs (Katherine Fraser 45, Kathryn Bryce 14; Hane Tau 1/8, Pauke Siaka 1/16)\n\nPakistan v Bangladesh, Karwan Sports Club Cricket Ground, Ajman, UAE\n\nBangladesh 108/9 in 20 overs (Nigar Sultana 27, Shorna Akter 21 not out; Tuba Hassan 3/26, Nashra Sundhu 2/13)\n\nPakistan 112/2 in 15.5 overs (Sadaf Shamas 37, Muneeba Ali 31 not out; Sobhana Mostary 1/4, Shorna Akter 1/15)\n\nThailand 136/2 in 20 overs (Natthakan Chantham 55, Nannapat Khoncharoenkai 54 not out; Heather Siegers 2/15)"
