    "md5": "c5c21dcca12594d986f1e2b0a167f8f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1058,
    "chunk_text": "Yoshitha trial adjourned to  26 Nov. as accused cites ill health\n\nThe Colombo High Court yesterday postponed further proceedings in the money laundering case against Yoshitha Rajapaksa to 26 November, after the accused failed to appear citing a back ailment.\n\nHigh Court Judge Udesh Ranatunga fixed the new date for the trial to resume.\n\nRajapaksa is charged under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act with acquiring assets through unlawful means.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Sampath Mendis, appearing for the accused, told Court his client was unwell with a back-related condition and could not attend. He tendered a medical certificate in support.\n\nDeputy Solicitor General Janaka Bandara, appearing for the prosecution, said the State had hoped to wrap up its case yesterday. Only three prosecution witnesses remain, he said, and all three would be summoned for the next hearing.\n\nThe Attorney General filed the case, alleging Rajapaksa violated the money laundering law by spending over Rs. 730 million to buy five parcels of land in Dehiwala and Ratmalana."
