    "md5": "6b21cd482d0e82e4984ff34db1d0e5c7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 950,
    "chunk_text": "The Committee also discussed the technology for converting fuel vehicles to electric, the need for training programs, and standards and regulatory mechanisms to ensure the safety of converted vehicles.\n\nOn the Inventors Commission, the Committee reviewed its electric fencing projects aimed at curbing the wild elephant threat, the setting up of university-affiliated incubation centres, and plans to promote innovation through digital platforms. Officials also said three of the four electric fencing projects implemented so far were operating successfully.\n\nMembers also discussed a proposal to amend the Intellectual Property Act to introduce a \u201cPetty Patent system,\u201d intended to protect inventors\u2019 rights and speed up the commercialisation of inventions.\n\nMPs Lasith Bashana Gamage, Chathura Galappaththi, Thanura Dissanayake, Hasara Liyanage and Chandima Hettiarachchi attended, along with officials of the Science and Technology Ministry."
