    "description": "JXG, Ceylon Chamber launch new initiative to support entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/JXG-Ceylon-Chamber-launch-new-initiative-to-support-entrepreneurs/34-800039",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1794524526.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d32209867eeb3bb98ef2f0d7aeb424a9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "JXG, Ceylon Chamber launch new initiative to support entrepreneurs\n\nFrom left: Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Senior Assistant Secretary General Manori Dissanayaka , Lead Consultant\u00a0Dr. Nirmal De Silva, Secretary General/CEO Shiran Fernando, Chairperson Krishan Balendra,\u00a0 JXG Founder and Chairman Emeritus C.T.A Schaffter, JXG Managing Director/Group CEO Ramesh Schaffter, Deputy CEO Dilshan Wirasekara and Chief Marketing Officer Gamika De Silva \u2013 Pic by Shehan Gunasekera\n\nNational program BREAKTHROUGH targets promising businesses across all nine provinces\n\nIndividual funding allocations range from Rs. 1 m to Rs. 5 m\n\nSelected businesses to receive 12 months of mentoring and professional support\n\nJanashakthi Group (JXG) and the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce have launched BREAKTHROUGH, a national entrepreneur development program aimed at identifying and supporting high-potential businesses across Sri Lanka through funding and business development support.\n\nThe program will cover all nine provinces and focus on two categories of applicants: existing businesses, including micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs), and startups operating in the manufacturing and services sectors.\n\nA total of Rs. 70 million will be awarded to 20 selected businesses, with individual grants ranging from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 5 million. Applications will remain open\u00a0 until 20 January 2027.\n\nJXG Founder and Chairman Emeritus C.T.A. Schaffter said that the initiative seeks to help Sri Lankan entrepreneurs strengthen their businesses, expand their operations and realise their commercial potential. The launch comes as Sri Lanka seeks to accelerate private-sector growth, create employment opportunities and build more competitive enterprises. While several Sri Lankan companies have grown into globally recognised businesses, many entrepreneurs still face challenges in scaling their operations and accessing growth opportunities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f",
    "num": "dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f",
    "date_str": "2026-11-13",
    "description": "JXG, Ceylon Chamber launch new initiative to support entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/JXG-Ceylon-Chamber-launch-new-initiative-to-support-entrepreneurs/34-800039",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1794524526.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9a13db5c495e659a07ca22589b3457ce",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1829,
    "chunk_text": "JXG Founder and Chairman Emeritus C.T.A. Schaffter said that the initiative seeks to help Sri Lankan entrepreneurs strengthen their businesses, expand their operations and realise their commercial potential. The launch comes as Sri Lanka seeks to accelerate private-sector growth, create employment opportunities and build more competitive enterprises. While several Sri Lankan companies have grown into globally recognised businesses, many entrepreneurs still face challenges in scaling their operations and accessing growth opportunities.\n\nJXG Managing Director and Group CEO Ramesh Schaffter said the initiative was designed to provide entrepreneurs with practical support rather than simply recognise achievement.\n\n\u201cDo not count this as another awards ceremony. BREAKTHROUGH is about helping entrepreneurs build stronger businesses and equipping them with the resources, expertise and guidance needed to take the next step,\u201d he said.\n\nReflecting on JXG\u2019s legacy, he said successful businesses are often built by people willing to pursue opportunities beyond familiar boundaries and take calculated risks. He pointed to companies such as Expolanka, Virtusa and Vega Innovations as examples of Sri Lankan enterprises that began on a small scale before growing into significant ventures.\n\nSchaffter said Sri Lanka has entrepreneurs with the ability to innovate, create jobs and contribute to economic development, and that JXG was committed to sharing its experience and professional expertise to help more local businesses realise that potential.\n\nThe initiative combines JXG\u2019s experience in building and managing businesses with the Ceylon Chamber\u2019s extensive network and institutional reach. The Chamber has also invited ecosystem partners to contribute expertise and resources to strengthen the program\u2019s impact."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f",
    "num": "dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f",
    "date_str": "2026-11-13",
    "description": "JXG, Ceylon Chamber launch new initiative to support entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/JXG-Ceylon-Chamber-launch-new-initiative-to-support-entrepreneurs/34-800039",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1794524526.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-fa7b6f1f-0002",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "456298bb9f87eea2d1580a377ce1fe34",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "The initiative combines JXG\u2019s experience in building and managing businesses with the Ceylon Chamber\u2019s extensive network and institutional reach. The Chamber has also invited ecosystem partners to contribute expertise and resources to strengthen the program\u2019s impact.\n\nHe welcomed the partnership with JXG and said BREAKTHROUGH would provide a structured platform to identify promising enterprises and support their development through financial assistance and year-long professional guidance.\n\n\u201cWe believe this initiative can make a meaningful contribution to business growth, employment generation and the development of more competitive Sri Lankan enterprises,\u201d Fernando said.\n\nSpeaking about the selection process, he said it will begin with provincial-level assessments, followed by workshops, mentoring and business development sessions for shortlisted applicants.\n\nFinal selections will be made by an expert panel based on business viability, innovation, scalability, sustainability, ethical practices and potential economic and community impact.\n\nFunding allocations will be determined according to each business\u2019s stage of development, growth objectives and funding requirements. Beyond the grants, the 20 selected businesses will participate in a structured 12-month post-award development program, gaining access to mentoring, investor networks, banking and insurance support, professional expertise and quarterly progress reviews.\n\nJXG\u2019s senior leadership and professionals from across the Group will contribute expertise in finance, human resources, information technology, marketing and legal services to help participating businesses strengthen governance, improve decision-making and prepare for sustainable growth.\n\nThrough BREAKTHROUGH, JXG and the Ceylon Chamber aim to make business development opportunities more accessible to entrepreneurs across the country and help promising enterprises translate ambition into long-term commercial success."
  },
