    "chunk_text": "Liberty Lands and Developments Chairman and Managing Director Imthiaz J. Cader said: \u201cThe foundation of our business was built on my father\u2019s belief that success must come through honesty, hard work and the trust of the people we serve. As the second generation, our responsibility was not only to preserve what he established, but to strengthen the business and prepare it for the future. We have navigated many challenges over the decades, but our commitment to quality, integrity and long-term value has remained unchanged. Today, it is encouraging to see the next generation taking this legacy forward, introducing new ideas and expanding into sectors that contribute to the lives of Sri Lankans.\u201d\n\nThe Group\u2019s origins date back to 1955, when the late Jabir A. Cader established the iconic Liberty Cinema, laying the foundation for a business built on integrity, innovation and customer trust. Under the second-generation leadership of Imthiaz J. Cader, the business navigated significant changes in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and entertainment landscape, preserving its cinema heritage while establishing a stronger foundation for future expansion. His leadership was instrumental in the formal establishment of Liberty Lands and Developments in 1995, bringing its growing business interests under a common corporate structure. Across three generations, the Cader family has continued to build on this legacy, identifying opportunities to introduce new experiences to the Sri Lankan market.\n\nToday, LLD\u2019s entertainment presence is reflected through Scope Cinemas, which has transformed the local moviegoing experience by introducing premium cinema formats, advanced screening technologies and Sri Lanka\u2019s first IMAX theatre. Complementing this, Liberty Cinemas and Next Frame Global continue to strengthen the Group\u2019s involvement in international film distribution, connecting Sri Lankan audiences with major Hollywood studios and global releases."
