    "chunk_size_bytes": 1790,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s $ 5 b ICT/BPM export target by 2030 under spotlight\n\nEDB and Digital Economy Ministry strengthen collaboration to achieve growth ambitions\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s aim to achieve its $ 5 billion ICT/BPM exports in terms of the National Export Development Plan (NEDP) 2026\u20132030 came under spotlight recently, at a high-level review involving the Export Development Board (EDB) and the Digital Economy Ministry officials.\n\nThe progress and challenges of Sri Lanka thus far on implementing the NEDP was discussed focusing on strengthening the contribution of the ICT/BPM sector towards achieving the country\u2019s export growth ambitions.\n\nThe meeting was chaired by Digital Economy Deputy Minister Eng. Eranga Weeraratne, Digital Economy Ministry Secretary G. G. S. C. Roshan, Chief Adviser to the President on Digital Economy and Information and Communication Technology Agency (ICTA) Chairman Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, EDB Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe, Director General Erandika Dissanayake, EDB Additional Director General-Development Kumudinie Mudalige, and senior officials of GovTech and the EDB.\n\nThe NEDP 2026\u20132030, formulated by the EDB under the guidance of the Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry with technical assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), serves as Sri Lanka\u2019s national framework for advancing export development. The Plan sets an ambitious target of increasing total exports to $ 36 billion by 2030, including a dedicated target of $ 5 billion from digital products and services.\n\nThe discussion focused on identifying strategic interventions and strengthening the role of the Digital Economy Ministry and its affiliated institutions, including GovTech, as lead implementing agencies responsible for delivering key actions under the NEDP."
  },
