    "chunk_size_bytes": 1265,
    "chunk_text": "The discussion focused on identifying strategic interventions and strengthening the role of the Digital Economy Ministry and its affiliated institutions, including GovTech, as lead implementing agencies responsible for delivering key actions under the NEDP.\n\nThe discussion also highlighted the importance of introducing mandatory registration for exporters, and strengthening the inclusion of services in bilateral and regional trade agreements to improve international market access.\n\nThe meeting underscored the importance of strong institutional leadership, high-level policy intervention and coordinated action among relevant government institutions to accelerate the implementation of these strategic initiatives. The collaboration between the EDB, Digital Economy Ministry, GovTech and other relevant stakeholders is expected to play a pivotal role in strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy and expanding its footprint in international markets.\n\nThe EDB continues to engage with key Ministries and State agencies to facilitate the implementation of the NEDP 2026\u20132030, ensuring stronger inter-agency coordination, effective implementation of sectoral priorities and collective progress towards achieving national export target of $ 36 billion by 2030."
