    "chunk_size_bytes": 1664,
    "chunk_text": "Aitken Spence records strong 1H performance with PBT up 71%\n\nDrawing on the strength of its diversified portfolio, Aitken Spence PLC said yesterday it\u00a0 recorded a Profit Before Tax (PBT) of Rs. 2.8 billion for the six months ended 30 September 2026, an increase of 71.4% over the corresponding period of the previous financial year.\n\nEarnings before interest expenses, tax, depreciation and amortisation (EBITDA) increased by 20.6% to Rs. 10.1 billion. Furthermore, the Group\u2019s revenue for the period amounted to Rs. 41.7 billion, while the Profit After Tax (PAT) recorded a 229% increase to Rs. 1.4 billion.\n\nThe Maritime and Freight Logistics sector remained a key contributor to Group earnings, recording PBT of Rs. 3.3 billion while the sector\u2019s revenue saw a 20% increase to Rs. 9.5 billion. The performance was supported by stronger contributions across the maritime, integrated container operations and freight businesses, driven by higher volumes, improved freight rates and favourable market conditions. Both local and overseas airline segments fared well. The bunkering operation recorded a significant increase in profits during the period supported by higher oil prices. Overseas port operations\u00a0 reported improved profitability with increased domestic and transshipment throughput.\n\nThe Tourism sector recorded revenue of Rs. 26 billion during the period, while the sector result, a loss of Rs. 1.6 billion, was impacted by occupancy pressures and higher operating costs in the Maldives. Improved room rates provided some support, alongside stronger margins in Sri Lanka and growth in passenger volumes and contribution at Aitken Spence Travels."
  },
