    "chunk_text": "The Tourism sector recorded revenue of Rs. 26 billion during the period, while the sector result, a loss of Rs. 1.6 billion, was impacted by occupancy pressures and higher operating costs in the Maldives. Improved room rates provided some support, alongside stronger margins in Sri Lanka and growth in passenger volumes and contribution at Aitken Spence Travels.\n\nThe Services sector recorded a PBT of Rs. 1.5 billion with a noteworthy increase of 179% and alongside a revenue of Rs. 998 million. The performance during the quarter was supported by Group\u2019s equity-accounted Port City BPO venture which reported strong growth and gains from the disposal of an investment property during the period.\n\nIn a statement Aitken Spence said beyond financial performance, the Group continued to advance its sustainability strategy during the first half of the year prioritising impact control over energy, water, emissions, effluents, solid waste, resource and land use and ecosystem conservation. In addition to the Group\u2019s effort to reduce direct emissions, a total of 97,994 MT metric tonnes of municipal solid waste was repurposed from the western province through the Group\u2019s waste-to-energy operations, continuing the Group\u2019s systemic contribution to keeping our cities clean. At other operations, 29,272 cubic meters (m3) of rainwater was harvested to support water security efforts. The Group continued to strengthen the systems and processes supporting its sustainability, climate resilience and disaster risk reduction programmes, while progressing its net-zero strategy."
