    "chunk_text": "For countries such as Sri Lanka, this transformation is particularly important. Assistance should go beyond stabilisation programs, debt restructuring and infrastructure financing. Countries need support in building competitive industries, attracting foreign direct investment, developing human capital, retaining talent and creating sustainable employment. Economic reforms must ultimately translate into better livelihoods, reduced poverty and improved living standards. Fiscal discipline and macroeconomic stability are indispensable, but they must create the foundation for productive investment and inclusive growth, not become ends in themselves.\n\n1. Ajay Banga, World Bank President \u2013 Remarks at the 2026 Annual Meetings Plenary, October 2026.\n\n2. Kristalina Georgieva, IMF Managing Director \u2013 AI Will Transform the Global Economy. Let\u2019s Make Sure It Benefits Humanity, IMF, January 2024.\n\n3. World Bank Group \u2013 Small AI: More and Better Jobs, Annual Meetings 2026, Bangkok."
