    "chunk_text": "\u201cThrough these discussions, practical areas of cooperation can be incorporated into regional action plans and implemented collectively,\u201d he pointed out.\n\nPandey highlighted both the opportunities available through BIMSTEC and the need for stronger commitment from member States to translate regional initiatives into practical results.\n\nMeanwhile, he commended Sri Lanka\u2019s chairmanship of BIMSTEC. During the period when former Ambassador Aryasinha served as Sri Lanka\u2019s Foreign Secretary, the BIMSTEC Charter and rationalised areas of cooperation were negotiated and finalised in 2019\u20132020, and later adopted at the summit.\n\nHe noted that Sri Lanka had convened key sectoral meetings not only in the areas it leads but also in other sectors, and appreciated the country\u2019s willingness to go beyond its own sectoral responsibilities.\n\nHe also commended the recently concluded 8th Meeting of the BIMSTEC Network of Policy Think Tanks, held in Colombo and coordinated by the Lakshman Kadirgamar Institute, in which the RCSS and several other Sri Lankan think tanks played an active role. He said wider consultation with think tanks would allow BIMSTEC to benefit from diverse insights.\n\nOffering a Sri Lankan economic perspective on regional cooperation, Institute of Policy Studies of Sri Lanka Chairman Dr. Ganeshan Wignaraja said the economic rationale for BIMSTEC remained compelling, particularly at a time of global economic uncertainty and the weakening of multilateral institutions.\n\nHe pointed to the challenges facing major multilateral institutions, including the World Trade Organisation (WTO), the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund (IMF), noting that the world was witnessing a structural shift in global governance.\n\n\u201cThe second is the Global South, which includes all the BIMSTEC countries, are really looking to regionalism to foster cooperation, trade and also public goods,\u201d he said, identifying regional cooperation as another important reason for strengthening BIMSTEC."
