    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe second is the Global South, which includes all the BIMSTEC countries, are really looking to regionalism to foster cooperation, trade and also public goods,\u201d he said, identifying regional cooperation as another important reason for strengthening BIMSTEC.\n\nHe noted that regional cooperation could help member States expand trade, strengthen economic partnerships and provide public goods.\n\nHe also identified several areas that could help advance this agenda, including developing regional supply chains, modernising the BIMSTEC Free Trade Area framework to address emerging areas such as e-commerce, intellectual property and artificial intelligence, and improving regional connectivity.\n\nDr. Wignaraja pointed out that intra-regional trade among BIMSTEC members remained at around 5\u20136% of their total trade, highlighting the scope for stronger economic links. He also stressed the need to identify and finance genuinely regional infrastructure projects, including roads and railways, rather than focusing solely on projects benefiting individual countries."
