    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ec18c9a4270fc2aca5249b2c0974bbb2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "A Budget of billions, but where is Sri Lanka heading?\n\nThe 2027 Budget risks confusing fiscal arithmetic, political promises and economic transformation\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake presented the 2027 Budget yesterday promising to move Sri Lanka from economic stabilisation to transformation. The speech offered impressive figures, numerous allowances and major infrastructure proposals. Yet the central question remains unanswered: What kind of economy are we building, and how will ordinary Sri Lankans share in its progress?\n\nA national Budget should explain how a country will create productive jobs, raise real incomes, attract investment and withstand external shocks. Judged against these tests, this Budget is less convincing than its presentation suggests. It is politically attractive, but its developmental direction remains uncertain.\n\nThe Government deserves recognition for maintaining macroeconomic stability following Sri Lanka\u2019s devastating economic crisis. Fiscal discipline, stronger revenue collection and improved debt management are important achievements.\n\nThe Budget nevertheless raises difficult questions. Its tables project Rs. 6.18 trillion in revenue and grants against Rs. 7.93 trillion in expenditure when supplementary disaster-related spending is included. The resulting deficit is approximately Rs. 1.75 trillion, or 4.5% of GDP. Interest payments alone are estimated at Rs. 2.64 trillion\u2014roughly 43% of projected Government revenue, excluding grants.\n\nThe Government targets economic growth of at least 7% in the medium term, while the World Bank projects 4.2% for 2027. Its own revenue forecast of 15.8% of GDP for 2027 also sits below its medium-term ambition of at least 16%.\n\nThese ambitions require clearly identified investments, institutional reforms and productivity improvements. Economic stability is an achievement, but it is not the same as economic prosperity."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-ad276818",
    "num": "dailyftlk-ad276818",
    "date_str": "2026-11-13",
    "description": "A Budget of billions, but where is Sri Lanka heading?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/A-Budget-of-billions-but-where-is-Sri-Lanka-heading/4-800050",
    "lang": "en",
