    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b6e3f8b98265f334841cc489eea28a25",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1946,
    "chunk_text": "Where is the measurable plan for private-sector jobs in export industries, technology, modern agriculture, logistics and high-value services?\n\nHow many new jobs will be created, at what wage levels, in which districts, and by when?\n\nThe promise of a \u201cbeautiful life\u201d must be tested against who actually benefits from economic recovery.\n\nThe World Bank finds poverty considerably higher outside the Western Province. Female labour force participation was only 32.7% in the second quarter of 2026.\n\nThese disparities require more than general statements about inclusive development.\n\nAllocations for rural programs, housing and welfare are welcome. But how will they raise lasting incomes in the North, East, estate communities and neglected rural districts?\n\nWhat benchmarks will demonstrate that poor households are moving from welfare dependence towards productive livelihoods?\n\nSocial protection shields people from hardship. Development should create opportunities for them to escape poverty permanently.\n\nGrowth that fails to improve the distribution of opportunity cannot be considered successful development.\n\nThere are constructive proposals: Rs. 2 trillion for public investment including supplementary reconstruction, Rs. 80 billion for railway electrification, concessional finance for smaller enterprises, export-related tax incentives and measures to simplify trade.\n\nThe Government also proposes enhanced capital allowances for qualifying Board of Investment projects.\n\nThe President himself correctly observed that economic transformation means more than presenting another list of expenditures.\n\nInvestors seek predictable taxation, reliable energy, secure land rights, efficient approvals, skilled workers and consistent policy.\n\nThe proposed national single window for investment is still at the consultant-selection stage. This illustrates the distance between announcing investment facilitation and actually making it work."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-dailyftlk-ad276818",
    "num": "dailyftlk-ad276818",
    "date_str": "2026-11-13",
    "description": "A Budget of billions, but where is Sri Lanka heading?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/A-Budget-of-billions-but-where-is-Sri-Lanka-heading/4-800050",
