    "md5": "6d35a8d4e8da9d004c4aeb77019ab742",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "Massive Microsoft outage disrupts businesses, schools and governments around the world\n\nCNN - A massive Microsoft outage has left people around the world without access to Outlook email, Teams meeting tools and other staples of modern office life.\n\nIn the United States, fed-up workers at some companies went home early on Thursday. In Australia, businesses couldn\u2019t print invoices and some schools couldn\u2019t hold online classes on Friday.\n\nAnd there was no quick fix. As of 3:30 a.m. GMT on Friday, the outage was still widespread, affecting untold millions of people.\n\nMicrosoft is posting updates on X and on its \u201cservice health status\u201d page.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re seeing positive results with our efforts to restart affected infrastructure and recover server availability in an isolated manner,\u201d Microsoft said in an update at 1:59 a.m. GMT.\n\nBut in another post at 3:13 a.m. GMT, the company said, \u201cWe\u2019ve monitored the status of the changes applied to improve serviceability and confirmed they\u2019re not taking as expected.\u201d\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re identifying alternate workstreams that can be applied to increase capacity in the face of sustained traffic management imbalances,\u201d the company added, leaving users on X befuddled.\n\no: If your Outlook email account isn\u2019t receiving or sending email, that\u2019s why.\n\nThe disruption has been going on for many hours, causing a wide range of reactions.\n\nSome US office workers celebrated the email blackout and joked that they could start the weekend early. Others barely missed a beat, connecting with colleagues via Slack, phone and even the old-fashioned in-person way.\n\nBut the outage, which began around noon on the US East Coast, caused serious headaches, especially when it dragged on for more than an hour or two.\n\nMicrosoft 365 services that interact with Exchange Online and email services were all impacted. That includes Outlook, SharePoint, Teams, 365 and Copilot AI."
  },
