    "chunk_size_bytes": 1044,
    "chunk_text": "Leopard rescued from snare in Norwood\n\nColombo, Nov. 13 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0A three-and-a-half-year-old female leopard caught in a snare at Athad Estate in Norwood was rescued by wildlife officers and taken to the Randenigala Veterinary Unit for treatment yesterday (12).\n\nThe leopard was found trapped in a snare at the estate, which belongs to the Bagawantalawa Plantation Company, within the Norwood Divisional Secretariat Division.\n\nFollowing information received, officers from the Nallathanniya Wildlife Office launched a rescue operation. They cleared the area of onlookers to prevent the animal from becoming agitated.\n\nA team comprising a veterinarian from the Randenigala Veterinary Unit and wildlife officers subsequently freed the leopard from the snare and transported it to the veterinary unit for treatment.\n\nChief Veterinary Officer at Randenigala, Dr. Akalanka Pinidiya, said the leopard was feeding normally.\n\nHe said the animal would remain under medical care for a few days before being released back into its natural habitat."
