    "chunk_size_bytes": 1574,
    "chunk_text": "Budget Speech 2027\n\nOur government presents its third Budget with the honest and genuine determination of making the story, cherished over many generations, of building a thriving nation to a reality. Every Budget we have presented bears witness to our collective resilience, and has established a firm conviction that, as a nation, we are emerging from the deepest crisis and are on a correct and well-planned trajectory.\n\nWe have been able to kindle an unfading dawn of hope in the hearts of hundreds of thousands of our people. I wish to recall that we are unconditionally fulfilling the expectations of the noble trust that the entire people of this country placed in us two years ago.\n\nEradicating poverty, building a just society, uprooting bribery and corruption, accelerating economic development, restoring the trust of the people and providing every citizen with the opportunity to build a decent life are among our key objectives. However, the foundation for all of these must be the creation, through education, of citizens who are equipped with knowledge, endowed with virtue, think critically and act creatively, as well as visionary leaders. What we need is to build an educated Sri Lankan generation that is rich in knowledge and intellect, contributes to the world through new ideas and new inventions, and is capable of facing any challenge at the international level. Our aim is to create a situation where, wherever in the world a Sri Lankan is recognized, he or she is accepted as a person endowed with knowledge, intellect, creativity and good virtues."
  },
