    "md5": "1967cd1087be81ec93be9a37b51238e8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1702,
    "chunk_text": "Central Government debt stood at 114 percent in 2022, the year in which the economy was plunged into crisis. What is taken into consideration in debt sustainability is the capacity to repay debt relative to GDP and Government revenue, and whether there is adequate liquidity to settle the debt servicing obligations falling due in the near term.\n\n2.2 Accelerating Economic Growth Driven by Investment, Production and Exports\n\nOur target is to accelerate the structural transformation towards a high productivity, export-competitive production economy. Expanding domestic and foreign private investment, diversifying export products and markets, integrating with international value chains and promoting industries and services with higher value addition are the main areas of this.\n\nWe are taking steps to broaden access to finance for small and medium-scale enterprises and to establish a clear and transparent investment environment for investors.\n\nWe give priority to enhancing national productivity by strengthening education, competency development, research, innovation and digital transformation, modernizing public services, expanding digital infrastructure, encouraging the use of new technologies and strengthening collaboration among educational institutions, research institutions and industries.\n\nIn particular, it is essential to equip our younger generation with the competencies required for the changing domestic and global job market, and to transform knowledge and innovation into income-generating enterprises and services. Creating a technologically capable workforce and a more productive economy will also enhance export competitiveness and the capacity to earn foreign exchange."
  },
