    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2c8d3b48f44696113ede43fc927da938",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1874,
    "chunk_text": "In particular, it is essential to equip our younger generation with the competencies required for the changing domestic and global job market, and to transform knowledge and innovation into income-generating enterprises and services. Creating a technologically capable workforce and a more productive economy will also enhance export competitiveness and the capacity to earn foreign exchange.\n\nA new economic transformation at the rural level can be brought about by encouraging small and medium-scale entrepreneurs, creating new economic opportunities for rural people, and developing the technical, vocational and linguistic skills required for the modern job market.\n\nRising international fuel prices, supply chain disruptions and climatic changes form the basis of instability in the energy sector in our country. Our objective is to change these underlying conditions that we face with regard to energy. For this, it is also necessary to expand renewable energy, and to improve electricity transmission networks, energy storage and energy efficiency. Our target is to minimize the long-term pressure on foreign exchange spent on imported fuel, while safeguarding the continuity of essential energy supply through the use of diverse supply routes and energy sources.\n\nIt is important to follow standards capable of withstanding future disasters, early warnings and proper maintenance plans. Along with this, food supply chains, storage, public transport and the mechanisms for distributing essential goods must be strengthened. The continuity of services such as essential communication facilities and electricity must be ensured. Although the risks arising from natural disasters that may occur in the future cannot be completely eliminated, our objective is to significantly minimize the resulting paralysis of economic activities and the pressure on people\u2019s lives."
