    "chunk_size_bytes": 1580,
    "chunk_text": "It is important to follow standards capable of withstanding future disasters, early warnings and proper maintenance plans. Along with this, food supply chains, storage, public transport and the mechanisms for distributing essential goods must be strengthened. The continuity of services such as essential communication facilities and electricity must be ensured. Although the risks arising from natural disasters that may occur in the future cannot be completely eliminated, our objective is to significantly minimize the resulting paralysis of economic activities and the pressure on people\u2019s lives.\n\nOur medium-term economic target is to move towards a sustainable economic growth of 7 percent or higher. A strong and credible fiscal foundation is essential for the economic transformation we envisage. Accordingly, we expect to continue fiscal consolidation in line with the responsibility framework established by the \u201cMedium-Term Fiscal Framework 2027\u20132031\u201d and the \u201cPublic Financial Management Act\u201d. Maintaining a primary surplus of 2.3 percent of GDP, maintaining the budget deficit at a level below 5 percent, and placing public debt on a sustainable path are our core fiscal targets.\n\nOur objective is to maintain Government revenue at a level not less than 16 percent of GDP in the medium term, and to gradually increase it to about 20 percent in the long term. To achieve these targets, the necessary reforms will be implemented to broaden the tax base, rationalize tax exemptions and incentives, digitalize tax administration and strengthen tax compliance."
