    "chunk_size_bytes": 1773,
    "chunk_text": "Through the \u201cConvention on the Suppression of Terrorist Financing (Amendment) Act, No. 18 of 2026\u201d, the financing of global terrorism using Sri Lanka, which poses a threat to national security, has been prevented by strengthening the financial system.\n\nThe \u201cPublic-Private Partnership (PPP) Act\u201d has already been published in the Gazette for the initiation, development, management and monitoring of public-private partnership projects. It is expected to be presented to Parliament in early 2027.\n\nThe draft \u201cState Owned Business Enterprises Management Bill\u201d has already been referred to the Attorney General to incorporate a holding company for the efficient management of companies in which the State holds shares. 34 State-owned enterprises have already been identified for this purpose.\n\nThe draft \u201cInvestment Protection Bill\u201d has already been referred to the Attorney General to promote and protect investments and assets belonging to investors, to ensure fair and equitable treatment, and to make provisions relating to the payment of compensation and the settlement of disputes.\n\nThe draft \u201cColombo Port City Economic Commission (Amendment) Bill\u201d has been referred to the Attorney General to attract foreign investment to the Colombo Port City and to provide greater facilities for investors and those employed there.\n\nThe \u201cInstitute of Professional Actuaries of Sri Lanka Act\u201d required to establish a new institute aimed at ensuring the quality of professional actuaries and improving professional training is being drafted.\n\nData and information are most important in policy decision-making in this era. The \u201cNational Statistics Act\u201d is being drafted for the preparation, coordination and governance of official statistics in Sri Lanka."
