    "md5": "810c96764826610adec8b5f70a726b5d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "Data and information are most important in policy decision-making in this era. The \u201cNational Statistics Act\u201d is being drafted for the preparation, coordination and governance of official statistics in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe \u201cFinancial Reporting Regulatory (Amendment) Act\u201d will be amended to formalize the Sri Lanka Accounting Standards, Sri Lanka Auditing Standards and the regulatory standards on quality control.\n\nThe \u201cExcise (Special Provisions) Act\u201d will be amended to provide solutions to long-standing issues that have arisen in its implementation.\n\nThe \u201cFinance Business Act\u201d will be amended to strengthen the regulation and supervision of finance companies, the investigation and prosecution of unauthorized finance businesses, and the requirements for winding up nonviable finance businesses.\n\nThe \u201cPublic Asset Management Act\u201d will be introduced to meet the requirements of public asset management.\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has appointed an expert committee to reform labour laws that have been in place for decades, so as to align them with current social and economic needs. This initiative aims to create a conducive working environment required for investment and production processes, to be carriedout in an effective and efficient manner and to promote employer-employee relations in which professional responsibility and accountability are clearly defined. This committee is in the process of formulating recommendations, taking into account the views and proposals of relevant stakeholders, including the National Labour Advisory Council.\n\nAn officials\u2019 committee has been appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers to look into minimizing delays in providing Government lands to investors, and to submit recommendations on the concessions to be granted according to the national importance of the project, the number of jobs generated and the area in which the investment is made."
  },
