    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9a95c469caf51c87db10e51380d41f64",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1965,
    "chunk_text": "An officials\u2019 committee has been appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers to look into minimizing delays in providing Government lands to investors, and to submit recommendations on the concessions to be granted according to the national importance of the project, the number of jobs generated and the area in which the investment is made.\n\nThe Gambling Regulatory Authority has already been established to regulate casinos, online gambling and other games that fall into the category of gambling. The necessary regulations have already been finalized with expert assistance.\n\nThe National Single Window for Trade, which has been launched as a pilot project from the fifth of this month for the export of several selected goods, is expected to connect exporters as the first phase in the first half of 2027, and importers and re-exports in the second half of 2027. Rs. 1,990 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\nBids have been called to obtain a consultancy firm for the creation of the National Single Window for Investment, and these bids are currently being evaluated. Rs. 100 million has been allocated for its establishment.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million for the procurement of body scanners and container scanners, aimed at expanding the scanning system to strengthen the border protection process of Sri Lanka Customs.\n\nIt is proposed to modernize the existing \u201cTemporary Importation for Export Processing\u201d (TIEP) process, under which goods imported for export are cleared with tax concessions, in order to introduce \u201cinter-port trading\u201d mechanisms and to direct small and medium-scale industrialists towards exports.\n\nWe expect to update the existing Free Trade Agreements and enter into new trade agreements with more countries in order to connect Sri Lanka to the global trade network.\n\nAn officials\u2019 committee has already been appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers to expand the existing Free Trade Agreement with India."
  },
  {
