    "md5": "b60fff941e465b41a4627387945bc1af",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1831,
    "chunk_text": "With the aim of promoting renewable energy generation, enhancing energy security, and ensuring stability by minimizing imbalances in the national power system, it is proposed to provide a subsidy for the purchase of the batteries required for energy storage to domestic consumers who install rooftop solar power systems equipped with battery storage facilities under the Net Plus scheme.\n\nAlthough the need for supplementary power supply in the event of an emergency at the Norochcholai Lakvijaya Power Plant has been discussed for a long time, no appropriate steps have been taken to address it. Measures are now being taken to establish a BESS with a capacity of 30 MW to provide this supplementary power.\n\nRs. 500 million has been allocated for the preliminary work of the 400 kV Northern main transmission network from Kilinochchi to New Habarana, with the aim of completing it by 2030. We expect to obtain financial assistance of USD 150 million from the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) to construct the transmission line.\n\nIt is expected to invite private investments for the construction of 2 transmission lines of 220 kV from Norochcholai to Wariyapola and from Moneragala to Hambantota, and the New Habarana\u2013Kirindiwela 400 kV transmission line.\n\nIn 2027, smart meters will be provided free of charge to 300,000 electricity consumers who use more than 180 units, on a grant of USD 12 million from the Asian Development Bank (ADB). Smart meters will be provided to all electricity consumers who use more than 120 units in the areas served by Lanka Electricity Company (LECO).\n\nA new capacity of 370 MW generated from wind power will be added to the system by 2029. Of this, steps will be taken to add 50 MW in 2027. By the end of 2029, the installed capacity generated from wind power will increase to 674 MW."
