    "language": "en",
    "md5": "319f141c6b68da143a09cdf20cdb618e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "The Personal Data Protection Act has been amended and the Data Protection Authority has already been established and made operational.\n\nThe Bill for the establishment of the Digital Economy Authority and the National Digital Economy Council (Digital Economy Bill) is expected to be passed in the first quarter of 2027.\n\nThere is a problematic situation in the Government procurement process when purchasing digital solutions and facilities. Therefore, Government procurement guidelines specific to digital solutions and facilities have been prepared, and discussions have already commenced with the Procurement Commission. Accordingly, it will be possible to introduce these procurement guidelines in the first half of 2027.\n\nEstablishing a National Artificial Intelligence Centre of Excellence at Wijerama Mawatha, bringing the Government, the expert community and industry under one roof to build national AI capabilities and promote the responsible use of AI;\n\nEstablishing the \u201cShared Platform First and Buy Before Build Policy\u201d, which, in parallel with the standard for integrating public institutions through digital public infrastructure, gives priority to purchasing standardized solutions, and to shared use, before developing new software in software procurement;\n\nExpanding the Lanka Government Cloud (LGC) system from LGC 2.0 to LGC 3.0 and establishing the core foundation of sovereign infrastructure for Artificial Intelligence;\n\nDigitalising the services provided by Divisional Secretariats and Grama Niladharis so that citizens can easily access Government services;\n\nLaunching the \u201cPresidential Digital Excellence Awards\u201d programme to appriase high-performing public institutions with the aim of rapidly promoting digitalization;\n\nAdopting and expanding cashless payment methods such as GovPay and QR to steer towards a digital revenue economy;\n\nFurther, preparing the necessary regulatory basis for Virtual Asset Service Providers (VASP) through the establishment of a formal legal framework;"
