    "md5": "78f86276be1fa6fd1e4481f20d300bed",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1341,
    "chunk_text": "Adopting and expanding cashless payment methods such as GovPay and QR to steer towards a digital revenue economy;\n\nFurther, preparing the necessary regulatory basis for Virtual Asset Service Providers (VASP) through the establishment of a formal legal framework;\n\nProviding electricity tariff concessions and other incentives to encourage investors selected under formal criteria, with the expectation of encouraging investment in the establishment of data centres;\n\nProviding broadband vouchers to 750,000 selected school students to enhance digital literacy among them;\n\nStrengthening the Digital Startup Fund of Funds to attract private investment into Sri Lankan businesses;\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 10,000 million for the above proposals.\n\nRs. 18,500 million has already been allocated to the Ministry of Digital Economy for the year 2027 to support the digital transformation and the development of the digital economy of the country under 6 key areas, namely 1) institutional strengthening, policy and regulation, 2) digital Government transformation, 3) digital industry development and growth, 4) empowering the digital revenue economy, 5) empowering digital activities in strategic industries, and 6) promoting inclusive access and adoption, and capacity development, and this amount will be increased to Rs. 28,500 million."
