    "md5": "6c3276ef18363917b4092d98e32477de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1621,
    "chunk_text": "Rs. 18,500 million has already been allocated to the Ministry of Digital Economy for the year 2027 to support the digital transformation and the development of the digital economy of the country under 6 key areas, namely 1) institutional strengthening, policy and regulation, 2) digital Government transformation, 3) digital industry development and growth, 4) empowering the digital revenue economy, 5) empowering digital activities in strategic industries, and 6) promoting inclusive access and adoption, and capacity development, and this amount will be increased to Rs. 28,500 million.\n\nAt present, there are problems with the Quality of Service and Quality of Experience in the mobile (broadband) connectivity networks in the country, and rural people in particular face great difficulty. To identify and correct these accurately, the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission will commence the introduction of an automated monitoring system in 2027 for this purpose, for the first time in Sri Lanka, through which it is expected to improve the Quality of Service and Quality of Experience of the networks of mobile (broadband) connectivity providers in the country. With the aim of correcting the financial loss incurred by the country as a result of the frequency spectrum belonging to the people of this country being issued without effective and efficient management, the installation of an Automated Spectrum Management System and an Automated Spectrum Monitoring System will commence in 2027. The Telecommunications Regulatory Commission has allocated Rs. 3,100 million for the procurement of all these systems."
