    "chunk_size_bytes": 1644,
    "chunk_text": "At present, there are problems with the Quality of Service and Quality of Experience in the mobile (broadband) connectivity networks in the country, and rural people in particular face great difficulty. To identify and correct these accurately, the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission will commence the introduction of an automated monitoring system in 2027 for this purpose, for the first time in Sri Lanka, through which it is expected to improve the Quality of Service and Quality of Experience of the networks of mobile (broadband) connectivity providers in the country. With the aim of correcting the financial loss incurred by the country as a result of the frequency spectrum belonging to the people of this country being issued without effective and efficient management, the installation of an Automated Spectrum Management System and an Automated Spectrum Monitoring System will commence in 2027. The Telecommunications Regulatory Commission has allocated Rs. 3,100 million for the procurement of all these systems.\n\nOur objective is to build an efficient public service and a competitive digital economy, while making the daily lives of the people easier through digital technology.\n\nEducation holds the greatest responsibility in building the human resources required for the modern world. Therefore, a qualitative transformation in education as well as a new technological transformation in the delivery of education is required. For this, it is essential to develop the necessary infrastructure and human resources.\n\nThe new education reforms have already commenced for Grade 1 and will commence for Grades 2 and 6 next year."
