    "md5": "9747fa832fcbaa76ad1273fe66c4b4cc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1641,
    "chunk_text": "Education holds the greatest responsibility in building the human resources required for the modern world. Therefore, a qualitative transformation in education as well as a new technological transformation in the delivery of education is required. For this, it is essential to develop the necessary infrastructure and human resources.\n\nThe new education reforms have already commenced for Grade 1 and will commence for Grades 2 and 6 next year.\n\nTo support students pursuing their education at Pirivenas and to help meet their educational needs, we are taking steps to increase the daily allowance provided to student monks from Rs.15 to Rs.50, and the daily allowance for lay students from Rs.5 to Rs.25, with effect from April 2027.\n\nWith the aim of producing a generation of children endowed with values, morality and virtue, steps will be taken to increase by Rs.5,000, from Rs.7,500 to Rs.12,500, the annual allowance currently paid from 2027 to Dhamma School teachers who contribute voluntarily to safeguard the quality of Dhamma School education.\n\nSteps will be taken to provide the school uniforms donated by the Government of China in the same manner next year as well. The Government of China has expressed its agreement to provide this donation for the next few years as well.\n\nOur target is to provide reliable internet connections to all secondary schools. At present, reliable internet connections have been provided to 6,225 schools, including 3,009 connections provided this year. Steps will be taken to provide connections to the remaining 750 schools expeditiously. This programme will also be launched for primary schools."
