    "chunk_size_bytes": 1783,
    "chunk_text": "Rs.2,250 million has been allocated for the development of academic and infrastructure facilities, including the construction of a fully-fledged building for the Faculty of Science of the Eastern University, laboratory complexes with computer and research facilities for the Universities of Ruhuna and Sabaragamuwa, buildings for the Faculty of Allied Health Sciences of the University of Jaffna and for the Faculty of Commerce and Management Studies and the Faculty of Science of the University of Kelaniya, a laboratory complex for the Rajarata University, and multipurpose buildings for the Faculties of Management of the Uva Wellassa University and the University of Colombo.\n\nIt is proposed to commence a Rs. 2,050 million official quarters project in 2027 to provide residential facilities for the academic and non-academic staff of the University of Vavuniya.\n\nRs.6,150 million has been estimated for the restoration of the damage caused to the infrastructure of the University of Peradeniya by Cyclone \u201cDitwah\u201d. In 2027, Rs. 700 million has been allocated for restoration work in higher educational institutions, including this.\n\nAlthough approximately 42,000 students are admitted to government universities annually, many students who qualify for university entry are denied this opportunity due to limited resources. With the objective of providing higher education opportunities for these students, the government has implemented a programme, facilitated through state banks, that offers interest-free loans to eligible students, enabling them to pursue degree programs at private higher education institutions. It is proposed to increase the monthly subsistence allowance currently available to these students from Rs. 6,250 to Rs. 10,000, effective from April 2027."
