    "chunk_text": "Although approximately 42,000 students are admitted to government universities annually, many students who qualify for university entry are denied this opportunity due to limited resources. With the objective of providing higher education opportunities for these students, the government has implemented a programme, facilitated through state banks, that offers interest-free loans to eligible students, enabling them to pursue degree programs at private higher education institutions. It is proposed to increase the monthly subsistence allowance currently available to these students from Rs. 6,250 to Rs. 10,000, effective from April 2027.\n\nIn 2027, Rs. 800 million has been allocated for the Rs. 3,380 million project to develop hostel, canteen, laboratory and workshop facilities at the University of Vocational Technology in Ratmalana.\n\nRs. 200 million has been allocated in 2027 for improving the infrastructure of institutions belonging to the technical education and training sector, including the German Technical Training Institute and the Automobile Engineering Training Institute.\n\nRs. 1,500 million has been allocated for the year 2027 for the project costing Rs. 6,000 million to modernize 25 selected Technical Colleges in 25 districts.\n\nIt is expected to make a capital investment of Rs. 11 billion for the development of the vocational education and training sector, to modernize infrastructure, update curricula, integrate new technologies and strengthen collaboration between the public and private sectors.\n\n9. Towards an Economic Transformation through Research, Development and Innovation"
