    "chunk_text": "It is expected to make a capital investment of Rs. 11 billion for the development of the vocational education and training sector, to modernize infrastructure, update curricula, integrate new technologies and strengthen collaboration between the public and private sectors.\n\n9. Towards an Economic Transformation through Research, Development and Innovation\n\nMonitoring and regulating research and development activities carried out by the public as well as the private sector.\n\nDirecting research in a manner that contributes to national development goals and economic growth.\n\nDeveloping the capabilities of local researchers and supporting advanced research of international standard.\n\nTransforming the results of research carried out in laboratories and universities into products or services useful to society and the industrial sector.\n\nPreparing national research and development policies to suit the future needs of the country.\n\nTaking new technologies discovered through research to commercialization and integrating them into the country\u2019s economy.\n\nThe National Innovation Agency, Sri Lanka Inventors Commission, the National Science Foundation and the National Research Council, the National Science and Technology Commission, and the Sri Lanka Council for Agricultural Research Policy, which come under the Ministry of Science and Technology, are scheduled to be incorporated into this National Council for Research and Development.\n\nSteps will also be taken to provide the institutional, technical and infrastructure facilities necessary to carry out research covering various subject areas through research institutions and other public institutions under various Ministries. Through Government investment, Rs. 23,800 million has been allocated for research and development programmes in 2027.\n\nRs. 7,600 million, including operational expenses, has been allocated to coordinate all such research activities under the Ministry of Science and Technology."
