    "chunk_text": "Steps will also be taken to provide the institutional, technical and infrastructure facilities necessary to carry out research covering various subject areas through research institutions and other public institutions under various Ministries. Through Government investment, Rs. 23,800 million has been allocated for research and development programmes in 2027.\n\nRs. 7,600 million, including operational expenses, has been allocated to coordinate all such research activities under the Ministry of Science and Technology.\n\nThrough this Budget, we expect to make the largest investment in the development of highways, expressways and railways. Rs. 251 billion has been allocated for this purpose in this Budget. Further, we expect to spend Rs. 487 billion, including Rs. 146 billion as new proposals and Rs. 90 billion from the Ditwah Supplementary Estimate for the restoration of damage caused to railways, highways and bridges by Cyclone Ditwah. Mainly;\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 30,000 million for the construction from Kurunegala to Galewela as the first step of the Kurunegala\u2013Dambulla expressway section, which is the 4th phase of the Central Expressway.\n\nAn amount of Rs. 18,680 million has been allocated in 2026 for the initial activities of the development of the first phase of the Ruwanpura Expressway from Kahathuduwa to Ingiriya, and it is proposed to allocate Rs. 27,000 million in 2027.\n\nRs. 53,450 million has been allocated for the year 2027 with the aim of completing the Kadawatha\u2013Mirigama section of the Central Expressway by September 2028, which had been stalled due to the collapse of the economy.\n\nRs. 4,500 million has been allocated for the year 2027 with the aim of completing the Pothuhera\u2013Rambukkana section of the Central Expressway by May 2027.\n\nRs. 23,050 million has been allocated for the year 2027 with the aim of completing the Rambukkana\u2013Galagedara section of the Central Expressway, which commenced in 2026 by July 2029."
