    "chunk_text": "Rs. 4,500 million has been allocated for the year 2027 with the aim of completing the Pothuhera\u2013Rambukkana section of the Central Expressway by May 2027.\n\nRs. 23,050 million has been allocated for the year 2027 with the aim of completing the Rambukkana\u2013Galagedara section of the Central Expressway, which commenced in 2026 by July 2029.\n\nIt is also proposed to construct several new flyovers to minimize traffic congestion and improve transport efficiency. Accordingly, Rs. 1,900 million has been allocated in this Budget for the construction of 2 flyovers at the Alawwa and Kurunegala\u2013Muttettugala railway crossings, and a new flyover near the Kandy Post Office to provide access to the newly constructed Kandy Multimodal Transport Hub bypassing the Kandy\u2013Matale railway line.\n\nRs. 600 million has been allocated for the construction of the Kokkilai Bridge, Rs. 400 million for the construction of the Kiran Bridge, Rs. 200 million for the construction of the Ponduhalchenai Bridge, Rs. 340 million for the construction of a new bridge across the Verugal River in the Punnaiyadi area, and Rs. 500 million for the construction of the Vadduvakkal Bridge in 2027. The total estimate for these projects is Rs. 10,630 million.\n\nRs. 22,000 million has been allocated for the widening and development of selected road sections in order to minimize traffic congestion in the road network and ensure road safety.\n\nRs. 680 million has been allocated for carrying out feasibility studies on road developments identified from time to time, including the Ratnapura Bypass,the Kahawatta Bypass, the Kiribathgoda Bypass and the Katunayake\u2013Chilaw Expressway.\n\nThe development of the railway sector, which is considered as the backbone of passenger transport, has been identified as a Government\u2019s priority. Accordingly, an investment of over Rs. 1,200 billion is scheduled to be made to electrify three main railway lines. For the implementation of the first phase of this programme, for the year 2027;"
