    "md5": "876b7a9e777482c4782e8e6128d95b00",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1672,
    "chunk_text": "The development of the railway sector, which is considered as the backbone of passenger transport, has been identified as a Government\u2019s priority. Accordingly, an investment of over Rs. 1,200 billion is scheduled to be made to electrify three main railway lines. For the implementation of the first phase of this programme, for the year 2027;\n\nRs. 16,400 million for the electrification of the Main line from Maradana to Ragama;\n\nRs. 17,700 million for the electrification of the Coastal line from Maradana to Panadura;\n\nRs. 900 million for other operational expenses, including land acquisition, it is proposed to allocate Rs. 80,000 million, including the above.\n\nWe have recognized that the development of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) is most essential for a rapid transformation of the economy. Accordingly, in 2026, we have allocated Rs. 54,136 million for interest subsidies and refinancing for a number of schemes such as collateral-free loans, interest-free loans and low-interest loans. Through this, the State and private banking system has been able to grant loans amounting to Rs. 97,100 million owing to the surge that took place in that sector. Owing to the surge in that sector, we have been able to provide this entire allocation within this year.\n\nAlso, in 2027, Rs. 67,687 million has been allocated for interest subsidies and refinancing to banks. Through this, it is expected to provide Rs. 174 billion as concessionary loans to entrepreneurs through State and private banks. This includes the following loan schemes.\n\nRefinance and Interest Subsidy Loan Scheme for Reviving the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise Sector (Re-MSME Plus)"
