    "md5": "d081307811ff589382f167723c980124",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1924,
    "chunk_text": "Also, in 2027, Rs. 67,687 million has been allocated for interest subsidies and refinancing to banks. Through this, it is expected to provide Rs. 174 billion as concessionary loans to entrepreneurs through State and private banks. This includes the following loan schemes.\n\nRefinance and Interest Subsidy Loan Scheme for Reviving the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise Sector (Re-MSME Plus)\n\nIn order to make the fisheries sector eligible for this concessionary loan scheme, it is proposed to grant loans to enterprises engaged in the fisheries industry by considering only the business turnover in the definition of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises.\n\nSchemes Implemented with the Financial Assistance of the Asian Development Bank\n\nIn order to meet the existing demand for concessionary interest loan programmes, a further Rs. 30,000 million has been allocated, with the funding assistance of the Asian Development Bank, for granting loans for the capital and working capital requirements of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises.\n\nPledge Loan Scheme for Small and Medium-Scale Paddy Mill Owners\n\nIt is proposed to implement the Pledge Loan Scheme for small and medium scale paddy mill owners for the purchase of paddy at the Government guaranteed price as an interest-free loan scheme from 2027. It is expected to provide financial facilities of Rs. 20,000 million through this programme. In addition to the Rs. 350 million currently allocated, further allocations are proposed to bear the additional interest subsidy of this loan scheme.\n\nA special programme is essential for uplifting women-headed family units. In particular, the living standards of such families living in rural areas are at a relatively low level. In order to strengthen such families economically, it is proposed to implement a group loan scheme of up to Rs. 1 million at a concessionary annual interest rate of 3 percent through the Samurdhi Bank."
