    "md5": "b8c4e5c07cf733860415df4aa81fffc0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1499,
    "chunk_text": "A special programme is essential for uplifting women-headed family units. In particular, the living standards of such families living in rural areas are at a relatively low level. In order to strengthen such families economically, it is proposed to implement a group loan scheme of up to Rs. 1 million at a concessionary annual interest rate of 3 percent through the Samurdhi Bank.\n\nWith the aim of strengthening enterprises in rural areas and empowering Aswesuma beneficiaries, it is expected to provide loans to entrepreneurs through the Samurdhi Bank up to a maximum of Rs. 5 million at a concessionary annual interest rate of 4 percent. In order to qualify for this loan facility, it is mandatory for such entrepreneurs to provide employment opportunities to at least five Aswesuma beneficiaries. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 200 million for interest subsidies for this purpose. Through this, it is expected to provide loans amounting to Rs. 5,000 million.\n\nIt is proposed to provide a maximum loan amount of up to Rs. 500 million through banks at an annual interest rate of 5 percent to large-scale fisheries industrialists with export potential, fish product suppliers, boat manufacturers and manufacturers of other fishing gear required for the fisheries industry, to obtain the modern technology and other inputs they require. It is proposed to provide Rs. 1,000 million as interest subsidies for this purpose. Through this, it is expected to provide loans amounting to Rs. 15,000 million."
