    "md5": "a12d4b68615511a216833a80a2ad4e9e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1950,
    "chunk_text": "It is proposed to provide a maximum loan amount of up to Rs. 500 million through banks at an annual interest rate of 5 percent to large-scale fisheries industrialists with export potential, fish product suppliers, boat manufacturers and manufacturers of other fishing gear required for the fisheries industry, to obtain the modern technology and other inputs they require. It is proposed to provide Rs. 1,000 million as interest subsidies for this purpose. Through this, it is expected to provide loans amounting to Rs. 15,000 million.\n\nThe data and information required to access all these loan schemes have been included on the website of the Department of Development Finance of the Ministry of Finance, and a hotline of 1819 has also been introduced.\n\nLocated at a highly strategic position on the East-West global sea route, the Port of Colombo holds 20th place among the ports of the world. Developing the port and its related services brings great importance to the country\u2019s economy. Our target is to increase its total shipping capacity to over 30 million Twenty-foot Equivalent Units (TEUs) by 2040, and to develop it as a re-export shipping and logistics hub.\n\nWith financing from the Asian Development Bank and the World Bank, a 3.2 kilometre breakwater will be constructed for the West Terminal II and the development required for handling 3.2 million containers will be carried out.\n\nThe feasibility study currently being carried out for the development of the Colombo North Port is expected to be completed in the first half of next year. It is expected to spend Rs. 300 million from the funds of the Ports Authority to expeditiously carry out the additional study on the Kelani River estuary, which is a decisive factor in the development of the North Port.\n\nRequests for Proposals (RFP) for the establishment of a Logistics Centre in the Port of Colombo through a public-private partnership will be called within the next 2 months."
  },
