    "chunk_text": "A feasibility study will be carried out for the widening of the road in front of the airport and the construction of a flyover to minimize traffic congestion at and around the airport. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 200 million for this purpose.\n\nA new car park will be constructed by AASL at a cost of Rs. 400 million to minimize vehicle congestion in and around the airport.\n\nThe Ratmalana International Airport will be developed for pilot training, and domestic, business and regional aviation. To ensure aviation safety, a project of Rs. 6,000 million to rehabilitate the existing runway and extend it from 1,400 metres to 1,771 metres will commence in 2027 with the funds of AASL.\n\nThe Mattala International Airport, which was constructed with a loan of USD 190 million and commenced flight operations in 2013, has today recorded an accumulated loss of over Rs. 70,000 million. Moreover, this loss grows annually. Therefore, Expressions of Interest (EOI) have already been called and concluded for the development of the areas of airport operations, data centres, food and catering services, and aircraft services and maintenance jointly with international companies. Steps are being taken to call for Requests for Proposals (RFP) from the selected companies. We expect to select new investors for this within the next year.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 100 million for improving the facilities, including the passenger terminal, of the Sigiriya Domestic Airport for the promotion of tourism centred in Sigiriya.\n\nThe necessary investments for improving the facilities, including the passenger terminal, of the China Bay Airport will be made by AASL in 2027."
  },
