    "chunk_size_bytes": 1786,
    "chunk_text": "It is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 100 million for improving the facilities, including the passenger terminal, of the Sigiriya Domestic Airport for the promotion of tourism centred in Sigiriya.\n\nThe necessary investments for improving the facilities, including the passenger terminal, of the China Bay Airport will be made by AASL in 2027.\n\nRs. 750 million has been allocated for activities including holding \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2027\u201d in January, and promoting export diversification, competitiveness and high-value exports by implementing the priorities identified under the National Export Development Plan (NEDP).\n\nA feasibility study will be carried out to establish a knowledge and experience centre that expands links between industry and universities, promotes research and development, and supports the commercialization of new products and processes.\n\nThe Kurunchantivu Salt Pan, where production activities had been halted until now, will be restarted using the funds of the National Salt Limited with the aim of creating employment opportunities in the Northern region. The General Treasury has provided Rs. 236 million for the year 2026 for the construction of the necessary access roads and the provision of services for this purpose.\n\nThe National Gem and Jewellery Authority Act, No. 50 of 1993 will be amended to include the necessary legal provisions for issuing licences to the jewellery industry.\n\nThe acquisition of the land required for the establishment of an International Gem and Jewellery Trade Hub, where gem and jewellery trade, export facilities, laboratory services and licensing services can be obtained from a single location, is being carried out, and a preliminary feasibility study is expected to be carried out by the University of Moratuwa."
  },
