    "language": "en",
    "md5": "da7d17ea152574cd2bd42260059eed5c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1386,
    "chunk_text": "The acquisition of the land required for the establishment of an International Gem and Jewellery Trade Hub, where gem and jewellery trade, export facilities, laboratory services and licensing services can be obtained from a single location, is being carried out, and a preliminary feasibility study is expected to be carried out by the University of Moratuwa.\n\nAt present, the number of persons actively trading in connection with the Colombo Stock Exchange is only around 0.7 percent of the population over 18 years of age. Therefore, it is proposed to implement a new programme named \u201cA Share for Everyone\u201d under the vision \u201cLet\u2019s Know, Let\u2019s Learn, Let\u2019s Invest\u201d. With the aim of actively connecting students in schools who are studying for the Advanced Level in Grade 13 and are over 18 years of age with the stock market, it is proposed to introduce the project to provide a share portfolio subject to a maximum of Rs. 10,000/-, in accordance with a formal selection procedure.\n\nIt is proposed to introduce a mechanism to encourage the listing on the stock market of small and medium-scale enterprises (SME Listing Support Mechanism), which makes a significant contribution to the economy and job creation.\n\nFor the above proposals, the Colombo Stock Exchange will deploy Rs. 250 million, and it is proposed to allocate an additional Rs. 500 million for this purpose."
