    "chunk_size_bytes": 1698,
    "chunk_text": "It is proposed to introduce a mechanism to encourage the listing on the stock market of small and medium-scale enterprises (SME Listing Support Mechanism), which makes a significant contribution to the economy and job creation.\n\nFor the above proposals, the Colombo Stock Exchange will deploy Rs. 250 million, and it is proposed to allocate an additional Rs. 500 million for this purpose.\n\nExploration of the quantity of the graphite reserve in the Kahatagaha Graphite Mine, which extends over an area of 102 acres, is scheduled to be carried out jointly with the Geological Survey and Mines Bureau. Once the size of the reserve has been identified, further steps are scheduled to be taken to identify a suitable investor for the graphite value addition project, including graphite mining and processing activities.\n\nCabinet approval has been granted to allocate 58 grids containing mineral sands along the eastern coastal belt to Lanka Mineral Sands Limited. A Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee and a Project Committee have been appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers to select an investor for a value addition industry for the mineral sands mined by Lanka Mineral Sands Limited.\n\nExploration is already being carried out on the silica sand deposit extending over an area of 40 acres in the Nattandiya area. After identifying the potential of the relevant mineral resources, steps will be taken to identify a suitable investor in 2027.\n\nAn area of 28 metric grid units has been identified in relation to the Kotigambokka quartz deposit located in the Wellawaya area. Steps will be taken to identify a suitable investor in 2027 for the mining and value addition project of this quartz deposit."
