    "md5": "ab917032158c2606196d89fe154b6622",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1894,
    "chunk_text": "An area of 28 metric grid units has been identified in relation to the Kotigambokka quartz deposit located in the Wellawaya area. Steps will be taken to identify a suitable investor in 2027 for the mining and value addition project of this quartz deposit.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million for the development of the infrastructure required for the fisheries industry in the Northern Province, anchorages and the Pesalai Fishery Harbour.\n\nRs. 300 million has been allocated for the development of the Chilaw and Wellamankaraya fishery harbours.\n\nRs. 1,500 million has been allocated for the development of the Gandara Fishery Harbour.\n\nThe Peliyagoda Fish Market is currently facing many problems, such as the absence of a formal waste disposal mechanism, inadequate cold storagefacilities and inadequate sanitation facilities. It is proposed to provide Rs. 1,000 million as equity capital to resolve these issues. It is expected to manage this centre under a new business structure.\n\nIt is proposed to provide provisions of Rs. 500 million as equity capital to the North Sea Limited, which manufactures and repairs net gear, to purchase the machinery required to strengthen new technical facilities and to construct a new net manufacturing and repair centre.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 300 million for the development of the Aquaculture Development Centre in Polonthalawa, which currently carries out development activities relating to the inland fisheries industry.\n\nIt is proposed to provide Rs. 200 million to the Ceylon Fisheries Corporation as equity capital for the development of the sales outlets owned by the Ceylon Fisheries Corporation.\n\nPilot projects have confirmed that cage fish farming in inland reservoirs yields higher harvests. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 250 million to provide concessions to fishing communities to further popularize cage fish farming."
  },
