    "md5": "dffc3fd70dbbb743e58e09b0f6402406",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1709,
    "chunk_text": "Pilot projects have confirmed that cage fish farming in inland reservoirs yields higher harvests. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 250 million to provide concessions to fishing communities to further popularize cage fish farming.\n\nRs. 1,000 million has been allocated for sustainable development projects for fisheries resource management through ocean surveys, habitat mapping, fish stock assessments, the collection of monitoring data, laboratory analyses and ecosystem restoration activities.\n\nIt is proposed to increase the compensation paid in the event of the sudden death of a fisherman engaged in the fisheries industry due to an accident while engaged in the industry from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 2 million.\n\nThe main livelihoods of rural people are bound up with farming. Although agriculture accounts for 23.9 percent of the labour force and around 39 percent of land use, and more than Rs. 200 billion has been spent annually on public investment and subsidies over the past few years, its contribution to the national economy is close to 8.4 percent. These data themselves demonstrate the problem of farming life. It will not be possible to emerge from this crisis without subjecting this sector to a radical new transformation.\n\nPrivate sector investment will be encouraged to increase large-scale agricultural production and its quality, improve the efficiency of agricultural value chains and expand markets.\n\nIt is proposed to give paddy land owners the freedom to use uncultivated or low-productivity paddy lands, after they have been identified through an accurate survey, for field crops or permanent crops. Rs. 1,550 million has been allocated to encourage cultivation on these selected lands."
  },
