    "md5": "81394ef367d7b94d3d7f56991cf1be35",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1752,
    "chunk_text": "It is proposed to give paddy land owners the freedom to use uncultivated or low-productivity paddy lands, after they have been identified through an accurate survey, for field crops or permanent crops. Rs. 1,550 million has been allocated to encourage cultivation on these selected lands.\n\nFor rural agricultural development, Agrarian Service Centres will be transformed into \u2018One-Stop Shops\u2019 through the establishment of digital infrastructure, the creation of machinery pools, the empowerment of farming communities and the establishment of a digital platform through which realtime information can be exchanged. Rs. 250 million has been allocated to launch this as a pilot project in 5 main agricultural districts.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate an additional sum of Rs. 300 million in addition to Rs. 700 million already allocated for food security to enable cooperative societies which have been already selected to receive paddy dryers in 2026 and possess the necessary machinery capacity to purchase paddy from the Paddy Marketing Board and release it to the market. Furthermore, priority will be given to meeting the working capital requirements of these societies, under an approved framework to facilitate the immediate commencement of these operations. This allocation is also intended to assist these cooperative societies in purchasing the machinery required for rice production.\n\nAn Integrated Plant Nutrient Management System (IPNM) is required to promote the integrated use of chemical fertilizer and organic fertilizer, increase crop productivity and strengthen soil quality and nutrient status. It is proposed to implement a 4-year project for this purpose, and Rs. 47 million has been allocated for the year 2027 as an initial step."
