    "chunk_text": "Rs. 7,500 million has been allocated to accelerate the work of the Lower Malwathu Oya Project, construction of which has already commenced, for the agricultural and social development of the Anuradhapura, Vavuniya and Mannar districts.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to meet the water requirements of the Batticaloa and Ampara districts, minimize flood risk and commence the Mundeni Aru River Basin Development Project.\n\nRs. 5,000 million has been allocated for irrigation projects such as the implementation of the Wayamba Canal Project to divert surplus water from the Weemedilla Reservoir to the Mee Oya basin in the Kurunegala district, the modernization of the over 50-year-old Rajanganaya lift irrigation scheme, the completion of work on the halted feeder canal from the Siyambalangamuwa Oya to the Mahagalgamuwa Oya, and the mitigation of floods in Gampaha town.\n\nRs. 19,500 million has been allocated for the Mahaweli Water Security and Investment Programme, including the North Central Province Greater Canal Project.\n\nIt is expected to carry out feasibility studies to recommence the Kumbukkan Oya Reservoir Project aimed at meeting the water requirements of the Moneragala district and the Heda Oya Reservoir Development Project aimed at improving the water supply of the Ampara district. It is proposed to allocate an additional Rs. 200 million for the preliminary work of such irrigation projects."
