    "chunk_text": "It is expected to carry out feasibility studies to recommence the Kumbukkan Oya Reservoir Project aimed at meeting the water requirements of the Moneragala district and the Heda Oya Reservoir Development Project aimed at improving the water supply of the Ampara district. It is proposed to allocate an additional Rs. 200 million for the preliminary work of such irrigation projects.\n\nRs. 2,500 million has been allocated for the development of minor irrigation under the \u201cWari Mahimaya \u2013 Ape Urumaya\u201d programme, and Rs. 1,500 million has also been allocated for the rehabilitation of minor irrigation schemes damaged by the Ditwah disaster.\n\nIncluding these, around Rs. 15,000 million has been allocated directly for the maintenance and development of minor irrigation schemes.\n\nRs. 800 million has been allocated in 2027 to further strengthen the ongoing Bimsaviya programme.\n\nProgrammes for the registration of land titles, the digitalization of land records and the modernization of land information systems will also be continued, and Rs. 140 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIt is also expected to implement in 2027 the programme to digitalize the plans relating to 3.5 million land parcels held in hard copy by the Survey Department and integrate them with the land information system. Provisions have been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIt is expected to increase the export earnings of USD 3 billion currently generated by the plantation sector to USD 5 billion by 2030. For this, Rs. 13,000 million has been allocated for the development of the plantation sector in 2027.\n\nRs. 730 million has been allocated to implement the programme to establish 500 tea villages covering the Southern, Sabaragamuwa, North Western, Western, Uva and Central Provinces through an integrated approach, aimed at increasing the overall productivity of the smallholder tea sector, which contributes around 70 percent of tea production."
