    "chunk_text": "Rs. 650 million has been allocated to encourage rubber growers, provide concessions for new planting and replanting, and promote rubber cultivation in non-traditional areas.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to provide a fertilizer subsidy of Rs. 4,000 per bag, with the aim of ensuring the continued application of fertilizer in rubber plantations.\n\nThe lease agreements for Regional Plantation Companies are set to expire in the year 2045. The Cabinet has appointed a committee of officials to review these agreements, with the objective of safeguarding the rights of both estate owners and employees, while also analyzing the productivity of the respective estates.\n\nWe are focusing on building the common infrastructure required for the training of sportsmen and sportswomen to win victories at national and international level, and for building a sports culture among the general public for a healthy life, as well as on building human resources comprising skilled referees and coaches.\n\nA National High-Performance Centre will be established to provide sports science methods, physical fitness training, nutrition counselling, sportsmedicine services and mental preparation facilities to elevate the talents of sportsmen and sportswomen to international level. Its first phase will commence at the Torrington Stadium, and Rs. 300 million has been allocated for establishing the second phase within the Diyagama Sports Complex.\n\nProvisions of Rs. 1,500 million have been allocated for the development and modernization of the Sugathadasa National Indoor Sports Complex, the purchase of the required sports equipment and the construction of a synthetic running track at the Sugathadasa International Stadium.\n\nRs. 2,500 million has been allocated to establish a sports culture with the aim of enhancing the sports skills of school students and the youth community and directing the elderly generation towards sports."
