    "chunk_text": "Rs. 75 million has been allocated for the construction of four new wards and a wastewater management system for homeless and destitute persons at the Rediyagama Kalana Detention Home.\n\nDay care centres will be constructed for children with disabilities, and Rs. 200 million has been allocated to provide transport facilities for children with disabilities.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 500 million to provide facilities for high-capacity children\u2019s homes.\n\nWe must take a new approach to connect the knowledge and abilities of Sri Lankans living abroad and their children, as well as their bond to the motherland, to the future development journey of the country. Accordingly, we propose to introduce a \u201cGlobal Sri Lankan Heritage Citizen\u201d programme for the second and third generations of the overseas community of Sri Lankan origin. Accordingly, we propose to grant dual citizenship, free of any charge, to the spouse and children of an applicant for dual citizenship, as well as to third-generation children.\n\nA highly concessionary housing loan scheme of up to Rs. 5 million will be implemented to meet the housing needs of migrant workers. Under this scheme, steps will be taken to provide an interest subsidy of 10 percent for up to Rs. 3 million and an interest subsidy of 5 percent for the remaining Rs. 2 million.\n\nIt is proposed that, for the first Rs. 3 million, a contribution of 6 percent be borne by the Government and a contribution of 4 percent by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment, and for the remaining Rs. 2 million, a contribution of 3 percent be borne by the Government and a contribution of 2 percent by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate a sum of Rs. 1,000 million in 2027 as the Government contribution for the implementation of this interest subsidy scheme.\n\nThe installation of a modern Doppler Radar System for highly accurate weather forecasting, received as a JICA grant, will commence in 2027."
