    "chunk_text": "It is proposed to allocate a sum of Rs. 1,000 million in 2027 as the Government contribution for the implementation of this interest subsidy scheme.\n\nThe installation of a modern Doppler Radar System for highly accurate weather forecasting, received as a JICA grant, will commence in 2027.\n\nRs. 500 million has been allocated to provide disaster response equipment essential for strengthening early warning.\n\nRs. 670 million has been allocated to establish an island-wide digital radio communication system.\n\nRs. 500 million has been allocated for the rehabilitation of 77 existing coastal early warning towers, the construction of 120 new land-based towers covering flood, landslide and tsunami-prone areas in 25 districts, and the establishment of a multi-hazard early warning communication system.\n\nIncluding the above proposals, Rs. 2,900 million has been allocated for 13 new disaster management projects.\n\nA Dam Safety Act will be introduced to provide the legal safeguards necessary to ensure the safety of major dam systems.\n\nCapital expenditure of Rs. 131 billion has been allocated for maintaining and improving the public health service so that every citizen is able to obtain the quality health services they require through all medical systems administered by the central Government and the Provincial Councils.\n\nA large number of vacancies existed due to the non-recruitment of health staff over a long period. In order to deliver a quality health service, the required human resources have been recruited, namely 1,797 doctors, 303 indigenous medical practitioners, 64 dental surgeons, 3,441 nurses, 952 public health midwives and 3,415 support staff in various areas."
