    "chunk_text": "There are 400 ambulances in the health service that are more than 20 years old, of which around 50 percent are more than 25 years old. In order to ensure a better quality and more efficient service to the people, it is proposed to allocate Rs. 3,000 million in 2027 to add new ambulances to the system in place of the old ambulances. In addition, 25 ambulances through Asian Development Bank loan assistance and 20 new ambulances as a grant from Japan, coordinated by the Asian Development Bank, will be added within the next year.\n\nAn organ transplant centre, including for the liver, at a cost of Rs. 3,155 million, will be established within the National Hospital of Colombo with the financial contribution of local and foreign institutions and organizations. Rs. 50 million has been allocated in 2027 for the initial activities.\n\n*Rs. 400 million has been allocated to implement widely within the country the biological Wolbachia dengue vector control method, with the technical contribution of the World Mosquito Program (WMP) and the co-financing contribution of the Government, to control the dengue epidemic.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 100 million to provide spectacles free of charge to school children to minimize disruptions to education caused by visual impairments.\n\nIn addition to the development projects currently being implemented in hospitals providing secondary and tertiary care services, Rs. 1,245 million has been allocated to commence a number of new projects, including official quarters, at the Badulla and Batticaloa Teaching Hospitals, the Matale and Nawalapitiya District General Hospitals, and the Puttalam Base Hospital."
