    "chunk_size_bytes": 1857,
    "chunk_text": "Provisions have already been allocated to obtain vessels and machinery worth Rs. 3,380 million under Japanese cooperation to strengthen the capacity to respond promptly to marine and coastal pollution caused by oil spills, in order to protect the environment of the coastal belt.\n\nThe protection of the Central Highlands, which are under severe threat, is the protection of the future of our nation. For this, it is proposed to establish an Upper Watershed Area Management Authority to establish an integrated watershed management approach and for restoration activities. It is expected to present the relevant Act to Parliament very soon. Discussions have already commenced to obtain loan assistance of USD 100 million for the functions to be assigned to this Authority.\n\nIt is the expectation of our Government to usher in a new era in the transport sector to ensure an efficient, comfortable public transport service. Accordingly, a record Rs. 95,000 million will be deployed for modernizing railway and passenger bus services, strengthening connectivity between transport networks and promoting sustainable public transport.\n\nIt is expected to extend the Metro Bus service introduced around Colombo this year to the urban areas of Kandy, Galle and Jaffna as well.\n\nThe Government has invested in Metro Buses up to now. More than 120 buses are already in operation. A further 50 buses are scheduled to be added to that company in 2027. In addition, we have also planned to introduce electric buses. 100 buses are scheduled to be received for this purpose as a donation from the Government of China. Activities such as the construction of the depots required for these buses, the provision of the necessary charging facilities and the provision of training will commence next year, and provisions of Rs. 4,500 million have been allocated for this purpose."
