    "chunk_text": "The Government has invested in Metro Buses up to now. More than 120 buses are already in operation. A further 50 buses are scheduled to be added to that company in 2027. In addition, we have also planned to introduce electric buses. 100 buses are scheduled to be received for this purpose as a donation from the Government of China. Activities such as the construction of the depots required for these buses, the provision of the necessary charging facilities and the provision of training will commence next year, and provisions of Rs. 4,500 million have been allocated for this purpose.\n\nSteps have already been taken to import 600 air-conditioned buses to provide a comfortable and safe service to long-distance passengers.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to purchase 50 small buses of 22 seats required for rural areas with narrow hill roads.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 4,000 million to obtain 200 small buses of 33 seats required for passenger services in rural areas.\n\nRs. 200 million has been allocated for the Digital Transformation and Integrated Management Systems Development Project of the Sri Lanka Transport Board.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 600 million to establish the Department of Motor Traffic on the Werahera premises in order to provide a more efficient service.\n\nRs. 700 million has been allocated to establish a modern digital system for the process of vehicle registration and transfer of ownership, with the aim of providing efficient and transparent services to the public.\n\nRs. 1,500 million has been allocated to establish a new digital Driver Demerit Points System and a road safety enforcement system, integrating the Department of Motor Traffic and the Sri Lanka Police, to minimize road accidents and for road safety.\n\nRs. 5,000 million has been allocated to purchase 5 new trains for the railway service."
