    "chunk_text": "Provisions will continuously be provided to resolve step by step the problems relating to drinking water in the Jaffna and Vanni districts, such as seawater intrusion, high hardness, high mineral salts and bacterial contamination. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million for this purpose.\n\nRs. 12,000 million has been allocated to implement projects, including improving the capacity of existing drinking water projects, expanding distribution and constructing sanitation facilities.\n\nRs. 2,000 million has been allocated for improving community water supply schemes across the island.\n\nRs. 1,740 million has been allocated to implement the Ella, Moratuwa and Ekala wastewater management projects with the aim of improving sanitation facilities and managing wastewater in a formal manner.\n\nA secure house and a healthy urban environment are the most fundamental basis for the progress of a nation and its human resources. Our expectation is to uplift the living standards of the people by planning economic, social and physical development in an integrated manner, while protecting the natural and built environment.\n\nIt is expected to construct 70,000 houses under the \u201cA Place of One\u2019s Own \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d programme to resolve the housing problem of low-income earners. Under this programme, which has already commenced, it is expected to construct 10,000 new houses in 2027. The housing assistance provided per house under this programme will be increased from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 1.5 million. It is proposed to increase the provision currently allocated for this purpose to Rs. 15,000 million.\n\n13,000 families displaced due to the armed conflict that prevailed in the North and East have still not been resettled. It is the target of our Government to complete the resettlement of these families within 2 years. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated for this purpose, and it is proposed to allocate a further Rs. 4,000 million."
