    "chunk_text": "13,000 families displaced due to the armed conflict that prevailed in the North and East have still not been resettled. It is the target of our Government to complete the resettlement of these families within 2 years. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated for this purpose, and it is proposed to allocate a further Rs. 4,000 million.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 1,000 million for providing houses to those in areas such as Abaranchimulla, Serakkuliya, Mangalapura, Kandasamy Nagar and Nithya Nagar in Vavuniya, Pediyafarm, Polonnaruwa, Mullaitivu, Tissamaharama, Divulapitiya, Dimbulagala and Hennanigala South who were affected by the Ditwah disaster but did not become entitled to a house due to the existing criteria.\n\nThe owners of a large number of housing projects, which were commenced in the years 2015 - 19 on small financial assistance of Rs. 20,000 and Rs. 40,000 and were abandoned midway, have been put to great hardship. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million for financial assistance of up to Rs. 500,000 to eligible beneficiaries to complete the remaining construction work of half-completed houses.\n\nIt is expected to allocate Rs. 90,000 million through the Supplementary Estimate for the construction of houses under the Ditwah Housing Project.\n\nA requirement of 50,000 houses has been identified for urban low-income earners, of which construction of more than 16,000 houses has already been fully completed and construction of a further 5,000 houses has been partially completed. The partially completed housing projects at Torrington, Colombage Mawatha, Kolonnawa, Peliyagoda, Moratuwa, Maharagama and Dematagoda will be completed in 2027. It is also proposed to commence the construction of new housing complexes in the Meethotamulla and Wilgoda, Kurunegala areas. Rs. 26,820 million has been allocated for all these housing projects."
