    "chunk_text": "A requirement of 50,000 houses has been identified for urban low-income earners, of which construction of more than 16,000 houses has already been fully completed and construction of a further 5,000 houses has been partially completed. The partially completed housing projects at Torrington, Colombage Mawatha, Kolonnawa, Peliyagoda, Moratuwa, Maharagama and Dematagoda will be completed in 2027. It is also proposed to commence the construction of new housing complexes in the Meethotamulla and Wilgoda, Kurunegala areas. Rs. 26,820 million has been allocated for all these housing projects.\n\nInitiatives have already commenced to transform ten towns, Jaffna, Matale, Hatton, Batticaloa, Chilaw, Thambuttegama, Vavuniya, Eheliyagoda, Badulla, and Matara, into well-organized and systematic urban centers, as part of a city branding and tourism-focused urban development program. A sum of Rs. 2,700 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIn addition, it is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million for the year 2027 for 19 towns, namely Trincomalee, Kantale, Kalmunai, Dehiwala, Kalutara, Panadura, Matugama, Maharagama, Ratnapura, Kegalle, Bandarawela, Ella, Galle, Akuressa, Kurunegala, Puttalam, Nattandiya, Kiribathgoda, and Nuwara Eliya over and above the provisions already made for development activities through project estimates totaling Rs. 65,000 million.\n\nThe need to efficiently maintain drainage systems, carry out emergency operations during floods, and systematically maintain small canals and drainage systems in order to minimize flood risk in urban low-lying areas is increasing. For this, steps will be taken to obtain multipurpose machinery worth Rs. 1,250 million for the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation, and it is proposed to provide Rs. 625 million of this as Government equity capital."
