    "md5": "281ea0f7fb488940b4f35ce11306dd31",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "Severe congestion has arisen within the prison system of our country. Exceeding the capacity to hold around 16,500 persons in 22 prisons and 14 work camps, nearly 36,500 inmates, around twice that number, are currently being held.\n\nOfficers as well as inmates have lost their lives due to unfortunate incidents that occurred within prisons as a result of this congestion and the drug menace.\n\nIn line with the Galle Heritage City Development Plan and tourism zone promotion activities, it is proposed to allocate a sum of Rs. 500 million in this Budget for the commencement of the relocation of the current Galle Prison from its location to the Boossa area.\n\nRs. 1,000 million has been allocated for the expansion of the Wariyapola and Watareka Prisons, where development work has already commenced, to increase their holding capacity.\n\nRs. 500 million has been allocated for the relocation of the Matara Prison to the Kotawilawatta area in Matara.\n\nProvisions of Rs. 250 million have been allocated for the establishment of a Defence Development Research Centre, affiliated to the Ministry of Defence, for research carried out by the security forces.\n\nThere are teams in the security forces recruited for construction work. It is proposed to provide a special allowance to these personnel when they are deployed in various development programmes of the Government.\n\nAs a tribute to the parents of war heroes who joined the Armed Forces before 2009, it is proposed that the Ministry of Defence expeditiously prepare a programme to increase the monthly allowance of Rs. 750 currently paid to the mother and the father, and to implement it from July 2027.\n\nAn institution to provide consultancy services for public sector construction will be established by attaching professionals, including engineers, serving in the tri-forces. This institution will function as a consultancy institution in the planning, monitoring and supervision of Government projects."
  },
