    "md5": "8d95f57952e5e5f61ba16328f7882a4d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2000,
    "chunk_text": "An institution to provide consultancy services for public sector construction will be established by attaching professionals, including engineers, serving in the tri-forces. This institution will function as a consultancy institution in the planning, monitoring and supervision of Government projects.\n\nOur national identity has been established through all ethnicities and religions living in harmony as one family. It is one of our foremost responsibilities to formally conserve that heritage in order to bequeath it to future generations.\n\nFor this, steps will be taken to digitalize and conserve sacred places, historical artefacts and cultural identities through digital technological innovations such as 3D Laser Scanning used internationally as well as locally. This will make it possible to permanently maintain accurate three-dimensional models of the national heritage even in the face of natural disasters or weather impacts.\n\nRs. 7,000 million has been allocated in this Budget for the promotion and development of artistic activities associated with various ethnicities and religions.\n\nAnuradhapura is a sacred area of national and international importance in which many unique historical, archaeological, religious and cultural heritages of Sri Lanka are concentrated. It represents the historical heritage of Buddhist civilization. Therefore, we expect to implement a number of development activities, including improving the facilities required by devotees, road rehabilitation and waste management, while safeguarding its archaeological and religious values for future generations. An advisory council, co-chaired by the Acting Chief Prelate of the Atamasthana, has already been established to monitor and guide this programme. For this purpose, Rs. 1,076 million has already been allocated by the Central Cultural Fund for the year 2027. The Urban Development Authority has prepared an estimate of Rs. 8,200 million, and it is proposed to allocate Rs. 500 million for the year 2027."
