    "chunk_text": "The Government has provided provisions of Rs. 722 million for the rehabilitation of 1,328 places of religious worship damaged by the Ditwah disaster, comprising 758 Buddhist temples, 272 Hindu places of worship, 199 Muslim places of worship and 99 Christian places of worship. In addition, among the 1,328 destroyed places of religious worship, Rs. 40 million from the Buddha Sasana Fund for 30 Buddhist temples, and Rs. 523 million from the Central Cultural Fund for archaeological sites, including places of religious worship, are being utilized for rehabilitation, and a temple is also being rehabilitated through the Anagarika Dharmapala Trust with funds donated by the Maha Bodhi Society of India.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate Rs. 100 million to offer higher education scholarships and to provide support for the technological access required in journalism, in order to provide the necessary support for the skills development of journalists in keeping with the advancement in the field of mass media in parallel with modern technology.\n\nThe \u2018Clean Sri Lanka\u2019 programme aims to transform Sri Lankan life, extending well beyond mere physical cleanliness, by steering it toward a positive direction in social, environmental and ethical terms. Under its social pillar, the programme seeks to strengthen quality of life, dignity, safety, equal access, inclusivity, community participation and social harmony; under its environmental pillar, it focuses on promoting environmental protection, conservation, stewardship, biodiversity, responsible resource utilization and sustainability; and under its ethical pillar, it seeks to strengthen responsibility, honesty, discipline, fairness, efficiency and accountability regarding public resources. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated to implement these programmes."
