    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "The \u2018Clean Sri Lanka\u2019 programme aims to transform Sri Lankan life, extending well beyond mere physical cleanliness, by steering it toward a positive direction in social, environmental and ethical terms. Under its social pillar, the programme seeks to strengthen quality of life, dignity, safety, equal access, inclusivity, community participation and social harmony; under its environmental pillar, it focuses on promoting environmental protection, conservation, stewardship, biodiversity, responsible resource utilization and sustainability; and under its ethical pillar, it seeks to strengthen responsibility, honesty, discipline, fairness, efficiency and accountability regarding public resources. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated to implement these programmes.\n\nUnder the \u201cPivithuru Purawara\u201d (Clean Cities) National Waste Management Program, the objective is to increase the waste collection rate, currently at 32 percent to 60 percent by 2029, while promoting safe waste management and fostering a healthy, secure environment. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million to implement this project across 100 selected local government authorities under the \u201cClean Sri Lanka\u201d initiative.\n\nThe \u2018Clean Island\u2019 project, proposed to be implemented with the support of the Ministry of Energy, will develop the islands of Delft, Nainativu, and Analaitivu as \u2018model islands\u2019 for integrated development and transformation.\n\nA four-year project will be implemented to enhance the revenue-generating capacity of Local Government Institutions, utilize existing resources productively and strengthen financial sustainability. Through this, it is expected to continuously maintain the essential services of Local Government Institutions, and provisions of Rs. 1,000 million have been allocated for this purpose."
