    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "A four-year project will be implemented to enhance the revenue-generating capacity of Local Government Institutions, utilize existing resources productively and strengthen financial sustainability. Through this, it is expected to continuously maintain the essential services of Local Government Institutions, and provisions of Rs. 1,000 million have been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 50,000 million, at Rs. 2,000 million per district, to implement the District Development Programme and the Decentralized Budget Programme. Of this, Rs. 47,750 million will be allocated for special development programmes identified at district level, and the remaining Rs. 2,250 million for implementing the Decentralized Budget Programme, at Rs. 10 million per Member of Parliament.\n\nPlans are in place to improve both roads and bridges as part of the development of the rural road network. A sum of Rs. 55,000 million has been allocated for this purpose. In addition, Rs. 5,500 million has been allocated for the improvement of rural bridges including those under the purview of local government authorities while Rs. 20,000 million has been set aside for the maintenance and rehabilitation of Provincial Council roads. Accordingly, when the allocations under the District Development Programme are added to the aforementioned Rs. 80,000 million, a total of approximately Rs. 100,000 million has been earmarked for the development of rural roads.\n\nRs. 1,100 million has been allocated for the construction of new District Secretariat offices in the Vavuniya, Puttalam and Anuradhapura districts with the aim of providing an efficient and quality public service to the public.\n\nRs. 265 million has been allocated for the commencement of the construction of new Divisional Secretariat office buildings in Dehiattakandiya and Elapatha to further formalize public services at the regional level."
