    "chunk_text": "Rs. 265 million has been allocated for the commencement of the construction of new Divisional Secretariat office buildings in Dehiattakandiya and Elapatha to further formalize public services at the regional level.\n\nProvisions of Rs. 1,100 million have been allocated to complete the construction of the Kegalle and Nuwara Eliya District Secretariat offices and the Negombo, Homagama, Kalutara, Pitabeddara, Angunakolapelessa and Deraniyagala Divisional Secretariat offices, work on which has already commenced, in order to enhance the efficiency of public officers and provide a quality service to the public.\n\nRs. 4,500 million has been allocated to provide a new stock of computers in place of the old stock of computers held by public institutions. It is proposed to provide a further Rs. 2,200 million in addition.\n\nIt is proposed to resolve the issues existing within departmental services and other executive services, in alignment with the promotion mechanisms currently in place for island-wide services.\n\nIn order to provide adequate human resources for maintaining an efficient and quality public service in public institutions, approval has already been granted by the officials\u2019 committee on staff management appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers and the Department of Management Services for recruitment to 148,940 vacancies, while reviewing the recruitment process of the public service. Of this number, around 40,000 recruitments have been completed so far, and provisions will be allocated to recruit further 110,000 in the future.\n\nThe Sethsiripaya Stage III Project in Battaramulla has commenced. This project is expected to be completed in 2028, and Rs. 6,800 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIt is proposed to implement the Sethsiripaya Stage IV Project, with a day care centre, at Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Battaramulla, by deploying the funds of the Urban Development Authority."
