    "md5": "22f0e93825d87048146fa349abb78b6a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "The Sethsiripaya Stage III Project in Battaramulla has commenced. This project is expected to be completed in 2028, and Rs. 6,800 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\nIt is proposed to implement the Sethsiripaya Stage IV Project, with a day care centre, at Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Battaramulla, by deploying the funds of the Urban Development Authority.\n\nMeanwhile, public servants in various sectors have submitted requests to revise their allowances, considering the increase in the related expenses they have to bear in the performance of their duties. Taking into account those requests as well as the fiscal space currently available to the Government, we expect to increase several allowances on a priority basis through this Budget. Requests to revise other allowances will be considered in phases in future Budgets, taking into account the fiscal capacity of the Government.\n\nExecutive officers who are entitled to an official vehicle under Public Administration Circular No. 05/2016 but use their private vehicles in the performance of official duties are currently paid a monthly transport allowance of Rs. 50,000. Considering the increase in maintenance, repair and other operational costs when private vehicles are used for official duties, and since it is more cost-effective for the Government for officers who own a vehicle to use their private vehicle rather than being provided with a Government vehicle, in order to encourage this, it is proposed to increase the monthly transport allowance currently paid to Rs. 100,000.\n\nWith the aim of encouraging the use of electric vehicles, it is proposed to increase by 150 percent, with effect from July 2027, the monthly allowance paid in terms of Public Administration Circular 13/2008(V) to officers entitled to an official vehicle who use fully electric private vehicles."
