    "chunk_text": "With the aim of encouraging the use of electric vehicles, it is proposed to increase by 150 percent, with effect from July 2027, the monthly allowance paid in terms of Public Administration Circular 13/2008(V) to officers entitled to an official vehicle who use fully electric private vehicles.\n\nTo strengthen the national health system, it is proposed to increase the monthly special duty allowance of nursing officers and officers in the paramedical and supplementary medical services from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 12,000, and the monthly special duty allowance of other health staff from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000.\n\nIt is proposed to pay the above allowance increases proposed for the health sector in two steps. Accordingly, 50 percent of the increase will be paid from July 2027, and the remaining 50 percent in 2028.\n\nConsidering the important role played by university academic staff in improving the quality of higher education, promoting research activities and developing human resources, it is proposed to increase the monthly academic allowance currently paid to such staff by Rs. 25,000. It is expected to pay 50 percent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 percent from July 2028.\n\nIn order to attract external lecturers with specialist knowledge to universities for academic activities, it is proposed to increase the payments made to external lecturers threefold in line with the existing rates. Accordingly, it is proposed to increase the allowance currently paid per hour from Rs. 1,500 to Rs. 4,500. Further, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 600 paid per hour to external advisers for practical examinations to Rs. 1,800.\n\nIn order to attract external lecturers with specialist knowledge to vocational and technical institutions for vocational skills education, it is proposed to increase the payments made to external lecturers by 100 percent in line with the existing rates."
