    "md5": "ce1e86745c41c29f1af5af693825efa1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1899,
    "chunk_text": "In order to attract external lecturers with specialist knowledge to vocational and technical institutions for vocational skills education, it is proposed to increase the payments made to external lecturers by 100 percent in line with the existing rates.\n\nFood and Accommodation Allowance of Officers of the Sri Lanka Police\n\nConsidering the increase in food and accommodation expenses that police officers have to bear in the performance of their duties, it is proposed to increase the monthly food and accommodation allowance currently paid to meet such expenses by Rs. 10,000 with effect from July 2027.\n\nTaking into account the difficult and high-risk working conditions faced by prison officers in the performance of their duties, steps will be taken to increase the monthly risk allowance currently paid by 100 percent, from Rs. 8,000 to Rs. 16,000.\n\nLikewise, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 2,250 currently paid to civil officers serving in the Department of Prisons to Rs. 10,000.\n\nIt is proposed to pay these proposed allowances of officers serving in the Department of Prisons with effect from July 2027.\n\nConsidering the role played by field officers in directly providing essential public services to the community, and the increase in the costs associated with their field-based duties, it is proposed to increase the monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Grama Niladharis from Rs. 1,600 to Rs. 4,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 3,000 to Rs. 6,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\nThe monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Development Officers will be increased from Rs. 300 to Rs. 1,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 1,000 to Rs. 2,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 750 to Rs. 1,500 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas."
