    "chunk_text": "The monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Development Officers will be increased from Rs. 300 to Rs. 1,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 1,000 to Rs. 2,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 750 to Rs. 1,500 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\nIt is proposed to increase the monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Agriculture Research and Production Assistants from Rs. 400 to Rs. 1,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 3,000 to Rs. 6,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\nThe above allowances for field officers will be revised from April 2027.\n\nConsidering the professional responsibilities, the nature of service and the role of officers in the judicial sector, it is proposed to increase by Rs. 25,000 the monthly professional allowance currently paid to High Court Judges, Special Grade Judicial Officers and Judicial Officers of other grades. Steps will be taken to pay 50 percent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 percent in 2028.\n\nWith effect from July 2027, it is proposed to increase by Rs. 50,000 the monthly transport allowance currently paid to officers entitled to official vehicles, to increase the monthly driver allowance paid to entitled officers from Rs. 25,000 to Rs. 50,000, and, considering the increase in the expenses that have to be borne to meet their residential needs in instances where the Government has not provided an official residence, whether owned or obtained on a lease basis, to increase by 100 percent the monthly housing allowance currently paid to High Court Judges and other Judges."
