    "chunk_text": "Taking into account the role played by judicial support staff in maintaining the efficient functioning of the judicial system, their workload and the responsibilities assigned to them, steps will also be taken to increase the relevant allowances paid to these officers with effect from April 2027.\n\nMonthly Allowances of Independent Commissions, Other Commissions and Statutory Institutions\n\nThe monthly allowances paid to the Chairpersons and members of other Commissions will be revised as per the Annexure VI.\n\nFurther details on the revision of the above allowances are included in the Technical Note.\n\nThe Government is implementing a phased pension revision programme with the objective of ensuring a fair and structured pension system for all pensioners by systematically eliminating the disparities that exist among the pensions of retired public servants.\n\nThrough the first Budget in 2025, steps were taken to convert, in three phases, the pensions of public servants who retired prior to 2020 to the 2020 basic salary scale, and its first and second phases have already been completed. Its final phase is scheduled to be implemented in 2027.\n\nIt is also the objective of the Government to minimize and eliminate in phases, taking into account sustainable public financial management, the disparity that has arisen, due to the new basic salary revision implemented in 2025, between the pensions of public servants who retired before 2025 and those retiring in or after 2025.\n\nIt is proposed to provide a monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500, with effect from July 01, 2027, as a relief to pensioners who retired during the period from 2020 to 2024, until the pension revision scheduled to be carried out under the new 2025 basic salary structure is implemented."
