    "chunk_size_bytes": 1701,
    "chunk_text": "The tax slab to which the 6 percent tax rate applies will be Rs. 70,833 per month, and thereafter the tax slabs will be widened from Rs. 41,667 per month to Rs. 50,000 per month. The tax rates will be set at 6 percent, 12 percent, 18 percent, 24 percent, 30 percent and 36 percent, applying a rate of 12 percent instead of 18 percent after the 6 percent rate.\n\nAccordingly, as a combined result of the tax reforms introduced in 2025 and the revisions proposed for 2027, the total monthly tax relief provided by our Government to each individual taxpayer will increase ranging from a minimum of Rs. 4,250 to a maximum of Rs. 36,250.\n\n36.2 Enhanced Capital Allowances for Export-Oriented Manufacturing and Tourism Businesses Approved by the Board of Investment (BOI)\n\nWith the aim of encouraging private sector investment, promoting export-oriented manufacturing and strengthening the tourism sector, it is proposed to introduce enhanced capital allowances as an investment incentive for enterprises operating under agreements with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka.\n\nAccordingly, BOI-approved enterprises engaged in export-oriented manufacturing or tourism development activities with a minimum qualifying investment of USD 3 million will be permitted subject to meeting the relevant requirements to opt for an enhanced capital allowance equivalent to 200 percent of qualifying capital expenditure in place of the existing allowance regime.\n\n36.3 Exemption of Exercise Books and Printed Books from Value Added Tax (VAT)\n\nPrinted books and other printed materials became subject to Value Added Tax (VAT) effective from January 2024, while exercise books had been subject to VAT even before that date."
