    "md5": "bf587c97e550da07d3b6b709f1773de0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1977,
    "chunk_text": "36.3 Exemption of Exercise Books and Printed Books from Value Added Tax (VAT)\n\nPrinted books and other printed materials became subject to Value Added Tax (VAT) effective from January 2024, while exercise books had been subject to VAT even before that date.\n\n36.4 Revising the Basis for Calculating VAT Liability on Cinema Ticket Revenue\n\nWith the aim of ensuring the fair and equitable application of Value Added Tax within the film industry, we propose to revise the basis for calculating the VAT liability arising from the sale of cinema tickets.\n\nAccordingly, the VAT liability of film producers, distributors, the National Film Corporation and cinema hall operators will be determined on the basis of the share of cinema ticket revenue received by or allocated to each party at each stage, rather than calculating VAT on the full ticket value.\n\n36.5 Facilitating Earlier Qualification of Newly VAT Registered Exporters as \u201cEligible Exporters\u201d\n\nWith the aim of facilitating export-oriented businesses, I propose to revise the criteria under which newly VAT registered Exporters are recognized as Eligible Exporters.\n\nAccordingly, newly VAT registered persons will be recognized as Eligible Exporters where more than 80 percent of their turnover during the preceding six months has been derived from exports, without having to satisfy the existing requirement relating to the preceding Calander year.\n\n36.6 Use of the Indicative Exchange Rate of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka for Value Added Tax on Foreign Currency Supplies\n\nIn order to ensure greater transparency, consistency and fairness in valuing taxable supplies denominated in foreign currencies, it is proposed to use the Indicative Exchange Rate published by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka for the conversion of foreign currencies into Sri Lanka Rupees for VAT purposes. The Commissioner General of Inland Revenue (CGIR) will specify by way of a circular the manner in which such exchange rate is to be applied."
