    "language": "en",
    "md5": "48f62c77950cda273f64abb3bee111b5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1760,
    "chunk_text": "However, until a new Act is introduced, we propose to bring amendments to the Excise Ordinance by further simplifying this complex process and incorporating amendments into the existing Ordinance itself.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate as provisions for 2027 the amount that has not been utilized so far, due to reasons including the war situation in the Middle East, out of the Supplementary Estimate of Rs. 500 billion approved by Parliament for the reconstruction of Ditwah damage. Budgetary provisions of Rs. 260 billion have to be secured again for 2027 to properly complete the Ditwah reconstruction activities.\n\nAccordingly, in addition to the 2027 Budget I have presented, it is proposed to present to Parliament a Supplementary Estimate for Ditwah reconstruction expenditure in accordance with the provisions of Section 16 of the Public Financial Management Act.\n\nIt is proposed to table that Supplementary Estimate today, following the Budget Speech.\n\nOur Budget proposals are not confined to paper alone. They are proposals that are implemented in practice on the ground. Therefore, every new proposal will have a clearly accountable institution, outcome indicators, national priorities, a cash flow plan and a transparency that can be easily observed by the public. What we are striving to build is a country that safeguards the dignity of the citizen, ensures the safety of the child, gives due value to labour, creates opportunities for knowledge and protects natural resources for future generations.\n\nHaving overcome the challenges that prevailed and built stability in the economy, our next target is to commence a forward-looking and transformative era in 2027. For this, the collective strength and contribution of all of you is essential to us."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
