    "chunk_index": 95,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "72c416cfada9b71092b7f9340d9160a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1716,
    "chunk_text": "Having overcome the challenges that prevailed and built stability in the economy, our next target is to commence a forward-looking and transformative era in 2027. For this, the collective strength and contribution of all of you is essential to us.\n\nPolitics must be done by going among the people on the ground, not by tying threads in cemeteries at night, nor by wasting the time of Parliament reciting curse verses.\n\nLikewise, read the Kalama Sutta, which the Lord Buddha preached to the Kalamas (the residents of the town of Kesaputta), pointing out that nothing should be accepted blindly but should be examined with wisdom, and understand the revolution the Lord Buddha made against blind faith. Read the Agga\u00f1\u00f1a Sutta, which the Lord Buddha preached against superstition, and the Kevatta Sutta, preached against false incantations, and understand the ideological revolution brought about by the Lord Buddha.\n\nIn the Tevijja Sutta, the Lord Buddha asks whether, if a man standing on this bank of a river, wishing to go to the other bank, neither swims nor uses a boat but prays to the far bank, saying \u201cCome here, far bank, come here\u201d, the far bank would come to this side.\n\nWe have a very clear, progressive and proud dream for our motherland. Our hope is to make this country not merely an island, but one of the most advanced countries, not only in Asia but in the whole world, rich in knowledge, skills and modern technology.\n\nToday, we are implementing a strong programme towards that end. We have commenced the transformation of making our younger generation and our children across the country fully skilled, advanced citizens by providing them with modern technology, science and global knowledge."
  },
  {
