    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a5a831671b3de00747455408cb29f14f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1532,
    "chunk_text": "Today, we are implementing a strong programme towards that end. We have commenced the transformation of making our younger generation and our children across the country fully skilled, advanced citizens by providing them with modern technology, science and global knowledge.\n\nCriticize the Government. Question our policies. Present a better alternative programme than ours. We fully accept your democratic right to do so. But bring alternative policies instead of curse verses, creative solutions instead of sorcery, and intelligent dialogue instead of yaga and homa rituals into the politics of this country. When the people of our country are moving forward with technology and intelligence, should the politics of the Opposition alone turn upside down and go backwards? I would like to remind at this moment that building a political culture that befits the civilized, enlightened and proud Sri Lankan identity we are trying to build before the world is a fundamental responsibility entrusted not only to the Government, but also to the Opposition. The intelligent people of this country will never again set foot in that old darkness.\n\nWhat we must leave behind for future generations is not our party disputes, but a prosperous and just country whose future they can take over with confidence.\n\nTherefore, let us make the name \u201cSri Lankan\u201d not merely a name we pronounce with pride, but a proud name that the whole world accepts with respect.\n\nLet us prove our pledge towards that, not merely in words, but through action."
  },
