    "md5": "e009104f74993bd2b5ebe5f94a4d16d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1590,
    "chunk_text": "EDB and Digital Economy Ministry strengthen collaboration to achieve US$ 5bn ICT export target by 2030\n\nA high-level discussion on the implementation of Sri Lanka\u2019s National Export Development Plan (NEDP) 2026\u20132030 was held between the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) and the Ministry of Digital Economy recently, focusing on strengthening the contribution of the ICT/BPM sector towards achieving the country\u2019s export growth ambitions.\n\nThe meeting was chaired by Eng. Eranga Weeraratne, Deputy Minister of Digital Economy, with the participation of G. G. S. C. Roshan, Secretary to the Ministry of Digital Economy, Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, and senior officials of GovTech. The EDB delegation was led by Mangala Wijesinghe, Chairman, and included Erandika Dissanayake, Director General, Kumudinie Mudalige, Additional Director General (Development) and other senior officials.\n\nThe NEDP 2026\u20132030, formulated by the EDB under the guidance of the Ministry of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, with technical assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), serves as Sri Lanka\u2019s national framework for advancing export development. The Plan sets an ambitious target of increasing total exports to US$ 36 billion by 2030, including a dedicated target of US$ 5 billion from digital products and services.\n\nThe discussion focused on identifying strategic interventions and strengthening the role of the Ministry of Digital Economy and its affiliated institutions, including GovTech, as Lead Implementing Agencies responsible for delivering key actions under the NEDP."
  },
