    "chunk_text": "Aitken Spence\u2019s 2Q attributable profit slips 4%\n\nAitken Spence PLC\u2019s profit attributable to shareholders fell 4 percent to Rs. 381.1 million in the September quarter, even as Group pre-tax profit rose 67 percent to Rs. 1.07 billion on a stronger contribution from equity-accounted investees. Earnings per share eased to 94 cents from 98 cents a year earlier.\n\nGroup revenue rose 6 percent to Rs. 22.76 billion in the second quarter of FY2026/27, according to interim results filed with the Colombo Stock Exchange. Operating profit fell 32 percent to Rs. 851.9 million as staff costs and indirect operating expenses rose and the Group recorded a net charge of Rs. 386.5 million under other operating income, compared with income of Rs. 21.2 million a year earlier.\n\nNet finance costs rose 29 percent to Rs. 1.43 billion. The Group\u2019s share of profit from equity-accounted investees more than tripled to Rs. 1.65 billion from Rs. 488.5 million, more than offsetting the decline in operating profit and the increase in finance costs.\n\nGroup profit after tax climbed to Rs. 340.9 million from Rs. 16.1 million. Losses attributable to non-controlling interests narrowed to Rs. 40.2 million from Rs. 381 million a year earlier, accounting for the divergence between the rise in Group profit and the decline in earnings attributable to Aitken Spence shareholders.\n\nFor the six months ended September, Group revenue rose 2.6 percent to Rs. 41.72 billion and pre-tax profit increased 71.4 percent to Rs. 2.82 billion. First-half profit attributable to shareholders nearly doubled to Rs. 1.83 billion from Rs. 930.8 million, lifting earnings per share to Rs. 4.51 from Rs. 2.29."
