    "chunk_text": "For the six months ended September, Group revenue rose 2.6 percent to Rs. 41.72 billion and pre-tax profit increased 71.4 percent to Rs. 2.82 billion. First-half profit attributable to shareholders nearly doubled to Rs. 1.83 billion from Rs. 930.8 million, lifting earnings per share to Rs. 4.51 from Rs. 2.29.\n\nTourism remained the Group\u2019s largest business by revenue, generating Rs. 25.96 billion in the first half. Its pre-tax loss nearly doubled to Rs. 1.64 billion, with the company citing weaker occupancy and higher operating costs in the Maldives. The listed hotel subsidiary, Aitken Spence Hotel Holdings PLC, separately reported a September-quarter loss of Rs. 970.8 million despite a 12 percent increase in net revenue to Rs. 10.86 billion.\n\nThe strategic investments division\u2019s first-half pre-tax loss widened to Rs. 325.7 million from Rs. 186.8 million. The company said maintenance disrupted power generation and its apparel operations continued to report losses. On 3 November, Aitken Spence completed the sale of its entire stake in an apparel subsidiary with three production facilities."
