    "chunk_text": "Net Interest Income (NII) reached Rs. 169.2 billion, reflecting an 10 percent increase compared with the corresponding period of the previous year. Interest income increased by 6 percent to Rs. 390.8 billion, while interest expenses increased by 3 percent to Rs. 221.6 billion. This performance reflects the Bank\u2019s continued focus on optimizing its earning assets, managing funding costs and maintaining an effective asset-liability position amid changing market conditions.\n\nOperating profit before taxes on financial services reached Rs. 118.8 billion. After accounting for taxes on financial services amounting to Rs. 24.7 billion and income tax expenses of Rs. 35.4 billion, the Bank recorded a Profit Before Tax (PBT) of Rs.\u00a0 94.1 billion and a Profit After Tax (PAT) of\u00a0 \u00a0Rs. 58.7 billion respectively.\n\nExtending its contribution beyond financial performance, BOC contributed Rs.\u00a0 60.1 billion in direct taxes to the Government during the period, reaffirming its significant contribution to national revenue and economic stability.\n\nDuring the period, the Bank recognized an impairment charge of Rs. 16.8 billion on loans and advances, compared with Rs. 18.7 billion in the corresponding period of 2025. This reflects the Bank\u2019s continued focus on assessing expected credit losses across lending segments and maintaining adequate provisioning buffers.\n\nAsset quality remained a key priority, with the Stage 3 loan ratio (Net) standing at 4.97 percent. The Stage 3 provision coverage ratio stood at 61.70 percent, reflecting the Bank\u2019s provisioning strength and continued focus on maintaining portfolio resilience.\n\nStrengthened credit evaluation, proactive portfolio monitoring, enhanced recovery mechanisms and disciplined lending practices continued to support the Bank in effectively managing credit exposures and maintaining sound asset quality."
