    "md5": "474ec01adac6865b78d5dd30d06f495e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1706,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath posts Rs. 8.68bn 3Q profit, pre-tax earnings fall 7%\n\nSampath Bank PLC\u2019s group net profit rose 15 percent to Rs. 8.68 billion in the September quarter, helped by a lower income tax bill. Profit before income tax fell 7 percent to Rs. 11.18 billion, with higher operating costs and impairment charges absorbing the gains from stronger lending income.\n\nGroup net interest income climbed 26 percent to Rs. 25.27 billion and net fee and commission income rose 11 percent to Rs. 6.93 billion. A Rs. 4.76 billion net trading loss, against a Rs. 355 million gain a year earlier, held total operating income growth to 10 percent. Operating expenses rose 23 percent to Rs. 15.68 billion and impairment charges more than doubled to Rs. 1.13 billion. The group\u2019s income tax expense fell 45 percent to Rs. 2.51 billion. At the bank level, quarterly net profit rose 18 percent to Rs. 8.01 billion, while profit before income tax fell 8 percent to Rs. 10.08 billion. Net interest income rose 24 percent to Rs. 23.13 billion and net fees grew 14 percent to Rs. 6.70 billion. Operating income increased 9 percent, while expenses rose 22 percent and the impairment charge more than doubled to Rs. 1.07 billion. The bank\u2019s quarterly income tax expense halved to Rs. 2.07 billion.\n\nFor the first nine months, group net profit increased 15 percent to Rs. 26.54 billion, while profit before income tax slipped 1% to Rs. 37.81 billion. The bank\u2019s standalone net profit also rose 15 percent, to Rs. 24.63 billion, even as profit before income tax fell 2 percent to Rs. 34.64 billion. Sampath attributed the reduction in the bank\u2019s nine-month tax bill primarily to the finalisation of prior-year tax assessments."
