    "chunk_text": "For the first nine months, group net profit increased 15 percent to Rs. 26.54 billion, while profit before income tax slipped 1% to Rs. 37.81 billion. The bank\u2019s standalone net profit also rose 15 percent, to Rs. 24.63 billion, even as profit before income tax fell 2 percent to Rs. 34.64 billion. Sampath attributed the reduction in the bank\u2019s nine-month tax bill primarily to the finalisation of prior-year tax assessments.\n\nThe stock of Stage 3 loans, which are classified as credit-impaired, fell by Rs. 14.4 billion from year-end. The nine-month charge for loan impairments rose to Rs. 8.1 billion from Rs. 2.3 billion, which Sampath attributed mainly to higher collective provisions on its expanded loan book and additional buffers. A Rs. 1.3 billion impairment reversal on other financial instruments, linked mainly to lower provisions on foreign-currency bonds following Fitch\u2019s sovereign upgrade, helped limit the bank\u2019s total impairment charge to Rs. 6.0 billion.\n\nThe bank\u2019s common equity Tier 1 ratio fell to 12.27 percent from 14.75 percent at end-2025, while its total capital ratio declined to 15.32 percent from 17.65 percent. Sampath said loan growth increased risk-weighted assets and that its capital ratios remained above regulatory requirements. The bank raised Rs. 10 billion through a Basel III-compliant debenture issue in October, after the reporting period."
