    "chunk_text": "Operating profit before taxes on financial services rose 11.3 percent to Rs. 96.49 billion. Taxes on financial services increased 25.4 percent to Rs. 16.75 billion, leaving profit before income tax at Rs. 79.74 billion, up 8.7 percent. Group gross loans and advances increased by Rs. 348.37 billion, or 16.7 percent, from end-2025 to Rs. 2.43 trillion at September 30. The loan book was 27.6 percent larger than a year earlier. Group deposits rose 15.5 percent from end-2025 to Rs. 3.12 trillion, while total assets increased 14.7 percent to Rs. 3.87 trillion.\n\nCurrent and savings accounts accounted for 37.08 percent of deposits at end-September, down from 39.65 percent at end-2025.\n\nThe bank\u2019s gross impaired loan ratio fell to 5.31 percent from 5.81 percent at end-2025 and 6.25 percent a year earlier. Its net impaired loan ratio declined to 1.47 percent from 1.54 percent at end-2025, while provision coverage of impaired loans fell to 72.35 percent from 73.50 percent.\n\nCommercial Bank\u2019s Tier 1 capital ratio declined to 12.50 percent from 13.03 percent at end-2025, while its total capital ratio fell to 16.35 percent from 16.69 percent. Both remained above the regulatory minimums of 10 percent and 14 percent respectively. The bank attributed the declines to asset growth and the exclusion of third-quarter profit from the capital calculations."
