    "chunk_text": "Ports, partnerships and protections anchor Budget 2027\u2019s investment pitch\n\nThe main objective of this Budget is to move from economic stability towards transformation. It is to achieve a progressive transformation in every sphere, including investment, exports, productive employment, social welfare and sustainability\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development presenting the 2027 Budget in parliament yesterday\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s pitch to investors comes with a timetable where within two months, the government expects to seek proposals for a privately backed logistics centre at the Port of Colombo. In early 2027, it plans to take a public-private partnership law to parliament.\n\nBoth will offer early tests of whether President Anura Kumara Dissanayake\u2019s third budget can turn economic stability into projects businesses are prepared to finance.\n\nPresenting the Budget to parliament yesterday, Dissanayake traced a progression from stabilising the economy in his first budget to giving greater weight to production, investment and institutional reform in his second. The third, he said, would put those reforms into effect.\n\n\u201cThe main objective of this Budget is to move from economic stability towards transformation. It is to achieve a progressive transformation in every sphere, including investment, exports, productive employment, social welfare and sustainability,\u201d said President Dissanayake."
