    "chunk_size_bytes": 1779,
    "chunk_text": "Pat Cummins reveals reason behind \u2019spat\u2019 with wife Becky. It\u2019s Usman Khawaja\n\nNDTV SPORTS - Australian skipper Pat Cummins broke his silence on his viral video of an apparent argument with his wife Becky, saying that it was not a spat; rather, she was \"really unhappy\" with his former teammate Usman Khawaja's fresh revelations on the 2018 ball-tampering scandal during the South Africa tour.\n\nCummins on Friday addressed a presser, denying Khawaja's bombshell 2018 Sandpaper Gate revelations made in his autobiography titled 'Sabr' and the effect it has had on him and the Australian cricketing fraternity. Hours before the presser took place, a video of Cummins appearing to have a tense argument with his wife went viral on social media.\n\nSpeaking during the presser, as quoted by Fox Sports, the Aussie skipper said that it was \"a bit ridiculous\" to have his private life being made public, but revealed that the discussion was around Khawaja, with Becky really \"frustrated and unhappy\" with the former batter's claims that have sparked a fresh discussion around the eight-year-old controversy and the need to reinvestigate it.\n\n\"While we are on the topic, because we think it was funny - we were not having a spat,\" he said. \"Becky was very frustrated and animated and really unhappy with Usman,\" he added.\n\n\"We weren't having a spat. Becky was very frustrated, animated, and really not happy with Usman.\" MORE: https://t.co/0PIKdMHu6W https://t.co/xJvtxQaqYu\n\nEarlier, speaking during the presser at Sydney's Cricket Central, Cummins said, as quoted by Fox Sports, that Khawaja's claims that everyone, including the bowling quartet of Cummins, Mitchell Starc, Josh Hazlewood and Nathan Lyon, were aware of sandpaper being brought to the field were 100 per cent wrong."
