    "chunk_text": "SriLankan Airlines increases Melbourne flights to 10 per week\n\nColombo, Nov. 13 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0SriLankan Airlines will operate three additional weekly flights to Melbourne from November 15, increasing its services to Australia to 14 flights a week amid rising travel demand between the two countries.\n\nThe additional flights will operate on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Sundays, adding to the airline\u2019s existing daily Melbourne service.\n\nUnder the revised schedule, flight UL608 will depart Colombo at 2.15 p.m. and arrive in Melbourne at 5.40 a.m. the following day. The return flight, UL609, will depart Melbourne at 7.10 a.m. and arrive in Colombo at 12.10 p.m.\n\nThe existing daily service will continue, with flight UL604 departing Colombo at 12.35 a.m. and arriving in Melbourne at 4.00 p.m. Its return flight, UL605, will leave Melbourne at 5.30 p.m. and arrive in Colombo at 10.30 p.m.\n\nIn a statement, the national carrier said the expansion was in response to growing travel demand between Sri Lanka and Australia.\n\nAustralia has also emerged as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s fastest-growing inbound tourism markets, supported by leisure travellers and the Sri Lankan diaspora."
