    "chunk_text": "SLFP still a recognised political party, Election Commission clarifies\n\nThe Sri Lanka Freedom Party (SLFP) continues to be recognised as a political party, although a dispute over the party\u2019s secretary position remains unresolved, the National Election Commission has clarified.\n\nThe clarification was issued following reports suggesting that the SLFP was no longer recognised as a registered political party.\n\nAccording to the Commission, the SLFP has retained its status as a recognised political party but has been placed under the category of parties with a disputed secretary position since 2025.\n\nThe situation arose following a disagreement between two rival factions within the party over who holds the position of secretary.\n\nThe Commission said it had summoned representatives of both factions for discussions on November 6 following requests to intervene and resolve the dispute.\n\nAt the meeting, both parties agreed that the matter should remain unresolved until the Western Province Civil Appellate High Court delivers its judgment in the case currently before it.\n\nAccordingly, the Commission said a decision on the disputed secretary position would be made after the court ruling. It"
