    "md5": "f3b4f464b797bdcfbf82998e67d6e197",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 865,
    "chunk_text": "India is simultaneously making its medical visa system more flexible. Conventional medical treatment will fall under the M-1 category, while M-3 will cover treatment through AYUSH traditional medicine systems.\n\nThe measures support India\u2019s broader \u201cHeal in India\u201d initiative, targeting international patients requiring several consultations or extended treatment.\n\nOther reforms streamline visas for foreign students, researchers, investors and business professionals.\n\nIndia currently offers electronic visas to nationals of 172 countries. Its authorities are updating the technology supporting the new framework, with implementation expected by the end of 2026.\n\nFor international tourism operators, the wider visitor provisions could make India a more attractive destination for travelers combining leisure with wellness, education and business activities."
