    "chunk_size_bytes": 1210,
    "chunk_text": "Three Chinese food businesses fined Rs. 444,000\n\nColombo, Nov. 13 (Daily Mirror) - Three Chinese food businesses operating in Colombo have been fined a total of Rs. 444,000 over 148 violations of food safety regulations.\n\nThe fines were imposed by the Maligakanda Magistrate\u2019s Court on Friday (13), following legal action initiated by the Colombo Municipal Council (CMC) based on inspections carried out by its Public Health Inspectors (PHIs).\n\nThe businesses include two Chinese restaurants operating inside a popular shopping mall in Colombo and an ice cream company.\n\nThe two restaurants were fined a combined Rs. 360,000 after being found guilty of 120 charges relating to food safety violations.\n\nDuring surprise inspections, PHIs discovered imported food products being sold and used for consumption without proper labels. They also found stocks of expired food items at the establishments.\n\nFollowing the discoveries, the CMC initiated legal proceedings against the companies operating the restaurants.\n\nThe Maligakanda Magistrate\u2019s Court subsequently imposed fines totalling Rs. 360,000 on the two businesses.\n\nThe three businesses were fined a combined Rs. 444,000 over 148 food safety violations."
