    "chunk_size_bytes": 1201,
    "chunk_text": "Bus driver involved in fatal Rambewa accident found to have been under influence of drugs\n\nColombo, Nov. 14 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Mihintale Police have confirmed that the driver of the bus involved in the recent accident, which killed four people and injured 76 others, had been under the influence of drugs, according to the post-mortem examination.\n\nPolice said reckless driving by the driver had caused the accident. The ill-fated bus belonged to the Kebithigollewa depot. The driver has been identified as Lanka Jayanath, a resident of Ataweeragollewa, Hirallugama, Kebithigollewa.\n\nEarlier, Transport Minister Bimal Rathnayake also confirmed that the driver had been under the influence of drugs at the time of the accident.\n\nThe accident occurred when a Colombo-bound bus travelling from Janakapura collided head-on with a Jaffna-bound bus travelling from Akkaraipattu. Meanwhile, another Colombo-bound private bus travelling from Vavuniya crashed into the two buses from behind.\n\nThe accident occurred on the morning of November 10 near the Rambewa\u2013Weli Oya junction on the A9 Kandy\u2013Jaffna main road in Anuradhapura. Four people were killed and 76 others were injured when three buses collided."
  },
