    "chunk_size_bytes": 1143,
    "chunk_text": "The risk of flash floods and landslides is considered particularly high as the ground across much of the country is already saturated following heavy rainfall experienced over the past week.\n\nThe advisory further noted that approximately 17 major reservoirs had reached spill levels last week, while landslide early warnings had been issued for seven districts from November 12.\n\nThe developing weather system could also bring thundershowers accompanied by strong gusty winds reaching 60 to 70 kilometres per hour, along with lightning.\n\nMeanwhile, sea conditions off the northern and eastern coasts could become rough, prompting further caution for coastal communities and those engaged in maritime activities.\n\nUrging the public and businesses to take precautionary measures, A-PAD SL advised people to clear drainage systems, move vehicles and valuable equipment to higher ground and avoid travelling through flooded roads.\n\nThe organisation also stressed the importance of closely monitoring official weather updates and following evacuation instructions issued by the Disaster Management Centre to minimise the risk to lives and property."
