    "md5": "3ecd205640babc3e0910c5b71e09d9d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1504,
    "chunk_text": "Truck and bus crash in India\u2019s Assam state kills at least 24 people\n\nAl Jazeera - At least 24 people have been \u2060\u2060killed and 11 others injured, after a container truck collided with a bus in \u2060\u2060India\u2019s northeastern state of Assam, police said.\n\nThe crash happened on Friday on a highway in Golaghat district, near Kaziranga National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site famous for its one-horned rhinos, about 225km (140 miles) east of the state capital, Dispur.\n\nSeveral children and the bus driver were among the dead, officials said, as Assam Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma said on X he was \u201cdeeply distressed by the tragic accident\u201d.\n\n\u201cThe scale of this loss has shaken all of us, and my heart goes out to every family that has lost a loved one. No words can ease their pain, but I want them to know that they are not alone. All of Assam stands with them in this hour of grief,\u201d Sarma said.\n\nHe added that local authorities were at the site and \u201cpersonally overseeing the relief arrangements \u2026 to make sure the injured receive the best possible medical care without delay\u201d.\n\nSwapnaneel Deka, superintendent of police of Golaghat district, told the Reuters news agency that \u201cit is likely the death toll will increase\u201d. He said the bus \u2060\u2060was travelling to a neighbouring district, with about 30 people on board.\n\nIndia has one of the highest rates of road fatalities in the world, with accidents happening regularly in part due to poorly maintained roads and vehicles."
  },
