    "chunk_text": "Republic and robe\n\nTo rescue the spiritual heritage from political manipulation, the State must look back to move forward. It must re-establish the core tenets of Ashokan Buddhism that Arahat Mahinda brought to the island. Ashokan governance was defined not by giving a monastic monopoly unchecked constitutional vetoes, but by active State purification of the Sangha, enforcing strict moral accountability. These make-believe edifices built on elite preservation and structural immunity are historically unsustainable\n\nAnuradhapura, the enduring crucible witness to grand history of our noble kings, has today turned into an amphitheater for a comic opera staged by a disparate and desperate opposition.\n\nIn a frantic bid for survival, a strange coalition of the Rajapaksa\u2019s Ranil Wickremesinghe, Sajith Premadasa, and Dilith Jayaweera have all lined up to present themselves as the new champions of the saffron robe.\n\nOf all the opposition mandarins, Sajith Premadasa stands out as the most eloquent reservoir of hogwash, vehemently insisting that no secular law can ever supersede the inviolability of the saffron robe.\n\nHe completely forgets that the Enlightened Master explicitly directed his followers to stitch their robes out of \u2018paansa kula\u2019 the discarded, decaying cloths gathered from cemetery cadavers.\n\nThey all rush to the Ancient City to launch their bids to return to relevance and credibility! Yet, the street-level agitations of the saffron-clad political actor known as Balangoda Kassapa was never a spontaneous movement.\n\nIt is nothing but a theatrical curtain-raiser for a much broader, systemic offensive against the NPP Government and President Anura Kumara Dissanayake (AKD).\u00a0 It is a war by other means\u2014the other means being the saffron shield."
