    "chunk_text": "We would do well to remember that even the Kandyan King Keerthi Sri Rajasinha, who facilitated the historic 1753 return of the higher ordination from Siam, fiercely retained absolute sovereign authority over the clergy.\n\nIf an 18th-century absolute monarch understood that spiritual robes do not grant immunity against the laws of State survival, why has a modern democratic republic forgotten it? President AKD, it is time to learn from our history.\n\nThe current standoff exposes the ultimate irony of our contemporary political landscape. A disgruntled political class, having lost their grip on the nation\u2019s rudder, is now reduced to the sorry state of clinging to the aging udder of a worn-out sacred cow. When retired Admiral Sarath Weerasekara\u2014a blinkered ideologue of the old guard and now media mogul DJ\u2019s fellow\n\ntraveller\u2014is seen holding backroom meetings at five-star hotels with Kasun Kularatne alias Balangoda Kassapa under the guise of paying homage, the farce is laid bare.\n\nSurely, the Buddha Sasana Ministry should possess the precise details of Balangoda Kassapa\u2019s\u00a0 registration, the recognised Nikaya to which he belongs, and the specific ecclesiastical lineage from which he received his higher ordination!\n\nThat it does not is the ultimate proof of an intentionally constructed blind spot in this whole business.\n\nThe old regime can no longer rely on the traditional Sangha hierarchy, which has occasionally shown institutional restraint.\n\nInstead, they are forced to subsidise, amplify, and weaponise independent actors masquerading in saffron to manufacture moral panics on demand.\n\nThey are aided by private television channels brazenly dedicated to giving them unhindered, unlimited exposure under the convenient cover of freedom of expression.\n\nUnder free-market global commerce, the essence of Prince Siddhartha\u2019s renunciation has been distorted into a corporate shield by an entrepreneurial priestly class."
