    "chunk_text": "A brief commitment in the forthcoming Budget would be a valuable beginning, even if the full program is developed during 2027. It would not require Government to choose every business, find its customers or finance its investments. It would establish something more enduring: a responsibility to keep opening productive opportunities and to show, quarter by quarter, what has become possible. The question at each review would be simple: what new earning activity can Sri Lankans undertake today that they could not undertake three months ago?\n\nOur grandparents planted trees without knowing who would gather the fruit. We continue to enjoy their gift. Let us respond with the same quiet sense of duty: open the channels now, enable new activities to take root, and allow time for them to flourish. The harvest may take years, but the planting must be done now.\n\n(The author is a Chartered Engineer, Founder and Chairman of the KIK Group of Companies, an export-oriented engineering and switchgear manufacturer and a Presidential Export Award winner. The views expressed are his own. He can be reached at [email\u00a0protected])"
