    "md5": "15c91a9f57da04271a82538a1dd8b2d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "LifeServ celebrates 25 years of healthcare service in Sri Lanka\n\nLifeServ Ltd., a Sumathi Holdings Company, marked its 25th anniversary recently, commemorating 25 years of growth and service within Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare sector. Established in 2001, the company has evolved from a focused healthcare product operation into an integrated healthcare solutions provider supporting hospitals, healthcare professionals, pharmacies, patients and households across the country.\n\nOver the past 25 years, LifeServ\u2019s journey has been shaped by changing healthcare needs and an expanding portfolio covering medical and surgical devices, pharmaceuticals and domestic healthcare products. The company has also developed capabilities across brand management, tenders, warehousing, retail and distribution, strengthening its presence across the healthcare ecosystem.\n\nThis growth has been supported by relationships with international healthcare manufacturers and organisations, including Abbott Vascular (USA), A&D Medical (Japan), Lobeck Medical (Switzerland), Kawaza (China), Beta Drugs Limited (India). These partnerships have enabled LifeServ to expand its portfolio and bring a wider range of healthcare products and solutions to the Sri Lankan market.\n\nReflecting on the milestone, CEO Chaminda Bandara said: \u201cI have been with LifeServ since the day it began, and the trust we have earned over these 25 years is a responsibility I hold close. This legacy belongs to our people, partners and healthcare professionals. Together, we will continue bringing trusted care and quality healthcare solutions closer to patients across Sri Lanka.\u201d"
  },
