    "chunk_size_bytes": 1980,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka reaffirms renewable energy ambitions at 9th session of International Solar Alliance\n\nSri Lanka reaffirmed its commitment to accelerating the transition to renewable energy and strengthening international cooperation in clean energy at the Ninth Session of the International Solar Alliance (ISA) Assembly, held in New Delhi from 3 to 5 November 2026 alongside the Bharat Renewable Energy Summit and Expo 2026.\n\nEnergy Deputy Minister Muhammadu Ilyas Muhammadu Arkam represented the Government of Sri Lanka at the Assembly and delivered Sri Lanka\u2019s National Statement during the High-Level Ministerial Segment.\n\nIn his statement, the Deputy Minister reiterated Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to increasing the share of renewable energy in electricity generation to 70% by 2030 and achieving carbon neutrality in the electricity generation sector by 2050, in line with Sri Lanka\u2019s Nationally Determined Contributions under the Paris Agreement.\n\nHe outlined Sri Lanka\u2019s efforts to expand renewable energy capacity while strengthening the resilience, reliability and efficiency of the national electricity system. These include initiatives relating to green hydrogen, electric mobility and charging infrastructure, battery energy storage systems and the strengthening and modernisation of the national electricity grid.\n\nThe Deputy Minister also highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s significant potential for further renewable energy development. Particular attention was drawn to opportunities for floating solar projects in identified reservoirs, as well as solar and wind development in the Northern, Eastern and Southern regions. The ongoing development of wind power projects in Mannar and the assessment of Sri Lanka\u2019s offshore wind potential were also highlighted as areas of future opportunity.\n\nSri Lanka further emphasised the importance of technology, knowledge-sharing, investment and capacity-building in translating its renewable energy ambitions into tangible outcomes."
  },
