    "md5": "1e52cffe1b12ee7dd94eb6d25cf2b3e5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "India-Sri Lanka Innovation Forum\n\nWith a view to continue the momentum and support private sector led endeavors, the India-Sri Lanka Innovation Forum was launched on 12 November 2026 in Colombo, in the presence of Indian High Commissioner\n\nThe launch was supported by the presence of corporate leaders including from Dialog Axiata PLC, John Keells Holdings PLC, Hayleys PLC, Hemas Holdings PLC and Sunshine Holdings PLC and prominent innovation- related networks and Centres of Excellence such as Trace Expert City, nVentures, Hatch, Slasscom, Lanka Angel Network and Yarl IT.\n\nIIT Madras Pravartak CEO Dr. Shankar Raman, Centre for Cellular and Molecular Platforms (C-CAMP) CEO and Director Dr. Taslimarif Saiyed, Atal Innovation Mission Director Dr. Deepak Bagla and Nasscom SME Council Chairman Maulik Bhansali also joined the event virtually.\n\nThe business-led Innovation Forum will bring together business leaders, incubators and funds to support innovation by startups, decide on joint projects and strengthen linkages between innovation ecosystems on both sides.\n\nIndia and Sri Lanka enjoy a strong partnership and goodwill across various sectors of the bilateral relationship. Through concerted effort, a distinct new pillar of collaboration has evolved which is focused on technology, innovation and startup collaboration.\n\nDuring the recent years, significant progress has been achieved in this regard, especially through the collaboration between the private sector and industry on both sides. This includes collaboration between StartUp India and ICTA (GovTech) and exploration of each other\u2019s startup ecosystems. Nasscom\u2019s \u2018Disha\u2019 program for Tech SMEs was extended to Sri Lanka as the first country outside India.\n\nIIT Madras Pravartak has run a six-week capacity building and full immersion programme for Sri Lankan startups, and has signed an MoU with SLASSCOM and Dialog PLC."
