    "chunk_text": "Kavantissa was a distinguished tusker, celebrated for his size, stature, temperament, and grandeur. He was a symbol of distinction, prestige, and public admiration. To an ideology uncomfortable with distinction, prestige, and status such a symbol can become an obstacle, not much as a physical obstacle, but as a powerful psychological one. When an ideology seeks to reshape a society, it does not stop with changing institutions. It seeks to redefine what people admire, respect, and aspire to become.\n\nAre you, as a Sri Lankan, prepared to be a victim of such an ideology? Today it may be Kavantissa. Tomorrow, could it be you?\n\n(The author, an Engineering Professor born, bred, and educated in Sri Lanka, a graduate from the Faculty of Engineering at the University of Peradeniya with First Class Honours, can be reached via: [email\u00a0protected])"
