    "chunk_size_bytes": 1981,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka to feature in exclusive Four Seasons private jet experience\n\nTravel Weekly - Four Seasons has a new around-the-world Private Jet Experience for 2028 called \u201cCoastlines & Culture,\u201d which travels from San Francisco to the English countryside, with stops in Asia, Africa, the Middle East and the South of France along the way.\n\nFour Seasons Private Jet Experiences use a custom-configured Airbus A321neo-LR that seats just 48 travelers. The experiences are operated and sold by TCS World Travel, and the aircraft itself is operated by Titan Airways Limited.\n\nThe new \u201cCoastlines & Culture\u201d journey runs May 6\u201326, 2028, and goes like this: Launching from San Francisco, guests cross the Pacific to Seoul, where they\u2019ll experience Korea\u2019s spiritual traditions through an immersive visit to Jingwansa Temple. Next stop is Hangzhou. There, guests join tea masters for a private experience at Meijuawu Tea Plantation and spend time at the centuries-old Jinshan Temple before a day trip to Shanghai.\n\nGuests then travel to Sri Lanka to visit a private cinnamon estate. From there, the route continues to Zanzibar, where guests stay at the highly anticipated Four Seasons Resort Zanzibar and Swahili heritage and longstanding spice traditions offer a window into the island\u2019s history. Next comes Sharm El Sheikh, where the Sinai desert meets the Red Sea, and the stay includes a private yacht charter along the coastline.\n\nFrom the Red Sea, guests make their way to Cap-Ferrat for a stay at one of the French Riviera\u2019s most iconic hotels, Grand-H\u00f4tel du Cap-Ferrat, A Four Seasons Hotel. A privately chartered yacht excursion to Cannes offers a relaxed way to explore the coast before the itinerary\u2019s final chapter in Hampshire. There, the English countryside sets the scene for a closer look at Britain\u2019s royal history, including exclusive access to Hampton Court Palace.\n\nA dedicated journey team includes a concierge, executive chef and journey physician."
