    "chunk_size_bytes": 1137,
    "chunk_text": "Mitsubishi seven-seater vehicle range places high emphasis on road safety and passenger protection\n\nFrom 19 September 2026, every passenger travelling on Sri Lanka\u2019s expressways is required to wear a seat belt, reinforcing the importance of passenger safety for motorists across the country.\n\nMitsubishi\u2019s seven-seater vehicle range addresses this need by providing seven seats, each equipped with a three-point Emergency Locking Retractor (ELR) seat belt, allowing families to travel together without compromising passenger safety.\n\nThe Mitsubishi Xpander, Mitsubishi Xpander Cross and Mitsubishi Destinator are seven-seater MUVs and SUVs designed to accommodate the travel needs of Sri Lankan families, combining passenger protection with comfort and practicality.\n\nEach of these models offers seven designated seating positions with individual three-point ELR seat belts, enabling passengers across all three rows to travel with appropriate restraint systems. This is particularly relevant under the expressway regulations, where seat belt compliance extends to every occupant, including those seated in the second and third rows."
