    "language": "en",
    "md5": "97185fa39719c7b94d16afa3002538da",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1646,
    "chunk_text": "Connect to Care strengthens platform for regional philanthropic partnerships\n\nConnect to Care (CTC) has reached two significant institutional milestones with its NGO registration and an Equivalency Determination (ED) on file with NGOsource, strengthening its foundation for philanthropic partnerships and its ability to support development priorities in Sri Lanka and across the wider region.\n\nConnect to Care Consulting\u2019s Equivalency Determination recognises the organisation as equivalent to a US public charity for international grantmaking purposes and remains valid until 31 March 2028. Together with its NGO registration, the milestone provides CTC with a stronger institutional platform to engage philanthropic organisations, development partners, governments and technical experts around programmes designed to deliver sustainable impact.\n\nThese developments represent an important step for CTC in its broader ambition to serve as a neutral platform for collaboration, connecting local knowledge and institutional experience with global expertise, philanthropy and implementation capabilities.\n\nChandita Samaranayake, Chairman of Connect to Care, said, \u201cThese milestones strengthen the institutional foundation from which Connect to Care can build meaningful partnerships in Sri Lanka and across the region. Our role is to bring together organisations and individuals with complementary capabilities around development priorities where collaboration can create lasting value. We want to provide a credible platform through which local experience, global expertise and philanthropic support can come together around shared outcomes.\u201d"
  },
