    "md5": "5c46a74fd32221a6ece775ed4478b440",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1449,
    "chunk_text": "Chandita Samaranayake, Chairman of Connect to Care, said, \u201cThese milestones strengthen the institutional foundation from which Connect to Care can build meaningful partnerships in Sri Lanka and across the region. Our role is to bring together organisations and individuals with complementary capabilities around development priorities where collaboration can create lasting value. We want to provide a credible platform through which local experience, global expertise and philanthropic support can come together around shared outcomes.\u201d\n\nThe Equivalency Determination is expected to further support CTC\u2019s engagement with US-based philanthropic organisations by simplifying an important aspect of the international grantmaking process for participating foundations. This creates a clearer pathway for CTC to develop partnerships that can support locally grounded programmes while connecting them with international expertise and resources.\n\nEmaali Gunasekara, Chief Executive Officer of Connect to Care, said, \u201cThere is significant knowledge and capability across the Global South, but that expertise often sits within individual institutions, countries or sectors. We see an opportunity to connect those capabilities more effectively. Our aim is not to create parallel structures, but to strengthen existing efforts by bringing the right partners, technical knowledge and resources together around clearly defined development priorities.\u201d"
