    "chunk_size_bytes": 1561,
    "chunk_text": "Seven SLIIT academics among world\u2019s top 2% scientists\n\nSeven academics from the Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology (SLIIT) have been recognised in the Stanford\u2013Elsevier World\u2019s Top 2% Scientists lists, highlighting the university\u2019s contribution to internationally acclaimed research.\n\nThe academics recognised in 2026 have produced pioneering researchin areas such as Artificial Intelligence and Intelligent Systems,Smart Energy, Wireless Communication, IoT, Nanotechnology, Biotechnology,Advanced Materialsand Structural Engineering.\n\nProf. Bhagya Nathali Silva of the Faculty of Computing, Prof. Charitha Jayaruk and Prof. Dhanushka Udayanga of the Faculty of Humanities and Sciences, Prof. Dushantha Jayakody, Dr. Pasindu Meddage of the Faculty of Engineering, Senior Deputy Vice-Chancellor and Provost, Prof. Nimal Rajapakse have been recognised for their research contributions in 2025.\n\nIn addition, Prof. Nimal Rajapakse, Prof. Priyan Dias, and Prof. Dushantha Jayakody have been recognized for their career-long contributions to research in their respective fields.\n\nDrawing on Elsevier\u2019s Scopus database, the Stanford\u2013Elsevier assessment uses standardised citation indicators to identify influential researchers across scientific disciplines.\n\nThe 2026 edition evaluates single-year citation impact during 2025 and career-long impact up to the end of 2025.Resonating with the international scientific community, the SLIIT-based scientistsare proof of SLIIT\u2019s deliberate move to position itself as a leading research university."
