    "md5": "e1bbd3dd4f7061d8660a8953e35baeb9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1859,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Port City Rotaractors take Project Aloka to Jaffna\n\nThe Rotaract Club of Colombo Port City brought its environmental initiative to Jaffna recently, together with the Rotaract Club of Jaffna Midtown and Rotaract Club of Chunnakam for a tree planting project at Kokuvil Hindu College.\n\nConducted under Project Aloka, the initiative brought together young volunteers with a shared commitment to protecting the environment and encouraging greater awareness of climate change and deforestation.\n\nThe project aimed to do more than add trees to the school premises. It sought to encourage students and the surrounding community to recognise the importance of tree planting, protect the existing green spaces and take greater responsibility for the environment. Through the participation of three Rotaract clubs, the initiative also brought together young Rotaractors from different parts of the country, uniting them around a cause that affects us all.\n\nSri Lanka continues to face growing environmental challenges, from changing weather patterns and rising temperatures to the loss of forest cover and the effects of deforestation. While these issues require long term attention and action, community initiatives such as Project Aloka demonstrate how young people can contribute to the effort through practical action.\n\nRotaract Club of Colombo Port City President Dhanush said, \u201cProject Aloka is built around a simple idea: meaningful change begins with simple action. Planting a tree may seem like a small contribution but it represents a commitment to the environment and to the generations that will follow us. Through this collaboration with our fellow Rotaractors in Jaffna, we hope to inspire more young people and communities to take an active interest in environmental conservation. Protecting our environment is a responsibility we all share.\u201d"
  },
