    "chunk_text": "Rotaract Club of Colombo Port City President Dhanush said, \u201cProject Aloka is built around a simple idea: meaningful change begins with simple action. Planting a tree may seem like a small contribution but it represents a commitment to the environment and to the generations that will follow us. Through this collaboration with our fellow Rotaractors in Jaffna, we hope to inspire more young people and communities to take an active interest in environmental conservation. Protecting our environment is a responsibility we all share.\u201d\n\nFor the Rotaract Club of Colombo Port City, Project Aloka is part of a wider commitment to community service and sustainable development. By taking the initiative to Jaffna, the club hopes to encourage more people to make tree planting and environmental conservation part of their everyday lives. As the trees planted at Kokuvil Hindu College take root, the message behind Project Aloka remains clear: a greener Sri Lanka will depend not only on the decisions made today but also on the actions taken by its people."
