    "language": "en",
    "md5": "eb02661578e4c64b730d7d7bb757114a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1495,
    "chunk_text": "Amana Bank invites children to \u2018My Future, My Dream\u2019 essay competition\n\nAmana Bank invites children to dream, imagine and express their aspirations, as it brings back its \u2018My Future, My Dream\u2019 all island essay competition.\n\nEndorsed by the Education Ministry, the competition invites children across Sri Lanka to showcase their creativity and share their dreams for the future.\n\nOpen to children between the ages of 10 and 18, the competition features two age categories. The participants between the ages of 10 and 14 can submit essays of up to 250 words, while those between 15 and 18 can submit essays of up to 400 words.\n\nThe essays can be submitted in Sinhala, Tamil or English, allowing the participants to express their thoughts and creativity in the language they are most comfortable with.\n\nThe competition offers participants an opportunity to express their ideas while competing for attractive cash prizes across six categories based on age and language.\n\nThe first prize winners in each category will receive Rs.30,000, while the second prize winners will receive Rs.20,000. The third, fourth and fifth prize winners will each receive Rs.10,000, recognising the creativity and talent demonstrated through their essays.\n\nAdding further value, the winners who hold an Amana Bank Kids account or Teen account will receive double the respective prize value. The winning essays will be adjudicated by an eminent panel of judges comprising university lecturers and school teachers."
  },
