    "chunk_size_bytes": 1758,
    "chunk_text": "Tokyo Cement invests Rs.100mn in Trincomalee housing project\n\nFamilies in Verugal, Muthur and Seruwila receive new homes in community upliftment initiative\n\nFifteen families in Verugal, Muthur and Seruwila receive new homes in community upliftment initiative\n\nIn a significant contribution towards rebuilding the lives of the flood-affected communities in the Eastern province, Tokyo Cement Group has committed Rs.100 million to construct 15 homes for families whose houses were destroyed in the aftermath of Cyclone Ditwah.\n\nSpanning the Divisional Secretariat areas of Muthur, Verugal and Seruwila in the Trincomalee district, the housing project is being implemented in three phases, providing permanent homes to families in need while supporting the recovery of communities affected by natural disasters.\n\nEastern Province Governor Prof. Jayantha Lal Ratnasekera and Tokyo Cement Group Chairman Dr. Harsha Cabral, PC, ceremonially handed over the keys to five families in Muthur, marking the completion of the first phase of the housing project.\n\nThe event was also attended by Tokyo Eastern Cement Factory General Manager V.M. Ravinthirakumar, Mutur Divisional Secretariat Assistant Divisional Secretary and Assistant GA M.S.F. Roshana, Eastern Province Housing Authority Chairman Eng. Sugumaran and Buildings Department Chief Engineer Eng. Thuwaragan, together with the other state sector representatives.\n\nThe initiative comprises of 15 single-storey, two-bedroom houses, equipped with essential amenities, including electricity and water, to provide the beneficiary families with safe and comfortable living conditions.\n\nThe second phase of the project, comprising another five houses, is nearing completion, with the handover scheduled for November."
