    "description": "Budget 2027 backs stock market listings for SMEs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Budget-2027-backs-stock-market-listings-for-SMEs/215-354909",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794642028.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-14-dailymirrorlk-348c8be0-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "478889354ff9d5b7cbe0abf856106882",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "Budget 2027 backs stock market listings for SMEs\n\nThe Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC) warmly welcomed the government\u2019s Budget 2027 and is particularly encouraged that two proposals submitted and consistently advocated by the SEC have been recognised and incorporated into the national budget framework: \u2018A Share for Everyone\u2019 and the SME Listing Support Mechanism.\n\n\u201cThese initiatives represent a significant milestone in our collective efforts to deepen Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market, broaden investor participation and strengthen the link between economic growth and capital formation,\u201d a statement issued on Budget 2027 by SEC Chairman Senior Prof. Hareendra Dissabandara stated.\n\nThe powers, duties and functions of the SEC include advising the government on the development of the securities market and assisting in the effective implementation of the policies and programmes of the government, with respect to the securities market.\n\n\u201cIt is in this capacity that the SEC put forward these proposals and we are pleased to see them taken forward,\u201d it further stated.\n\nThe SEC has long emphasised that a vibrant capital market must be accessible to all segments of society.\n\nThe introduction of \u2018A Share for Everyone\u2019, under the vision of \u2018Let\u2019s Know, Let\u2019s Learn, Let\u2019s Invest\u2019, is a groundbreaking step toward cultivating a new generation of investors.\n\nBy providing the eligible Advanced Level students with an opportunity to enter the capital market and gain firsthand exposure to investing, the programme will enhance financial literacy, promote long-term wealth creation and foster a culture of informed investment among young Sri Lankans.\n\nEqually important is the introduction of the SME Listing Support Mechanism. The small and medium enterprises (SMEs) are the backbone of Sri Lanka\u2019s economy, contributing significantly to employment generation, innovation and regional economic development."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
