    "chunk_id": "2026-11-14-dailymirrorlk-348c8be0-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9e18e626fbc41f12abe8b5f5cfbdcd68",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2001,
    "chunk_text": "Equally important is the introduction of the SME Listing Support Mechanism. The small and medium enterprises (SMEs) are the backbone of Sri Lanka\u2019s economy, contributing significantly to employment generation, innovation and regional economic development.\n\nAt present, participation in the capital market remains relatively low compared with the country\u2019s full potential. The two initiatives directly address this challenge from both the supply and demand sides.\n\nWhile \u2018A Share for Everyone\u2019 aims to expand the investor base and build a stronger investment culture, the SME Listing Support Mechanism will encourage more businesses to enter the market, thereby increasing the diversity and depth of investment opportunities available to Sri Lankan investors.\n\nThe SEC is particularly pleased by the government\u2019s recognition of the important role the capital market can play in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic transformation. A broader investor community and a wider range of listed companies will contribute to improved capital mobilisation, increased financial inclusion, enhanced market liquidity and stronger long-term economic resilience.\n\n\u201cWe also appreciate the commitment demonstrated through the allocation of resources for these initiatives and the collaborative approach involving the Colombo Stock Exchange and other market stakeholders.\n\nThis partnership reflects a shared vision of building a more inclusive, dynamic and accessible capital market ecosystem that benefits students, entrepreneurs, businesses, investors and the wider economy.\u201d\n\nThe SEC looks forward to working closely with the Finance Ministry, Colombo Stock Exchange, market intermediaries, educational institutions and industry stakeholders to ensure the successful implementation of these programmes.\n\n\u201cWe are confident that the measures announced in Budget 2027 will serve as catalysts for a new era of capital market participation and contribute meaningfully to Sri Lanka\u2019s economic growth and prosperity.\u201d"
  },
