    "md5": "d97ae8524730499fb80c88b7cb7cf8d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 947,
    "chunk_text": "It said more than 20 of its proposals were reflected in the budget, including the establishment of a professionally managed investment promotion agency.\u00a0 It also welcomed the continued efforts to strengthen the one-stop services for the investors and noted that the government was considering a successor programme with the International Monetary Fund.\n\nAmong the reforms carried forward from 2026 were the rollout of the Trade National Single Window, phased removal of para-tariffs, Customs reforms and efforts to widen market access through new free trade agreements.\n\nThe CCC also cited the expansion of Bandaranaike International Airport, continued financing support for small and medium-sized businesses and reforms to the management of state-owned enterprises.\n\n\u201cThe priority now must be effective and timely implementation to translate policy commitments into investment, competitiveness, exports and sustainable growth,\u201d the CCC said."
