    "md5": "732a5c7a033e1ea20d3ca4be9ab27412",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 980,
    "chunk_text": "The Solicitor General further informed the Court that the definition of a \u2018serious crime\u2019 would be narrowed to cover offences listed in the First Schedule, punishable by more than four years\u2019 imprisonment, when committed by a member of an organised criminal group.\n\nHe emphasised that the provisions of the proposed legislation would apply only to structured groups rather than individuals acting independently.\n\nOne thing is clear: no powerful government can bulldoze its way past the checks and balances enshrined in the Constitution. Civil society activism, backed by responsible media, holds sway. Today, the government has relented, like a dog tucking its tail between its hind legs.\n\nCivil society activism, coupled with responsible media scrutiny and judicial oversight, has once again demonstrated why democratic checks and balances matter. This is a lesson the government must not forget, particularly when it embarks on the exercise of drafting a new Constitution."
