    "md5": "458c7364f465e8dbffd69bcb0b7fc572",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1747,
    "chunk_text": "Balfour\u2019s shadow hangs over Gaza\u2019s biting winter\n\nPalestinians children try to clear water outside their flooded tents amid heavy rainfall in Gaza City. Pic courtesy - AFP\n\nIn the world\u2019s largest and cruellest open prison, about half a million children endure biting 12-degree Celsius cold every night as torrential rains flood ramshackle tents, soaking their blankets and mattresses. Scenes of young parents carrying newborn babies while wading through filthy floodwaters mixed with sewage are heart-rending, to say the least.\n\nThis is Gaza today. The children cannot count themselves lucky merely to have survived the genocide. The horror continues, albeit at a slower pace, despite a sham ceasefire. Children barely seven or eight years old dig drains with pieces of tin sheeting to divert water away from flooded tents. Some are barefoot. Some are orphans whose parents were killed in Israeli bombings. Hypothermia is not their foremost concern. Their main aim is to protect their decrepit canvas tents, riddled with holes. These barely provide shelter, let alone privacy.\n\nWith the ceasefire deal brokered by United States President Donald Trump and promises of a Board of Peace and Reconstruction, the Gaza crisis has been downplayed in much of the Western media. The global uproar witnessed during the height of Israel\u2019s genocidal campaign has dwindled to little more than an occasional whimper. Trump\u2019s deal has not stopped the killings. His much-hyped Board of Peace talks more and does less. The dire situation endured by Gazans appears to be nobody\u2019s concern. The food aid that began to trickle in after Israeli vetting is barely sufficient to address the besieged territory\u2019s hunger crisis. There are restrictions galore."
