    "chunk_text": "With the ceasefire deal brokered by United States President Donald Trump and promises of a Board of Peace and Reconstruction, the Gaza crisis has been downplayed in much of the Western media. The global uproar witnessed during the height of Israel\u2019s genocidal campaign has dwindled to little more than an occasional whimper. Trump\u2019s deal has not stopped the killings. His much-hyped Board of Peace talks more and does less. The dire situation endured by Gazans appears to be nobody\u2019s concern. The food aid that began to trickle in after Israeli vetting is barely sufficient to address the besieged territory\u2019s hunger crisis. There are restrictions galore.\n\nThe genocide by other means continues. The flood crisis cannot and should not be viewed in isolation. Alongside it, Palestinians are enduring a health crisis compounded by damage to hospitals and critical infrastructure, including Gaza\u2019s drainage and sewage systems. Health organisations in Gaza report a significant increase in the number of newborns with congenital anomalies (birth defects) since the outbreak of the war in October 2023.\n\nThese crises did not emerge out of nothing. They are unfolding by design. This is genocide and ethnic cleansing by other means.\n\nIt is amidst this suffering and the brutality of winter that Palestinians were reminded of the horror of all horrors on November 2, the day Britain issued a declaration supporting the establishment of a national home for the Jewish people in Palestine. Not all Jews wanted such a national home. It was the project of the European Zionist Jews who collaborated with the European powers.\n\nOn November 2, 1917, Arthur James Balfour, then Britain\u2019s foreign secretary, sent a letter to Lord Walter Rothschild, a British Zionist leader, declaring:"
