    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "27721e2868562d89a9c14f0d0ff7aeee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "Did Bing Chun really fail safety tests? The company finally responds\n\nNov 15 (Daily Mirror) - Bing Chun Sri Lanka has clarified that recent laboratory findings concerning vanilla and chocolate ice cream sold at its Kompannaweediya (Slave Island) outlet related to prescribed compositional standards, and did not expressly establish that the products were contaminated, harmful to health or unfit for human consumption.\n\nIn an official public statement issued in response to media reports on proceedings before the Maligakanda Magistrate\u2019s Court, the company said the matter concerned minimum fat content and total solids requirements under Sri Lanka\u2019s Food (Standards) Regulations.\n\n\u201cIt is important to distinguish between a product's compliance with prescribed compositional standards and a determination that a product is unsafe or unfit for human consumption,\u201d the company said.\n\nClarification Regarding Recent Media Reports and Our Commitment to Quality and Regulatory Compliance\n\nTo our valued customers, the general public, and the relevant regulatory authorities of Sri Lanka,\n\nBing Chun Sri Lanka wishes to address the recent media reports concerning the proceedings before the Maligakanda Magistrate's Court relating to certain products sold at the Bing Chun Kompannaweediya (Slave Island) outlet.\n\nWe recognise the concerns expressed by our valued customers and members of the public. We sincerely regret any concern or uncertainty arising from this matter and wish to provide the following clarification.\n\nThe matter concerned the prescribed compositional standards applicable to two products marketed as vanilla ice cream and chocolate ice cream, particularly the minimum requirements relating to fat content and total solids under the relevant Food (Standards) Regulations of Sri Lanka.\n\nIt is important to distinguish between a product's compliance with prescribed compositional standards and a determination that a product is unsafe or unfit for human consumption."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
