    "chunk_text": "Chamara Sampath pooh-poohs President\u2019s Mannar Basin oil and gas exploration plan\n\nNov 15 (Daily Mirror) - Opposition MP Chamara Sampath Dassanayake dismissed President Anura Kumara Dissanayake\u2019s budgetary proposal to pursue offshore oil and gas exploration in the Mannar Basin as unrealistic.\n\n\u200bSpeaking during today's budget debate, Dassanayake noted that successive governments have mooted the proposal since 1975 without it ever seeing the light of day.\n\n\u200bHe pointed out that the current rulers, while in the opposition, had criticized the idea of upstream petroleum development during the presidency of Mahinda Rajapaksa.\n\n\u200b\"We won't stand in your way if you try, but you will never extract oil and gas from the Mannar Basin during the remainder of your term,\" he said."
