    "chunk_text": "Consumer Affairs Authority summons LAUGFS Gas officials over price increase\n\nNov 15 (Daily Mirror) - The Consumer Affairs Authority (CAA) has summoned officials of the LAUGFS Gas to explain the recent sharp increase in domestic gas prices.\n\nThe company representatives have been asked to appear before the Authority at 10 a.m. tomorrow (16) and clarify the reasons for the price revision, the CAA said.\n\nLAUGFS Gas increased the prices of its domestic cylinders with effect from midnight on November 13.\n\nThe price of a 12.5kg cylinder was raised by Rs. 1,775, from Rs. 4,965 to Rs. 6,740, while the price of a 5kg cylinder went up by Rs. 732, from Rs. 1,988 to Rs. 2,720.\n\nThe company attributed the increase to rising international market prices, shipping and insurance costs, which it said had increased the cost of importing bulk gas into the country."
