    "chunk_text": "NASA's Space Shuttle system that \u200bferried astronauts to the \u2060International Space Station before its 2011 retirement was partially reusable; its external fuel tanks that got it off Earth were discarded after each flight. The reusable spacecraft itself had to go through extensive refurbishment before re-flying.\n\nNASA expects Starship, along with another moon lander \u200bunder development by Jeff Bezos' Blue Origin, to start crewed flights to the moon in 2028, though several challenging development milestones remain with both mooncraft.\n\nFor Starship, those milestones include demonstrating complex fuel transfers between Starship tanker \u200brockets in orbit, a critical process that will enable the ship to travel beyond Earth's orbit to the moon."
