    "md5": "124e7499508c4c736a3d2557a711a4f8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1188,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan governmen to roll out \u2018Alternative Care Policy\u2019 in 2027 following Knuckles teenage childbirth incident\n\nNov 15 (Daily Mirror) - Following the shocking discovery of a 15-year- old girl and her newborn baby after an unsafe childbirth, Women and Child Affairs Minister Saroja Savithri Paulraj announced that the Ministry will implement a new \u2018Alternative Care Policy\u2019 starting in 2027 to protect vulnerable children.\n\nIssuing a special statement on November 14, the Minister said it was a relief that both the underage mother and the newborn are currently safe. She added that relevant authorities had been instructed to ensure their immediate and ongoing physical and mental well-being.\n\nPaulraj noted that economic, social, and political complexities\u2014combined with a breakdown in communication between parents and children\u2014are increasingly placing minors at risk.\n\nShe urged parents to foster open dialogue and build unwavering trust at home so children feel safe turning to their families.\n\nThe Minister also acknowledged that state institutions and frontline responders dealing with vulnerable individuals must become more accessible and trustworthy to the public."
