    "md5": "dabbaa5a2a4307eb37131c655c79d4e8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1134,
    "chunk_text": "Thai superstar Jeff Satur also made an appearance, hitting the high notes in his performance of Black Tie.\n\nEurovision in Asia was an idea that has been talked about for decades, but one that never seemed to materialise - despite many false starts - until now.\n\nSpeaking after the show, fan Zelie Pereira - who travelled from Scotland to Thailand to attend - said she was \"very happy\" with Carmelle's win.\n\nKorea, Vietnam and Laos also received praise from Pereira and her friends Michael Peters and Scarlett Massie, both from England.\n\n\"The dance was amazing. The sets were amazing. The costumes were amazing. The singing was amazing. Incredible\", Peters added.\n\nThey confidently declared that \"Asia Vision\" should be the name for next year's show.\n\nFor some, it seems the excitement for another edition is already building.\n\nHowever the crowd at the One Bangkok Arena thinned out not long after the Philippines singer Carmelle lifted the trophy.\n\nThe arena was crowded, but not full, and it's still not clear how much commitment there is among regional broadcasters to keep the contest going and expand it to more than 11 countries."
  },
