    "chunk_text": "New ten-storey Professorial Ward Complex opens at Karapitiya\n\nColombo, Nov. 15 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The newly constructed ten-storey Professorial Ward Complex (PWC) of the Faculty of Medicine, University of Ruhuna, in Karapitiya was officially handed over to the public today, at a ceremony held under the patronage of Minister of Health and Mass Media Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Minister Jayatissa highlighted the unprecedented financial allocations made to the education and healthcare sectors in the current national budget. He stated that Rs. 740 billion has been allocated for education, while Rs. 710 billion has been set aside for healthcare.\n\nThe Minister also recalled that construction of the Professorial Unit at Galle National Hospital began in 2019 with an initial estimated cost of Rs. 1.3 billion. However, the project was eventually completed at a total cost of Rs. 2.808 billion.\n\nHe further announced that Rs. 8.5 billion will be invested in several other development projects at Galle National Hospital. In addition, new professorial units are planned for the medical faculties in Sabaragamuwa, Badulla and Kalutara.\n\nHighlighting the government's commitment to modernizing healthcare facilities, the Minister revealed that Rs. 21.5 billion has been allocated for purchasing advanced medical equipment, including MRI and Linear Accelerator (LINAC) machines. He also stated that the government aims to complete all hospital construction projects that were suspended midway by 2028.\n\nThe newly opened Professorial Ward Complex is equipped with modern healthcare facilities and has a total capacity of 300 beds. These beds are allocated for medical, surgical, psychiatric and specialized gynaecological wards. The complex also features an eight-bed Intensive Care Unit (ICU), three fully equipped operating theatres, eight outpatient clinic rooms and a dedicated clinical examination hall."
