    "chunk_text": "ICC approves window for major men\u2019s tournaments till 2035\n\nICC - The International Cricket Council (ICC) Board has approved the windows for the established ICC major men\u2019s events until 2035, following its meetings in Bali, Indonesia.\n\nThis includes the ICC Men\u2019s Cricket World Cup, the ICC Men\u2019s T20 World Cup, the ICC Men\u2019s Champions Trophy and the ICC World Test Championship final.\n\nThe confirmed schedule runs from the ICC Men's T20 World Cup 2028 in Australia and New Zealand up to the ICC Men's Cricket World Cup 2035.\n\n\u201cThe ICC events portfolio and schedule are critical components of cricket's global architecture and deliver elevated context, competitiveness and consequence to the ecosystem. These tournaments serve as pinnacle moments for fans and players alike, with the associated pathways driving aspiration and access for the broader cricketing landscape.\n\n\"We also recognise the importance of providing athletes and member associations long-term visibility of these events to enable development of improved player pathways, focused high-performance programmes and structured calendars.\"\n\nFollowing the 11th edition of the Men\u2019s T20 World Cup in Australia and New Zealand, which takes place from 12 October to 12 November in 2028, the tournament will next be held in 2030, with England co-hosting it with Scotland and Ireland.\n\nThe next two editions are slated to take place in 2032 and 2034, with the venues yet to be decided.\n\nAfter next year\u2019s ICC Men\u2019s Cricket World Cup in southern Africa, the tournament returns to the sub-continent, with India and Bangladesh co-hosting from 9 October to 23 November.\n\nThe following edition in 2035 has been confirmed too, and is slated to take place in the October-November period, with the hosts yet to be confirmed.\n\nThe ICC World Test Championship Final will continue to remain a biennial fixture in June till 2035. England will be the hosts for the 2029 and 2031 editions as well, while the hosts are to be confirmed for 2033 and 2035."
  },
