    "chunk_text": "Many CEB engineers support renewable energy, yet senior decision makers appear to discount their views while continuing to favor imported, polluting fossil fuels. Without transparent, evidence-based explanations, this pattern suggests that longstanding bureaucratic resistance persists despite restructuring and personnel changes, the \u201cdemocratic dilemma\u201d in practice. Authorities commonly argue that accommodating more rooftop solar would require a $ 4-5 billion grid upgrade taking 7\u201312 years or longer. Because the basis and alternatives behind that estimate have not been publicly explained here, it should be independently examined rather than treated as conclusive.\n\nThe same policy choices also affect Sri Lanka\u2019s ability to meet Sustainable Development Goal 7. The Sri Lanka SDG Report 2024 states that renewable energy\u2019s share of total final energy consumption remains below the country\u2019s 2030 ambition. Restricting distributed solar while delaying the phase-out of fossil fuels therefore risks widening the gap between national commitments and actual progress. In simple terms, the Government\u2019s actions do not make any technical or political sense."
