    "chunk_text": "The same policy choices also affect Sri Lanka\u2019s ability to meet Sustainable Development Goal 7. The Sri Lanka SDG Report 2024 states that renewable energy\u2019s share of total final energy consumption remains below the country\u2019s 2030 ambition. Restricting distributed solar while delaying the phase-out of fossil fuels therefore risks widening the gap between national commitments and actual progress. In simple terms, the Government\u2019s actions do not make any technical or political sense.\n\nSri Lanka already possesses substantial renewable resources and technical expertise; its energy future now depends on whether public institutions use them transparently, consistently, and in the national interest. By protecting citizen-led rooftop solar and investing in storage and grid modernisation, not only can the country reduce its dependence on imported fossil fuels and move toward energy security but also drive the much-needed equal wealth distribution that the Government touts is the foundation of prosperity. Not only the elected officials, but we, the public, also have a responsibility to ensure that administrative institutions implement democratic policy for the good of the country rather than obstructing it with ulterior motives."
