    "md5": "c4e73681827e8de8b03761d8a489435a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1936,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka prepares to celebrate Global Entrepreneurship Week 2026\n\nMillions of people around the world have the ideas, talent, and ambition to build something better for themselves and their communities \u2014 but have never seen entrepreneurship as a path available to them. Global Entrepreneurship Week changes that. This campaign meets people where they are and connects them to networks, tools, and supports them to take that first step \u2014 showing what\u2019s possible in their own communities.\n\nAt a moment when the forces reshaping work, technology, and economies are moving faster than at any point in modern history, the Global Entrepreneurship Network (GEN) is looking ahead to Global Entrepreneurship Week (GEW). The campaign arrives at a moment when communities in every country are considering how to navigate these shifts, who will lead the way, and how to make sure everyone has a path forward.\n\nThe stakes are shared. According to the World Economic Forum's Future of Jobs Report 2025, 92 million jobs globally are expected to be displaced by 2030. Those same forces reshaping work are creating demand for entirely new kinds of enterprise \u2014 and entrepreneurs are how societies answer that call.\n\nThe question is not whether new business formation matters \u2014 it is whether the millions of people in every country who have the ideas, talent, and ambition to start something, have ever been shown that entrepreneurship is a path available to them. Global Entrepreneurship Week changes that. This campaign, powered by 11,000 partner organisations across 200 countries, meets people where they are and connects them to the networks, tools, and support to take that first step \u2014 showing what is possible in their own communities. More than 40,000 workshops, events, and programs are expected to take place beyond traditional startup hubs, in public spaces such as libraries, community centres, and schools \u2014 in every country."
  },
