    "chunk_text": "The question is not whether new business formation matters \u2014 it is whether the millions of people in every country who have the ideas, talent, and ambition to start something, have ever been shown that entrepreneurship is a path available to them. Global Entrepreneurship Week changes that. This campaign, powered by 11,000 partner organisations across 200 countries, meets people where they are and connects them to the networks, tools, and support to take that first step \u2014 showing what is possible in their own communities. More than 40,000 workshops, events, and programs are expected to take place beyond traditional startup hubs, in public spaces such as libraries, community centres, and schools \u2014 in every country.\n\nThe premier celebration of entrepreneurship, startup culture and innovation in Sri Lanka.\u00a0 In November 2008 Sri Lanka was among 77 countries that launched GEW under the visionary leadership of Deshabandu Patrick Amerasinghe and the Young Entrepreneurs Sri Lanka (YESL) Organisation.\n\nSince 2022 the Information and Communication Technology Agency (ICTA) has hosted GEW Sri Lanka with distinction and saw Sri Lanka climb within the top 10 in 2023 and 2024, and ranked 4th place in 2025 on the GEN GEW Global Leaderboard.\n\nSince 2008, GEW Sri Lanka has grown into a nationally scaled, globally recognised entrepreneurship movement with expanded participation, stronger institutional support, and higher international rankings. GEW Sri Lanka has been recognised as one of the world\u2019s largest national GEW campaigns, hoping to reach over 100,000 participants in 2026, increasing government and corporate sponsorship, and scaling events nationally across all 25 districts and all 9 provinces. The initiative increasingly focused on inclusion, innovation, and regional empowerment, strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s entrepreneurial ecosystem. This growth reflects both deliberate ecosystem development and Sri Lanka\u2019s Entrepreneurial Spirit."
  },
