    "chunk_size_bytes": 1734,
    "chunk_text": "Samsung retains No. 5 position in Interbrand\u2019s Best Global Brands 2026 for seventh consecutive year\n\nSamsung Electronics has secured the No. 5 position in Interbrand\u2019s Best Global Brands 2026 rankings for the seventh consecutive year, with its brand value reaching $ 105.2 billion. Samsung remains the only Asia-based company to maintain a place among the world\u2019s top five brands since 2020.\n\nThe recognition reflects Samsung\u2019s continued growth and investments in artificial intelligence (AI), including its developments in AI semiconductors and the integration of AI experiences across its product range. Interbrand\u2019s assessment also recognised the company\u2019s customer-focused brand strategy under its One Samsung approach, which connects products and services across its business.\n\nSamsung Lanka and Maldives Managing Director Dongkyun Lee said: \u201cMaintaining a position among the world\u2019s top five brands for seven consecutive years is an important recognition of Samsung\u2019s continued focus on innovation and customer experiences. Our investments in AI, connected technologies and product development reflect our commitment to making technology more useful in people\u2019s everyday lives. As we continue to bring these experiences to customers in Sri Lanka, this recognition reinforces the importance of building products and services around their changing needs.\u201d\n\nSamsung\u2019s Device Solutions (DS) Division continued to strengthen its position in the semiconductor industry through its supply of high-value memory products to meet growing demand for AI. The division also achieved a significant technological milestone with the mass production and commercial shipment of the industry\u2019s first HBM4 memory products."
