    "chunk_text": "The Seethawaka Export Processing Zone offers potential for integrated resource management, improved common wastewater treatment, environmental monitoring, and industrial symbiosis.\n\nThe BOI\u2019s work towards real-time effluent monitoring and improved wastewater and sludge management provides a foundation for stronger environmental performance and future resource recovery.\n\nA proposed Green Investment Promotion Program would target international investors in clean energy, circular-economy technologies, industrial resource recovery, low-carbon manufacturing, and environmental infrastructure.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka can promote not merely industrial land, but a sustainable industrial ecosystem capable of meeting emerging global investment expectations,\u201d Welagedara said.\n\nCOP31 offers Sri Lanka a platform to connect with technology providers, climate-finance institutions, development partners, and sustainable investors. The BOI has highlighted investment opportunities including:\n\nThe BOI also emphasised that successful international cooperation requires technically sound, financially viable, and investment-ready projects supported by credible institutional arrangements."
