    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "29729e3d70cdce26b41927061afee1f9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "Seafood exporters hail Budget 2027, eye $ 680 m by 2030\n\nThe Seafood Exporters\u2019 Association of Sri Lanka (SEASL) yesterday said it \u201cstrongly supports\u201d the Government\u2019s 2027 Budget proposals, recognising their potential to accelerate investment, expand value-added seafood processing, strengthen sustainable fisheries and improve Sri Lanka\u2019s international competitiveness.\n\nThe Association extends its appreciation to President and Finance, Planning and Economic Development Minister Anura Kumara Dissanayake for recognising the strategic importance of the fisheries and seafood export industry. SEASL also thanks Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources Minister Ramalingam Chandrasekar and Deputy Minister Rathna Gamage for their commitment to developing the sector and supporting fishing communities.\n\nSEASL believes Sri Lanka has the potential to achieve $ 680 million in annual seafood export earnings by 2030, provided the industry is supported by sustained investment, greater value addition, modern infrastructure and efficient trade policies.\n\nThe proposed concessionary financing scheme offering loans of up to Rs. 500 million at 5% annual interest to qualifying large-scale fisheries enterprises represents an important opportunity to accelerate investment in processing capacity, modern technology and cold-chain infrastructure.\n\nThe 200% enhanced capital allowance for qualifying BOI-approved export-oriented manufacturing investments of at least $ 3 million could further encourage expansion, new processing facilities and the development of higher-value seafood products.\n\nThese measures can help attract investment, strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s processing capabilities and create additional employment across the industry.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s seafood industry has demonstrated the considerable potential of value-added processing, particularly through the importation of raw materials for processing and re-export."
  },
