    "md5": "fdeaf5ef787c1ee2b1a8c48e127bba8e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1914,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe are excited about the opportunities ahead for our aquaculture farmers, particularly those engaged in shrimp farming. They have an important contribution to make towards expanding production, creating rural employment and strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s seafood exports. As an industry, we are committed to supporting their growth, encouraging investment and helping connect farmers with international markets,\u201d SEASL\u2019s Dilan Fernando said.\n\nEqually significant is the Rs. 1 billion allocation for sustainable fisheries resource management, including scientific stock assessments, habitat mapping and monitoring.\n\nThe recent Marine Stewardship Council (MSC) certification of Sri Lanka\u2019s North-Western Blue Swimming Crab Fishery demonstrates the value of responsible fisheries management and internationally recognised sustainability standards in accessing premium export markets.\n\nSEASL encourages continued collaboration between Government institutions, research organisations, fishing communities, aquaculture farmers and exporters to strengthen scientific management, traceability and international certification.\n\nThe proposed customs reforms, improvements to the TIEP scheme and reduction of CESS rates across selected tariff lines could enhance the competitiveness of Sri Lankan seafood exports.\n\nThe Association also supports efforts to strengthen international trade relationships and expand market access, particularly in Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East.\n\nSEASL believes these measures, combined with continued investment in food safety, sustainability and product innovation, can position Sri Lanka as a leading regional hub for value-added seafood processing.\n\nWhile the Budget provides an encouraging policy direction, SEASL stresses that timely implementation and close cooperation between Government and industry will be essential to achieving the country\u2019s export ambitions."
  },
