    "chunk_text": "Camarena had angered them after he had discovered and then destroyed a vast marijuana plantation in Chihuahua, which belonged to the criminal group.\n\nHis death sparked one of the biggest manhunts the US government has ever launched in North America.\n\nIn the 1980s, Joaquin 'El Chapo' Guzm\u00e1n was introduced to F\u00e9lix Gallardo, who put him in charge of handling logistics for his drug organisation.\n\nFrom the subsequent break-up of F\u00e9lix Gallardo's organisation after his arrest, the Sinaloa Cartel emerged, led by Guzm\u00e1n, now another man synonymous with large-scale drug trafficking.\n\nIn 2019, Guzm\u00e1n was sentenced to life in prison for charges including drug trafficking and money laundering following one of the most high-profile trials in recent US history.\n\nF\u00e9lix Gallardo's life has been portrayed in a number of television programmes including the Netflix series Narcos: Mexico. The show depicted his rise to power as well as his relationship with Guzm\u00e1n"
