    "chunk_text": "The project will be located at Hope Town, Port Blair, in Andaman Island and is expected to strengthen the island\u2019s electricity infrastructure, enable long-term energy security through LNG infrastructure, and facilitate future economic development. The Lakdhanavi Ltd., engineering team would be responsible for the execution of the project, with W\u00e4rtsil\u00e4 Corporation of Finland being the supplier of the power-generating equipment to Lakdhanavi Ltd.\n\nEnergy Minister Anura Karunathilaka met LTL\u2019s management and expressed the Government\u2019s delight over this achievement, welcoming the success of a Sri Lankan company in securing a major infrastructure contract in a large and competitive market such as India. This underscored the national significance of the achievement and the value of Sri Lankan companies taking their expertise to international markets.\n\nBeyond its commercial significance, the project is a practical reflection of longstanding economic ties between Sri Lanka and India. While bilateral economic engagement has often been viewed through the lens of Indian investment, development assistance, and infrastructure participation in Sri Lanka, Lakdhanavi\u2019s success demonstrates that opportunities can arise in both directions and that Sri Lankan companies should pursue them with diligence.\n\nThe contract demonstrates how Sri Lankan businesses can contribute their skills and capabilities for mutual development of both countries, complementing the close cooperation of the two Governments with tangible private-sector partnerships. It offers an encouraging example of how the two neighbouring countries can deepen economic cooperation and create mutually benefitting opportunities."
