    "md5": "7e50e69b69d0bd3beeade6109fd7344d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "Anti-Houthi forces retreat in Yemen as Iran strikes Bahrain\n\n(Reuters) - Iran and its allies ramped up pressure on the US and allied Gulf states on two fronts on Sunday, with Saudi-backed forces retreating in their battle against the Iran-aligned Houthis in Yemen and Iran itself firing \u200bdrones at US bases in Bahrain.\n\nIn Yemen, Saudi Arabia's campaign against the Houthis suffered a major setback, as its allies, fighting on behalf of the internationally recognised Yemeni government, pulled back from \u200cthe Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend their temporary capital Aden on the southern coast.\n\nThe announcement signalled the apparent end of a six-week government counteroffensive to drive the Houthis from the mouth of the Red Sea to secure a key oil route.\n\nMeanwhile, Iranian attacks on Bahrain, headquarters of the US Fifth Fleet in the Gulf, were likely to put new pressure on US President Donald Trump to resolve the war he launched nearly nine months ago.\n\nSince the unpopular war contributed to a defeat for his Republicans in midterm elections this month, Trump \u200bhas played down the need for a diplomatic breakthrough.\n\nMajor warfare between the US and Iran has calmed since the early phase of the conflict, but with diplomacy stalled there is little immediate prospect of \u200ba resolution either to the wider conflict or the war in Yemen.\n\nSunday's announcement of a Yemeni government retreat raises the prospect of new Houthi advances towards Aden on the \u2060southern coast, base of the internationally recognised government since the Houthis drove it from the capital Sanaa more than a decade ago.\n\n\"The Southern Armed Forces announce the implementation of a redeployment operation for its forces from Dhubab Airport \u200band the Bab el-Mandeb area, west of Taiz Governorate,\" the main military force fighting for Yemen's government in the south of the country said in a statement."
  },
