    "md5": "9953103f5ae146c2bab06b51cb76d1b5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1821,
    "chunk_text": "First Capital Holdings reports first half results amid challenging market conditions\n\nFirst Capital Holdings PLC, a subsidiary of JXG (Janashakthi Group) recorded a Loss after Tax of Rs. 1.27 billion for the first half of the financial year ended on 30 September 2026, compared to a Profit after Tax of Rs. 3.43 billion from the corresponding period of the previous year. For the second quarter of FY 2026/27, the Group\u2019s Loss after Tax was Rs. 0.54 billion.\n\nThe Group\u2019s performance reflects a challenging market environment, shaped by changes in monetary policy and pressure on fixed-income yields.\n\nOperational conditions during the period were heavily influenced by a 100-basis-point increase in the monetary policy rate of May 2026, driven by inflationary pressures linked to geopolitical tensions in the Middle East.\n\nYields on government securities experienced volatility and came under pressure towards end of the first quarter and the second quarter, impacting performance across fixed-income, debt and equity trading portfolios.\n\nHowever, market cycles are not unfamiliar territory for First Capital. The Group has successfully navigated similar periods of market volatility in the past, demonstrating its experience in operating through different phases of the financial cycle. During FY 2021/22, the Group recorded a Loss after Tax of Rs. 652 million amid challenging market conditions. As market conditions evolved, it returned to profitability, recording a Profit after Tax of Rs. 2.65 billion in FY 2022/23, followed by Rs. 10.16 billion in FY 2023/24, Rs. 5.02 billion in FY 2024/25 and Rs. 2.10 billion in FY 2025/26. This track record reflects First Capital\u2019s depth of market experience and its ability to navigate shifting conditions while maintaining its focus on long-term business performance."
  },
