    "chunk_text": "However, market cycles are not unfamiliar territory for First Capital. The Group has successfully navigated similar periods of market volatility in the past, demonstrating its experience in operating through different phases of the financial cycle. During FY 2021/22, the Group recorded a Loss after Tax of Rs. 652 million amid challenging market conditions. As market conditions evolved, it returned to profitability, recording a Profit after Tax of Rs. 2.65 billion in FY 2022/23, followed by Rs. 10.16 billion in FY 2023/24, Rs. 5.02 billion in FY 2024/25 and Rs. 2.10 billion in FY 2025/26. This track record reflects First Capital\u2019s depth of market experience and its ability to navigate shifting conditions while maintaining its focus on long-term business performance.\n\nConcurrently, the Corporate Dealing Securities division posted a Loss after Tax of Rs. 834 million, compared to a Profit after Tax of Rs. 1.78 billion in H1 2025/26, following difficult trading conditions in the debt and equity markets.\n\nIn contrast, the Corporate Finance Advisory division recorded growth, reporting a Profit after Tax of Rs. 69 million, up from Rs. 25 million achieved in the corresponding period of the previous financial year.\n\nThe Wealth Management division reported a marginal Loss after Tax of Rs. 3 million against a Profit after Tax of Rs. 48 million in H1 2025/26, with the division\u2019s Assets under Management maintaining at Rs. 92.4 billion as of 30 September 2026.\n\nThe Stock Brokering division maintained profitability, although Profit after Tax declined to Rs. 12 million for the six-month period, compared to Rs. 116 million from the corresponding period last year."
  },
