    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d3d189a8dcf9df590da92f5c2e2a1ea2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1073,
    "chunk_text": "The Stock Brokering division maintained profitability, although Profit after Tax declined to Rs. 12 million for the six-month period, compared to Rs. 116 million from the corresponding period last year.\n\nWe have also continued to strengthen the composition of our Boards and our broader governance and oversight frameworks as part of our ongoing commitment to organisational development and long-term institutional effectiveness.\u201d\n\nDilshan Wirasekara, Managing Director / CEO, First Capital Holdings PLC noted, \u201cOur Loss after Tax of Rs. 1.27 billion for the six months ended on 30 September 2026 was primarily attributed to the impact of higher interest rates and pressure on government securities yields. While consistent policy direction is important to supporting investor confidence and long-term market development, our focus remains on the areas within our control. We continue to strengthen our customer reach and enhance access to investment opportunities through digital services while remaining responsive to evolving investor needs and market conditions.\u201d"
