    "md5": "812ce08ffb33f162736342847cd18de0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1940,
    "chunk_text": "Cargills Bank-Toyota Lanka sign landmark MoU\n\nIn a move that promises \u2018A Smarter Way to Drive\u2019, Cargills Bank PLC has announced a strategic partnership with automotive giant Toyota Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd.\n\nThe collaboration was cemented through a memorandum of understanding (MoU) officially signed recently, creating a seamless and highly rewarding pathway for the customers to own their dream Toyota vehicle.\n\nThis landmark partnership introduces a suite of exclusive financing solutions designed to give Sri Lankan motorists a smarter financial choice when investing in a world-class automobile. The joint initiative allows the prospective Toyota owners to drive home with more benefits, enjoying unprecedented flexibility and cost-saving features.\n\nThe prospective buyers can now enjoy repayment periods of up to 10 years on vehicle loans, offering greater flexibility with highly manageable monthly instalments tailored to fit their budgets.\n\nAdditionally, the partnership unlocks special interest rates with highly competitive financing options, making Toyota ownership more accessible than ever.\n\nIn a major boost for financial freedom, the customers will also benefit from a zero early settlement fee if they choose to pay off their facility after three years, subject to applicable terms and conditions.\n\nFurthermore, the collaboration introduces a Flexi Draft facility, an innovative financial tool designed to give the customers even greater control over their funds and repayment strategies.\n\nToyota Lanka Chairman Masaaki Kawabata expressed his enthusiasm for the collaboration.\n\n\u201cIt is a special day as we sign this MoU with Cargills Bank,\u201d Kawabata stated.\n\n\u201cThe Cargills group is a prominent and highly respected organisation and we are very happy to sign this\u2014our first MoU with them. Moving forward, we will try our best to collaborate with the service fund to continually support and uplift our Toyota customers.\u201d"
  },
