    "chunk_text": "Sungrow bets big on home and business storage as Sri Lanka\u2019s solar hits night-time ceiling\n\nSungrow will double its sales teams, marketing budget and service investment next year to drive its home and business storage push\n\nWith Budget 2027 proposing subsidies for household solar batteries, the company\u2019s systems could help Sri Lanka absorb surplus solar power now curtailed on Sundays and public holidays\n\nChinese solar inverter and storage major Sungrow will double its sales and technical teams, marketing budget and service investment next year to capture distributed energy demand from homes and businesses, a market it expects to grow by 25 percent a year over the next four years, a top official said.\n\nSungrow Distribution Sales and Marketing System President Simon Liu made the remarks on November 11 at the company\u2019s Global Energy Pioneer Summit (GEPS) 2026 in Hefei. The event drew more than 1,200 guests from over 80 countries, among them delegates from Sri Lanka, with Mirror Business representing the Sri Lankan media. He noted that while residential demand would maintain steady growth, the commercial and industrial (C&I) segment was poised to expand far more rapidly. \u201cAsia-Pacific and Europe remain our key anchors, while Latin America, the Middle East and Africa are showing extraordinary growth momentum,\u201d he told delegates.\n\nSungrow will also open 10 more local warehouses and 10 more service centres, while hosting over 300 events across more than 50 countries next year.\n\nLiu added that the company would deepen collaboration with select loyal partners to enter new territories and product categories such as small C&I and plug-in systems, while lifting its brand premium and partner margins.\n\n\u201cPlease remember Sungrow, we will never compete only with price,\u201d he stressed."
