    "chunk_text": "Liu added that the company would deepen collaboration with select loyal partners to enter new territories and product categories such as small C&I and plug-in systems, while lifting its brand premium and partner margins.\n\n\u201cPlease remember Sungrow, we will never compete only with price,\u201d he stressed.\n\nFounded in Hefei in 1997, Sungrow has a cumulative 1,100 GW of power electronic converters installed worldwide, up from over 1,000 GW at end-2025. S&P Global ranked Sungrow first in PV inverter shipments for 2025, while Wood Mackenzie placed it first in its inaugural global battery storage integrator ranking. Liu pointed out that the company\u2019s products now power 5.51 million homes and businesses through nearly 100,000 installers. Speaking at the launch of the Sungrow Power Club, a four-tier installer rewards and training programme, Sungrow Distribution Business Partner Group Center Director Iris Xu observed that the installer base had grown more than 15-fold from about 6,000 in 2020.\n\nAt the summit, Sungrow launched PowerStack 3.0, a C&I storage system built around a dock that accepts power conversion, solar, EV charging and microgrid modules. A single cabinet can therefore serve as standalone storage, a solar-plus-storage system without a separate inverter, a charging hub or a microgrid. The company claims it cuts a 5 MWh plant\u2019s footprint by 43 percent from the previous generation, and says its AI assistant Bubbly can lift returns by more than 12 percent when compared to a conventional self-consumption mode. It also introduced PowerKeeper Lite, an indoor battery system for smaller commercial sites."
