    "chunk_text": "At the summit, Sungrow launched PowerStack 3.0, a C&I storage system built around a dock that accepts power conversion, solar, EV charging and microgrid modules. A single cabinet can therefore serve as standalone storage, a solar-plus-storage system without a separate inverter, a charging hub or a microgrid. The company claims it cuts a 5 MWh plant\u2019s footprint by 43 percent from the previous generation, and says its AI assistant Bubbly can lift returns by more than 12 percent when compared to a conventional self-consumption mode. It also introduced PowerKeeper Lite, an indoor battery system for smaller commercial sites.\n\nMeanwhile, these systems arrive as Sri Lanka\u2019s solar boom runs into a night-time ceiling. Sustainable Energy Authority Chairperson Dr. Wijendra J. Bandara stated in October that installed solar capacity had reached 3,053 MW, above the night-time peak demand of about 3,000 MW, leaving storage as the key to further growth.\n\nThe strain peaks on Sundays and public holidays, when factories and offices close and demand falls while solar output keeps flowing. National System Operator (NSO) Chairman Dr. Pradeep Perera said in August that commercial and industrial buildings with solar installations above 200 kW were being asked to disconnect on Sundays to balance the grid. Rooftop owners were asked to switch off their systems from 8.00 a.m. to 3.00 p.m. over the Vesak long weekend in May. Earlier, an island-wide blackout on a sunny Sunday in February 2025 was attributed to low system stability amid high solar output and weak demand."
