    "chunk_size_bytes": 1698,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank sustains strong earnings momentum with Rs.52.1bn pre-tax profit\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank delivered a strong financial performance for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, building on its earnings momentum and demonstrating financial resilience in an evolving global and domestic economic environment.\n\nThe Bank achieved a standalone Profit Before Tax (PBT) of Rs.52.1 billion, supported by sustained core banking performance, prudent balance sheet management and disciplined credit and risk management. This performance underscores the strength of the Bank\u2019s financial fundamentals and its ability to sustain progress while navigating changing economic and geopolitical conditions.\n\nStrong growth across core income streams reinforced the Bank\u2019s earnings momentum during the nine months ended September 30, 2026. Total operating income rose by 18.7 percent to Rs.145.1 billion, from Rs.122.2 billion in the corresponding period of the previous year, while net interest income increased by 21.5 percent to Rs.126.2 billion from Rs.103.9 billion. The Bank also strengthened its Net Interest Margin (NIM) to 4.4 percent from 4.1 percent, supported by effective asset and liability repricing and disciplined balance sheet management. Together, these improvements highlight the strength of its core banking performance.\n\nSustained lending momentum was another key feature of the Bank\u2019s performance. Gross loans and advances reached Rs.2.1 trillion, reflecting continued growth in core lending activities. At the same time, total assets stabilised at Rs.3.9 trillion, demonstrating the Bank\u2019s ability to advance its lending business while maintaining overall balance sheet stability."
  },
