    "md5": "b3aed8b579cb1434a77210ec9f6a35f3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1640,
    "chunk_text": "Sustained lending momentum was another key feature of the Bank\u2019s performance. Gross loans and advances reached Rs.2.1 trillion, reflecting continued growth in core lending activities. At the same time, total assets stabilised at Rs.3.9 trillion, demonstrating the Bank\u2019s ability to advance its lending business while maintaining overall balance sheet stability.\n\nProgress in asset quality complemented the Bank\u2019s loan portfolio expansion during the first nine months of 2026. The impaired loans (Stage 3) ratio (net) improved to 6.3 percent, while the Stage 3 provision coverage ratio strengthened to 54.1 percent. These improvements, achieved alongside continued loan portfolio growth, underscore enhanced recovery efforts, prudent credit risk management and the Bank\u2019s commitment to a resilient balance sheet.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank\u2019s strong performance momentum extended to the Group during the first nine months of 2026, supported by healthy core banking expansion and improved margins. Group Profit Before Tax grew by 23.8 percent to Rs.59.3 billion, compared with Rs.47.9 billion in the corresponding period of the previous year, reflecting improved operating performance alongside disciplined cost and risk management.\n\nThe Group also sustained its business expansion, with gross loans and advances increasing to Rs.2.4 trillion and total assets stabilising at Rs.4.3 trillion. This performance reinforces the Group\u2019s scale and business growth across key segments. Net interest income rose by 24.4 percent to Rs.148.6 billion from Rs.119.5 billion, supported by effective balance sheet repricing and sustained lending activity."
