    "chunk_size_bytes": 1887,
    "chunk_text": "The Group also sustained its business expansion, with gross loans and advances increasing to Rs.2.4 trillion and total assets stabilising at Rs.4.3 trillion. This performance reinforces the Group\u2019s scale and business growth across key segments. Net interest income rose by 24.4 percent to Rs.148.6 billion from Rs.119.5 billion, supported by effective balance sheet repricing and sustained lending activity.\n\nCommenting on the strong performance achieved during the first nine months of 2026, Chairman Chandana Guniyangoda highlighted People\u2019s Bank\u2019s continued resilience, financial strength and stability amid an evolving global and domestic economic environment. He observed that Sri Lanka\u2019s economy has sustained its recovery momentum, supported by improved macroeconomic stability and growth across key sectors, even as geopolitical tensions, global uncertainties and emerging inflationary pressures continue to pose challenges.\n\nThe Chairman stressed that the Bank\u2019s performance is underpinned by a continued focus on stronger financial fundamentals, greater operational efficiency, sound governance and prudent risk management. He reaffirmed People\u2019s Bank\u2019s commitment to advancing national economic priorities by facilitating productive economic activity, supporting businesses and promoting financial inclusion, thereby contributing to sustainable and inclusive economic growth.\n\nChief Executive Officer/General Manager Clive Fonseka described the Bank\u2019s performance as a demonstration of its sustained positive momentum, driven by robust core income generation, improved margins, stronger asset quality and a stable balance sheet. He emphasised that strong capital and liquidity positions, disciplined financial management and continued investments in digital banking, customer experience and operational efficiency position the Bank well for sustainable growth."
