    "date_str": "2026-11-16",
    "description": "Political violence and the shaming of the yellow robe",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Political-violence-and-the-shaming-of-the-yellow-robe/172-354996",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794813783.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-16-dailymirrorlk-289949e2-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "76c81e583c2efb28153be3c481f57392",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "Political violence and the shaming of the yellow robe\n\nOn Friday, President Anura Kumara Dissanayake (AKD) presented his third budget since assuming the post of\u00a0 Minister of Finance. While he was presenting the country\u2019s budget for the financial year 2027, another drama was unfolding in Anuradhapura.\n\nA group of Buddhist monks led by Kassapa Thera of the \u2018Release Gnanasara Thera\u2019 fame had organised yet another satyagraha at the premises of the Ruwanwelisaya (one of Buddhism\u2019s most sacred sites in the country) demanding the government drop its planned development of the sacred city of Anuradhapura.\n\nThe satyagrahees claim without any proof that the development programme is part of an Indian government plan\u00a0 to construct other religious places of worship within the expanded sacred area, place restrictions on religious activities and build a proposed fence around the Ruwanweliseya itself.\n\nThey threatened a fast unto death campaign at the site unless the government dropped its proposed plan.\n\nThe Anuradhapura Magistrate, at the request of the police, ordered the satyagrahees to vacate the site. The satyagrahees rejected the Magistrate\u2019s order. As this country has seen on earlier occasions, the police failed to implement the Magistrates order when dealing with members of the Buddhist clergy.\n\nBalangoda Kassapa Thera said he would not comply with any court order. He claimed that no court order could be served on him and that only a Sangha Adhikarana had the authority to issue orders concerning him.\u00a0 On Wednesday morning another group opposed to the satyagraha, led by an ex-monk arrived at the Ruwanwelisaya claiming the satyagraha was politically motivated and demanding the satyagrahees leave the sacred site. Soon physical violence broke out between the two groups."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-16-dailymirrorlk-289949e2",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-289949e2",
    "date_str": "2026-11-16",
    "description": "Political violence and the shaming of the yellow robe",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Political-violence-and-the-shaming-of-the-yellow-robe/172-354996",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794813783.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-16-dailymirrorlk-289949e2-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1557ca5ed80a51084edec93888f01e73",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2034,
    "chunk_text": "Balangoda Kassapa Thera said he would not comply with any court order. He claimed that no court order could be served on him and that only a Sangha Adhikarana had the authority to issue orders concerning him.\u00a0 On Wednesday morning another group opposed to the satyagraha, led by an ex-monk arrived at the Ruwanwelisaya claiming the satyagraha was politically motivated and demanding the satyagrahees leave the sacred site. Soon physical violence broke out between the two groups.\n\nVerite Research in its publication \u2018Inaction and Impunity: Incidents of religious violence targeting Christians and Muslims 2015 \u2013 2019\u2019 points out: \u201c\u2026The state played a significant role in perpetrating and facilitating religious violence targeting Christians and Muslims during the period from January 2015 to August 2019.\u201d\n\nThe report adds: \u201cThe level of state involvement remained the same from the previous five-year period (2010-2014). State officials were identified as\u00a0 key perpetrators in over 40 percent of all incidents of violence.\u201d\n\nAdditionally, the study records an overwhelmingly negative police response to incidents of violence perpetrated by non-state actors such as the Buddhist clergy.\n\nIn turn,\u00a0 this has led sections within the Buddhist clergy to believe they are above the law. Balangoda Kassapa Thera\u2019s statement as reported in the media (13 November 2026) that \u201che would not comply with any court order\u201d\u2026 and that \u201cno court order could be served on him and only a Sangha Adhikarana had the authority to issue orders concerning him\u2026\u201d comes out of this mentality. This is a dangerous trend and it needs to be nipped in the bud. Whether Kassapa Thera is merely a tool in the hands of disgruntled politicians will be realised later. But both the government and the heads of the Buddhist Nikkayas need to ensure that all persons in this country realise none is superior to the other.\n\nOur Constitution gives foremost place to Buddhist beliefs \u2013NOT to bigoted personalities clothed in saffron robes."
  },
