    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka has adequate resources, but we lack the institutions and the capacity for economic rejuvenation, in many ways due to the approach of past regimes in power and the neoliberal policies spanning close to five decades. Amidst an unravelling global order and years ahead bound to be times of turmoil, Sri Lanka needs to leave behind its history of dependency on external powers and forge a different economic programme. Sri Lanka as a small state \u2013 facing reckless global giants with little concern for consequences and middle powers guarding their own interests \u2013 needs to think of both its domestic policies and external relations in ways to ensure the welfare of its people.\n\nBudget 2027 should not be seen as set in stone, but as an opportunity for critical engagement both within and outside the state. We need to chart an alternative economic trajectory grounded in social justice that depends not just on the Government, but also the engagement of movements \u2013 of youth, co-operatives and trade unions \u2013 and the working people more broadly."
  },
