    "md5": "92dd60813162ba76ce2bfb25321c3879",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "Jay Shah reappointed as ICC chairman for second term\n\nHindustan Times - The International Cricket Council (ICC) on Monday announced the reappointment of Jay Shah as its chairman for a second term. His original three-year tenure was due to end next year, but the Board has opted to extend his term to ensure continuity. He will now remain in the position until the end of 2030.\n\nThe former BCCI secretary was elected unopposed, with his appointment confirmed following a proposal by the ICC directors at the governing body's board meeting in Bali.\n\nShah was appointed ICC chairman in August 2024 and officially took charge in December that year, succeeding Greg Barclay.\n\nThe Board has shown confidence in Shah's leadership, opting for continuity as cricket looks to expand its global footprint. The sport is also gearing up for its return to the Olympics in 2028 in Los Angeles. Recently, the ICC announced an expanded long-term programme of competitions, aimed at increasing participation and creating more development pathways.\n\nThe ICC Board also reaffirmed its commitment to strengthening cricket's foundations, with continued support for the women's game and Associate Members remaining a priority.\n\n\u201cI am deeply honoured by the confidence the ICC Board has placed in me and sincerely grateful to every Director for their continued trust and support. Serving as Chair of the ICC is both a privilege and a responsibility, and I remain committed to working with our Members to advance the interests of cricket across the world,\" Shah said in an official statement.\n\n\u201cWe are entering one of the most important and exciting periods in our sport\u2019s history. Cricket\u2019s return to the Olympic Games at LA28 presents an extraordinary opportunity to introduce our game to new audiences and inspire a new generation of players and fans,\" he added."
  },
