    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6f713563d20464f81437faac3a637370",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "China stands out as the leading example, accounting for 2,543 SEZs, or 47.2% of the global total. Since 1978, China has made the development of SEZs a major component of its economic development strategy. These zones have helped attract domestic and foreign investment, facilitate manufacturing,expand exports and introduce new economic activities. Importantly, many Chinese zones also cater to the domestic market rather than being exclusively export-oriented.\n\nHowever, the international experience also demonstrates that establishing an SEZ alone is not a recipe for economic success. Some countries have experienced disappointing results in cases of weak institutional arrangements, limited integration with the domestic economy, tax evasion and smuggling.\n\nThe question, therefore, is whether Colombo Port City can provide Sri Lanka with an opportunity to position itself within the expanding global network of investment and business centres. Colombo Port City is a geographic area reclaimed from the sea adjacent to the Colombo Port and gazetted as part of the Colombo District in the Western Province. The more important question is not one of sovereignty, but how the project can move beyond property development and establish itself as an internationally competitive destination for financial services, technology-based enterprises, professional services and other high-value economic activities.\n\nThe experience of established Asian SEZs, particularly those in China, demonstrates the potential of such developments to support economic diversification and attract international capital. Colombo Port City, however, is still at a nascent stage compared with mature zones in China, Dubai, Malaysia and India. Sri Lanka is not yet widely recognised as an international investment destination and does not have the depth of business ecosystems, financial markets or investor networks available in those centres."
  },
