    "chunk_text": "William and Kate play \u2018gully\u2019 cricket with Sachin Tendulkar to begin India trip\n\nINDEPENDENT - William and Kate played street cricket with former cricketer Sachin Tendulkar in Mumbai on Monday to launch a three-day trip to India for the Earthshot Prize awards.\n\nThe royal couple were welcomed in the Ballard Estate business district by Mr Tendulkar, the former India skipper widely regarded as one of the sport\u2019s greatest batsmen.\n\nWilliam tried his hand at batting, then bowled to Kate and later to Mr Tendulkar.\n\nThey played alongside schoolgirls from the Mumbai neighbourhood of Nagpada.\n\nMr Tendulkar supports sports, health and education initiatives for underprivileged children through the Sachin Tendulkar Foundation.\n\nThe couple were greeted by drummers and served \u201ccutting chai\u201d, tea in small portions, in earthen cups at a stall under a banyan tree.\n\nMumbai hosts the sixth Earthshot Prize ceremony on Tuesday, the first time the awards are being held in India.\n\nWilliam founded the prize in 2020 as a 10-year project to repair the planet, and it is now at its mid-way point. Kate is reportedly \u201cenormously proud\u201d of the project.\n\nIt gives \u00a31 million each to five winners in categories that include protecting nature, cleaning the air and reviving the oceans.\n\nFifteen finalists were announced in September. They include a project in Argentina that uses artificial intelligence and satellite data to track wildfires across Latin America.\n\nThe visit is the Princess of Wales\u2019s most high-profile overseas trip since undergoing cancer treatment in 2024. She is now in remission and is taking on more public engagements.\n\nHer only significant overseas visit in that time was a two-day trip to Italy in May to promote her work on early childhood development.\n\nThe India programme also includes a ride on Mumbai\u2019s metro and meetings with Bollywood stars, who will attend Tuesday\u2019s ceremony, before the couple travel to Delhi on Wednesday to meet India\u2019s prime minister, Narendra Modi."
