    "chunk_text": "Turning to public sector remuneration, the SJB MP criticized the targeted salary hikes proposed in Budget 2027, claiming that only 16 percent of state employees stand to benefit, leaving 84 percent of the public workforce without relief.\n\nPointing to stalled infrastructure, Dr. de Silva noted that the budget failed to allocate funds to complete the Prabhaswara cold storage facility, despite its ceremonial opening by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake. He further revealed that he had received reports today of thieves breaking into the facility and stealing equipment.\n\nConcluding his remarks, Dr. de Silva emphasized that Sri Lanka requires genuine economic transformation, accusing the administration of stalling the Economic Transformation Act purely out of political reluctance because it was introduced by a previous government."
  },
