    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c24b6f094713a085057afba9b5997d8a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1953,
    "chunk_text": "Iran\u2019s proxy in Iraq rakes in hundreds of millions through oil smuggling\n\nReuters\u00a0- Iran's most powerful Shi'ite militia ally in Iraq has been raking in hundreds of millions of dollars from oil stolen from the state, Iraqi officials say, prompting the prime minister to ready his security forces to confront the heavily \u200barmed group.\n\nPrime Minister Ali al-Zaidi has launched his toughest challenge yet to the group Kataib Hezbollah by cracking down on an oil smuggling network it \u200chas run for years, senior security, army, police and oil officials told Reuters.\n\nThey said the smuggling, carried out with accomplices among some security and oil officials, has robbed the government of hundreds of millions of dollars dating back to 2021.\n\nKataib Hezbollah, branded a terrorist organisation by the US, is one of dozens of heavily armed pro-Iranian groups that have semi-official status in Iraq. It denies the smuggling and calls the crackdown part of \u200ba campaign to seize its weapons.\n\n\"We are therefore being subjected to the greatest campaign of blackmail aimed at forcing us to relinquish the weapons of dignity that have \u200bupheld sovereignty and protected the rights of Iraqis at multiple stages,\" the group said in a statement.\n\nIran, the Middle East's main Shi'ite Muslim \u2060power, has had deep influence in majority Shi'ite Iraq since the United States toppled Sunni Muslim dictator Saddam Hussein in 2003.\n\nThe Iranian-backed armed groups have resisted repeated calls by both Zaidi \u200band his ally US President Donald Trump to disarm, and have struck US troops and targets in Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates in solidarity with Tehran since the United \u200bStates and Israel launched their war against Iran in February.\n\nJasim al-Bahadli, an Iraqi security analyst specialising in studying armed Shi'ite groups aligned with Iran, said the government anti-smuggling campaign has become a political confrontation with the militia."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-16-dailymirrorlk-324686bb",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-324686bb",
    "date_str": "2026-11-16",
    "description": "Iran\u2019s proxy in Iraq rakes in hundreds of millions through oil smuggling",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/international/Irans-proxy-in-Iraq-rakes-in-hundreds-of-millions-through-oil-smuggling/107-355021",
    "lang": "en",
