    "md5": "95567846d26d824800e432c8bff26772",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1242,
    "chunk_text": "Two security sources who \u2060took part in an inspection mission on Saturday to Jurf al-Sakhar said investigators had found evidence that smugglers had punctured a crude oil pipeline and siphoned crude into makeshift storage pits dug in the ground.\n\nThe 26-inch pipeline carries at least 200,000 barrels per day of crude, according \u200bto an Iraqi Oil Ministry document reviewed by Reuters.\n\nTwo Iraqi oil officials with direct knowledge of the investigation said it was too early to quantify losses without knowing how long the tapping points had been operational, but estimated the value of crude potentially siphoned since 2021 could amount to hundreds of millions of dollars.\n\nThe crackdown is set \u2060against a \u200bbackdrop of mounting US pressure on Iraq over the role of pro-Iranian groups in the country's oil sector.\n\nIn May, \u200bWashington sanctioned Iraq's deputy oil minister, alleging he had facilitated the diversion of Iraqi oil for the benefit of Iran and its proxy militias. Sanctions were also imposed on militia leaders and networks Washington said were exploiting Iraq's \u200boil wealth to finance Tehran-aligned groups.\n\nReuters reported in 2024 that a fuel oil smuggling network had raked in $1 billion for Iran and its proxies."
