    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a34292a7fe61c365a54817dae396fbed",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "Risk of nuclear accident in Ukraine increasing this winter, atomic safety regulators say\n\nReuters\u00a0- The risk of a nuclear accident in Ukraine is increasing this winter, \u200bnuclear safety regulators representing 38 countries said on Monday, urging Russia to stop its attacks on the country's power infrastructure.\n\nMoscow has stepped \u200cup its drone and missile attacks on Ukrainian energy installations, such as plants, power lines and electricity substations, a system already weakened after nearly five years of conflict.\n\n\"Together we... express our deep concern about the increasing risks to nuclear safety arising from Russia's war against Ukraine, and its continued attacks on the country's energy infrastructure,\" the bodies \u200bsaid in a joint statement seen by Reuters ahead of publication.\n\n\"Together, (we) see an urgent need for Russia to cease attacks against Ukraine's nuclear \u200bfacilities and the energy infrastructure essential to their safe operation.\"\n\nThe regulators' key concern is that, without a stable electricity \u2060supply from the grid, it becomes more and more difficult for Ukrainian nuclear plants to keep their nuclear material cool and avoid a meltdown.\n\nIf \u200bthat were to occur, there could be releases of radioactivity into the air as happened during the 1986 Chornobyl disaster, considered to be the world's \u200bworst civil nuclear accident.\n\nThe accident spread iodine-131, caesium-134 and caesium-137 across parts of Ukraine, Belarus, Russia, and northern and central Europe.\n\nThe bodies behind the call are HERCA, the Heads of the European Radiological Protection Competent Authorities; WENRA, the Western European Nuclear Regulators Association; and NORA, the Heads of the Nordic Radiation Safety Authorities.\n\nTogether they represent 38 countries, including \u200ball EU countries, the US, Britain, Canada and Japan, among others."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
