    "chunk_text": "The budget\u2019s digital agenda now has to manage exactly this risk. The speech commits money to digital government transformation, a Cyber Security Authority and an AI Centre of Excellence at Wijerama. Those investments will put AI tools in the hands of thousands of officials drafting procurement papers, policy notes and, eventually, budget documents.\n\nThe Treasury could set one simple standard before the first Presidential Digital Excellence Award is handed out: every AI-assisted finding in an official document carries a human-verified source reference. A page number, a table or a dataset. No reference, no inclusion.\n\nThe same rule applies to the rest of us. Business owners, journalists and consultants, myself included, will use AI to read budgets, annual reports and contracts faster than ever. The 30 seconds I saved on the first read cost me an hour on the second, and that hour was the difference between an embarrassing post and an accurate one.\n\nAI found the questions in Budget 2027. People still have to find the answers.\n\n(The author is Founder and CEO of INOTREND Int., a neuromarketing and behavioural strategy consultancy, and CIM UK Brand Ambassador for Sri Lanka)"
