    "chunk_size_bytes": 1644,
    "chunk_text": "ISMM marks 54 years of excellence  with National Supply Chain Awards 2026\n\nThe Institute of Supply and Materials Management (ISMM) celebrated its 54th anniversary by hosting Sri Lanka's premier supply chain event, the National Supply Chain Day 2026 and National Supply Chain Excellence Awards 2026, at Monarch Imperial, Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte, on 24 October 2026.\n\nAs the apex professional body for supply chain and materials management in Sri Lanka, ISMM brought together leading professionals, academics, policymakers, and industry leaders to recognise excellence and discuss the future of supply chains in an increasingly interconnected world.\n\nThe day's proceedings commenced with a highly engaging seminar under the theme \"Geopolitics, Technology and the Future of Global Supply Chains.\" The Chief Guest was Sri Lanka Accreditation Board for Conformity Assessment Chairman AVM Prasanna Ranasinghe (Rtd), Guest of Honour was Ceylon Biscuits Ltd., Director/CEO Nalin Karunaratne, the special guest Organisation of Professional Associations (OPA) President and ISMM Immediate Past President and Capital Maharaja Group Industrial Hub Director Supply Chain Jayantha Gallehewa, and the Keynote Speaker Exterminators PLC Group Managing Director and Dreamron Group of Companies Managing Director Dr. Kishu Gomes and ISMM President Lilantha Subasinghe.\n\nThe grand Awards Ceremony in the evening was graced by High Commissioner of New Zealand to Sri Lanka, Pakistan, Maldives and Bangladesh David Pine, as a Chief Guest together with Industrial Development Board Chairman Yasas Hewage as a Guest of Honour, and ISMM President Lilantha Subasinghe."
