    "chunk_text": "The grand Awards Ceremony in the evening was graced by High Commissioner of New Zealand to Sri Lanka, Pakistan, Maldives and Bangladesh David Pine, as a Chief Guest together with Industrial Development Board Chairman Yasas Hewage as a Guest of Honour, and ISMM President Lilantha Subasinghe.\n\nThe National Supply Chain Excellence Awards have established themselves as a significant national platform for recognising outstanding achievements and contributions to the advancement of Supply Chain Management in Sri Lanka. The awards aim to encourage best practices, operational excellence, innovation, efficiency, resilience, and professional development across industries.\n\nThis year, the awards received more than 128 nominations, reflecting the growing recognition and enthusiasm of organisations and professionals towards supply chain excellence. Following the evaluation process, 54 organisations and 9 individual professionals were recognised for demonstrating exceptional achievements and contributions to the field.\n\nA total of 63 National Awards were presented under two main award titles:\n\nn National Award of Excellence \u2013 Best Supply Chain Practicing Organisation 2026\n\nn National Award of Excellence \u2013 Best Supply Chain Professional 2026\n\nThe organisational awards recognise outstanding supply chain practices across four business scales: Extra Large, Large, Medium, and Small, with categories covering Manufacturing, Service, and Trading sectors, as applicable. The Best Supply Chain Professional award recognises individual excellence under two categories: Corporate and Business.\n\nHigh Commissioner of New Zealand to Sri Lanka, Pakistan, Maldives and Bangladesh David Pine\n\nWinners of the National Award of Excellence \u2013 Best Supply Chain Practicing Organisation 2026\n\nn 1st Runner-Ups: John Keells Logistics Ltd., and Global Transportation and Logistics Ltd.\n\nn 2nd Runner-Ups: Logicare Ltd. and Ocean Maritime Ceylon Ltd."
