    "md5": "e81aa79054903420bca164ce76a65861",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1929,
    "chunk_text": "Manufacturing, services PMI expand at faster pace in October\n\nActivity in the country\u2019s manufacturing and services sectors expanded at a faster pace in October, according to the Purchasing Managers\u2019 Index (PMI) released yesterday by its compiler, the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL).\n\nThe PMI is based on a monthly survey of businesses. A reading above the neutral threshold of 50 shows expansion compared with the previous month, and a reading below 50 shows contraction.\n\nThe Manufacturing PMI rose to 55.3 in October from 53 in September. The CBSL said the expansion was broad-based, with all sub-indices above the neutral threshold. However, the index was still below the 61 recorded in October 2025.\n\nThe New Orders sub-index rose to 55 from 51. The CBSL said the increase was driven by the textiles and wearing apparel and the food and beverages sectors, reflecting seasonal demand. Production rose to 52.2 from 51, also driven by seasonal demand in the textiles and wearing apparel sector.\n\nEmployment continued to expand, although at a slower pace, with the sub-index easing to 51.1 from 52.6. Stock of Purchases rose to 56.1 from the neutral 50 recorded in September, in line with the growth in New Orders and Production. Meanwhile, Suppliers\u2019 Delivery Time lengthened further, with the sub-index rising to 66.1 from 63, reflecting increased demand for inputs.\n\nThe CBSL said the outlook for manufacturing activities over the next three months is favourable, underpinned by anticipated demand during the upcoming festive season.\n\nThe Services PMI, measured by the Business Activity Index, rose to 62.5 in October from 60.5 in September, indicating that services activities expanded at a higher rate. The index was below the 66 recorded in October 2025.\n\nBusiness Activity was driven primarily by improvements in other personal services, with notable contributions from financial services and goods transportation."
  },
