    "chunk_text": "The Services PMI, measured by the Business Activity Index, rose to 62.5 in October from 60.5 in September, indicating that services activities expanded at a higher rate. The index was below the 66 recorded in October 2025.\n\nBusiness Activity was driven primarily by improvements in other personal services, with notable contributions from financial services and goods transportation.\n\nServices Employment rose to 56.1 from 54, supported by recruitment across several sub-sectors to meet rising operational requirements. Meanwhile, Backlogs of Work declined at a faster rate, with the sub-index falling to 48.1 from 49.4.\n\nExpectations for Business Activity over the next three months stayed positive, although the sub-index eased to 74.7 from 76.2. The CBSL said expectations were supported by favourable macroeconomic conditions, anticipated increases in tourist arrivals and the upcoming festive season. However, it warned that prevailing global uncertainties continue to pose downside risks to the outlook.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s expansion comes as PMIs in major economies continue to rise. The CBSL release cites S&P Global data as of 16 November, 2026. On that data, manufacturing activity was rising at a slower rate globally and in India, China, the US and the Eurozone, and at a higher rate in the UK. Services activity was rising at a slower rate globally and in China, the US and the Eurozone, and at a higher rate in India and the UK."
