    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "Teejay Group posts strong recovery in 2Q\n\nThe Teejay Group yesterday said it has achieved a decisive improvement in its 2Q FY2026/27 performance, reflecting tangible gains from its ongoing restructuring and transformation initiatives.\n\nNotably, the group recorded a net profit of Rs. 0.4 billion for the quarter ended 30 September 2026, representing a significant 168% increase over the corresponding period of the previous year. This strong quarterly result enabled the group to recover substantially from the Rs. 0.5 billion loss recorded in 1Q, lowering the cumulative loss for the first half to a marginal Rs. 0.1 billion.\n\nOn an encouraging note, the group delivered revenue of Rs. 18.3 billion for the quarter ended 30 September 2026, recording an 18% year-on-year (YoY)\n\ngrowth, while first-half revenue increased by 9% compared with the corresponding period last year. This performance underscores the group\u2019s ability to sustain business momentum and respond effectively to evolving customer expectations and market dynamics, despite persistent geopolitical and economic uncertainties across key export markets. Its marketing strategy remains centred around strengthening strategic customer relationships, capitalising on emerging market opportunities, optimising the product mix and diversifying the customer and market portfolio to support sustainable long-term growth.\n\nMeanwhile, gross profit for the quarter reached Rs. 1.6 billion, representing a 30% YoY increase, supported by 18% revenue growth during the period. This improvement was driven by higher business volumes and stronger revenue generation. The group continued to demonstrate disciplined cost management, with distribution expenses declining by 9% year on year to Rs. 0.13 billion, while administrative expenses decreased by 5% to Rs. 0.84 billion compared with the corresponding quarter of the previous financial year."
