    "chunk_size_bytes": 1937,
    "chunk_text": "Bangladesh batter explains emotional century celebration\n\nNOV.17 - Litton Das explains his celebration against South Africa as Marques Ackerman enjoys his own milestone moment.\n\nBangladesh veteran Litton Das has revealed the reasons behind his unique celebration when scoring his eighth Test century against South Africa in Johannesburg on Monday.\n\nDas pulled a note out of his pocket when he brought up his century on the second day of the first ICC World Test Championship fixture against the Proteas at the Wanderers, with the right-hander dedicating his innings to his daughter Anayra who has just turned three.\n\nThe note read: 'Happy Birthday my Princess. This 100 for you', with Das providing more insight into his message at stumps on the second day after South Africa reached 287/4 at the close in reply to Bangladesh's first innings total of 400.\n\nDas revealed he had a Bangladesh staff member write the message on the morning of the second day when he was on 92*, with the 32-year-old confident he was going to complete his milestone on Monday given he only needed eight more runs to reach triple figures.\n\n\"I miss her,\" Das said in relation to his note for his daughter Anayra.\n\n\"Whenever you think of the future, you will think about positive things. I definitely thought last night that I would do that and I did.\"\n\nThere was a century of a different kind later in the day in Johannesburg when South Africa opener Marques Ackerman brought up his maiden hundred on his way to a brilliant innings of 157 that helped swing the momentum back into the favour of the hosts.\n\nAckerman was asked if he considered a similar celebration to the one that Das performed earlier in the day, but the left hander kept things a bit more simple as he acknowledged the role of his family and his teammates as he went that little bit better then the superb 95 he stroked against Australia last month in what was just his second Test appearance."
  },
