    "chunk_text": "Ackerman was asked if he considered a similar celebration to the one that Das performed earlier in the day, but the left hander kept things a bit more simple as he acknowledged the role of his family and his teammates as he went that little bit better then the superb 95 he stroked against Australia last month in what was just his second Test appearance.\n\n\"The last time I was in the press I said that it (innings of 95 against Australia) was motivation to try and get it the next time, so it was a big relief and a lot of emotion came out.\n\n\"It was a special feeling, especially that the family was also here.\"\n\nWhile Ackerman's ton helped the Proteas work their way back into the contest, Das believes Bangladesh is still well placed for victory and a strong chance to keep their hopes alive of reaching next year's World Test Championship Final at The Oval.\n\n\"The game plan is quite simple now. We have to take wickets, bowl them out. We can't allow them a big lead,\" Das added.\n\n\u201cWith the current playing conditions, I don't think we have too many runs on the board. 100-120. But still, if we can come early tomorrow and take two or three wickets, the scenario will be different,\u201d said Litton. \u201cBut if we can't, then we will have to work a bit harder, and the game should go on a bit longer, and we shouldn't leak runs too quickly. That will be our target.\" - ICC"
