    "chunk_text": "Imran Khan seeks urgent medical care fearing he \u2019may not return alive\u2019\n\nBBC - Pakistan's jailed former PM Imran Khan has appealed for urgent medical treatment, saying that his and his wife's health has been deteriorating.\n\n\"At 74, this unrelenting state is taking me to a place from which I may not return alive,\" the cricket star-turned-politician wrote in a letter published by his lawyer Salman Safdar.\n\nAuthorities in Islamabad maintain that Khan gets seen weekly by doctors, who have assessed that he is of \"satisfactory\" health.\n\nKhan, who faces more than 100 charges, has been in prison since August 2023. His wife Bushra Bibi was jailed along with him last year. Khan argues the cases against them, ranging from corruption to selling state gifts, are politically motivated.\n\nConcerns over Khan's health have grown louder in the past year, with his family claiming he has lost most of his vision in his right eye after prison authorities failed to take action.\n\nIn his letter, Khan wrote that doctors have told him he is \"highly vulnerable to a brain haemorrhage and cardiac arrest\", and that his heart has already \"suffered damage\".\n\nHe also expressed concern for Bushra Bibi, whom he says suffered a detached retina in April and underwent surgery in secrecy. Khan said he fears she may lose her sight without further surgery.\n\n\"I have fought impossible legal battles in countless cases, and I have not stopped. But the system has stopped giving me justice,\" he wrote.\n\nHe said that he is being held in solitary confinement for up to 22 hours a day, where he is allowed neither visits by his family nor access to books and television, and that this has \"taken a heavy toll\" on his mental health.\n\nHe also claimed he had only seen his lawyers four times over the past year.\n\n\"I will only remain able to prove my innocence if I stay alive,\" he wrote."
