    "chunk_size_bytes": 1892,
    "chunk_text": "Robert Pattinson to replace Daniel Craig as James Bond\n\nBBC - The announcement was made by Amazon MGM Studios in a social media post on Monday, with a picture showing Pattinson in character as 007.\n\nThe 40-year-old becomes the seventh actor to play the famous fictional spy and will star in the 26th Bond movie, due to be released in 2028.\n\nIn a statement, the London-born actor said: \"James Bond is one of the most legendary characters in cinema, and to be entrusted with 007 is the honour of a lifetime.\"\n\nThe next Bond film will be directed by Denis Villeneuve and written by Steven Knight, but its title and exact release date have not yet been announced.\n\nIn his statement, Pattinson said he was \"deeply grateful\" to the film's creative team \"for their belief in me\".\n\n\"To say this role is a dream come true is an understatement,\" he added. \"I couldn't be more excited about this partnership and the work ahead with this fantastic team.\"\n\nThe announcement comes after years of intense speculation about who will take over from Daniel Craig in one of the most high-profile - and highly scrutinised - roles in entertainment.\n\nThe next 007 film will be the first since long-term Bond producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G Wilson stepped back and Amazon took creative control of the franchise, after acquiring the series' parent company MGM.\n\nBy the time the 26th Bond film is released, it will have been seven years since the last - 2021's No Time To Die - the biggest gap in the franchise's history.\n\nDirector Villeneuve is best known for films including the Dune trilogy, Prisoners, Sicario, Arrival and Blade Runner 2049, while writer Knight is known for TV hits Peaky Blinders and House of Guinness, and films including Burnt, Spencer and Locke.\n\nPattinson has already worked with Villeneuve on Dune: Part 3, where he stars as a new villain, Scytale. The film is released next month."
