    "md5": "2207e4181490f51dfd7b1fb0e11fde42",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1999,
    "chunk_text": "Director Villeneuve is best known for films including the Dune trilogy, Prisoners, Sicario, Arrival and Blade Runner 2049, while writer Knight is known for TV hits Peaky Blinders and House of Guinness, and films including Burnt, Spencer and Locke.\n\nPattinson has already worked with Villeneuve on Dune: Part 3, where he stars as a new villain, Scytale. The film is released next month.\n\n\"We were surrounded by extraordinary talent, but there can only be one 007. I am overjoyed to welcome Robert Pattinson as our new James Bond.\n\n\"He has the timeless soul of 007 and brings a spirit that is completely new. I cannot wait to begin.\"\n\nPattinson's casting was also welcomed by Buckingham Palace, with a post on Instagram sharing the news and adding: \"Welcome to His Majesty's Secret Service, Mr Bond.\"\n\nAustralian actor George Lazenby, who played James Bond in the 1969 film On Her Majesty's Secret, posted a video on social media welcoming Pattinson to \"the most exclusive club in the world\".\n\n\"Remember to enjoy yourself... Let's see if you'll have 'this never happened to the other fella' moment,\" Lazenby said.\n\nSeveral other actors, including Josh O'Connor, Callum Turner and Jack Lowden, were reported to be in the frame for the role as screen tests took place in recent weeks.\n\nBut Amazon MGM ultimately went with a household name, choosing a more bankable movie star who is widely seen as a safe pair of hands.\n\nProducers Amy Pascal and David Heyman said the \"legacy of James Bond is in great hands with Robert Pattinson\".\n\n\"His fearlessness as an actor, his self-deprecating wit and his ability to continually reinvent himself make him the perfect Bond for our times.\"\n\nAt 40, Pattinson is one of the older actors who was thought to have auditioned for the role of Bond.\n\nReports last week suggested Pattinson's deal committed him to playing 007 for three films, rather than the four that had reportedly been discussed with some of the other actors, but that has not been officially confirmed."
