    "md5": "448b094618904f227aea3f571f82a322",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "Reports last week suggested Pattinson's deal committed him to playing 007 for three films, rather than the four that had reportedly been discussed with some of the other actors, but that has not been officially confirmed.\n\nHe went on to play vampire Edward Cullen in Twilight, the hugely popular film series based on Stephenie Meyer's best-selling novels.\n\nPattinson starred opposite Kristen Stewart in five Twilight films in total, which collectively made more than $3bn (\u00a32.2bn) at the box office worldwide.\n\nHe has gone on to star in other major films such as 2022's The Batman and Christopher Nolan's The Odyssey, released earlier this year.\n\nBut he is also respected within the industry for how many roles he has taken in smaller movies - often independent, experimental or arthouse films.\n\nHis other credits include The Lighthouse, Mickey 17, Life, The Drama, Good Time, The Rover, Bel Ami, Primetime, Tenet and The Lost City of Z.\n\nPattinson follows in the footsteps of only six actors to have played James Bond in the official film series \u2013 Sean Connery, George Lazenby, Roger Moore, Timothy Dalton, Pierce Brosnan and Daniel Craig.\n\nCraig appeared in five Bond movies in total, starting with 2006's Casino Royale, and spent 16 years as the secret agent created by author Ian Fleming.\n\nIn a statement, Fleming's estate said they were \"delighted to welcome Robert Pattinson to the James Bond family\".\n\nThe next film will mark a new era for the franchise. Amazon purchased MGM for $8.5bn in 2021, which included the rights to distribute James Bond.\n\nThen in 2025, long-time Bond producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G Wilson agreed to sell creative control of the franchise to Amazon MGM.\n\nBefore that, the franchise had been under the Broccoli family's control since 1962's Dr. No, when Sean Connery first starred as Bond."
