    "chunk_size_bytes": 1282,
    "chunk_text": "A special expert discussion involving the Deputy Minister and medical specialists was also held during the programme. A set of special guidelines aimed at improving the health and well-being of premature babies and their long-term health outcomes was unveiled.\n\nAlthough advances in medical science have improved survival rates among premature babies, proper medical treatment and long-term follow-up remain essential to minimise complications associated with premature birth.\n\nSuch interventions are also important in reducing the long-term social and economic impact of premature births on families and society.\n\nThe Perinatal Society of Sri Lanka is a multidisciplinary professional organisation comprising specialists in obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics and neonatal care. It works to improve maternal, fetal and newborn healthcare through research, professional training and the promotion of scientific knowledge.\n\nThe event was attended by Society President Professor Ruwanthi Perera, Secretary Consultant Physician Dr. Jithma Fonseka, Treasurer Consultant Physician Dr. Ruwan Silva, President-elect Consultant Physician Dr. Sri Tharan and Immediate Past President Consultant Physician Dr. Harendra Dissanayake, along with other medical specialists and representatives."
