    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "Namal Rajapaksa among 41 accused in Hambantota protest case\n\nNov. 17 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Hambantota High Court ordered yesterday that indictments be served on 41 individuals, including Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa, over alleged damage to public property during a protest held in Hambantota against the proposed sale of Mattala International Airport and the Hambantota International Port to the private sector.\n\nHigh Court Judge Duminda Mudunkotuwa issued the order when the case was taken up before the Hambantota High Court.\n\nThe 35th accused, Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa, who is currently in remand custody, was not produced before the Hambantota High Court as he had to appear in another case before the Colombo High Court.\n\nParliamentarian D.V. Chanaka, former MPs Upali Kodikara and Prasanna Ranaweera, former Provincial Councillor Ajith Prasanna and Sampath Athukorala were among those who appeared before the court. All the other accused, except three individuals, were also present.\n\nThe court officials distributed the indictments separately to the accused after they were lined up inside the courtroom.\n\nThe judge ordered that all 41 accused be released on bail, subject to two sureties of Rs. 500,000 each and a cash bail of Rs. 10,000 per person. The court also imposed a travel ban on all the accused, preventing them from travelling overseas.\n\nThe case relates to a protest held on or around October 6, 2017, during which protesters blocked the road leading to the Hambantota International Port and obstructed access to the Indian High Commission and its official residence.\n\nThe accused face charges including violating a court order, causing damage to public and private property and unlawful assembly."
