    "chunk_text": "The case relates to a protest held on or around October 6, 2017, during which protesters blocked the road leading to the Hambantota International Port and obstructed access to the Indian High Commission and its official residence.\n\nThe accused face charges including violating a court order, causing damage to public and private property and unlawful assembly.\n\nThe case was taken up under High Court case number HAM/HC/PP/00032/2026.\n\nMeanwhile, the lawyer appearing for the 35th accused, Chamira de Silva, instructed by President's Counsel Sampath Mendis, requested the court to issue directions on how Namal Rajapaksa should be produced at the next hearing.\n\nThe lawyer requested that Rajapaksa be produced through prison authorities if he remained in remand custody by the next hearing date, or otherwise be allowed to appear before court through the normal procedure.\n\nThe judge accordingly ordered that Rajapaksa be produced through prison authorities if he remained in remand custody on the next hearing date. Otherwise, he should appear before court through his lawyers.\n\nThe judge also directed that copies of the National Identity Cards and certificates from the respective Grama Niladharis of the 6th, 12th and 29th accused be submitted to court at a later date."
