    "md5": "10c206cd870385f44f83a947f584edb0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1796,
    "chunk_text": "Italian Cuisine Week launched to promote authentic food and culinary heritage\n\nFrom left: Chef Nicky Brian Perera - 11th MasterChef Italy Semi-finalist; Damiano Francovigh - Ambassador of Italy to Sri Lanka; Krishan Balendra, Chairperson - John Keells Group; Charitha Subasinghe, President - Retail - John Keells Group and Alberto Arcidiacono, Deputy Head of Mission - Italian Embassy\n\nThe Italian Trade Agency (ITA), in collaboration with the Embassy of Italy in Colombo and Keells Supermarkets, officially launched the Week of the Italian Cuisine in the World 2026 (Settimana della Cucina Italiananel Mondo), an initiative dedicated to promoting Italian culinary heritage, authentic food products and the culture and traditions behind Italian cuisine.\n\nThe press conference took place on 13 November at the Italian Ambassador\u2019s Residence in Colombo, bringing together representatives of the media and selected influencers to celebrate Italian gastronomy and highlighting the availability of Italian products in the Sri Lankan market.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Ambassador of Italy to Sri Lanka Damiano Francovigh said \u201cThe Week of Italian Cuisine in the World celebrates Italy\u2019s rich gastronomic heritage and the quality of its food products. Through our collaboration with Keells, we are delighted to introduce the first islandwide Italian food tasting programme, bringing authentic Italian flavours closer to Sri Lankan consumers. The newly opened Colombo Desk of the Italian Trade Agency will further strengthen commercial relations, creating new opportunities for businesses in both countries,\u201d he said.\n\nThe programme included a live cooking demonstration by Rome-based Italian Chef Nicky Brian Perera, whose own story weaves Sri Lankan roots through the Italian culinary heritage."
  },
