    "chunk_text": "Addressing the gathering, Ambassador of Italy to Sri Lanka Damiano Francovigh said \u201cThe Week of Italian Cuisine in the World celebrates Italy\u2019s rich gastronomic heritage and the quality of its food products. Through our collaboration with Keells, we are delighted to introduce the first islandwide Italian food tasting programme, bringing authentic Italian flavours closer to Sri Lankan consumers. The newly opened Colombo Desk of the Italian Trade Agency will further strengthen commercial relations, creating new opportunities for businesses in both countries,\u201d he said.\n\nThe programme included a live cooking demonstration by Rome-based Italian Chef Nicky Brian Perera, whose own story weaves Sri Lankan roots through the Italian culinary heritage.\n\nThe participating stores are Keells Union Place-Colombo 2, Gampaha, Kalutara South, Kandy - Peradeniya Road, Kegalle, Kurunegala - Bauddhaloka Mawatha, Anuradhapura, Jaffna, Matara - Kumaratunga Mawatha, Ambalangoda and Ratnapura.\n\nChairperson of John Keells Group PLC, Krishan Balendra highlighted the importance of international partnerships in strengthening commercial relationships between countries, noting that the collaboration would create new business opportunities while introducing Sri Lankan consumers to the diversity and quality of authentic Italian cuisine.\n\nThe occasion also served to formally announce the opening of the Colombo Desk of the Italian Trade Agency (ITA), marking an important step in strengthening economic and commercial relations between Italy and Sri Lanka."
