    "md5": "126a7b4b010e56045c8a174b543d2d8b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1526,
    "chunk_text": "Payable CEO named \u2018FinTech Leader of the Year\u2019\n\nYohan Wijesiriwardane, Co-Founder and CEO of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest payments aggregator Payable, was recognised as \u2018FinTech Leader of the Year\u2019 at Sri Lanka FinTech Festival 2026, honouring his contribution towards helping move Sri Lanka\u2019s financial technology industry forward.\n\nPresented at FinTech Night at Shangri-La Colombo, the special award recognises individual leadership that advances the country\u2019s fintech sector. The peer-nominated category forms part of the Sri Lanka FinTech Awards, organised by FinTech Forum Sri Lanka in collaboration with the Ministry of Digital Economy, with the Postgraduate Institute of Management as Knowledge Partner.\n\nHeld across two days, Sri Lanka FinTech Festival 2026 brought together financial institutions, fintech businesses, policymakers, investors and technology providers to strengthen collaboration and support the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy. Its programme included CEOs Night, the FinTech Expo and FinTech Night, combining industry discussions, technology showcases and recognition of progress across the sector.\n\nThe festival\u2019s discussions focused on fintech innovation, sustainable business growth, financial inclusion, as well as security and fraud prevention. By bringing these conversations together with its awards programme, the event delivered a platform to share practical experiences, build partnerships and recognise the people helping Sri Lanka\u2019s digital finance industry progress."
