    "chunk_size_bytes": 1927,
    "chunk_text": "Home Lands awards construction of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo to CHEC\n\nWang Gang (left) and Nalin Herath after signing the agreement\n\nHome Lands Group has awarded the construction of its landmark 40-storey twin-tower development project at Port City Colombo, Central Park Boulevard to the world-renowned China Harbour Engineering Company (CHEC) in a major construction, conceptual and structural design collaboration.\n\nThe strategic construction collaboration between Home Lands and CHEC began earlier this year with Home Lands awarding the construction of its iconic mega project Pentara Residencies Thummulla Handiya to CHEC.\n\nThe construction of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo being undertaken by CHEC marks the second time Home Lands has placed its trust on CHEC to deliver a world class product based on CHEC\u2019s expertise and impressive track record. The agreement was signed by Nalin Herath, Chairman of Home Lands Group, and Wang Gang, Managing Director of China Harbour Engineering Company Ltd South Asia and South East Asia.\n\nAs one of the world\u2019s leading engineering and construction companies, CHEC brings decades of expertise across Asia, Africa, Europe and the Middle East. Its work across ports, highways, bridges and large-scale reclamation projects has earned the company a global reputation for quality, scale and timely delivery.\n\nThe architecture of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo has been designed by SOG Architects (Singapore) and PWA Architects (Sri Lanka). SOG Architects, an internationally acclaimed design studio with experience across Asia, Europe and the Middle East, brings global design excellence, blending timeless architecture, refined spatial planning and contemporary luxury. PWA Architects, one of the country\u2019s respected architectural practices, brings deep local insight, ensuring the design responds to Sri Lanka\u2019s climate, culture and way of life."
  },
