    "md5": "ee2a77a7ec52ea8b70e36eef24f5cfb5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1685,
    "chunk_text": "The architecture of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo has been designed by SOG Architects (Singapore) and PWA Architects (Sri Lanka). SOG Architects, an internationally acclaimed design studio with experience across Asia, Europe and the Middle East, brings global design excellence, blending timeless architecture, refined spatial planning and contemporary luxury. PWA Architects, one of the country\u2019s respected architectural practices, brings deep local insight, ensuring the design responds to Sri Lanka\u2019s climate, culture and way of life.\n\nThe Principal Structural Engineer of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo is East China Architectural Design & Research Institute (ECADI), one of China\u2019s foremost design institutes, with work spanning supertall towers such as Tianjin 117 and Wuhan Center, major transport hubs including Shanghai Pudong International Airport, and projects across 23 countries. The structural design is independently peer reviewed by Meinhardt Singapore, part of the global Meinhardt Group with over 4,500 specialists across Asia, Australia, the Middle East and Europe, ensuring every structural element meets the highest international standards.\n\nSpeaking on the project, Nalin Herath said, \u201cCentral Park Boulevard Port City Colombo sets a new benchmark for luxury living in Sri Lanka. For every element of this development, we have engaged the finest expertise in the world, and Home Lands brings these elements together under one vision and one standard. Our customers deserve a true masterpiece, and that is what we are delivering. With construction progressing ahead of schedule, we are on track to complete the project in 36 months.\u201d"
