    "language": "en",
    "md5": "be6f36ff5a4e51d1ba09b6a1d84e088a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank launches Payable TAP in South Asia\u2019s 1st deployment of Mastercard Cloud Commerce\n\nHelps businesses accept contactless card payments with greater ease and flexibility\n\nReaffirming its position as Sri Lanka\u2019s leader in technology and digital banking innovation, Commercial Bank of Ceylon has announced the launch of Payable TAP in partnership with Payable (Pvt.) Ltd and Mastercard, marking South Asia\u2019s very first deployment of Mastercard Cloud Commerce technology.\n\nUnveiled at Mastercard\u2019s Access Unlocked Summit in Sri Lanka in the presence of senior government representatives, the solution enables any NFC-enabled Android smartphone to function as a secure, fully compliant contactless payment terminal, eliminating the need for dedicated point-of-sale hardware.\n\nA live contactless transaction demonstrated at the summit highlighted the solution\u2019s readiness for daily use, enabling micro and small merchants to accept contactless payments via physical or virtual cards.\n\nPowered by Mastercard Cloud Commerce, Payable TAP represents a significant evolution in Software Point of Sale technology, shifting core payment processing, authentication and security functions from the device to the cloud. This architecture enhances scalability, enables real-time fraud monitoring and ensures continuous updates without disruption to the merchants.\n\nPayable TAP allows the merchants to accept physical credit and debit cards as well as digital wallet payments, using the Tap and Pay technology, with a transaction limit of up to Rs.100,000 per tap. The platform also supports QR payments.\n\nDesigned for accessibility, Payable TAP features a trilingual interface available in Sinhala, Tamil, and English and issues instant digital receipts via SMS or email. The businesses can activate multiple smartphones under a single account, making it an ideal solution for delivery operations and multi-point retail environments."
  },
