    "md5": "2bb7d160f59cd90a919df0bfa99d29fe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1673,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWhen acceptance moves from hardware to software and from devices to the cloud, the barriers that once limited participation in the digital economy effectively disappear. What we are enabling through this collaboration is not just acceptance but a more resilient and future-ready payments ecosystem that can adapt rapidly to the changing customer behaviours and business models.\u201d\n\nPayable is Sri Lanka\u2019s leading fintech and digital payments provider.\n\n\u201cMastercard\u2019s Tap on Phone capabilities have helped democratise card acceptance across more than 110 markets worldwide. With Cloud Commerce, we are taking that vision a step further by moving critical payment functionality to the cloud, enabling greater flexibility, scalability and accessibility,\u201d said Mastercard Country Manager Sri Lanka Mahesha Amarasuriya.\n\n\u201cThis launch marks an important milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s digital payments ecosystem. Together with Commercial Bank and Payable, we are helping reduce barriers to acceptance and making secure, affordable digital payment capabilities accessible to micro and small merchants. This collaboration reflects the power of innovation in advancing financial inclusion, empowering entrepreneurs and accelerating the country\u2019s journey toward a more connected and digitally enabled economy.\u201d\n\nThe merchants can be onboarded through Payable in a simple four-step process, after which they can download the application, log in and begin accepting payments immediately. At the point of sale, the customers simply tap their contactless card or device on the merchant\u2019s smartphone, with transactions processed in real time via Mastercard Cloud Commerce."
