    "md5": "2181d353c5837734af56e86479474013",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 784,
    "chunk_text": "A proposed 200 percent enhanced capital allowance for qualifying Board of Investment-approved export manufacturing projects worth at least US $ 3 million could also encourage the processors to expand capacity and develop higher-value products, the association said.\n\nA further Rs.1 billion is earmarked for fisheries resource management, including scientific stock assessments, habitat mapping and monitoring.\n\nThe SEASL identified shrimp farming as another source of export growth and called for closer links between the aquaculture farmers, processors and exporters. It cited the Marine Stewardship Council certification of Sri Lanka\u2019s North-Western Blue Swimming Crab Fishery as an example of how recognised sustainability standards can help the producers access premium markets."
