    "md5": "e4faa13fea9e4c83edb577cf0e22551a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1948,
    "chunk_text": "Teejay group records strong recovery in 2Q FY2026/27\n\nThe Teejay group achieved a decisive improvement in its 2Q FY2026/27 performance, reflecting tangible gains from its ongoing restructuring and transformation initiatives.\n\nNotably, the group recorded a net profit of Rs.0.4 billion for the quarter ended September 30, 2026, representing a significant 168 percent increase over the corresponding period of the previous year. This strong quarterly result enabled the group to recover substantially from the Rs.0.5 billion loss recorded in 1Q, lowering the cumulative loss for the first half to a marginal Rs.0.1 billion.\n\nOn an encouraging note, the group delivered revenue of Rs.18.3 billion for the quarter ended September 30, 2026, recording an 18 percent year-on-year (YoY) growth, while the first-half revenue increased by 9 percent compared with the corresponding period last year.\n\nThis performance underscores the group\u2019s ability to sustain business momentum and respond effectively to the evolving customer expectations and market dynamics, despite the persistent geopolitical and economic uncertainties across key export markets.\n\nIts marketing strategy remains centred around strengthening strategic customer relationships, capitalising on emerging market opportunities, optimising the product mix and diversifying the customer and market portfolio to support sustainable long-term growth.\n\nMeanwhile, gross profit for the quarter reached Rs.1.6 billion, representing a 30 percent YoY increase, supported by an 18 percent revenue growth during the period. This improvement was driven by higher business volumes and stronger revenue generation.\n\nThe group continued to demonstrate disciplined cost management, with the distribution expenses declining by 9 percent YoY to Rs.0.13 billion, while the administrative expenses decreased by 5 percent to Rs.0.84 billion compared with the corresponding quarter of the previous financial year."
  },
