    "chunk_text": "The group continued to demonstrate disciplined cost management, with the distribution expenses declining by 9 percent YoY to Rs.0.13 billion, while the administrative expenses decreased by 5 percent to Rs.0.84 billion compared with the corresponding quarter of the previous financial year.\n\nTeejay Group Chairman Ajit Gunewardene commented, \u201cWhile the operating environment continued to present challenges, the group made encouraging progress in strengthening its performance during the second quarter in FY2026/27. Our strategic priorities and disciplined execution of the transformation agenda strengthened the overall performance and reinforced the group\u2019s ability to navigate the challenging times. We remain committed to building on this momentum, responding proactively to the evolving market conditions and creating sustainable long-term value for our shareholders.\u201d\n\nElaborating further Teejay Group CEO Pubudu De Silva said, \u201cTeejay Lanka is pleased to report improved second quarter earnings for FY2026/27 despite the external headwinds. The sustained financial strength and healthy liquidity position in the quarter under review reinforces the group\u2019s resilience and its capacity to meet the ongoing business requirements while implementing strategic growth initiatives. We believe our winning strategy will help drive greater profitability during the upcoming quarters of the financial year.\u201d"
