    "chunk_size_bytes": 883,
    "chunk_text": "Applying Rostow\u2019s framework to Sri Lanka, Dr. Wijewardena argued that the country had already completed the preconditions for take-off, with the support of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and that Budget 2027 would lay the foundation for take-off over the next five years.\n\nHowever, he cautioned that the IMF programme would end in March next year, with no assurance of an immediate follow-on arrangement, leaving Sri Lanka to rely on its own economic policy programme for the last nine months of 2027.\n\nLikening the economy to a hybrid vehicle that has been running on both a gasoline engine and an IMF-supplied electric motor, he stressed that once the motor is removed, the president must supply \u201cthe torque for take-off\u201d from the domestic engine alone.\n\n\u201cNow it is time for Sri Lanka to move forward with this pragmatic development of the country,\u201d he added. (NF)"
