    "chunk_text": "Elsewhere, three people have been injured in a Russian missile attack in the Cherkast region, according to local officials.\n\nThe latest round of tit-for-tat strikes came after US, Ukrainian and European officials held talks on ways to facilitate \"direct engagement\" between Russia and Europe to end the war.\n\nHe added that Nato \"will remain a critical pillar of European security\", and that preparations are underway for a further multilateral meeting \"in the near future\".\n\nZelensky said that the meeting was \"difficult\", adding that more needed to be done to support Ukraine's defence against Russian ballistic missile strikes, which he said were being provided by North Korea.\n\nThe Ukrainian president has long called for European nations to be included in any peace talks, which he argues is necessary because of Kyiv's longer-term ambition to join the EU.\n\nMeanwhile, Ukrainian officials said the final death toll from a Russian attack on the southern Ukrainian village of Kamyshuvakha earlier this month had reached 72.\n\nFour people are still considered missing after the bombing, which Ukrainian officials said was one of the deadliest individual attacks since the start of the war in 2022.\n\nFootage, from a camera on one of the killed police officers, showed residents going to an underground shelter after the initial attack on 2 November. Soon after a blast is heard and flames are seen as the shelter is hit.\n\nUkrainian police said of those killed were police officers, \"staff of the gymnasium, utility workers and medical personnel\".\n\nRussia's launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. Approximately one-fifth of Ukraine is now under Russian occupation and Kyiv has refused Putin's demand to give up areas of Ukraine's eastern Donbas that remain under its control."
