    "chunk_text": "Graduate teacher recruitment: School preference system opens today\n\nColombo, Nov. 17 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Ministry of Education has announced that the online system for submitting school preferences for graduate teacher recruits will be available from today (November 17).\n\nThe system is for graduates recruited to Class 3-1 (a) of the Sri Lanka Teachers' Service to fill vacancies for Sinhala, Tamil and English medium teachers in national and provincial schools islandwide.\n\nApplicants can access the \u201cTeacher Recruitment Application System\u201d through the Ministry of Education's official website and submit their school preferences.\n\nTo log in, applicants must enter their National Identity Card (NIC) number or examination index number, along with the one-time password (OTP) provided in the letter sent with their interview call-up.\n\nThe Ministry said applicants who have not yet received their letters by post would not be able to access the system until they receive them.\n\nHowever, it assured applicants that there was no need for concern over delays in receiving interview call letters, adding that the system would remain accessible until each applicant's scheduled interview date.\n\nThose who have not received their letters by the interview date will be given an opportunity to submit their school preferences on the day of the interview."
  },
