    "chunk_text": "Seven new envoys present credentials to President\n\nColombo, Nov. 17 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Seven newly appointed Ambassadors and High Commissioners presented their Letters of Credence to President Anura Kumara Dissanayake at a ceremony held at the Presidential Secretariat today (17).\n\nThe newly appointed envoys represent the Republic of Korea, Switzerland, the European Union, Egypt, Laos, Namibia and Singapore.\n\nThe envoys, in order of precedence, are Kim Youn-Jung of the Republic of Korea, Daniel Hunn of Switzerland, Sylvia Hartleif of the European Union and Ahmed El-Sayed Abdel Halim Amer Helal of Egypt.\n\nThe other three are Vithaya Xayavong of Laos, Wing Commander Alex L. Tukuhupwele (Retd.) of Namibia and Patrick Daniel of Singapore.\n\nWhile the envoys from South Korea, Switzerland, the European Union and Egypt are based in Colombo, the representatives of Laos and Namibia are based in New Delhi. Singapore\u2019s High Commissioner-designate is based in Singapore.\n\nThe respective governments and the European Union appointed the envoys to represent them in Sri Lanka with the agreement of the Government of Sri Lanka.\n\nFollowing the formal presentation of their credentials, President Dissanayake held cordial discussions with the newly appointed diplomats.\n\nMinister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Vijitha Herath and Secretary to the President Dr Nandika Sanath Kumanayake were also present at the ceremony."
