    "chunk_text": "IRD exceeds 2026 target with Rs. 2.44 trillion collection\n\nColombo, Nov. 17 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Inland Revenue Department (IRD) has surpassed its annual revenue target of Rs. 2,402 billion for 2026, collecting Rs. 2,441.9 billion as of November 16, the department announced.\n\nThe collection exceeds the annual target by Rs. 39.9 billion, marking a significant boost to Government revenue ahead of the end of the year.\n\nThe department said it had collected an additional Rs. 491 billion compared to the corresponding period in 2025, reflecting a 115% increase in revenue collection.\n\nAccording to the Commissioner General of Inland Revenue, the achievement reflects improvements in tax administration, greater efficiency in revenue collection and increased public compliance with tax laws and regulations.\n\nThe department said the achievement marked an important milestone in the Government's efforts to strengthen revenue generation."
