    "chunk_text": "Israel set for new parliament speaker as Netanyahu grip loosens\n\nARAB NEWS - Israel\u2019s parliament is set Tuesday to select a new speaker opposed to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, a first step in rolling back the legacy of the country\u2019s divisive veteran leader even though he is still trying to stay in office.\n\nGadi Eisenkot, a former military chief who has until next month to form a government to replace Netanyahu, has put forward his ally Matan Kahana to be the next speaker.\n\nNetanyahu\u2019s Likud party is expected to try to draw out debate to scuttle Kahana\u2019s election in the parliament, known as the Knesset.\n\nLikud in a statement demanded that lawmakers hold off on \u201csevere, unilateral measures\u201d and on \u201creplacing the Knesset speaker at a time that negotiations are ongoing to form a national-unity government.\u201d\n\nLikud has said it will put forward Ofir Katz as its own candidate for Knesset speaker, but Kahana is the favorite ahead of the vote.\n\nThe parliament speaker is an important office given that it sets the timetable for parliamentary business and can therefore speed up or delay debates or votes on proposed laws.\n\nNeither Eisenkot nor Netanyahu won a majority in the 120-member Knesset in October 27 elections.\n\nBut Kahana can easily reach the 61-vote threshold in Tuesday\u2019s vote thanks to votes by the Arab-Israeli parties, which made historic gains in the election on the back of anger over Netanyahu\u2019s hard-right government.\n\nNetanyahu\u2019s and Eisenkot\u2019s parties met Sunday on the possibility of joining a unity government but the meeting appeared to be largely a formality, with both men saying they should be prime minister.\n\nNetanyahu, who has been urging US President Donald Trump to resume war on Iran, has talked up the threat from Tehran as he insists on the need for a unity government."
