    "language": "en",
    "md5": "253a540079639654be16d075333ee37a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1970,
    "chunk_text": "Licensed finance companies and leasing institutions can provide financing for machinery, commercial vehicles, equipment, renewable-energy systems and other productive assets. These institutions can serve smaller businesses that may not always fit conventional banking products.\n\nThe Budget\u2019s reference to public-private partnerships, including the proposed logistics centre at Colombo Port, also creates opportunities for project finance, infrastructure bonds, institutional investment and insurance services.\n\nCommercial banks can arrange project financing and working capital, while insurers can manage construction and operational risks. Pension funds and other institutional investors could contribute longer-term capital through appropriately structured investment instruments.\n\nA more diversified financial system would reduce excessive dependence on bank balance sheets and create additional sources of funding for long-term development.\n\nThe Budget\u2019s proposed SME Listing Support Mechanism and the \u2018A Share for Everyone\u2019 initiative are positive steps towards broadening capital-market participation.\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange is expected to deploy Rs. 250 million, with a further Rs. 500 million proposed for these initiatives. The Budget Speech also notes that active stock-market traders represent only around 0.7% of the population above 18 years of age.\n\nFor growing businesses, equity capital can be an important alternative to borrowing. Unlike debt, equity financing does not impose fixed interest and principal repayment obligations. It can therefore provide a more suitable funding structure for businesses undertaking expansion or innovation with uncertain short-term cash flows.\n\nHowever, encouraging SMEs to list requires more than financial incentives. Businesses need support in accounting, corporate governance, auditing, valuation, legal compliance and investor relations. Market liquidity and investor confidence are equally important."
  },
