    "md5": "4ff6acc7c26d9ca3959ed1762bf493fb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1905,
    "chunk_text": "FCCISL says Budget 2027 opens way for growth from districts and villages\n\nThe Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry of Sri Lanka (FCCISL) in a statement welcomed Budget 2027\u2019s focus on public investment and enterprise support.\n\nTo turn those proposals into jobs and orders for local businesses, FCCISL calls for realistic project budgets, timely payments and early government intervention when delivery is at risk. District and Divisional Secretaries can help agencies and businesses resolve obstacles close to where projects are delivered.\n\nAnnex III of the Budget Speech presented on 12 November puts public investment at Rs. 1,750 billion, 18.2% above the revised 2026 estimate. A proposed Rs. 260 billion supplementary estimate for Cyclone Ditwah reconstruction includes Rs. 250 billion for public investment and Rs. 10 billion for recurrent spending. With that supplement, proposed public investment reaches Rs. 2,000 billion, 35.1% above the revised 2026 estimate. The Budget was presented at Second Reading.\n\nThe Citizens Budget shows that transport has the largest capital component among the themes shown below. For district suppliers and contractors, the next steps are the publication of project scopes, funding schedules and tender dates.\n\nDistrict and divisional secretaries can connect projects to local needs\n\nFCCISL proposes that District Secretaries convene line agencies, local authorities and chambers to review project readiness and publish expected tender dates. Divisional Secretaries can flag land, access, water and utility constraints early. Chambers can identify firms with the skills and equipment to bid and help others prepare for prequalification.\n\nThe capital schedule includes Rs. 2.8 billion for the Ingiriya\u2013Ratnapura section of the A008. District chambers can help firms assess demand for construction and logistics services as project scopes become clear."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
