    "language": "en",
    "md5": "257171d95263c795d1613d6c9d1bdb47",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1984,
    "chunk_text": "The capital schedule includes Rs. 2.8 billion for the Ingiriya\u2013Ratnapura section of the A008. District chambers can help firms assess demand for construction and logistics services as project scopes become clear.\n\nThe Budget Speech provides Rs. 1.5 billion in 2027 towards modernising 25 technical colleges across 25 districts and Rs. 800 million towards University of Vocational Technology facilities. District employers can identify shortages in skilled trades, hospitality and digital operations and offer supervised placements.\n\nThe Budget proposes Rs. 300 million from tourism authority funds to review and strengthen the Southern Mist Triangle across Galle, Matara and Ratnapura. Accommodation providers, guides, food suppliers and transport operators can develop joint offerings around visitor demand, reliable utilities and conservation requirements.\n\nThe Easter Sunday attacks, COVID-19, the economic crisis and changes in policy direction weakened many firms\u2019 working capital, staffing and equipment capacity. Contractors and suppliers still face debt repayments and uneven receipts. Timely certification and payment can help viable firms finance mobilisation and retain skilled workers.\n\nThe Budget Speech proposes Re-MSME Plus lending at 5% and rural enterprise lending at 4% up to Rs. 5 million. The Citizens Budget also lists working-capital loans for growers of 35 eligible crops, including paddy, at 5% up to Rs. 3 million. Participating lenders and agencies should publish eligibility, security requirements and decision timelines. Partial credit guarantees and lender-led restructuring can help viable firms facing collateral or repayment constraints.\n\nA profitable order can still leave a business short of cash when wages, suppliers and instalments fall due before customers pay. Positive operating cash flow gives SMEs and entrepreneurs room to reinvest and hire. Firms should test collection periods and working-capital needs before committing to new orders."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-18-dailyftlk-2853f001",
    "num": "dailyftlk-2853f001",
    "date_str": "2026-11-18",
    "description": "FCCISL says Budget 2027 opens way for growth from districts and villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/opinion/FCCISL-says-Budget-2027-opens-way-for-growth-from-districts-and-villages/14-800220",
