    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a1a3f89d5afb2a4b5f2aaf6fea3f4e49",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "FCCISL and its chamber and industry association networks stand ready to support implementation by identifying the procedures that add the most time and cost and sharing practical feedback with the responsible agencies.\n\nThe Citizens Budget identifies Rs. 19.53 billion under digitisation of government services, including Rs. 9.48 billion for digital government transformation, Rs. 970 million for digitising divisional secretariats and Rs. 610 million for government-service cybersecurity. Assisted access and published response times can help rural businesses use those services.\n\nFCCISL\u2019s proposals cover GovData SL, public service transformation, national business recovery, B-READY regulatory reform, a Galle district pilot, Sri Lanka\u2013New Zealand cooperation and a public\u2013private consortium model. These priorities offer scope for cooperation on secure data sharing, enterprise recovery, dairy development and transparent project partnerships.\n\nSkills shortages, utility outages, climate hazards, global conflict and cyber incidents can disrupt deliveries. Before bidding, firms should assess whether they have the cash, staff, equipment and materials to meet realistic schedules.\n\nFCCISL calls for rapid and sustained Government intervention to help distressed businesses resume operations. A standing mechanism could receive early notices, convene public clients, lenders and chambers, set decision deadlines and refer unresolved matters. Joint reviews and mediation can prevent disagreements from escalating.\n\nBusinesses should be able to seek early intervention even where binding agreements apply. Any extension, variation or other relief should follow applicable contracts, procurement rules and statutory approvals.\n\nPublic clients can prevent payment and contract disputes by clarifying responsibilities, certifying work promptly and referring unresolved matters through established channels."
  },
