    "chunk_text": "Businesses should be able to seek early intervention even where binding agreements apply. Any extension, variation or other relief should follow applicable contracts, procurement rules and statutory approvals.\n\nPublic clients can prevent payment and contract disputes by clarifying responsibilities, certifying work promptly and referring unresolved matters through established channels.\n\nFCCISL appreciates two years of budget dialogue, including the opportunity for district chamber leaders to present proposals at the Presidential Secretariat. The Federation welcomes the consideration given to its proposals and the inclusion of regional priorities in government programmes.\n\nFCCISL President Dr. Rohitha Silva and the State Affairs Committee, chaired by Ruwan De Silva, reaffirm their readiness to work with Government through district and sectoral chambers, associations and institutions. FCCISL calls for public institutions to make business revival, entrepreneurship development and enterprise growth explicit priorities in their service mandate. Clear requirements, predictable response times and coordinated support at district and divisional levels can help entrepreneurs start and expand businesses, sustain profitability and create jobs."
