    "chunk_size_bytes": 1799,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys backs Sri Lanka Expo 2027 as Gold sponsor, opening a path to global markets for Sri Lankan SMEs\n\nHayleys PLC receives partner recognition for Sri Lanka Expo 2027 at the Partnership Appreciation\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s largest listed conglomerate supports the nation\u2019s flagship trade exhibition as it returns for the first time since 2012\n\nHayleys PLC has joined Sri Lanka Expo 2027 as a Gold Partner. The Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) will host the international trade exhibition from 14 to 17 January 2027 at the BMICH, Colombo, which returns after 15 years.\n\nThe Expo is expected to bring together about 750 Sri Lankan exporters and over 1,500 international buyers, investors and trade delegates. It covers sectors ranging from apparel, rubber and engineering to tea, spices, coconut products, ICT and logistics.\n\nIn September 2026, the country\u2019s merchandise exports reached $ 1.38 billion, the highest monthly value on record. Total exports for the first nine months of the year rose 5% to $ 13.6 billion.\n\nHayleys is Sri Lanka\u2019s number one ranked listed company (LMD 100 \u2013 2025/26) and is one of the country\u2019s largest export earners. The Group accounts for around 5% of the country\u2019s export income, close to $ 800 million in foreign exchange. It operates in more than 20 countries and its products reach over 80 markets.\n\nIts export strength is built on value addition across the Group. Hayleys exports gloves, activated carbon, coconut fibre-based eco solutions products, textiles, aluminium extrusions, agricultural products and Ceylon tea. Its transportation and logistics businesses help keep the country\u2019s trade moving as a facilitator for country\u2019s exports. Each of these businesses competes on technology, research and quality in demanding international markets."
  },
