    "chunk_text": "Its export strength is built on value addition across the Group. Hayleys exports gloves, activated carbon, coconut fibre-based eco solutions products, textiles, aluminium extrusions, agricultural products and Ceylon tea. Its transportation and logistics businesses help keep the country\u2019s trade moving as a facilitator for country\u2019s exports. Each of these businesses competes on technology, research and quality in demanding international markets.\n\nThe Group\u2019s purpose is \u201cto inspire an inclusive world and a thriving planet\u201d, and that purpose shapes how it builds export value. Hayleys businesses bring smallholder farmers, out-growers and rural communities directly into global value chains, so they share in the value created. This work is driven by Hayleys Lifecode, the Group\u2019s ESG and sustainability framework. Hayleys companies have together been named Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen six times by the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce.\n\nThrough its sponsorship, Hayleys aims to help Sri Lanka\u2019s small and medium enterprises compete on the international stage the Expo provides.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka\u2019s SMEs are the next link in that chain. As Gold Sponsor of Expo 2027, we want to help local entrepreneurs do what Hayleys has done for generations: adopt sustainable practices, showcase their innovative products, and grow their portfolio to reach global markets. When they grow, Sri Lanka\u2019s export base grows with them,\u201d said Hayleys PLC Group Executive Director Sarath Ganegoda."
