    "md5": "aaf58755e327f6f1fe7c5bea84ea482a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1814,
    "chunk_text": "WSO2 rebrands as Choreo Labs\n\nWSO2, the open source company whose software processes an estimated 60 trillion transactions a year and manages 2.5 billion identities, has announced it has a new name, Choreo Labs.\n\nThe Company said enterprises are moving AI agents out of pilots and into production, and need to govern every one of those agents across the APIs, systems, and identities it touches, effectively choreographing each agent\u2019s journey. As that happens, the company\u2019s platform has moved beyond connecting enterprise systems to sitting at the centre in empowering enterprises to meet this demand for AI governance. The new name reflects that evolving role.\n\nFounded in 2005, WSO2 took its name in the web services era. Today, its API management, integration, and identity products run in production for more than 950 customers in 90-plus countries, including banks, governments, hospitals, and telcos. The world\u2019s leading analyst firms have recognised the company for its comprehensive product offerings and success in meeting enterprise customers\u2019 demands. Over those two decades, enterprise software has moved from web services to cloud, APIs, and now AI agents that act on their own, and the company has moved with it.\n\nThrough each of those shifts, the company\u2019s mission has stayed the same: connecting systems and controlling what moves between them. AI agents raise the stakes.\n\nChoreo Labs CEO Harry Ault said: \u201cFor over 2 decades, our mission has been to make sure enterprise systems talk to each other safely at scale. AI agents don\u2019t change that mission. In fact, they make it far more urgent. Enterprises won\u2019t put agents into production until they can see, govern, and trust every action those agents take. That is the problem we were built to solve, and our new name says so.\u201d"
  },
