    "chunk_size_bytes": 1221,
    "chunk_text": "Choreo Labs CEO Harry Ault said: \u201cFor over 2 decades, our mission has been to make sure enterprise systems talk to each other safely at scale. AI agents don\u2019t change that mission. In fact, they make it far more urgent. Enterprises won\u2019t put agents into production until they can see, govern, and trust every action those agents take. That is the problem we were built to solve, and our new name says so.\u201d\n\n\u201cChoreo\u201d comes from choreography. Inside every enterprise, agents, APIs, integrations, identities, and services each have their own part to play, and none of them ever stops moving. Choreo Labs gives organisations both the freedom for each part to move and the control to keep them in step. Choreo, the company\u2019s platform, brings APIs, integration, identity, agents, and the internal developer platform that runs them together in one place.\n\n\u201cLabs\u201d reflects the company\u2019s research and engineering culture. It has long innovated in open source and open standards, from its integration programming language to its latest agent management product. Technical staff make up more than 75% of its 850-plus employees, and the same engineers who design the platform work alongside customers to deploy it."
