    "md5": "2db2f433e7d599aabf4262b1beb1ba05",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1990,
    "chunk_text": "GEW Sri Lanka 2026 aims to expand opportunities for entrepreneurs nationwide\n\nDigital Economy Deputy Minister Eng. Eranga Weeraratne (second from left) speaks at the panel. Others from left: MayaHive Co-Founder LMS, AI and SaaS Consultant Sanjaya Elvitigala (Moderator), NGage Strategic Alliance Managing Director Sheron Jayasundara, Global Entrepreneurship Network National Ambassador for Sri Lanka and\u00a0 Lanka Fishing Flies Managing DirectorSuresh de Mel and Kapruka Holdings Founder and Chairman Dulith Herath\n\n2,500 events, 100,000 participants and 5,000 entrepreneurs targeted under GEW Sri Lanka 2026\n\nSri Lanka ranked fourth among more than 200 countries for GEW engagement\n\nPanelists spotlight AI, branding, global markets and networking for business growth\n\nGlobal Entrepreneurship Week (GEW) Sri Lanka 2026 was launched with a renewed focus on strengthening the country's entrepreneurial ecosystem, bringing together aspiring entrepreneurs, startups, small and medium enterprises (SMEs), business leaders and innovators to explore new pathways for growth and innovation.\n\nOrganised by the Global Entrepreneurship Network (GEN Global) in collaboration with the Ministry of Digital Economy, the Ministry of Industries and Entrepreneurship Development and the Ministry of Science and Technology, the initiative aims to connect entrepreneurs, businesses and ecosystem stakeholders across all 25 districts. The launch took place during Science Week, with the national campaign set to commence symbolically during Global Entrepreneurship Week from 16 to 22 November before continuing throughout the year through workshops, networking sessions, business exhibitions and entrepreneurship-focused events.\n\nA key feature of the initiative will be the Entrepreneurship Marathon, which will bring together government institutions, private-sector organisations, academia, ecosystem enablers and bilateral and multilateral organisations to help entrepreneurs develop and scale their businesses."
  },
