    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6559837e6af87f115eaa8ca6876698e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "A key feature of the initiative will be the Entrepreneurship Marathon, which will bring together government institutions, private-sector organisations, academia, ecosystem enablers and bilateral and multilateral organisations to help entrepreneurs develop and scale their businesses.\n\n\u201cEntrepreneurship is vital to Sri Lanka's economic development, and we need entrepreneurs who can transform innovative ideas into products and services, access global markets and generate foreign exchange,\u201d he said.\n\nWeeraratne noted that Sri Lanka had secured fourth place globally for its implementation of Global Entrepreneurship Week initiatives and said the program provides opportunities for students, innovators and entrepreneurs to access knowledge, guidance and local and international business networks.\n\nGEW Sri Lanka 2026 Program Director Charith Kandamulla said organisers hope to build on the momentum generated over the past year and expand support for entrepreneurs nationwide. \u201cIn 2025, we conducted 1,864 events nationwide, and GEN Global ranked Sri Lanka fourth among more than 200 countries for its active engagement in entrepreneurship. This year, we aim to build on these achievements by delivering 2,500 events, engaging 100,000 participants and supporting 5,000 entrepreneurs,\u201d he said.\n\nHe added that the Entrepreneurship Marathon would serve as a platform for stronger collaboration across the entrepreneurial ecosystem, helping local businesses access the support, networks and opportunities required to grow.\n\nIndustry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe stressed the need for stronger policy support to nurture entrepreneurship and innovation. \u201cEntrepreneurship is a key requirement. We must recognise it, categorise it, and develop the policy framework necessary to build an ecosystem that enables it to move forward,\u201d he said."
  },
