    "chunk_text": "He noted that different markets often require different pricing strategies, product variations and approaches to customer engagement. Entrepreneurs must therefore invest time in understanding customer expectations and market conditions before pursuing growth overseas.\n\nHe added that creativity, branding and product differentiation are increasingly important in helping businesses command stronger prices and compete effectively in crowded global markets.\n\nHerath said artificial intelligence is also transforming how consumers discover businesses and products online.\n\nAs AI-powered search and recommendation tools become more widely used, entrepreneurs need to think about how their businesses are represented within these emerging digital ecosystems.\n\n\u201cEntrepreneurs should think about how their businesses can be represented in these new channels.\u201d\n\nHe suggested that businesses that successfully adapt to new discovery mechanisms could benefit from increased visibility and access to new customers.\n\nHow can Sri Lanka prepare its workforce for an AI-driven future?\n\nLooking ahead, Weeraratne said Sri Lanka must focus on both adopting new technologies and preparing people for the changes they will bring.\n\nHe noted that future workforce requirements will extend beyond technical expertise and include entrepreneurship, management and organisational change capabilities.\n\n\u201cWe need people who can develop and implement solutions within organisations.\u201d\n\nAccording to Weeraratne, practical learning opportunities and industry exposure will be essential in helping individuals develop the skills required in an increasingly technology-driven economy.\n\nAddressing competition, Jayasundara said startups should avoid trying to become smaller versions of already established brands.\n\nInstead, entrepreneurs should identify underserved customer needs and market gaps where they can create meaningful differentiation and deliver greater value. \u201cLearn from the leading brands, but find your own niche.\u201d"
