    "chunk_text": "Nuwara Eliya records lowest temperature; Mullaitivu highest\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Nuwara Eliya recorded the lowest minimum temperature in the country at 12.4 degrees Celsius, while Mullaitivu recorded the highest minimum temperature at 26.6\u00b0C yesterday (18), according to the Department of Meteorology.\n\nBandarawela recorded the second-lowest temperature at 16.8\u00b0C, followed by Badulla at 19.8\u00b0C and Maha Illuppallama at 20.7\u00b0C.\n\nAmong other areas, Katugastota recorded 22.1\u00b0C, Polonnaruwa 22.3\u00b0C, Puttalam and Vavuniya 22.4\u00b0C each, Anuradhapura and Monaragala 22.6\u00b0C each, and Jaffna 22.8\u00b0C.\n\nTrincomalee recorded 23\u00b0C, Kurunegala 23.4\u00b0C, Batticaloa 24\u00b0C, Katunayake 24.2\u00b0C, Ratnapura 24.5\u00b0C, while Colombo and Ratmalana recorded 25.4\u00b0C each.\n\nMeanwhile, Hambantota recorded 25.5\u00b0C, Galle 25.8\u00b0C, Mannar 25.9\u00b0C and Pottuvil 25.1\u00b0C.\n\nThe figures were released in the Department of Meteorology's minimum temperature report for November 18, 2026."
