    "chunk_text": "Pakistan declared their first innings after posting a strong total of 434/9, with five batters reaching half-centuries. In reply, Sri Lanka edged ahead with a slender 12-run lead, thanks to centuries from Dhananjaya de Silva and captain Kusal Mendis. The visitors were on course for a massive lead before debutant Saqib Khan\u2019s seven-for derailed their innings.\n\nThe two teams are currently contesting the second and final Test, where the hosts made a strong start to the match by bowling out Sri Lanka for 98 in the first innings."
