    "md5": "45f2fe3b768fe8ee6c6cabbaf4bf2b9e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1936,
    "chunk_text": "Court orders SSP to explain failure to arrest Rajanganaya Saddharathana over Anuradhapura clash\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Anuradhapura Chief Magistrate Siyapath Sasindu Wickramaratne has ordered the Anuradhapura Senior Superintendent of Police (SSP) to personally appear before Court on November 26 and explain why Rajanganaya Saddharathana and other suspects allegedly involved in instigating a clash near the Ruwanweliseya had not been arrested and produced before Court.\n\nThe order was issued yesterday (17) after lawyers appearing for four Buddhist monks, two male civilians and a woman, who are currently in remand custody over the incident, accused the police of failing to take action against those they claimed had provoked the confrontation.\n\nSenior lawyers Indika Imbulpitiya and Nuwan Bellanthudawa, appearing for the suspects, told Court that more than 25 people, including Rajanganaya Saddharathana, had allegedly instigated the clash at the Satyagraha site in the Dansal Zone near the Ruwanweliseya.\n\nThey alleged that while their clients had been arrested and remanded, those who had allegedly provoked the incident were being allowed to remain at large without being arrested.\n\nThe lawyers also questioned the conduct of the police officers deployed at the scene, particularly the Anuradhapura Headquarters Chief Inspector, claiming that the confrontation could have been prevented if the police had acted appropriately.\n\nReferring to video footage of the incident, they said there were grounds to question whether police officers had facilitated the groups allegedly responsible for triggering the violence.\n\nThe lawyers sought bail for Kahathagasdigiliya Vijitha, Balangoda Anuruddha, Pilimathalawa Revatha and Deniyaya Soratha Theras, along with two male civilians and a woman, who were remanded until November 26 over allegations of assault and obstructing police officers in the discharge of their duties."
  },
