    "chunk_text": "The lawyers sought bail for Kahathagasdigiliya Vijitha, Balangoda Anuruddha, Pilimathalawa Revatha and Deniyaya Soratha Theras, along with two male civilians and a woman, who were remanded until November 26 over allegations of assault and obstructing police officers in the discharge of their duties.\n\nHowever, the Chief Magistrate rejected the bail application and directed SSP Prasanna Brahmanage to appear personally before open Court on November 26 to explain why Rajanganaya Saddharathana and the other alleged suspects had not been arrested and produced before Court.\n\nBalangoda Kassapa Thera, the first suspect in the case, was not included in the latest bail application. Explaining the omission, lawyer Indika Imbulpitiya told the media that no bail application had been made on his behalf as he was also facing an allegation of contempt of Court.\n\nBalangoda Kassapa Thera and the other suspects, including four monks, two male civilians and a woman, were remanded until November 26 by the Anuradhapura Chief Magistrate on November 11."
