    "chunk_text": "Cancer patients left waiting as Rs. 1 billion radiation units remain idle\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Cancer patients in Badulla and Hambantota are being left waiting for life-saving radiation treatment as newly installed Linear Accelerator machines remain unused due to administrative and technical delays, a medical professional has alleged.\n\nConsultant Physician Dr. Chamal Sanjeewa, President of the Medical Professionals' Alliance for Medical and Civil Rights, said the machines had been installed at the Badulla Provincial General Hospital and Hambantota General Hospital but radiation treatment services had still not commenced.\n\nHe said installation at Badulla was completed in April, while work at Hambantota was finalised in the first week of October. Despite this, patients in both districts are yet to benefit from the facilities.\n\nAccording to Dr. Sanjeewa, the delay has been attributed to the lack of dosimetry equipment required to operate the machines. However, he questioned why the equipment could not be temporarily obtained from the Apeksha Hospital in Maharagama to start treating patients without further delay.\n\nHe said Deputy Health Minister Hansaka Wijayamuni had also instructed officials during an inspection visit to Badulla General Hospital to obtain the necessary dosimetry equipment from Apeksha Hospital.\n\nDr. Sanjeewa alleged that the failure to create the necessary conditions to commence treatment had raised serious concerns, particularly when cancer patients could not afford further delays.\n\nThe five Linear Accelerator machines were procured for the Badulla Provincial General Hospital, Ratnapura Teaching Hospital, Hambantota General Hospital, Kurunegala Teaching Hospital and Anuradhapura Teaching Hospital.\n\nEach machine costs more than Rs. 600 million, while the total investment in a complete radiation therapy unit at each hospital exceeds Rs. 1 billion.\n\nOf the five machines, three have so far been delivered to Badulla, Ratnapura and Hambantota."
  },
