    "chunk_size_bytes": 1588,
    "chunk_text": "Lessons, courage set by my father give me strength to face challenges - Namal\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Namal Rajapaksa has sent an emotional birthday message to his father, former President Mahinda Rajapaksa, saying that his love and respect for him transcend the walls of his prison cell.\n\nIn a message shared on the occasion of his father's birthday, Namal said he was unable to be by his father's side to wish him personally as he was going through a difficult period separated from his family and loved ones.\n\nHe said the lessons, courage and example set by his father had given him strength to face challenges in life.\n\nRecalling his father's leadership during one of the darkest periods in the country's history, Namal said Mahinda Rajapaksa had brought peace to countless families by standing firm without fear.\n\nHe said he had come to understand more deeply the patience, courage and determination his father had demonstrated while shouldering enormous responsibilities.\n\nNamal also said his own experience of facing difficulties while fighting for the truth had helped him better understand the strength required of a father.\n\nAlthough he could not be with his father on his birthday, Namal said his children would visit their grandfather and embrace him on his behalf.\n\nDescribing Mahinda Rajapaksa as a man firmly rooted in Giruwapattuwa who had endured hardships, political pressure and insults, Namal wished him good health, mental strength and happiness.\n\n\"The bond between a father and a son is something that even distance cannot break,\" he said in his message."
