    "md5": "9c62f8482201d9b6c2c57dfe97a9058b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1923,
    "chunk_text": "Nvidia says it won\u2019t reinstate Huang as firm reports bumper results\n\nBBC - Nvidia's quarterly sales doubled to top $100bn for the first time as the company insisted it has no plans to reinstate ousted co-founder Jensen Huang.\n\nIn the company's first results since Huang's dramatic exit, interim chief executive Colette Kress said it is \"business as usual\" and told investors: \"We've got this.\"\n\nThe company's quarterly sales doubled from a year earlier, reaching $115.8bn (\u00a386.9bn), with shares in the company jumping by 4.8% in after-hours trading.\n\nEarlier on Tuesday, Huang said he would be \"honoured\" to return and lead Nvidia, having quit following alleged extramarital affairs, including one with a suspected spy for China.\n\n\"The board does not intend to reinstate him,\" Nvidia chair Harvey Jones said during a call on Tuesday with financial analysts.\n\nThe company's profits also doubled from a year ago. For the quarter, which covered the three months to 25 October, profit hit $65bn. Its revenue from data centres, a significant part of Nvidia's business, also doubled to $107bn in the same period.\n\nGoing forward, the company said its rapid growth is poised to continue, and revenue will rise by another 13% in the next quarter.\n\nGiven the uncertainty surrounding the company after Huang's exit, financial analysts had been unsure that Nvidia would provide any forward-looking guidance.\n\nDaniela Hathorn, a senior analyst for trading platform Capital.com, said Nvidia's results \"offer a strong answer to concerns that demand for AI infrastructure is cooling\" and temper immediate worries that Huang was irreplaceable as a leader.\n\n\"The harder question is whether Nvidia can preserve the strategic advantage Huang helped build,\" Hathorn added. \"His exit is unlikely to change orders already committed, but could matter more when Nvidia makes its next round of decisions on products, partnerships and investment.\""
