    "chunk_text": "However, on Sept 14, 2026, a federal judge in Massachusetts issued a nationwide preliminary injunction temporarily blocking that order.\n\nBy going ahead with these restrictions, the US is said to be foregoing a lot of income - $43 billion annually.\n\nYounger students feel more homesick than older ones. Some researchers suggest that universities should organise orientation sessions for students from the Global South, and social workers should visit such students to advice them on behaviour expectations in the host society.\n\nThe Western education system is based on self-study and free expression of ideas even in opposition to handed-down knowledge. But this is alien to the majority of South Asian students who are used to the top-down approach.\n\nSouth Asian students from non-elite institutions back home, tend to be accused of plagiarism. They become more professional over time, but initial rejections by the system can be very hurtful. Therefore, academic expectations should be made clear to them at the very outset, and they should be encouraged to think on their own, express themselves in their own words, and cite sources if information and analyses are borrowed.\n\nIt is also important for Western educational institutions to first understand the cultural context of South Asian students, instead of rushing to punish them if they did not meet local standards."
