  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-18-dailymirrorlk-686aa361",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-686aa361",
    "date_str": "2026-11-18",
    "description": "Capital Trust Holdings joins European Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Capital-Trust-Holdings-joins-European-Chamber-of-Commerce-of-Sri-Lanka/215-355173",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794985697.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-18-dailymirrorlk-686aa361-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e3c9d054d9541da20878d8a8f009f9f5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1639,
    "chunk_text": "Capital Trust Holdings joins European Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka\n\nFrom left: European Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka Vice President Mario Stubbs, President Ahamed ur Rahman, Capital Trust Properties Chairperson and CEO Minoli Wickramasinghe and Head of Business Development Aruni De Mel Ahkil\n\nStrengthens investment links between Sri Lanka and Europe across financial and real estate sectors\n\nCapital Trust Holdings, through its subsidiary Capital Trust Properties (Pvt.) Ltd, has joined the European Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka (ECCSL), strengthening its engagement with European businesses and investors while expanding opportunities across Sri Lanka\u2019s financial and real estate sectors.\n\nThe membership provides a platform for the European investors to explore opportunities in Sri Lanka\u2019s capital and equity markets, alongside residential and commercial real estate.\n\nIt also creates scope for greater collaboration between local businesses and international investors, supported by professional advisory services and access to market expertise.\n\nAs the first real estate transaction and wealth management advisory company to join the chamber, Capital Trust Holdings aims to facilitate cross-border investment, strengthen commercial relationships and encourage the exchange of international best practices.\n\nThe move comes as Sri Lanka seeks to attract greater international investment and deepen its commercial ties with overseas markets. Access to reliable market intelligence, transparent transaction processes and professional advice remain important for the investors assessing opportunities in emerging markets."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
