    "md5": "35168581811ee273d09f3e23b8af5f18",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1590,
    "chunk_text": "SLIIT wins Best/Model Internal Quality Assurance Award\n\nSLIIT brings home Best/Model Internal Quality Assurance Award 2026 from the Asia Pacific Quality Network (APQN).\n\nThe award was presented at APQN Quality Awards 2026, held at Symbiosis International University in Pune, India.\n\nSLIIT\u2019s work in this area is led by Dean Academic Development and Quality Assurance Prof. Colin N. Peiris.\n\n\u201cQuality is not a one-off exercise. It is something we check and improve every day,\u201d Prof. Peiris said.\n\n\u201cThis award belongs to everyone at SLIIT who upholds these standards and is committed to strive towards excellence.\u201d\n\nInternal quality assurance refers to the processes through which a university reviews its own courses and teaching, gathers feedback and acts on its findings. The APQN award is given to member institutions that have made such practices a regular part of their operations and is decided by the network.\n\nThe recognition spotlights the culture of continuous improvement at SLIIT and contributes to SLIIT\u2019s recognition as Sri Lanka\u2019s leading non-state university in the Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026. It is also ranked first among non-state universities in computer science and engineering in the 2026 subject rankings.\n\nFor SLIIT\u2019s students, quality is judged where learning happens - in the lecture hall, laboratory and examination room.\n\n\u201cStandards only mean something if students and staff feel them in the classroom,\u201d Prof. Peiris said.\n\n\u201cThat is what we aim to uphold every day and this award encourages us to keep doing so.\u201d"
  },
  {
