    "md5": "6ec3a3596813d9ea6b6255fdfd5f7e28",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "Former British High Commissioner joins George Steuart board\n\nGeorge Steuart & Company Ltd has announced the appointment of former British High Commissioner to Sri Lanka and the Maldives James Dauris as an Independent Non-Executive Director of its board, with effect from January 1, 2027.\n\nDauris brings over three decades of experience spanning international diplomacy, commercial relations and strategic advisory. His distinguished career includes serving as British High Commissioner to Sri Lanka and the Maldives from 2015 to 2019, British Ambassador to Peru and Panama and holding senior leadership positions within the UK\u2019s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office.\n\nA graduate in Law from the University of Cambridge, he began his professional career as a solicitor in London, specialising in corporate and commercial law, before entering diplomatic service.\n\nThe appointment reinforces George Steuart & Company\u2019s British heritage, reflected in its legacy of having British board directors for over 150 years, until 1988. Further, it is a timely and strategic appointment that aligns well with the group\u2019s renewed vision and focus on expanding its global footprint.\n\nDauris becomes the fourth Independent Non-Executive Director on the board and his appointment reaffirms the company\u2019s commitment to strong corporate governance. The increased representation of independent directors reflects George Steuart\u2019s commitment to independent oversight, broader perspectives in board deliberations and sound decision-making in the interests of all its shareholders.\n\nGeorge Steuart & Company Group Chairman Sarva Ameresekere stated, \u201cWe are honoured to welcome James to the board. We believe his vast international experience and understanding of Sri Lanka will be valuable as we strive to explore opportunities beyond our shores. His addition to the board adds further depth and diversity of expertise to support the group\u2019s growth aspirations.\u201d"
  },
