    "md5": "8423a2ae995b0c4ecb6f9d57741f3452",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1676,
    "chunk_text": "Parents urged to nurture child development during first five years\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The first five years of a child's life are crucial for brain development, language acquisition, emotional control, social interaction and learning abilities, highlighting the importance of parental involvement in early childhood development.\n\nThe home environment plays a significant role in shaping a child's physical, emotional, intellectual and social development, with parents serving as the child's first teachers.\n\nEarly Childhood Development should therefore not be considered a process confined to preschool education, as it must begin at home through love, affection, protection, proper nutrition, meaningful communication and activities that stimulate learning.\n\nAgainst this backdrop, the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs has launched awareness videos on Home-Based Early Childhood Care and Development (HB-ECCD) under the \u2018Senehe Thatakaya\u2019 programme.\n\nThe videos were launched recently at the Ministry under the patronage of Deputy Minister Dr. Namal Sudarshana.\n\nImplemented by the National Secretariat for Early Childhood Development, the programme aims to empower parents and caregivers with the knowledge and skills needed to create a nurturing environment for children at home.\n\nIt also seeks to strengthen family nutrition and food security and ensure the early identification of vulnerable children and children with special needs so that they can be referred to appropriate services.\n\nThe programme is aligned with the National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development and the National Multi-Sectoral Strategic Action Plan for 2025\u20132029."
  },
