    "md5": "1fbcc48f62d16d69cbf76f133ea20ff6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1976,
    "chunk_text": "AICPA & CIMA Sri Lanka to decode Budget 2027\n\nUpcoming forum to bring together Treasury Secretary, business leaders and leading economists to explore implications of Sri Lanka\u2019s Budget 2027\n\nAICPA & CIMA Sri Lanka will host its highly anticipated Post Budget Forum 2026 on November 19, 2026, at 6:00 p.m., at the CIMA Auditorium, bringing together the policymakers, business leaders, economists, tax experts, investors and finance professionals to examine the implications of Budget 2027 and its impact on Sri Lanka\u2019s economic future.\n\nHeld under the theme \u2018Sri Lanka 2027 and Beyond: Budget Insights and Future Prospects\u2019, the forum will provide a platform for insightful discussion and expert analysis of the policy measures shaping the country\u2019s next phase of economic growth and development.\n\nThe keynote address will be delivered by Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriapperuma, FCMA (UK), CGMA, who will share valuable insights into the government\u2019s economic priorities, fiscal strategy and policy direction for 2027 and beyond.\n\nHis perspectives will provide the attendees with a deeper understanding of the measures proposed in the budget and the broader vision for sustaining economic growth, strengthening fiscal resilience and driving long-term national development.\n\nAlso addressing the forum will be Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, FCMA (UK), CGMA, who will speak on the topic \u2018From Stability to Strength: Making Industry and Enterprise the Engine of Sri Lanka\u2019s 2027 Growth\u2019.\n\nDrawing on both the global economic shifts and domestic industrial realities, his address will examine how the local enterprises can enhance competitiveness, navigate the evolving international supply chains and leverage the Budget 2027 policies to scale innovation and export-led growth.\n\nThe forum will also feature a distinguished line-up of industry experts who will analyse the budget from multiple perspectives."
  },
