    "chunk_text": "Drawing on both the global economic shifts and domestic industrial realities, his address will examine how the local enterprises can enhance competitiveness, navigate the evolving international supply chains and leverage the Budget 2027 policies to scale innovation and export-led growth.\n\nThe forum will also feature a distinguished line-up of industry experts who will analyse the budget from multiple perspectives.\n\nKPMG Sri Lanka Principal Tax and Regulatory Suresh R.I. Perera, FCMA (UK), CGMA, will provide a comprehensive analysis of the budget\u2019s tax proposals and their implications to the business sector.\n\nThe speakers will be joined by an eminent panel comprising Brandix Group Managing Director Hasitha Premaratne, FCMA (UK), CGMA, Jetwing Travels Managing Director Shiromal Cooray, FCMA (UK), CGMA, Finance and Planning Ministry Tax Policy Advisor Thanuja Perera and First Capital Holdings PLC Managing Director and CEO and Janashakthi Group Deputy CEO Dilshan Wirasekara.\n\nModerated by BDO Sri Lanka Managing Partner Ashane Jayasekara, FCMA (UK), CGMA, the discussion will bring diverse perspectives on the economic, fiscal, tax and business implications of Budget 2027, exploring how the organisations can navigate the opportunities and challenges ahead.\n\nAICPA & CIMA\u2019s annual Budget Forums are among the most anticipated post-budget knowledge platforms attracting senior finance professionals, CEOs, business leaders, policymakers, entrepreneurs, academics and students.\n\nRenowned for the comprehensive analysis, practical insights and high-calibre speaker panels, these forums provide the participants a valuable opportunity to understand the economic, regulatory, tax and business implications of the budget directly from the policymakers and industry experts.\n\nThe forum is open to the CIMA members, students, professionals and public. The registration fee is Rs.3,500 for students and members and Rs.4,000 for non-members."
