    "md5": "1aa914c0c95e9ca36b4153ba562a4745",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1883,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka Ashok Leyland reports strong half-year performance\n\nLanka Ashok Leyland PLC (LAL) has recorded an impressive financial performance for the six months ended 30th September 2026, with revenue increasing by 78 percent to Rs. 13.76 billion, compared to Rs. 7.75 billion during the corresponding period last year.\n\nThe Company\u2019s profit before tax increased by 66 percent to Rs. 2.80 billion, while profit after tax grew by 67 percent to Rs. 1.95 billion, compared to Rs. 1.17 billion in the previous year. Revenue from new vehicle sales increased by 86 percent to Rs. 12.61 billion, reflecting strong demand for Lanka Ashok Leyland vehicles.\n\nCommenting on the Company\u2019s performance, Umesh Gautam, Chief Executive Officer of Lanka Ashok Leyland PLC, stated that one of the most significant achievements during the period was the Company\u2019s ability to generate its entire bus and truck sales from the private sector, without any Government vehicle purchases.This clearly demonstrates our ability to sustain growth independently of Government procurement.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s passenger transport sector is gradually moving towards modernization, with increasing demand for luxury, comfortable and air-conditioned buses. Private passenger transport operators are increasingly investing in higher-value buses to meet changing passenger expectations.\n\nRecognizing this market transformation, Lanka Ashok Leyland has aggressively marketed its Luxura AC luxury bus range, which has contributed positively to the Company\u2019s revenue growth and profitability.\n\nGautam further stated, \u201cThe passenger transport industry is undergoing a significant transformation, with operators increasingly recognizing the commercial potential of modern luxury buses. Our strategic focus on promoting Luxura AC buses has enabled us to capitalize on this growing demand while improving our profitability.\u201d"
  },
