    "md5": "bdc3c7d0273b512bf902849bdc42681d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1426,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank and Justice Ministry partner to digitize judicial payment system\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank and the Ministry of Justice and National Integration have signed an agreement to facilitate the implementation of an Internet Payment Gateway (IPG) for accepting court-related payments electronically, marking another significant milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s judicial digital transformation journey.\n\nThe agreement was exchanged between Ayesha Jinasena, PC, Secretary to the Ministry of Justice and National Integration, and Chandana Guniyangoda, Chairman of People\u2019s Bank, recently at the Ministry of Justice premises in Colombo 10. I. K. Indika, Deputy General Manager \u2013 Payments & Cards, People\u2019s Bank, along with Card Centre officials and representatives of the Ministry of Justice, also participated in the event.\n\nThis partnership further strengthens the longstanding collaboration between the two institutions in introducing convenient, secure and efficient digital payment facilities across the country\u2019s judicial system.\n\nThe introduction of the Internet Payment Gateway will further expand these facilities by enabling court users to make applicable payments through online payment channels, reducing the need for physical visits to court payment counters or bank branches. This is expected to provide greater convenience to litigants, Attorneys-at-Law and other members of the public accessing judicial services."
  },
