    "language": "en",
    "md5": "69495bc37fd344f7bb98e72051be06cd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1450,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka to host Sustainability Summit 2026 next month\n\nSri Lanka Brand Forum has announced that it will host the Sri Lanka Sustainability Summit 2026 on 7 December at Cinnamon Grand, Colombo.\n\nOrganised under the Forum\u2019s Sustainable Brand Initiative, the summit will convene under the theme \u201cReimagining Sri Lanka\u2019s Responsible Future.\u201d\n\nThe forum will convene business leaders, sustainability practitioners, policymakers, investors and academics around a pivotal strategic shift: why Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) has evolved from a voluntary compliance exercise into an indispensable prerequisite for companies seeking to stay competitive, investable and trusted.\n\nResponsible Business Conduct reflects the fundamental expectation that businesses identify, prevent and address adverse impacts across their operations and value chains on people, planet and society. It covers fair labour standards, human rights, environmental stewardship, robust governance and transparent stakeholder engagement, these expectations are anchored in global benchmarks such as OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the UN Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights. Increasingly, global buyers, institutional financiers and regulators use these frameworks\u00a0 as a baseline criteria for market engagement.\n\nThe summit will feature four distinguished international keynotes, delivering operational, academic, and board-level perspectives."
  },
