    "chunk_size_bytes": 1504,
    "chunk_text": "Responsible Business Conduct reflects the fundamental expectation that businesses identify, prevent and address adverse impacts across their operations and value chains on people, planet and society. It covers fair labour standards, human rights, environmental stewardship, robust governance and transparent stakeholder engagement, these expectations are anchored in global benchmarks such as OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the UN Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights. Increasingly, global buyers, institutional financiers and regulators use these frameworks\u00a0 as a baseline criteria for market engagement.\n\nThe summit will feature four distinguished international keynotes, delivering operational, academic, and board-level perspectives.\n\nCommenting on the initiative,\u00a0 Rohan Somawansa, Co-Founder of Sri Lanka Brand Forum said, \u201cResponsible Business Conduct is no longer optional for Sri Lankan companies. It is the licence to operate in global markets and the foundation of brands that last. With the Sri Lanka Sustainability Summit, we want to move the conversation from intent to action, and help our business community lead the region in building a responsible future.\u201d\n\nThe Sri Lanka Sustainability Summit 2026 is supported by Strategic Partners the Asia Marketing Federation (AMF), and the World Marketing Council (WMC), Marketing Education Partner: the Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (SLIM), Knowledge Partner: CIM Sri Lanka, Outdoor Partner: Emerging Media."
