    "chunk_size_bytes": 981,
    "chunk_text": "Yields dip marginally on the back of modest buying\n\nModest buying dominated overall investor sentiment yesterday, prompting a marginal downward adjustment of yields while trading volumes and investor participation appeared moderate.\n\nAmong the traded maturities, 15.09.2029 and 15.10.2029 both traded at 10.70%. Within the 2030 segment, 15.05.2030, 01.08.2030 and 15.10.2030 changed hands between11.00% to 10.90%.\n\nFurther along the curve, 15.12.2032 was seen trading from 11.45% to 11.40%. At the belly of the yield curve, 15.01.2033 traded within 11.55% to 11.50% while 01.06.2033 and 01.11.2033 traded from 11.65% to 11.60%. Moving ahead, both 15.06.2034 and 15.10.2034 changed hands from 11.85% to 11.75%. Finally, 15.08.2036 was seen trading at 12.00%.\n\nOn the external front, the LKR depreciated against the USD, standing at LKR 332.74/USD, compared to LKR 332.62/USD seen previously.\n\nCBSL is yet to release the data pertaining to overnight liquidity for 17th November 2026."
  },
