    "chunk_text": "DFCC completed its acquisition of Standard Chartered\u2019s Sri Lankan wealth and retail banking business on August 1 for Rs. 4.42 billion in cash, inclusive of taxes. The transaction brought about 50,000 customer accounts and 260 employees into DFCC, Chief Executive Thimal Perera said. The bank cited staff joining through the acquisition and higher card-related costs among the factors behind its increase in expenses over the nine months.\n\nAt bank level, loans grew 18 percent from end-December to Rs. 610 billion and customer deposits rose 23 percent to Rs. 694 billion. The net Stage 3 impaired loan ratio eased to 3.44 percent from 4.55 percent at year-end. The group\u2019s total capital adequacy ratio fell to 14.11 percent from 15.99 percent, above the regulatory minimum of 12.5 percent."
