    "md5": "a03cbaa9de304e1eaec0850a7988e28c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1673,
    "chunk_text": "Above-band inflation prompts call for Treasury-CBSL talks\n\nWants the CBA Coordination Council to meet fortnightly instead of quarterly\n\nSays CBSL\u2019s \u201cexternal shocks\u201d explanations amount to a policy of inactivity\n\nThe Treasury and the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) should jointly fight inflation through a fortnightly coordination mechanism, as monetary policy alone cannot rein in prices above the 7 percent ceiling without pushing the economy into contraction, former CBSL Deputy Governor Dr. W.A. Wijewardena urged.\n\nDelivering the keynote address on Monday at the Budget Highlights 2027 forum organised by the Institute of Certified Management Accountants of Sri Lanka (CMA Sri Lanka), Dr. Wijewardena proposed that the Coordination Council established under the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act of 2023 be given revised terms of reference and convened every two weeks. He elaborated thus\u00a0 would allow Treasury and CBSL officials to work out relief measures together whenever inflation breaches the upper limit of the target band.\n\nThe Council is chaired by the CBSL Governor and includes the Secretary to the Treasury as a member. It was set up as a platform for policy dialogue after the new Act removed the Treasury Secretary from the CBSL\u2019s decision-making bodies, and it is required to meet once a quarter.\n\n\u201cWe have provided independence to the Central Bank, which is the correct thing, but of course we must now set up a mechanism where the Treasury officials and the Central Bank officials will meet at least once in two weeks and discuss how they should jointly provide relief to the people when inflation is above 7 percent,\u201d Dr. Wijewardena said."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-18-dailymirrorlk-9b9d215f",
