    "md5": "be723ed131b5d032de03aef638a300cd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 953,
    "chunk_text": "Drawing on \u2018Inflation: A Guide for Users and Losers\u2019 by political economists Mark Blyth and Nicol\u00f2 Fraccaroli, he contended that once inflation breaches the upper limit and the central bank is unable to rein it in, the responsibility falls on the fiscal authorities. In his view, budgetary policy then has to be geared towards providing relief to the people.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s a matter for the Treasury as well as the Central Bank to do this job jointly,\u201d he stressed. He expressed hope that Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, who was present at the forum, would take up the proposal seriously and arrange for the Council to meet fortnightly.\n\nDr. Wijewardena also listed a joint inflation defence by the Finance Ministry and the CBSL among the benchmarks he set for the forum\u2019s panel discussion. The other benchmarks were a seamless handover from the IMF programme and the ignition of economic take-off."
