    "chunk_size_bytes": 910,
    "chunk_text": "Court of Appeal upholds four-year jail term for Gnanasara Thera\n\nColombo, Nov. 18 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Court of Appeal has upheld the four-year rigorous imprisonment sentence imposed on Bodu Bala Sena (BBS) General Secretary Ven. Galagoda Aththe Gnanasara Thera for making remarks deemed insulting to Islam.\n\nThe court dismissed an appeal filed by the Thera seeking to be acquitted and released from the sentence imposed by the Colombo High Court in 2024.\n\nThe Attorney General had filed charges against him under Section 291 of the Penal Code over remarks made at a press conference held in Kirulapone on March 30, 2016, concerning the Kuragala temple.\n\nHe was accused of insulting the Islamic religion and making statements detrimental to harmony among different races and religious communities.\n\nAfter finding him guilty, the Colombo High Court sentenced him to four years of rigorous imprisonment in 2024."
