    "md5": "13583d7a0fa6d2d62c7a3bcd54807358",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "Iran attacks US bases in Gulf countries despite diplomatic efforts\n\nReuters\u00a0- Gulf countries said on Wednesday they intercepted missiles and drones from Iran and its Houthi allies \u200bin Yemen, after the United States had struck Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz in an uptick of hostilities despite \u200cefforts to end the nine-month-old war.\n\nThe back-and-forth attacks were a reminder of the hurdles facing diplomatic efforts to end a war that has destabilised the Middle East, pushed up global energy prices and helped fuel the US voter anger that punished President Donald Trump's Republican Party in the November elections.\n\nThe Iranian army said it had targeted US drone and missile installations at Kuwait's Ali Al Salem \u200bbase, after the US ally said its air defences were countering hostile drone attacks. It was the first Iranian attack on the oil-rich country \u200bsince September.\n\nNeighbouring Bahrain said it intercepted Iranian aerial attacks for the third time this week. It accused Tehran of maintaining a \"systematic \u2060hostile approach\" of targeting the country, which hosts the US Navy's Fifth Fleet.\n\nThe Saudi-led coalition fighting the Iran-aligned Houthis in Yemen said it destroyed a \u200bcruise missile launched by the militia towards the Saudi capital of Riyadh.\n\nOn Tuesday, on the opposite side of the Gulf, US fighter jets fired on a \u200bRevolutionary Guards missile launch site on Qeshm Island, said a US military official, who spoke on condition of anonymity.\n\nThe official said the strike was in response to Iran's attacks on US personnel and assets.\n\nIranian media, citing an Iranian official, said the US attack did not damage infrastructure.\n\nTrump said on Tuesday the US was taking seriously the possibility that Iran could \u200bbe planning an attack on Washington, when asked about a CNN report that cited US intelligence assessments on a potential Iranian plot involving a so-called dirty \u200bbomb."
