    "chunk_text": "Russia, China should \u2018lead\u2019 push to multipolar world, Xi tells APEC summit\n\nALJAZEERA - Chinese President Xi Jinping has said that Beijing and Moscow should \u201clead and advance the trend towards a multipolar world\u201d following a meeting with Russian President Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit.\n\nXi and Putin held bilateral discussions on Wednesday in the southern Chinese city of Shenzhen.\n\nFollowing Xi, Putin took to the stage, telling the summit that Western powers were \u201cformer hegemons\u201d, adding that Europe was in the midst of a \u201chumiliating decline\u201d.\n\n\u201cExperience has shown that the traditional tools of economic dominance and de facto coercion have largely run their course, having lost much of their intimidating power,\u201d Putin said.\n\n\u201cWhile sanctions, tariffs and export restrictions may still exert a certain deterrent effect, they are incapable of halting growth \u2013 let alone crushing the economies of competitors.\u201d\n\nRussia\u2019s economy has been heavily sanctioned by the US and Europe because of its war against Ukraine, which began in February 2022 when Moscow invaded its neighbour.\n\nAPEC was established in 1989 and has 21 members, accounting for more than 50 percent of global gross domestic product (GDP) and representing about 2.7 billion people.\n\nThe organisation aims to support economic growth and prosperity in the Asia Pacific region.\n\nLeaders are expected to discuss a range of important issues at this year\u2019s summit, including artificial intelligence (AI) and trade \u2013 two areas in which the US and China play dominant roles.\n\nA key issue for APEC members and the wider world is the trade truce between Washington and Beijing, and whether it will be extended beyond January."
