    "chunk_text": "The eBird display will be among several interactive exhibits at the P. B. Karunaratne Memorial Exhibition, which will also feature a simulated rainforest, wetland biodiversity displays, bird songs and a live bird-banding station.\n\nVisitors will also be able to learn how researchers use modern technologies, including satellite tagging, to track bird movements across continents.\n\nThe National Zoological Gardens and the National Museum will contribute special displays, while university undergraduates will present interactive models explaining Sri Lanka's terrestrial and aquatic ecosystems.\n\nThe exhibition will also feature expert seminars, children's activities and an art corner, providing opportunities for visitors of all ages to explore the world of birds and nature conservation.\n\nThe four-day exhibition will be held from November 19 to 22 at the Faculty of Science premises of the University of Colombo, from 8.30 a.m. to 7.00 p.m. daily.\n\nUnder the theme of encouraging the next generation of conservationists, FOGSL hopes to inspire more people to take an interest in bird research and environmental protection as it marks five decades of work.\n\n\"The birds you meet today need you tomorrow,\" is the message behind the Golden Jubilee celebrations."
