    "chunk_text": "Trump shakes hands with Putin and Xi ahead of historic talks in China\n\nBBC - Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin met for the first time in over a year on Wednesday, as the pair prepared for landmark talks in China with Xi Jinping.\n\nThe US president was greeted off his plane by the Chinese leader as he arrived in Shenzhen for a summit of Asia-Pacific leaders, which will culminate in a closely-watched meeting between the pair and the Russian president.\n\nAfter a carefully choreographed handshake and hug between Trump and Xi on the tarmac, the US president later greeted and exchanged pleasantries with Putin ahead of a reception.\n\nTrump and Putin are expected to hold one-on-one talks on the sidelines of the summit on Thursday, in which the conflict in Ukraine could be discussed.\n\nHowever the main focus during the Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation forum (Apec) will be on the US-China-Russia talks on Thursday - the first time the trio of leaders have met together in person.\n\nA full agenda has not been made public but there have been various hints about what could be discussed, including the conflicts in Ukraine and Iran, nuclear proliferation, trade tensions and developments in artificial intelligence.\n\nIt was not clear on Wednesday what form separate Trump-Putin talks would take, though a Kremlin spokesperson indicated short informal talks may happen without large delegations in the room.\n\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has raised fears of a plan to end the war being discussed in the absence of representatives from Kyiv or Europe.\n\nWednesday's handshake was the first in-person meeting between Trump and Putin since August 2025, when the Russian leader travelled to Alaska for talks on the Ukraine war which failed to deliver a breakthrough.\n\nXi's personal reception for Trump at the airport mimicked a similar move by the US president when the Chinese leader visited Washington in September, a gesture Xi described as \"special\"."
