    "chunk_text": "Wednesday's handshake was the first in-person meeting between Trump and Putin since August 2025, when the Russian leader travelled to Alaska for talks on the Ukraine war which failed to deliver a breakthrough.\n\nXi's personal reception for Trump at the airport mimicked a similar move by the US president when the Chinese leader visited Washington in September, a gesture Xi described as \"special\".\n\nChinese state-run news agency Xinhua quoted Xi as saying he wanted to pursue a \"constructive strategic and stable relationship based on respect, fairness, and equality\".\n\nXi's greeting will be seen as a diplomatic gesture designed to begin the week's talks with his American counterpart on a cordial note.\n\nThe south-east Chinese city the Apec summit is being held in is a booming area for manufacturing and advanced tech.\n\nIt comes against the backdrop of the ousting of Nvidia chief executing Jensen Huang, who admitted to having an affair with a woman suspected by US intelligence of spying for Beijing - a claim dismissed as a \"smear\" by China.\n\nTrump has pursued warmer relations with China but the incident points to ongoing tensions between the two powers.\n\nSeveral hours before Trump's arrival, Putin landed in Shenzhen and held around two hours of talks with Xi, with whom he has pressed for closer economic and defence relations.\n\nXi said both countries would \"move forward steadily and boldly\" and that the relationship was \"stable as a mountain, unshaken by storms\"."
