    "chunk_text": "Initial five-day box office reports indicate that this massive financial gamble is generating significant early returns. The film has recorded remarkable ticket sales across a broad geographic footprint, taking in strong numbers not only in domestic Indian centers but also throughout North America, Europe, Australia, New Zealand, and Southeast Asia.\n\nSeveral distinct factors have converged to drive this foreign performance:\n\nTargeted digital strategy: A multi-platform digital marketing campaign tailored for international audiences created widespread online awareness well ahead of release.\n\nHigh-profile cross-cultural talent: The inclusion of world-renowned creators\u2014most notably legendary film composer Hans Zimmer alongside premier international visual effects studios\u2014helped bridge the aesthetic gap for global moviegoers, framing the film as a global spectacle rooted in an exotic Eastern narrative.\n\nAI-assisted globalisation: The production team deployed a streamlined, shorter English language edit featuring artificial intelligence-driven lip-sync technology, significantly reducing textual and linguistic barriers for non-native viewers.\n\nGenre alignment: The film successfully tapped into an existing global appetite for immersive, mythical world-building, positioning itself within the same viewing habits that support Western fantasy franchises.\n\nDespite these impressive early figures, a deeper analytical look reveals a more nuanced commercial picture. When evaluated strictly against global Hollywood behemoths such as Christopher Nolan\u2019s Oppenheimer or other recent tentpole releases, the film\u2019s initial five-day international revenue remains noticeably lower. Declaring the project a complete global crossover success requires qualification."
