    "chunk_text": "Harsha\u2019s contention on Marxism-Leninism and economics is vaporised by the achievement of the Communist Parties of China and Vietnam. His position is different from Sajith\u2019s contestable yet understandable declaration that China and Vietnam\u2019s economies are capitalist. (I\u2019d say they are better understood as \u2018hybrid systems\u2019 or a \u2018systemic fusion\u2019.) Sajith wisely never contradicts the fact that the foundations and core convictions of the Chinese and Vietnamese CPs are Marxist-Leninist.\n\nHarsha doesn\u2019t get the JVP-NPP\u2019s dark dualism: ultra-capitalist economics, one-party (\u2018Marxist-Leninist\u2019) political rule.\n\nSajith\u2019s Budget speech was a masterclass; intellectually, substantively, the best on both sides of the aisle. (https://youtu.be/T_Ss7xsvxrQ?si=FrsjJmNKfUYGQYnw)\n\nHe refused to give AKD \u2013 and Ranil Wickremesinghe\u2014a free pass on \u2018economic stabilisation\u2019. Instead, he de-constructed the \u2018economic stabilisation\u2019 itself:\n\n\u201c\u2026Therefore, indeed, when you claim conditions have normalised, I wish to state that normalisation has occurred to the advantage of multi-trillionaires and the ultra-rich\u2014to the disadvantage of the poor, the common public, the working class, and the middle class\u2026\u201d\n\nThe Daily FT report of his speech prefaces the text with key takeaways as bullet-points:\n\nSays poorest 20%\u2019s real household income fell 19.6% in 2019-2025, richest 20%\u2019s rose 6.8%\n\nClaims only $ 1 b FDI came in 2025 as several projects exited\n\n\u2018\u2026Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa yesterday\u2026charged that the 2027 Budget widens inequality, fails to draw foreign investment and offers no relief to farmers, small businesses or public servants."
