    "chunk_text": "\u2026He said farmers were promised Rs. 150 per kg of paddy, but prices had fallen to a maximum of Rs. 95. He said the promised interest-free loans and price support through small and medium millers had not materialised, and that cultivation of big onions, potatoes, chillies, upland crops, fruit, export crops and upcountry vegetables had collapsed.\n\n\u201cYou have not provided even an atom of support for agriculture through this Budget,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said a World Bank report of October 2026 found that 60% of the country was poor, while the UNDP Multidimensional Poverty Report showed poverty had escalated severely. He said the Government and the Department of Census and Statistics wrongly used a blanket average of 2,030 kilocalories per person per day, when the Medical Research Institute showed needs vary by gender and activity. This error led to the claim that Rs. 17,742 a month was enough for one person, he said.\n\n\u2026He asked why the 15% interest on savings promised to senior citizens had not been granted, and said retirees\u2019 core problems remained unresolved.\n\nPremadasa said the Budget had no proposal for the promised 33% cut in electricity bills, and that pledges of a Rs. 1.2 million Vitz car, a Rs. 50,000 motorcycle and fuel at port landing prices had not been kept.\n\nHe said schools could not secure smart boards or computers, and the health sector faced severe shortages of drugs, equipment and staff. He asked what had happened to the promised fish-locating app and the plan to develop marine resources in the 200-nautical-mile exclusive economic zone. To stem the brain, drain, he urged the Government to grant vehicle permits to professionals, including doctors, rather than to MPs.\n\nPremadasa\u2026described it [the Budget] as one that \u201cstrikes the stomach of the common man and the poor\u201d."
