    "chunk_text": "He said schools could not secure smart boards or computers, and the health sector faced severe shortages of drugs, equipment and staff. He asked what had happened to the promised fish-locating app and the plan to develop marine resources in the 200-nautical-mile exclusive economic zone. To stem the brain, drain, he urged the Government to grant vehicle permits to professionals, including doctors, rather than to MPs.\n\nPremadasa\u2026described it [the Budget] as one that \u201cstrikes the stomach of the common man and the poor\u201d.\n\nThe statistics and diagrams that Sajith tabled reveal that the seismic shift of real income from the poor and working people to the very rich began in 2019. This establishes the truth: the model which enables the unprecedented dominance of \u201cthe multi-trillionaires, the ultra-rich\u201d; the tectonic shift in policy paradigm, began with Gotabaya Rajapaksa, ran through Gota\u2019s choice (unelected) Ranil Wickremesinghe, and reached the next level with Anura Dissanayake.\n\nI was there with Sanja, seated behind Mahinda Rajapaksa, when it happened in May 2018 at the Viyath Maga 2nd Convention at the Hotel Shangri-la. The top corporate owners and head-honchos were all present. As I noted at the time:\n\n\u2018\u2026we were able to see the heaviest hitters of Colombo\u2019s corporate class\u2026Ken Balendra, Harry Jayawardena, and Merrill Fernando among them. The heavy hitters weren\u2019t lurking on the flanks, hedging their bets. They didn\u2019t mind being up front, literally and metaphorically. The bourgeoisie had just defected from a UNP Government.\u2019"
