    "md5": "0561eaed26593b9715c22478bc82d044",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "At Viyath Maga-2 (2018), the ultra-rich shifted from Ranil\u2019s UNP to Gotabaya. When the Aragalaya ousted Gota, they shifted back to his nominee Ranil. From Ranil they transitioned to Anura and obtained the greatest and most direct policy influence since Independence.\n\nSajith Premadasa\u2019s deconstruction of the 2027 Budget and the AKD administration\u2019s trajectory since 2024 (preceded by Ranil Wickremesinghe\u2019s), is the first ideological and doctrinal departure in the democratic political mainstream from the hegemonic elite consensus dating from 2018, and the first pivot to a social democratic centrism.\n\nSajith\u2019s Budget speech (belatedly) approximates the advice given to him (on camera, reported in the media) by the finest Finance Minister we had, Ronnie de Mel, when Sajith and Harsha paid a call on his 91st birthday: \u201c[to revive the Open Economy] bring the whole thing under the control of the ideas you hold, and infuse it with a strong dose of socialist values.\u201d\n\nThis year Sajith explicitly critiqued neoliberal right-wing economics and asserted the imperative of \u2018Middle Path-Social Democracy-Social Market Economy\u2019 to an audience of Opposition (not merely SJB) politicians at a Pre-Budget Workshop in Colombo. (https://youtu.be/4u_NNpIrCj4?si=l6sxaaIELwR-EoLn)\n\nNamal Rajapaksa\u2019s fact-armed, \u2018Ninja\u2019 assault on Government performance in the Budget debate (14 Nov.), highlighted multiple broken promises and the tax policy that suctions wealth from the poor to the rich. Immaculately attired and coolly self-assured, he displayed \u2018grace under pressure\u2019--the quality legendarily commended by Ernest Hemingway. (https://www.youtube.com/live/2aB7RE_adR4?si=FV4L4gzAMMTBM0xJ)\n\nIf Sirima Bandaranaike wasn\u2019t disenfranchised and Aung San Suu Kyi jailed, there wouldn\u2019t have been an armed uprising in Sri Lanka and wouldn\u2019t be one in Myanmar."
