    "chunk_text": "Namal Rajapaksa\u2019s fact-armed, \u2018Ninja\u2019 assault on Government performance in the Budget debate (14 Nov.), highlighted multiple broken promises and the tax policy that suctions wealth from the poor to the rich. Immaculately attired and coolly self-assured, he displayed \u2018grace under pressure\u2019--the quality legendarily commended by Ernest Hemingway. (https://www.youtube.com/live/2aB7RE_adR4?si=FV4L4gzAMMTBM0xJ)\n\nIf Sirima Bandaranaike wasn\u2019t disenfranchised and Aung San Suu Kyi jailed, there wouldn\u2019t have been an armed uprising in Sri Lanka and wouldn\u2019t be one in Myanmar.\n\nA wide space for progressive populist-centrism is opening up as the Government relentlessly moves further Right in its economic policies and public discontent mounts over affordability.\n\nResting on the legacy of stellar economic achievement of paternal Presidents, Sajith and Namal are scornful of the Government\u2019s mediocre performance and exude confidence that each could revive rapid development. Sajith\u2019s discourse is more social-democratic and pluralist, parsing Buddhist scripture to present its rational core; Namal\u2019s is more hard-charging, bearing a nationalist religio-cultural sub-text. Voters will have two credible options for change."
