    "chunk_size_bytes": 989,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka has remained decoupled from this cycle for the past five years due to the 2022 economic collapse, but the IMF\u2019s primary mission today is to forcefully reintegrate Sri Lanka into global financial markets as a vehicle for surplus extraction. This is precisely why the IMF opposes exchange controls in the third world. These measures will enable the region to function independently of global speculative capital, delivering a lethal blow to this new form of dependency and surplus extraction towards the core from the periphery.\n\nFinally, we emphasise that the horrendously repressive Protection of the State from Terrorism Act (PSTA) and Prevention of Organised Crimes Bill (POCA) have been deliberately introduced by the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) regime to stamp out future public dissent, silence opposing voices against the increasingly unbearable living costs and crumbling state of essential services, and secure the interests of local and global speculative capital."
