    "chunk_text": "The Opposition Leader summed up his case by saying the Government has \u201csignalled left and turned right\u201d and playing on the Sinhala word for Budget: \u201cThis is not an ayawaya [Budget]; it is a pachawaya [a Budget of tall tales].\u201d As an alternative, he called for \u201cthe middle path, social democracy and a social market economy\u201d. A social market economy would let markets drive growth and investment while the State protects the vulnerable, which is exactly the balance Budget 2027 lacks.\n\nIn conclusion, the Government owes the country evidence, not promises. By exposing the key weaknesses of Budget 2027, the Opposition Leader has questioned the Government on the principle of social justice, and that questioning deserves to be heard.\n\n(The author is Head of Department of Economics and Statistics, University of Peradeniya)"
