    "chunk_size_bytes": 1642,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Digital Economy Authority is a principal tool that will drive, regulate and manage the digital transformation. The confluence of several regulatory bodies including the TRCSL and other agencies will further strengthen the digital economy, where the council will be the apex body. It will include the President, so that we can provide quick responses to any query. We must establish the necessary regulations and set in place the cybersecurity so we stay ahead of the curve,\u201d Dr. Wijayasuriya said.\n\nThe CEO of Advocata Dhananath Fernando had suggestions on fast tracking reforms and growth. \u201cThe single entity for investment promotion is important. One major issue is that you need to pay top salaries to attract the best people to run these State institutions. This is a difficult one for Government as the public sector is already quite large, and one option is to move the excess lower ends out so you can improve capacity to attract top talent. But that is not going to happen three years to an election.\u201d\n\nFernando also noted the restructure of some State-owned entities, the draft Customs ordinance have taken too long, including trade liberalisation\n\nperhaps due to pressure coming from domestic industries. He also urged the Government to expedite the privatisation\u00a0of SriLankan Airlines.\n\nResponding to his concerns during the panel discussion, Treasury Secretary Dr. Suriyapperuma noted the amendments to the Customs Ordinance are the final stage and it could come into effect early next year, and said attracting talent is a key factor for Government, and a renewed KPI-driven approach is being mooted in this regard."
  },
