    "chunk_text": "\u201cThere are many changes in the regulatory aspect, and more are coming. There is a pilot underway where you could register a business in just two days. Access to market is a barrier we are struggling with, especially for SMEs, but we are looking to support them by going digital. Our programs are aligned to help them scale all the way to even reach global markets. But we should get rid of the word protection. Our consumers must have the best. We need to have a set of standards for what is coming into the country,\u201d Abeysinghe said.\n\nFrom an industrial perspective, he said: \u201cThere is need for two-tier expansion. Short to medium-term gains can be got where we can increase capacity. The capital allowance in the budget for companies that invest $ 3 million will benefit the export sector as that will make us more competitive. We have to get our cost per unit down. There is enough volume and business as long as we get our cost right. I hope automation investments are included in this bracket, as we need to get our exports up fast. If we lose out to competition from other countries it is difficult to bring them back.\u201d\n\nPremaratne also praised efforts to enhance ease of doing business, and pointed to the single window of transaction as a key initiative. He explained how the industry was skeptical of return payments when SVAT was abolished, but proceedings had been reasonably good and expressed hope it continues so. Technology must come into make Sri Lanka more productive and cost competitive, he said."
