    "chunk_size_bytes": 1379,
    "chunk_text": "Seven new envoys present credentials to President\n\nNew Ambassadors and High Commissioners from Republic of Korea, Switzerland, EU, Egypt, Lao PDR, Namibia and Singapore also accredited\n\nSeven newly appointed Ambassadors and High Commissioners presented their Letters of Credence to President Anura Kumara Dissanayake at a ceremony held at the Presidential Secretariat on 17 November, the President\u2019s Office said.\n\nIn order of precedence, the newly accredited envoys are Republic of Korea Ambassador Kim Youn-Jung, Switzerland Ambassador Daniel Hunn, European Union (EU) Ambassador Sylvia Hartleif and Arab Republic of Egypt Ambassador Ahmed El-Sayed Abdel Halim Amer Helal, all resident in Colombo.\n\nThey are followed by Lao People\u2019s Democratic Republic Ambassador Vithaya Xayavong and Republic of Namibia High Commissioner Wing Commander Alex L. Tukuhupwele (Retd), both resident in New Delhi, and Republic of Singapore High Commissioner Patrick Daniel, who is resident in Singapore.\n\nThe envoys were appointed by their respective Governments, with the concurrence of the Government of Sri Lanka, to represent their countries in Sri Lanka. The EU Ambassador was appointed to represent the EU in Sri Lanka.\n\nForeign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and Secretary to the President Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake were also present at the ceremony."
