    "md5": "4dfbdc2ae9b8e5990cbb4eafdc35ac0e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1629,
    "chunk_text": "CanCham Sri Lanka builds bridges for economic partnerships through mission to Canada\n\nLed by Co-founders and Board Directors Mohamed Hameez and Priyantha Chandrasekara, the Canadian Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka (CanCham Sri Lanka) continued its Business Promotion Mission to Canada with a series of Government meetings, investment discussions, institutional visits and business networking activities across Toronto, Ottawa and Montr\u00e9al, as part of its wider effort to advance and strengthen bilateral trade, investment and economic cooperation between Canada and Sri Lanka and the wider Indo-Pacific region.\n\nThe delegation met with Ontario Economic Development, Job Creation and Trade Minister Victor Fedeli. Both sides discussed opportunities for deeper economic partnerships, investment facilitation and cross-border collaboration between Ontario and Sri Lanka. Fedeli highlighted the importance of collaboration in technology, artificial intelligence (AI) and research and development (R&D) as key drivers of future economic growth and job creation. The meeting was attended by representatives of the CanCham business mission, including delegates from CHEC Colombo Port City, ECD Holidays, and Horizon College and Campus.\n\nDiscussions were held with Invest Ontario, the province's investment promotion agency, on opportunities for investment collaboration, business partnerships and greater connectivity between the two markets. These discussions formed part of CanCham Sri Lanka's broader efforts to introduce Sri Lankan investment opportunities to Canadian stakeholders and encourage greater private-sector engagement."
  },
