    "chunk_text": "Discussions were held with Invest Ontario, the province's investment promotion agency, on opportunities for investment collaboration, business partnerships and greater connectivity between the two markets. These discussions formed part of CanCham Sri Lanka's broader efforts to introduce Sri Lankan investment opportunities to Canadian stakeholders and encourage greater private-sector engagement.\n\nAnother significant networking initiative was an HNI Business Networking Session organised by Marsa Business Solutions Inc. at the White Field Convention Center in Scarborough. The Sri Lankan delegation connected with institutional investors and business representatives from the United States, South Korea, India, Indonesia and the Philippines. Discussions covered investment opportunities in Port City Colombo, joint ventures involving educational institutions, and potential developments in retirement, wellness and resort projects, opening avenues for investment in Sri Lanka's tourism and health and wellness sectors.\n\nThe delegation also participated in networking sessions with members of the Sri Lankan diaspora, high-net-worth individuals, investors and the Lions Club of Scarborough. The sessions helped strengthen connections with the Canadian-based business community and opened opportunities to explore investment and commercial partnerships across the real estate and education sectors.\n\nDevika Anthony hosted additional business networking sessions at the Grand Hyatt Toronto, while Caliber Mortgage Inc. Director and Mortgage Broker Kelum Hewage provided opportunities to connect with Canadian business professionals and explore collaboration in the sectors of financial services, property investment and real estate development."
