    "chunk_text": "Devika Anthony hosted additional business networking sessions at the Grand Hyatt Toronto, while Caliber Mortgage Inc. Director and Mortgage Broker Kelum Hewage provided opportunities to connect with Canadian business professionals and explore collaboration in the sectors of financial services, property investment and real estate development.\n\nIn Ottawa, the delegation attended a business forum with Sri Lanka's Acting High Commissioner to Canada Chathura Weerasekara. The Trade and Investment Discussion and Networking Event was jointly facilitated by the High Commission of Sri Lanka in Ottawa and CanCham Sri Lanka, with participation from members of the diplomatic corps, officials from Global Affairs Canada, Canadian business representatives and the visiting Sri Lankan delegation.\n\nWeerasekara highlighted Sri Lanka Expo 2027 as a platform to showcase the country's export capabilities and emerging sectors. Hameez outlined CanCham Sri Lanka's role in promoting bilateral trade and investment, while Home Lands Group Chairman Nalin Herath presented the group's developments and business activities in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe delegation also met with officials of the High Commission of Sri Lanka in Ottawa, including Minister Counsellor Kiritharan Kumarasamy, during its visit to the mission. The program also included a visit to the Senate of Canada, organised by the High Commission of Sri Lanka, providing the delegation with an opportunity to observe Canada's parliamentary proceedings and learn more about its legislative system.\n\nThe delegation met with Global Affairs Canada Executive Director for Pakistan, Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka and Maldives Yannick Lamonde, and Trade Facilitation Office (TFO) Canada Executive Director Steve Tipman. Discussions focused on trade development and capacity building, including strengthening Sri Lankan exporters' readiness, improving access to Canadian market information and understanding market requirements and compliance standards."
