    "chunk_text": "The delegation met with Global Affairs Canada Executive Director for Pakistan, Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka and Maldives Yannick Lamonde, and Trade Facilitation Office (TFO) Canada Executive Director Steve Tipman. Discussions focused on trade development and capacity building, including strengthening Sri Lankan exporters' readiness, improving access to Canadian market information and understanding market requirements and compliance standards.\n\nThe Montr\u00e9al leg of the mission coincided with Sri Lanka's participation in the International Tourism & Travel Show (SITV), held from 30 October to 1 November, 2026. During the exhibition, the CanCham Sri Lanka leadership met with Tourism Deputy Minister Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe.\n\nThe CanCham team presented the Deputy Minister with a copy of its Tourism Plan, together with the Five-Year Action Plan, which outlined the proposed priorities for its tourism sector, and further briefed him on the proposed Global Health and Wellness Summit Sri Lanka 2027 (GHWSSL) and its potential to support the development of Sri Lanka as a health and wellness tourism destination.\n\nAs a follow-up to the mission, discussions are underway to organise an inward business delegation from Canada to Sri Lanka. The proposed visit would provide Canadian investors, prospective buyers, manufacturers and tourism stakeholders with an opportunity to experience Sri Lanka's business and investment landscape first-hand, explore potential partnerships and gain a better understanding of opportunities across key sectors. The mission has also opened avenues for continued engagement, with CanCham Sri Lanka receiving invitations to participate in future business and industry events in Canada."
