    "chunk_size_bytes": 1287,
    "chunk_text": "Nepal achieves a perfect personal optimism score of 5.00 \u2013 the only country to do so and ranked third overall. Nepal also has the highest economic optimism (4.80), suggesting that despite its lower-income status, students feel strongly positive about their individual prospects.\n\nKazakhstan is the fourth most optimistic nation according to the students polled, students report high economic confidence (4.56) along with the third-highest political optimism in the study (3.76).\n\nAmong Western nations, Canada ranks highest at sixth (4.08), comfortably ahead of the US (3.99), the UK (3.61), Germany (3.73), and France (3.22).\n\nOxford Scholastica Academy Co-Director Lavinia Abell said: \u201cIn every aspect of society, there are things to be anxious and pessimistic about. This could be the rise in Artificial Intelligence (AI), war, the cost-of-living increasing, and much more. This will be especially worrisome for young people, facing challenges as they enter the world of work. What this study highlights is the attitudes of each nationality towards these uncertainties. What is particularly striking is how low Italy\u2019s political optimism scores are compared to other European nations. Even France and Poland, which also rank near the bottom, show slightly different patterns.\u201d"
  },
