    "md5": "fc3753f923aea6add4a3d0f0317f03df",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1857,
    "chunk_text": "INSEE Lanka wins Gold at Presidential Environment Awards 2026\n\nThe INSEE Lanka team receiving the Gold Award from Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya\n\nINSEE Lanka has been awarded the Gold Award of Commendation at the Presidential Environment Awards Ceremony 2026.\n\nThe award recognised the company\u2019s excellent contribution to environmental sustainability within the Mineral Related Manufacturing Industry. The ceremony, organized by the Central Environmental Authority under the Ministry of Environment took place on 19 October, at the BMICH Main Hall.\n\nEng. Thusith Gunawarnasuriya, CEO, INSEE Lanka said, \u201cThis national-level recognition reaffirms that INSEE continues to demonstrate industrial growth, and environmental stewardship can coexist through responsible operations, innovation and long-term environmental commitment.\u201d\n\nUnder the Climate and Energy pillar, INSEE continues to develop lower-carbon cement. In 2021, it became the pioneer to introduce Portland Composite Cement (PCC) to the market, reducing CO\u2082 emissions compared to conventional Ordinary Portland Cement (OPC). The company is focused on promoting low-carbon cement production, improving energy efficiency, and increasing thermal energy substitution through waste-derived alternative fuels, reducing dependency on fossil fuelssuch as coal.\n\nThrough INSEE Ecocycle, the company\u2019s specialized waste management arm, a circular economy is driven utilizing cement kiln co-processing. The process transforms industrial waste into alternative fuel and raw materials in cement production, reducing reliance on coal. Additionally, the company repurposes fly ash, a waste by-product from Coal Power Plants, as a supplementary cementitious material to reduce clinker use, conserve natural resources and lower the carbon footprint of cement, as an industrial symbiosis initiative."
