    "md5": "16d0b91d29dce3d56464fb9b1cbaa74a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1943,
    "chunk_text": "GEW Sri Lanka 2026 to connect entrepreneurs and open new opportunities for biz growth\n\nGlobal Entrepreneurship Week (GEW) Sri Lanka 2026 brings together aspiring entrepreneurs, startups, small and medium enterprises (SMEs), business leaders and young innovators to strengthen the country\u2019s entrepreneurial ecosystem and create opportunities for business growth.\n\nOrganised by the Global Entrepreneurship Network (GEN Global), in close collaboration with the Ministry of Digital Economy, the Ministry of Industries and Entrepreneurship Development, and the Ministry of Science and Technology, GEW Sri Lanka 2026 connects entrepreneurs, innovators, businesses and ecosystem stakeholders across all 25 districts.\n\nThe GEW Sri Lanka 2026 Launching Ceremony was held on the second day of Science Week, in collaboration with the Ministry of Science and Technology. The national campaign commences during Global Entrepreneurship Week, from 16 to 22 November 2026, with activities continuing throughout the year to expand and scale entrepreneurship initiatives across the country.\n\nThe campaign features panel discussions, workshops, networking sessions and business exhibitions, providing entrepreneurs with opportunities to exchange knowledge, showcase their businesses and connect with industry stakeholders.\n\nThe launching ceremony was attended by Deputy Minister of Digital Economy, Eranga Weeraratne; Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, Chathuranga Abeysinghe; Secretary to the Ministry of Science and Technology, Roshanie Dissanayake; Mastercard Country Manager for Sri Lanka, Mahesha Amarasuriya; GEN Global National Ambassador for Sri Lanka, Suresh de Mel; Managing Director of NGage Strategic Alliance, Sheron Jayasundara; Founder and Chairman of Kapruka Holdings PLC, Dulith Herath; and LMS, AI and SaaS Consultant, CEO of eLearning.lk and Co-Founder of MayaHive, Sanjaya Elvitigala, who served as the moderator."
