    "description": "Sri Lanka Insurance General unveils country\u2019s first-ever Virtual Motor Claim Office",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Sri-Lanka-Insurance-General-unveils-countrys-first-ever-Virtual-Motor-Claim-Office/215-355242",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1795057388.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-55218e5f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c90171734d95a7b5a59c24633ab85dd5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1735,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Insurance General unveils country\u2019s first-ever Virtual Motor Claim Office\n\nSri Lanka Insurance Corporation General Ltd (SLICGL) has unveiled the country\u2019s first-ever Virtual Motor Claim Office, a mobile-accessible web platform, which delivers the entire post-accident claims journey directly to the customers\u2019 smartphones.\n\nThe motor insurance policyholders islandwide can now bypass physical branch visits when filing vehicle claims and connect with SLICGL anytime and anywhere.\n\nDealing with a vehicle accident means navigating stressful, paperwork-heavy processes and making repeated trips to physical branches. Built on over 64 years of government-backed trust and reliability, SLICGL has launched the digital platform to replace traditional delays with speed, transparency and convenience.\n\nThe new workflow is straightforward and puts full control in the driver\u2019s hands. Once an SLICGL technical officer completes the initial vehicle inspection, the policyholder receives a dedicated, secure web link. Through this portal, the customers can easily complete their claim forms, upload supporting documents and enter their bank details for direct financial settlements without ever stepping foot inside an office.\n\nIn addition to submissions, the platform offers complete visibility and direct support throughout the repair process. The policyholders can review their uploaded files, track approval stages and monitor payment settlements in real time. Whenever questions come up, the customers can message their assigned claim officers directly through a built-in online chat during office hours. For the eligible claims within specified value limits, even the final post-repair inspection can be completed online."
  },
