    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6feb34679dbaccdb139a3157a09b8fb5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1912,
    "chunk_text": "Seylan Bank extends financing facilities to Electricity Generation Lanka\n\nSeylan Bank PLC recently extended financing facilities to Electricity Generation Lanka Private Limited (EGL), a key successor entity established following the restructuring of the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB), up to Rs.6.6 billion, further strengthening its commitment to Sri Lanka\u2019s power and energy sector.\n\nThe transaction represents another significant milestone in the enduring collaboration between Seylan Bank and Sri Lanka\u2019s power sector and reflects the bank\u2019s continued commitment to supporting nationally significant infrastructure and strategically important sectors of the economy.\n\nThe financing marks an extension of Seylan Bank\u2019s long-standing partnership with the CEB into the restructured electricity sector. With the bank continuing to support EGL\u2019s funding, trade finance and operational requirements, Seylan Bank\u2019s financing facilities are expected to support the entity\u2019s ongoing commercial and operational requirements associated with maintaining critical generation infrastructure and ensuring the continuity of electricity generation across the island.\n\nSeylan Bank also surpassed Rs.1 trillion in total assets in September 2026, becoming the fourth private sector bank in Sri Lanka to achieve the landmark and marking a significant milestone in its growth journey among Sri Lanka\u2019s leading private sector banks.\n\nEGL plays a critical role within Sri Lanka\u2019s restructured electricity sector, having been entrusted with strategically important power generation assets essential to meeting the country\u2019s rising demand for electricity. As a principal generation entity in Sri Lanka, EGL is responsible for maintaining the continued operation and availability of major generation infrastructure, making its operations integral to the reliability and stability of the national electricity supply."
  },
