    "md5": "b304c2478d76f9bcbb504633797c7e55",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1561,
    "chunk_text": "HNB FINANCE surpasses Rs.100bn in assets as 1H profit rises 50%\n\nProfit after tax rose by 50% YoY to Rs.929mn, supported by stronger core earnings\n\nNet interest income rose by 46% YoY to Rs.5.48bn, reflecting strong core business performance\n\nHNB FINANCE PLC surpassed the Rs.100 billion asset milestone in the first half of the financial year 2026/27, with total assets reaching Rs.106.67 billion as at September 30, 2026.\n\nThe company also recorded a 50 percent year-on-year (YoY) increase in profit after tax to Rs.929 million for the six months ended September 30, 2026, reflecting the sustained earnings growth.\n\nThe company\u2019s profit before tax increased by 50 percent to Rs.2.47 billion, compared to Rs.1.65 billion in the corresponding period of the previous year. The net interest income increased by 46 percent to Rs.5.48 billion, from Rs.3.76 billion, further supporting the improvement in profitability.\n\nThe company\u2019s asset base expanded by 13 percent from Rs.94.39 billion as at March 31, 2026. Net assets increased by 37 percent to Rs.12.68 billion, from Rs.9.26 billion, contributed by the Rs.2.5 billion rights issue and growth in profitability, thereby further strengthening HNB FINANCE\u2019s overall financial position.\n\nThe lending portfolio expanded by 7 percent to Rs. 81.95 billion, from Rs.76.33 billion during the six-month period. Leasing remained a key contributor to portfolio growth, recording a 17 percent increase to Rs.59.92 billion, from Rs.51.02 billion. The deposit base improved to Rs.71.43 billion as at September 30, 2026."
  },
