    "chunk_text": "The budget seeks to accelerate work in Ingiriya, Dambulla, Raigama, Millaniya and Katunayake and upgrade the infrastructure at the existing estates. Kahawalage urged the officials to ensure timely spending across the government\u2019s wider investment programme including transport, highways, railways, water supply, irrigation, health, education, housing, urban development, energy, digital infrastructure, ports and regional projects.\n\nHe also backed the push to digitise public administration, saying it could improve the efficiency and transparency of the government operations.\n\nKahawalage cited President Anura Kumara Dissanayake\u2019s aim to deliver a budget that \u201cstrengthens the production economy, protects the small and medium-scale industries, makes room for investment, connects knowledge and technology to the economy through digital economic activities, protects the environment and ensures social justice\u201d.\n\nThe CNCI said it would continue to work with the government on its economic programme."
