    "md5": "ca10dc29dfe843ae9772aefbf7cbfcfe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe interim post-mortem report has revealed that these three injuries were not responsible for the death of the animal. Therefore, a comprehensive investigation should be conducted into the treatment provided to Kawanthissa.\n\nHe also alleged that although Rs.1000 million had been allocated through the budget for wild elephant conservation, only around 30% of the allocated funds had been spent, while more than 70% had remained unutilised, raising concerns about the effective use of public funds for the welfare of wild elephants.\n\nMeanwhile, Magistrate Ravindra Ranjan Bandara rejected the request by the parties to appoint an independent foreign team to conduct a post-mortem examination, observing that such a request should be made by the prosecution rather than a third party.\n\nHowever, the court permitted several parties, including wildlife photographer Pathum Bandara and environmental organisation Voice for Bharhiya, to intervene in the magisterial inquiry.\n\nThe Wildlife Department informed court that the Criminal Investigation Department (CID), together with the Department of Wildlife Conservation, was conducting an investigation into the incident. It also informed court that a Presidential Commission had been appointed to investigate Kawanthissa\u2019s death. The CID was noticed to appear before court on December 7.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Upul Jayasuriya, with Attorneys-at-Law Lakmal Sooriyagoda, Gihan Siriwardena and Kanchana Samaradiwakara, appeared on behalf of Pathum Bandara.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Anura Meddegoda, with Attorneys-at-Law B. Priyanga and Nipuni Dissanayaka, appeared for Voice for Bharhiya."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-e6a150c5",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-e6a150c5",
    "date_str": "2026-11-19",
    "description": "Who is not afraid of the US?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Who-is-not-afraid-of-the-US/172-355258",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
