    "chunk_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-e6a150c5-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b858bac4a07bec6345de709b072bb21b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1905,
    "chunk_text": "Who is not afraid of the US?\n\nThe NPP finds itself unable to follow, as a government, the policies it promoted as a political party, especially regarding IMF, PTA, Palestine, imperialism and socialism\n\nMeanwhile, Hakeem served as a minister in governments where massive corruption\u2014which is currently being exposed\u2014took place. How many of those corruption cases he questioned remains a big question mark\n\nThe government has decided to purchase four drones from Israel at a cost of Rs. 4.2 billion through a government-to-government arrangement without calling for tenders on the global market.\n\nStrongly condemning this decision, Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) Member of Parliament and Leader of the Sri Lanka Muslim Congress (SLMC), Rauff Hakeem, sharply criticised the foreign policy of the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) government last Monday.\n\nSpeaking during the budget debate, Hakeem stated that these drones are being purchased to spy on Iranian ships around Sr Lanka and questioned whether Sri Lanka is going to use its Navy and Air Force to conduct espionage on behalf of the United States.\n\nHe also raised the question, \u201cWho knows how much commission was received from the Israeli government for this drone purchase?\u201d\n\nAlso, he strongly criticised several decisions taken by the government in the past regarding foreign affairs. Although the Leader of the House and Minister of Transport, Bimal Rathnayake, attempted to respond, it was apparent that he struggled to justify the incidents pointed out by Hakeem regarding the government\u2019s foreign policy.\n\nWhile Hakeem\u2019s arguments appear reasonable overall, doubts arise as to whether some of his points are valid and whether others are justified. In particular, the suspicion he raised that the government or ministers might have taken a commission for the Israeli drones is unjustified, as there is no credible evidence to support it."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-e6a150c5",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-e6a150c5",
    "date_str": "2026-11-19",
    "description": "Who is not afraid of the US?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Who-is-not-afraid-of-the-US/172-355258",
