    "chunk_text": "However, the contention that Sri Lanka is buying drones from Israel just to spy for the United States does not seem plausible. If Sri Lanka wanted to do that, it could have purchased the drones directly from the United States itself. The question then arises: if they had done so, would Hakeem have questioned it?\n\nHowever, not only Sri Lanka, but many powerful nations such as India, Japan, China, Malaysia and Indonesia also refrained from condemning the United States in this regard and merely expressed their concern. True, the policies of the leaders of most of those non-condemning nations and the policies of the NPP are not the same. The NPP is, more or less, the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) which is an anti-imperialist party.\n\nIn that sense, it is true that Sri Lanka\u2019s actions must be watched closely. Yet, the core issue here is whether Sri Lanka is in a position to antagonise the United States\u2014especially a President like Donald Trump, who does not respect international law and whose mind cannot be read.\n\nThe Palestine issue is another complex problem facing the government. Even though the NPP had been stating that Israel is engaging in genocide, the NPP government does not use the word \u201cgenocide.\u201d Pointing this out, Hakeem criticised the government reminding that Minister Bimal Rathnayake is the President of the Sri Lanka Committee for Solidarity with Palestine.\n\nNevertheless, Sri Lanka government, in September 2011, supported the UN General Assembly vote to grant Libya\u2019s UN seat to the National Transitional Council (NTC), a Libyan opposition coalition,\u00a0 after the forcible ouster of Muammer Gaddafi. Mr. Hakeem was the justice minister of that government. These are compulsions."
  },
