    "md5": "7c25f81283929ae3b2a66ebade361588",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 936,
    "chunk_text": "Nevertheless, Sri Lanka government, in September 2011, supported the UN General Assembly vote to grant Libya\u2019s UN seat to the National Transitional Council (NTC), a Libyan opposition coalition,\u00a0 after the forcible ouster of Muammer Gaddafi. Mr. Hakeem was the justice minister of that government. These are compulsions.\n\nIronically, U.S. officials, who had been urging for the repeal of that law, also found no fault in its use at that time. Later, when a youth pasted a sticker at a hotel in Colombo condemning Israel\u2019s atrocities in Gaza without making any threats whatsoever, he too was arrested under this same repressive law.\n\nThe NPP finds itself unable to follow, as a government, the policies it promoted as a political party, especially regarding IMF, PTA, Palestine, imperialism and socialism. Although other parties exploit the situation by portraying it as dishonesty, it, in fact is the result of a convoluted context."
