    "description": "Statutory rape is not a love story!",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Statutory-rape-is-not-a-love-story/172-355259",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1795058896.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-c1d41b65-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "da935da8da67839829494d4cdb856ebe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1786,
    "chunk_text": "Statutory rape is not a love story!\n\nThe recent incident of a 15-year old girl found in a forest cave with a two-month old baby has gained undue attention for mostly the wrong reasons.\n\nThe girl was reported missing to the Ududumbara Police in July. Following a tip-off about a man who had been purchasing small quantities of rice, officers at the Ududumbara Police station had followed him into the dense forest. According to statements given to the police, the baby was born in the cave without a doctor or midwife. The 23-year old man had told police that he cut the umbilical cord with a knife used for tapping kithul palms, and that he treated the mother and baby with herbal remedies from the forest.\n\nPolice arrested the 23-year-old man, identified as the baby\u2019s father, and a 36-year-old relative accused of helping him. According to police reports, the older suspect allegedly first sexually abused the girl in 2023. Police said the younger suspect later allegedly abused her and that both men were suspected of sexually abusing her on multiple occasions.\n\nMany so-called analysts on social media romanticised this incident by even comparing it to the mythical tale \u2018Sinhabahu\u2019! At least one individual praised the suspect for his innovative approach to cut the umbilical cord much to the dismay of a majority of social media users!\n\nUnder Sri Lanka\u2019s Penal Code, sexual intercourse with a girl under 16 is rape whether or not she consents. The offence carries a sentence of 10 to 20 years\u2019 imprisonment. Following the incident, Minister of Women and Child Affairs, Saroja Savithri Paulraj, said that children should be taught sex education and the basics of the country\u2019s laws from an early age. She described this incident as a \u2018clear case of statutory rape.\u2019"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-c1d41b65",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-c1d41b65",
