    "md5": "72c658aee52a91828e67e4c55dc0aa97",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1344,
    "chunk_text": "But sex education alone won\u2019t resolve this issue which has spread like a cancer, especially in rural areas of the country. Children need to be aware of the law and what it means to give consent. Parents need to be aware of their children\u2019s whereabouts. Many children are abandoned or neglected in rural settings as both parents go to work. They are left with their guardians such as grandparents or uncles and aunts. As a result, many children and adolescents and vulnerable to sexual abuse, rape and harassment most often done by a known individual.\n\nIf incidents of sexual abuse, rape, assault and harassment concerning minors become normalised due to dangerous social media trends it would become increasingly difficult to control the situation at grassroots level.\n\nWithout a secure future for children, Sri Lanka as a society would continue to undergo profound psychological, social and structural decay.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
  },
