    "chunk_text": "Colombo to remove unauthorised structures obstructing drainage system\n\nColombo, Nov. 19 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Colombo Municipal Council (CMC) is taking steps to identify and remove unauthorised constructions obstructing the city\u2019s drainage system, Colombo Mayor Vraie Cally Balthazaar said.\n\nShe said unauthorised structures remained a major obstacle to improving drainage in the city, as they restricted the flow of water and made it difficult for authorities to clean and maintain drainage canals.\n\nThe Mayor said the CMC was continuing efforts to identify such structures and remove them as part of a wider programme to improve Colombo\u2019s drainage infrastructure.\n\nMeanwhile, she welcomed the decision by several homeowners and companies to voluntarily remove unauthorised constructions on their properties, noting that such cooperation would support efforts to address the city\u2019s drainage problems."
