    "chunk_size_bytes": 846,
    "chunk_text": "He said children below two years of age, adults aged 65 and above, pregnant women and people with underlying medical conditions such as diabetes, heart disease, asthma and kidney disease face a greater risk of developing severe complications.\n\nPeople with weakened immune systems, including those undergoing cancer treatment or taking immunosuppressive medication, are also particularly vulnerable.\n\nPeople who develop symptoms should also stay at home, get adequate rest and avoid crowded places to prevent spreading the infection to others.\n\nThe public has further been urged to avoid self-medication and seek medical advice, particularly before taking antiviral medication.\n\nSri Lanka generally experiences two seasonal peaks in influenza infections, from May to July and November to January, although the virus circulates throughout the year."
