    "md5": "00d4c18c2b002513a647e16e80a8df07",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1884,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka tops global youth optimism survey\n\nColombo, Nov. 19 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Sri Lankan students have emerged as the most optimistic young people in the world, according to a new global survey that assessed Gen Z's confidence in their personal futures, the economy, the environment, politics and society.\n\nSri Lanka ranked first among 41 countries included in the study, scoring 4.32 out of five for overall optimism, despite the economic turbulence experienced in recent years.\n\nThe survey, conducted by Oxford Scholastica Academy, a summer school provider, gathered responses from 1,433 students across 100 countries to examine how young people view the future and the challenges facing their generation.\n\nSri Lankan students recorded the highest environmental optimism in the study, scoring 4.62, while personal optimism stood at 4.75. They also expressed strong confidence in the future of society, scoring 4.25.\n\nKenya ranked second with an overall optimism score of 4.31, with students expressing particularly strong confidence in the future of society, scoring 4.43, tied for the highest in the study alongside Cyprus. Kenya also recorded the highest political optimism, at 3.96.\n\nNepal ranked third, with an overall score of 4.30, and was the only country to record a perfect score of 5.00 for personal optimism. It also recorded the highest economic optimism, at 4.80, indicating strong confidence among students in their individual prospects despite the country's lower-income status.\n\nKazakhstan ranked fourth, scoring highly for economic optimism at 4.56 and recording the third-highest political optimism in the study, at 3.76.\n\nNigeria and Indonesia also featured among the most optimistic countries, scoring 4.08 and 4.07, respectively. Nigerian students recorded environmental optimism of 3.92, while Indonesian students expressed economic confidence, scoring 4.41."
  },
