    "chunk_text": "Miami court convicts US-Haitian pastor over 2021 assassination of president\n\nALJAZEERA - A Florida pastor with dual Haitian-American citizenship has been convicted in the United States on charges stemming from the assassination of Haitian President Jovenel Moise, following a nearly eight-week trial in a federal court in Miami.\n\nChristian Emmanuel Sanon, 68, was found guilty on Wednesday on all eight charges, including conspiring to kill the Caribbean nation\u2019s president, who was shot dead in his home on July 7, 2021.\n\nProsecutors said in court records that the scheme to kill Moise, 53, included paying about two dozen foreign mercenaries with money obtained from US government programmes that were intended to help businesses during the COVID-19 pandemic.\n\nThey said South Florida was a hub for planning and financing the plot to oust Moise and install a president of the conspirators\u2019 choosing.\n\nSanon acknowledged in trial testimony that he was in communication at one point with people trying to replace Moise, but said the group had moved on to another candidate long before the assassination. He denied any knowledge of plans to kill the president and maintained his innocence throughout the trial.\n\nHe was arrested in Haiti\u2019s capital, Port-au-Prince, days after the assassination. According to a report by local police seen by the Reuters news agency, when officers searched his residence, they found eight vehicle registration plates, 19 passports and 12 mobile phones, as well as 30 boxes of ammunition and 12 pistol holsters.\n\nMoise\u2019s widow, Martine Moise \u2013 a key witness in the trial \u2013 was flown to Florida for treatment for bullet wounds she sustained in the attack. She has now registered as a presidential candidate for Haiti\u2019s 2027 general election, the first in more than 10 years.\n\nSanon, who remains in federal custody, showed little reaction as the jury verdict was announced. He faces up to life in prison and is set to be sentenced on February 10."
