    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Cricket rejects reports of no ICC men\u2019s tournament hosting until 2035\n\nColombo, Nov. 19 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Sri Lanka Cricket (SLC) has rejected media reports claiming that Sri Lanka will not host any major International Cricket Council (ICC) men\u2019s tournament until 2035, saying that hosting allocations for the 2032\u20132035 cycle have not yet been confirmed.\n\nIn a media release, SLC clarified that the hosting arrangements for ICC men\u2019s white-ball tournaments covering the 2024\u20132031 cycle were announced on November 16, 2021.\n\nUnder those arrangements, Sri Lanka co-hosted the 2026 ICC Men\u2019s T20 World Cup with India, while India was allocated the hosting rights for the 2029 ICC Men\u2019s Champions Trophy. India and Bangladesh were also designated as joint hosts of the 2031 ICC Men\u2019s Cricket World Cup.\n\nSLC stressed that these allocations were made in 2021 and were not new decisions arising from the recent ICC meetings held in Bali.\n\nCommenting on the ICC announcement made on November 15, 2026, SLC said the global governing body had confirmed the tournament calendar and event windows through 2035. However, the host nations for men's events scheduled during the 2032\u20132035 cycle have yet to be announced.\n\nTherefore, the confirmation of tournament dates and event windows does not mean that hosting rights for the 2032\u20132035 cycle have been finalised or that Sri Lanka has been excluded from hosting future ICC men's tournaments, SLC said."
