    "chunk_text": "Residents of the Saudi capital were awoken by a loud boom in the early hours of Thursday.\n\nThe Houthi-run \u200bSaba news agency reported that Saudi aircraft had carried out airstrikes on the Houthi-controlled Yemeni capital Sanaa early on Thursday, without providing further details.\n\nThe prince met US Central Command chief Admiral Brad Cooper in Riyadh on Wednesday, Cooper's third publicly reported visit to Saudi Arabia since the Yemen conflict resumed.\n\nReuters reported on Wednesday that Saudi officials now foresee the campaign stretching on for up to six months, according to two Western officials briefed by the Saudis on the kingdom's plans. A third source familiar with the Saudi plans confirmed the accounts.\n\nThe sources said the Saudis, who replaced the commander \u200bof their coalition fighting in Yemen \u200bthis week, want to see their \u2060allies make gains on the ground before they enter any negotiations with the Houthis.\n\nBut meanwhile the situation in Yemen has appeared to favour the Houthis, who have seized Yemen's entire Red Sea coast including the strategically vital Bab \u200bel-Mandeb Strait at its mouth, and have surrounded the city of Taiz in highlands overlooking the government's temporary capital \u200bAden.\n\nIn the wider war, \u2060which began in February when the United States and Israel attacked Iran, there has been no sign of a breakthrough in negotiations mediated by Qatar."
