    "chunk_text": "The GMOA also claimed that doctors had contributed to savings of more than Rs. 44 billion over the past two years following the suspension of certain allowances due to the country's economic difficulties.\n\nThe association said Sri Lanka's healthcare system had achieved internationally recognised health standards and remained one of the country's most important social security services.\n\nHowever, it argued that the Government had failed to provide adequate salaries and allowances for medical professionals, including specialist doctors, and had not taken sufficient steps to address staff shortages.\n\nThe GMOA said that the President, the Health Minister and the Government should take full responsibility for any difficulties faced by patients if trade union action becomes necessary due to the failure to address its demands."
