    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/international/UNs-top-court-finds-Myanmar-guilty-of-genocide-against-Rohingya/107-355333",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1795101852.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-19-dailymirrorlk-cc22f309-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f7479eaa65e4a85594e94f16802b7bc5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1855,
    "chunk_text": "UN\u2019s top court finds Myanmar guilty of genocide against Rohingya\n\nALJAZEERA - The United Nations\u2019 top court has ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Muslim minority Rohingya population.\n\nThe International Court of Justice (ICJ) at The Hague delivered its judgement on Thursday about the military crackdown that drove more than 730,000 mainly Muslim Rohingya to flee to neighbouring Bangladesh.\n\nICJ President Yuji Iwasawa said the court, in a 9-6 decision, found that Myanmar \u201chas committed genocide against the Rohingya group in northern Rakhine state, in violation of its obligations under the Genocide Convention\u201d.\n\nIt is the first time a state has been found responsible for genocide at the court. The ruling marked only the fourth time since the Nazi Holocaust that an international court ruled that the crime had been committed.\n\nThe case was brought by the West African nation of The Gambia, which in 2019 accused Myanmar of seeking to destroy the Rohingya people. It asked the ICJ to rule that Myanmar breached the 1948 Genocide Convention, order it to end any illegal activities targeting the Rohingya and ensure those responsible for genocide are punished.\n\nMyanmar claimed its crackdown was in response to attacks on police posts by fighters from the Arakan Rohingya Salvation Army (ARSA).\n\nEvidence shows Myanmar forces killed 10,000 Rohingya, Iwasawa said during a three-hour readout of the verdict.\n\n\u201cThe Court finds that Myanmar\u2019s security forces killed thousands of Rohingya \u2060\u2060civilians, perpetrated widespread acts \u2060\u2060of sexual violence as well as acts of \u2060\u2060extreme violence against children and \u2060\u2060attacked fleeing Rohingya \u2060\u2060as they sought to flee in large numbers to \u200c\u200cBangladesh,\u201d he added.\n\nIn specific cases that he referred to, he said Myanmar had acted with \u201cgenocidal intent\u201d."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
