    "chunk_text": "From humble beginnings as a Junior Banker, Dr. Mendis rose through the ranks to Assistant General Manager, Corporate Planning and Business Development and Leasing in the banking industry. He has also worked at ANZ Bank, New Zealand, a Fortune 500 company, and was a Member of the Strategic Planning Committee at ANZ Bank for the North Shore Region of Auckland, New Zealand. He made a paradigm shift from banking to the consultancy and academic arena in 2008 and became the Chief Executive Officer of a private university in Sri Lanka.\n\nBeing a Distinguished Life Alumnus of PIM and Massey University, New Zealand, with several Unique Selling Propositions and distinctive competences, he currently focuses on incomparable specialised arenas, namely Strategic Affairs, International Business, Corporate Governance, Re-engineering of Companies, Banking, Policy Formulation, Tertiary Education, AML, Data-driven Decision Making and Geopolitics, as a Consultant and an Advisor. He has evaluated more than 1,000 balance sheets across the world in his career.\n\nDr. Mendis is an AIB qualified banker, with a Postgraduate Diploma in Financial Management from the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka. His first Master\u2019s Degree is from the Postgraduate Institute of Management, University of Sri Jayewardenepura. His second Master\u2019s Degree (MSc in Management) is from the prestigious Massey University in Auckland, New Zealand, and his Doctorate on Corporate Governance is from the University of Kelaniya."
  },
