    "md5": "aac932d3404ed4f65f03932d28c9af5b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "National policy framework for data centres and cloud infrastructure taking shape\n\nBOI and the Ministry of Digital Economy convene national stakeholder consultation to discuss the investment terms, with proposed data centre capacity targets of 25 MW by 2027 and 50 MW by 2028\n\nThe Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI), together with the Ministry of Digital Economy (MoDE) and GovTech Sri Lanka, has taken a decisive step towards establishing a national investment strategy for data centres, convening a National Stakeholder Consultation on the National Policy Framework for Data Centre and Cloud Infrastructure Investment on 6 November, 2026.\n\nCo-chaired by BOI Chairman Duminda Hulangamuwa and Chief Advisor to the President on Digital Economy Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, with the participation of BOI Director General Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena, the consultation brought together close to 40 senior representatives from the institutions that will underpin the sector. These included the Ministry of Energy, the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka, the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka, the National System Operator Ltd., Electricity Distribution Lanka Ltd., the National Transmission Network Service Provider Ltd., the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, the Central Environmental Authority and the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority.\n\nThe session marked the final stage of consensus-building on the core investment parameters for the sector, namely electricity tariffs, land and water allocations, connectivity requirements, access to renewable energy and fiscal incentives, while also confirming the readiness of zone infrastructure and the responsibilities of each institution."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
