    "md5": "76eb6d3230dc9bfa8bc13d6bb9a8d968",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1528,
    "chunk_text": "Speaking at the meeting, Committee Chair Rajapaksa noted the significant opportunities available within the sector and stressed the importance of collective action to unlock its full potential. Some members of the committee highlighted the need for continuous engagement with industry stakeholders to ensure that the Committee\u2019s recommendations translate into tangible outcomes.\n\nThe Committee also highlighted the opportunities presented by Sri Lanka Expo 2027, particularly in promoting marine-related investment opportunities, showcasing industry capabilities and connecting local businesses with international buyers and investors. Members were encouraged to identify potential buyers, investors and investment-ready marine-related projects for promotion at the event. The importance of aligning the Committee\u2019s activities with the National Export Development Plan (2026\u20132030) and strengthening coordination among relevant government institutions was also emphasised.\n\nThe inaugural meeting concluded with a shared commitment to translate the discussions and recommendations into practical initiatives, with an emphasis on measurable outcomes, effective implementation and collaborative actions among industry stakeholders and government institutions.\n\nThe establishment of the Marine-Based Services Advisory Committee marks an important step towards strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s blue economy and leveraging the country\u2019s strategic maritime location to generate sustainable economic growth and export-led development."
