    "description": "Govt. to evaluate BOI, SDP and Port City tax incentives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Govt-to-evaluate-BOI-SDP-and-Port-City-tax-incentives/34-800339",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1795128906.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-20-dailyftlk-92f241ba-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ad321ea241864ab47c562d3c3049eedd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1952,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. to evaluate BOI, SDP and Port City tax incentives\n\nBOI non-SDP exemptions rise to Rs. 53 b from nil a year earlier\n\nBOI firms get Rs. 28 b in VAT relief and Rs. 16 b in SSCL relief in 2025\n\nCustoms relief for Port City duty-free shop jumps to Rs. 757 m from Rs. 46 m\n\nNew laws set time limits for granting SDP and Port City incentives\n\nThe Government has begun cost-benefit reviews of tax incentives granted to Board of Investment (BOI) Strategic Development Projects (SDPs) and Colombo Port City businesses, as Corporate Income Tax (CIT) reliefs for BOI enterprises climbed 54% in 2024/25.\n\nAccording to the Finance Ministry\u2019s Tax Expenditure Statement 2025/2026 released on 12 November 2026, CIT reliefs for BOI companies rose to Rs. 65 billion in 2024/25 from Rs. 42 billion in 2023/24. Exemptions for non-SDP BOI companies, which were nil the previous year, amounted to Rs. 53 billion. Concessionary rates for these companies fell to Rs. 11.5 billion from Rs. 41.7 billion.\n\nSDPs accounted for Rs. 84 million in concessionary-rate CIT relief in 2024/25, compared with Rs. 123 million in exemptions the previous year. Port City projects received no CIT relief in 2024/25, after Rs. 143 million in exemptions in 2023/24.\n\nBOI companies also received Rs. 28.1 billion in Value Added Tax (VAT) relief and Rs. 15.8 billion in Social Security Contribution Levy (SSCL) relief in 2025, a combined Rs. 43.9 billion. In the first half of 2026 they received Rs. 18.9 billion in VAT relief and Rs. 10.1 billion in SSCL relief. Other manufacturing activities led BOI VAT reliefs in 2025 at Rs. 15.7 billion, followed by wholesale and retail at Rs. 9.3 billion. Textiles and garments led BOI SSCL reliefs at Rs. 5.9 billion.\n\nSDPs received Rs. 286 million in VAT relief in 2025, almost all of it in tourism, and Rs. 93 million in SSCL relief. Port City projects received Rs. 11 million in SSCL relief in 2025 and Rs. 13 million in the first half of 2026."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
