    "md5": "36353eab2ce3ec9610212cbb4f6a6b63",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 973,
    "chunk_text": "A financially unsavvy CEO is like Columbus sailing without a compass\n\nIt is a quiet, disheartening tragedy to watch Chief Executive Officers (CEOs), even at large, powerful organisations, freeze when faced with basic finance and accounting questions. They often retreat behind the reflexive, rehearsed refrain: \u201cI\u2019ll have to check with my Chief Financial Officer (CFO and get back to you.\u201d Whilst it is disturbing to witness such slavish reliance on the CFO to respond to basic queries, it reveals a glaring void in foundational financial literacy where it ought to be. Seeing someone hold absolute strategic authority while lacking a basic grasp of his/her own balance sheet, cash flows, profitability indicators, et cetera, exposes an uncomfortable reality. It is essential that a CEO is in intimate touch with the core of the business. Running a multi-billion-rupee enterprise on pure vibes and financial blindness is not just dismal; it is the gateway to failure."
  },
