    "chunk_text": "A primary responsibility of executive leadership is determining where capital should be deployed. Evaluating strategic growth initiatives, whether internal research and development, physical expansion, or corporate acquisitions, requires a firm grasp of discounted cash flow mechanics.\n\nSustaining profitability requires an understanding of how fixed overhead and variable costs interact under changing market conditions. Fixed costs represent overhead expenses that remain constant regardless of output volume, such as facilities leases and administrative salaries. Variable costs fluctuate directly with production levels, including raw materials, direct labor, and shipping. Identifying the break-even point establishes the precise sales volume needed to cover these combined costs, setting a baseline target for commercial strategy. In mature, capital-intensive sectors, cost control dictates survival. Ceylon Cold Stores (Elephant House) consistently applied this structural discipline in determining pricing of carbonated soft drinks in the face of powerful international and local competition."
