    "chunk_text": "Sustaining profitability requires an understanding of how fixed overhead and variable costs interact under changing market conditions. Fixed costs represent overhead expenses that remain constant regardless of output volume, such as facilities leases and administrative salaries. Variable costs fluctuate directly with production levels, including raw materials, direct labor, and shipping. Identifying the break-even point establishes the precise sales volume needed to cover these combined costs, setting a baseline target for commercial strategy. In mature, capital-intensive sectors, cost control dictates survival. Ceylon Cold Stores (Elephant House) consistently applied this structural discipline in determining pricing of carbonated soft drinks in the face of powerful international and local competition.\n\nCEOs are responsible for protecting corporate assets and maintaining the integrity of public reporting. This requires monitoring operational, market, and credit risks while establishing strict internal controls to prevent accounting errors or fraudulent activity. The collapse of Wirecard remains a cautionary example of failed governance. Under Markus Braun, aggressive off-balance-sheet misdirection and a total breakdown of internal controls obscured 1.9 billion euros in non-existent cash reserves, leading to complete insolvency and regulatory ruin."
