    "chunk_text": "The poorest 40% of Sri Lankans live with an average household income of Rs. 36,564. On the other hand, the official poverty line was Rs. 16,417 per person per month and an average household of 3-4 people would need Rs. 55-65,000 per month to meet their basic needs. This means that at least 40% of Sri Lankan households do not earn sufficiently to be above the poverty line.\n\nAll in all, this Budget lacks the decisiveness to address the many ills that plague our country; from underperforming State-owned entities to poverty and food insecurity. Although the President spoke a lot about economic, social and structural transformation, this Budget fails to embody it.\u00a0 What Sri Lanka really needs is a Government that is bold enough to push the envelope \u2013 to upset the apple cart. Otherwise, we risk sliding back into our old ways.\n\n(The author is an Economist and Co-Founder/Director of Arutha, an economic research and civic education organisation)"
