    "chunk_size_bytes": 1994,
    "chunk_text": "As Fiona put on weight and her health improved, the zoo\u2019s social media team began putting pictures and videos of the baby hippo online to let people follow her journey. The #TeamFiona hashtag began filling up social media with official updates from the zoo and requests and well wishes from fans all over the world.\n\nThe sporadic updates became daily as Fiona\u2019s fandom grew. Videos shared on social media showing keepers reading Fiona some of her fan mail or of her falling asleep in the shower went viral.\n\nThe hippopotamus drew thousands of people from around the world to the zoo, with travelers from as far away as Australia, Germany, Brazil and Japan visiting Cincinnati, Ohio, to see the globally adored ungulate.\n\nAt 9 years old, Fiona\u2019s death was considered early for a common hippopotamus, whose lifespan in captivity usually ranges from about 40 to 50 years, according to Flacke.\n\nIt is not the Cincinnati Zoo\u2019s first time experiencing the death of an animal celebrity. Harambe, a 17-year-old western lowland gorilla, was killed there in 2016 in an attempt by the zoo to save a boy who slipped into the animal\u2019s enclosure. The internet erupted with outrage and cries of \u201cjustice for Harambe\u201d after the incident.\n\nFiona\u2019s tragic death has sparked a similar outpouring of grief across social media, uniting everyone from Cincinnati sports teams to city and state lawmakers.\n\n\u201cFiona was a symbol of perseverance and joy\u201d in the city, said Cincinnati Mayor Aftab Pureval in a Thursday afternoon X post.\n\nOhio Gov. Mike DeWine and Gov.-elect Amy Acton offered similar sentiments, with Acton calling the hippo \u201cone of Cincinnati\u2019s most beloved icons.\u201d\n\nThe community left pink and white flower bouquets and cards honoring Fiona leaning against a statue of the beloved hippo and her mother outside the zoo, video from CNN affiliate WKRC shows. A card \u2014 with a drawing of Fiona, a heart and childlike handwriting \u2014 read, \u201cHope that you get well soon friend.\u201d"
