    "md5": "cadd938e87a21b88560ed8e8441954aa",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2016,
    "chunk_text": "Haiti police operation kills 34 suspected gang members in capital\n\nReuters\u00a0- A police operation in Haiti killed at least 34 alleged gang members on Thursday, the force said after a major \u200boperation in the south of Port-au-Prince against armed gangs that have taken over \u200cmuch of the capital and surrounding regions.\n\nHaiti's national police said that neither police officers nor civilians were hurt during the operation in Martissant, a residential area of the city, whose wider metropolitan \u200barea is home to about 3 million people.\n\nSecurity operations against heavily-armed gangs \u200bhave escalated in Haiti since the deployment of Salvadoran troops last month.\n\nAuthorities \u2060have not disclosed overall casualties but the UN estimates that over 2,250 people \u200bhave been killed during security operations in the first nine months of this year, \u200bincluding more than 300 civilians.\n\nHaitian police published a video on social media in which a building can be seen collapsing under a large cloud of smoke.\n\nReuters verified that the video released by \u200bHaitian police was filmed in Martissant, based on road layouts, buildings and greenery that \u200bmatched satellite imagery of the area.\n\nThe southwestern area of Martissant is under the influence of the \u200cGran \u2060Ravine, Ti Bwa and 5 Segond gangs, according to security analysts. They are all members of a broad alliance known as Viv Ansanm, designated a terrorist organization by Washington.\n\nPolice said the operation was run alongside the government's Task Force, a group which runs \u200boperations using explosive drones \u200bwith the support \u2060of a private military contractor run by Blackwater founder Erik Prince.\n\nPolice said no Salvadoran personnel took part in the operation. El Salvador's government \u200bdid not immediately reply to a request for comment.\n\nSalvadoran President Nayib \u200bBukele has \u2060published videos of dramatic security strikes since he deployed 2,000 troops after four members of a UN-backed mission went missing on October 18."
