    "md5": "0181328e39606432faeb429d77ac95c1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "A little girl on a bed, four lives lost; Firefighters recount Kaduwela tragedy\n\nColombo, Nov. 20 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0\u201cWe tried to break a window on the upper floor to get inside. The entire floor was filled with thick smoke. Then, through the smoke, we spotted a small child lying on a bed. Our officers were heartbroken,\u201d recalled D.S. Jayalal, team leader of the Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte Municipal Council Fire Brigade.\n\nWhat began as an early morning fire at an electrical appliance showroom turned into a devastating tragedy, claiming the lives of four members of a family who were living on the upper floor of the building.\n\nThe victims were identified as Narada Sandaruwan (35), his wife Nilakshika Madhushani (28), and their two daughters, Dineli Hasanya (5) and Oneli Hasanya (2), residents of Dutugemunu Mawatha, Thalangama North.\n\nThe bodies of the four victims were found on two beds on the upper floor by firefighters, who managed to reach them only after bringing the flames under control.\n\nThe tragedy came to light at around 5.30 a.m. yesterday (19), when an employee at the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation filling station opposite the building noticed smoke rising from the upper floor.\n\n\u201cI was working at the filling station when I noticed smoke coming from the upper floor of the building opposite. When I went closer, I could see what appeared to be a fire inside. The smoke kept getting heavier, so we immediately informed the officers at the nearby Kaduwela Police Post,\u201d the employee said.\n\nThe Kotte Municipal Council Fire Brigade received the alert at around 6.20 a.m. and rushed to the scene.\n\n\u201cWe reached the location within about half an hour. By then, the ground floor was already engulfed in flames, and the fire was spreading,\u201d Jayalal said.\n\nTwo fire engines were initially dispatched, but another was called in after firefighters learnt that four people could be trapped inside."
