    "chunk_text": "The parents had been working at the electrical appliance showroom and had moved into the upper floor of the building about three months earlier, police said.\n\nBut the building's layout and lack of emergency exits had made the rescue operation extremely difficult.\n\n\u201cEven our officers found it extremely difficult to get inside, despite wearing protective clothing. Their equipment kept getting caught in the obstructions. It appeared that little attention had been paid to basic safety arrangements,\u201d he said.\n\nThe building had only one staircase providing access, while another entrance had been locked with padlocks. There was no alternative exit at the rear.\n\n\u201cThe lack of basic safety arrangements may have cost these four people their lives. Every building where people live should have an alternative exit for emergencies. This building had no such safety provisions and was in an extremely unsafe condition,\u201d Jayalal said."
