    "md5": "591bc223a6efe66d9ac79e50cce6a7ae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1598,
    "chunk_text": "Historic Shenzhen summit as world teeters between  war and peace\n\nPutin, Xi and Trump ahead of their historic meeting in China\u2019s tech capital, Shenzhen\n\nInternational relations are so interconnected today that it is increasingly difficult to analyse developments in one country without referring to developments in other parts of the world, regardless of distance or significance.\n\nThe world appears to be a political island when the dots are connected. Yesterday, history was made as the world\u2019s three most powerful leaders, from China, Russia and the United States, held the first-ever trilateral talks on the sidelines of the APEC (Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation) summit in Shenzhen, China\u2019s technology capital. Needless to say, numerous global crises were on the agenda. According to media reports, topics such as nuclear disarmament, the wars in Iran and Ukraine, China\u2019s dominance in the rare-earth trade, and the United States\u2019 lead in artificial intelligence chip manufacturing were discussed.\n\nSadly, issues such as global warming, development assistance and international cooperation aimed at restoring respect for international law were reportedly absent from the agenda.\n\nIf the trilateral talks were to become a regular fixture, they would have the potential to usher in a new balance of power. But this depends on the sense and sensibility of the three leaders. A leader with sense makes sound decisions based on facts. A leader with sensibility understands the human consequences of those decisions. Someone who possesses both demonstrates wisdom tempered by compassion."
  },
