    "md5": "3b79a81364ef8684f73bd6344c7d21bc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1470,
    "chunk_text": "If the trilateral talks were to become a regular fixture, they would have the potential to usher in a new balance of power. But this depends on the sense and sensibility of the three leaders. A leader with sense makes sound decisions based on facts. A leader with sensibility understands the human consequences of those decisions. Someone who possesses both demonstrates wisdom tempered by compassion.\n\nHowever, he could display no such arrogance at yesterday\u2019s meeting with Xi and Putin in the Chinese city of Shenzhen. If the three leaders were to meet annually under a G3 framework, as G7 leaders do, it could become a valuable platform for addressing mutual concerns and fears, provided it does not evolve into a forum for deciding the fate of humanity, as the elusive or illusory Illuminati are sometimes said to do. Such concerns have already been voiced by the beleaguered Ukrainian leader, Volodymyr Zelensky. Adding to his concerns, Trump greeted Putin, Zelensky\u2019s b\u00eate noire, with a handshake, saying, \u201cHe is my friend.\u201d The chemistry among Putin, Trump and Xi appeared to be at its strongest during the Shenzhen meeting.\n\nAs the trilateral talks commenced yesterday, Xi described them as being of \u201cgroundbreaking significance\u201d, while Trump said the leaders were \u201creally making history\u201d. Meanwhile, Putin stated that Russia, China and the United States share a \u201cjoint responsibility\u201d for \u201cmaintaining international peace and security\u201d."
  },
