    "chunk_text": "Although Sri Lanka is not a member of the APEC forum, the decisions taken by the grouping have a bearing on the country, as it falls within the Asia-Pacific region both geographically and geopolitically. The Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (Quad) meeting that Trump attended in Manila during the US-ASEAN Summit, together with the leaders of Australia, India and Japan, may signal that Washington, after a period of apparent indifference to the Quad, is once again seeking to counter China\u2019s growing political influence in the Asia-Pacific region.\n\nOn the other hand, serious cybersecurity concerns have arisen in the United States over technology outages affecting the aviation sector, banks, email systems, software services and internal communications at the National Security Agency, coming on the heels of Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang\u2019s sex scandal allegedly linked to Chinese espionage.\n\nAdding to these concerns were claims in the US media that Iran was preparing to attack the US capital with a crude nuclear bomb. Iran has denied the allegation, while Iranian analysts have dismissed the report as a subterfuge or part of a false-flag operation devised by US and Israeli intelligence agencies to rally support for the war with Iran after the US electorate delivered a strong anti-war message in the midterm elections. Trump now claims that Iran is planning to use biological weapons against Americans."
