    "md5": "605ffeac798ab06e66b920050266bec2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1486,
    "chunk_text": "Financial turnaround, growth earn Nawaloka Hospitals\u2019 CFOs top national accolades\n\nNawaloka Hospitals PLC is celebrating a dual triumph in financial leadership, with its Group Chief Financial Officer Theja Vimuktha De Silva and Chief Financial Officer Sampath Thennakoon securing top national honours at prestigious industry awards in 2026.\n\nDe Silva was named as Best CFO of the Year 2026 at the CA Sri Lanka Best CFO Awards, organised by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka.\n\nDe Silva said, \u201cThis recognition is a testament to the collective resilience, discipline and vision of our entire team at Nawaloka Hospitals. Moving from a challenging financial period to sustainable profitability and double-digit growth demonstrates that strategic financial leadership goes beyond numbers\u2014 it is about empowering teams, strengthening governance and ensuring that our financial stability directly translates into superior patient care and long-term shareholder value. I am deeply grateful to our Chairman Dr. H.K. Jayantha Dharmadasa, Deputy Chairperson Anisha Dharmadasa, the board and our dedicated finance team for their support.\u201d\n\nMeanwhile, Thennakoon achieved a remarkable Triple Gold victory at CPM Sri Lanka Management Leadership Excellence Awards 2026, receiving Gold for Executive Decision Maker Leadership (Private Western Medicine Hospitals), Demonstrating Visionary Leadership Competency and the Overall Gold Award in Executive Decision Maker Leadership."
  },
