    "chunk_size_bytes": 1391,
    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, Thennakoon achieved a remarkable Triple Gold victory at CPM Sri Lanka Management Leadership Excellence Awards 2026, receiving Gold for Executive Decision Maker Leadership (Private Western Medicine Hospitals), Demonstrating Visionary Leadership Competency and the Overall Gold Award in Executive Decision Maker Leadership.\n\nThese accolades recognise the transformative financial leadership behind Nawaloka Hospitals\u2019 robust recovery, corporate governance and growth trajectory. Following a loss of Rs.305 million in FY23/24, the Nawaloka group returned to profitability with Rs.56 million in FY24/25.\n\nBuilding on this momentum, the group revenue expanded by 20.3 percent to Rs.13.24 billion in FY2025/26, with reported profit after tax reaching Rs.1.05 billion.\n\nReflecting the heightened market confidence, Nawaloka Hospitals\u2019 market capitalisation doubled from Rs.7.47 billion to Rs.14.94 billion during FY25/26. The share price surged from Rs.5.30 to Rs.10.60, hitting a peak of Rs.15.20 during the financial year. This value creation was underpinned by strategic debt restructuring, improved liquidity and rigorous capital allocation.\n\nComplementing the financial resilience, the group reinvested approximately Rs.1.54 billion into advanced medical equipment, including cutting-edge AI-powered radiology, reinforcing its commitment to clinical excellence and patient care."
