    "chunk_text": "Underworld figure \u2018Rotumba Amila\u2019 brought back to Sri Lanka from Russia\n\nColombo, Nov. 20 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Sepala Ratnayake Amila Sampath, alias \u2018Rotumba Amila\u2019, an alleged organised crime figure and international drug trafficker who had been hiding in Russia, was brought back to Sri Lanka this morning (20) by the Criminal Investigation Department (CID).\n\nThe 44-year-old suspect, a resident of Urubokka in Matara, arrived at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) in Katunayake on a flight from Moscow after being apprehended in Russia by CID officers.\n\nInvestigations have revealed that the suspect maintained close links with notorious underworld figures \u2018Angoda Lokka\u2019 and \u2018Makandure Madush\u2019. He has also been linked to the assassination of businessman Surendra Wasantha Perera, popularly known as \u2018Club Wasantha\u2019, on July 8, 2024, and a murder committed in the Mulleriyawa area on April 29, 2016.\n\nRotumba Amila was previously arrested in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on March 28, 2019, during a birthday party hosted by Makandure Madush. He was subsequently deported to Sri Lanka.\n\nHowever, after being released on bail on May 3, 2023, he fled the country and travelled to Russia. Interpol Red Notices were subsequently obtained through several Sri Lankan courts in connection with his arrest.\n\nCID officers took the suspect into custody upon his arrival at Katunayake Airport this morning. After recording his statement at the airport, he is due to be escorted under tight security to the CID Headquarters in Colombo for further investigations."
