    "chunk_size_bytes": 1937,
    "chunk_text": "Emirates tops TIME\u2019s inaugural World\u2019s Best Airlines 2027 rankings\n\nEmirates has been ranked the World\u2019s Best Airline in TIME and Statista\u2019s inaugural World\u2019s Best Airlines 2027 list, which recognises airlines around the world that excel in customer service and operational performance.\n\nThe airline also took first place in the Best Value and Business Travel categories, alongside high recognition in several other categories.\n\nEmirates Airline President Sir Tim Clark said, \u201cUndeterred by the challenges of this year, we continue to invest in product and service across almost every touchpoint. We will maintain that focus because, as this top ranking in TIME shows, customers notice when an airline gets the fundamentals right. A big credit goes to our people who bring the Emirates experience to life in the air and on the ground. Their professionalism and commitment are what our customers experience every day. In our business, there\u2019s no finish line and we\u2019re already working towards an even stronger 2027 and beyond, so you can expect more from Emirates.\u201d\n\nAccording to TIME, Emirates\u2019 rankings reflect its reputation for some of the industry\u2019s most luxurious flying, its expanding Premium Economy offering and Dubai\u2019s enduring appeal as a destination. Partnerships with tourism organisations across the Indian Ocean, Europe, Southeast Asia and the UAE also help attract more visitors across its network.\n\nStatista R Deputy CEO Niels Terfehr said, \u201cEmirates\u2019 results this year stand out for their consistency. Topping the overall World\u2019s Best Airlines ranking, while also leading the Best Value and Business Travel categories, reflects strong performance across both passenger experience and operational reliability - the two pillars our ranking is built on. It\u2019s a result grounded entirely in direct feedback from travellers around the world, combined with independent flight-performance data.\u201d"
  },
