    "md5": "397ff336c6f11828b20a7ca4d17ce554",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "NSBM featured in ACU report as a successful higher education financing model\n\nNSBM Green University has been featured as a successful model of higher education financing in a publication by the Association of Commonwealth Universities (ACU), titled \u2018Alternative Higher Education Financing: Global Trends and Commonwealth Policy Insights\u2019.\n\nThe publication examines sustainable approaches to financing higher education across the Commonwealth, highlighting NSBM as a case study of a successful self-financing higher education institution.\n\nIt explores how the university\u2019s self-financing model, coupled with international university partnerships, has contributed to institutional sustainability, expanded access to higher education and supported national development.\n\nA key policy insight highlighted in the case study is the importance of providing internationally recognised qualifications locally, particularly in countries experiencing significant outbound student mobility. It notes that such approaches, when supported by effective quality assurance frameworks, can strengthen domestic higher education capacity, reduce educational outflows, retain talent within the country and contribute to economic development.\n\nEstablished with the objective of broadening access to quality higher education in Sri Lanka, NSBM has developed into one of the country\u2019s prominent higher education institutions over the past decade. Operating as a fully self-financing institution without reliance on public funds, it has continued to invest in educational infrastructure, academic development and international university partnerships while expanding opportunities for Sri Lankan students to access internationally recognised qualifications within the country.\n\nThe recognition comes at an important juncture, as NSBM marked its 10th anniversary on October 26, 2026."
