    "md5": "7892387558d2c583f3995c9dd78b2d3c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1952,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Port City grants rule-based incentives with clear eligibility and approval framework\n\nA disciplined, criteria-driven system ensures incentives are earned through investment, performance and national economic impact\n\nColombo Port City operates under a defined, eligibility-based system for granting tax exemptions and investment incentives. The registration within the Special Economic Zone (SEZ) does not automatically entitle a business to incentives. Exemptions are granted only to designated Businesses of Strategic Importance (BSIs) that meet the prescribed criteria and follow the statutory approval process.\n\nThe tax incentives are used globally to attract investment, enhance competitiveness and stimulate economic activity. Their value to broader economic outcomes they generate, including employment, skills development, technology transfer, foreign exchange inflows and sustained business activity.\n\nThe BSI incentive framework has developed through successive regulations. Colombo Port City (Guidelines on the Grant of Exemptions or Incentives to Businesses of Strategic Importance) Regulations No. 1 of 2025 replaced the 2023 BSI regulations, which expired after a defined 24-month period. The 2025 BSI Regulations set out the current criteria, processes and conditions governing BSI designation and incentives.\n\nThe Colombo Port City Economic Commission (CPCEC) administers this framework, facilitating investment while ensuring compliance with applicable legislation and maintaining global competitiveness.\n\nOperating within the SEZ is distinct from qualifying for BSI designation; incentives require meeting the prescribed criteria and obtaining approval through the statutory process.\n\nColombo Port City spans 269 hectares of reclaimed land across 74 parcels designated for residential, commercial, hospitality and leisure uses. Approximately US $ 1.4 billion has been invested in land reclamation and horizontal infrastructure."
  },
