    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bc2bf1f44fff639a0dd0f18268d3894a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1740,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Lands Residencies delivers higher revenue growth and profitability in 1H FY2026/27\n\nPrime Lands Residencies PLC delivered impressive financial results for the six-month period ended 30th September 2026, with revenue rising 48 percent to Rs. 7.60 billion from Rs. 5.15 billion in the corresponding period of the previous financial year.\n\nFurthermore, profit for the period increased 10 percent to Rs. 1.03 billion, compared to Rs. 940.7 million a year earlier, reflecting continued revenue growth and an expansion in gross and operating profits. Gross profit improved 31 percent to Rs. 2.11 billion, while operating profit rose 33 percent to Rs. 1.47 billion, demonstrating the company\u2019s ability to sustain growth at the operating level.\n\nProfit before taxation increased by 9 percent to Rs. 1.41 billion, while earnings per share improved to Rs. 1.10 from Rs. 1.00.\n\nPrime Residencies PLC Executive Chairperson Sandamini Perera added, \u201cThe notable percent growth in revenue demonstrates the strength of our business performance during the period under review. Improvements in gross and operating profits provide a solid foundation for the remainder of the financial year. Our focus remains on translating revenue growth into stronger earnings and maintaining the financial capacity to support the company\u2019s continuing business objectives.\u201d\n\nThe robust 1H results for FY2026/27 position Prime Lands Residencies on a positive earnings trajectory for the 2026/27 financial year. With revenue, gross profit and operating profit all recording year-on-year growth, the company plans to sustain and improve on its operational performance, cost management and financial discipline as it progresses through the second half of the year."
  },
