    "md5": "b1102af4a2c39bf5b1eae0d56558084b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1742,
    "chunk_text": "Australian High Commissioner highlights bilateral ties in Colombo\n\nAustralian High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Matthew Duckworth briefed senior editorial staff from leading Sri Lankan media institutions recently on Australia\u2019s diplomatic mission and strategic bilateral initiatives in the country.\n\nThe media briefing, held in Colombo, was organized by the OzLanka Journalists\u2019 Consortium in collaboration with Australia\u2019s Market Development Facility (MDF).\n\nDuring the session, High Commissioner Duckworth held a productive discussion covering Australian investments, development partnerships, and Australia\u2019s broader contributions to Sri Lanka\u2019s economic growth.\n\nAddressing the gathering, the High Commissioner emphasized the strength of the relationship between the two nations ahead of a major diplomatic milestone next year.\n\n\u201cAustralia deeply values our longstanding partnership with Sri Lanka, and it is significant to note that next year marks 80 years of our bilateral relations,\u201d Duckworth said. \u201cWe take this very seriously and look forward to telling this story more broadly next year.\n\nAs neighbours in this region, we recognize each other as long-term partners and friends, and we want to continue supporting and building upon these ties.\u201d\n\nHighlighting the development aspect of the bilateral partnership, Market Development Facility (MDF) Sri Lanka\u2019s, Country Director Maryam Piracha outlined the Australian government-funded initiative\u2019s core mission in the country.\n\nOperating in Sri Lanka since 2015, MDF focuses on promoting sustainable, inclusive economic growth by co-investing with private sector businesses in high-value, export-oriented sectors such as tourism, specialty coffee, and agriculture."
