    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b833ca620f3127a6bcebb1e05bd0cab3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1637,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank becomes only SL institution among Asia-Pacific\u2019s top debit card issuers\n\nCommercial Bank of Ceylon has become the only Sri Lankan institution to be ranked by The Nilson Report.\n\nThe Bank secured a top 50 position among the largest debit card issuers in the Asia-Pacific region based on debit card spend volumes in 2025, in the latest edition of the Nilson Report.This milestone builds on Commercial Bank\u2019s longstanding position as Sri Lanka\u2019s undisputed market leader in cumulative debit card spend, commanding the country\u2019s highest active card usage.\n\nThe achievement also represents an important endorsement of the Bank\u2019s leadership in Sri Lanka\u2019s payment industry and the success of its strategy to accelerate the adoption of digital payments, while placing Sri Lanka\u2019s growing participation in the global digital payments landscape firmly on the regional map.\n\nCommenting on the significance of the recognition, Sanath Manatunge, Managing Director/CEO of Commercial Bank said, \u201cThis achievement carries special meaning because it demonstrates that Sri Lanka can compete on the strength of its digital payment capabilities, in a region led by some of the world\u2019s largest economies and banking institutions. It is a testament to the confidence our customers place in Commercial Bank, the progress we have made in advancing digital payments and our commitment to making modern payment experiences accessible, secure and rewarding. More importantly, it represents a milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s payment industry, showing that our country\u2019s digital payment ecosystem can make its mark well beyond our shores.\u201d"
  },
