    "chunk_text": "Advisory Committee on Marine-Based Industries holds inaugural meeting to drive industry growth\n\nThe inaugural meeting of the Advisory Committee on Marine-Based Industries was held on 16 November at the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), bringing together key public and private sector stakeholders to discuss strategic priorities, industry challenges and emerging opportunities for the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s marine-based industries.\n\nThe meeting was attended by the Chairman of the Export Development Board, the Director General, and the Additional Director General (Development), underscoring the importance placed on the sector as a key component of Sri Lanka\u2019s export diversification and economic growth agenda.\n\nDuring the meeting, Kaushal Rajapaksha was appointed\u00a0 Chairman of the Marine-Based Services Advisory Committee, while Ricky Barnett was appointed as Co-Chairman.\n\nThe EDB Chairman delivered the main presentation, outlining the current status of the sector, emerging global opportunities, and the strategic priorities required to position Sri Lanka as a competitive regional hub for marine-based services. The presentation highlighted the sector\u2019s growth potential and the need for coordinated efforts to enhance value addition, innovation, skills development, and international market access. The Committee also discussed opportunities to strengthen marine infrastructure and tourism-related activities, including the development of marinas, sheltered anchorages, breakwaters, boatyards and other marine tourism facilities. The potential to develop existing harbors, including Galle and other coastal locations, as marine tourism and boating hubs was highlighted."
