    "chunk_text": "The EDB Chairman delivered the main presentation, outlining the current status of the sector, emerging global opportunities, and the strategic priorities required to position Sri Lanka as a competitive regional hub for marine-based services. The presentation highlighted the sector\u2019s growth potential and the need for coordinated efforts to enhance value addition, innovation, skills development, and international market access. The Committee also discussed opportunities to strengthen marine infrastructure and tourism-related activities, including the development of marinas, sheltered anchorages, breakwaters, boatyards and other marine tourism facilities. The potential to develop existing harbors, including Galle and other coastal locations, as marine tourism and boating hubs was highlighted.\n\nSpeaking at the meeting, Chairman Rajapaksha noted the significant opportunities available within the sector and stressed the importance of collective action to unlock its full potential.\n\nTo facilitate focused discussions and effective implementation of proposed initiatives, the establishment of specialized subcommittees covering Boat Building and Manufacturing, Shipbuilding and Ship Repair, Regulatory Affairs, Training and Skills Development, Marketing and Export Promotion, Nautical and Marine Tourism, and Offshore Services was discussed.\n\nThe Committee also highlighted the opportunities presented by Sri Lanka Expo 2027, particularly in promoting marine-related investment opportunities, showcasing industry capabilities and connecting local businesses with international buyers and investors.\n\nThe establishment of the Marine-Based Services Advisory Committee marks an important step towards strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s blue economy and leveraging the country\u2019s strategic maritime location to generate sustainable economic growth and export-led development."
