    "chunk_size_bytes": 1870,
    "chunk_text": "Restored Golden Canopy of Sri Dalada Maligawa unveiled\n\nThe newly restored Golden Canopy (Ran Viyana) of the historic Sri Dalada Maligawa (Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic) in Kandy was unveiled today (20).\n\nRestoration work on the iconic canopy\u2014which shelters the two-storey inner shrine built in 1592 AD by King Vimaladharmasuriya I housing the Left Sacred Tooth Relic of Gautama Buddha\u2014commenced in 2025. Over time, the gold leaf plating had tarnished and worn away, diminishing its original luster and grandeur.\n\nOriginally constructed and offered to the Temple in 1987 by then-Prime Minister late Ranasinghe Premadasa to enhance the beauty and security of the shrine's interior and frontage, the canopy was initially designed by the State Engineering Corporation under the leadership of Engineer Gemunu Silva, alongside local and foreign engineering teams. Prior to the current project, the canopy underwent restorations twice, in 2002 and 2018.\n\nToday's unveiling ceremony was attended by the Most Venerable Mahanayake Thero of the Asgiriya Chapter, venerable members of the Maha Sangha of both the Malwathu and Asgiriya Chapters, a Thai delegation led by the revered meditation master Most Venerable Luang Por Anan Aki\u00f1cano of Wat Marp Jan in Thailand, Diyawadana Nilame Pradeep Nilanga Dela, and other distinguished guests.\n\nCarried out under the advice of the Mahanayake Theros of the Malwathu and Asgiriya Chapters, the guidance of the Diyawadana Nilame, and the full sponsorship of the Vishwa Parami Foundation, the 2,900-square-foot surface of the Golden Canopy was restored using durable 24-karat gold mosaic technology. The project incorporated technical consultations, designs, and recommendations from a renowned Italian company, alongside advisory support from leading international engineering firms and contributions from several local companies."
