    "md5": "6235a673b457d318c8e44aee92d6fa8b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1997,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe believe the sovereign\u2019s credit profile improvement has reduced insurers\u2019 investment and liquidity risks, which are closely linked to those of the sovereign and domestic banks because insurers\u2019 investment portfolios are dominated by local-currency fixed-income government securities, corporate debt and deposits with financial institutions,\u201d Fitch said.\n\nFitch cited strong group profitability in upgrading HNB Life and its wholly owned general insurance subsidiary. HNB Life\u2019s gross written premiums grew by an average of 30 percent over 2023\u20132025, ahead of the industry\u2019s 19 percent. HNB General\u2019s risk-based capital ratio fell to 198 percent at end-June from 219 percent in 2024. Fitch expects HNB Life to provide capital support if needed.\n\nPeople\u2019s Insurance\u2019s annualised return on equity rose to 12 percent in the first half of 2026 from 6 percent in 2025, helped by tighter underwriting and better investment returns. Co-operative Insurance\u2019s annualised return on equity reached 6 percent in the first half, against a three-year average of 0.3 percent. Fitch also improved its assessment of Co-operative\u2019s corporate governance following measures to address earlier weaknesses.\n\nContinental swung to a Rs. 654 million net loss in 2025 from a Rs. 436 million profit a year earlier after higher medical claims pushed its combined ratio to 119 percent from 100 percent. The ratio eased to 113 percent in the first half of 2026, and Fitch said continued losses could weaken its capital position. Janashakthi PLC\u2019s proposed initial acquisition of an 81 percent stake from Melstacorp PLC remains subject to final regulatory approval.\n\nThe state-owned Construction Guarantee Fund recorded a recovery in core guarantee income in the first half as foreign-funded infrastructure projects lifted demand for bonds and guarantees. Fitch said investment income remained the main contributor to profitability and earnings were sensitive to the pace of project implementation."
