    "chunk_text": "2,100 cannabis plants seized in Monaragala forest reserve\n\nColombo, Nov. 20 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0A suspect has been arrested after 2,100 illegally cultivated cannabis plants, estimated to be worth around Rs. 1 million, were discovered during a raid in the Unakanda Forest Reserve in Monaragala.\n\nAccording to the Sri Lanka Army, the raid was carried out yesterday (19) by officers of the Monaragala Narcotics Unit, acting on information received from Army Intelligence.\n\nDuring the operation, authorities discovered 2,100 cannabis plants, each measuring approximately three feet in height.\n\nThe suspect was arrested at the scene, while all the cannabis plants were seized by the authorities."
