    "chunk_size_bytes": 1387,
    "chunk_text": "FBI team visits Sri Lanka for scam probe\n\nColombo, Nov. 20 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) and the US Department of Justice (DOJ) have conducted a weeklong visit to Sri Lanka to strengthen cooperation with local law enforcement authorities in investigating scam centres targeting Americans.\n\nThe visit, held from November 16 to 22, focused on advancing investigations into transnational scam networks and strengthening collaboration between US and Sri Lankan authorities.\n\nDuring the visit, FBI and DOJ personnel held discussions with the Attorney General\u2019s Department and the Sri Lanka Police, including the Computer Crimes Investigation Unit (CCID), Criminal Crime Investigation Bureau (CCIB) and Technical Aid Unit (TAU).\n\nThe discussions focused on investigative strategies, digital evidence training, and the extraction of evidence recovered during Sri Lanka Police raids, while also strengthening coordination against transnational scam networks.\n\nAccording to the US Embassy in Sri Lanka, two active scam centre investigations were reviewed during the engagement, while more than 80 electronic devices were examined for digital evidence.\n\nThe Embassy said Sri Lankan law enforcement authorities and their US counterparts would continue sharing information, pursuing investigative leads and working together to disrupt transnational criminal networks."
