    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "Poland says Russian missile hit its territory during attack on Ukraine\n\nFRANCE 24 - Warsaw on Friday said that at least one Russian missile hit southeast Poland during Moscow's overnight attack on Ukraine, adding that authorities were investigating three impact sites, with a drone and a possible second missile also suspected.\n\n\"There are three impact sites. In Nowy Lipowiec, we can already confirm it was a Kh-101 missile, in the second place there is also talk of a missile, in the third it was most likely a jet-powered drone,\" Poland's Defence Minister Wladyslaw Kosiniak-Kamysz said, according to Polish media.\n\n\"Nobody was hurt, we did not note any infrastructure destruction,\" he added.\n\nThe Russian embassy in Warsaw did \u200cnot immediately respond to an emailed request for comment.\n\nDrones have repeatedly strayed \u2060into the airspace of countries on NATO's eastern flank since Russia invaded Ukraine in February 2022, fuelling tension with the NATO military alliance and stoking fears \u200bthat the war could spread.\n\nFootage \u200cshared on social media from what appeared to be a security camera at a property in the nearby village \u200bof Chmielek showed an explosion in the distance.\n\nPolish Infrastructure Minister Dariusz Klimczak said on X that a traffic controller had heard a loud bang near railway premises in Rudnik \u200bnad Sanem, about 50 kilometres west of Nowy Lipowiec.\n\nHe said no visible \u200bdamage to the railway had been found but that an \u200binspection vehicle had been dispatched.\n\nKlimczak also said air traffic controllers had been evacuated at the airport in Rzeszow, the largest \u200bcity in southeastern Poland.\n\nPrime Minister Donald Tusk said he had received reports about security in the area and that there was currently no threat from the air.\n\nEuropean countries are worried that Russia's war in Ukraine could spill \u2060over Ukraine's border, and are seeking a place at talks on ending the conflict."
