    "md5": "81b8c7971430268979c6e792562a4077",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1826,
    "chunk_text": "Appeal Court sets 13-year jail term for Hindu Poosari over rape of war-displaced student\n\nColombo, Nov. 21 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Court of Appeal yesterday dismissed the appeal and affirmed the conviction of a Hindu temple priest (Poosari) who was found guilty of raping a 17-year-old war-displaced student staying at his residence in Mullaitivu in 2011.\n\nWhile upholding the conviction, the two-judge bench reduced his prison sentence from 17 years to 13 years of rigorous imprisonment.\n\nThe judgement was delivered by Justice Dr. Sumudu Premachandra, with Justice Amal Ranaraja, in an appeal filed by Nithiyananthan Mohan Raj against his conviction by the Vavuniya High Court.\n\nAccording to the judgement, the victim, a 17-year-old internally displaced person (IDP) living at a displaced camp, moved into the residence of the accused in August 2011 to attend G.C.E. Advanced Level classes.\n\nOn or about November 11, 2011, the accused forcibly had sexual intercourse with the teenager. Following an attempted second assault the next day, the accused threatened her, warning that her life would be in danger if she told anyone.\n\nThe crime only came to light six months later when camp health workers noticed she was pregnant. A subsequent medical examination confirmed her six-month pregnancy, prompting a formal police complaint and the arrest of the accused. DNA testing later established that the accused was the biological father of the child. During her pregnancy, the victim was cared for at a convent, and the child was placed for adoption following birth.\n\nThe High Court acquitted the accused of the attempted rape charge due to insufficient evidence of a separate attempt, but convicted him of rape, sentencing him to 17 years of rigorous imprisonment, a Rs. 5,000 fine, and Rs. 300,000 in compensation to the victim."
  },
