    "chunk_text": "The High Court acquitted the accused of the attempted rape charge due to insufficient evidence of a separate attempt, but convicted him of rape, sentencing him to 17 years of rigorous imprisonment, a Rs. 5,000 fine, and Rs. 300,000 in compensation to the victim.\n\nAlthough the Court affirmed the conviction, noting that the rape of a girl under 18 carries a mandatory minimum sentence of 10 years and up to 20 years under Section 364(2) of the Penal Code, the bench took into account that the appellant is a first-time offender and a father of five children.\n\nConsequently, the Court reduced his sentence from 17 years to 13 years of rigorous imprisonment, effective from the date of his conviction, while leaving the Rs. 5,000 fine, the Rs. 300,000 victim compensation order, and default prison terms intact."
