    "chunk_text": "He said the practice is monitored more closely in urban areas and that plastic waste burning had declined over the years, although it continues to occur. He pointed to limitations in local authority waste collection services, including inadequate staffing and outdated or insufficient vehicles, affecting the ability to collect waste effectively. Enforcement is further hampered by the limited availability of Environmental Police personnel, making it difficult to take action against those violating the regulations.\n\nAs part of efforts to improve plastic waste management, the Ministry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government has introduced a Material Recovery Facility (MRF) plan covering the 2025\u20132027 period. The initiative aims to bring polythene and plastic waste to designated facilities for separation and recycling, reducing the amount released into the environment, as means of a more systematic way of managing waste disposal and discouraging burning as a disposal method."
