    "chunk_text": "2027 Budget: Opportunities, challenges, and way forward\n\nThe effectiveness of the proposed budget will depend not just on the allocation of financial resources but also on the quality of implementation, institutional coordination, transparency and accountability. . Its ultimate success will depend on whether it can translate fiscal discipline into productive investment, economic recovery into sustainable growth and national economic progress into tangible improvements in the living standards of the people\n\nThe 2027 Budget presented to the Parliament of Sri Lanka represents more than an annual exercise in estimating Government revenue and expenditure. It reflects the Government\u2019s broader economic vision and its policy direction towards transforming the national economy from a phase of economic stabilisation to a more sustainable, productive and growth-oriented development model. The important emphasis of the Budget is on strengthening domestic production, promoting investment, expanding export capacity, improving economic competitiveness and ensuring inclusive social development."
