    "chunk_size_bytes": 1167,
    "chunk_text": "Therefore, the 2027 Budget should be evaluated not simply as an annual financial statement, but as a strategic economic policy framework that will influence Sri Lanka\u2019s future development path. Its ultimate success will depend on whether it can translate fiscal discipline into productive investment, economic recovery into sustainable growth and national economic progress into tangible improvements in the living standards of the people. The critical question is whether the policies and financial allocations proposed in the Budget are sufficiently practical, financially sustainable and effectively implementable to achieve the country\u2019s long term economic transformation.\n\nTherefore, in addition to maintaining fiscal discipline, priority must be given to expanding domestic production capacity, diversifying exports, attracting foreign investment, fostering technological innovation and developing human resources. Ultimately, the success of the Budget is determined not only by achieving the stated financial targets, but by translating them into tangible economic outcomes, such as job creation, growth in public income and an improved standard of living."
