    "chunk_size_bytes": 1875,
    "chunk_text": "The 2027 Budget proposes an allocation of Rs. 95 billion for the modernisation of transport and road infrastructure. Key proposals under this initiative include expanding the metro bus service to major cities, providing the necessary facilities for 100 electric buses, procuring 200 small buses to strengthen rural transport, acquiring five railway carriages, and modernising railway stations. Furthermore, investments have been proposed for the expansion of the highway network, including the Central and Ruwanpura Expressway projects.\n\nThe 2027 Budget proposes the allocation of funds for the education and vocational training sectors, with the objective of creating a workforce equipped with the knowledge and technical skills required to meet future economic demands. Accordingly, it is proposed to allocate Rs. 4,000 million for the digitalisation of general education, Rs. 2,000 million for human resource development within the education sector, Rs. 1,500 million for the modernisation of technical and vocational colleges, and Rs. 800 million for the development of facilities at the University of Vocational Technology.\n\nThe primary objective of these investments is to develop human resources capable of adapting to technological changes and possessing skills that align with the demands of the job market. However, the success of these programs should not be evaluated solely based on the amount of funds allocated or the scale of physical facilities provided; rather, it should be assessed through measurable indicators such as the development of students\u2019 skills, post-vocational training employment rates, alignment with the labor market, and outcomes in research and innovation. Consequently, it is essential that investments in education are implemented in a manner that strengthens the nation\u2019s human capital and contributes to long-term economic growth."
