    "chunk_text": "The primary objective of these investments is to develop human resources capable of adapting to technological changes and possessing skills that align with the demands of the job market. However, the success of these programs should not be evaluated solely based on the amount of funds allocated or the scale of physical facilities provided; rather, it should be assessed through measurable indicators such as the development of students\u2019 skills, post-vocational training employment rates, alignment with the labor market, and outcomes in research and innovation. Consequently, it is essential that investments in education are implemented in a manner that strengthens the nation\u2019s human capital and contributes to long-term economic growth.\n\nThe 2027 Budget focuses on enhancing agricultural productivity and strengthening the rural economy. Although approximately 23.9% of the national workforce is engaged in agriculture, its contribution to the national economy stands at only about 8.4% a figure that underscores the need to improve productivity and the adoption of technology within this sector. Accordingly, key proposed measures include promoting collective farming methods, expanding the use of agricultural machinery, improving product quality and market access, modernising agrarian service centers, and incentivising private sector investment. The success of these initiatives will be determined by their ability to increase farmer incomes, minimise post-harvest losses, and enhance the competitiveness of domestic agricultural products."
