    "chunk_text": "The 2027 Budget focuses on enhancing agricultural productivity and strengthening the rural economy. Although approximately 23.9% of the national workforce is engaged in agriculture, its contribution to the national economy stands at only about 8.4% a figure that underscores the need to improve productivity and the adoption of technology within this sector. Accordingly, key proposed measures include promoting collective farming methods, expanding the use of agricultural machinery, improving product quality and market access, modernising agrarian service centers, and incentivising private sector investment. The success of these initiatives will be determined by their ability to increase farmer incomes, minimise post-harvest losses, and enhance the competitiveness of domestic agricultural products.\n\nEnsuring the equitable distribution of the benefits of economic development among the people is another key objective of the 2027 Budget. Provisions have been proposed to enhance healthcare facilities, procure medical equipment, expand ambulance services, and strengthen regional health infrastructure. Furthermore, the Budget incorporates social protection programs for low-income families, persons with disabilities, the elderly, and those affected by disasters. The focus here extends beyond the mere provision of subsidies; it aims to improve the income generating capacity of these groups and enhance their opportunities to participate in the economy."
