    "chunk_text": "To swiftly translate the objectives of the 2027 Budget into tangible, practical outcomes, it is essential to establish a mechanism for monthly and quarterly progress reviews regarding the utilisation of Budgetary allocations and to expedite delayed development projects. Furthermore, it is important to introduce Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for State institutions and implement a results based evaluation framework. The accelerate the digitalisation of tax administration and public services another important factor. The expand financial and technical support for small and medium sized enterprises (SMEs). Additionally, economic stability can be strengthened by enhancing supply chain efficiency and market competitiveness, rather than relying solely on price controls.\n\nThe 2027 Budget aims to advance the process of stabilising Sri Lanka\u2019s economy by fostering an economic transformation rooted in production, investment, exports, technology and social equity. Its success hinges on establishing a coherent alignment between the proposals presented in the Budget speech and the financial allocations set out in the Appropriation Bill. Furthermore, it is essential that the allocated funds are utilised in a timely manner, in accordance with the correct priorities, and in a way that yields measurable outcomes. The primary challenge facing Sri Lanka today lies not merely in maintaining economic stability, but in translating that stability into tangible development one that enhances the public\u2019s income, employment opportunities, business growth and overall quality of life."
  },
