    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "Manivannan makes global appeal at APSCO 2026\n\nR. M. Manivannan delivering his address at the 4th Leadership Development Forum of the Asia-Pacific Space Cooperation Organisation (APSCO), held in Beijing, China\n\nSupremeSAT Chairman calls on international space industry leaders to invest in Sri Lanka, share advanced technologies and empower the next generation of innovators\n\nSupreme Global Holdings and SupremeSAT Chairman R. M. Manivannan delivered a powerful address at the 4th Leadership Development Forum of the Asia-Pacific Space Cooperation Organisation (APSCO) in Beijing (18-20 November 2026), calling for greater international investment, technology partnerships and knowledge-sharing opportunities for developing nations.\n\nAddressing international space industry leaders, policymakers, scientists and technology experts, Manivannan urged advanced economies to help countries such as Sri Lanka become active participants in the global space industry rather than remain dependent on technologies developed elsewhere.\n\n\u201cTalent exists everywhere. Opportunity should too,\u201d he declared, highlighting the need to create opportunities for talented young people in developing countries.\n\nRecalling Sri Lanka\u2019s entry into the commercial space industry, Manivannan described the historic launch of SupremeSAT-1 on 27 November 2012 from China\u2019s Xichang Satellite Launch Centre, made possible through cooperation with Chinese industry partners.\n\n\u201cThey did not look at how small our country was. They looked at how big our dream was,\u201d he said, expressing gratitude to China for supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s ambitions.\n\nToday, SupremeSAT operates its Kandy Teleport, providing satellite and ground-station services to international customers, with ambitions to establish Sri Lanka as a regional satellite communications hub."
  },
