    "chunk_size_bytes": 1242,
    "chunk_text": "Today, SupremeSAT operates its Kandy Teleport, providing satellite and ground-station services to international customers, with ambitions to establish Sri Lanka as a regional satellite communications hub.\n\n\u201cWe are not asking for charity. We are asking for partnership,\u201d he emphasised.\n\nHe also highlighted Supreme Global Holdings\u2019 involvement in emerging sectors, including artificial intelligence data centres, renewable energy, green ammonia and satellite communications.\n\nHis vision is to create a future where Sri Lankan engineers can work with world-class technologies without leaving their homeland, while children in remote communities gain access to global educational opportunities.\n\nCalling for stronger cooperation through APSCO, he urged international partners to use space technology to address practical challenges, including natural disasters, climate change, food security and education.\n\nConcluding his address, Manivannan delivered a memorable appeal: \u201cFourteen years ago, together, we helped Sri Lanka reach space. Now, together, let us use space to help everyone reach a better future.\u201d\n\nHis message reinforced Sri Lanka\u2019s potential to become a meaningful participant in tomorrow\u2019s global technology economy."
