    "md5": "442bcafe40fcbff1dc507195e9f1de42",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1330,
    "chunk_text": "US Ambassador leads pledge of service for 34 new Peace Corps volunteers in Sri Lanka\n\nThirty-four Americans took the Peace Corps Pledge of Service this week, beginning a two-year commitment to work alongside Sri Lankan teachers and communities in the Northern and North Central provinces to strengthen English-language education.\n\nThrough classroom co-teaching, teacher workshops, and collaboration with local educators, Peace Corps Volunteers will help students build American English-language skills. Beyond the classroom, they will live with Sri Lankan host families, share American traditions, discover Sri Lankan culture, and build lasting friendships that strengthen US-Sri Lanka ties.\n\nUS Ambassador to Sri Lanka Eric Meyer administered the Peace Corps Pledge of Service to the 34 Americans at a ceremony in Kotapanwila, Bulathsinhala, joined by Foreign Affairs Deputy Minister Arun Hemachandra and Education Ministry Director of the English and Foreign Languages Branch Nimali Baduraliya.\u00a0 The group represents the fourth cohort since the Peace Corps program was re-established in Sri Lanka in 2018 and the largest single cohort sent to the country. The ceremony recognised the Volunteers\u2019 commitment to service and the vital role of Sri Lankan teachers, host families, and communities in welcoming and supporting them."
  },
