    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank and Justice Ministry partner to introduce digital gateway for Court payments\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank and the Justice and National Integration Ministry have signed an agreement to implement an Internet Payment Gateway (IPG) for accepting court-related payments electronically, marking another significant milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s judicial digital transformation journey.\n\nJustice and National Integration Ministry Secretary Ayesha Jinasena PC and People\u2019s Bank Chairman Chandana Guniyangoda exchanged the agreement recently at the Justice Ministry premises in Colombo 10. People\u2019s Bank Payments and Cards Deputy General Manager I.K. Indika, along with Card Centre officials and representatives of the Justice Ministry, also participated in the event.\n\nThe partnership further strengthens the longstanding collaboration between the two institutions in introducing convenient, secure and efficient digital payment facilities across the country\u2019s judicial system.\n\nThe Internet Payment Gateway will further expand these facilities by enabling court users to make applicable payments through online channels, reducing the need for physical visits to court payment counters or bank branches. This is expected to provide greater convenience to litigants, Attorneys-at-Law and other members of the public accessing judicial services.\n\nThe initiative is aligned with the Government\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda and the E-Courts Project, which aims to modernise Sri Lanka\u2019s judicial administration through technology-driven solutions, improve operational efficiency, enhance transparency and facilitate better access to justice."
  },
