    "chunk_text": "The initiative is aligned with the Government\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda and the E-Courts Project, which aims to modernise Sri Lanka\u2019s judicial administration through technology-driven solutions, improve operational efficiency, enhance transparency and facilitate better access to justice.\n\n\u201cPeople\u2019s Bank is proud to be a strategic banking partner in supporting the digital transformation of Sri Lanka\u2019s judicial system. Our collaboration with the Justice Ministry has already demonstrated encouraging results. Today\u2019s agreement represents an important next step in expanding digital payment acceptance through an Internet Payment Gateway,\u201d Guniyangoda said.\n\n\u201cOur vision is to move beyond conventional payment methods and establish a comprehensive digital payment ecosystem that provides convenient, secure and accessible payment facilities to citizens, while conforming to the highest standards in governance, risk management and compliance. We also look forward to exploring opportunities to extend these facilities through mobile banking, internet banking, QR-based payments and other digital payment channels, in line with the Ministry\u2019s requirements and the country\u2019s broader digitalisation objectives. People\u2019s Bank remains committed to supporting the Government\u2019s efforts to build a digitally empowered Sri Lanka.\u201d\n\nThe proposed Internet Payment Gateway will provide a foundation for further integration with the Ministry\u2019s digital platforms, including relevant E-Courts services and electronic case-related processes. Subject to future requirements and technical integration, opportunities may also be explored to facilitate multiple payment channels, automated payment confirmations and electronic receipts, together with improved transaction monitoring and reconciliation facilities."
