    "chunk_size_bytes": 1723,
    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka brings together leading experts to analyse Budget 2027\n\nThe Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka) hosted a comprehensive post-Budget seminar last week to provide members, business leaders, tax professionals and policymakers with an in-depth analysis of the key economic, fiscal and taxation proposals in National Budget 2027.\n\nHeld at CA Sri Lanka, the seminar attracted over 700 participants, both in person and virtually. It featured leading experts from the public and private sectors, who shared insights on the Budget\u2019s potential impact on economic growth, investment, taxation, exports, public finances and tax administration.\n\nSpeaking at the event, CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe said Budget 2027 marks a significant phase in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic journey as the country moves from a period of stabilisation towards sustainable growth and development. He also spoke on the performance of the country\u2019s revenue-generating agencies and highlighted the importance of maintaining fiscal discipline while strengthening foreign exchange earnings, investment and economic resilience. He further stressed the importance of effective implementation in achieving the Budget\u2019s growth objectives.\n\nCA Sri Lanka Faculty of Taxation Chairman Saman Srilal observed that the Budget places considerable emphasis on productive sectors of the economy through investments in export-oriented manufacturing, tourism, agriculture, technology, digitalisation and SMEs. He welcomed several tax measures, including personal income tax relief, investment incentives to encourage export-oriented projects, and initiatives to strengthen tax administration and improve compliance processes."
  },
