    "md5": "27ca816b11bbb79ff8ffdbe8914f5cb5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1790,
    "chunk_text": "Give citizens and regions chance, and Sri Lanka grows richer\n\nThe 13th Amendment gave the regions a voice in 1987; the 12 June framework would give promises a penalty. Together they turn development from a gift into an opportunity, and opportunity into shared prosperity and trust. The question is whether Parliament will act before the street, and a generation, makes the argument for it\n\nHuman development is driven by people, not delivered to them. The State must do its part. The 13th Amendment already gives every province the means. A country that lets its citizens and regions build will be richer for it\n\nThis autumn, from Paris to Tirana and Belgrade, Europe\u2019s young are marching against rising costs and failing services. Young protesters give the same explanation: nobody heard us.\n\nSri Lanka knows that sentence. The grievance is the same: sacrifice without a fair share, a real say, or anyone answerable when promises fail. More than 300,000 Sri Lankans left for foreign employment in 2024. A State that loses its young loses its future.\n\nAnd the first rung of the ladder is breaking. Stanford researchers find that since late 2022, employment of 22- to 25-year-olds in the occupations most exposed to AI has fallen steadily behind their peers, a gap that has now widened to 19%, mainly because firms are simply not hiring them. The World Bank ranks Sri Lanka among South Asia\u2019s most AI-exposed economies and last in jobs where AI complements workers rather than replaces them; nearly a quarter of our workforce is in exposed occupations. The clerical, call-centre and junior coding jobs our graduates queue for are the first to go. If Colombo cannot promise those first jobs, the regions must be free to create new ones, in work that needs local hands and local knowledge."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-20-dailyftlk-9f0a2478",
    "num": "dailyftlk-9f0a2478",
    "date_str": "2026-11-20",
    "description": "Give citizens and regions chance, and Sri Lanka grows richer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Give-citizens-and-regions-chance-and-Sri-Lanka-grows-richer/4-800403",
    "lang": "en",
