    "description": "Give citizens and regions chance, and Sri Lanka grows richer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Give-citizens-and-regions-chance-and-Sri-Lanka-grows-richer/4-800403",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1795198588.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-20-dailyftlk-9f0a2478-0005",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e6028f1528a439f83d36efd0c4a08a91",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 490,
    "chunk_text": "Will we not all be richer for it? The Western Province holds 28% of the people and produces 42% of output. The other eight provinces hold nearly three-quarters of the people, most of the land and water, and produce less than three-fifths. If they closed even half the gap in output per person with the West, the national economy would be roughly a quarter larger, without a rupee of new debt. That wealth will come not from Colombo but from people given the chance to build where they live."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-20-dailyftlk-0421c09d",
