    "language": "en",
    "md5": "053af28c5342299691dc0787f43a5a2e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1779,
    "chunk_text": "The Vrindavan: The land of love\n\nSome journeys are made to explore new places. Some are made to experience something beautiful. And then there are journeys that quietly change the way we look at life.\n\nI had always been fascinated by this sacred land of Shree Radha and Lord Krishna, the land of divine love. The devotion of its people, the stories of divine love, the temples, the saints, the sacred River Maa Yamuna, and the lives of those who surrender themselves to the path of Bhakti had always drawn my attention.\n\nI went there with curiosity, devotion, and a desire to experience something beyond ordinary travel.\n\nWhen I finally arrived in Vrindavan, I felt as though I had entered a different world. The narrow streets were filled with people, vehicles, pilgrims, monks, and wandering animals. Yet, amidst all the noise and movement, one expression seemed to connect everyone: \u201cRadhe Radhe!\u201d\n\nPeople greeted one another with Radhe Radhe. Shopkeepers, strangers, pilgrims, and devotees seemed to carry the name wherever they went. It was more than a greeting; it felt like the heartbeat of the city, a city that seemed to breathe Radhe Radhe.\n\nThat evening, I visited Nidhivan, Seva Kunj, and Shri Banke Bihari Ji Temple. Each place had its own atmosphere and carried its own stories of devotion.\n\nBut something about my visit to Banke Bihari Ji was especially beautiful. I felt a quiet anticipation, almost as though I were going to meet someone very dear to me. And when I finally stood before Bihari Ji, I felt as if He had been waiting for me all along.\n\nWhat a beautiful feeling! It was something beyond ordinary words.\n\nBut the most wonderful experience of my journey was yet to come.\n\nThe Braj Raj: The adorable and tender touch of the sacred soil of Vrindavan"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-20-dailyftlk-0421c09d",
    "num": "dailyftlk-0421c09d",
