    "chunk_text": "Based on all of the above, it is clear that despite some efforts, the health and environment risks arising from the proliferation of plastic and widespread plastic waste generation and mismanagement continues without a vision and goals and objectives to address this issue along with strategies that are needed to address them. While much lip service is made about them, the actual efforts and outcomes have been far from satisfactory. There are insufficient programs in place to educate the public about the health hazards of plastics and the plastic waste and there is insufficient monitoring of whatever programs that may be in place. Addressing this serious issue needs serious strategies and the participation of the public in taking ownership of the cause and effects arising from the proliferation of plastic and the destructive methods used to get rid of plastic waste. Strategies must also include educational programs in schools, and amongst civil society entities, as well as in religious institutions, to apprise the public about the dangers arising to the health of humans and other living beings and to the environment, which in the end impacts on the health and well-being of all.\n\nFinally, a serious effort is needed from policy makers about the use of plastics and to explore and promote, with incentives, the use of alternative environmentally friendly local materials. Plastic is convenient but it enriches manufacturers in other countries while causing the after-effect damage in Sri Lanka, to our health and the environment."
