    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b1eaecf1df2f8421b026f10253e0aa75",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "The identification of demographic changes will allow probable transitions that may rigour business development opportunities for new products and services in the market.\u00a0 Identifying and tailoring such products and services to fulfill the needs of older adults will enable strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s economic landscape and fostering an inclusive economic growth.\n\nThe term \u201csilver economy\u201d was born to the world in the year 1970 when Japanese National Railways suggested \u201csilver seats\u201d to elderly citizens. The world over, the aging population is catalysing the future proofing,\u00a0 Silver Market and has become a powerful force to build new markets with products and services while creating and redefining aging as economic and social value. The silver economy refers to the economic activities created by the needs and the spending power of the population of older adults\n\nSri Lanka has been traditionally heavily relying on labour migration and their remittances; now it prompts for new pathways for diverse arrays for new business projects and to offer different services for older adults for their unique consumption patterns and services. This is where the country should review the tailored economic policies that are essential to the shifts in the economic platform to maximise the benefits to all stakeholders to harness the full potential of the silver economy.\n\nThe inclusive policies would improve the citizens of all walks of life that entrust and broaden the strategic approaches in managing human capital for better economic creation,\u00a0 thus ensuring that older adults\u00a0 too, are actively contributing to the economy without becoming an economic burden. In addition, it provides flexible retirement systems and provides a focus business market for eldercare products and infrastructure to expand the business platforms leveraging the silver economy."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
