    "chunk_size_bytes": 1719,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka stands at a pivotal juncture where the challenges of an aging population can be transformed into opportunities for sustainable growth. By strategically investing in social support systems such as healthcare, workforce participation, and digital inclusion,\u00a0 the nation can foster a robust silver economy. Such an economy would not only enhance the quality of life for older citizens,\u00a0 but also strengthen overall economic resilience by recognising older adults as vital contributors to Sri Lanka\u2019s human capital.\n\nThe Silver Economy focuses on economic activities, markets, and also on policy frameworks regarding older adults, above age 50 for their evolving needs and could generate many significant opportunities for social development and sustainable economic growth in Sri Lanka. A challenging country policy framework may transform the perceived social challenge of an ageing population into a great opportunity to use the knowledge, entrepreneurship, productivity, investments consumption etc.\n\nSri Lanka can unlock the demographic opportunity of a Silver Economy with the Silver Dividend to turn longer lives, to stronger economic lives. The question is whether Sri Lanka is ready to turn longevity into an economic opportunity as the population ages; economic dependency is not necessary when older adults are empowered to remain contributing to society as long as they are ready and able,\u00a0 and they are seen\u00a0 as an economic asset.\n\n(Dr. Heather Fernando is Chief Manager \u2013 Human Resources, Sanasa Development Bank PLC, Council Member, CIPM Sri Lanka - 2024/2025, 2025/2026, 2026/2027 and Chairperson-CIPM Standing Committee on National HR Data Hub with Research and Development Capabilities)."
