    "chunk_text": "The letter was written following a decision at a meeting held on 16 November. Justice for All had announced the meeting to the President in a letter dated 9 November, inviting him to the discussion at ICES in Colombo 8, or to nominate a representative if he could not attend. It said it had also invited other members of the Government and others involved in its 2022-2023 campaign.\n\n\u201cWe acknowledge the support and solidarity extended by you and senior members of your party during this period, including attending events held across the country,\u201d the organisation said.\n\nIt said engaging the human rights community, people affected under the PTA and other stakeholders was vital to repealing the Act and discussing the two Bills. \u201cWe believe such constructive engagement is critical in Sri Lanka\u2019s law reform, with implications for human rights, the economy and the rule of law,\u201d it said.\n\nThe 19 November letter was signed by Karu Jayasuriya, Prof. Jayadeva Uyangoda, Prof. Savithri Gunasekara, Dr. Jayampathy Wickramaratne PC, Dr. Dinesha Samararatne, Eran Wickramaratne, Chandra Jayaratne, M.A. Sumanthiran PC, Jehan Perera, Saliya Pieris PC, Rohana Hettiarachchi, A.M. Faaiz, Lakshan Dias, MP Shanakiyan Rasamanickam, M. Amitha Priyanthi, Bhavani Fonseka, Hejaaz Hizbullah, Ermiza Tegal, Dr. Gehan Gunatilleke, Nadishani Perera, Sandun Thudugala, Jerusha Crosette-Thambiah, Maheshi Herat, Benislos Thushan, Jeevaratnam Suresh, Sampath Samarakoon, Selvaraja Rajasegar, Manjula Gajanayake and Nabeela Iqbal."
