    "chunk_text": "Again, I return to the fact that our forefathers believed farmers and nature\u2019s bounty should be celebrated and protected. However, today\u2019s governments and administrations do not seem to share that belief. I think that is where the problem lies.\n\nThat\u2019s why there are so many religions which honour the sun.\n\nQ How can we draw on ancient agricultural wisdom in the modern context? In the past, farmers relied on traditional knowledge, such as observing cloud patterns to predict rainfall and plan their cultivation accordingly. How can such indigenous knowledge be integrated with modern agricultural practices and weather forecasting?\n\nThis is a lengthy interview response. I have edited it for grammar, clarity, coherence and flow, while retaining the speaker\u2019s arguments, examples, political observations and conversational tone. I have also preserved the interviewer\u2019s questions and the transition between subjects."
