    "md5": "ede6d8e5fba44d1a889e94c50e0849b3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 788,
    "chunk_text": "Afternoon thundershowers expected across most parts of the island in coming days\n\nColombo, November 21 (Daily Mirror)- The Meteorology Department has forecast fairly heavy rainfall exceeding 75mm in some areas of the Western, Sabaragamuwa, North Western, Central and Uva provinces, as well as in the Galle and Matara districts, during the evening or night.\n\nAccording to the Department, atmospheric conditions are becoming favourable for afternoon thundershowers across most parts of the island over the next few days.\n\nMisty conditions are also expected in several parts of the country during the early morning hours.\n\nThe public has been urged to take necessary precautions against possible damage caused by temporary localized strong winds and lightning associated with thundershowers."
