    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "Wine Evening and Fashion Show on November 26\n\nColombo prepares for an evening of French-inspired fashion, fine wine this November\n\nThe Sri Lanka-France Business Council of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, in collaboration with Modart International, will host its annual Wine Evening and Fashion Show on November 26, 2026, at 6:00 p.m. onwards, at Cinnamon Grand Colombo.\n\nThe event, which has become a feature of Colombo\u2019s social and fashion calendar, will bring together the business community, fashion enthusiasts and guests for an evening celebrating French-inspired design, craftsmanship and fine wines.\n\nAmbassador of France to Sri Lanka R\u00e9mi Lambert will be the chief guest, reflecting the close cultural and business connections between the two countries.\n\nThis year\u2019s fashion showcase will feature collections inspired by the craftsmanship and design traditions of French fashion houses, with an emphasis on artistry, detail and creative expression. The runway presentation, complemented by a selection of fine wines, will be a central feature of the evening.\n\nBeyond the fashion showcase, the event will offer an opportunity for the members of the business community and other guests to meet and connect in a relaxed setting.\n\nSri Lanka-France Business Council President Shaameel Mohideen said, \u201cEvents such as these provide an opportunity to celebrate the cultural and creative dimensions of the relationship between Sri Lanka and France, while creating space for people from different sectors to connect. We look forward to welcoming our members, partners and guests for an evening of fashion, craftsmanship and conversation.\u201d\n\nThe Wine Evening and Fashion Show continues the council\u2019s efforts to promote engagement between the two countries beyond traditional business interactions, recognising the role of culture, creativity and personal connections in strengthening bilateral relations."
