    "md5": "c4b9f78a85f69e140667cc7e1ca78b21",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1805,
    "chunk_text": "Tudawe Trading Company opens 4th automated car-wash facility in Wattala\n\nTudawe Trading Company (Pvt.) Ltd, the sole authorised agent for K\u00e4rcher products in Sri Lanka, officially opened its fourth automated car-wash facility at Sandagiri Tire House, No. 643, Hendala, Wattala, recently.\n\nThe facility was inaugurated by Tudawe Trading Chief Executive Officer Eshan Tudawe, Sandagiri Tire House owner Niluka Dilhani and others.\n\nTudawe Trading Company marks another milestone in modernising the country\u2019s vehicle-care industry with the opening of its fourth Karcher automated car-wash facility at Sandagiri Tire House.\n\nPowered by Karcher\u2019s advanced German cleaning technology, the CW3 automated car-wash system delivers a consistent, paint-safe vehicle wash in under eight minutes, redefining convenience, efficiency and quality.\n\nPaint-safe technology: Specially designed washing components help minimise scratches and protect vehicle paintwork.\n\nGerman engineering: Precision automation and controlled detergent application ensure reliable cleaning results.\n\nResource efficiency: Optimised water and detergent consumption helps minimise wastage.\n\nSmarter business model: Reduced reliance on manual labour, improved operational efficiency and the potential to serve more vehicles per day.\n\nWith the rising labour costs, increasing demand for convenience and growing expectations for professional vehicle care and automated car washing presents an attractive opportunity for entrepreneurs, fuel stations, automotive service centres and commercial investors.\n\nBacked by Karcher\u2019s globally established cleaning technology and Tudawe Trading\u2019s over 40 years of local industry experience, the CW3 represents a shift towards a more efficient, scalable and professional car-wash industry in Sri Lanka."
  },
