    "md5": "973f1b5ae2562c3ac477bdb88feaee5c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1739,
    "chunk_text": "Full\u2019r Burgers brings seasonal innovation to Sri Lanka with Halloween campaign\n\nGiga Foods celebrated Halloween in Sri Lanka with a Full\u2019r Burgers campaign combining specially curated seasonal burgers, themed outlet experiences and an activation at Crescat Boulevard, Colombo.\n\nThe campaign introduced Voodoo Chick, a crispy chicken burger and Butcher\u2019s Double, a double beef burger.\n\nDeveloped specifically for Halloween, both products reflected Giga Foods\u2019 focus on seasonal product innovation, connecting its menu with creative brand storytelling.\n\nThe campaign began with an office launch, where Full\u2019r\u2019s Night Cook character came to life and colleagues experienced the products firsthand. A movie night completed the internal celebrations.\n\nFollowing the launch, Full\u2019r Burgers\u2019 outlet teams brought the campaign to customers through the seasonal menu, Halloween d\u00e9cor and customer engagement. Their coordinated execution carried the campaign\u2019s identity across the restaurant experience.\n\nThe celebrations continued in partnership with Crescat Boulevard. The activation featured Full\u2019r-inspired Halloween decorations, a pop-up market, mini canvas painting and children\u2019s face painting, with creative activities hosted by Whiz Creations.\n\nThe Night Cook also visited participants, adding an interactive element to the event. Canvas painting participants received a special Full\u2019r Burgers discount, linking their creative experience with the brand\u2019s food offering.\n\nThrough seasonal products, team collaboration and local partnerships, Giga Foods brought its Halloween concept from the menu into customer experiences. The company looks forward to introducing fresh ideas and new flavours in the coming season."
