    "md5": "16bb4db1a821441c85889bc3f54ff448",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1736,
    "chunk_text": "LLD unites diverse ventures under one vision\n\nLLD Chairman and Managing Director Imthiaz Cader with LLD Directors Fahmy Cader and Ayesha Hasheem\n\nLiberty Lands & Developments (LLD), a diversified Sri Lankan business group with a legacy spanning over seven decades, has unveiled its unified corporate identity, bringing together its established presence across entertainment, hospitality, food and beverage, film distribution and audiovisual technology.\n\nThe move marks a new chapter in the group\u2019s journey, reinforcing its commitment to introducing international standards and delivering quality experiences that enhance the everyday lives of Sri Lankans.\n\nGuided by its corporate philosophy \u2018The Future, Built Right\u2019, LLD remains focused on responsible growth, operational excellence and building businesses that serve future generations. As the group strengthens its corporate presence, it aims to continue introducing globally inspired experiences while supporting local enterprise and contributing to Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving commercial landscape.\n\nLLD Chairman and Managing Director Imthiaz J. Cader said, \u201cThe foundation of our business was built on my father\u2019s belief that success must come through honesty, hard work and the trust of the people we serve. As the second generation, our responsibility was not only to preserve what he established but to strengthen the business and prepare it for the future.\n\nWe have navigated many challenges over the decades but our commitment to quality, integrity and long-term value has remained unchanged. Today, it is encouraging to see the next generation taking this legacy forward, introducing new ideas and expanding into sectors that contribute to the lives of Sri Lankans.\u201d"
  },
