    "md5": "d3d3fbca5393c2673a21187ad478d5f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1634,
    "chunk_text": "Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 opens 15th outlet in Kandy\n\nChinese Dragon Caf\u00e9, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s long-standing names in Chinese cuisine, has further strengthened its presence in the country with the opening of its newest restaurant in Kandy, marking another important milestone in the brand\u2019s expansion journey.\n\nThe new outlet brings the brand\u2019s much-loved Chinese cuisine to one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most celebrated cities, extending a legacy that began more than eight decades ago.\n\nLocated at No. 454 Piachaud Garden, Kandy, approximately 230 meters from Peradeniya Road towards Piachaud Garden, near Lighthouse Church, the restaurant becomes Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9\u2019s 14th outlet in Sri Lanka and 15th outlet worldwide.\n\nRenowned for its rich cultural heritage, historical significance and scenic surroundings, Kandy is also one of the country\u2019s leading tourism and commercial destinations, making it a strategic location for the brand to reach a wider customer base comprising local residents, business communities and visitors from across Sri Lanka and overseas.\n\nChinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 Chief Operating Officer Lahiruwan Lakmal said, \u201cKandy is a city with a distinctive identity, bringing together a rich cultural heritage, a thriving tourism sector, business activity and a diverse community. We recognise the potential of this market and see this expansion as an important opportunity for Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 to reach new customers. We are delighted to bring our brand and much-loved Chinese cuisine to Kandy. We look forward to welcoming the community and establishing long-term relationships with our customers in the city.\u201d"
