    "md5": "c33c325ebaea08acb02921a4864b34ac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1702,
    "chunk_text": "Ting debuts with new approach to how SL shops, sells, delivers\n\nTing is now available in Colombo, bringing food, groceries and everyday essentials together in one app, with multi-vendor ordering and built-in bill splitting\n\nSri Lankan-owned, innovation-first platform launched with free delivery for a limited time, connecting consumers, businesses and delivery riders through a locally built ecosystem\n\nSri Lankan technology company Edine Services (Pvt.) Ltd has launched \u2018Ting\u2019, a locally developed on-demand platform designed to bring consumers, merchants and delivery operations together within a single ecosystem.\n\nGoing beyond conventional delivery services, Ting aims to create a model that combines customer convenience with new commercial opportunities for businesses and a more integrated approach to delivery operations.\n\nAt a time when digital platforms are reshaping how people discover, purchase and receive goods, Ting is entering the market with a distinctly local perspective: that the future of delivery should work not only for customers but also for the businesses that serve them and the people who make each delivery possible. Its approach combines locally developed technology with dedicated delivery operations, direct customer support and a merchant model designed to create commercial opportunities beyond individual transactions.\n\nLaunching with more than 300 vendors across food, groceries and everyday essentials, Ting gives customers access to a broad selection of products through a single app. Features include Favourite lists for convenient repeat ordering and multi-vendor ordering with integrated bill splitting, supported by a dedicated customer support hotline."
  },
