    "md5": "e9cc121e3845ca9e76dd97db27c9e819",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1567,
    "chunk_text": "Launching with more than 300 vendors across food, groceries and everyday essentials, Ting gives customers access to a broad selection of products through a single app. Features include Favourite lists for convenient repeat ordering and multi-vendor ordering with integrated bill splitting, supported by a dedicated customer support hotline.\n\nThe platform is also investing in the people behind the delivery experience. Through its dedicated rider operation, Ting is investing in facilities, training and support intended to provide delivery riders with a more structured working environment and greater financial stability. The company sees the long-term strength of a delivery ecosystem as dependent on the experience of everyone involved, not simply the convenience delivered to the end customer.\n\nTo mark its launch, Ting is offering free delivery on eligible orders for a limited time. The introductory programme also includes promotions from participating merchants and dedicated cardholder promotional days for Commercial Bank, Sampath Bank and HNB customers.\n\nFully Sri Lankan-owned and locally developed, Ting represents an investment in homegrown technology and the operational capabilities needed to support it. The business also has ambitions to develop connections across the wider supply chain, with the aim of building a more integrated ecosystem for consumers, merchants and delivery partners.\n\nOperating under the brand promise \u2018Ting \u2013 The one ting for everything\u2019, the app is now available for download on Apple App Store and Google Play Store."
