    "md5": "b50657aa306fcc6d1d53a2fbd753f719",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1621,
    "chunk_text": "Cargills Bank-Mastercard introduce  Sri Lanka\u2019s 1st ocean plastic debit card\n\nTurns ocean-bound plastic into a payment solution that supports a more sustainable future\n\nCargills Bank, in collaboration with Mastercard, has launched Sri Lanka\u2019s first ocean plastic debit card, introducing a more sustainable material into a payment product used every day.\n\nMade using recycled ocean-bound plastic sourced from the Indian Ocean region, including the Maldives and Dominican Republic, the card reflects the bank\u2019s commitment to sustainable banking and responsible innovation.\n\nThe launch reinforces Mastercard\u2019s commitment to helping financial institutions develop innovative solutions that advance sustainability while meeting the evolving consumer expectations. By incorporating recycled ocean-bound plastic into a widely used financial instrument, Cargills Bank and Mastercard are demonstrating how sustainability considerations can be integrated into everyday transaction experiences.\n\nAs an island nation, Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and environmental well-being is closely connected to the health of its oceans and coastlines. The ocean plastic debit card aims to help raise awareness of marine pollution and resource conservation while encouraging greater consideration of circular-economy principles.\n\nIt also delivers the same security, durability and payment functionality that the consumers expect, supported by Mastercard\u2019s global acceptance network.\n\nThe new card has been developed in collaboration with Lake House Printers and Publishers PLC, whose technical expertise supported the production of the card."
  },
