    "md5": "b2f6c482d70e1f21403eae91ae362a2c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1803,
    "chunk_text": "JKH unveils 1st Wendy\u2019s with Elephant House drinks on menu\n\nFrom left: John Keells Group Chairperson Krishan Balendra, Ambassador of the United States of America to Sri Lanka and the Maldives Eric S. Meyer and Wendy\u2019s International Senior Vice President and Managing Director APMEA Chris Conway\n\nChicken-heavy menu with local twists such as Lankan Fire Burger\n\nJohn Keells Holdings (JKH) has pledged the full strength and resources of the group to making Wendy\u2019s a success, as the US burger chain unveiled its first Sri Lankan restaurant at One Galle Face this week, ahead of its public opening, with the group\u2019s own Elephant House soft drinks on its menu.\n\nAddressing the ceremonial opening in Colombo, JKH Chairperson and CEO Krishan Balendra noted that the Group Executive Committee considered the franchise a strong fit when it was first proposed.\n\nWendy\u2019s marks the conglomerate\u2019s entry into quick service restaurants and the group already has a presence in food and beverages through the Elephant House soft drinks and ice cream, Keells processed meats and hot meals sold at the Keells supermarkets.\n\nElephant House Ginger Beer, Cream Soda and Necto are on the drinks menu alongside Coca-Cola, Coke Zero and Sprite, giving the group\u2019s beverage arm a foothold in its new restaurant business from the outset.\n\n\u201cWe saw an opportunity because we feel there is a vacuum in this space in the market in Sri Lanka. It will be an excellent addition to the offering to the Sri Lankan consumer,\u201d Balendra remarked.\n\nHe added that the partnership would bring Wendy\u2019s expertise, training, technology and modern ways of working \u201cnot just for the Wendy\u2019s franchise but to Sri Lanka\u201d.\n\n\u201cWe will put our full weight behind making this business a success,\u201d he assured the stakeholders."
