    "chunk_text": "He added that the partnership would bring Wendy\u2019s expertise, training, technology and modern ways of working \u201cnot just for the Wendy\u2019s franchise but to Sri Lanka\u201d.\n\n\u201cWe will put our full weight behind making this business a success,\u201d he assured the stakeholders.\n\n\u201cOne of my priorities as US Ambassador is to help create opportunities for the American companies here,\u201d US Ambassador to Sri Lanka Eric S. Meyer told the gathering.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s not just about bringing an American company to Sri Lanka. It\u2019s about bringing American innovation, standards and quality as well,\u201d he added.\n\nMeyer also pointed out that the opening creates opportunities for Sri Lankan producers and suppliers and he thanked the John Keells group for the partnership.\n\nHe said he looked forward to seeing more Wendy\u2019s outlets \u201copen here in Sri Lanka, I think very soon\u201d.\n\nThe menu leans heavily on chicken. The Classic and Spicy Chicken Burgers, the hand-breaded Chickenator, a Grilled Chicken Burger, Chicken Tenders, Chicken Bites and a value range of Chicken Tender Burgers sit alongside Wendy\u2019s signature square beef burgers, which are built on a 120-gram patty and come in single, double and triple versions.\n\nThe local flavours come through in the Lankan Fire Burger, billed as the \u201cNai Miris\u201d burger, as well as a Yellow Rice Bowl and a Paneer Double Decker. The brand\u2019s signature Frosty dessert, made with real dairy, comes in vanilla and chocolate.\n\nThe Wendy\u2019s Company Senior Vice President and Managing Director for Asia Pacific, Middle East and Africa Chris Conway explained that the Lankan Fire Burger was developed for the Sri Lankan market from the start.\u00a0 He said this reflected the brand\u2019s aim of being \u201cglobally great and locally loved\u201d.\n\nConway recalled that around 18 months had passed since the two parties first spoke and that the restaurant had arrived nine months after the kick-off meeting.\n\n\u201cSo, here\u2019s to many, many more Wendy\u2019s babies in the future,\u201d he quipped."
