    "chunk_text": "Conway recalled that around 18 months had passed since the two parties first spoke and that the restaurant had arrived nine months after the kick-off meeting.\n\n\u201cSo, here\u2019s to many, many more Wendy\u2019s babies in the future,\u201d he quipped.\n\nThe franchise also carries a minimum outlet commitment over five years, which the management is \u201cquite confident\u201d of meeting. At the first-quarter webinar in July, the management said the business could open \u201cabout eight to 10 stores annually. Maybe more\u201d.\n\nThe restaurants are run by John Keells Restaurants (Private) Limited, a wholly-owned subsidiary set up in 2025. Wendy\u2019s was founded in the United States in 1969 and has more than 7,000 restaurants worldwide.\n\nTo mark the launch, the restaurant will offer unlimited drinks and sauces through its opening month."
