    "chunk_size_bytes": 1847,
    "chunk_text": "Vietjet launches new Colombo-Maldives flights\n\nVietJet is set to expand its regional connectivity with the launch of new flights between Colombo and the Maldives, commencing December 5, 2026, offering the travellers greater convenience and enhanced connectivity between the two destinations.\n\nThe new service will operate three times weekly, on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Saturdays, providing an additional travel option for the passengers travelling between Sri Lanka and the Maldives, while further strengthening Colombo\u2019s position as an important regional aviation hub.\n\nThe introduction of this service reflects VietJet\u2019s continued commitment to expanding its regional network and providing the travellers with greater accessibility, competitive travel options and convenient connections across Asia.\n\nVietJet Sri Lanka General Sales Agent Mahen Kariyawasan said, \u201cWe are delighted to announce the introduction of VietJet\u2019s new flights connecting Colombo with the Maldives.\n\nThis is an exciting development for Sri Lanka\u2019s aviation and tourism sectors, creating new opportunities for travel, tourism, trade and regional cooperation.\u201d\n\n\u201cThe Maldives is an important tourism destination and the introduction of this service will offer greater convenience to travellers while also creating opportunities for Sri Lanka to strengthen its position as a regional gateway. We believe this new connection will benefit both leisure travellers and the wider travel and tourism industry, while further enhancing the connectivity between Sri Lanka, the Maldives and VietJet\u2019s broader network.\u201d\n\nThe three weekly flights, operating on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Saturdays from December 5, 2026, are expected to provide an attractive travel option for the holidaymakers, business travellers and passengers seeking convenient regional connections."
  },
