    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/CRIB-expands-credit-information-ecosystem/215-355460",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1795247197.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-21-dailymirrorlk-8079ebf5-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a1ba3a8b68a9c47e3da99bac33ba4151",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2014,
    "chunk_text": "CRIB expands credit information ecosystem\n\nFrom left: Lak Jaya Microfinance CEO Nimesh Fernando, Berendina Micro Investments Company CEO Charith Fernando, Lanka Microfinance Practitioners\u2019 Association President Wasantha Gunawardena, CRIB Director and General Manager Pushpike Jayasundera, Central Bank Supervision of Non-Bank Financial Institutions Department Director R.M.C.H.K. Jayasinghe, Dumbara Micro Credit CEO Gnanasiri Abeywardena and Sejaya Micro Credit CEO Rizanth Francis\n\nCRIB Chairman and Central Bank Deputy Governor K.G.P. Sirikumara addresses gathering\n\nThe Credit Information Bureau of Sri Lanka (CRIB) has announced a significant expansion of the country\u2019s credit information ecosystem, with the onboarding of four licensed microfinance institutions, following the publication of the relevant government gazette notification.\n\nThis initiative marks an important step towards strengthening credit information sharing within the microfinance sector, enhancing the availability of reliable credit information and promoting greater financial inclusion by facilitating improved access to formal credit for underserved individuals and businesses.\n\nUnder the powers vested in Credit Information Bureau of Sri Lanka Act, No. 18 of 1990, four licensed microfinance companies have been formally declared as designated lending institutions. The newly included institutions are Berendina Micro Investments Company Limited, Lak Jaya Micro Finance Limited, Dumbara Micro Credit Limited and Sejaya Micro Credit Limited.\n\nThis regulatory inclusion integrates the microfinance institutions into the CRIB\u2019s centralised credit information infrastructure, enabling them to both contribute credit information and access borrower profiles within a secure and well-governed framework.\n\nThis development will strengthen the institutions\u2019 capacity to expand their reach to the underserved and marginalised segments of the economy by improving the visibility of data and supporting more informed lending decisions."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-21-dailymirrorlk-8079ebf5",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-8079ebf5",
    "date_str": "2026-11-21",
    "description": "CRIB expands credit information ecosystem",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/CRIB-expands-credit-information-ecosystem/215-355460",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
