    "chunk_id": "2026-11-21-dailymirrorlk-8079ebf5-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "18fd10cdb87bf385ee8290322f122793",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1647,
    "chunk_text": "This development will strengthen the institutions\u2019 capacity to expand their reach to the underserved and marginalised segments of the economy by improving the visibility of data and supporting more informed lending decisions.\n\nA ceremony to mark the onboarding of microfinance data to the CRIB was held recently with the participation of CRIB Chairman and Central Bank Deputy Governor K.G.P. Sirikumara as the chief guest, Central Bank Supervision of Non-Bank Financial Institutions Department Director R.M.C.H.K. Jayasinghe, CRIB Director and General Manager Pushpike Jayasundera, Lanka Microfinance Practitioners\u2019 Association President Wasantha Gunawardhane, chief executive officers of the respective companies, other officials of the companies and the CRIB.\n\nJayasundera stated, \u201cThe formal integration of the licensed microfinance companies into the CRIB framework marks a pivotal step toward building a truly inclusive financial ecosystem in Sri Lanka. Microfinance plays a vital role in supporting micro-entrepreneurs, small businesses and grass-roots economic activity.\n\nBy bringing these institutions into our national credit intelligence network, we are mitigating information asymmetry at micro level, encouraging responsible borrowing and enabling financial institutions to extend credit with greater risk confidence.\u201d\n\nThe inclusion of these institutions aligns with the CRIB\u2019s broader strategic objective to expand credit coverage beyond mainstream commercial banking into grassroots and micro-finance sectors, further driving financial inclusion, credit discipline and sustainable economic revitalisation across Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
