    "chunk_size_bytes": 784,
    "chunk_text": "The medium-term expectations, however, stayed around the 5 percent target. That gave the board room to act in quarter-point increments while May\u2019s larger increase continued to feed through to the borrowing costs.\n\nThe board also raised the banks\u2019 statutory reserve requirement from 2 percent to 3 percent, from December 9, a move Dr. Weerasinghe estimated would absorb about Rs.150 billion of the excess rupee liquidity built up through the Central Bank\u2019s dollar purchases.\n\nThe government bond yields moved higher in early trade, with the dealers quoting the August 2030 bond at 11.20-11.40 percent, against 11.00-11.05 percent the previous day.\n\nFor the businesses, the impact will become clearer when the banks reprice the working-capital lines and loans due for refinancing."
