    "language": "en",
    "md5": "30c47e64184383a5c8eed3c0e661d814",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1431,
    "chunk_text": "These delays have resulted in containers being held at ports for extended periods, increasing costs for importers through additional storage and related charges. Accordingly, the Committee emphasised the need to improve coordination among government agencies and streamline procedures to facilitate faster clearance of imported goods.\n\nThe importance of introducing appropriate quality standards for electric vehicles and their batteries was also emphasised. In addition, the need to establish suitable Harmonized System (HS) codes to ensure accurate Customs classification and taxation of electric vehicles was discussed.\n\nThe Committee also underscored the importance of simplifying tax policies to encourage the adoption of electric vehicles and make them more accessible to the general public. Promoting renewable energy solutions, particularly solar power and battery energy storage systems, was identified as another important measure to minimise the additional pressure that EV charging could place on the national electricity grid.\n\nIn this regard, the Committee discussed the introduction of tax concessions and other policy incentives to encourage electric vehicle imports and usage, updating Customs classifications and HS codes in line with international standards, and establishing a comprehensive system for the environmentally responsible collection, disposal and recycling of end-of-life electric vehicle batteries."
  },
