    "chunk_size_bytes": 774,
    "chunk_text": "Doctors to launch two-hour island-wide trade union action tomorrow\n\nColombo, Nov. 22 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Government Medical Officers\u2019 Association (GMOA) will launch a two-hour island-wide trade union action tomorrow (23), protesting the failure of the 2027 Budget to address doctors\u2019 longstanding grievances.\n\nThe GMOA said doctors would withdraw from routine duties from noon to 2 p.m. to attend emergency meetings of branch unions across the country.\n\nThe association said the action was prompted by the Government\u2019s failure to address issues relating to doctors\u2019 salaries, allowances, professional concerns and working conditions through the Budget.\n\nIt urged the Government to introduce solutions during the remaining stages of the Budget debate in Parliament."
  },
