    "chunk_size_bytes": 1212,
    "chunk_text": "Divulapitiya e-waste facility\u2019s licence suspended after fire\n\nColombo, Nov. 22 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The environmental licence of an electronic waste processing facility in Wewagedara, Divulapitiya, has been temporarily suspended following a fire that broke out at the premises on November 16.\n\nMinister of Environment Dr. Dhammika Patabendi said the decision was taken as a precautionary measure following the incident, which raised concerns over possible environmental pollution caused by burning electronic waste.\n\nHe said the Central Environmental Authority (CEA) had also issued a series of recommendations to prevent air pollution and contamination of the surrounding environment.\n\nThe recommendations aim to minimise the environmental impact of smoke and other pollutants released during the fire, as well as prevent possible contamination from electronic waste materials.\n\nThe CEA is also expected to take necessary steps to ensure that environmental risks arising from the incident are properly addressed.\n\nThe facility's environmental licence will remain suspended temporarily, pending further action by the relevant authorities.\n\nCEJ sends letter of demand to CEA over Divulapitiya e-waste facility fire"
