    "md5": "bc6e64cd97ddb77d2b906e503669a3f2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1609,
    "chunk_text": "Russian cargo ship still on fire off Finland after attack\n\nReuters\u00a0- A fire onboard a Russian cargo ship that was struck by drones in the Baltic Sea continued to burn through the night \u200beven as efforts were made to douse the flames, Finland's \u200ccoast guard said on Sunday.\n\nThe Finnish military has said the strike on the Sparta II on Saturday was likely carried out by Ukraine and that the vessel \u200blater drifted into Finnish waters where it remains at anchor. \u200bThe 16 crew members were evacuated onto a nearby Russian \u2060ship.\n\nGet a look at the day ahead in European and global markets with the Morning\n\nPictures and video released by the coast guard showed several vessels \u200bspraying the Sparta II with water cannons during the night in a \u200bbid to put out the flames and cool down containers stacked on its deck.\n\nUkraine has sent waves of military drones towards Russia's northwest coastal Leningrad region this year, including \u200bsome that strayed into the airspace of nearby Baltic countries, leading \u200bto fears that the war was spilling onto NATO territory.\n\nThe ship, bound for Russian \u200cexclave \u2060Kaliningrad, was damaged in international waters west of Russia's Gogland island, Finland's Defence Forces have said, corroborating an account by Russian officials.\n\nThe risk of further attacks in the Gulf of Finland, a narrow arm of the \u200bBaltic Sea, cannot \u200bbe ruled out, \u2060Estonian Navy Commander Ivo Vark told public broadcaster ERR on Sunday.\n\nFinland's military said last week it had detected a \u200bstrike on a Russian warship in the same area \u200bduring \u2060Ukrainian drone attacks."
