    "md5": "2fec575572afcb0264d4aa94e78047a6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 916,
    "chunk_text": "Among the significant provisions is the authority for the President, through a Gazette notification issued at the request of the relevant Minister, to assign limited immigration enforcement powers to members of the three Armed Forces and the Coast Guard to prevent illegal entry into the country.\n\nIt also provides the legal foundation for introducing automated electronic immigration gates (E-Gates), enabling passengers to clear immigration without the conventional passport-stamping process.\n\nThe proposed legislation further updates official designations within the immigration administration, replacing existing titles such as Controller, Deputy Controller and Authorised Officer with Controller General, Additional Controller General and Immigration Officers.\n\nThe Committee also examined provisions and related legal issues concerning the granting of visas to foreign nationals married to Sri Lankan citizens."
