    "chunk_size_bytes": 1020,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cA Government that weaponises the criminal justice system to disqualify an opponent betrays its own lack of confidence in facing the people at the next election. If you believe you have earned a second mandate, go before the country, defend your record and ask for it. What right have you to narrow the people\u2019s choice before a single vote has been cast?\u201d\n\nHe recalled that Bandaranaike returned as Prime Minister for a third time in 1994, arguing that political opponents should be challenged at the ballot box rather than through the misuse of State institutions.\n\n\u201cHave the courage to face your opponents at the polls. Leave the choice to the people,\u201d he told the Government benches.\n\nHe warned that the erosion of judicial independence could have a chilling effect on trade unionists, Opposition politicians, and ordinary citizens, particularly those seeking to challenge Government actions or expose wrongdoing, adding that an independent judiciary remained the last safeguard against executive overreach."
