    "chunk_text": "In my view, the IPS \u2018State of the Economy\u2019 report is far too precious a document to be ignored by those entrusted with shaping the economic future of this country. It is an indispensable roadmap, yet it suffers from one persistent, recurring vulnerability: it continues to cater almost exclusively to technically competent academics and data analysts. Not every decisionmaker, particularly within the volatile political arena, possesses the specialised training required to instantly digest its complex macroeconomic messaging and dense policy equations.\n\nMy final recommendation is to Parliamentarians: Study this report from cover to cover, and if necessary, get IPS experts to explain complex matters they have presented, and use it productively for policymaking. Otherwise, it will simply remain a report, as it has happened in the past, consumed only by technical experts.\n\n(The writer, a former Deputy Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, can be reached at [email\u00a0protected])"
