    "chunk_size_bytes": 1936,
    "chunk_text": "Adequate Tourist Police facilities should be established in major tourist destinations across the Eastern Province. At present, there is a lack of properly equipped Tourist Police posts with even basic facilities. Therefore, the necessary infrastructure, accommodation, communication facilities and other essential requirements should be provided to enable Tourist Police officers to ensure the safety and security of tourists effectively.\n\nEstablishment of Tourist Information Centres in Nilaveli, Arugam Bay and Pasikuda\n\nTourist Information Centres should be established in Nilaveli, Arugam Bay and Pasikuda to provide information, guidance and assistance to both local and foreign tourists. These centres would help visitors obtain reliable information about tourist attractions, accommodation, transportation, local services and other essential facilities. Considering the significant contribution of tourism in these areas to the country\u2019s foreign exchange earnings, the establishment of such centres would improve the quality of tourist services, enhance visitor experiences and further promote these destinations as attractive international tourism hubs.\n\nDeclaration of Pottuvil, Lahugala and Thirukkovil Divisional Secretariat Divisions as Tourism Zones\n\nThe Pottuvil, Lahugala and Thirukkovil Divisional Secretariat Divisions should be officially identified, developed and declared as Tourism Zones, considering their tourism potential, natural attractions, coastal resources and cultural heritage. This initiative would help attract public and private sector investment, encourage the development of tourism-related infrastructure and facilities, create employment opportunities for local communities and promote new tourism destinations in the Eastern Province. It would also facilitate better coordination among relevant Government institutions in planning and implementing tourism development activities in these areas."
  },
