    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f72c97c5ca33a31f6ee52171c601363e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1182,
    "chunk_text": "Imagine walking through the historic heart of Kandy without the constant movement of vehicles\u2014stopping at an old building, discovering a small shop, sitting beside the lake, visiting the temples and experiencing the city rather than simply passing through it.\n\nKandy should not merely be a place tourists pass through on their way to somewhere else. Kandy itself should be the destination.\n\nWith proper conservation, pedestrianisation, traffic management, restoration of historic buildings, carefully designed tourism infrastructure and a clear long-term vision, Kandy could become one of the greatest cultural tourism destinations in Sri Lanka\u2014and potentially one of the most distinctive heritage cities in Asia.\n\nWhat Kandy needs now is not more concrete. It needs imagination, protection, investment and, above all, a vision.\n\nI hope the authorities will take a closer look at the extraordinary beauty and tourism potential of Kandy before more of its historic character disappears.\n\nWe still have the opportunity to make Kandy what it was always meant to be\u2014a living world heritage city, where history is not merely preserved behind glass, but experienced on every street."
  },
