    "md5": "1e5c055c0bfd48843ba84f75dd824bc4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka and Lebanon explore opportunities to expand bilateral trade\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Lebanon Anura Withanage (left) with Lebanon\u2019s Economy and Trade Minister Amer Bisat\n\nThe Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Lebanon, Anura Withanage, met with Lebanon\u2019s Economy and Trade Minister Amer Bisat, on 17 November 2026 to discuss ways of strengthening commercial relations between the two countries.\n\nThe discussions focused on expanding bilateral trade, diversifying traded products and addressing challenges faced by exporters and importers.\n\nAmbassador Withanage drew the Minister\u2019s attention to the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) concluded between the Chamber of Commerce, Industry and Agriculture of Beirut and Mount Lebanon and the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce. He noted that the agreement provided a framework for connecting businesses in both countries and identifying opportunities for trade and commercial partnerships.\n\nThe Ambassador also briefed the Minister on the Embassy\u2019s recent promotional activities in Lebanon, including the \u2018Discover Sri Lanka\u2019 tourism promotion event, a business forum at the Beirut Chamber featuring a presentation on Sri Lanka Expo 2027 and a Ceylon tea tasting, an international tea-tasting event, and Sri Lanka\u2019s participation in the Nations Day Festival. These initiatives introduced Lebanese businesses to a wider range of Sri Lankan products and services.\n\nWithanage also highlighted the potential for Sri Lankan exports beyond Ceylon Tea to enter the Lebanese market.\n\nMinister Bisat identified Lebanese olive oil and fresh fruit as products that could be introduced to buyers in Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism and hospitality sectors. He expressed interest in participating in future trade promotion events and holding virtual meetings with representatives of the Sri Lankan business community."
  },
