    "language": "en",
    "md5": "317b9399aa3d4d154125d714f5996d8a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1715,
    "chunk_text": "Heritance Ahungalla celebrates 45 years of architectural legacy with \u201845 to Infinity\u2019\n\nA celebration of Geoffrey Bawa\u2019s timeless vision, four and a half decades of hospitality and a horizon of possibilities\n\nThe Heritance Ahungalla marks its 45th anniversary on 23 November 2026 with \u201845 to Infinity\u2019, a celebration honouring the architectural legacy of Geoffrey Bawa, the people who have shaped the property\u2019s journey and its enduring place in Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality landscape.\n\nMore than a milestone, the anniversary reflects four and a half decades of evolution, during which the property has remained deeply connected to its natural surroundings and architectural identity.\n\nOriginally opened in 1981 as the Triton Hotel, Heritance Ahungalla was conceived as a distinctive coastal retreat by Geoffrey Bawa, Sri Lanka\u2019s pioneering architect and a leading figure of Tropical Modernism. At a time when resort design often placed buildings at the centre of the experience, Bawa envisioned a property that embraced its environment, allowing the ocean, tropical gardens, natural light and coastal breezes to shape its character.\n\nOne of the most defining expressions of this vision is the property\u2019s iconic infinity pool, designed to create a seamless visual connection between the pool, the Indian Ocean and the sky. Its disappearing edge captures Bawa\u2019s philosophy of dissolving the boundaries between architecture and nature, an experience that remains as striking today as it was when the hotel first opened. The anniversary theme, \u201845 to Infinity\u2019, draws inspiration from this architectural landmark, connecting the property\u2019s 45-year heritage with an endless horizon of possibilities."
  },
