    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "69b2ec7a5b9ff3a0be69f5c3511c1629",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1763,
    "chunk_text": "Beyond the Obvious: SLID and Frankfurt School of Finance and Management to present executive program on risk management\n\nFrankfurt School of Finance and Management Competence Centre in Risk Management Senior International Adviser and Lead Consultant Dr. Joachim Bald\n\nAs organisations navigate an increasingly complex business environment, effective risk management has become integral to sound corporate governance and strategic leadership. Recognising the importance of strengthening risk oversight at board level, the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID), in collaboration with Frankfurt School of Finance and Management, will present \u2018Beyond the Obvious: Risk Management,\u2019 an executive program for directors and senior professionals.\n\nMarking an inaugural initiative in the SLID\u2019s collaboration with Frankfurt School of Finance and Management, this program establishes a partnership with one of Germany\u2019s leading business schools, bringing international expertise and perspectives in risk management to Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate and professional community.\n\nThe program will take place on 1 December, from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m., at the Ivy Room, Cinnamon Grand Colombo. It will be led by Frankfurt School Competence Centre in Risk Management Senior International Adviser and Lead Consultant Dr. Joachim Bald.\n\nWith extensive advisory experience across Europe, Asia, Africa, and the Middle East, Dr. Bald has worked with leading financial institutions and development organisations, including the European Investment Bank (EIB), the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), KfW, Development Bank Ghana, RawBank, Alex Bank, and Banque Misr. He also serves on the Supervisory Boards of KMF Bank in Kazakhstan and Bailyk Finance in Kyrgyzstan."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-23-dailyftlk-0e35e254",
    "num": "dailyftlk-0e35e254",
