    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d23114f9d148490fc719cd9acc125885",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1874,
    "chunk_text": "With extensive advisory experience across Europe, Asia, Africa, and the Middle East, Dr. Bald has worked with leading financial institutions and development organisations, including the European Investment Bank (EIB), the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), KfW, Development Bank Ghana, RawBank, Alex Bank, and Banque Misr. He also serves on the Supervisory Boards of KMF Bank in Kazakhstan and Bailyk Finance in Kyrgyzstan.\n\nThe program will explore how directors and senior executives can move beyond conventional approaches to risk identification and incorporate analytical insights into strategic decision-making. As organisations face economic uncertainty, technological developments, and evolving regulatory and sustainability requirements, boards must be equipped to assess potential exposures, recognise early warning signals, and evaluate the implications of emerging risks.\n\nKey areas of focus will include quantitative risk assessment and management, risk analytics, key performance indicators (KPIs), scenario analysis, risk dashboards, and early warning indicators. The program will also address sustainability-related risks and the requirements of IFRS S1 and IFRS S2, alongside board risk oversight, reporting, and accountability. Practical case studies and applications will connect these concepts with the challenges faced by organisations and their boards.\n\nThrough this inaugural collaboration, the SLID and Frankfurt School of Finance and Management aim to establish a platform for continued knowledge exchange and international engagement, bringing global expertise and practical insights to Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate sector. By strengthening participants\u2019 understanding of risk analysis and oversight, the program seeks to support more informed decision-making, stronger governance practices, and greater organisational resilience."
  },
