    "md5": "f7231b40708a2ee38e903c2415c34612",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1653,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys enters healthcare business\n\nForges strategic partnership with international network of AI-powered preventive health screening centres, Nura operated by Japan\u2019s Fujifilm and India\u2019s Dr. Kutty\u2019s Healthcare\n\nJapanese-inspired health screening experience focused on the early detection of several major lifestyle-related diseases and common cancers\n\nNura, the international network of AI-powered preventive health screening centres operated by Fujifilm DKH LLC, is set to expand to Sri Lanka through a strategic partnership with Innovative Health Solutions Ltd., a subsidiary of the Hayleys Group.\n\nA health screening at Nura typically takes around 120 minutes, without the need for fasting or a doctor\u2019s prescription. Guests move through a carefully sequenced series of scans and tests covering major lifestyle-related diseases and common cancers, using advanced screening methods designed with comfort and safety in mind.\n\nThe screening experience includes a one-on-one doctor consultation, with the health report provided on-site, allowing guests to complete the entire process in a single visit. The streamlined process is designed with guest comfort in mind, making comprehensive health screening convenient and easy to fit into a busy routine.\n\nNura\u2019s screening features Fujifilm\u2019s globally trusted Japanese imaging technology, including ultra-low-dose CT systems that use up to 97% less radiation than conventional CT scans. Drawing on decades of Fujifilm\u2019s imaging research, AI-assisted technologies enhance image quality and help doctors identify potential areas of concern, supporting clinical assessment and decision-making."
