    "chunk_size_bytes": 1795,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Thailand exchange visa-free travel agreement\n\nColombo, Nov 23 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake met Thai Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Sihasak Phuangketkeow at the Presidential Secretariat yesterday (22), with the two countries exchanging an agreement on visa exemption for holders of ordinary passports.\n\nPhuangketkeow is visiting Sri Lanka as the Royal Representative of Thai King Maha Vajiralongkorn to attend the Royal Kathina Robe Offering Ceremony at the Asgiri Maha Viharaya in Kandy.\n\nDuring the meeting, the two leaders discussed ways to further strengthen bilateral relations, recalling the longstanding cultural and religious ties between Sri Lanka and Thailand.\n\nPresident Dissanayake said diplomatic visits of this nature would further reinforce the historic religious and cultural relations between the two countries.\n\nThe Thai Deputy Prime Minister said the Thai Prime Minister was keen to visit Sri Lanka. In response, President Dissanayake said he would invite the Thai Prime Minister to visit Sri Lanka to witness the historic Kandy Esala Perahera scheduled to be held in August next year.\n\nThe two sides also discussed expanding cooperation in trade, investment, tourism, agriculture and foreign employment.\n\nMeanwhile, the agreement on visa exemption for holders of ordinary passports was exchanged between Thai Deputy Prime Minister Sihasak Phuangketkeow and Sri Lankan Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Vijitha Herath.\n\nPhuangketkeow said the agreement would significantly contribute to promoting tourism between the two countries and strengthening business ties.\n\nHe also said Thailand's ready to provide technical assistance to Sri Lanka, particularly in the agricultural sector, when needed."
  },
