    "md5": "31e07c5072b01ca181f50907dfe09015",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2021,
    "chunk_text": "Aber Kawas becomes first Palestinian in New York state Senate history\n\nALJAZEERA - \u201cYou have all elected the first Palestinian in New York Senate history!\u201d Aber Kawas shouted over cheers to hundreds of Democratic Socialists of America (DSA) members at a bar on election night.\n\nAs chants of \u201cAber! Aber! Aber!\u201d filled the patio of Bohemia Beer Garden on November 3, media cameras flashed against her shiny blazer, embroidered with traditional Palestinian tatreez in gold and red.\n\nKawas, 34, made history as the first Palestinian, and the first Muslim woman, in the New York state Senate and the state legislature. She won the seat representing district 12 in northwest Queens, home to one of New York City\u2019s largest Arab communities, where nearly half of residents were born outside the United States.\n\nAs her speech ended and chants of \u201cFree, Free Palestine\u201d rang through the garden, Stylianos Karolidis, a DSA organiser on Kawas\u2019s team, stepped up to remind supporters that she really, really had not wanted to run for office. The DSA had to \u201chound her non-stop\u201d until she acquiesced, he said.\n\nKawas had worked with New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani when he was in the state legislature, so they knew her organising skills.\n\nKawas said she did not initially think it was possible to run for office without compromising her commitment to Palestinian liberation. Her victory, with 74.5 percent of the vote against Republican Han Khon To, was part of a broader tide of wins for pro-Palestine and democratic socialist candidates in the midterm elections, including Senator-elect Abdul El-Sayed in Michigan and Mayor-elect Nithya Raman in Los Angeles, California.\n\n\u201cThis midterm election showed a politics of human rights that includes Palestinians is a winning platform,\u201d said Institute for Middle East Understanding policy project executive director Margaret DeReus. \u201cFor millions of Americans, holding Israel accountable for genocide and supporting Palestinian freedom are the litmus test.\u201d"
  },
  {
