    "md5": "fcf17b0ebb49a717471fca980d78dafa",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 871,
    "chunk_text": "Collecting water is only part of the task. Storage must be safe and suited to local conditions. Water intended for drinking must be tested and treated appropriately. Authorities must map rainfall, identify suitable sites and protect downstream communities and ecosystems. The expertise exists. What is missing is the political commitment to coordinate it.\n\nSri Lanka cannot control the monsoon or climate patterns. It can control whether it prepares for the dry months. It can repair neglected tanks, protect catchments, build storage, enforce existing rules and make rainwater harvesting a normal feature of homes and public infrastructure.\n\nIf Sri Lanka one day finds itself running short of water, it will not be because the island was never blessed with rain. The rain will continue to fall. The question is whether the country will finally have the sense to save it."
