    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "750c2a475204e8477d1ee44f12ae28d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1630,
    "chunk_text": "Public opinion remains divided. While the memory of the 2019 Easter Sunday attacks drives strong support for heightened security, there is an equally strong demand for the protection of democratic values. The media and civil society organisations have become vital conduits for this national conversation, pushing for a narrative that views safety and freedom as complementary rather than mutually exclusive.\n\nAs Sri Lanka moves forward, the PSTA stands as an ambitious attempt to balance the necessity of national defense with the sanctity of individual rights. The true test of this legislation will lie in its application\u2014whether it can provide the security the nation demands while steadfastly honoring the freedoms that define a democratic society.\n\nIn the meantime, the current government should remember its election promise to repeal the Prevention of Terrorism Act (PTA) and similar laws. As the main stakeholder of the NPP government, JVP members suffered greatly under the PTA and experienced the dark side of this Act. If this government does not repeal the PTA and refrains from introducing a similar act like the PSTA, such a change is unlikely to ever occur under any future government.\n\nTherefore, they should consider how to improve the legal system to address the challenges of terrorism without introducing separate acts like the PSTA. Several countries have transitioned away from standalone emergency or special terrorism legislation, opting instead to integrate terrorism-related offenses into their broader criminal codes to ensure consistency with standard rule-of-law principles. Here are some examples:"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-23-dailymirrorlk-93c557cf",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-93c557cf",
    "date_str": "2026-11-23",
    "description": "Balancing Security and Rights:  The Evolution of Sri Lanka\u2019s Anti-Terrorism Framework",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Balancing-Security-and-Rights-The-Evolution-of-Sri-Lankas-Anti-Terrorism-Framework/172-355526",
