    "chunk_size_bytes": 1927,
    "chunk_text": "India-funded KKS Harbour, Jaffna airport projects stalled, claims Indian MP\n\nColombo, Nov. 23 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Indian MP Dr. Thol. Thirumavalavan has accused the Sri Lankan Government of failing to make progress on the development of Kankesanthurai (KKS) Harbour and Jaffna International Airport, despite India\u2019s willingness to fund the projects.\n\nThe leader of the Viduthalai Chiruthaigal Katchi (VCK) made the allegation at a media briefing held at the Jaffna Press Club on Sunday (22), claiming that the Government was reluctant to develop the two facilities as it could boost economic activity in the Northern and Eastern Provinces.\n\nHe alleged that Sri Lanka\u2019s development approach was centred on the interests of the South, with commercial connectivity being channelled through Colombo rather than allowing the North and East to benefit from direct international links.\n\nThirumavalavan said the KKS Harbour and Jaffna International Airport could play a significant role in the economic development of the North and East, adding that India had offered assistance to take over and develop both facilities.\n\nHe also raised concerns over disruptions to flights between Jaffna and Chennai in recent days due to fog and air pollution, which had reduced visibility and prevented aircraft from landing.\n\nThe MP said he was shocked to learn that runway lights had not been installed at Jaffna International Airport, claiming that the lack of basic infrastructure was affecting connectivity and discouraging Indian businesspeople and potential investors from travelling directly to Jaffna.\n\nHe alleged that investors were instead compelled to enter Sri Lanka through Colombo, limiting opportunities for the Northern region.\n\nThirumavalavan said he would raise the matter with the Indian Government and lodge a complaint with India\u2019s Minister of External Affairs over the alleged delays in developing the harbour and airport."
  },
