    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4f34831b9b5b9d9607d12a401fd347d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1862,
    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka brings together leading experts to analyse National Budget 2027\n\nThe Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka) hosted a\u00a0comprehensive post-budget seminar last week to provide members, business leaders, tax professionals and policymakers with an in-depth analysis of the key economic, fiscal and taxation proposals contained in National Budget 2027.\n\nHeld at CA Sri Lanka, the seminar attracted over 700 participants, both in person and virtually, and featured leading experts from the public and private sectors who shared insights on the Budget\u2019s potential impact on economic growth, investment, taxation, exports, public finances, and tax administration.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Tishan Subasinghe, President of CASri Lanka, noted that Budget 2027 marks a significant phase in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic journey as\u00a0 the\u00a0 country\u00a0 transitionsfrom a period of stabilisation towards sustainable growth and development. He also spoke on the performance of the country\u2019s revenue-generating agencies and highlighted the importance of maintaining fiscal discipline while strengthening foreign exchange earnings, investment and economic resilience.\n\nSaman Srilal, Chairman of the CA Sri Lanka Faculty of Taxation, observed that the Budget places considerable emphasis on productive sectors of\u00a0 the\u00a0 economy\u00a0 throughinvestments in export-oriented manufacturing,\u00a0 tourism,agriculture, technology, digitalisation and SMEs. He welcomed several tax measures including personal income tax relief, investment incentives to encourage export-oriented projects, and initiatives aimed at strengthening tax administration and improving compliance processes.\n\nDelivering the budget highlights, Sulaiman Nishtar, Partner and Head of Tax at EY Sri Lanka, provided a detailed overview\u00a0 of\u00a0 the\u00a0 Budget proposals and the legislative process."
  },
