    "md5": "cccd54f53f3fb92f4933cd44c39f2f73",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1676,
    "chunk_text": "Morison embarks on exports   journey with medical marketing operations in Cambodia\n\nDinesh Athapaththu formalising the commencement of the pharmaceutical export operations in Cambodia.\n\nMorison, a Sri Lankan pharmaceutical manufacturing with over 60 years of industrial expertise and a member of the Hemas Group, recently embarked on its landmark exports journey, establishing its own medical marketing operations in Cambodia.\n\nThe first export consignment was shipped to the country on 11th November 2026, marking a significant milestone and a historic first in the company\u2019s journey of taking home-grown pharmaceuticals to the world.\n\nThe endeavour distinguishes Morison as the first Sri Lankan pharma manufacturer to initiate medical marketing operations in a foreign country through its own team of medical representatives. Headed by a Sri Lankan country manager, Morison has already secured thirteen product registrations in Cambodia, with another seven currently in the process of being approved.\n\nReflecting on the significance of this milestone for the Group, Murtaza Esufally, Chairman of the Hemas Healthcare Cluster said, \u201cFor the past 70 years, Hemas has been importing pharmaceuticals to Sri Lanka. Therefore, witnessing Hemas-manufactured pharmaceuticals being exported to another country for the first time is\u00a0a particularly proud moment for us. It marks a significant milestone in our journey and reflects our ambition to take Sri Lankan pharmaceutical manufacturing beyond our shores.\u201d\n\nThe inaugural shipment comprised three of Morison\u2019s newly launched niche novel therapies, carrying the same brand names under which they are marketed in Sri Lanka."
