    "md5": "3e309fa42f61570f70bf3207f613108f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1543,
    "chunk_text": "Reflecting on the significance of this milestone for the Group, Murtaza Esufally, Chairman of the Hemas Healthcare Cluster said, \u201cFor the past 70 years, Hemas has been importing pharmaceuticals to Sri Lanka. Therefore, witnessing Hemas-manufactured pharmaceuticals being exported to another country for the first time is\u00a0a particularly proud moment for us. It marks a significant milestone in our journey and reflects our ambition to take Sri Lankan pharmaceutical manufacturing beyond our shores.\u201d\n\nThe inaugural shipment comprised three of Morison\u2019s newly launched niche novel therapies, carrying the same brand names under which they are marketed in Sri Lanka.\n\nCambodia\u2019s market of approximately 18 million people is currently valued at nearly USD 350 million and dependent on imports for nearly 95 percent of its pharmaceutical needs. The country operates in line with WHO GMP guidelines, making it a natural first destination for medicines manufactured to international\u00a0\u00a0standards in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe timing of the first shipment also carries a special significance for Morison. Exactly four years ago, on 11th November 2022, the company announced its entry into the branded generics space in Sri Lanka, making 11th November a special day in the Morison calendar.\n\nLeading the Cambodian operations as Country Manager is Prabuddha Walpita, previously Senior Manager Commercial at Morison. Having been with the company for the last 10 years, he has built his career at Morison, rising through the ranks across a variety of roles."
