    "md5": "7631e4a6e132595c4ed1a29ff46f60d5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1927,
    "chunk_text": "Gardiner Group acquires The Pickle Island in strategic leisure expansion\n\nFounders Dilshan and Ronali Michael with Aravinda de Silva and Sanjeev and Seshaan Gardiner\n\nGardiner Group has acquired The Pickle Island, a Sri Lankan pickleball venture focused on developing the sport and its growing community, marking its entry into the country\u2019s emerging sports and recreational leisure market.\n\nWith seasoned investor and entrepreneur Aravinda de Silva joining as a partner, the acquisition represents the first step in what the group describes as a broader investment strategy to build a portfolio of diversified leisure businesses in Sri Lanka.\n\nGardiner Group is a Sri Lankan hospitality and investment group with a long-standing legacy in the country\u2019s hospitality industry. Its portfolio includes the iconic Galle Face Hotel, established in 1864, Ceylon Hotels Corporation PLC, with its portfolio of hotels and resthouses and The Kandy Hotels Company (1938) PLC, which owns the historic Queen\u2019s Hotel and Hotel Suisse in Kandy.\n\nThe group also holds 50:50 joint venture interests in Uga Giri Ella and Radisson Hotel Kandy.\n\nBuilding on this established hospitality heritage, Gardiner Group is expanding its business interests into complementary areas of leisure, lifestyle and experiences, reinforcing its long-term commitment to Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality and leisure sectors.\n\nGardiner Group Director Investments and M&A Seshaan Gardiner said, \u201cOur heritage is in hospitality but our vision extends well beyond the traditional hotel experience, as we see significant opportunities to invest in Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving leisure and lifestyle landscape. The Pickle Island represents one of several strategic investments we intend to make as we expand into new sectors, create meaningful experiences and build on our long-term confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s potential, both for those who call it home and those who visit.\u201d"
  },
