    "chunk_text": "The property itself straddles past and present. EKHO Belihuloya now has 16 rooms, all in the deluxe category, after the old staff quarters upstairs were converted into guest rooms. The larger rooms on the far side interconnect for families, Dias noted. The grounds stretch across more than five acres.\n\nThe guests who dip their feet in the water are soon surrounded by shoals of small fish nibbling at the skin, a free, natural version of the fish pedicure that spas elsewhere charge for.\n\nThe island\u2019s rocky streams are home to the Ceylon stone sucker, Garra ceylonensis, known locally as \u2018gal paandiya\u2019, an endemic fish whose habit of nibbling dead skin has made it a sought-after \u201cdoctor fish\u201d in the spa trade. A sucker-like disc lets it cling to rocks and graze on algae in fast-flowing water.\n\nScientists have found that populations in different river basins, though identical in appearance, belong to six genetically distinct lineages and the species\u2019 popularity in the spa and aquarium trade has seen it listed nationally as near threatened.\n\n\u201cThe staff we have right now are from the old staff. They have been working here for a long time and they know those signature dishes,\u201d Dias explained.\n\nHe was referring to the fried fish and fried \u2018handalla\u2019 that even the first-time guests still ask about when they call. The rice and curry buffet now runs at weekends, when the crowds return.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s not much but they love to have that next to the river,\u201d he added.\n\n\u201cEarlier it was more of a rice and curry spot that everyone stopped at. Now we have added more international dishes and more dishes that reflect the ingredients of the area that we could source,\u201d Hamid observed.\n\nBeyond the table, EKHO has partnered with operator Belihuloya Safari on customisable packages to Nonpareil Estate and Baker\u2019s Bend, each taking in two or three points of interest.\n\nStargazing, signature dining and in time, glamping on the grounds are also in the pipeline."
