    "chunk_text": "LankaPay is owned by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) and 24 licensed commercial banks, and the Central Bank holds the largest single stake at 19.59 percent, according to the company. The two state banks, People\u2019s Bank and Bank of Ceylon, hold a further 27.80 percent between them, which takes the combined state-linked holding to 47.39 percent. The company\u2019s Chairman is appointed by the CBSL Governor.\n\nUnder the draft rules, controllers will be required to notify the DPA within 72 hours of becoming aware of a breach, and to inform affected individuals where the risk to them is high. Data subject rights under Part II and the penalty regime under Part VII are still waiting on a further gazette order. Part VII provides for fines of up to Rs.10 million for each failure to comply with a DPA directive."
