    "chunk_size_bytes": 912,
    "chunk_text": "On appeal , the Supreme Cour t under took a detailed examination of the legal principles governing oral contracts. While reaffirming that oral agreements are recognised under both Roman-Dutch and English law, as well as by Sri Lankan courts, the Court emphasised that a party alleging the existence of an oral agreement bears the burden of proving it. In this case, it found that the evidence fell short of establishing, on a balance of probabilities, that such an agreement had ever been concluded.\n\nThe ruling underscores the evidential hurdle facing parties who seek to establish contractual rights founded on conversations and understandings that were never reduced to writing.\n\nAvindra Rodrigo, President\u2019s Counsel, with Christina Hettiarachchi and Hashendra Jayasuriya, instructed by F J & G de Saram, appeared for the Prince, while Roshan Hettiarachchi, instructed by Kalindi Silva, appeared for Rafick."
