    "chunk_size_bytes": 1542,
    "chunk_text": "FitsAir resumes  direct flights  between Colombo  and Chennai\n\nFitsAir, Sri Lanka\u2019s first privately owned international airline, has announced the resumption of direct flights between Colombo and Chennai, effective December 15, 2026.\n\nThe service will operate daily, offering passengers greater convenience and flexibility when travelling between the two cities.\n\nTo mark the relaunch, FitsAir is offering introductory return fares from Rs.66,000, inclusive of a 20kg checked baggage allowance and 7kg of hand luggage.\n\nThe airline said the resumption of the Chennai service strengthens its presence in the Indian market while expanding regional connectivity. As a major commercial, healthcare and cultural hub in South India, Chennai plays a significant role in business, tourism and personal travel between the two countries.\n\nThe daily flights are expected to further support these links, giving travellers an affordable option while contributing to the growing economic and tourism ties between Sri Lanka and India.\n\nCommenting on the relaunch, a senior FitsAir representative noted, \u201cThe resumption of our Chennai service reflects our commitment to building a stronger, more sustainable airline, with a network that responds to market demand while remaining true to our promise of delivering the right price and a dependable travel experience.\u201d\n\nFitsAir noted that the Airline continues to position itself as a practical and accessible choice for regional travellers, prioritising affordability, punctuality and hassle-free travel."
