    "md5": "44ea12aa2af16ac49eea7d54645286da",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1541,
    "chunk_text": "CHC plots 50-hotel EKHO push from wayside rest houses\n\nBRAND RECAST FOR YOUNGER TRAVELLERS, WITH ELLA, BELIHULOYA AND KITHULGALA FORMING NEW ADVENTURE CLUSTER\n\nMGT. CONTRACTS TO CARRY EXPANSION BEYOND CHC\u2019S OWN REST HOUSE PORTFOLIO\n\nCeylon Hotels Corporation PLC (CHC) is setting its EKHO Hotels and Resorts brand on course for 50 hotels within five years, reinventing its historic wayside rest houses for a new generation of travellers and taking on properties under management contracts to reach the target, according to a senior official.\n\n\u201cThe whole idea for us is to convert more of the rest houses into the EKHO brand, but the long term is to get 50 EKHO hotels,\u201d CHC Marketing and Communications Manager Sherin Hamid said.\n\nHowever, the ambition marks a sharp acceleration for a brand launched in 2016 through the conversion of properties such as the Polonnaruwa Rest House, now EKHO Lake House. EKHO is taking its count to seven as Belihuloya and Kithulgala join its hotels in Bentota, Tissamaharama, Sigiriya, Polonnaruwa and Ella. Reaching 50 would mean adding close to nine hotels a year, roughly 12 times the pace at which it assembled its first seven over the past decade.\n\nWith CHC running just three other rest houses with accommodation, in Dambulla, Pussellawa and Ambepussa, even a full conversion would lift the brand to only 10 hotels. The balance is set to come from properties EKHO will operate under management contracts, an asset-light route that lets the brand scale without carrying the full cost of ownership."
  },
