    "chunk_text": "Complaints on frauds and scams lodged with the FCRD against banks and finance companies rose by about 80 percent between 2023 and 2025, according to FCRD officials.\n\nMeanwhile, Visa data shows Malaysia\u2019s card-not-present fraud rate climbed 44 percent in 2025, even as the Asia Pacific average fell by 15 percent.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s 2023 financial consumer protection regulations already hold banks liable for fraud losses unless the customer\u2019s negligence is proved, but set no reporting window, liability cap or refund deadline for card fraud. CBSL in May directed banks to check card transactions before approving them, while a central fraud monitoring system at LankaPay is not due until September 2027.\n\n\u201cIndia has shown the way. Our regulator can do the same,\u201d Dr. Pinto stressed."
