    "chunk_text": "One victim told jurors that he had sex with her \u201cabout 20 or 30 times\u201d over several months, regularly visited her home and considered her his girlfriend.\n\nHe had fallen in love but kept their relationship secret because Bowen had \u201cdrummed it\u201d into him that he must not tell anyone, the court heard.\n\nFormer pupil Tobias Oliver told jurors Bowen flirted and openly discussed sex in class.\n\nHe said she once sat on a desk and slowly opened her legs, revealing her underwear.\n\nMr Oliver also recalled her discussing sexual positions from the Kama Sutra during a lesson.\n\n\u201cThe topics of conversation in class often strayed away from chemistry and became quite sexual,\u201d he said.\n\nBowen denied the allegations as \u201ctotal fabrication\u201d and claimed a medical condition made sex difficult and painful.\n\nShe denied flirting, saying: \u201cI didn\u2019t flirt with students, I was just friendly.\u201d\n\nDefending her clothes, she said she \u201cwasn\u2019t going to dress like Margaret Thatcher\u201d."
