    "chunk_size_bytes": 634,
    "chunk_text": "The Houthis have claimed a series of attacks on Saudi energy facilities in recent months. Reported targets include the country's East-West Pipeline and refineries in Jazan in the south and Ras Tanura in the east. However, Saudi authorities have yet to officially confirm attacks on these refineries.\n\nThe Red Sea shipping routes near Saudi Arabia's energy facilities are major maritime trade corridors linking Europe and Asia. Analysts warn that if damage from attacks on energy facilities and other infrastructure is confirmed, both crude oil and petroleum product shipping rates and international oil prices could fluctuate sharply."
