    "chunk_size_bytes": 857,
    "chunk_text": "Army rowers dominate Defence Services Championship\n\nColombo, Nov. 23 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Sri Lanka Army emerged as the overall champions of the 14th Defence Services Rowing Championship held at the Diyawanna Rowing Centre, winning six of the seven events contested.\n\nThe Army secured both the men\u2019s and women\u2019s championships, with its rowers winning six gold, four silver and two bronze medals.\n\nIn the men\u2019s category, the Army won three gold, two silver and two bronze medals, while its women\u2019s team secured three gold and two silver medals.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Air Force finished as the overall runners-up with one gold, three silver and four bronze medals. Its men\u2019s team won one gold, two silver and one bronze, while the women\u2019s team secured one silver and three bronze medals.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Navy won one bronze medal in the men\u2019s category."
