    "chunk_size_bytes": 1776,
    "chunk_text": "Zelenskyy says Ukraine behind drone attacks on Russian ships near Libya\n\nALJAZEERA - Ukraine\u2019s president says forces sank \u2060\u2060a Russian warship off the coast of Libya, hailing an \u201cexemplary Ukrainian operation in response to Russia\u2019s war\u201d.\n\nPresident Volodymyr Zelenskyy said on Monday that Ukrainian forces also hit a Russian dry \u2060\u2060cargo ship used to transport weapons.\n\nZelenskyy said the Merkury, one of Russia\u2019s newest warships, sank after Ukrainian forces launched seven naval drones on Sunday. A KA-27 combat helicopter was also destroyed in the attack, according to his statement.\n\nHe confirmed that Ukraine\u2019s forces also attacked the cargo ship Angara. Libya\u2019s eastern health ministry in Benghazi said all crew members had been rescued and were receiving treatment.\n\nAuthorities in eastern Libya said the ship was docked in the port of Benghazi when the explosion occurred.\n\n\u201cThe ship was en route back to Russia and its stop was for refuelling and resupply. It is suspected that the ship was attacked by drones.\n\nThe United Nations has called for an independent investigation into Sunday\u2019s drone attacks on the two ships.\n\nOn Monday, the United Nations Support Mission in Libya (UNSMIL) expressed \u201cserious concern\u201d over the attacks, calling for \u201can immediate, independent and transparent investigation\u201d.\n\n\u201cLibya cannot afford and must not become a battleground for foreign conflicts,\u201d UNSMIL wrote on X.\n\nThe eastern administration did not identify who was behind Sunday\u2019s attack but said Libya was \u201cnot a party to the Russian-Ukrainian war\u201d.\n\nThe oil-rich nation of Libya has been divided between the government in Tripoli and a rival administration in the east since the overthrow of longtime ruler Muammar Gaddafi in 2011."
