    "md5": "23ed46cb6ad6b0ae4d218cbd10525c03",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1585,
    "chunk_text": "Zimbabwean Pastor Uebert Angel arrested over sexual assault\n\nNEWS GHANA - Zimbabwe police arrested preacher Uebert Angel, founder of Spirit Embassy and the country\u2019s ambassador-at-large, on 22 November 2026 over allegations of indecent assault and sodomy.\n\nUebert Angel shares close relations with pastor Jerome Fernando in Sri Lanka\n\nThe Zimbabwe Republic Police (ZRP) confirmed the arrest in a post on social media that afternoon. \u201cThe ZRP confirms the arrest of Prophet Uebert Angel this afternoon on indecent assault and sodomy allegations. More details to follow in due course,\u201d the statement said.\n\nNational police spokesperson Commissioner Paul Nyathi confirmed the development, saying further details would be released in due course, the state-owned Herald reported on 23 November 2026. The police have not said who made the allegations, when the alleged offences took place, or when he will appear in court.\n\nSeveral Zimbabwean outlets reported that he was arrested during a Sunday church service at the Hippodrome in Harare. The Herald and NewsDay placed the arrest at the Hippodrome, the Harare headquarters of Angel\u2019s Spirit Embassy, ZimDaily reported.\n\nAngel, whose birth name is Uebert Mudzanire, is one of Zimbabwe\u2019s most prominent religious figures and one of its most visible diplomats, according to EEW Magazine. He holds the title of presidential envoy and ambassador-at-large.\n\nNo public response from Angel, his lawyers or his church could be found at the time of publication. An arrest is not a charge, and the allegations have not been tested in court."
  },
