    "md5": "b80513c2d55eff3b8aacf02c94afd1f5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1954,
    "chunk_text": "Bangladesh vows to arrest Hasina if she returns from India\n\nReuters\u00a0- Bangladesh will arrest and jail former \u200bPrime Minister Sheikh Hasina if she returns from India, a senior government minister said, as her plans to come home in \u200cDecember fuel political tension and renewed street violence.\n\nDhaka is instead seeking Hasina's extradition from India, where she has lived since fleeing Bangladesh in 2024, and expects New Delhi to comply with an existing extradition treaty, State Minister for Foreign Affairs Shama Obaed Islam told Reuters.\n\nIndia's foreign ministry did not immediately respond to a request for \u200bcomment. In April, the ministry said it was examining Bangladesh's request to extradite Hasina.\n\nHasina faces a death sentence in Bangladesh and \u200bher Awami League party is banned following the 2024 uprising that ended her long rule. The United Nations \u2060has said as many as 1,400 people were killed during the unrest.\n\nHasina fled Dhaka in August 2024 as protests demanding her resignation swept the \u200bcountry. She has since sought a new passport and identity card ahead of a planned return in December, requests the government has rejected.\n\n\"As soon as \u200bshe tries to enter Bangladesh, she will be arrested. And she will be taken to jail, and the law will take its course,\" Obaed said in an interview on Sunday.\n\n\"We would like India to honour the extradition treaty and return her as a convict, and the law will take its course. She (Hasina) will have to \u200bface the music.\"\n\nThe standoff has brought Hasina's Awami League supporters out on the streets. The party this month announced a week of protests and rallies \u200bin support of Hasina's return, culminating in a nationwide lockdown on November 19.\n\nPolice have recorded dozens of crude bomb blasts and incidents of arson targeting vehicles \u200cin at \u2060least 28 districts over the past 10 days, with several police officers and civilians injured, according to local media."
  },
