    "chunk_text": "Through Oceanswell, she has worked to strengthen marine science capacity in Sri Lanka by training and mentoring a new generation of marine scientists.\n\nThe MBA said her Fellowship recognised not only her individual achievements but also the growing contribution of Sri Lanka\u2019s marine science community.\n\nIn 2020, she received the inaugural Maxwell-Hanrahan Award in Field Biology and was named Sea Hero of the Year by Scuba Diving magazine.\n\nHer other accolades include the Vanithabhimani Lifetime Achievement Award and the T\u00e4llberg-SNF-Eliasson Global Leadership Prize in 2021, and the British Ecological Society\u2019s Equity and Diversity Champion title in 2023.\n\nIn 2026, she was selected as a Thinker-in-Residence at the Forrest Research Foundation.\n\nShe is also an Adjunct Research Fellow at the Oceans Institute of the University of Western Australia."
