    "md5": "1c59892d928aa51b8af18c8e23274021",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1764,
    "chunk_text": "AKD, take that first step \u2014 The journey from which  there is no return\n\nAn invocation to courage, conscience and the unfinished destiny of Sri Lanka\n\n\u201cIf no one responds to your call, then go your own way alone.\u201d\n\nAKD, take that first step. Take it with the courage of a man who knows that history does not always announce the hour of its arrival. Sometimes it comes silently, without ceremony, without the thunder of drums or the applause of assembled multitudes. Sometimes it arrives disguised as uncertainty, demanding of one solitary individual the courage to venture where generations before him feared to tread.\n\nTake that first step, AKD. For the road ahead is not one upon which the timid may travel, nor one from which the determined may return unchanged.\n\nYou may not recognize the landscape into which you are entering. Its mountains may appear unfamiliar, its valleys treacherous, its pathways concealed beneath the accumulated dust of centuries. The comforting landmarks of yesterday may disappear behind you. Those who once walked beside you may hesitate at the threshold, and those who await you beyond it may speak in unfamiliar voices, carrying unfamiliar dreams.\n\nYet do not mistake unfamiliarity for hostility, nor hesitation for betrayal.\n\nFor somewhere beyond the boundaries of party, class, caste, creed and ethnicity, there are men and women who have waited all their lives for this journey to begin. They may never have sung your songs, carried your banners or embraced your political philosophy. They may have opposed you yesterday and may question you tomorrow. But in the deepest chambers of their conscience, they too have heard the same ancient summons.\n\nIt is the summons of a nation yearning to become worthy of its own people."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-23-dailyftlk-20058f28",
