    "md5": "2f9fed10bb604207554295f1f413853e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1910,
    "chunk_text": "And now, perhaps, the hour has arrived when that ancient promise demands more than another speech, another election, another government or another procession of triumphant politicians.\n\nNot merely a change of rulers, but a change in the very meaning of rule.\n\nNot merely the redistribution of political power, but the restoration of moral purpose to public life.\n\nAKD, your greatest companions on this journey may not be those who applauded you most loudly at the beginning. They may be those who challenge your assumptions, question your certainties and insist that the dream of a new Sri Lanka must be larger than the ideology of any single movement.\n\nFor a nation\u2019s rebirth cannot be accomplished by the faithful alone. It requires the courage of former adversaries, the wisdom of dissenters, the imagination of the young and the experience of those who have witnessed both the triumphs and the failures of generations past.\n\nLet the Tamil mother who still waits for answers, the Muslim citizen who seeks security without suspicion, the Sinhala villager who demands a fair chance in life, and the young professional who wonders whether to remain in the country of his birth all recognize themselves in the future you seek to build.\n\nLet no citizen be asked to surrender an identity in order to claim a place in the nation.\n\nAnd remember: the journey is irreversible not because one leader must remain forever in power, but because a people, once awakened to their own dignity, must never again be persuaded to surrender it.\n\nThere will be dark mornings. There will be betrayal and disappointment. There will be moments when the burden of expectation weighs more heavily than the machinery of government itself. The applause of the multitude may fade, and the solitude of leadership may become almost unbearable.\n\nBut history has never reserved its finest pages for those who chose comfort over conviction."
  },
