    "chunk_text": "Some foreign nationals have arrived in Sri Lanka and taken jobs that are meant for our own citizens. Some have set up businesses, including guesthouses, surf schools, caf\u00e9s and restaurants, and some of these establishments do not even welcome locals. In our own country, Sri Lankans are being made to feel unwelcome in places run by visitors. How can this happen? Who issued the approvals? Who is checking the visas? Who is collecting the taxes?\n\nOur business community has already sounded the alarm. In August, the BRICS Chamber of Commerce (Sri Lanka) wrote to the President and the Minister of Foreign Affairs about the vacancies in both the United States and China, urging the appointment of envoys with proven diplomatic skill and commercial standing. Our apparel exporters, our investors and the hundreds of thousands of workers who depend on them cannot afford to have Sri Lanka\u2019s case presented by default.\n\nI therefore urge the Government to nominate ambassadors to Washington and Beijing without further delay, and to place those names before the Committee on High Posts at the earliest opportunity. Those chosen must be selected on merit \u2013 for their experience, their judgement and their understanding of trade and investment \u2013 not as a reward for political loyalty. And they should be appointed together. Filling both posts at the same time would itself send a message, East and West alike, that Sri Lanka gives equal weight to both relationships. An empty embassy in one capital is a misfortune; empty embassies in both, for months on end, risk being read as indifference, and that is a message no non-aligned nation can afford to send."
