    "chunk_text": "I therefore urge the Government to nominate ambassadors to Washington and Beijing without further delay, and to place those names before the Committee on High Posts at the earliest opportunity. Those chosen must be selected on merit \u2013 for their experience, their judgement and their understanding of trade and investment \u2013 not as a reward for political loyalty. And they should be appointed together. Filling both posts at the same time would itself send a message, East and West alike, that Sri Lanka gives equal weight to both relationships. An empty embassy in one capital is a misfortune; empty embassies in both, for months on end, risk being read as indifference, and that is a message no non-aligned nation can afford to send.\n\nAs a former Deputy Minister of Tourism, I have watched with pride as our tourism industry has recovered from the Easter Sunday attacks, the pandemic and the economic crisis. Last year, Sri Lanka welcomed 2,362,521 tourists, the highest number in our history, surpassing the previous record set in 2018. Tourism feeds families in every corner of this island: the three-wheeler driver, the cook, the guide, the fisherman who supplies the beach restaurant. But I am deeply concerned about what is happening in some of our best-known resorts.\n\nSome foreign nationals have arrived in Sri Lanka and taken jobs that are meant for our own citizens. Some have set up businesses, including guesthouses, surf schools, caf\u00e9s and restaurants, and some of these establishments do not even welcome locals. In our own country, Sri Lankans are being made to feel unwelcome in places run by visitors. How can this happen? Who issued the approvals? Who is checking the visas? Who is collecting the taxes?"
