    "md5": "0dd13a88929c087ae9a47e85c508e1fe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1358,
    "chunk_text": "I have therefore called upon the Government to take four steps:\n\n1. Carry out a comprehensive, district-by-district audit of foreign-run tourism businesses, so that we know the true scale of the problem.\n\n3. Introduce clear and transparent rules for foreigners who genuinely wish to invest or work in tourism, so that the honest are welcomed and the dishonest are removed.\n\n4. Make it unlawful for any tourism establishment in Sri Lanka to refuse service to Sri Lankans on the ground of their nationality.\n\nThe threads of this argument run together. A warship in distress, a tariff in Washington, an investment from Beijing and a caf\u00e9 in Arugam Bay may seem to be unrelated matters. They are not. Each tests whether we are willing to put the interests of Sri Lanka and its people first \u2013 calmly, consistently and without fear. Each demands that we know our strength, respect our obligations and speak with one voice. And that voice must be heard where it matters most: we cannot speak with one voice in Washington and Beijing if there is no one there to speak for us.\n\nMrs. Bandaranaike showed us that a small country can be respected by all and dominated by none, if it knows its strength, acts with consistency and speaks with one voice. Friends with all, subservient to none. That must be our foreign policy, our economic policy and our tourism policy."
