    "md5": "dd01f206fdd125acb8dec1de506ff0e0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "While this is good progress, the global trade landscape is shifting rapidly. With world trade projected to outperform IMF and WTO forecasts in 2026, and India aggressively pursuing FTAs with the EU and the UK, Sri Lanka must inject urgency into its trade agenda and rapidly build its institutional negotiation capacity. Our forthcoming work includes suggestions for how a deeper FTA with India can unlock substantial economic dividends for Sri Lanka.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s economy has successfully stabilised following a deep crisis. However, insulating the country from future shocks requires a relentless commitment to economic transformation. The 2027 Budget sets a strong, forward-looking direction that echoes several core ODI/CEPA proposals. Yet, against a backdrop of global economic volatility, the window for action is narrow\n\nInstead, policymakers must urgently collaborate with the private sector to remove structural bottlenecks \u2013 such as cumbersome business regulations, infrastructure gaps, skill shortages and limited SME finance \u2013 to unlock the potential of the broader productive economy. Following the blueprint of successful East Asian economies, any State incentives and support must strictly be targeted, time-bound and performance-based to ensure global market competitiveness.\n\nThe 2027 Budget rightly positions the digital economy as a major pillar of Sri Lanka\u2019s future growth model, moving beyond recovery towards a knowledge- and technology-based economy. To remain competitive, Sri Lanka must transition from relying on low wages and natural resources to competing on skills, innovation, technology adoption and digital connectivity.\u00a0 As highlighted in a recent ODI Global / SLASSCOM report, many trading firms already leverage e-commerce for global reach,\u00a0 but critical gaps in customs logistics, cross-border payments, cybersecurity and digital literacy require urgent, targeted policy intervention."
  },
