    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka reach two knockout stages as UK lands 2035 World Cup\n\nSri Lanka Set Up Emerging Nations Trophy Final Against Ireland\n\nNov.24 (Mirror Sports) - Sri Lanka will face Ireland in the final of the ICC Women's Emerging Nations Trophy 2026 after both teams completed unbeaten Super Six campaigns, winning all three of their matches in Ajman.\n\nSri Lanka secured a thrilling four-run victory over Pakistan, while Ireland defeated the Netherlands by 44 runs to book their places in the title decider. The final is scheduled to take place at the Seven Districts Sports Club on Wednesday, November 25.\n\nImesha Dulani and Sathya Sandeepani played key roles in Sri Lanka's narrow victory over Pakistan. Dulani top-scored with 56 off 38 deliveries, helping Sri Lanka post 140 for six after being asked to bat first.\n\nPakistan struggled early in their chase, losing three wickets for just 16 runs. Omaima Sohail (36) and Tuba Hassan (24) attempted to revive the innings, while Tasmia Rubab provided late resistance with an unbeaten 23 off just 11 balls.\n\nHowever, Sandeepani claimed three wickets for 29 runs as Pakistan were restricted to 136 for nine, handing Sri Lanka a four-run win. Umm-e-Hani also impressed with the ball, taking three wickets for 17 runs.\n\nIreland secured their place in the final with a convincing 44-run victory over the Netherlands. Lara Maritz led the batting effort with an unbeaten 57 off 45 balls, while Cara Murray delivered an outstanding bowling performance, claiming five wickets for just 17 runs.\n\nIreland posted 162 for three before bowling out the Netherlands for 118 in 19.3 overs to complete their unbeaten Super Six campaign."
