    "language": "en",
    "md5": "db006522537781f64e9ce922ae8c040b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1588,
    "chunk_text": "He urged the Election Commission to ensure Provincial Council elections are held at least in 2027. He noted that while the Commission had most recently conducted the Local Government elections, the provincial polls had been postponed for several years. The absence of elected Provincial Councils deprived people of their democratic right to representation at the provincial level, he said, and he urged the authorities to use the funds allocated for elections to hold the polls next year.\n\nLarge quantities of beer bottles, medical vials and plastic waste were frequently washing ashore along the district\u2019s coastline, much of it believed to come from vessels at sea rather than from coastal residents. He asked the Government to provide specialised beach-cleaning machinery to the district, noting that the Kaluwanchikudy Pradeshiya Sabha had also submitted a proposal for such machinery. He also called for adequate public toilet facilities in public places throughout the district.\n\nHe also called for the additional allowance paid to parliamentary employees to be reviewed and increased. At Rs. 750, it had remained unchanged for about 10 years despite the rising cost of living and the responsibilities these employees carry.\n\nConcluding, Rasamanickam said the Government must show its commitment to human rights, democratic governance and accountability through concrete action rather than assurances given in Parliament or before international institutions.\n\n\u201cRespect for fundamental rights, accountability and the rule of law must begin with the Government itself,\u201d he said."
