    "md5": "c386254d69102e8ed5bfbe03544e03bc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1955,
    "chunk_text": "Ceylon Chamber secures new institutional link to Italy\u2019s business network\n\nSigns MoU with Italian Union of Chambers of Commerce, Industry, Handicraft and Agriculture\n\nSri Lankan businesses will have new avenues to access the Italian market and establish commercial partnerships following a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signed between The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce and Unioncamere, the Italian Union of Chambers of Commerce, Industry, Handicraft and Agriculture.\n\nThe agreement establishes a framework for direct engagement between the business communities of the two countries, with a focus on trade promotion, investment opportunities and business collaboration.\n\nThe signing took place at Unioncamere headquarters in Piazza Sallustio, Italy, with representatives of Unioncamere and the Italian diplomatic mission in attendance. Representatives of the Ceylon Chamber, the Sri Lanka\u2013Italy Business Council (SLITBC) and the Sri Lankan diplomatic mission joined the ceremony virtually from Sri Lanka.\n\nRepresenting Unioncamere were President Andrea Prete and Internationalisation Manager Pietro Infante. The Sri Lankan participants included Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Italy Satya Rodrigo, Minister and Head of Chancellery at the Sri Lankan Embassy in Rome Dhawood Amanullan, Ambassador of Italy to Sri Lanka Damiano Francovigh and Ceylon Chamber CEO/General Secretary Shiran Fernando and SLITBC President Dushy Jayaweera whilst Immediate Past President Daminda Mulgama, of SLITBC also joined the ceremony virtually, alongside other representatives of both institutions.\n\nThe agreement provides a direct institutional link to Italy\u2019s extensive chamber network, creating opportunities for Sri Lankan companies to identify business partners, explore market opportunities and establish commercial relationships. Planned areas of cooperation include business delegations, B2B matchmaking, knowledge exchange and the promotion of trade and investment."
  },
