    "md5": "31c9f7e0bc1aaf9fee4b51d733bc2ade",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 750,
    "chunk_text": "It can preserve the land that absorbs water, build infrastructure that manages excess rainfall, plan settlements around natural drainage systems, and create institutions capable of anticipating and responding to disasters.\n\nThe real challenge is not simply to prevent the next flood. It is to ensure that the next exceptional rainfall event does not become the next national disaster.\n\nWhat is required now is sustained political commitment, coordinated execution and the willingness to treat water management as a core component of national development rather than an emergency service activated whenever the heavens open!\n\n(The writer is the Editor-at-large of LMD and is a senior journalist with a Post-graduate Diploma in Politics and Governance)"
