    "chunk_size_bytes": 959,
    "chunk_text": "Nearly 450kg of suspected smuggled beedi leaves found on Chilaw coast\n\nNearly 450 kilogrammes of beedi leaves suspected to have been smuggled into the country by sea were found abandoned along the Chilaw coastline during a joint operation by the Sri Lanka Coast Guard and the Navy early today (24).\n\nThe operation was launched around 5 a.m. following information received by personnel at the Chilaw Coast Guard Station.\n\nThe operation involved the crew of patrol vessel CG 105, which was conducting night patrols, and personnel from the Thoduwawa Naval Task Force.\n\nDuring the operation, officers found 15 sacks containing beedi leaves abandoned on the beach. Each sack was estimated to weigh around 30 kilogrammes.\n\nOfficials suspect that those involved in the smuggling had abandoned the consignment and fled when Coast Guard personnel arrived at the scene.\n\nThe seized stock is to be handed over to the Excise Department in Chilaw for further legal action."
