    "chunk_text": "\"Hasina is a convicted criminal; a fugitive terrorist,\" Humaiun Kobir, Bangladesh's minister of state for foreign affairs, told Reuters.\n\n\"She can only return home by extradition treaty; in handcuffs, and under strict surveillance.\"\n\nOn the request to arrange a flight, Kobir said: \"Bangladesh \u200bwill not entertain any such delusional request\".\n\nAminul Islam, chief prosecutor of Bangladesh's International Crimes \u200bTribunal, which sentenced \u2060Hasina to death, said it was unreasonable for a convicted fugitive to expect the government to arrange her return.\n\nA Bangladeshi minister told Reuters on Sunday that Hasina would be arrested and jailed on return and that there had been no official discussions \u2060with \u200bIndia about sending an aircraft to bring her back.\n\nThe United Nations has \u200bsaid as many as 1,400 people were killed during the unrest that forced her out of power."
