    "chunk_text": "Fire breaks out at Will Smith and Jada Pinkett Smith\u2019s Calabasas compound\n\nLos Angeles Times: Police and firefighters were called to the Will Smith and Jada Pinkett Smith\u2018s Calabasas compound early Monday morning.\n\nJust after midnight on Nov. 23, deputies from the Malibu/Lost Hills Station responded to a call from the Smith\u2019s security team that there was a structure fire at the property, the Los Angeles County Sheriff\u2019s Department confirmed to The Times. When law enforcement arrived, deputies saw a maintenance shed, or \u201clarge 20-by-40-foot barn\u201d-type of structure engulfed in flames.\n\nShortly after, Los Angeles County Fire Department personnel arrived and extinguished the fire. No other structures were damaged, and no one was injured, according to LASD, who noted that the cause of the fire was accidental.\n\n\u201cWe do have a shed on fire with no spread to the brush,\u201d firefighters reported, according to 911 call audio obtained by Page Six.\n\nThe Smiths have been attached to the property, nestled in the Santa Monica Mountains, for nearly 30 years. They first acquired a ranch in 1997 and shortly after bought the adjacent plots that would ultimately create the 150-acre compound where they built their Stephen Samuelson-designed, 25,000-square-foot adobe-style home.\n\n\u201cEverything needed to be done by hand,\u201d Will Smith told Architectural Digest in 2011. \u201cWe wanted to feel the love and labor that went into every piece of this place.\u201d\n\nThe Smiths spent seven years building the home, which features antique carved panels and doors they\u2019ve collected from the Southwest as well as the Middle East, Asia and Africa. Jada Pinkett Smith told the publication the project was a \u201cspiritual endeavor.\u201d\n\nAfter years of messy reports concerning the couple\u2019s relationship status \u2014 since Will Smith\u2019s slap-heard-round-the-world at the Academy Awards ceremony in 2022 \u2014 they moved back in together in recent years, People reported in July."
