    "md5": "f63eace88e84630b9e144ffc52ec7cb6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1593,
    "chunk_text": "Bhasha Lanka celebrates 15 years of innovation\n\nBhasha Lanka Founder and CEO Dhanika Perera (centre), creator of Helakuru, alongside the Bhasha team\n\nSri Lankan technology company Bhasha Lanka (Pvt) Ltd celebrated its 15th anniversary in October 2026, marking a significant milestone in its journey from a university-led Sinhala language innovation to a growing ecosystem of digital solutions spanning communication, information, payments, commerce, entertainment and mobility.\n\nFounded in 2011 by technology entrepreneur Dhanika Perera, Bhasha has built its journey around the vision of \u201cEmpowering Masses Digitally.\u201d Celebrated under the theme \u201cVision, Innovation & Impact,\u201d the anniversary brought together employees, customers, business partners, investors and early supporters who contributed to the company\u2019s growth.\n\nBhasha\u2019s journey began with SETT Browser, developed by Perera while studying at the University of Moratuwa. At a time when Sinhala content was not reliably supported on Android smartphones, the browser enabled users to access online information in their native language. The innovation received international recognition through the mBillionth South Asian Award in 2011.\n\nThe breakthrough subsequently attracted commercial interest from Etisalat Sri Lanka, whose then CEO Dumindra Ratnayaka approached Perera regarding the technology. This led Perera, then a third-year university student, to establish Bhasha Lanka in 2011, with Etisalat becoming its first customer through a per-user licensing arrangement, providing the foundation for further innovation."
