    "chunk_text": "The breakthrough subsequently attracted commercial interest from Etisalat Sri Lanka, whose then CEO Dumindra Ratnayaka approached Perera regarding the technology. This led Perera, then a third-year university student, to establish Bhasha Lanka in 2011, with Etisalat becoming its first customer through a per-user licensing arrangement, providing the foundation for further innovation.\n\nBhasha\u2019s entrepreneurial journey expanded into financial technology with the establishment of PayHere in 2016.\n\nThe company\u2019s innovation ecosystem also includes Esana, delivering real-time news and information; HelaPay, facilitating bank-account-based digital transactions, utility payments, mobile reloads and fund transfers; and HelaRoo, providing access to Sri Lankan digital entertainment.\n\nMore recently, HelaGo, launched in January 2026, extended this locally driven innovation approach into ride-hailing, focusing on improving convenience and creating fairer experiences for passengers and drivers. While these platforms share a common entrepreneurial foundation, certain businesses have evolved into separately incorporated entities, reflecting the wider growth and diversification of the Bhasha innovation ecosystem.\n\nThe anniversary celebrations also recognised the people behind the company\u2019s achievements. Addressing the gathering, Founder and Chief Executive Officer DhanikaPerera reflected on the commitment of employees, trust of customers and continued support of partners who helped transform an emerging university innovation into a technology business serving millions of Sri Lankans. Long-serving employees were honoured for their contributions, while promotions recognised individual performance and professional development."
