    "chunk_text": "Xiteb\u2019s xCommerz marks 3 years of int\u2019l recognition\n\nThree consecutive years of recognition at the Asia eCommerce Awards mark another international milestone for xCommerz, the proprietary enterprise digital commerce suite by Xiteb, reflecting sustained investment in research and development and contributions from software engineers and technology experts across Sri Lanka, Vietnam, Malaysia and India.\n\nDeveloped through extensive research into international commerce practices, including those of Walmart, IKEA and Amazon, xCommerz supports single-vendor eCommerce and multi-vendor marketplaces, combining scalable enterprise architecture, flexible deployment models, advanced customisation and integration capabilities to address diverse business requirements.\n\nThe ninth Asia eCommerce Awards 2026 brought together leading technology providers, digital commerce specialists and multinational brands from Asia and Oceania, a region that includes Australia and New Zealand, with Xiteb shortlisted in three categories: Best eCommerce Innovation, Best eCommerce Solution and Best eCommerce Consultant.\n\nAmong the shortlisted competitors were Flipkart Commerce Cloud, AnyMind Group, DKSH, Intrepid Asia, Imagic Esolutions, Exabytes Network and iProspect Taiwan, with competing projects involving internationally recognised brands such as Nestl\u00e9, L\u2019Or\u00e9al, Beiersdorf, Crocs, Unilever and Haleon.\n\nA panel of 19 industry executives from organisations including Samsung Electronics, Philips, 3M, Beiersdorf, Electrolux, Lufthansa Group and Mondel\u0113z International evaluated entries against criteria covering technological innovation, business effectiveness, strategic execution and commercial impact, reflecting the increasingly sophisticated expectations of the competition."
