    "chunk_size_bytes": 1786,
    "chunk_text": "HighVoltagePR leads influencer rollout for Daraz 11.11 Big Boss Sale\n\nFrom left; Sanjula Peiris, Safwan Yaseen, Daraz Sri Lanka Managing Director Rukshan Xavier, HighVoltagePR Managing Director Supun Dias and Mafaz Mohideen\n\nBoutique public relations and influencer marketing agency HighVoltagePR is spearheading the ongoing influencer and affiliate marketing campaign for the flagship Daraz Sri Lanka 11.11 Big Boss Sale, held in a landmark year as Daraz marks its 10th anniversary.\n\nManaging a diverse network of over 130 content creators and affiliates, the agency launched with a high-impact teaser phase before transitioning into the main 11.11 rollout \u2013 driving sustained digital engagement, consumer discovery, and conversion momentum throughout the sale period, which runs until 21 November 2026. To maximise reach across Sri Lanka\u2019s digital landscape, HighVoltagePR structured a multi-tiered creator strategy combining high-reach lifestyle figures, niche category reviewers, and performance-driven affiliates. By aligning creator storytelling with real-time flash deals and platform promotions, the campaign maintains continuous visibility across major social platforms while guiding shoppers directly to the Daraz app.\n\nHighVoltagePR Managing Director Supun Dias said, \u201cExecuting an influencer campaign at this scale requires more than just volume \u2013 it demands precision, alignment, and real-time agility. Managing over 130 creators and affiliates simultaneously for Sri Lanka\u2019s largest e-commerce event demonstrates how far our digital capabilities have evolved over the past decade. By pairing authentic creator voices with data-backed campaign management, we are delivering measurable visibility and strong consumer engagement at every stage of the 11.11 sale.\u201d"
  },
