    "md5": "b1f553889780ab799ed38164264850b2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1689,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cFor over 2 decades, our mission has been to make sure enterprise systems talk to each other safely at scale,\u201d said Harry Ault, CEO of Choreo Labs. \u201cAI agents don\u2019t change that mission. In fact, they make it far more urgent. Enterprises won\u2019t put agents into production until they can see, govern, and trust every action those agents take. That is the problem we were built to solve, and our new name says so.\u201d\n\n\u201cChoreo\u201d comes from choreography. Inside every enterprise, agents, APIs, integrations, identities, and services each have their own part to play, and none of them ever stops moving. Choreo Labs gives organizations both the freedom for each part to move and the control to keep them in step. Choreo, the company\u2019s platform, brings APIs, integration, identity, agents, and the internal developer platform that runs them together in one place.\n\n\u201cLabs\u201d reflects the company\u2019s research and engineering culture. It has long innovated in open source and open standards, from its integration programming language to its latest agent management product. Technical staff make up more than 75 percent of its 850-plus employees, and the same engineers who design the platform work alongside customers to deploy it.\n\nExisting customers don\u2019t need to take any action. Products, contracts, support, and open source licenses continue as they are, and other product names will move to the new brand over the coming months.\n\nThe company will make its first appearance under its new name at AWS re:Invent in Las Vegas, November 30 to December 4, 2026, where it will showcase its unified platform. Ault will also deliver a keynote at apidays Paris, December 1 to 3, 2026."
  },
