    "chunk_size_bytes": 943,
    "chunk_text": "Das, a former journalist, became one of the faces of the CJP - a Gen Z-led movement that began as satire but has since emerged as a youth-led pressure group.\n\nIn July, protests spearheaded by the CJP over exam paper leaks led to the resignation of India's Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan .\n\nThe same month, Das and Ashutosh Ranka, another CJP leader, were jailed for seven days after being arrested for trespassing at a banned protest site in Delhi.\n\nAbhijeet Dipke, the founder of CJP, wrote on X that if Das \"had looted a bank or committed financial fraud\", he may have been allowed to fly to London, referring to billionaire bank-loan defaulters who have left India.\n\nThere have been other instances in recent years of people being prevented from boarding flights.\n\nIn September 2025, Bhanu Tatak, an environmental and anti-dam activist from India's north-eastern Arunachal Pradesh state, was stopped from boarding a flight to Dublin."
