    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "283e900f7a1188074dea96ee6005719d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "Saroja wins Global Business Excellence Award\n\nManaging Director of S G Actuarial Consultancy (Pvt) Ltd, Saroja Gunatilleke, has won the Woman of Excellence in Actuarial and Insurance Leadership award at the Global Business Excellence Awards 2026.\n\nPresented by London Business Consultancy (UK), the awards programme carries institutional recognition through the DEC under Sri Lanka\u2019s Ministry of Industry.\n\n\u201cI am deeply honoured to receive the Global Business Excellence (GBE) Award, which recognises the contributions of outstanding individuals and organisations. I see this recognition as an acknowledgement of my ongoing efforts to advance the actuarial profession and contribute to Sri Lanka\u2019s development,\u201d Saroja said.\n\nThe award adds to the Global CEO Forum\u2019s 45 Under 45 Leadership Excellence Platinum Award she received in 2024, and acknowledges her continuing contribution to the actuarial and insurance sectors.\n\nWith 15 years of experience spanning actuarial science, risk management, regulation and insurance, Saroja has built a career distinguished by academic excellence and professional leadership. She holds a B.Sc. (Hons) in Mathematics, along with a Graduate Diploma and an M.Sc. in Actuarial Science, from UK universities, all achieved with First Class or Distinction passes.\n\nIn 2010, aged 26, she qualified as an Associate of the Institute and Faculty of Actuaries (IFoA), UK, becoming the youngest person and the only woman in Sri Lanka to hold the qualification at the time. Two years later, she achieved Fellowship of the institute and was then the only Sri Lankan Fellow Actuary of the IFoA working in the country.\n\nToday, Saroja leads S G Actuarial Consultancy, which provides tailored consultancy services in areas including risk management, strategic planning, gratuity valuation and regulatory compliance, as well as training for non-actuarial professionals and students."
  },
