    "md5": "9fbdbd6a8334ac9c20de893788cf1a1a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys backs Sri Lanka Expo 2027 opening SMEs path to global markets\n\nHayleys PLC has joined Sri Lanka Expo 2027 as a Gold Partner. The Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) will host the international trade exhibition from 14th to 17th January 2027 at the BMICH, Colombo, which returns after 15 years.\n\nThe Expo is expected to bring together about 750 Sri Lankan exporters and over 1,500 international buyers, investors and trade delegates. It covers sectors ranging from apparel, rubber and engineering to tea, spices, coconut products, ICT and logistics.\n\nIn September 2026, the country\u2019s merchandise exports reached US$ 1.38 billion, the highest monthly value on record. Total exports for the first nine months of the year rose 5 percent to US$ 13.6 billion.\n\n\u201cGrowing exports is a key pillar of Sri Lanka\u2019s economic future, and it has been at the heart of Hayleys\u2019 strategy,\u201d said Mohan Pandithage, Chairman and Chief Executive, Hayleys PLC.\n\n\u201cOur growth and the nation\u2019s growth rest on Sri Lankan products competing, and winning, in global markets.At the Expo, we are proud to feature Hayleys\u2019 own sustainable innovations, home-grown solutions that have already won over customers in more than 80 markets.\u201d\n\nThe Group\u2019s purpose is \u201cto inspire an inclusive world and a thriving planet\u201d, and that purpose shapes how it builds export value. Hayleys businesses bring smallholder farmers, out-growers and rural communities directly into global value chains, so they share in the value created. This work is driven by HayleysLifecode, the Group\u2019s ESG and sustainability framework. Hayleys companies have together been named Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen six times by the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce.\n\nThrough its sponsorship, Hayleys aims to help Sri Lanka\u2019s small and medium enterprises compete on the international stage the Expo provides."
  },
