    "md5": "b49da7686fe75539824eb9c4245ae831",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "Falcon Valley Hydro rings market opening bell to mark Empower Board listing\n\nFrom left: Rohan Senewiratne, Managing Director \u2013 Atarah Capital (Private) Limited; Air Vice Marshal Andrew Wijesuriya, Director \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited; Ruchit Kandage, Director \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited; Nilupa Perera, Chief Regulatory Officer \u2013 Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE); Air Chief Marshal Gagan Bulathsinghala (Retd.), Chairman \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited; Dimuthu Abeyesekera, Chairman \u2013 CSE; Bernard Tan, Director, Projects \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited; Thusitha Peiris, Chief Executive Officer \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited; Gerard Suares, Chief Financial Officer \u2013 Falcon Valley Hydro Limited.\n\nFalcon Valley Hydro Limited (FVH) rang the market opening bell on the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) trading floor last week to mark the listing of its 16,000,000 Ordinary Voting Shares on the Empower Board by way of introduction.\n\nThese shares, comprising the FVH\u2019s entire issued and paid-up share capital, were listed at a Reference Price of Rs. 31.00 per share determined in consultation with Atarah Capital (Private) Limited, the Financial Advisor & Manager to the Introduction and Sponsor.\n\nIncorporated in Sri Lanka, FVH operates the 2.4 MW Falcon Valley mini-hydro power plant in Medadumbara, Kandy, which was commissioned in 2012 and is fed by the Retiyagama Oya. FVH is wholly owned by Khen Energy Ltd through its subsidiaries, a company listed on the Catalist Board of the Singapore Exchange. Looking ahead, the Company seeksto explore new renewable energy projects across hydro and solar.\n\n\u201cThis listing brings Falcon Valley Hydro into greater public view and strengthens our accountability and transparency in an established hydropower business. It holds us to the discipline that public markets demand,\u201d said Air Chief Marshal Gagan Bulathsinghala (Retd.), Chairman of Falcon Valley Hydro Limited."
  },
