    "md5": "2466f613aba3e48c2d41cd12bc7c4159",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1503,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThis listing brings Falcon Valley Hydro into greater public view and strengthens our accountability and transparency in an established hydropower business. It holds us to the discipline that public markets demand,\u201d said Air Chief Marshal Gagan Bulathsinghala (Retd.), Chairman of Falcon Valley Hydro Limited.\n\nThrough a listing by introduction, FVH\u2019s existing shares are admitted for trading on the secondary market without a public share issue or immediate capital raising, giving the Company greater visibility, stronger governance, and future access to capital markets.\n\n\u201cOn behalf of the CSE, I congratulate Falcon Valley Hydro on its listing today,\u201d remarked Nilupa Perera, Chief Regulatory Officer of the CSE, during her welcome address at the ceremony. \u201cListing on the CSE marks an important step in corporate governance, aligning the company with the high standards of disclosure and risk management we uphold to build lasting market confidence.\u201d\n\nFVH\u2019s listing aligns with the CSE\u2019s broader commitment to advancing Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) integration, sustainable finance across Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market and the transition towards a green economy. Since introducing GSS+ bonds (Green, Social, Sustainability, and Sustainability linked bonds) in 2024, the Exchange has facilitated 12 issuances mobilising over Rs. 92 billion with three Sri Lankan institutions earning international recognition at the 2026 Environmental Finance Sustainable Debt Awards."
