    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6e64d91d1cc844064a703827c8a9b219",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1846,
    "chunk_text": "AI-powered identity fraud threatening business globally, software giant warns\n\nThe leadership teams of LankaPay, Lumin and Finetech Consultancy Private Ltd officially exchanging the onboarding agreement.\u00a0 From left: Joel Foster- Chief Commercial Officer (Lumin); Chamathka Fernando - Deputy CEO (Finetech); Nancy Ridge - Head of Global Partnerships (Lumin); Sujatha Nadesan \u2013 Director (Finetech); Channa De Silva \u2013 CEO (LankaPay) and Lakshman Silva \u2013 Chairman (LankaPay)\n\nIdentity fraud has become more sophisticated globally, and businesses urgently need greater security and confidence specially when signing and managing agreements. 56 percent of companies (over 1000 large companies) from United States, Australia, New Zealand and other parts of the world surveyed recently have experienced identity fraud in the past year, which is a staggering number, a New Zealand based, leading document management and PDF software company noted.\n\nAs per the survey, 94 percent of companies believe that agreement workflows are vulnerable to AI-powered fraud, as document manipulation and AI-generated signatures are widespread. Though AI brings a lot of capabilities to organisations and to people\u2019s lifestyle and to businesses, there is also the flip side of it. Therefore, companies should ensure their customers are protected from these threats with proven identities in the form of verifiable digital credentials, said Chief Commercial Officer of Lumin, Joel Foster in Colombo last week.\n\nOne of the rising threats we have today is \u2018deepfakes\u2019.\u00a0 Companies particularly in sectors such as banking, finance, legal, property, insurance, and consultancy are highly targeted. Apart from obvious things like operational disruption, delayed work, reputational damage, the financial losses caused by an identity fraud is massive, Foster added."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-24-dailymirrorlk-5dd3089d",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-5dd3089d",
    "date_str": "2026-11-24",
    "description": "AI-powered identity fraud threatening business globally, software giant warns",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/AI-powered-identity-fraud-threatening-business-globally-software-giant-warns/215-355630",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
