    "chunk_id": "2026-11-24-dailymirrorlk-5dd3089d-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "219f8e307295094174d6767f98c6dd4f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1941,
    "chunk_text": "One of the rising threats we have today is \u2018deepfakes\u2019.\u00a0 Companies particularly in sectors such as banking, finance, legal, property, insurance, and consultancy are highly targeted. Apart from obvious things like operational disruption, delayed work, reputational damage, the financial losses caused by an identity fraud is massive, Foster added.\n\nFoster shared these views at the event held at Amari Colombo to announce the strategic partnership between Lumin, Finetech and LankaPay to introduce secure, legally binding digital signature solutions to businesses and government institutions across Sri Lanka. The partnership brings together Lumin\u2019s digital signature technology and LankaPay\u2019s national payment and identity infrastructure, with Finetech leading the integration. The collaboration aims to establish a national standard for secure and authenticated digital signatures across Sri Lanka\u2019s enterprise sector.\n\nCommenting on the partnership, Lumin\u2019s Head of Global Partnerships Nancy Ridge said, \u201cWe are delighted to partner with Finetech and LankaPay to bring secure digital signing capabilities to businesses and institutions in Sri Lanka. By combining Lumin\u2019s global digital document technology with trusted local infrastructure, we aim to simplify the way organisations manage agreements and approvals, enabling them to operate more efficiently and confidently in an increasingly digital world.\u201d\n\nChief Executive Officer of LankaPay Channa De Silva said, \u201cThis partnership is an important step in strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s digital ecosystem by extending trusted digital infrastructure beyond payments into document authentication and signing. By bringing together global technology and national infrastructure, we aim to support businesses and government institutions in adopting secure, efficient and compliant digital processes, contributing to the country\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda.\u201d"
  },
