    "md5": "9a4d2023b61ff060d0859dd665c7d7d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1272,
    "chunk_text": "Chief Executive Officer of LankaPay Channa De Silva said, \u201cThis partnership is an important step in strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s digital ecosystem by extending trusted digital infrastructure beyond payments into document authentication and signing. By bringing together global technology and national infrastructure, we aim to support businesses and government institutions in adopting secure, efficient and compliant digital processes, contributing to the country\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda.\u201d\n\nThe solution will also help accelerate business processes by reducing turnaround times for contracts, approvals and onboarding. At the same time, minimising paper consumption and manual document handling will contribute to lower operational costs and a reduced environmental footprint.\n\nSharing views with Mirror Business on the level of digital transformation Sri Lanka and other South Asian countries have achieved currently, Foster said Sri Lanka is positioned in the middle, but the associated challenges faced are no different to anywhere else seen in the world. \u201cIndia in the meantime is doing some amazing things in this space. They have the ability. I am very impressed with what\u2019s going on there, and we are starting to do more work with them.\u201d"
