    "md5": "375fabea602f8366b2db72fae7d4d1e5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1804,
    "chunk_text": "Iconic Galadari reborn as Radisson Blu Hotel Galadari Colombo\n\nForeign Affairs and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath leading a ceremonial cake-cutting to mark the occasion\n\nLandmark hotel unveils Radisson Blu identity after US$ 48.5mn transformation\n\nTargets December opening as island heads for a record tourism year\n\nColombo Fort\u2019s Galadari Hotel ushered in a new era on Sunday evening as it celebrated its grand opening as Radisson Blu Hotel Galadari Colombo, unveiling a landmark reimagined from its foundations to blend four decades of local heritage with the standards of a global hospitality brand.\n\nThe ceremony at the hotel\u2019s Lotus Road premises was held under the patronage of Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Vijitha Herath. Guests included Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA) Chairman Suranjith Wevita, diplomats, senior principals of the Galadari Brothers group, hoteliers and business leaders. Managing Director for South East Asia and Pacific Bert Fol represented Radisson Hotel Group.\n\nThe highlight of the evening was the on-stage unveiling of the new brand, in which Minister Herath, senior Galadari representatives and Director of Operations Bilal Shafi took part. The Minister also led a ceremonial cake-cutting with a traditional sword to mark the occasion.\n\nFirst opened in 1984 as the Galadari Meridien, the hotel has spent more than four decades as a fixture of Colombo\u2019s commercial and social life, a legacy General Manager Marko Janssen placed at the heart of his video address to guests. \u201cOver the years, this hotel has been part of Colombo\u2019s story.\n\nIt hosted weddings, business deals, farewell dinners, and first dates,\u201d he noted, adding that a hotel \u201cis only as alive as the memories it creates. And this one has plenty.\u201d"
  },
