    "md5": "8315385455a457d14019d442e1b59bf7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1422,
    "chunk_text": "Reflecting on the journey, Janssen admitted that \u201ca closed hotel is a quiet, strange place\u201d, but maintained that \u201ca building can be closed while its spirit is not\u201d. He acknowledged that the road to the grand opening brought delays, difficult decisions and plans that had to be rewritten more than once. Each setback, he argued, pushed the team to ask what the hotel could become rather than how to restore what it once was.\n\nGaladari Hotels (Lanka) PLC, 63.57 percent owned by Dubai-based Galadari Brothers Co. (LLC), raised its total investment in the project to US$ 48.5 million last year from an initial US$ 33.5 million, an increase of nearly 45 percent. Janssen thanked the owners for their vision and patience, telling them, \u201cYou stayed committed when it would have been easier not to.\u201d Chairman M. A. I. Galadari has likewise expressed confidence in the company\u2019s latest annual report that the repositioned hotel will \u201cemerge as a strong contender within Colombo\u2019s 5-star hospitality landscape\u201d.\n\nJanssen kept his warmest words for the hotel\u2019s team, a blend of long-serving staff and recruits who joined during the transition, including through the \u2018Race to the Blu Future\u2019 careers drive launched in January. \u201cWalls and furniture create a building, but you create experience. Your pride, your smile, and your care are what guests will remember long after they check out,\u201d he told them."
