    "chunk_text": "\u201cThis program will help the Government of Sri Lanka build a stronger, more inclusive financial ecosystem that enables MSMEs to grow, innovate, and withstand economic shocks and disasters related to the changing climate,\u201d ADB Country Director for Sri Lanka Shannon Cowlin said. The programme will support legal reforms to establish the Microfinance and Credit Regulatory Authority, strengthen oversight and curb predatory lending. It will also strengthen credit reporting so lenders have better information to assess borrowers and expand guarantees that help lenders share the risk of lending to smaller firms.\n\nThe green credit lines will finance environmentally sustainable investments. At least 20 percent of firms supported to invest in climate mitigation and adaptation will be owned or led by women.\n\nThe programme will also help growth-stage small and medium-sized companies raise equity."
