    "chunk_size_bytes": 868,
    "chunk_text": "University non-academic staff to stage one-day strike tomorrow\n\nColombo, November 24 (Daily Mirror) - University non-academic staff have decided to launch a massive protest campaign tomorrow (25), accompanied by a one-day symbolic strike, alleging that their salaries and allowances have been reduced.\n\nMangala Devathilina Dabarera, Co-President of the University Trade Union Joint Committee (UTUJC), said the employees, who staged a symbolic strike last week over budget-related allowances, had decided to step up their trade union action.\n\n\"If these issues remain unresolved, we have decided to launch another protest campaign on December 1 and 2, accompanied by a two-day symbolic strike,\" he said.\n\nHe said that the issue was not simply about making new demands but about the reduction of allowances and privileges that university employees had enjoyed previously."
