    "md5": "07650421f9485a1e80866bd9d42f617e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1242,
    "chunk_text": "India grants Rs. 600 million for Puttalam Hospital upgrade\n\nThe Government of India has agreed to provide a grant of Rs. 600 million for the construction of a new building at the Puttalam Base Hospital, with the Government planning to upgrade the hospital under the Central Government.\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved a proposal to construct a six-storey building with a total floor area of 8,640 square metres within four years.\n\nThe proposed building will house an Accident and Emergency Unit, clinics, a short-stay inpatient treatment unit, a blood bank, and diagnostic and laboratory facilities.\n\nThe Indian grant will cover the construction of the first three floors, where the Accident and Emergency Unit is to be established.\n\nThe Cabinet approval also covers entering into a Memorandum of Understanding with the Government of India to obtain the grant.\n\nPuttalam Base Hospital, which previously functioned under the North Western Provincial Council, was approved for takeover by the Central Government at the Cabinet meeting held on March 3, 2026, with the concurrence of the Provincial Governor.\n\nThe move is aimed at improving the hospital's infrastructure and ensuring quality and uninterrupted medical services to patients."
