    "md5": "af659c9a8805aff0e8747a7e69ccf92d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 966,
    "chunk_text": "OPEC Fund to provide Sri Lanka with $30 million loan for reforms\n\nSri Lanka is set to receive a US$30 million policy-based loan from the OPEC Fund for International Development to support its economic reforms and recovery programme.\n\nThe loan is intended to support the Government's development policy operation, titled \"Sri Lanka Reforms for Growth, Resilience and Openness\", which aims to restore macroeconomic stability, ensure fiscal sustainability and promote sustainable and inclusive economic growth.\n\nThe funding will complement financial assistance provided by the World Bank under its Development Policy Operation.\n\nThe US$30 million facility comprises US$24 million from the OPEC Fund's Ordinary Capital Resources and US$6 million from its Special Capital Resources.\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved a proposal submitted by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake in his capacity as Finance, Planning and Economic Development Minister to obtain the loan."
  },
