    "md5": "55b44ea7db89d024409d1a6d63cd25c2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 783,
    "chunk_text": "Magnitude 6.5 earthquake recorded in Indian Ocean; no tsunami threat to Sri Lanka\n\nColombo, November 24 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0A magnitude 6.5 earthquake was recorded in the Indian Ocean in the Mauritius-Reunion region at 4.36 p.m. today (24), according to preliminary seismic data.\n\nThe earthquake occurred at a depth of 10 kilometres, with its epicentre located at latitude 17.78\u00b0 South and longitude 65.82\u00b0 East.\n\nHowever, there is no tsunami threat to Sri Lanka as a result of the earthquake, and all coastal areas of the country have been declared safe, authorities said.\n\nThe announcement was made in consultation with relevant national and international agencies.\n\nThe public has been informed that there is no need for concern regarding a tsunami threat to Sri Lanka at present."
  },
