    "md5": "2c39ba281e796ab83cc754dcfe41eca8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1917,
    "chunk_text": "Another marvel is the Yoda Ela, an 87 km (54 mi) long single-banking water canal constructed in 459 AD, carrying excess water from the Kala Wewa reservoir in Anuradhapura to the Tissa Wewa reservoir. The Yoda Ela is acclaimed for its low gradient of 6 inches per mile which, even with modern-day survey equipment, would be a difficult feat to achieve with such accuracy.\n\nTwo respected judges, Justice Amerasinghe and Justice Weeramantry, in judgments delivered independently in two different cases, emphasised that Anuradhapura is not simply an archaeological city or a destination for tourism; it represents one of the world's remarkable ancient hydraulic civilisations, where water management, agriculture, religious heritage, engineering and environmental conservation were developed as one integrated system.\n\nAnuradhapura's ancient reservoirs, canals, waterways, catchment areas, forests, elephants, Buddhist monuments and archaeological remains form an interconnected national heritage.\n\nIn a landmark judgment issued in the Eppawela Phosphate case of 2000 (Bulankulama and others vs Freeport-McMoRan and others), Justice Amerasinghe, with two other learned Justices of the Supreme Court in agreement, stated without ambiguity that any development that affects this heritage must be considered not merely as an exercise in planning, economics or tourism, but as a matter of national responsibility, environmental protection and the rule of law.\n\nGovernment is the temporary custodian and cannot distribute State land\n\nIn this landmark judgment, Justice Amerasinghe examined the proposed phosphate mining project in the Anuradhapura District.\n\nThe Court considered the potential consequences for the ancient irrigation systems of Rajarata, the water and soil conservation ecosystems, underground aquifers and agricultural lands, the archaeological and cultural heritage and the livelihoods of local communities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
