    "chunk_text": "Seizing new opportunities in China\u2019s development, writing a new chapter in China-Sri Lanka cooperation\n\nGuided by the principles of mutual respect, fairness and justice, we will work together to overcome obstacles and rise to the challenges, implement the common understandings reached by the two countries\u2019 leaders in a practical manner, walk side by side on the path to modernisation, and continue to advance our strategic cooperative partnership featuring sincere mutual assistance and everlasting friendship. Together, we will work towards building a China-Sri Lanka community with a shared future\n\nThe year 2026 marks the launch of China\u2019s 15th Five-Year Plan for economic and social development. Against the backdrop of a sluggish global economic recovery and ongoing international turbulence, China\u2019s economy has pressed ahead under pressure, maintaining overall stability while making steady progress and breaking new ground amid global changes, showcasing a promising outlook. China\u2019s recently released economic report for the first three quarters of the year once again delivered a stronger-than-expected performance, demonstrating the resilience and high quality of its growth. This is further proof that China\u2019s economy enjoys bright prospects, robust growth momentum and a promising future.\n\nFirst, the foundation for economic stability has continued to strengthen. In the first three quarters of 2026, China\u2019s gross domestic product (GDP) reached 107.1 trillion yuan, up 4.6% year on year. The economy expanded by 5.7 trillion yuan, the largest increase in five years. This growth rate remains in a leading position among major global economies. Employment and prices remained generally stable, while people\u2019s livelihoods continued to improve. China\u2019s sound economic fundamentals and positive long-term growth trajectory has become even more evident."
