    "chunk_text": "First, the foundation for economic stability has continued to strengthen. In the first three quarters of 2026, China\u2019s gross domestic product (GDP) reached 107.1 trillion yuan, up 4.6% year on year. The economy expanded by 5.7 trillion yuan, the largest increase in five years. This growth rate remains in a leading position among major global economies. Employment and prices remained generally stable, while people\u2019s livelihoods continued to improve. China\u2019s sound economic fundamentals and positive long-term growth trajectory has become even more evident.\n\nThird, the benefits of deeper integration with the world economy are continuing to unfold. China remains committed to \u201csharing benefits with the whole world\u201d. Through opening up at a higher level, China is embracing the broader trend of global development, injecting valuable vitality into the world economy and working with the international community to achieve shared development and prosperity. In the first three quarters of 2026, China\u2019s total imports and exports of goods reached 39.94 trillion yuan, up 18.8% year on year, bucking the trend of sluggish global trade. Imports grew by 22.3%, significantly faster than exports, which rose by 16.4%. Trade with Belt and Road partner countries increased by 17.1%. China continues to expand institutional opening-up, extending zero-tariff treatment to 63 countries and promoting trade liberalisation and investment facilitation. The \u201cBig Market for All: Export to China\u201d initiative has created new channels for quality foreign goods and services to enter the Chinese market. Meanwhile, high-tech products made in China continue to support global industrial upgrading and the green transition, while making everyday life more convenient for people around the world.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Disanayake (left) with Chinese President Xi Jinping at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, January 2025"
