    "chunk_size_bytes": 933,
    "chunk_text": "The five-year plan may contain worthwhile proposals. But the public deserves to know whether it includes a sufficiently independent investigation into existing expenditure, contracts and financial controls.\n\nBefore approving further major expansion, Parliament should demand clear answers.\n\nSriLankan Airlines does not need another recovery plan that merely promises a brighter future.\n\nIt needs a recovery program that identifies the real problems, takes corrective action and demonstrates measurable results.\n\nStop the financial bleeding. Investigate the leakages. Eliminate unnecessary expenditure. Establish accountability. Restore financial discipline. Then expand responsibly.\n\nThat is how SriLankan Airlines can begin rebuilding its financial strength, public confidence and long-term future.\n\n(The author is a former SriLankan Airlines Representative in Singapore, with over 13 years of aviation experience at Changi Airport)"
