    "md5": "11dcf6765eaf29466cd6461572f3f6f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1597,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s Budget 2027: From economic recovery to better livelihoods\n\nUltimately, the success of Budget 2027 should be measured not merely by how much revenue the Government collects, but by how effectively that revenue improves the lives of the people of Sri Lanka. Sri Lanka's future lies not merely in tax revenue, but in production, investment, employment, entrepreneurship, fiscal discipline and public confidence. Budget 2027 must therefore become an opportunity to transform economic recovery into genuine and lasting prosperity for the nation\n\nTax Revenue, Investment, Employment and Social Welfare \u2013 The Next Phase of Economic Transformation\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Budget 2027 represents an important attempt to move the country beyond economic stabilisation towards a more sustainable model of economic transformation. Following years of financial crisis, fiscal adjustment and considerable hardship among households and businesses, the central challenge is no longer simply restoring macroeconomic stability. It is translating that stability into higher productivity, stronger investment, employment opportunities and improved living standards.\n\nPresented under the theme \u201cA Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d, Budget 2027 seeks to strengthen economic growth while addressing the expectations of citizens who continue to experience the consequences of the economic crisis. Its success, however, will ultimately depend not on the scale of financial allocations announced, but on the effectiveness with which these resources are converted into measurable economic and social outcomes."
  },
