    "md5": "4a03c17870eada9697980b13a402cb46",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1982,
    "chunk_text": "However, the long-term sustainability of personal income tax relief depends on broadening the tax base, improving compliance and bringing more economic activity into the formal system. The Government must therefore strengthen digital tax administration, improve information-sharing between institutions and reduce opportunities for tax evasion, while ensuring that compliant taxpayers are treated fairly.MA more transparent, predictable and efficient tax system would strengthen taxpayer confidence and improve the environment for private investment.\n\nQualifying enterprises with a minimum investment of $ 3 million may opt for an enhanced capital allowance equivalent to 200% of qualifying capital expenditure, subject to the prescribed conditions. This proposal could strengthen the attractiveness of Sri Lanka as an investment destination, particularly for export-oriented manufacturing, tourism infrastructure and other productive activities.\n\nNevertheless, tax incentives are only one component of the investment decision. Investors also require policy consistency, efficient administrative procedures, reliable energy supply, competitive logistics, skilled labour, access to finance and a predictable regulatory environment. Investment incentives should therefore be evaluated against measurable outcomes such as additional capital formation, export earnings, employment creation, technology transfer and productivity improvements.\n\nA well-designed incentive framework should reward genuinely additional investment rather than provide concessions for activities that would have taken place without them.\n\nOne of the notable proposals in Budget 2027 is the \u201cA Share for Everyone\u201d initiative, which seeks to introduce eligible students aged 18 and above to investment in the Colombo Stock Exchange through a share allocation valued at Rs. 10,000. This initiative has the potential to promote financial literacy, investment awareness and long-term savings among young people."
