    "chunk_size_bytes": 1754,
    "chunk_text": "Financial assistance should also be complemented by business development services, accounting and financial management support, digitalisation, market access and export readiness. Particular attention should be given to women-led enterprises, rural businesses, young entrepreneurs and enterprises operating in sectors with significant employment potential. The objective should be to transform MSMEs from survival-oriented businesses into productive, competitive and sustainable enterprises.\n\nHowever, infrastructure investment should not be evaluated merely by the number of projects commenced or completed. Its economic value depends on whether it reduces production costs, improves access to markets and generates sustainable benefits. Housing is another important component of the Budget.\n\nUnder the \u201cA Place of One\u2019s Own \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d program, the Government aims to construct 70,000 houses for low-income households, including 10,000 houses during 2027. The assistance per house is proposed to increase from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 1.5 million. Housing programs can improve living standards, create employment in construction and related industries, and support local economic activity.\n\nNevertheless, implementation should be supported by transparent beneficiary selection, appropriate infrastructure, access to essential services and effective monitoring of construction quality. Regional development must also receive sustained attention.\n\nEconomic growth cannot be concentrated exclusively in Colombo and other major urban centres. The allocation of Rs. 50 billion for district development programs provides an opportunity to strengthen regional infrastructure, improve local economic activity and address disparities in development."
