    "chunk_text": "The objective must be to move beyond subsistence-oriented production towards commercially viable, competitive and market-oriented agriculture. Rural economic development should therefore be integrated with transport infrastructure, financial services, digital connectivity and entrepreneurship.\n\nThe expansion of digital public services could reduce administrative costs, improve transparency and make Government services more accessible to citizens and businesses. Digitalisation also has significant implications for tax administration.An integrated digital tax system, supported by reliable taxpayer information, electronic transactions, improved data analytics and effective compliance monitoring, can help broaden the tax base and reduce revenue leakage.\n\nHowever, digital transformation must be accompanied by institutional reform, data protection, cybersecurity, staff capacity development and appropriate governance arrangements. Public accountability is equally important. Every major Budget program should have clearly defined implementation deadlines, responsible institutions, measurable performance indicators and transparent monitoring arrangements.\n\nThe public should be able to assess not only how much money has been allocated, but also what has been achieved through those allocations. Regular reporting on project progress, expenditure performance, employment outcomes and economic benefits would strengthen public confidence and improve fiscal accountability.\n\nBudget 2027 provides opportunities to strengthen economic recovery through investment, entrepreneurship, infrastructure development, social protection and digital transformation."
