    "chunk_size_bytes": 1125,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka's economic recovery has created an opportunity to move towards a more productive, investment-oriented and inclusive economy. Budget 2027 seeks to support this transition through personal income tax relief, MSME financing, investment incentives, housing, infrastructure, health, education, agriculture, fisheries and digitalisation. The challenge now is implementation. Government institutions must translate Budget proposals into practical programs, while the private sector must respond through investment, innovation, entrepreneurship and employment creation.\n\nUltimately, the success of Budget 2027 should be measured not merely by how much revenue the Government collects, but by how effectively that revenue improves the lives of the people of Sri Lanka. Sri Lanka's future lies not merely in tax revenue, but in production, investment, employment, entrepreneurship, fiscal discipline and public confidence. Budget 2027 must therefore become an opportunity to transform economic recovery into genuine and lasting prosperity for the nation.\n\n(The author is Managing Partner of A.G. Sarma, Chartered Accountants)"
