    "chunk_size_bytes": 1363,
    "chunk_text": "Sathuta Builders gets Rs. 1.69 b contract for Uva-Wellassa Uni. Faculty of Medicine building\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved the award of the contract for constructing the first phase of the Faculty of Medicine at Uva-Wellassa University of Sri Lanka to Sathuta Builders Ltd., worth over 1.69 billion (excluding tax).\n\nThe contract award is based on the recommendations of the Higher Level Procurement Committee, which evaluated the bids received for the project.\n\nApproval to begin procurement activities for the planning and construction of the first phase of the Faculty of Medicine had earlier been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 9 June 2025.\n\nBids were subsequently invited under the National Competitive Procurement Procedure, and six bids were received, the Government said.\n\nAfter the evaluation of these bids, the Higher Level Procurement Committee recommended Sathuta Builders Ltd., for the contract, and the Cabinet has now endorsed that recommendation.\n\nThe establishment of a Faculty of Medicine at Uva-Wellassa University, located in Badulla, is expected to expand access to medical education in the Uva Province and strengthen the country\u2019s higher education sector.\n\nThe proposal to this effect was submitted by Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya in her capacity as Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Minister."
