    "chunk_size_bytes": 1724,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2013Nordic Business Council marks 25 years, elects new President\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013Nordic Business Council marked its 25th Annual General Meeting, celebrating a quarter-century of strengthening business relations between Sri Lanka and the Nordic countries. Maleena Awn, Director of Operations at Meridian Maritime Services Ltd., was elected President for 2026/27.\n\nThe AGM was attended by Chief Guest Royal Norwegian Embassy in New Delhi Embassy Secretary, Political Affairs Tormod Nuland, and featured a keynote address by Norwegian Foreign Affairs Ministry Senior Adviser Aneela Shah Khan. Honorary Consul General of Norway Mano Sekeram was also present.\n\nIn her address, Shah Khan noted that Sri Lankan exports to Norway reached nearly $ 62 million in 2025, registering a 20% increase over 2024. She pointed to opportunities for greater cooperation in areas such as maritime services, renewable energy and technology, citing the collaboration between Colombo Dockyard and Norway\u2019s Misje Eco Bulk on hybrid vessels as an example of the potential for partnerships between the two countries.\n\nShe also highlighted Norway\u2019s support for Sri Lanka in areas including entrepreneurship, skills development and sustainable business practices, stressing the importance of policy predictability and transparency in attracting investment.\n\nOutgoing President Shaameel Mohideen reflected on the Council\u2019s work over the past 25 years, noting the importance of its role in connecting businesses and creating opportunities for engagement with the Nordic region. He highlighted the region\u2019s strengths in innovation, renewable energy, digitalisation and sustainable development as areas with scope for greater collaboration."
  },
