    "chunk_text": "The importance of these measures was reflected in Deloitte\u2019s webinar discussions, where panellists examined the challenges of improving access to finance, strengthening investment facilitation and reducing administrative barriers. The conversations highlighted that financial allocations alone may not be sufficient without stronger institutional capabilities and practical mechanisms to support implementation.\n\nThe wider discussion on trade and the economy also drew attention to power-sector efficiency, particularly the need to achieve a lower unit cost of electricity and address policy challenges that influence business competitiveness over the longer term.\n\nTaken together, Budget 2027 outlines a range of fiscal and structural measures intended to support Sri Lanka\u2019s transition towards sustainable growth. Their longer-term significance will depend on effective implementation, institutional co-ordination and the ability to translate policy priorities into meaningful economic outcomes.\n\nFor a more comprehensive understanding of Budget 2027, including its key proposals, fiscal measures and implications for businesses, explore Deloitte Sri Lanka\u2019s Budget 2027 Key Highlights, Comprehensive Budget Analysis Report and webinar recording.\n\nAccess Deloitte\u2019s Budget 2027 insights, reports and webinar recording here:"
