    "md5": "7880bc252b652214062a4d8e34b8c99b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1643,
    "chunk_text": "Tokyo Cement strengthens market position to sustain growth in 2Q\n\nTokyo Cement Group (Tokyo Cement) has posted a turnover of Rs. 20.9 billion for the second quarter ending 30 September 2026, reflecting a 28% increase from Rs. 16.3 billion recorded in the corresponding period of the previous year. Profit After Tax (PAT) stood at Rs. 870 million, compared to Rs. 1 billion in the same period last year.\n\nThe increase in turnover reflects the growth in volume and price increase from the previous quarter. However, profitability remained under pressure due to elevated raw material costs and currency volatility during the period, the company said.\n\nIt said the volatile and unpredictable nature of the Iran conflict continued to cloud the economic outlook during the quarter, with frequent fluctuations in global fuel prices and the looming threat of complete disruption of diesel supply weighing heavy on consumer confidence. These uncertainties, compounded by rising energy costs and climate-related risks, contributed to a more cautious investment climate and moderated economic momentum during the quarter.\n\nThe domestic economy faced mounting cost pressures, with fuel and energy expenditure rising sharply alongside a global fertiliser shortage, and the potential impact of severe El Ni\u00f1o conditions on the agriculture sector. Over the quarter, the Rupee was observed to depreciate against the US Dollar increasing pressures on reserves. Furthermore, year-on-year headline inflation, measured by the National Consumer Price Index (NCPI) reached 8.1% in August, exceeding the Central Bank\u2019s target range for a second consecutive month."
