    "chunk_text": "Tokyo Cement Group further strengthened its market position during the quarter, gaining market share as coastal shipping improved access to the Western Province and beyond. The expanded market reach supported higher utilisation of the Group\u2019s enhanced production capacity, driving greater operational efficiency.\n\nAs the financial sector anticipates a moderation in private sector credit growth over the coming quarters, the trajectory of the Middle East conflict, global energy prices and supply chain conditions will remain critical determinants of national economic momentum and sectoral growth prospects.\n\nAgainst this backdrop, the sovereign credit rating upgrade represents a significant positive development, with the potential to strengthen investor confidence and attract diversified foreign currency inflows. Despite persistent external shocks, the national economic outlook remains broadly stable, underpinned by sustained fiscal revenue and steady forex remittances. However, elevated import costs and a slower-than-anticipated recovery in tourism continue to pose near-term challenges, while geopolitical tensions and weather-related uncertainties remain key downside risks.\n\nRealising the economy\u2019s growth potential will depend on timely execution of public sector infrastructure projects and the policy direction set out in the forthcoming November budget. Together, these will be instrumental in translating improving macroeconomic confidence into tangible economic activity and investment.\n\nWithin this broader context, the construction sector maintains a cautiously optimistic outlook, supported by infrastructure development initiatives already underway by regional Government institutes. Sustaining this momentum will depend on the timely commencement and implementation of planned large-scale public investment projects, alongside an enabling policy environment that encourages private sector participation and reinforces investor confidence.