    "chunk_text": "The hack targeted a nationwide database that allows federal, state and local law enforcement agencies to share criminal justice information.\n\nIt came two months after hacking group ShinyHunters claimed to have stolen personal information about FBI employees and job applicants from the bureau's recruitment website.\n\nThe failures have highlighted weaknesses in key infrastructure networks, financial institutions and everyday digital services relied upon by millions.\n\nTrump officials have insisted that the widespread disruptions do not appear to be a coordinated cyber strike.\n\nDirector of National Intelligence Jay Clayton tried to reassure Americans Sunday in TV interviews, saying that the breakdowns mostly result from urgent system updates meant to counter cybercriminals who are increasingly leveraging advanced AI tools to launch attacks of unparalleled size and frequency."
