    "md5": "96d6abd0d47c47f81d6ee25e73490729",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1856,
    "chunk_text": "US issues fresh security alert for Americans across Middle East over Iran, Houthi attack threat\n\nHindustan Times - The US State Department has issued a fresh security alert for American citizens across the Middle East. The department warned of an increased threat from Iranian-backed Houthi forces and possible attacks targeting US government personnel and facilities.\n\nThe advisory urged Americans to remain vigilant amid rising regional tensions that could trigger flight cancellations, airspace closures and broader travel disruptions.\n\nThe warning comes as the United States says Iran and its allied groups have expanded attacks against American interests and regional partners.\n\nIn security messages published through several US embassies in the region on Tuesday, the State Department advised US citizens to closely monitor local developments and prepare for rapidly changing security conditions.\n\n\u201cAmericans in the Middle East should exercise heightened vigilance due to the increased threat of armed attacks by Iranian-supported Houthis and Iranian efforts to target U.S. government officials and facilities in the region,\u201d the department said.\n\nThe advisory also urged travellers to remain aware of \u201cpotential alerts, flight cancellations, airspace closures and travel disruptions,\u201d saying the regional security situation could deteriorate quickly.\n\n\u201cThe hostilities have the potential to escalate rapidly,\u201d the department warned.\n\nThe State Department said Iran had previously launched attacks targeting US assets in Bahrain and Kuwait. Meanwhile, Iranian-backed Houthis have continued military operations against Saudi Arabia, including strikes on civilian airports and key infrastructure.\n\nThe advisory follows a reported Houthi attack earlier on Tuesday that struck one of the towers at Riyadh\u2019s Financial Centre in Saudi Arabia."
