    "chunk_text": "In the private and plantation sectors, project partnered with key industry and labour bodies, including the Employers\u2019 Federation of Ceylon (EFC), the UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka, the National Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka (NCCSL), and the National Labour Advisory Council (NLAC), to advance gender equality and workplace safety.\n\nWith roughly two-thirds of Sri Lanka\u2019s workforce operating within the informal economy, the project also targeted grassroots participation. The project partnered with the Centre for Poverty Analysis (CEPA), the Coalition for Inclusive Impact, and World Vision Lanka to support 33 community forums across the Gampaha, Badulla, and Batticaloa districts.\n\nOver 180 forum members received policy and advocacy training to better articulate local priorities to district-level authorities. As a result, workers in fisheries, agriculture, and plantations now have direct channels to raise concerns with district officials, ensuring grassroots realities help inform national policymaking.\n\nAs the formal project concludes, UN agencies and government partners emphasised that maintaining active engagement across all tiers of society will be critical to preserving these trust-building gains and advancing long-term stability in Sri Lanka."
