    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "\"During a meeting, I saw him and heard his voice, triumphant, master of everything: \"Now I have obtained everything I wanted\", the pontiff noted.\n\n\"I cannot forget the powerful rasp of his voice. The Lord gave me the opportunity to leave that meeting and so I was freed.\"\n\nThese were times of spiritual crisis for the Argentine pontiff, between 2021 and 2022, observes Cardinal Fern\u00e1ndez who, although he has been one of the religious figures closest to the Pope for almost twenty years, never received confidences from him on the subject.\n\n\"The Pope perceives what he calls pagan seduction. The difficulty of managing power. The power a pope has is not only internal to the curia [administrative body of the Catholic Church]; it concerns international relations. And for him it represented a strong temptation\", said the cardinal in an interview on Monday with the newspaper Corriere della Sera.\n\n\"There are no gestures of his that show a man obsessed with power, who mistreats people. It was something interior. The fear of reaching a demonic point. The need to remember that he was a simple man, a creature of God, someone in need\", Fern\u00e1ndez added, admitting that he had doubts about publishing these writings so as not to \"upset anyone\".\n\nAmong the visions experienced and described by Begoglio in fact, there is also one of hell. \"I saw the gates of hell. Pagan seduction with all its force\", he wrote in Spanish in the original collected by the prefect.\n\n\"I leaned forward to look a little and it terrified me. It was before sleeping\", Francis recounted. \"Into hell one slips as the most natural thing. It is not the first time in my life that I have had this experience, but this time it was of a devouring intensity. It is dangerous to approach the gates of hell because the flames can come out and burn you.\"\n\nFern\u00e1ndez has tried to explain what the Pope's temptations might have been, whom he describes as a \"mystic\"."
  },
