    "chunk_size_bytes": 1144,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cYou have come nicely dressed today\u201d: Speaker to Sajith\n\nColombo, Nov. 25 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Speaker Jagath Wickramaratne complimented Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa on his choice of attire in Parliament today (25), after Premadasa attended the session dressed in orange to mark the launch of the global \u201816 Days of Activism against Gender-Based Violence\u2019 campaign.\n\nDuring his remarks in Parliament, Premadasa said that although the campaign was observed over 16 days, efforts to protect women and girls from violence should continue throughout the year, 24 hours a day.\n\nHe also commended Prime Minister Harini Amarasuriya for her remarks on violence against women, particularly her observation that abuse often occurs within close personal relationships.\n\nPremadasa said he had worn orange to express solidarity with women and children.\n\nAs the Speaker urged him to conclude his remarks due to time constraints, Premadasa thanked the Chair for allowing him to speak despite interruptions.\n\nResponding in a lighter vein, the Speaker remarked, \u201cYou have come nicely dressed today,\u201d before inviting the Prime Minister to respond."
