    "chunk_text": "Jurors watched a video that, according to prosecutors, showed a Huawei employee slipping a piece of a T-Mobile testing robot into his backpack, and heard about a Huawei engineer sneaking into a Fujitsu booth at a trade show to photograph a device.\n\nThe defense argued that HSBC and the other banks knew about Huawei\u2019s business in Iran and were competing for Huawei\u2019s business.\n\nHeberlig accused prosecutors during his closing argument of having \u201ccherry-picked\u201d a handful of disparate incidents to support their claim of a 20-year conspiracy. Heberlig said Huawei succeeded through \u201chard work, innovation, and investment in research and development.\u201d\n\nThe company has more than 200,000 employees and operates in approximately 170 countries."
