    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ca3cd90a677f823be575df02a62fa6c8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2019,
    "chunk_text": "But, in this real life case as in Greene\u2019s fictitious one (perhaps based on a real life story known to him), police can\u2019t establish a motive. It\u2019s nothing personal, and the impersonal quality of the act is truly chilling.\n\nStreet gangs are a significant problem in the United Kingdom, and they are more violent than the one in \u2018Destructors.\u2019 Orrganised gang activity and violence are heavily concentrated in major cities such as London, Birmingham, Manchester, Liverpool, and Glasgow\u2014as well as certain regional areas and smaller towns.\n\nThese gangs are associated with serious youth violence, knife and firearm offenses, \u201ccounty lines\u201d drug supply networks,\u00a0 retail theft and counterfeiting. But according to research,\u00a0 the violence mainly takes the form of confrontations\u00a0 between rival groups; it poses less of a threat to the general public.\n\nIn Asia, Hong Kong was known for violent street gangs \u2013 it was said that Bruce Lee studied martial arts to escape street violence. But the\u00a0 city no longer has a major street gang problem, though organised criminal syndicates known as triads still exist. These triad groups have shifted toward cybercrime, online scams, money laundering, and white-collar schemes.\n\nIn India, criminal activity by young men and teenagers takes a different hue \u2013 there are no street gangs like in the US and UK, but adolescent and older males have weaponised rape and use it\u00a0 to intimidate girls and women. Sometimes, the victims are killed to silence them. One such victim was reported from Gujarat State\u2019s Surat City, known for\u00a0 its diamond polishing industry. The girl was 9-11 years old, and her\u00a0 battered body bore 86 injury marks.\n\nAccording to a BBC report, the police believe she was held captive, tortured and ravaged. More than 10 days after they found her body, the police checked the list of some 8,000 missing children and couldn\u2019t identify her. \u201cThere was no sign of struggle at the spot where the body was found,\u201d the local police chief said."
  },
