    "chunk_size_bytes": 1110,
    "chunk_text": "Can a Government undertake tourism and infrastructure development in Anuradhapura without first establishing, through proper archaeological, hydrological and environmental studies, that the ancient water systems, archaeological landscape and sacred character will be protected?\n\nAnuradhapura is not simply land available for development. It is a national inheritance held in trust for generations yet unborn. It is a government\u2019s duty is to preserve its archaeological integrity, ancient water civilisation, sacred character and historical landscape.\n\nDevelopment must serve this heritage, not destroy or diminish it. Two essential original authorities to attach to this article: The Eppawala Supreme Court judgement \u2013 Bulankulama and others Vs Freeport-McMoRan and others. https://elaw.org/resource/sri-lanka-bulankulama-v-min-industrial-development-eppawala-case-sc-application-no-88499-fr) ; Justice Weeramantry\u2019s international environmental jurisprudence and Sri Lanka\u2019s ancient irrigation wisdom.\n\n(Kirthimala Gunaskera is a senior Attorney at Law who worked\u00a0 with\u00a0 Justice A R B\u00a0 Amerasinghe)."
