    "md5": "168afc91be814c711e237925ed85c0f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "As an initiative awareness idea, People\u2019s Leasing has dedicated its 2026 annual calendar to this important theme, using it as a creative communication platform to bring the message of lung health and disease prevention into homes, workplaces and communities across the country. This initiative marks the beginning of a series of community-focused programmes and awareness campaigns the company has lined up, with the broader objective of educating the public, encouraging preventive healthcare and supporting national efforts to safeguard the well-being of the present and future generations.\n\nAt People\u2019s Leasing, we believe that our responsibility as a corporate citizen extends far beyond financial services and business performance. We have a greater role to play in contributing to the well-being of society and the future of our nation. We selected lung health as the focus of our 2026 annual calendar because it is an issue that touches every family and deserves greater public attention.\n\nThrough this initiative, we hope to take an important health message to every corner of the country, encourage greater awareness and support the collective effort towards building a healthier nation. We believe that a healthy nation is the foundation of a prosperous nation,\u201d said People\u2019s Leasing Chairman Prof. Ajantha Samarakoon, expressing his views on why the company chose this cause.\n\nThe company intends to deliver the message \u2013 communication, public engagement, partnerships and practical action.\n\n\u201cAlongside the launch of the \u2018Suwa Husma\u2019 national programme, we have dedicated our 2026 annual calendar to lung health, utilising this widely accessible communication medium to keep an important health message alive and visible among the public throughout the year. Our intention is to transform awareness into meaningful action."
