    "chunk_text": "\u201cAlongside the launch of the \u2018Suwa Husma\u2019 national programme, we have dedicated our 2026 annual calendar to lung health, utilising this widely accessible communication medium to keep an important health message alive and visible among the public throughout the year. Our intention is to transform awareness into meaningful action.\n\nThis calendar is just the beginning of a broader programme of activities that People\u2019s Leasing has planned in collaboration with the relevant stakeholders. Through these initiatives, we aim to reach diverse communities, encourage preventive healthcare practices and make a practical contribution to improving the quality of life of our people,\u201d said People\u2019s Leasing General Manager and CEO Sanjeewa Bandaranayake.\n\nThe SLCP joining the project as the principal medical and technical partner brings the essential medical expertise, professional credibility and national healthcare experience to the campaign.\n\n\u201cLung health is fundamental to the overall well-being and quality of life of every individual; yet, respiratory diseases continue to pose a significant health challenge. One of the most effective ways to address this challenge is through public awareness, early recognition of symptoms, timely medical intervention and preventive healthcare practices. We greatly appreciate the initiative taken by People\u2019s Leasing and its partners to bring the importance of lung health into the national conversation. What makes this programme particularly valuable is its intention to reach people across the country, taking essential health messages beyond hospitals and healthcare institutions and into everyday communities.\n\nWe hope this initiative will encourage people to pay greater attention to their respiratory health, protect their lungs and recognise that keeping our lungs healthy is ashared responsibility. A healthier nation begins with healthier lungs,\u201d stated SLCP President Dr. D.M. Sumana Handagala."
