    "chunk_text": "SriLankan Airlines Senior Manager Product Development Maria Sathasivam stated, \u201cRecognition of this nature is particularly meaningful to us because it comes directly from our passengers and reflects the actual experiences of those who travel with us. It reaffirms the importance of continuously listening to our passengers and evolving our product. Moreover, retaining our Four-Star Major Airline rating for eight consecutive years is especially encouraging, as it speaks to our commitment to delivering a consistent passenger experience.\n\nThe enhancements include increased local content showcasing Sinhala variety programmes, binge-worthy teledramas in box-set format and insightful documentaries covering travel, culture, industry and current affairs.\n\nThe local lineup is further enriched with exclusive podcasts and interviews from leading Sri Lankan publications, alongside vibrant music videos and curated audio compilations featuring seasonal playlists, tributes and emerging local artists.\n\nComplementing its homegrown offerings, the airline has also broadened its regional entertainment portfolio to reflect the diverse tastes of passengers travelling across the Indian subcontinent and beyond. The travellers can now enjoy an expanded catalogue of popular Tamil, Hindi and South Asian cinema, paired with a wider selection of contemporary regional music albums across multiple genres, delivering a richer and more inclusive onboard experience."
