    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "At Frankfurt School, Dr. Bald is Academic Director of the Certified Expert programmes in Risk Management, Treasury and Markets and Climate Risk Management. His expertise spans quantitative analytics, machine learning and generative AI, supported by his background in software development and statistics, a doctorate in economics, a German MBA and the US Certified Management Accountant qualification.\n\nThe programme will explore how the directors and senior executives can move beyond conventional approaches to risk identification and incorporate analytical insights into strategic decision-making.\n\nKey areas of focus will include quantitative risk assessment and management, risk analytics, key performance indicators, scenario analysis, risk dashboards and early warning indicators.\n\nThe programme will also address sustainability-related risks and the requirements of IFRS S1 and IFRS S2, alongside board risk oversight, reporting and accountability. Practical case studies and applications will connect these concepts with the challenges faced by organisations and their boards.\n\nThrough this inaugural collaboration, the SLID and Frankfurt School of Finance & Management aim to establish a platform for continued knowledge exchange and international engagement, bringing global expertise and practical insights to Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate sector.\n\nBy strengthening participants\u2019 understanding of risk analysis and oversight, the programme seeks to support more informed decision-making, stronger governance practices and greater organisational resilience.\n\nEarly-bird registration is open until November 23, 2026, at a fee of Rs.120,000 for the SLID members and Rs.130,000 for non-members. Interested participants are encouraged to register early to secure their places. For registrations and further information, participants may contact the SLID via [email\u00a0protected], call 076 545 4279, or visit www.slid.lk."
