    "language": "en",
    "md5": "813830a37d3542f490cbdfec4aa76cc9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1826,
    "chunk_text": "Access Engineering takes largest slice of Ruwanpura Expressway in Rs.68bn contract haul\n\nThree RDA packages worth Rs.68bn, over 5 times last year\u2019s civil engineering revenue\n\nNew wins alone exceed Rs.62.9bn order book estimated as at June\n\nAccess Engineering PLC (AEL) has secured three Road Development Authority (RDA) contracts worth a combined Rs.68 billion on the Central and Ruwanpura expressways, a haul which on its own amounts to more than five times the revenue its civil engineering arm generated last financial year, a stock filing showed.\n\nThe company received letters of acceptance dated November 19 for Package 1J of Section 4 of the Central Expressway, valued at Rs.22.39 billion and for Packages 1E and 1G of Phase 1 of the Ruwanpura Expressway, worth Rs.27.99 billion and Rs.17.62 billion, respectively. All three values are stated exclusive of VAT and will be added to its construction order book.\n\nThe letters followed the Cabinet\u2019s approval last week of 23 packages worth Rs.494.81 billion across the two projects. These cover the Kahathuduwa-Ingiriya first phase of the Ruwanpura Expressway, including the system interchange linking it to the Southern Expressway and the 38.5-kilometre Kurunegala-Galewela stretch that forms the first phase of the Central Expressway\u2019s fourth section.\n\nAt Rs.45.61 billion, AEL\u2019s two Ruwanpura packages make up 18.1 percent of Rs.251.37 billion awarded for the phase. That is the largest combined share won by any contractor, ahead of Maga Engineering\u2019s Rs.39.99 billion across two packages, although International Construction Consortium holds the single biggest package at Rs.34.94 billion.\n\nAEL\u2019s Central Expressway package represents 9.2 percent of Rs.243.44 billion awarded under 12 packages, giving the company 13.7 percent of the overall value approved."
  },
