    "chunk_size_bytes": 1746,
    "chunk_text": "At Rs.45.61 billion, AEL\u2019s two Ruwanpura packages make up 18.1 percent of Rs.251.37 billion awarded for the phase. That is the largest combined share won by any contractor, ahead of Maga Engineering\u2019s Rs.39.99 billion across two packages, although International Construction Consortium holds the single biggest package at Rs.34.94 billion.\n\nAEL\u2019s Central Expressway package represents 9.2 percent of Rs.243.44 billion awarded under 12 packages, giving the company 13.7 percent of the overall value approved.\n\nIn its earnings summary for the September quarter, released on November 19, HNB Stockbrokers noted that the two Ruwanpura packages \u201cshould meaningfully expand its order book\u201d. It also expects the year-end government capital spending, which is typically concentrated in the December quarter, to speed up the conversion of the existing orders into revenue.\n\nThe new packages also replenish a construction pipeline that had thinned as several flagship projects reached completion. According to its annual report, AEL handed over Package 1M of Section 3 of the Central Expressway to the RDA in December 2025 and the 1,000-unit Stadiumgama housing project to the Urban Development Authority in February 2026, while Phase 1 of the West Container Terminal at the Colombo Port was also handed over during the 2025/26 financial year.\n\nCompany-level revenue, which is anchored in construction, slipped 10 percent to Rs.10.89 billion in the six months to September when compared to the same period last year.\n\nHowever, the civil engineering segment has grown more profitable. Its operating profit climbed 28.9 percent to Rs.1.96 billion in the first half and the operating margin widened to 23.9 percent, from 17.2 percent a year earlier."
  },
