    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "However, the civil engineering segment has grown more profitable. Its operating profit climbed 28.9 percent to Rs.1.96 billion in the first half and the operating margin widened to 23.9 percent, from 17.2 percent a year earlier.\n\n\u201cLooking ahead, the civil engineering segment is expected to benefit from the opportunities arising from the next phases of the Central Expressway,\u201d the company stated in its 2025/26 annual report.\n\nThe work should also flow through to AEL\u2019s construction materials arm, which runs asphalt plants, quarries and crusher plants across the island. The segment\u2019s first-half revenue fell 18.4 percent to Rs.2.67 billion, with HNB Stockbrokers linking a steeper 26 percent drop in the September quarter to the lower concrete demand after the West Container Terminal project was completed in March 2026.\n\nIn its annual report, the company had flagged the continued development of the Central Expressway network as a key driver of demand for asphalt, ready-mix concrete and aggregates.\n\nAt group level, revenue rose 63 percent to Rs.36.97 billion in the six months ended September 30, 2026, when compared to the same period last year. The handovers at the Marina Square condominium project brought in Rs.8.99 billion, while the automobile revenue grew 47.5 percent to Rs.15.46 billion.\n\nProfit before tax climbed 67 percent to Rs.6.62 billion and the profit attributable to the shareholders rose 128 percent to Rs.5.79 billion, from Rs.2.54 billion.\n\nMeanwhile, AEL\u2019s interest cover improved to 4.34 times, from 3.75 times a year earlier. The operations generated Rs.2.75 billion in net cash during the half, reversing an outflow of Rs.5.51 billion in the same period last year, helped by a Rs.7.69 billion reduction in inventories since March.\n\nThe net gearing improved to 0.81 times, from 0.91 times in March, as per HNB Stockbrokers, with equity growing 13.7 percent over the period while the net debt edged up by less than 2 percent to Rs.39.5 billion."
