    "chunk_size_bytes": 899,
    "chunk_text": "The net gearing improved to 0.81 times, from 0.91 times in March, as per HNB Stockbrokers, with equity growing 13.7 percent over the period while the net debt edged up by less than 2 percent to Rs.39.5 billion.\n\nThe combined Rs.494.81 billion in the expressway contracts is equal to 24.7 percent of the Rs.2 trillion capital expenditure allocation for 2027, as the government pushes to speed up public investment. HNB Stockbrokers, which puts that allocation at about 40 percent higher than this year\u2019s, expects it to \u201csupport new order intake\u201d.\u00a0 The budget allocates Rs.30 billion for the Kurunegala-Galewela section and Rs.27 billion for the Ruwanpura Expressway next year, together 11.5 percent of the value awarded, which means the work and revenue that comes with it, will be spread over several years.\n\nThe construction on the Ruwanpura Expressway is slated to begin on December 1. (NF)"
