    "chunk_text": "We recently concluded some projects addressing female genital mutilation, and are continuing programmes on legal and counselling support to victims of GBV, providing digital skills, vocational skill support to women in tourism, and political empowerment of women. We also work with the National Commission on Women. We look at supporting making more structural changes to make a real change. One example is the project we are currently implementing with the Family Planning Association of Sri Lanka to Integrate Gender Based Violence (GBV) Screening in Antenatal Care in Sri Lanka.\n\nLike I said, we are in this all together. Sri Lanka is active in preventing violence against women. Let\u2019s learn from each other\u2019s experiences and best practices. When compared with the regional neighbours, Sri Lanka recorded the lowest score in Intimate Partner Violence. However, there is still more to do to ensure a much safer Sri Lanka for women and girls. The vast majority of women face harassment on public transport. Let\u2019s work all together on including men in the equation to prevent GBV.\n\nQ What is the latest progress on the preservation of Dutch heritage sites in Sri Lanka?"
