    "chunk_text": "Like I said, we are in this all together. Sri Lanka is active in preventing violence against women. Let\u2019s learn from each other\u2019s experiences and best practices. When compared with the regional neighbours, Sri Lanka recorded the lowest score in Intimate Partner Violence. However, there is still more to do to ensure a much safer Sri Lanka for women and girls. The vast majority of women face harassment on public transport. Let\u2019s work all together on including men in the equation to prevent GBV.\n\nQ What is the latest progress on the preservation of Dutch heritage sites in Sri Lanka?\n\nCurrently, there is a Dutch Research Council-funded programme headed by the Sri Lanka National Archives to document the Sri Lankan palm leaf manuscripts in the collections of Dutch museums. This is a very important programme in which Dutch and Sri Lankan partners work collaboratively to document and digitise this corpus. Last November, the Netherlands provided the Sri Lanka National Archives with a high-tech industrial scanner for digitisation of the 300 metres of VOC archives. This will in time provide everybody with access to (machine-translated) archive material of that period.\n\nQ What is the latest on the plan to return artefacts taken during the colonial time?\n\nAfter the first repatriation in 2023, the Sri Lankan Government had submitted a second Repatriation request of six more artefacts housed in the Rijksmuseum and the World Museum. This request is currently being processed by the Colonial Collections Committee of the Netherlands together with the newly appointed Sri Lankan Restitution Committee.\n\nQ As a member of European Union, how do you see the new counter terrorism law- Prevention of State from Terrorism Bill and the Organised Crimes Bill?"
