    "chunk_size_bytes": 1707,
    "chunk_text": "After the first repatriation in 2023, the Sri Lankan Government had submitted a second Repatriation request of six more artefacts housed in the Rijksmuseum and the World Museum. This request is currently being processed by the Colonial Collections Committee of the Netherlands together with the newly appointed Sri Lankan Restitution Committee.\n\nQ As a member of European Union, how do you see the new counter terrorism law- Prevention of State from Terrorism Bill and the Organised Crimes Bill?\n\nSri Lanka will apply in the coming months for the extension of GSP+ after 2029. The new laws will certainly be considered. If your economy keeps on growing like this, you will graduate from GSP+ within six to seven years to the level where you need an FTA, which is something most people are not aware of yet.\n\nQIn Europe, youth activists create violence, posing fresh challenges to democratic governance. How does the Netherlands view it?\n\nRecent protests in Europe find their roots in calls from young people to improve the educational systems and changes in the labour market, as well as the high cost of living. In the Netherlands, protests are mostly conducted in an orderly way and without great violence and looting. The Netherlands has one of the most affordable educational systems that facilitates social mobility and is better prepared for an ageing society because of a robust pension system. The economy is doing relatively well, and there is still a great demand for workers and low youth unemployment. But we need to make sure that this relatively successful economic model also keeps on delivering for young people because the model is under pressure by, for instance, housing shortages and AI."
