    "chunk_text": "HIP said its marine services include afloat repairs, underwater services, surveys, provisions, bunker supplies and lay-up facilities, subject to availability.\n\nThe port also maintains firefighting and rescue tugs on round-the-clock standby, supported by a dedicated Emergency Response Unit and equipment to handle oil and chemical spills.\n\nDuring the MT New Diamond tanker fire off Sri Lanka in September 2020, two tugs from Hambantota joined the wider firefighting operation, while the port received 20 crew members from the vessel.\n\nIn February 2022, HIP's Emergency Response Unit, together with its Quality, Health, Safety and Environment Department and Port Control, responded to a fire in the emergency generator room of the drillship West Polaris, which was berthed at the port. The fire was brought under control within 33 minutes of the teams' arrival, preventing serious damage to the vessel and surrounding area.\n\nHIP said its location, approximately 10 nautical miles from the main East-West shipping route, further strengthens its ability to assist vessels offshore and respond to maritime emergencies.\n\nMeanwhile, Ceyline Maritime Services provides ship agency and engineering support at ports across Sri Lanka, including vessel repairs, lay-up assistance, underwater inspections and the clearance and delivery of ship spare parts."
