    "time_ut": 1795602639.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-25-dailymirrorlk-ecffb68f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "39d56453aaa2ec99f2680a681e3fc4dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1739,
    "chunk_text": "China lashes out at US for \u2018suppressing\u2019 Chinese companies after Huawei conviction\n\nHindustan Times - China on Wednesday criticised the United States for \u201csuppressing\u201d Chinese companies after a US jury found telecommunications giant Huawei guilty of stealing trade secrets and other criminal offences.\n\nThe remarks came after a federal jury in Brooklyn, New York, found Huawei guilty on 10 of the 12 criminal counts it faced, including bank fraud, conspiracy to steal trade secrets and conspiracy to defraud the United States. The verdict followed a trial lasting more than two months and involved allegations concerning Huawei's business in Iran and its dealings with American technology companies.\n\n\u201cThe Chinese government firmly opposes the US suppressing and containing Chinese enterprises and firmly supports Chinese enterprises in safeguarding their legitimate rights and interests,\u201d Chinese foreign ministry spokesperson Guo Jiakun said at a news briefing on Wednesday, when asked about the conviction, AFP reported.\n\nHuawei and three of its affiliates faced 12 charges, including bank fraud, wire fraud, violations of US sanctions and conspiracy to steal trade secrets. Prosecutors alleged that the company concealed details of its Iranian operations from financial institutions and obtained technology belonging to several US businesses.\n\nJurors found the company guilty on 10 counts but acquitted it of racketeering conspiracy, which accused Huawei of operating as a criminal enterprise, Reuters reported.\n\nThe jury also acquitted Huawei of conspiring to obstruct justice, according to Reuters. The trial lasted more than two months, with prosecutors calling over 60 witnesses and the defence presenting 15 witnesses."
  },
