    "md5": "54d9b012e003784aac95daae1f130dd9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1820,
    "chunk_text": "Use & Reuse: circularity, water-use monitoring and efficiency, with treated wastewater returned to productive use;\n\nAudit & Accounting: metering, water audits and a Water Balance Sheet for every site;\n\nThe 5 i's: from problem to proven impact. Every project, in every district, moves through the same five steps:\n\ni1 Incidence: know the problem before funding the fix, through baseline surveys, science-based targets, GIS mapping and early metering, producing a baseline Water Balance Sheet;\n\ni2 Innovation: design the solution, the programme and the financing together, using green, low-energy technology aligned with national priorities and SDG 6;\n\ni3 Invitation: bring government, the private sector, civil society and communities to one table, agreeing a Water Compact on who pays, who builds and who measures;\n\ni4 Intervention: build and run the solution on the ground, operated locally, starting with a showcase cluster and then scaling district by district;\n\ni5 Impact: measure results against the baseline, have them independently assured, and certify verified water as AquaKredits.\n\nAquas360 gives Sri Lanka a complete picture of its water; the 5 i's give it a repeatable way to act on that picture. Together with AqVerium for finance and the Water Parliament for standards, they turn the five pillars into a programme that can be delivered, financed and proven. Financing the mission: AqVerium as a water sustainability financing platform\n\nPublic budgets alone cannot carry a national mission of this scale, and they should not have to. Across the world, impact funds, ESG funds and companies with water stewardship commitments are looking for credible water projects to back. What has held them back is not willingness but trust: they need to know that every rupee they invest delivers real, measurable water."
