    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "Public budgets alone cannot carry a national mission of this scale, and they should not have to. Across the world, impact funds, ESG funds and companies with water stewardship commitments are looking for credible water projects to back. What has held them back is not willingness but trust: they need to know that every rupee they invest delivers real, measurable water.\n\nESG funds and institutional investors looking for credible, disclosure-ready water assets;\n\nPrivate sector contributions, from corporate social responsibility budgets to water stewardship commitments; and\n\nDevelopment and climate finance, blended with private capital to lower risk and raise scale.\n\nWhat makes this capital flow is accurate and assured measurement of impact. Every project financed through AqVerium is baselined before it begins, metered at source and cross-checked with satellite data as it runs, aligned with science-based parameters, hydrogeological analysis, and independently verified before any result is recognised, with AqVerium\u2019s Assurance Partner.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, this creates a simple promise to every funder: you will see exactly what your money achieved, in litres, in a specific basin, assured by an independent party. For the Government, it means more projects delivered for every rupee of public money, with national priorities and national authorisation always in the lead. AqVerium has already issued over 7 million AquaKredits, and the same infrastructure stands ready to serve Sri Lanka\u2019s mission. Why I have dedicated my life to water\n\nFor over 16 years, Team AquaKraft and I have worked where water problems are most real: in villages, towns and industries struggling with scarcity and pollution. Those years have taught us that the people closest to the problem often hold the answer, if we give them the tools and the trust to act."
