    "chunk_text": "For over 16 years, Team AquaKraft and I have worked where water problems are most real: in villages, towns and industries struggling with scarcity and pollution. Those years have taught us that the people closest to the problem often hold the answer, if we give them the tools and the trust to act.\n\nthe Geo Soil Filter, turning wastewater into a resource through nature-based treatment;\n\nAqVerium, building the digital infrastructure to verify and value water outcomes;\n\nthe Unified Water Protocol, which reconciles nine leading global water standards into one common data dictionary of 44 fields;\n\nthe Global Water Registry, giving verified water outcomes a permanent, transparent record; and\n\nthe Water Parliament itself, a global platform to bring every conscious stakeholder together to democratically discuss, deliberate and decide on emerging trends of water sustainability.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, this means a partner that brings not a single technology, but an integrated system, and my lifelong commitment to water sustainability. The Water Parliament: a home for every conscious stakeholder\n\nNo nation can become water positive alone, and no single company, bank or university can make it happen. Water positivity is a shared ambition, and it needs a shared platform."
