    "md5": "db8b921c1be980bbd9b70d5d6f20603a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1391,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka: More than just a tourist destination - A home to many foreigners\n\nColombo, Nov. 25 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Of the approximately 20,000 foreign nationals living, working and investing in Sri Lanka, a significant number are presently on the wrong visa type or are overstaying their visas. This is often through no fault of their own, but rather because of poor advice and guidance from substandard visa agents.\n\nThere is no doubt that Sri Lanka is one of the most sought-after destinations in the world to visit and live in. Its geographic location, its beaches being declared among the world's best in 2026, the Pekoe Trail being named one of TIME's World's Greatest Places, and its many other accolades all add to its appeal. Combined with the opportunities it offers for employment and investment, these qualities place Sri Lanka on the bucket list of many a global citizen.\n\nYet it tugs at the heartstrings to hear of a foreign woman who was told unequivocally by a visa agent that she could work as a yoga instructor at a wellness spa without a valid private sector employment visa, only to be deported for not holding the correct visa.\n\nThen there is the elderly English gentleman who was advised that he could run his guest house and employ foreign nationals without SLTDA approval. And so the list goes on.\n\nBut first, let us focus on why they are here, in this beautiful country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-25-dailymirrorlk-a3a1170f",
