    "chunk_text": "The reality is that a legitimate stay in Sri Lanka, and the peace of mind that comes with it, depend on following the correct procedures. These procedures are designed to protect Sri Lanka's interests as well as those of its foreign residents. Any agent who fails to explain, for example, that employment visas require recommendations from the relevant line ministry, that tourism-related businesses employing foreign nationals should be registered with the SLTDA, which bank accounts are required for an investor visa, or the difference between an IIA account and a VPFCA account, undermines this framework and compromises the stability of the foreign national's stay in the country.\n\nFor those hoping to make Sri Lanka a long-term home, falling in love with the country is only the beginning. Living here legitimately depends on accurate information, the correct documentation, and a sound understanding of the country's immigration framework. These may be less glamorous than the surf in Arugam Bay or the tea estates of Hatton, but they are the reality.\n\nSo, as Frank closes his laptop, looks out at the bay, and wonders whether to take a swim or have a cold beer, let us hope that he is here on the correct visa, enjoying the peace of mind that comes with it and living his best life on the Pearl of the Indian Ocean.\n\nKavitha is a Barrister-at-Law (Lincoln\u2019s Inn), a senior legal academic and the Head of Operations at Ceylon Migration Pvt. Ltd."
