    "md5": "bffe89c8db7dcbacd0088c0494610adb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1814,
    "chunk_text": "President stresses need to fast-track district development projects\n\nColombo, Nov. 25 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has stressed the need to expedite district-level development projects while ensuring the efficient and effective utilisation of public funds.\n\nThe President instructed ministries and government institutions to prepare plans for implementing their respective development projects from the beginning of each financial year and conduct monthly reviews to assess their progress.\n\nHe made these remarks at a recent meeting of the Ministerial Consultative Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development, held at Parliament under his chairmanship.\n\nThe President explained that funds remaining unutilised at the end of a financial year could be carried forward to the following year only if certain conditions had been met, including the opening of Letters of Credit (LCs) for the relevant projects.\n\nOtherwise, the allocated funds would have to be returned to the General Treasury, and fresh allocations would need to be obtained through the following year's Budget.\n\nAgainst this backdrop, he stressed the importance of closely monitoring district-level project implementation based on the project report books submitted to District Development Committees.\n\nThe meeting also discussed the provision of fertiliser subsidies to farmers and the management of paddy stocks during the Maha cultivation season. Particular attention was drawn to the need to dispose of or utilise the remaining paddy stocks in storage facilities before the next Maha harvest is received.\n\nSeveral options were considered for converting the existing paddy stocks into rice for distribution through welfare programmes or utilising them for other purposes, including animal feed and other products."
  },
