    "chunk_text": "The Yale Budget Lab and other trade trackers didn't offer an immediate read on how the new tariffs would affect overall tariff levels, but the group calculated earlier this month that the effective US tariff rate sits at about 11.3% across all trading partners. That same measure was 13.86% just before the Supreme Court struck down Trump's blanket tariffs in February and was above 15% for much of 2025.\n\nThis investigation has long been expected to wrap up by the end of the year, but the unveiling this week was notable amid growing concerns in Washington over semiconductor exports, Nvidia, and questions about \"mass smuggling\" of advanced chips to China.\n\nThe announcement also came on the heels of a trip to Asia where President Trump had a trade signing ceremony with Thailand and announced what he called a trade deal with the Philippines but left many of the major trade issues between the US and China unresolved.\n\nThat meeting ended with no apparent agreement to extend the truce that has lowered tariffs between the US and China that expires on Jan. 10.\n\nUS prepares higher tariffs on China, EU and 14 other nations"
