    "chunk_size_bytes": 924,
    "chunk_text": "Thabbowa Reservoir spill gates to be opened, residents warned\n\nColombo, Nov. 25 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Two spill gates of the Thabbowa Reservoir are expected to be opened by 10 p.m. today to control the rising water levels amid prevailing rainy weather conditions, the Irrigation Department said.\n\nEach gate is expected to be opened by six inches, releasing an estimated 220 cubic feet of water per second into the Mee Oya.\n\nThe Irrigation Department has urged residents living along both banks of the Mee Oya downstream of the Thabbowa Reservoir to remain vigilant and closely monitor changes in water levels.\n\nThe department said the extent of spill gate openings could be adjusted depending on the volume of water flowing into the reservoir and rainfall in its catchment area.\n\nResidents have been advised to follow announcements and safety instructions issued by the Irrigation Department and Disaster Management authorities."
