    "md5": "13d130e3ed4dbaabf80c08e6bbc96b39",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1434,
    "chunk_text": "Ending violence requires connecting Government commitments to a powerful public narrative. Sri Lanka possesses deeply ingrained cultural values of respect, protection, care and dignity for women. We must draw on these values to nurture children who understand consent, build communities that firmly reject violence, and engage men and boys as active partners in positive change. No woman should ever have to alter how she dresses, travels, works or lives simply to stay safe and free from violence.\n\nUNFPA has supported the Government of Sri Lanka in these efforts, providing technical and financial assistance for the National Gender Equality and Women\u2019s Empowerment Policy and technical support towards the Women Empowerment Act and its strategic action plan. We remain dedicated to accompanying national partners in translating these legislative milestones into lasting, progressive change.\n\nSri Lanka has made commendable progress. We must recognise these achievements, build upon them and find the collective courage to address what remains unfinished. Success will be defined when fewer women experience violence, when survivors seek help without fear, and when every woman and girl lives with uncompromised dignity and freedom.\n\nJustice must never be something a woman has to fight endlessly to achieve; it must be a right she can confidently expect. That is the promise of #JusticeIsMyRight, and together, we must fulfil it."
  },
