    "chunk_size_bytes": 1967,
    "chunk_text": "Prof. Athukorala said the ratio had already reached the pre-crisis level as repayment of past due interest (PDI) bonds began in 2025. It would rise further once ISB coupon payments resume after 2027.\n\nPresident AKD\u2019s unprecedented, needless induction of the Chairman of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, which also contained ISB holders, as one of his two Economic advisors and a negotiator with the IMF and private foreign ISB holders, wasn\u2019t smart.\n\nI was amazed and amused to read Dr WA Wijewardena recommending Walt Rostow\u2019s \u2018The Stages of Economic Growth: An Anti-Communist Manifesto\u2019, to President Anura Dissanayake, adding that when he was a student of economics in the 1960s, Rostow was a \u2018hero\u2019. (https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Wijewardena-urges-AKD-to-follow-Rostows-Non-Communist-Manifesto-for-take-off/215-355071)\n\nAmong the best and brightest of Ceylonese economists of the 1960s, he wasn\u2019t.\n\nThough only a (precocious) boy, I got around quite a bit with my father and was in the room or restaurant when he was in conversation with his personal friends who were top economic thinkers and policy-makers: Gamani Corea, Godfrey Gunatilleke, Lal Jayawardena, Jayantha Kelegama, Nihal Kappagoda, David Loos to name a few. Their main concerns were Development (as distinct from mere \u2018Growth\u2019), greater autonomy for the Third World, and social welfare to maintain a decent, rising Quality of Life for the people. JK Galbraith and Raul Prebisch were among the giants in vogue at the time. Back issues of the MARGA journal would trace the intellectual lineage of the economic thinking of the day.\n\nAs for university students in the 1960s, they rebelled violently twice, clashing with the Police and the Army at Colombo and Peradeniya. I doubt my old friend, Economics student at Peradeniya in the mid-1960s, N. Shanmugaratnam, currently Professor Emeritus of Development Studies at a Norwegian university, ever regarded Rostow \u2018a hero\u2019."
  },
