    "chunk_text": "The economic policy elite which for the first time since 1948 overlaps with the actual economic elite, commended the President and Govt for the Budget, but urged expeditious movement along the same trajectory, to free or minimise exchange controls and liberalise labour and land laws. (https://www.ft.lk/top-story/Sri-Lanka-must-prove-recovery-is-more-than-a-cycle-Hosking/26-800322)\n\nOpposition Leader Sajith Premadasa directed a withering critique at the President\u2019s Budget and its social impacts.\n\nHowever, the Opposition as a whole didn\u2019t address and rule out some of the more drastic neoliberal measures lobbied for by the economic elite\u2014such as a return to the international money markets, further liberalisation of exchange controls, and \u2018liberalisation\u2019 of labour and land laws. The parameters of the alternative economic policy of the Opposition are as yet unknown.\n\nA Third Perspective from outside the economic and political establishments including the parliamentary Opposition, coming from \u2018the Movement\u2019, contains an intellectually serious, impressive analysis. The clearest scan of and sharpest scalpel dissecting the Budget was a substantive statement signed by a network of 38 trade unions and civic organisations, calling itself \u2018Trade Unions and People\u2019s Power!\u2019. (2027 Budget: Red herring to neutralise public and relink Sri Lanka with new financial colonialism | Daily FT)\n\nThe necessary convergence of academically-trained intellect and organised wage-earners has\u00a0 commenced. I gather that Dhanusha Pathirana, co-author of the book \u2018A History of Underdevelopment and Political Economy of Inflation in Sri Lanka\u2019 (Palgrave Macmillan, UK), is a member of the network and a principal author of this high-quality text.\n\nThe analysis contains a penetrating diagnosis and makes a logical, credible, extremely disturbing case.\n\nHere are the key take-aways from the text, in its own words, reproduced as bullet points. All bullet-points in this column are direct excerpts."
