    "chunk_text": "The analysis contains a penetrating diagnosis and makes a logical, credible, extremely disturbing case.\n\nHere are the key take-aways from the text, in its own words, reproduced as bullet points. All bullet-points in this column are direct excerpts.\n\nWhile Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate sector benefits by maintaining enormous tax breaks\u2026 crumbs [are] thrown to the general public through indirect tax relief on a few essentials. Reducing taxes on sprats, dry fish and exercise books\u2014alongside nominal salary increases for Government servants\u2014will do nothing to halt the worsening living costs or reverse the steep cuts in essential spending mandated by the 2027 proposals.\n\nHyper-inflationary indirect taxes are set to escalate by Rs. 170 billion, while the increase in direct tax income will be negligible at Rs. 30 billion, worsening the ratio between the two components to around 80% from 78% this year.\n\nSubsidies and transfers are slashed brutally by a staggering Rs. 100 billion (dropping from Rs. 1.57 trillion to Rs. 1.47 trillion)\u2014showing total disregard for mass poverty at 16% according to the Ministry of Health and malnutrition among school children as high as 25% (UNICEF Sri Lanka).\n\nCorporate income tax holidays, on the other hand, which cost a mammoth Rs. 190 billion in 2024/25 according to the Ministry of Finance Tax Expenditure Report, continue unabated.\n\n85% of the burden of the expected tax revenue increase falls squarely on the general public.\n\nThe statement sets out the cumulative negative consequences of Budget 2027 policies."
