    "chunk_text": "The 2027 Budget will ensure that this structural stagnation in the economy persists.\n\nThe \u2018Movement\u2019 statement then proceeds, as the parliamentary Opposition does not, to unmask what the Government is actually doing: the deliberate \u2018manufacture\u2019 of \u2018artificial\u2019 budget surpluses.\n\nThe current Government utilised only 8% of the funds allocated for Cyclone Ditwah victims by mid-2026, according to the World Bank. By overachieving revenue targets and underspending 2026 budgetary allocations by roughly Rs. 1 trillion compared to the proposed Rs. 7 trillion, the Government has manufactured a surplus of Rs. 22 billion on the back of neglected public services.\n\nWhile the 2026 Budget allocated a combined public investment of Rs. 425 billion to healthcare (Rs. 120 billion), education (Rs. 99 billion), water supply and sanitation (Rs. 95 billion), public transport (Rs. 67 billion) and housing (Rs. 44 billion), the Mid-Year Fiscal Position Report shows that only Rs. 55 billion of these commitments were actually met in the first six months.\n\nOut of the allocated sum of Rs. 33.6 billion for providing meals to school children (reduced to Rs. 33.5 billion in 2027), only Rs. 12.7 billion was utilised in the first half of 2026, even as child malnutrition across the country continues to rise.\n\nThe 38 organisations\u2019 statement penetrates way deeper than the Parliamentary Opposition to uncover and name the very logic that runs through and holds together the Government\u2019s economic strategy.\n\nThe primary goal of the current regime is to manufacture budget surpluses to appease international speculative finance and regain the capacity to issue new International Sovereign Bonds (ISBs) under IMF mandates."
