    "chunk_text": "The primary goal of the current regime is to manufacture budget surpluses to appease international speculative finance and regain the capacity to issue new International Sovereign Bonds (ISBs) under IMF mandates.\n\nGiven Prof Prema-chandra Athukorala\u2019s dire warning about \u2018debt overhang\u2019, this is suicidal.\n\n\u2026the regime\u2019s alliance with a broadly unproductive, hyper-consumerist business elite prevents it from imposing exchange controls, halting illicit capital outflows to boost national savings destroyed through hyper-consumerism and resolving the balance of payments (BoP) crisis without resorting to speculative foreign financing through ISBs (rising BoP issues are indicated by the deficit in the current account recording over $ 400 million in the first nine months of 2026).\n\nAs Niccolo Machiavelli observed, only those at the base can see what the apex is like. Only the ruled know what the rulers are like.\n\nCenturies later, Marxism elaborated the point philosophically and epistemologically. Capitalism can be understood as a totality only by those who view it, not necessarily from the lived personal experience, but from the standpoint and perspective of the working classes\u2014the majority within the system, at the base.\n\nThis isn\u2019t to do with the class origins of the leaders/ members. One of the most refined African minds of the 20th century, Amilcar Cabral, founder-leader of the Guinea-Bissau national liberation movement, assassinated by the Portuese colonial secret service, famously said that the liberation movement, composed as it was of the petty-bourgeoisie, must \u2018commit class suicide\u2019 and be \u2018reborn\u2019 as the proletariat, i.e., with the class consciousness of the proletariat."
