    "md5": "a6ac20d605856977f8345b612ff8f7e1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 675,
    "chunk_text": "Stewardship means taking over something that is not yours and leaving it in better shape than you found it. Our banking system is stronger today than it has been for years. The task now is to cool the credit boom without breaking the businesses that keep this economy producing, employing and exporting.\n\nRaising rates and reserves treats one half of the problem. If we ignore the other half, we may find ourselves with less money, fewer goods, and prices that are still rising.\n\n(The author is a former senior banker, Regional Director of CIMA for the Middle East, South Asia and North Africa, Head of PPP (2017), and has served on two national Education Reform Commissions)"
