    "md5": "782cd6ff0430416c528812c5be21370f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "FACETS 2027 puts Sri Lankan jewellery in spotlight\n\nFACETS Sri Lanka 2027 takes place on 4\u20136 January 2027 at Cinnamon Life \u2013 City of Dreams, Colombo\n\nA grander pavilion, a \u201cBridges of Light\u201d design competition, Sapphire Night and a new Gem Conversations morning headline the 34th edition\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s gemstones have long dazzled the world. At FACETS 2027, the spotlight turns to the artistry that transforms them into jewellery. The Sri Lanka Gem & Jewellery Association (SLGJA) has announced the jewellery program for the 34th edition of FACETS Sri Lanka, to be held from 4 to 6 January 2027 at Cinnamon Life \u2013 City of Dreams, Colombo.\n\nRecognised as South Asia\u2019s premier gem and jewellery exhibition, FACETS celebrates the design excellence and manufacturing expertise that complement the country\u2019s coloured gemstones.\n\nSLGJA Vice President Shezard Careem, who leads the jewellery segment, said this year\u2019s program is built around four focus areas.\n\nA grander stage: With the exhibition moving to the larger main Lumina Ballroom, the Jewellery Pavilion will be positioned at the entrance, with new participants exhibiting alongside established jewellery houses to present fine jewellery collections and bespoke creations.\n\nBridges of Light: A dedicated area will showcase the Jewellery Design Competition, themed \u201cBridges of Light\u201d, which celebrates peace, unity and human connection. Ten finalist designs are being made by some of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading jewellery houses, and the completed pieces will be unveiled at the exhibition, where the winners will be announced. The competition aims to nurture emerging talent and raise design standards, while giving designers local and international exposure.\n\nSapphire Night: The industry\u2019s most glamorous occasion returns, blending fashion, entertainment and celebration for exhibitors, invited guests and international buyers."
  },
