    "chunk_text": "Commenting on her appointment, Nanayakkara said, \u201cIslandwide Scientific has built a strong reputation through its technical expertise, international partnerships and commitment to customer service. Our priority is to continue strengthening these capabilities while responding to the changing needs of Sri Lanka\u2019s scientific and research community. We remain committed to providing our customers with reliable solutions and specialised technical support to advance their work.\u201d\n\nThesath Nanayakkara, who oversees Technology and Data Innovation on the Advisory Board, holds a PhD in Computational and Applied Mathematics from the University of Pittsburgh, USA, and is also a Mathematics and Industrial Statistics graduate of the University of Colombo, Sri Lanka. His professional experience includes serving as a Quantitative Strategist and currently as a Machine Learning Scientist at leading US multi-national organisations, bringing expertise in machine learning, quantitative research and data analytics.\n\nYasas Nanayakkara brings 15 years of experience in Sales and Marketing. He is a Chartered Marketer (CIM, UK) and holds a Master of Business Administration from the University of Southern Queensland, Australia.\n\nThe team brings expertise spanning technology and data science, sales and marketing, operations and scientific instrumentation.\n\nUnder its new leadership, Islandwide Scientific will continue to develop its portfolio of internationally sourced scientific and analytical equipment while expanding its service capabilities. These include professional installation and training, rapid turnaround repairs, precision field calibration, and preventive maintenance services, supported by an experienced technical team and a dedicated engineering workshop at its Colombo head office. The company\u2019s extensive network of international manufacturers also enables it to bring specialised instrumentation and technical expertise to Sri Lankan laboratories and industrial facilities."
