    "chunk_text": "Drawing on Elsevier\u2019s Scopus database, the Stanford\u2013Elsevier assessment uses standardised citation indicators to identify influential researchers across scientific disciplines. The 2026 edition evaluates single-year citation impact during 2025 and career-long impact up to the end of 2025. Resonating with the international scientific community, the SLIIT-based scientists are proof of SLIIT\u2019s deliberate move to position itself as a leading research university.\n\nThe recognition of seven SLIIT academics places individual research achievement at the centre of this wider institutional direction. Alongside industry collaboration and international engagement, it supports a model of higher education in which Sri Lankan researchers contribute to global knowledge and students learn how to carry ideas into practice.\n\nTo strengthen the real-world impact of research, SLIIT is strategically expanding its footprint in innovation and entrepreneurship. This includes its membership in the Global Alliance of Entrepreneurial Universities as the first Sri Lankan member, a US patent, and growing collaboration with global industry leaders. Together, these efforts are helping SLIIT turn research into practical solutions, creating lasting value for industry and society."
