    "chunk_size_bytes": 1904,
    "chunk_text": "Varna wins National Silver and  Top 10 at CNCI Achiever Awards 2026\n\nVarna Packaging Ltd., Sri Lanka\u2019s pioneering flexible packaging manufacturer, has won a National Silver Award in the Extra-Large Category of the Manufacturing Sector and a Top 10 Award at the 25th CNCI Achiever Awards for Industrial Excellence, on 15 October 2026.\n\nThe awards come in the year Varna marks 65 years since its founding in 1961, and ahead of the completion in December of a new production building at its Ratmalana site. The building will house new gravure printing lines and add production capacity, strengthening the company\u2019s ability to serve customers in Sri Lanka and overseas. The company scaled significantly in the last 12 months, while the factory operated through a major construction program over the past 18 months, and managed to raise Varna\u2019s BRCGS grade from B+ to A.\n\n\u201cWhen we first entered these awards several years ago, we were awarded a Certificate of Merit,\u201d said Managing Director Chamindra Gamage. \u201cWe chose to invest in capability and our infrastructure over the past few years. It has been a bet on the growth we see ahead in the packaging industry and Sri Lanka as a nation. Earning a national Top 10 place while the factory was being upgraded is an early sign it is paying off. In December, our new gravure facility comes online and takes us a step further.\u201d\n\nThis year\u2019s result follows a record 2025, in which Varna became the only flexible packaging company in Sri Lanka to win 10 national awards in a single year. Those honours came from CNCI, the Chamber of Lankan Entrepreneurs, CIPM\u2019s Great HR Awards and FCCISL\u2019s Sri Lankan Entrepreneur of the Year.\n\nOver the past two years, Varna has also added several new pouch-making lines, expanded its research and development initiatives, introducing new and innovative sustainability focused products to the Sri Lankan market"
