    "chunk_size_bytes": 1596,
    "chunk_text": "CBL Investments named Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen at 23rd BCCS Awards\n\nCBL Investments has been named Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen for 2026, taking the top honour at the 23rd Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability (BCCS) Awards organised by The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce.\n\nThe awards ceremony, held at Shangri-La Colombo yesterday, recognised organisations setting high standards in corporate citizenship and sustainability across the country. Talawakelle Tea Estates and Commercial Bank of Ceylon were named first and second runners-up, respectively.\n\nRecognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s leading corporate sustainability awards, the BCCS Awards celebrate businesses that place responsible practices at the heart of their operations. They recognise organisations that balance economic performance with social and environmental responsibility and demonstrate how business can contribute to wider national progress.\n\nTalawakelle Tea Estates also secured the Category B Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Award 2026, presented to companies with an annual turnover of less than Rs. 15 billion. Elpitiya Plantations and Kelani Valley Plantations were named first and second runners-up, respectively, in this category.\n\nThe Top Ten Corporate Citizens award recognises organisations demonstrating outstanding sustainability performance. This year\u2019s ten recipients are CBL Investments, Citizens Development Business Finance, Commercial Bank of Ceylon, Elpitiya Plantations, Hatton National Bank, Haycarb, Hemas Holdings, Kelani Valley Plantations, Sampath Bank, and Talawakelle Tea Estates."
