    "chunk_size_bytes": 1083,
    "chunk_text": "Ex-cop wanted over T-56 rifle theft brought back from Dubai\n\nColombo, Nov 26 (Daily Mirror) - A former police officer wanted over the theft of his official T-56 assault rifle while on roadblock duty in Mount Lavinia has been arrested in Dubai and brought back to Sri Lanka today (26).\n\nThe suspect, identified as 26-year-old Jayakody Arachchige Kavindu Akash Jayakody, a resident of Halambagaswewa in Pemaduwa, Anuradhapura, is alleged to have stolen the firearm while serving at the Mount Lavinia Police and handed it over to members of an organised crime gang before fleeing the country.\n\nHe was arrested in a joint operation in Dubai involving officers of the Criminal Investigation Department (CID) and security personnel of SriLankan Airlines.\n\nThe suspect arrived at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) in Katunayake at around 5.20 a.m. today aboard SriLankan Airlines flight UL-226.\n\nUpon his arrival, CID officers took him into custody to record a statement. He is scheduled to be handed over to the Western Province South Crimes Division for further investigations."
