    "chunk_size_bytes": 1924,
    "chunk_text": "Thirty-one killed in massive fire as fuel tanker crashes on Cairo highway\n\nBBC - Thirty-one people have been killed and 21 others injured in a large fire on a busy highway in Cairo after a fuel tanker crashed, Egypt's health ministry says.\n\nHospitals nearby treated patients suffering burns and smoke inhalation after the incident, which occurred on a section of a ring road in the Warraq neighbourhood, to the north of the old city centre, on Wednesday evening.\n\nFootage circulating on social media showed billowing flames and black smoke towering high into the night sky, with multiple nearby vehicles torched.\n\nOfficials have not given an account of how the fire broke out, but state-owned media reported the tanker had overturned, dousing nearby vehicles with petrol.\n\nThe regional public prosecutor has launched an investigation into the incident and asked that DNA samples be taken from bodies of the dead.\n\nThe tanker, which belonged to a private contractor, had been travelling along the highway when a high-voltage cable fell in front of it, prompting the driver to lose control, Al-Ahram reports, citing sources with knowledge of the investigation.\n\nIt then crossed the central reservation, overturned and caught fire, the state-owned newspaper says.\n\nEgypt has suffered several deadly fires in recent years, with informal residential areas and often run-down infrastructure making incidents more common, the response to which is often complicated by slow emergency response times and locally improvised rescue efforts, even in the sprawling Egyptian capital.\n\nImages from the scene show a large crowd gathered on the highway after the fire had been extinguished, as emergency services blocked off entry routes.\n\nThe health ministry said 39 ambulances had been dispatched to respond to the fire, while it posted images of Egypt's health minister overseeing the treatment of the injured at one of Cairo's hospitals."
