    "chunk_size_bytes": 856,
    "chunk_text": "Quazi Judge, woman arrested over Rs. 65,000 bribe\n\nColombo, Nov. 26 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) has arrested a Quazi Judge of the Colombo North Quazi Court and a woman for allegedly soliciting and accepting a bribe of Rs. 65,000 in connection with a divorce case.\n\nThe suspects were identified as Quazi Judge Mohamed Sawahir Mohamed Ramees and Fathima Nasreena.\n\nThe Quazi Judge was arrested inside the office of the Colombo North Quazi Judge.\n\nThe bribe had allegedly been solicited and accepted in exchange for delivering a favourable ruling for the complainant in a divorce case (Mubara) and a compensation case filed by his wife under the Muslim Marriage and Divorce Act.\n\nThe two suspects were produced before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court and remanded until December 1, 2026."
