    "chunk_text": "People can obtain HIV tests through government sexual health clinics or by visiting **knowforsure.lk**. HIV self-testing kits are also available through the website and can be delivered to people's homes, allowing them to check their HIV status privately.\n\nShe also highlighted the importance of practising safer sex and avoiding behaviours that increase the risk of infection, including drug use associated with sexual activity.\n\nPeople diagnosed with HIV must take their medication every day, at the prescribed time, and continue treatment throughout their lives. Interrupting treatment or failing to take medication properly can weaken the immune system and increase the risk of HIV progressing to AIDS.\n\n\u201cSome people do not take their medication regularly or at the correct time. This can weaken their immune system and allow the disease to progress to AIDS. However, with proper treatment and regular medication, people living with HIV can maintain their health and lead normal lives, just like those who are not infected with the virus,\u201d she said.\n\nDr. Gunathilake said that HIV testing and treatment services are provided with strict confidentiality and urged people who may have been exposed to the virus to seek testing without fear or embarrassment.\n\nThe rising number of infections in Sri Lanka, particularly among young people, underlines the urgent need for greater public awareness, regular testing and proper treatment to prevent the spread of HIV."
