    "chunk_text": "Restrictions on marriage proposal, rituals and enchantment advertisements questioned\n\nColombo, Nov. 26 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The government\u2019s decision to impose restrictions on advertisements pertaining to marriage proposals, rituals and enchantment practices was questioned in Parliament yesterday.\n\nMP Dayasiri Jayasekera who questioned the move said restrictions should not be imposed. He was referring to a remark made by Minister of Women and Child Affairs Saroja Paulraj who has said certain advertisements including marriage proposals where the caste which a potential bride or a groom belongs to and advertisements on rituals and enchantment practices will be banned.\n\n\u201cThe move comes from those who spoke against worshiping of idols and certain trees and Bo trees. They also said that the historic Jethawanaramaya should be filled with garbage,\u201d the MP said.\n\nHe said people should be free to get the media to advertise anything while they should be allowed to engage in a profession of their choice.\n\nHowever, the Office of the Minister of Women and Child Affairs rejected media reports claiming that Minister Saroja Savithri Paulraj had announced plans to introduce legislation banning matrimonial advertisements that specify caste.\n\nIn a clarification issued yesterday, the Minister\u2019s Office said certain media outlets had taken the Minister\u2019s remarks out of context and published misleading headlines.\n\nThe clarification follows a media briefing held at the Department of Government Information on November 23 to explain the 16-day national campaign to eliminate gender-based violence.\n\nDuring the briefing, a journalist questioned whether the Government should intervene in matrimonial advertisements specifying social criteria such as caste, pointing out that such advertisements could subject certain sections of society to harassment and discrimination.\n\nResponding to the question, the Minister said certain matters could be disregarded when making personal decisions."
