    "chunk_text": "Govt refutes claims of barring Russian Prosecutor General from visiting AG\u2019s Office, CIABOC\n\nColombo, Nov. 26 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Justice Minister Harshana Nanayakkara refuted allegations that the government prevented the Prosecutor General of the Russian Federation, Alexander Gutsan, from visiting the Attorney General\u2019s Department and the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC).\n\nAddressing Parliament, the Minister clarified that the government had made no such decision. Instead, according to information available to him, the move was decided independently by the Russian Prosecutor General\u2019s own security detail after assessing the security situation.\n\nMinister Nanayakkara made this clarification in response to remarks by Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP\n\nChithral Fernando, who cited media reports claiming that Gutsan had been restricted from visiting the two state institutions."
