    "chunk_text": "\"Your Honour, the psychiatric report prepared by the medical specialists concerning the third suspect, Suresh Sallay, has been received. It consists of 311 pages and 1,185 paragraphs. There is no finding in the report that the third suspect had been subjected to torture. Sallay himself has made 95 statements, while approximately 30 statements have been provided by his wife.\n\nThe Additional Solicitor General further informed court that an informant had alerted the State Intelligence Service (SIS) about Zahran Hashim's activities approximately six months before the Easter Sunday attacks.\n\nAccording to statements recorded from SIS officers by the CID, an intelligence officer identified as Waris had received information through an informant named Thambi Annam that Zahran Hashim was undergoing training in India with a group in October 2018 and was preparing to carry out an attack in 2019.\n\nHe had reportedly conveyed the information to senior SIS officials, following which it was referred to the desk responsible for monitoring extremist activities within the intelligence service.\n\nASG further stated that an intelligence file had been maintained in relation to the information and that, following the Easter Sunday attacks, Assistant Superintendent of Police Nirosha Gunawardena had handed the file over to Suresh Sallay. However, investigations had subsequently revealed that the file had gone missing.\n\nAppearing for the third suspect, Suresh Sallay, Counsel Bhanuka Malawiarachchi disputed the prosecution's interpretation of the medical report.\n\nHe submitted that the medical reports had not reached a final conclusion regarding the allegations made by his client and had instead recommended further investigations.\n\n\"Your Honour, the medical reports state that officers of the Criminal Investigation Department had lowered my client's trousers and examined him. However, the medical panel has not reached a final conclusion regarding the incident and has recommended further investigations."
