    "chunk_text": "\"Your Honour, the medical reports state that officers of the Criminal Investigation Department had lowered my client's trousers and examined him. However, the medical panel has not reached a final conclusion regarding the incident and has recommended further investigations.\n\nThe report also states that CCTV footage from the location where my client was detained at the CID is retained for only around 30 days. I do not understand why CCTV footage from such a location is deleted after just 30 days.\"\n\nAt this stage, the Magistrate questioned whether the medical report had specifically described the alleged incident as an indecent act.\n\nIn response, the defence counsel clarified that the report had not used the word \"disgraceful\" but had referred to an indecent act and recommended further investigations into the incident.\n\nThe Additional Solicitor General, however, maintained that the medical report had not indicated that the suspect had suffered any psychological distress."
