    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9ad19b3a818dff0893d900b9a0898af9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1317,
    "chunk_text": "Without a doubt, doctors, consultants, medical practitioners and officers working at all levels deserve to be provided with allowances and other benefits. They work under stressful conditions, sometimes without proper sleep, meals and having to stay away from their families for long periods of time. They don\u2019t have proper boarding facilities and as a result many doctors are compelled to do private practice.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s state sector needs a complete overhaul to rectify this issue. It is an issue that not only affects medical practitioners or doctors but the entire state sector.\n\nThe public service is the backbone of state administration, delivering essential daily services and implementing government policy across the country. Therefore, it is the duty of the government to ensure that at least some of the key demands of these state sector public officials are being met.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
  },
