    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "Janashakthi restates pre-IPO profit as finance arm slips below capital minimums\n\nFY25 group profit restated 10.5% lower to Rs.4.69bn, against Rs.5.24bn in IPO prospectus\n\nParent says group strongly capitalised as finance arm\u2019s Tier I and total capital ratios breach minimums\n\nJanashakthi PLC has cut its group profit for 2024/25 by 10.5 percent to Rs.4.69 billion, after correcting a series of prior-period errors, revising the Rs.5.24 billion figure it presented to the investors in the prospectus for its Rs.5 billion initial public offering (IPO) in April, its audited accounts filed with the Colombo Stock Exchange showed.\n\nThe LKAS 8 restatement also cut the profit attributable to the shareholders by 15.2 percent to Rs.2.68 billion and total equity at end-March 2025 by 8.2 percent to Rs.15.87 billion.\n\nThe holding company profit fell 13.7 percent to Rs.3.02 billion, from Rs.3.50 billion in the prospectus, lowering the earnings per share to Rs.4.76, from Rs.5.52 on a pre-subdivision basis.\n\nBy Mirror Business calculations, the revision cuts the prospectus\u2019 36.3 percent return on equity to about 30.7 percent and lifts the implied price-to-earnings multiple at the Rs.10 issue price to about 6.0 times, from 5.15 times, although the restated book value is marginally higher.\n\nMost of the profit revision stems from the intra-group fair value gains booked by First Capital Holdings PLC on its stakes in Janashakthi Insurance PLC and Janashakthi Finance PLC, which were not eliminated on consolidation and inflated the 2024/25 profit by Rs.413.5 million.\u00a0 A 2017/18 consolidation entry had also been recorded twice, overstating the non-controlling interests by about Rs.1.4 billion in every year since, although correcting it lifted the equity attributable to the shareholders."
