    "chunk_text": "The parent\u2019s interim accounts, signed two days later, make no reference to the shortfall, with the executive summary instead stating that the finance company \u201cdemonstrated resilience\u201d and that \u201cthe group and its subsidiaries are strongly capitalised to absorb these uncertainties\u201d.\n\nIt also put the finance company\u2019s profit after tax at Rs.162 million, a figure matching its total comprehensive income rather than its Rs.198.6 million profit after tax.\n\nIts parent, with an effective 93.44 percent stake, has used Rs.1 billion of IPO proceeds to repay the borrowings and earmarked Rs.3.5 billion for acquiring or establishing insurance, microfinance and non-bank financial businesses, uses which the prospectus says include meeting prudential requirements and capitalising new or acquired entities, without naming Janashakthi Finance. Meanwhile, the group swung to a Rs.1.46 billion half-year loss from a Rs.3.08 billion profit a year earlier, with First Capital Holdings alone losing Rs.1.3 billion and its shares closed September at the Rs.10 IPO price.\n\nThe filings leave open when the errors were first identified, whether they were known before the prospectus was issued and whether any IPO proceeds will shore up Janashakthi Finance\u2019s capital. (NF)"
