    "chunk_text": "23rd Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Awards  CBL Investments named as Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen\n\nFrom left: Rathika de Silva, Sanath Manatunga \u2013 CEO Commercial Bank (Second Runner-Up), Phillip Ward \u2013 Director and Country Representative UNWFP, Shea Wickramasingha \u2013 Chairperson CBL Investments (Winner), Krishan Balendra \u2013 Chairperson Ceylon Chamber, Roshan Rajadurai \u2013 MD Talawakelle Tea Estates (First Runner-Up)\n\nCBL Investments has been named as Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen for 2026, taking the top honour at the 23rd Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability (BCCS) Awards, organised by The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce.\n\nThe awards ceremony, held at Shangri-La Colombo yesterday, recognised organisations setting high standards in corporate citizenship and sustainability across the country.\n\nTalawakelle Tea Estates and Commercial Bank of Ceylon were named as the First and Second Runners-Up, respectively.\n\nRecognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s leading corporate sustainability awards, the BCCS Awards celebrate businesses that place responsible practices at the heart of their operations.\n\nThey recognise organisations that balance economic performance with social and environmental responsibility and demonstrate how business can contribute to wider national progress.\n\nTalawakelle Tea Estates also secured the Category B Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Award 2026, presented to companies with an annual turnover of less than Rs.15 billion.\n\nElpitiya Planations and Kelani Valley Plantations were named respective First and Second Runners-Up in this category.\n\nThe Top Ten Corporate Citizens award recognises organisations demonstrating outstanding sustainability performance.\n\nThis year\u2019s 10 recipients are CBL Investments, Citizens Development Business Finance, Commercial Bank of Ceylon, Elpitiya Plantations, Hatton National Bank, Haycarb, Hemas Holdings, Kelani Valley Plantations, Sampath Bank and Talawakelle Tea Estates."
