    "chunk_text": "This year\u2019s 10 recipients are CBL Investments, Citizens Development Business Finance, Commercial Bank of Ceylon, Elpitiya Plantations, Hatton National Bank, Haycarb, Hemas Holdings, Kelani Valley Plantations, Sampath Bank and Talawakelle Tea Estates.\n\nThe winning projects for 2026 are Citizens Development Business Finance \u2013 CDB Elevate: Ditwah Recovery Centre \u2013 Restoration of the Information Technology Centre (ITC), University of Peradeniya; Coca-Cola Beverages Sri Lanka, with the Coca Cola Foundation as a key partner and funder \u2013 Strengthening Women and Youth Engagement in Informal Waste Management in Sri Lanka (SWYFT); Dipped Products \u2013 Firstlight Kirigovi Samithiya \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s First FSC-Certified Rural Smallholder Rubber Farmer Society; Hayleys Fentons \u2013 Roots of Resilience \u2013 Mangrove Ecosystem Restoration Project and Mirigama Dendro Power \u2013 Closing the Water Loop: A Circular Water Reuse Project for Renewable Energy.\n\nThe Triple Bottom-Line Awards recognise excellence across the three pillars of sustainability.\n\nTalawakelle Tea Estates received the Environmental Sustainability Award, MAS Holdings \u2013 the Social Sustainability Award and Bank of Ceylon \u2013 the Economic Sustainability Award.\n\nThe Category Awards recognise organisations for their performance across specific areas of corporate responsibility."
