    "chunk_text": "BOC Rings the Bell for Sri Lanka\u2019s Largest-Ever Listed Basel III Debenture Issue\n\nThe Bank of Ceylon (BOC) marked the listing of its historic Rs. 30 billion Listed Basel III Debenture Issue with a bell-ringing ceremony at the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), formally recognizing the largest ever, listed debenture issuance in Sri Lankan history.\n\nThe ceremony was attended by BOC\u2019s Chairman, Mr Kavinda de Zoysa, Board of Directors, General Manager/Chief Executive Officer, Mr Y.A Jayathilaka, and senior management, alongside the CEO of the CSE and key transaction stakeholders.Opened on 3 November 2026, the issue was oversubscribed and closed on the opening day after attracting over Rs. 39 billion in applications. Exercising its upsize options up to Rs. 30 billion, the transaction stands as a defining milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s domestic debt capital market.\n\nBOC Chairman Mr. Kavinda de Zoysa stated: \u201cThis bell ringing marks a historic milestone as we list Sri Lanka\u2019s largest-ever Basel III Compliant Listed debenture issue, being oversubscribed 3.9 times over the initial issue of Rs.10 billion on the opening day itself. This reflects strong investor confidence in BOC\u2019s financial strength, governance, and eight-decade legacy at the heart of Sri Lanka\u2019s financial ecosystem proving once again that BOC continues to lead and set new benchmarks for others to follow. We are deeply grateful to the Colombo Stock Exchange, our regulators, and our investors for their continued trust and participation in this landmark achievement.\u201d\n\nThe CEO of the Colombo Stock Exchange, Mr Rajeeva Bandaranaike added: \u201cWe congratulate the Bank of Ceylon on completing Sri Lanka\u2019s largest-ever listed debenture issue to date. Raising LKR 30 billion on the CSE demonstrates the growing capacity of our domestic debt market to support large-scale institutional funding. Issuances of this scale align with our efforts to expand market access and serve a broader investor base.\u201d"
