    "md5": "8ea4f5c8e02b64d28459fb1b35d47ea9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1615,
    "chunk_text": "Allianz reaches highest-ever brand value of US$ 30.7bn\n\nAllianz has once again been recognised as the world\u2019s most valuable insurance brand, securing this distinction for the eighth consecutive year in Interbrand\u2019s Best Global Brands 2026 ranking.\n\nThe Allianz brand reached a record value of US$ 30.7 billion, increasing by 9 percent year-on-year and advancing to 26th position among the world\u2019s most valuable brands across all industries.\n\nThe achievement reflects Allianz\u2019s continued financial strength, customer-focused approach, and commitment to building trust in an increasingly complex and interconnected world. The Group\u2019s brand growth is supported by strong business performance, including a record operating profit of EUR 9.4 billion in the first half of 2026, alongside sustained investments in innovation, customer experience, and brand management.\n\nThrough initiatives including the Allianz 3am Report, Allianz School for Life, Power of Unity, and Sense of Community, Allianz continues to support financial literacy, deepen understanding of customer needs, and strengthen connections within communities around the world.\n\nSport remains a powerful platform through which Allianz brings people together while promoting confidence, safety, and opportunity. In 2026, Allianz played a key role in supporting the safe and successful delivery of the Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games Milano Cortina 2026 as the Worldwide Insurance Partner of the Olympic and Paralympic Movements. The event welcomed more than 5.4 million spectators and reached an estimated global audience of 2.6 billion viewers."
