    "chunk_text": "Dialog launches \u2018Sayuru AI\u2019 Fisheries Advisory Voice Assistant\n\nFrom left: Nushan Rajapaksha, Associate Architect, AI Solutions, Dialog Axiata PLC; Tharusha Wanigasekara, Manager, Digital Innovation and Inclusion, Group Risk, Compliance & Sustainability, Dialog Axiata PLC; Asanga Priyadarshana, Group Chief Corporate Officer, Dialog Axiata PLC; Stepni Fernando, Member of Parliament, Gampaha District; Malith Fernando, Meteorologist, Department of Meteorology of Sri Lanka; Harshanath Jayasinghe, Manager, Negombo Fishery Harbour\n\nDialog Axiata PLC has launched \u2018Sayuru AI\u2019, Sri Lanka\u2019s first AI-powered fisheries advisory voice service, enabling fishing communities and other stakeholders to access essential fisheries information simply by dialling 828 from any mobile phone.\n\nAvailable in Sinhala, Tamil and English, the service reflects the company\u2019s commitment to enriching lives through technology by harnessing artificial intelligence to support safer fishing practices, informed decision-making, and greater digital inclusion across Sri Lanka\u2019s fisheries sector.\n\nDeveloped in partnership with the Department of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources and the Department of Meteorology, Aquatic and Ocean Resources, Sayuru AI was launched on 21 November to mark World Fisheries Day.\n\nThe newly introduced AI-powered voice assistant enhances Dialog\u2019s existing Sayuru Interactive Voice Response (IVR) service, enabling users to access fisheries-related information through natural voice interactions rather than navigating conventional menu-based systems. Available around the clock, the service provides information on marine weather forecasts, safety instructions at sea, fish market prices, and guidance on ornamental fisheries."
