    "md5": "f3ec384d30163096c442249ef5c84e5d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1596,
    "chunk_text": "The newly introduced AI-powered voice assistant enhances Dialog\u2019s existing Sayuru Interactive Voice Response (IVR) service, enabling users to access fisheries-related information through natural voice interactions rather than navigating conventional menu-based systems. Available around the clock, the service provides information on marine weather forecasts, safety instructions at sea, fish market prices, and guidance on ornamental fisheries.\n\nA Fisheries Ministry spokesperson said, \u201cThe fisheries sector plays a vital role in Sri Lanka\u2019s economy and in the livelihoods of communities across the country. Ensuring that fishing communities have access to timely and relevant information is important in supporting livelihoods and the sustainable development of the sector. Through initiatives such as Sayuru AI, collaboration between the government and the private sector can help extend the reach of essential services, strengthen support for fishing communities, and ensure that the benefits of technological advancement contribute to national development.\n\nThis initiative also marks an important step towards a new era of transformation in Sri Lanka\u2019s fisheries sector, moving beyond traditional practices towards a modern, technology enabled and knowledge driven industry. This transformation is expected to strengthen the resilience and the productivity of fisheries sector.\u201d A.L.K. Wijemannage, Director General of the Department of Meteorology said, \u201cTimely and reliable weather information is critical to the safety and livelihoods of Sri Lanka\u2019s fishing communities.\u201d"
