    "chunk_size_bytes": 1986,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018FACETS 2027\u2019 international gem and jewellery exhibition to kick off on Jan.4\n\nBuilding on Sri Lanka\u2019s legendary sapphires, Sapphire Night will return to FACETS 2027\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s gemstones have long dazzled the world. At FACETS 2027, the spotlight turns to the artistry that transforms them into jewellery.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Gem & Jewellery Association (SLGJA) has announced the jewellery programme for the 34th edition of FACETS Sri Lanka, to be held from 4 to 6 January 2027 at Cinnamon Life \u2013 City of Dreams, Colombo.\n\nRecognised as South Asia\u2019s premier gem and jewellery exhibition, FACETS celebrates the design excellence and manufacturing expertise that complement the country\u2019s coloured gemstones. SLGJA Vice President Shezard Careem, who leads the jewellery segment, said this year\u2019s programme is built around four focus areas.\n\nWith the exhibition moving to the larger main Lumina Ballroom, the Jewellery Pavilion will be positioned at the entrance, with new participants exhibiting alongside established jewellery houses to present fine jewellery collections and bespoke creations.\n\nA dedicated area will showcase the Jewellery Design Competition, themed \u201cBridges of Light\u201d, which celebrates peace, unity and human connection. Ten finalist designs are being made by some of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading jewellery houses, and the completed pieces will be unveiled at the exhibition, where the winners will be announced. The competition aims to nurture emerging talent and raise design standards, while giving designers local and international exposure.\n\nThe industry\u2019s most glamorous occasion returns, blending fashion, entertainment and celebration for exhibitors, invited guests and international buyers.\n\nFollowing the success of the Power Breakfast for Women, FACETS 2027 introduces The Gem Conversations \u2013 Stories That Sparkle, an intimate, invitation-only morning of gemstone stories, inspiring women and lively conversations about jewellery and creativity."
