    "chunk_size_bytes": 935,
    "chunk_text": "Muted trading continues to appear in secondary market\n\nAmidst the weekly T-bill auction held yesterday, the secondary market activity and trading volumes remained low, while the overall yield curve stood broadly stable across all maturities.\n\nAt the short-end, 01.05.2028 and 15.09.2029 traded at 10.70 percent and 10.99 percent, respectively.\n\nMoving ahead, 01.08.2030 traded at 11.30 percent, while 15.10.2030 changed hands at 11.35 percent.\n\nMoreover, the 15.12.2032 and 15.06.2034 bonds were dealt at 11.72 percent and 12.15 percent, respectively.\n\nOn the external front, the Sri Lankan rupee appreciated against the US dollar, standing at Rs.332.55/US dollar, compared to Rs.332.58/US dollar recorded previously.\n\nMarket liquidity in the banking system contracted to Rs.440.31 billion, compared to Rs.466.09 billion seen previously.\n\nThe PDMO is yet to publish the T-bill auction results for the auction held on November 25, 2026."
