    "chunk_text": "AMW launches Yamaha XSR-155 and NMAX-155 at Colombo Motor Show 2026\n\nAssociated Motorways (Private) Limited (AMW), the authorized distributor for Yamaha in Sri Lanka, unveiled two new 155cc two-wheelers for the local market the retro-styled Yamaha XSR-155 motorcycle and the Yamaha NMAX-155 scooterat the Colombo Motor Show 2026 at BMICH.\n\nWith the dual launch, Yamaha\u2019s Sri Lankan lineup now includes two distinct riding styles: a heritage-inspired manual motorcycle and a connected automatic scooter built for urban commuting.\n\nJawahar Ganesh, Group Managing Director of AMW said, \u201cSri Lankan riders are increasingly selecting two-wheelers according to their lifestyle, whether that means stress-free technology in everyday traffic in Colombo or weekend mechanical character. Backed by Yamaha\u2019s global Japanese engineering and AMW\u2019s nationwide after sales network, introducing the XSR-155 and NMAX-155 together at the Colombo Motor Show gives riders a clear choice between connected scooter practicality and retro motorcycle styling.\u201d\n\nDesigned for riders who want classic motorcycle proportions supported by modern hardware, the Yamaha XSR-155 combines a 155cc, air-cooled, 4-stroke, SOHC, 4-valve fuel-injected engine with a round LED headlight, LED taillight, digital instrument cluster, and 10-litre fuel tank. Paired with a 6-speed constant mesh gearbox and a wet multiple-disc clutch, the powertrain generates 13.5 kW (18.4 PS) at 10,000 rpm and 14.2 Nm of torque at 7,500 rpm. The 134 kg motorcycle has a Deltabox frame with telescopic front forks, a link-type swingarm rear suspension, 17-inch tubeless tyres, an 810 mm of seat height, 170 mm of ground clearance, and front and rear hydraulic single disk brakes with dual-channel ABS."
  },
