    "chunk_text": "Introducing the system on stage, Sungrow C&I Energy Storage Product Line General Manager Dr. Cao Wei pointed out that installers previously had to visit each site to work out its configuration, which often involved a huge amount of work. The commissioning agent now sets grid parameters automatically, runs communication checks and validates settings, cutting the risk of errors that come with manual verification and easing the training burden on service teams.\n\nBubbly\u2019s energy management agent goes further by changing how a battery earns its keep. Commercial storage plants have typically relied on a single revenue mode, such as storing solar power for self-consumption or shaving peak demand. The agent instead draws on solar generation and load forecasts to coordinate self-consumption, demand control, energy arbitrage and frequency regulation, continuously reshaping the dispatch plan to lift returns by more than 12 percent when compared to a conventional self-consumption mode.\n\nThe same logic runs through the company\u2019s smaller systems. For the PowerKeeper C&I battery, an AI-driven operating mode on Sungrow\u2019s iSolarCloud platform optimises energy scheduling to deliver 10 to 30 percent higher returns along with longer backup, Sungrow C&I Energy Storage Product Line Director Jim Hu told delegates. For homes, the flagship PowerHarbor applies similar AI scheduling around weather, solar output, battery levels and electricity prices. It also integrates EnergyBridge, which Sungrow bills as the industry\u2019s first mini backup solution, while Bubbly simplifies its installation and commissioning by up to 30 percent, according to the company."
