    "chunk_text": "The same logic runs through the company\u2019s smaller systems. For the PowerKeeper C&I battery, an AI-driven operating mode on Sungrow\u2019s iSolarCloud platform optimises energy scheduling to deliver 10 to 30 percent higher returns along with longer backup, Sungrow C&I Energy Storage Product Line Director Jim Hu told delegates. For homes, the flagship PowerHarbor applies similar AI scheduling around weather, solar output, battery levels and electricity prices. It also integrates EnergyBridge, which Sungrow bills as the industry\u2019s first mini backup solution, while Bubbly simplifies its installation and commissioning by up to 30 percent, according to the company.\n\nC&I storage systems are often scattered across remote locations, and after-sales teams typically drive long distances with testing equipment to check each system component by component, Dr. Cao noted. Bubbly\u2019s maintenance agent instead monitors system conditions around the clock and identifies more than 30 potential risks, generating a fault diagnosis report with maintenance recommendations for a 10 MWh plant within a minute. Sungrow has also upgraded iSolarCloud and introduced 24/7 AI-powered multilingual support for its partners.\n\nThat capability carries particular weight in emerging markets such as Sri Lanka, where specialised technical skills are not evenly spread. Sungrow told Mirror Business that Bubbly supports initial diagnostics and technical information searches for users and installers, while iSolarCloud allows service teams to track system performance and equipment health remotely. \u201cWe see digital innovation and local service capabilities as complementary rather than interchangeable,\u201d the company stressed, adding that combining AI-assisted diagnostics and digital operations and maintenance platforms with professional local service teams could deliver more timely and reliable support to end users."
