    "chunk_text": "That capability carries particular weight in emerging markets such as Sri Lanka, where specialised technical skills are not evenly spread. Sungrow told Mirror Business that Bubbly supports initial diagnostics and technical information searches for users and installers, while iSolarCloud allows service teams to track system performance and equipment health remotely. \u201cWe see digital innovation and local service capabilities as complementary rather than interchangeable,\u201d the company stressed, adding that combining AI-assisted diagnostics and digital operations and maintenance platforms with professional local service teams could deliver more timely and reliable support to end users.\n\nSensing and automated controls also underpin Sungrow\u2019s approach to battery safety. The PowerKeeper system is built on a patented three-layer architecture of proactive detection, instant interception and physical containment, Hu explained at a media briefing.\n\nThe first layer detects arc faults on both the solar and battery sides while monitoring temperature and other abnormal conditions. Once a fault is detected, an intelligent switch inside the inverter shuts down the array, removing the arc before it develops into a failure. The final layer, designed for extreme events such as thermal runaway, uses guided pressure relief to vent any explosion upwards so that nothing is ejected towards nearby people or buildings.\n\n\u201cMostly it\u2019s stopped by the first and second stage. The last stage is like the final extreme situation,\u201d Hu observed, adding that such an event had never occurred across the company\u2019s global shipments."
