    "chunk_text": "\u201cMostly it\u2019s stopped by the first and second stage. The last stage is like the final extreme situation,\u201d Hu observed, adding that such an event had never occurred across the company\u2019s global shipments.\n\nUnderneath the software, PowerStack 3.0 marks what Sungrow describes as a shift from all-in-one physical integration to \u201cScene-in-One\u201d design. Its multi-scenario dock accepts four modules covering power conversion, solar, EV charging and microgrid functions, allowing a single platform to serve as standalone storage, a solar-plus-storage system without a separate inverter, a solar-storage-charging hub or a microgrid with a zero-millisecond switchover to off-grid operation that needs no separate static transfer switch cabinet. A business that starts with solar and storage can later add EV charging by fitting the relevant module on site without replacing the battery, a Sungrow official explained at the media briefing.\n\nEach cabinet delivers 125 kW or 250 kW with 551 kWh of storage, giving roughly four-hour and two-hour configurations respectively, and up to 20 units can run in parallel for about 11 MWh. Its self-developed silicon carbide (SiC) power conversion system achieves a maximum conversion efficiency of 99.2 percent and, combined with 684 Ah stacked cells, delivers a round-trip efficiency of over 92 percent, with an energy density of up to 256 kWh per square metre."
