    "chunk_text": "Further evidence in Yoshitha Rajapaksa\u2019s money laundering case to be heard on December 3\n\nColombo, Nov. 26 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0The hearing of further evidence in the money laundering case filed by the Attorney General against Yoshitha Rajapaksa under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act was postponed till December 3 by Colombo High Court Judge Udesh Ranatunga.\n\nThe Attorney General filed this case against Yoshitha Rajapaksa, alleging that he committed an offence under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act by purchasing five plots of land in the Dehiwala and Ratmalana areas for a sum exceeding Rs. 730 million.\n\nYoshitha Rajapaksa received Rs. 5.15 million in Navy salaries and allowances over 10 years - Court told\n\nYoshitha Rajapaksa\u2019s case postponed till November 26 for further evidence\n\nYoshitha, former Navy Commander plead not guilty to corruption charges"
  },
