    "chunk_text": "Seven injured in huge Bangkok oil depot blast, four in critical condition\n\ncna - Seven people were injured, four of them critically, after a huge explosion rocked an oil facility in Bangkok on Thursday (Nov 26), according to a local emergency medical centre.\n\nThe Erawan Emergency Medical Centre, which is operated by city authorities, reported four \"red\" cases and three less severe \"yellow\" cases after the blast in the east of the Thai capital.\n\nAFP reporters saw a large fireball and black smoke rising above the city following the explosion at site run by Thai energy conglomerate Bangchak Corporation. It is Thailand\u2019s fifth-largest and is also the country\u2019s only refinery located in an urban area.\n\nThe Bangkok Metropolitan Administration advised residents to avoid the area.\n\nThe fire, which broke out at 2.51pm (3.51pm Singapore time), was later extinguished and the situation was returning to normal, according to government updates.\n\nBangchak said in a statement that it shut down all production units when the fire broke out.\n\nThe cause of the incident is under investigation, the company added.\n\n\u201cSitting at work, the building\u2019s shaking, smoke for an hour already,\u201d wrote X user JnKimnoeymi.\n\nAFP reporters a few kilometres away said the blast shook their doors.\n\nFlames rose high above the site, followed by black smoke that swept across the Thai capital's skyline, reported AFP.\n\nThe sirens of emergency vehicles could be heard heading to the scene."
