    "md5": "a3c14cfcfb76a8c8af0362e17b0a2acc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1384,
    "chunk_text": "Russia agrees to assist Sri Lanka in bringing crime suspects back\n\nColombo, Nov. 26 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Sri Lanka and Russia have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to strengthen bilateral legal cooperation, with Moscow agreeing to assist Sri Lanka in securing the return of individuals wanted over criminal activities who have fled to Russia.\n\nThe agreement was signed today (26) by Attorney General President\u2019s Counsel Parinda Ranasinghe and Prosecutor General of the Russian Federation Aleksander Gutsan during a meeting at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\n\nDiscussions focused on strengthening longstanding cooperation between the two countries and enhancing collaboration on bilateral legal matters.\n\nDuring the meeting, Gutsan assured that Russia would continue to assist Sri Lanka in tracing and securing the return of individuals involved in criminal activities in Sri Lanka who had fled to Russia, as well as locating their financial assets and properties held there.\n\nHe said such assistance would be extended in accordance with the provisions of Sri Lanka\u2019s Proceeds of Crime Act.\n\nThe Russian Prosecutor General also appreciated the cooperation extended by Sri Lanka in judicial matters and other areas of mutual interest.\n\nSenior officials from the Russian Federation and representatives of the Attorney General\u2019s Department of Sri Lanka attended the meeting."
