    "chunk_size_bytes": 1814,
    "chunk_text": "Diesel tanker carrying up to 7,000 tonnes sinks near Ibiza, killing one\n\nBBC - An oil tanker carrying up to 7,000 tonnes of diesel has sunk off the coast of Ibiza, leaving one crew member dead, authorities have said.\n\nThe Med Emre, a Malta-flagged vessel, was carrying 17 crew members who were all rescued. However seven were taken to hospital and one was later pronounced dead, Balearic Islands emergency services confirmed.\n\nThe six crew receiving treatment reportedly suffered minor injuries, such as hypothermia, Spanish media reports.\n\nThe possible environmental damage is being assessed by a plane and Spain's pollution control vessel, Clara Campoamor, which is owned by the country's national maritime rescue service.\n\n\"There is still little information available about a possible fuel spill,\" Balearic Islands' President Marga Prohens wrote on X.\n\nRegional emergencies director Pablo G\u00e1rriz said the tanker had not completely sunk, and was still partially submerged.\n\nThat made conditions more favourable for carrying out recovery operations, he said, \"as we have gone from the possibility of the vessel being at a depth of 1,000m to a situation that allows operations to be carried out on the surface.\"\n\nThe Med Emre sank 25 nautical miles (46 km; 29 miles) from Ibiza's coastline and 57 nautical miles from Valencia. It is unclear what caused the sinking.\n\nThe chemical tanker was en route from Algeciras, in southern Spain, to Barcelona in the north-east.\n\nRescuers in Valencia received a distress call around 22:30 local time (21:30 GMT) on Wednesday, according to Spanish media. Minutes later, the vessel reported a leak and the crew said it was leaning at a 90-degree angle.\n\nThe injured crew members have been taken to hospitals in Valencia and Can Misses Hospital in Ibiza, President Prohens said."
