    "chunk_text": "Whatever statements the UN may issue, the abuse of the veto by the United States has repeatedly scuttled UN-led efforts to find a just solution to the Palestinian question. The use of the veto, nearly on 50 occasions, to obstruct peace lends credence to accusations that US foreign policy is driven not by universal moral values but by power politics, which in turn rests on the use of force, the threat of violence and the intimidation of weaker nations.\n\nIn a travesty of justice, Palestine was partitioned under UN Resolution 181 with the minority Jews, most of whom were European migrants, being allocated 55 per cent of the territory, while the majority Arabs were allotted only 43 per cent. Jerusalem and its environs were to be placed under international administration.\n\nNeedless to say, a partition plan that disregarded the principles of natural justice and undermined the very objectives behind the creation of the United Nations became a trigger for a continuing Nakba, or ethnic cleansing of Palestinians, the 1948 Arab-Israeli war, and subsequent conflicts in 1967, 1973 and beyond, culminating in Israel\u2019s genocide in Gaza following a Hamas attack on Israeli communities near the border on October 7, 2023.\n\nToday, the Palestinians have been left with only a fraction of the territory once envisaged as their state. The area administered by the Palestinian Authority under the 1993 Oslo Accords constitutes less than 17 per cent of the territory allocated to Palestinians under the partition plan. Palestinian land continues to shrink as the Israeli government vigorously pursues an expansionist policy in blatant disregard of international law, amid growing criticism that Israel has become an apartheid state."
