    "chunk_text": "Today, the Palestinians have been left with only a fraction of the territory once envisaged as their state. The area administered by the Palestinian Authority under the 1993 Oslo Accords constitutes less than 17 per cent of the territory allocated to Palestinians under the partition plan. Palestinian land continues to shrink as the Israeli government vigorously pursues an expansionist policy in blatant disregard of international law, amid growing criticism that Israel has become an apartheid state.\n\nDirecting criticism solely at the United States and Britain for the Palestinian plight tells only half the story. The story is incomplete without a critical examination of the role of certain Arab states, which stand accused of betraying the Palestinian cause, colluding with Israel, and failing to exert sufficient diplomatic pressure to halt the violence in Gaza. Arab resolve to confront Israel has become so feeble and ineffective that one could bet one\u2019s life that even if a camel were to pass through the eye of a needle, the Arab nations would still not go to war with Israel."
