    "chunk_size_bytes": 1480,
    "chunk_text": "Defence Secretary calls for stronger regional collaboration on shared security challenges\n\nAttends NSA level meeting of Colombo Security Conclave in Mal\u00e9\n\nDefence Secretary Air Vice Marshal (Retd.) Sampath Thuyacontha attended the 8th National Security Advisers\u2019 (NSA) Meeting of the Colombo Security Conclave (CSC), in Mal\u00e9, Maldives on 25 November.\n\nDefence Secretary is among the top defence heads of regional countries attending the Conclave.\n\nAddressing the gathering the Defence Secretary expressed his appreciation to the Government of Maldives for hosting the meeting and for its hospitality. He observed that the Colombo Security Conclave has steadily evolved over the years into an important regional platform for addressing shared security challenges through dialogue, cooperation and collective action. He noted that the growing engagement among member countries reflects a common recognition that regional security and stability are fundamental to sustainable development and prosperity.\n\nHighlighting the importance of the Conclave\u2019s five pillars of cooperation, Maritime Safety and Security; Countering Terrorism and Radicalisation; Combating Trafficking and Transnational Organised Crime; Cyber Security and Protection of Critical Infrastructure and Technology; and Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief, the Defence Secretary stressed the need for strengthened regional collaboration in an increasingly interconnected and complex security environment."
