    "chunk_text": "Highlighting the importance of the Conclave\u2019s five pillars of cooperation, Maritime Safety and Security; Countering Terrorism and Radicalisation; Combating Trafficking and Transnational Organised Crime; Cyber Security and Protection of Critical Infrastructure and Technology; and Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief, the Defence Secretary stressed the need for strengthened regional collaboration in an increasingly interconnected and complex security environment.\n\nDrawing on the recent experience of Cyclone Ditwah, he further emphasised the importance of strengthening regional disaster preparedness, early-warning mechanisms, emergency response coordination, humanitarian assistance and the sharing of knowledge and best practices on climate change adaptation and resilience.\n\nHe emphasised Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to the objectives of the Colombo Security Conclave and expressed the country\u2019s readiness to work closely with all participating nations to strengthen practical cooperation, enhance institutional engagement and advance shared regional security priorities. He also pointed out the collective responsibility of the participating countries to work towards a peaceful, secure and prosperous Indian Ocean Region.\n\nThe 8th NSA Meeting brings together representatives of CSC member countries to discuss regional security priorities and further strengthen cooperation in addressing common and emerging challenges in the Indian Ocean Region.\n\nThe Chief of National Intelligence, Additional Secretary for South Asia and SAARC of the Ministry of\u00a0 Foreign Affairs Varuni Muthukumarana, and Senior Assistant Secretary of the Ministry of Defence Chinthaka Abeykoon, were also part of the Sri Lankan delegation."
