    "chunk_text": "The longstanding salary issues of the biggest group of the public sector cadre, of 225 000 professionals in teachers\u2019 service, remains unresolved. Teacher unions have now called for a token strike if the Government does not agree to grant the remaining two-thirds of the salary adjustments promised according to the Subodini Report and in the interim a cost-of-living allowance of Rs. 25 000.\n\nIndeed, a Budget that is crafted to win over the IMF, which is due for a visit to the country next week, is unlikely to be popular among the voters. It has demonstrated that a Government shackled by the conditionalities of the IMF cannot truly deliver economic justice. The NPP Government should not shackle the whole country to another IMF agreement.\n\n(The author is a PhD Candidate in Education at the University of Massachusetts Amherst and a member of the Feminist Collective for Economic Justice)"
