    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c5e8434f181aa227497d8cfabfaaf792",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1948,
    "chunk_text": "Consider a company that holds a 12% stake in a publicly listed company.\n\nThe company itself is owned by several corporate shareholders, each holding more than 10%.\n\nTwo of these shareholders are, in turn, owned by other companies, each also holding more than 10%.\n\nMultiple layers of ownership are not illegal. BO registration exists to identify the natural persons who ultimately own or control these companies. The difficulty is that the secretary responsible for the company at the end of the chain cannot obtain BO approval because some companies higher up have not yet received their own. One company\u2019s registration therefore depends on several others.\n\nThe company\u2019s Annual Return is due, and the statutory deadline has passed, but it cannot be filed without BO approval. Is it reasonable to hold one company responsible for delays caused by other companies in its ownership structure, which may themselves be waiting for the Registrar?\n\nThis also raises a question: who analyses these, and how often? Should the law be amended to hold a company responsible for reporting this information as a needed to know basis?\n\nThe BO requirements appear to be applied in the same way to every registered company, regardless of activity, ownership structure or financial capacity. Special consideration may be justified for:\n\nnGovernment-owned companies, which may need a different reporting procedure given their public ownership and existing accountability arrangements. What do they report, and where? The Treasury can have a list of all of its companies and so forth.\n\nCompanies that have not commenced business, which are registered but have never started trading.\n\nSmall companies, with annual turnover below a specified threshold, which may need simplified reporting.\n\nGuarantee companies, the Registrar of Companies gives verbal instructions to indicate the Board of Directors, while the e-ROC system has such information directly available."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-27-dailyftlk-9b209bed",
