    "md5": "861cddf4e8101fe05600b9c569b7640d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1755,
    "chunk_text": "Review the BO website with independent IT professionals and practising company secretaries, including adding the ability to save and edit applications.\n\nProvide proper human support, so applicants can resolve problems without repeatedly visiting the Registrar\u2019s office.\n\nThe Ministry of Finance, meanwhile, has a broader responsibility for creating an economic environment that facilitates rapid development and investment. Perhaps it is time to reconsider whether the ROC should be elevated to a more prominent institutional position under the Ministry of Finance, with the authority, resources, and technical capacity needed to fulfil its expanding responsibilities.\n\nCorporate transparency is not merely a regulatory requirement; it is a foundation for investor confidence and a modern economy. Shouldn\u2019t the institution responsible for safeguarding it be positioned accordingly?\n\nBO registration is an important requirement, but good legislation and good administration must go together. A compliance system should help businesses meet their legal obligations, not prevent them from doing so.\n\nIf the Government wants businesses to operate transparently, it must ensure its own institutions do the same: efficiently and accountably. The question is not whether Sri Lanka should adopt modern technology, which it certainly should. The question is whether the technology is properly designed, adequately tested and supported by people who understand the needs of those who use it.\n\nThe Government should not penalise businesses for delays created by its own administrative machinery. Digitalisation should make doing business easier, not turn company administration into a burden that pushes businesses to abandon the corporate structure altogether."
  },
