    "chunk_text": "Available in Sinhala, Tamil and English, the service reflects the company\u2019s commitment to enriching lives through technology by harnessing artificial intelligence to support safer fishing practices, informed decision-making and greater digital inclusion across Sri Lanka\u2019s fisheries sector.\n\nThe launch event brought together Government representatives, fisheries sector stakeholders and fishing community representatives to demonstrate how voice-based artificial intelligence can improve access to essential information and support more informed decision-making.\n\nA Ministry of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources spokesperson said: \u201cThe fisheries sector plays a vital role in Sri Lanka\u2019s economy and in the livelihoods of communities across the country. Ensuring that fishing communities have access to timely and relevant information is important in supporting livelihoods and the sustainable development of the sector. Through initiatives such as Sayuru AI, collaboration between the Government and the private sector can help extend the reach of essential services, strengthen support for fishing communities and ensure that the benefits of technological advancement contribute to national development. This initiative also marks an important step towards a new era of transformation in Sri Lanka\u2019s fisheries sector, moving beyond traditional practices towards a modern, technology-enabled and knowledge-driven industry. This transformation is expected to strengthen the resilience and productivity of the fisheries sector.\u201d"
