    "md5": "f317412abaef7d18ccc2833ded38c61a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1948,
    "chunk_text": "SL makes landmark appearance as Guest Country of Honour at 9th China International Import Expo 2026\n\nSri Lanka marked a significant milestone in its international trade promotion and economic diplomacy by participating as a Guest Country of Honour at the 9th China International Import Expo (CIIE 2026), held from 5 to 10 November 2026 at the National Exhibition and Convention Center in Shanghai, China.\n\nThis prestigious recognition highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s growing international presence and provided an important platform to promote its export excellence, investment opportunities, national identity and rich cultural heritage.\n\nOrganised by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), under the Ministry of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, in collaboration with the Embassy of Sri Lanka in Beijing and the Consulate General of Sri Lanka in Shanghai, the participation reflected a coordinated national effort to strengthen bilateral trade and investment relations with China. Sri Lanka\u2019s recognition as a Guest Country of Honour, alongside Canada, was particularly significant as the country has participated continuously in CIIE since its inauguration in 2018.\n\nUnder the national promotional theme \u201cYour Vital Island,\u201d Sri Lanka presented its unique strengths through a dedicated 252-square-metre National Country Pavilion, featuring five key institutions: the EDB, Sri Lanka Tea Board, Coconut Development Authority, National Gem and Jewellery Authority and Sri Lanka Handicrafts Board (Laksala). The pavilion showcased internationally recognised products, including Ceylon Tea, Ceylon Cinnamon and other spices, precious gemstones and jewellery, coconut-based products, coir products and traditional handicrafts. A major highlight was the visit of Chinese Vice Premier H.E. Ding Xuexiang to the Sri Lanka Pavilion, which further enhanced the country\u2019s international visibility and the significance of its participation."
  },
