    "chunk_text": "Under the national promotional theme \u201cYour Vital Island,\u201d Sri Lanka presented its unique strengths through a dedicated 252-square-metre National Country Pavilion, featuring five key institutions: the EDB, Sri Lanka Tea Board, Coconut Development Authority, National Gem and Jewellery Authority and Sri Lanka Handicrafts Board (Laksala). The pavilion showcased internationally recognised products, including Ceylon Tea, Ceylon Cinnamon and other spices, precious gemstones and jewellery, coconut-based products, coir products and traditional handicrafts. A major highlight was the visit of Chinese Vice Premier H.E. Ding Xuexiang to the Sri Lanka Pavilion, which further enhanced the country\u2019s international visibility and the significance of its participation.\n\nSri Lanka also showcased its cultural heritage at the CIIE Culture Night held on 6 November 2026, attracting approximately 650 distinguished guests. The event featured traditional cultural performances by Chandana Wickramasinghe and the Dancers\u2019 Guild, including the traditional \u201cUkusa Vannama.\u201d The program celebrated the longstanding friendship between Sri Lanka and China while highlighting the importance of cultural diplomacy and people-to-people connections alongside economic cooperation.\n\nAn important objective of Sri Lanka\u2019s participation was to promote Sri Lanka Expo 2027 among Chinese buyers, importers, distributors and investors, encouraging them to visit Sri Lanka, explore its export capabilities and establish long-term business partnerships. With bilateral trade between Sri Lanka and China reaching approximately $5.2 billion in 2025, including Sri Lankan exports of approximately $278.58 million, CIIE offered a valuable opportunity to further diversify exports and expand market access."
