    "chunk_size_bytes": 1308,
    "chunk_text": "Digital Trust Alliance President Lakmal Embuldeniya said: \u201cEach year, professional firms and think tanks provide valuable commentary on the Budget, and we aim to add a digital trust lens to that conversation. Budget 2027 makes a meaningful investment in digital public infrastructure. The dashboard allows anyone to see where that money is allocated, how it compares with last year, and whether investment in digital platforms is matched by investment in cybersecurity, data protection and oversight. It is a living tool that we will continue to improve, and we invite citizens to help shape it through their comments. We also hope it gives investors, both local and foreign, a clear and transparent view of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital priorities.\u201d\n\nAll 2027 figures are drafts and may change before Parliament\u2019s final vote on 14 December 2026. The DTA will update the dashboard to reflect the approved Budget.\n\nThe DTA is a Sri Lanka-based alliance that brings together professionals and organisations to advance cybersecurity, information security, governance, risk, compliance and privacy. Through knowledge-sharing, capacity building and evidence-based dialogue with policymakers, industry and civil society, the DTA works to strengthen trust in Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy and digital public services."
