    "md5": "1799ecb746680a1bce3bbd8b4cdc2166",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1618,
    "chunk_text": "AICPA - CIMA Sri Lanka Post Budget Forum charts priorities for reform, investment and growth\n\nPanel discussion moderated by BDO Sri Lanka Managing Partner Ashane Jayasekara which included Jetwing Travels Managing Director Shiromal Cooray, Brandix Group Managing Director Hasitha Premaratne, Finance and Planning Ministry Tax Policy Adviser Thanuja Perera, First Capital Holdings PLC Managing Director/CEO and Janashakthi Group Deputy CEO Dilshan Wirasekara\n\nGovt., business and economic leaders explore implications of Budget 2027 and Sri Lanka\u2019s economic outlook\n\nAs Sri Lanka moves from economic stabilisation towards its next phase of growth, the focus is increasingly shifting from policy commitments to implementation, with investment, competitiveness and consistency in the policy environment emerging as key priorities.\n\nThese themes took centre stage at the CIMA Post Budget Forum 2027, which brought together senior Government officials, business leaders, economists and finance professionals to examine the implications of the Budget for businesses, investors and Sri Lanka\u2019s broader economic outlook.\n\nHeld under the theme \u201cThe 2027 Budget and Beyond: Navigating the Future of Business and Growth\u201d, the forum explored the Government\u2019s fiscal direction, the evolving business landscape and the reforms required to build on Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery.\n\nSetting the context for the forum, Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, FCMA (UK), CGMA, delivered the keynote address, outlining the Government\u2019s economic priorities, fiscal direction and broader reform agenda under Budget 2027."
  },
