    "language": "en",
    "md5": "78b147c04637e7ebe3ff95b3098a1371",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1759,
    "chunk_text": "Setting the context for the forum, Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, FCMA (UK), CGMA, delivered the keynote address, outlining the Government\u2019s economic priorities, fiscal direction and broader reform agenda under Budget 2027.\n\nProviding a tax and regulatory perspective, KPMG Sri Lanka Principal \u2013 Tax and Regulatory Suresh R. I. Perera, FCMA (UK), CGMA, examined proposed changes relating to personal income tax, VAT administration and investment incentives, highlighting their practical implications for businesses, compliance and financial planning.\n\nAgainst the backdrop of Sri Lanka\u2019s progress towards economic stabilisation, Advocata CEO Dhananath Fernando focused on the structural reforms needed to sustain this momentum. His presentation addressed public-private partnerships, State-owned enterprise reform and investment protection as important elements in strengthening the country\u2019s long-term economic prospects. Bringing the corporate perspective to the discussion, John Keells Holdings Deputy Chairperson and Group Finance Director Gihan Cooray, FCMA (UK), CGMA, examined the commercial implications of Budget 2027, with particular focus on business confidence, capital allocation and long-term investment decisions.\n\nThe program culminated in a high-level panel discussion moderated by BDO Sri Lanka Managing Partner Ashane Jayasekara, FCMA (UK), CGMA.\n\nJoining the keynote speaker and presenters were Jetwing Travels Managing Director Shiromal Cooray, FCMA (UK), CGMA; Brandix Group Managing Director Hasitha Premaratne, FCMA (UK), CGMA; Ministry of Finance and Planning Tax Policy Advisor Thanuja Perera; and First Capital Holdings PLC Managing Director and CEO and Janashakthi Group (JXG) Deputy CEO Dilshan Wirasekara."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
