    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "17a7e2f945083c874f1ea58f5026b5f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1632,
    "chunk_text": "Joining the keynote speaker and presenters were Jetwing Travels Managing Director Shiromal Cooray, FCMA (UK), CGMA; Brandix Group Managing Director Hasitha Premaratne, FCMA (UK), CGMA; Ministry of Finance and Planning Tax Policy Advisor Thanuja Perera; and First Capital Holdings PLC Managing Director and CEO and Janashakthi Group (JXG) Deputy CEO Dilshan Wirasekara.\n\nThe conversation reinforced a central message: the impact of Budget 2027 will ultimately depend on how effectively policy commitments are translated into measures that strengthen investor confidence, productivity and competitiveness.\n\nPolicy consistency and predictability also remain important as businesses make decisions on capital allocation, expansion and long-term investment.\n\nAhead of the Budget, AICPA and CIMA submitted recommendations across eight priority areas aimed at strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s productivity, investment environment and overall economic competitiveness.\n\nSeveral of these priorities are reflected in measures announced under Budget 2027.\n\nAmong the key areas of alignment is State-owned enterprise reform, including the proposed holding-company structure for 34 enterprises. Measures relating to public asset management and public-private partnerships, supported by planned legislation, also reflect areas highlighted through the Association\u2019s pre-Budget advocacy.\n\nTrade and investment facilitation represents another area of convergence, including funding for the National Single Window for Trade, while efforts to pursue RCEP membership and expand trade agreements are expected to support greater international market access."
  },
