    "md5": "930c70abc914e73da0136d3aa983fb17",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1036,
    "chunk_text": "Trade and investment facilitation represents another area of convergence, including funding for the National Single Window for Trade, while efforts to pursue RCEP membership and expand trade agreements are expected to support greater international market access.\n\nThrough its pre-Budget advocacy and Post-Budget Forum, AICPA and CIMA continues to bring the expertise of the accounting and finance profession into Sri Lanka\u2019s economic policy dialogue, connecting policymakers with the practical perspectives of businesses, investors and finance professionals.\n\nThe post-Budget forum provides a platform to move the conversation beyond the measures announced in the Budget to consider what they mean in practice for enterprise, investment and economic growth. As Sri Lanka looks beyond stabilisation, the challenge is increasingly one of execution. Turning reform into results will be critical to building business confidence, attracting investment and strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness on the path towards sustainable growth."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-27-dailyftlk-9c3469a3",
