    "chunk_text": "Their potential contributions are distinct but complementary: business networks and institutional facilitation on one side; practical knowledge of handicraft retail, regional artisan development, product presentation and customer expectations on the other. Together, these could help bring rural producers closer to Colombo\u2019s commercial life\u2014not simply as recipients of assistance, but as suppliers with something valuable to offer.\n\nThis is where the engagement of Johnny Fernando and Anil Koswatte could be particularly valuable.\n\nThe International Chamber of Commerce is an international business organisation concerned with trade and enterprise, with ICC Sri Lanka (ICCSL) serving as its national committee.\n\nFernando\u2019s interest, alongside the focus of the Chairman and members of the ICCSL SME Facilitation Subcommittee, provides an opportunity to explore connections with businesses and institutional channels that might otherwise remain beyond the reach of village-based producers.\n\nFor a woman working from home in Mannar, access to a corporate buyer, retailer or experienced business mentor is not straightforward. An informed introduction can help bridge that distance. It can create a conversation about product requirements, pricing, delivery and the possibility of a continuing commercial relationship through structured SME support.\n\nThe opportunity is therefore wider than finding individual supporters. Through dialogue with ICCSL leadership, Palms Together hopes to explore how business connections could help rural enterprises become more visible and better prepared to serve new customers.\n\nKoswatte brings a complementary understanding through Lakarcade\u2019s work with Sri Lankan gifts, souvenirs and handicrafts.\n\nGuided by Koswatte, alongside COO\u2013Commercial Kelum Jayawardane and Project Director \u2013 Regional Arts and Crafts Development Dammika Jayawardane, the Lakarcade\u2019s team brings both commercial retail discipline and dedicated experience in working with regional craft producers."
  },
  {
