    "md5": "e3374825b6a85686547db622e426bd06",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1997,
    "chunk_text": "Guided by Koswatte, alongside COO\u2013Commercial Kelum Jayawardane and Project Director \u2013 Regional Arts and Crafts Development Dammika Jayawardane, the Lakarcade\u2019s team brings both commercial retail discipline and dedicated experience in working with regional craft producers.\n\nFor both palmyra artisans and handloom weavers, such guidance could connect traditional regional skills with urban and tourist demand without compromising the cultural authenticity of their craft.\n\nThese discussions are developing; they are not formal institutional commitments already concluded. Their significance lies in the opportunity to bring commercial understanding and regional craft development closer to the women who produce the goods.\n\nThe Daily FT reported in June 2026 that Lakarcade had been appointed a National Entity Member of the World Crafts Council AISBL. In October, the newspaper also reported that Lakarcade had been accepted as a participant of the UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka, reaffirming its commitment to sustainable and responsible business practices.\n\nFor Palms Together, the relevance is practical. The program seeks to connect traditional craftsmanship with commercially viable opportunities while keeping women\u2019s livelihoods at the centre. Engagement with a retailer whose leadership encompasses regional craft development and responsible business standards offers a useful basis for that conversation.\n\nThe challenge is to translate shared interests into achievable steps: informed feedback, suitable product selections, introductions and, where commercially appropriate, orders.\n\nPalms Together began in 2025 with a small stall at Colombo\u2019s Good Market, bringing palmyra handicrafts and handloom products to new customers.\n\nSince then, the program has secured two international grants: support from the Avery Dennison\n\nFoundation in September 2025, followed by the Government of Japan\u2019s Grant Assistance for Grassroots Human Security Projects program in October 2026."
  },
