    "chunk_text": "Colombo\u2019s retailers gain access to distinctive Sri Lankan goods. Prospective corporate buyers can explore locally made products. Artisans gain feedback, market information and opportunities to build more dependable income.\n\nThis is a different relationship from that of benefactor and recipient. It is an exchange in which each side brings something useful.\n\nIt does not require forgetting the past. It requires creating relationships through which people can build a future together.\n\nFor Palms Together, the grants are an important achievement\u2014but they are not the end of the story.\n\nThe next chapter depends on connecting women\u2019s production with sustained demand. Mr Johnny Fernando\u2019s business connections through ICCSL and Mr Anil Koswatte\u2019s retail and regional crafts expertise could help the program move towards that goal, working alongside the women leaders who have brought it this far.\n\nTheir interest in supporting SMEs, particularly in the war-affected North and East, offers a basis for cooperation that recognises both the difficulties these communities face and the commercial potential they possess.\n\nFor Colombo\u2019s business community, the invitation is practical: consider the products, share informed feedback, explore a purchase or make a useful introduction.\n\nA grant can help build a centre. Local women can organise production. The right business relationships can help turn both into lasting livelihoods."
