    "chunk_text": "Suspect arrested over Rs. 1 Mn bank fraud using fake website\n\nColombo, Nov. 27 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0A 25-year-old man has been arrested over the alleged theft of Rs. 1 million from a bank account using a fraudulent website designed to resemble the official website of a private bank.\n\nPolice said the suspect had allegedly obtained the victim\u2019s bank account login credentials through the fake website and subsequently transferred the money from the account.\n\nAn investigation was launched following a complaint lodged with the Wariyapola Computer Crime Investigation Division.\n\nBased on information uncovered during the investigation, the suspect was arrested yesterday afternoon (November 26).\n\nThe suspect, who is employed as a data entry operator at a private institution, is a resident of Ragama.\n\nThe Wariyapola Computer Crime Investigation Division is conducting further investigations into the incident."
