    "md5": "72eeb5f8733b14b9f7c397f79bc1e25d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "Western Hospital relaunched as Arora Hospital\n\nThe relaunch of Western Hospital as Arora Hospital was marked by a grand opening ceremony held on its premises on Cotta Road, Borella, Colombo 8, recently.\n\nThe ceremony was held under the patronage of hospital Chairperson Dr. Habeeba Sheriff.\n\nThe chief guest, Member of Parliament Dr. Najith Indika, hoisted the National Flag, while the guest of honour, Private Healthcare Services Regulatory Council Secretary Dr. T.M.I.S. Priyantha, hoisted the Arora Hospital flag.\n\nIndika also ceremonially cut the ribbon and unveiled the commemorative plaque to mark the official opening of the hospital. Zainab Sheriff delivered the welcome address.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Dr. Habeeba spoke of the beginning of a new chapter in a journey that commenced more than four decades ago \u2014 a journey driven by a vision and a heartfelt commitment to healing with empathy.\n\nShe recalled how the journey began with her late father, Prof. Rezvi Sheriff, a pioneer of nephrology in Sri Lanka, who dedicated his life to providing compassionate care to the patients suffering from kidney disease.\n\nShe further highlighted Prof. Sheriff\u2019s pioneering contributions to the field of nephrology and transplantation, describing him as an innovator who constantly pursued excellence and never settled for anything ordinary or mediocre.\n\nAmong his many groundbreaking achievements were the introduction of the first dialysis services, the first continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis programme and the first kidney transplantation in Sri Lanka as well as the introduction of new medications in the field of transplantation.\n\nProf. Sheriff\u2019s passion for healing also extended beyond Sri Lanka. He introduced immunosuppressive therapy for transplant patients in Nigeria and trained doctors in Fiji to perform renal biopsies, extending his knowledge and expertise to the international medical community."
  },
