    "md5": "7a7b4ae06a721ec7acb91572a9a7316c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Prof. Sheriff\u2019s passion for healing also extended beyond Sri Lanka. He introduced immunosuppressive therapy for transplant patients in Nigeria and trained doctors in Fiji to perform renal biopsies, extending his knowledge and expertise to the international medical community.\n\nIn keeping with this vision, Arora Hospital has implemented a state-of-the-art, AI-enabled hospital information system developed by 21C Care, a leading Sri Lankan software development company specialising in healthcare information systems.\n\nThe system enables doctors and nursing staff to access and monitor patients\u2019 medical records in real time. It also incorporates AI-powered predictive intelligence to assist doctors in evaluating and identifying the most appropriate treatment options, thereby supporting more informed clinical decision-making.\n\nShe emphasised that Arora is not merely a rebranding exercise but rather a reinvigoration of her father\u2019s enduring passion and commitment to providing quality and affordable healthcare to all patients.\n\nBuilt on the core values of compassion and care, Arora Hospital is committed to treating patients as individuals rather than simply addressing their illnesses. The hospital strives for excellence in every aspect of its services, with a promise to stand by patients throughout their healthcare journey \u2014 from admission and treatment to discharge and post-recovery care.\n\nDr. Habeeba also expressed pride in the hospital\u2019s dedicated, efficient and talented team, which includes some of the most experienced healthcare professionals in the field of renal medicine. She reaffirmed the hospital\u2019s commitment to continuously enhancing its services and embracing innovation to deliver better healthcare outcomes for its patients.\n\nIndika and Dr. Priyantha also addressed the gathering, extending their remarks and best wishes on the occasion."
