    "md5": "2cb11eb6c7576c8ac0d76ebf7b084115",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1718,
    "chunk_text": "Gallagher doubles  Sri Lanka office space;  signals further investment\n\nGlobal insurance brokerage and risk management firm Gallagher has doubled its office space in Sri Lanka, with the opening of a new office at Orion City IT Park, reaffirming its commitment to expanding operations and investing in local talent.\n\nThe new office, located on the 10th floor of Orion City IT Park, is twice the size of the company\u2019s previous premises on the 12th floor.\n\nThe expansion marks another milestone in Gallagher\u2019s growth in Sri Lanka since entering the country in 2022. The company started with a small team of 12 technology professionals and has since expanded its workforce to more than 130 employees.\n\nSpeaking at the opening ceremony, Gallagher Chief Information Officer EMEA Brent Kruger said the expansion reflected the company\u2019s confidence in Sri Lanka and its skilled workforce.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m proud of the Gallagher team and what we have built here in Sri Lanka. The support the team provides is highly valuable to our global business,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said the expansion demonstrated Gallagher\u2019s long-term commitment to Sri Lanka and its intention to continue investing in local professionals.\n\n\u201cIt shows our commitment to Sri Lanka and the fantastic skill sets that we have here. Gallagher plans to continue to invest in good people,\u201d he said.\n\nFounded in 1927, Gallagher is a global insurance brokerage, risk management and consulting services firm headquartered in the United States. It employs 73,000 people and operates in approximately 130 countries.\n\nGallagher Director Operations Malsha Jayamaha said the opening of the new office was a significant milestone for the company\u2019s Sri Lankan operations."
  },
