    "md5": "7a22f29099e18845b4d607c689848e90",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2017,
    "chunk_text": "Fitch upgrades Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation General to \u2018AA-(lka)\u2019\n\nSri Lanka Insurance Corporation General Limited (SLICGL) achieved a key financial milestone as Fitch Ratings upgraded its National Insurer Financial Strength (IFS) Rating to \u2018AA-(lka)\u2019, from \u2018A+(lka)\u2019, Outlook Stable, on November 19, 2026.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s leading general insurer, SLICGL holds the highest Fitch IFS rating among the rated non-life insurers islandwide.\n\nSLICGL\u2019s elevation highlights clear credit differentiation and places the company ahead of other Fitch-rated general insurers in Sri Lanka, which are rated \u2018A+(lka)\u2019 and below. The rating is backed by the company\u2019s profile, capitalisation and financial performance.\n\nThe rating action follows Fitch Ratings\u2019 comprehensive recalibration of its Sri Lankan national rating scale, which was triggered due to the upgrade of Sri Lanka\u2019s Long-Term Local-Currency Issuer Default Rating to \u2018B-\u2019, from \u2018CCC+\u2019, with a Stable Outlook, on September 22, 2026.\n\nNational ratings highlight an issuer\u2019s creditworthiness relative to other issuers in the country.\u00a0 In addition to the capital strength, the upgraded rating represents SLICGL\u2019s market leadership and a \u2018Favourable\u2019 company profile.\n\nAs the largest non-life insurer in Sri Lanka since 2024, SLICGL commands a 20 percent market share of non-life gross written premium as of 2025.\n\nFitch Ratings\u2019 assessment further acknowledges the company\u2019s long operating history, leading franchise and broad distribution network and solid profitability, with an average return on equity of 12 percent over 2024 and 2025.\n\nSLICGL was the first general insurer in Sri Lanka to hit a Rs. 30 billion topline and has further strengthened its no one position in general insurance in 2026.\n\nIn year-to-date 3Q 2026 (IASL 2026) SLICGL has strengthened its position in motor with its iconic Motor Plus brand as well and strengthened its non-motor position becoming no one in non-motor in the latest quarter 3Q."
  },
