    "chunk_text": "Singapore businesses explore Sri Lanka for expansion at Port City Colombo Investor Forum\n\nRepresentatives from the High Commission of Sri Lanka in Singapore, SLSTE and CHEC\u00a0 at the investor forum\n\nThe High Commission of Sri Lanka in Singapore and the Sri Lanka Singapore Tech Exco (SLSTE), in collaboration with Port City Colombo, hosted the Port City Colombo Investor Forum in Singapore on 20 November.\n\nThe evening forum was Port City Colombo\u2019s second in the country this year, following an earlier forum in January, and was designed to introduce Port City Colombo\u2019s investment and business setup proposition to businesses, particularly in the technology sector, that are looking to expand their operations or establish a presence in another jurisdiction.\n\nDelivering the opening address, Senarath Dissanayake, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka in Singapore, spoke to the strength of the relationship between the two countries and the opportunities for Singapore\u2019s business community in Sri Lanka. \u201cSingapore and Sri Lanka share strong economic and people-to-people ties, and Singapore\u2019s technology community is among the most dynamic in the region,\u201d he said. \u201cPort City Colombo offers businesses a modern, well-regulated base in Sri Lanka, and we are pleased to see it return to Singapore to share that opportunity directly with this community.\u201d\n\nMahesh Kavinda, President of SLSTE, opened the evening with welcoming remarks. \u201cSri Lankan tech professionals in Singapore, and the businesses they work with, are well placed to see what Port City Colombo can offer,\u201d he said. \u201cFor companies thinking about where to expand or set up next, this forum gives a clear look at the options, and SLSTE is pleased to help connect the two communities.\u201d"
