    "md5": "4d991558adb7c220c73a7d20ecc7d90e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2027,
    "chunk_text": "Everyone wants \u2018my share\u2019 despite pay hike, says Labour Minister\n\nSays sections of society demand their share regardless of what govt. delivers\n\nTies govt.\u2019s success to revenue collection, credits closed doors to corruption\n\nA three-stage public service pay hike has done little to quell demands from sections of society who want \u2018my share\u2019 regardless of what the government delivers, Labour Minister and Deputy Minister of Finance and Planning Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando said on Wednesday.\n\nSpeaking as chief guest at InsureChamp 2026, the Insurance Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka\u2019s (IRCSL) inter-university insurance quiz competition, Dr. Fernando pointed to a tendency within society to put individual claims first. \u201cThere is a little tendency within society that no matter what the government does, \u2018we need my share\u2019. Everyone claims this,\u201d he remarked.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look at what we have done over the last two years. We have stabilised, and we have offered a huge public service salary increase in three stages, with the last increase to be given on January 1, 2027. But still, people are not happy,\u201d he added.\n\nHis remarks came as trade unions representing engineers, university non-academic employees, teachers, principals and pre-school teachers intensified protests against Budget 2027. The Association of Public Service Engineers staged a token strike on November 13 before moving to island-wide action. Twenty trade unions representing executive service categories also announced strike action, while teacher and principal unions called a protest over the non-allocation of a proposed Rs.25,000 interim allowance.\n\nAlthough he did not name any union, Dr. Fernando took aim at professionals who rank their own contribution above everyone else\u2019s. \u201cIt could be a doctor, an engineer or an accountant. Yes, everyone\u2019s contribution to society is very, very important, but you can\u2019t say that \u2018my contribution is the biggest one\u2019. Everyone\u2019s contribution is critical,\u201d he insisted."
  },
