    "chunk_text": "High import protection, policy uncertainty and regulatory and institutional constraints had discouraged export diversification, she said.\n\n\u201cBut macroeconomic stability, while important, is not sufficient to deliver sustained growth and prosperity,\u201d Cowlin said.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s efforts to join the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) could open further opportunities in the region, Cowlin said. Turning that access into export growth would require domestic reforms to lower trade costs, improve the investment climate and help firms innovate, diversify and raise productivity.\n\nThe National Export Development Plan for 2026\u20132030, launched earlier this year with ADB support, provided a framework for diversifying exports. She said the value of the initiatives would ultimately be measured by whether they delivered tangible gains in exports, investment and productivity."
